            author = "Shockna",
            text = "Does this quest award any rep with the Stormpike Guard?",
            date = "2007-08-15T21:20:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6982#comments:id=138561",
        },
        {
            id = 1601109,
            score = 2,
            author = "622017",
            text = "I have tried to do this quest maybe thirty times. But I can never seem to get 10 of the supplies before the battleground ends. And the supplies all disappear from my inventory when the battle ends. The battles are just too short; usually 5 to 7 minutes each. And that isn't enough time to get to the mine, kill everything in my way, get the supplies, and turn them in after fighting my way back through the Horde. The supplies need to remain in our bags until the next time we do the BG.\n\nOr maybe someone has figured out how to do this one REALLY quick?",
            date = "2011-12-23T21:35:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6982#comments:id=1601109",
        },
    },
    [6985] = {
        {
            id = 340541,
            score = 3,
            author = "24541",
            text = "4 Gold, 40 Silver when completed at level 70.  You need sixty Irondeep supplies (6 stacks), to complete the ground assault (5-6 Level 70 Elites spawn that go attack the Alliance base).",
            date = "2008-07-30T13:23:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6985#comments:id=340541",
        },
        {
            id = 1625749,
            score = 3,
            author = "Anarchy",
            text = "Goodluck getting all 10 of them and heading back to the quest giver in time before a win/lose and not being killed by the enemy while handing the quest in.",
            date = "2012-02-13T05:06:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6985#comments:id=1625749",
        },
        {
            id = 1733203,
            score = 1,
            author = "Thorngral",
            text = "Okay, with the Resil changes, These guys are not funny. I swear they melee for 50k on plate- Each!\nSaw a blood dk who thought they were a joke and just rode in and attacked, he got gibbed in seconds!\nMy rogues taken to just running these all game, I get gold,\nIf the horde manages to think of defense before losing, We get troops and win. (if not, i get gold. i like gold).\n\nEdit: My point is they pierce resil, So clothys who stack resil and don't kite die in like one hit, Anything above takes two hits. Also Reinforcements only go down when towers and players do.. So defend and hold onto mines and AV can still go on for a long time.",
            date = "2012-10-06T08:49:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6985#comments:id=1733203",
        },
    },
    [7001] = {
        {
            id = 11168,
            score = 27,
            author = "Serpent",
            text = "The Frostwolf Stable Master is located along the east wall south of the Horde starting cave.\n\nYou must accept the quest given, use the Frostwolf muzzle on any wolf and tame it.  You then take the wolf back to the stable master to turn in and then get another quest.  It takes 25 wolves to complete this portion of summoning the wolf riders.\n\nIf you don't have it turned on it helps a lot to have quick quest text or whatever it's called turned on in the interface.  You don't really want to watch the quest text roll by slowly 25 times in a game.",
            date = "2006-12-08T13:50:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7001#comments:id=11168",
        },
        {
            id = 325663,
            score = 15,
            author = "Vlad",
            text = "#showtooltip\n/use Frostwolf Muzzle\n/click GossipTitleButton3\n/click GossipTitleButton1\n/click QuestFrameAcceptButton\n/click QuestFrameCompleteQuestButtonUse this macro to:Accept the quest\nTame the Frostwolf\nTurn in the tamed Frostwolf\nDeliver the quest\n(loop)",
            date = "2008-07-13T12:40:59-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7001#comments:id=325663",
        },
        {
            id = 1705899,
            score = 6,
            author = "Myebika",
            text = "You can spam this quest with your guild tabard for 365 guild rep per turn in, and it's repeatable.\n\nGet exalted with your guild in no time! :D\n\nEdit: as you try to save time turning in this quest faster and faster, MAKE SURE THE WOLF HAS CAUGHT UP TO YOU AND IS RIGHT NEXT TO YOU WHEN YOU TURN IN THE QUEST. Otherwise the wolf will not dissapear and you will have to relog.",
            date = "2012-08-29T19:14:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7001#comments:id=1705899",
        },
        {
            id = 749990,
            score = 4,
            author = "381031",
            text = "K so I did the quest like 4 times and I was the only one doing the quest cause everyone else was busy doin the actual pvpin and for some reason one of the wolves kept following after I truned it in. I was like 'Ok its just a glitch, no big deal' wll when I used the muzzle on another wolf it didn't take and the wolf kept attacking. I thought perhaps that too was a glitch. So I abandoned, got the quest again, tried again, same thing. Happened a afew times. Any advice?",
            date = "2009-06-18T03:03:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7001#comments:id=749990",
        },
        {
            id = 2844835,
            score = 3,
            author = "Gothy",
            text = "The muzzle works in BfA. I can complete the quest. I think I gained 1 point of Reputation with Frostwolf Clan or maybe it was just a coincidence with something else going on in the BG. The ! appears yellow but either it's broken or repeatable. Not sure what benefit is gained, if anything.",
            date = "2018-11-10T11:43:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7001#comments:id=2844835",
        },
    },
    [7002] = {
        {
            id = 11140,
            score = 20,
            author = "Serpent",
            text = "The Horde need 25 ram hides to get the Frostwolf Riders up and going.\n\nThe best location to get these is just south of Stormpike Graveyard in the valley down by the water.  A few sweeps of the area will net you 25 ram hides, you get one per kill.",
            date = "2006-12-08T13:38:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7002#comments:id=11140",
        },
        {
            id = 131602,
            score = 2,
            author = "Boshnak",
            text = "46,22 there are a lot of rams",
            date = "2007-08-03T09:56:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7002#comments:id=131602",
        },
        {
            id = 30008,
            score = 1,
            author = "19176",
            text = "I can't find the guy 4 the quest is he moving around and get killed by ally?",
            date = "2007-02-03T11:50:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7002#comments:id=30008",
        },
        {
            id = 6228010,
            score = 1,
            author = "Arkaan",
            text = "So, I turned in the  25 Ram hides (as Horde), both in normal Alterac Valley, and in Korrak's Revenge anniversary event, and the Frostwolf Rider option does not appear. I get an  emote for me to tell them to send the riders, but there is no chat option to select and thus, for now, this is a total waste of time in TWW expansion. We'll see later.",
            date = "2025-11-17T21:24:30-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7002#comments:id=6228010",
        },
        {
            id = 361587,
            score = -4,
            author = "168285",
            text = "Just as a point of reference, this is pretty much useless now. With most AV's only lasting 10 to 15 minutes (on average) you won't have enough time to ride all the way up, kill 25 rams and ride all the way back down to turn them in.\n\nI have tried this a few times with others helping to kill them faster and get the hides but in the end the AV was over before we could turn them in.",
            date = "2008-08-25T11:25:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7002#comments:id=361587",
        },
    },
    [7026] = {
        {
            id = 17193,
            score = 7,
            author = "Caffi",
            text = "You can find Frostwolf Hide's on the frostwolf's, one area to find a wolf is outside the iceblood tower.\nThe frostwolfs can be found all over the southern part of Alterac Valley though, just ride (or run) with the rest of the group, and loot a wolf when it falls.\n\nBut not even a epic mount can outrun a frostwolf, these wolfs are pretty fast. If you get aggro, you either take som hits and run far away, or you slay it, usually you will get some help if anyone is nearby.",
            date = "2006-12-19T02:32:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7026#comments:id=17193",
        },
        {
