    [7161] = {
        {
            id = 86610,
            score = 82,
            author = "53461",
            text = "This quest is given by Warmaster Laggrond in the Alterac Mountains at 62,59. I would recommend a group of at least 3 for this quest to be completed effectively.\n\nOnce you enter Alterac Valley, the entrance to the Wildpaw Cavern is located at 52,89. Once there, you need to fight your way in to retrieve a Frostwolf Banner (http://www.wowhead.com/?object=179025) for the quest.\n\nThe banner itself is located at 50,93, deep inside the cave. There are many mobs spaced closely together around the level of 52-56, so it is very possible that you will be pulling 3 at a go.\n\nNOTE: Watch out for Alterac Yeti (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=13959), a level 61 elite wandering the cave.\n\nThe reward from the quest, Frostwolf Insignia Rank 1 (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=17690) allows you to port back to Frostwolf Keep once every 2 minutes.\n\nThis trinket is upgraded as you gain reputation with the Frostwolf Clan.\n\nNeutral: Rank 1 (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=17690)\nFriendly: Rank 2 (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=17905)\nHonored: Rank 3 (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=17906)\nRevered: Rank 4 (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=17907)\nExalted: Rank 5 (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=17908)",
            date = "2007-05-21T03:39:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7161#comments:id=86610",
        },
        {
            id = 120122,
            score = 28,
            author = "6989",
            text = "You missed Rank 6 :)\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=17909#M0z\n\nThe surrounding mobs are level 66-68 in the level 61-70 version of Alterac Valley, three is standing near the flag and you'll have to fight them at once. Bring a friend, or a potion, if you are playing a class that can't heal yourself. The wandering Yeti is level 71, he hits for ~1500 on leather, so keep your eyes open.",
            date = "2007-07-13T16:27:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7161#comments:id=120122",
        },
        {
            id = 317221,
            score = 17,
            author = "Arkke",
            text = "I just solo'd this quest as a 66 Affliction Warlock. Of course, everyone in the 61-70 bracket is too busy telling you how long ago they finished the quest to actually help you complete it. So, a few failed battlegrounds later, I finally mastered the art. I assume most classes with mass CC could use this method (i.e., Priests with Psychic Scream, potentially a Frost Mage's Frost Nova, etc.)\n\nBasically, just zerg rush into the entrance of the cave. Rush straight between the two big groups on your left and right, fire off a Howl of Terror (if you have it on instant cast) once you've got a group behind you, fall off the ledge and head right. You'll come across a narrow passage with a couple decent-sized rocks against the right wall in the center of the passage; try to die as close to those rocks as you can. Once you're dead, release, and don't resurrect at the graveyard. Run back to your corpse in the cave, and try to resurrect by that rock, preferably closer to the entrance of the cave, and hug the wall. Check ahead of you to make sure you won't aggro the knoll that's standing farther back in the passage when you resurrect.\n\nNow, there's a gnoll that patrols the ledge immediately above the rocks I'm speaking of. If you keep an eye on him, you can resurrect just as he's walking away and you'll have plenty of time for a Voidwalker before you make your second zerg rush. Not at all necessary to summon a Voidwalker here; I didn't use one for the entire run. Just make sure he's far enough down his partol that you don't aggro him when you resurrect, or it will screw up your second rushS bigtime.\n\nOnce you've resurrected, catch your breath and rush straight down the passage, and take a hard right. You'll see the banner in the back on the passage, on an island in the middle of a frozen pond. The gnolls will likely kill you before you get there, so just die close enough that you can resurrect on top of the banner. Die again, and make one last corpse run, making sure your mass CC is completely cooled down.\n\nAs soon as you resurrect, gather up the five gnolls in the area of the banner (1 on the island, and 4 around it), try to get these as close to the center island as you can, and fire your CC. At my level, Howl of Terror lasts for 8 seconds; I was able to loot the banner in what appeared to be 6 seconds. So, I had about enough time to fire the CC, jump on the island and loot. So, even with lower-rank Howl of Terror, you should be able to take the banner with just barely enough time to spare. Just be careful not to do this too close to any of the groups beyond the icy pond, or you risk grabbing an add and spoiling the attempt.\n\nSo, assuming you don't mess up, you can easily get this banner in 3 deaths, assuming you let the gnolls kill you the last time rather than escaping. Try to do this as early and as quickly as you can; if you Allies capture your graveyards in the south and your team is already up north, you could end up running the length of the instance back to your corpse in the cave. I attempted this a few times and didn't even have a change to finish my attempt simply due to the fact that the game ended too quickly. It may take a few instances before you get the cave down, but once you do, you should have no trouble.\n\nGood luck getting your Insignia!",
            date = "2008-07-01T04:51:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7161#comments:id=317221",
        },
        {
            id = 907665,
            score = 12,
            author = "355344",
            text = "DOES NOT count towards Loremaster of Eastern Kingdoms\n\nDOES count towards total Quest Completion Achievement",
            date = "2009-12-06T11:53:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7161#comments:id=907665",
        },
        {
            id = 1297545,
            score = 9,
            author = "demonangel19",
            text = "And for those of you that are doing this quest for gits and shiggles, the cave you must enter is INSIDE the BG. spent forever trying to find it in hillsbrad, just to discover its in AV itself. so as soon as you pick it up, queue for it.",
            date = "2011-01-17T08:33:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7161#comments:id=1297545",
        },
    },
    [7162] = {
        {
            id = 277870,
            score = 103,
            author = "gpdoyon",
            text = "Let's be really-really clear...the quest is INSIDE an instance. You must join an Alterac Valley fight/instance in order to get to the cave.",
            date = "2008-04-26T16:32:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7162#comments:id=277870",
        },
        {
            id = 223,
            score = 79,
            author = "3687",
            text = "Inside Alterac Valley, head to the Harpy Cave (40,29) and work your way to the back and a large circular room.  The banner is in the middle of the room.  Loot it and return to the quest giver outside of AV for the turn in.\n\nTo get the next rank, you simply have to meet the reputation requirement, and he'll have another quest for you.  No need to repeat the banner, you just get a new Insignia from him each time.\n\nThere are 6 Stormpike Insignias:\n\n(Level 51, min) Rank 1: Quest - Can be done at Neutral\n(Level 51, min) Rank 2: Friendly (3000 rep)\n(Level 54, min) Rank 3: Honored (6000 rep)\n(Level 60, min) Rank 4: Revered (9000 rep)\n(Level 60, min) Rank 5: Exalted (21000 rep)\n(Level 60, min) Rank 6: Full Exalted (1000 rep)",
            date = "2006-09-13T10:27:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7162#comments:id=223",
        },
        {
            id = 100988,
            score = 35,
            author = "58941",
            text = "Its in Alterac Valley and not in Alterac Mountains. I made this mistake when i first got the quest :(.",
            date = "2007-06-08T20:48:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7162#comments:id=100988",
        },
        {
            id = 337279,
            score = 27,
            author = "152867",
            text = "Once you're near the end of the cavern, it'll fork. Do NOT take the one on the right leading up - there's a nasty level 71 elite Yeti hiding there.",
            date = "2008-07-27T03:01:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7162#comments:id=337279",
        },
        {
            id = 212476,
            score = 20,
            author = "Kastaje",
            text = "The name of the cave is icewing cavern and it's located south (a little southwest) from dun baldar for those who haven't got coords installed.\nThere are lots of level 62-63 Snowblind harpy and snowblind ambusher inside and outside the cave.  Good Luck!\n\nSnowblind Harpy (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=11678)\nSnowblind Ambusher (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=11678)",
            date = "2008-01-03T21:42:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7162#comments:id=212476",
        },
    },
