            score = 16,
            author = "Polegara",
            text = "The moonwell is now at (40,29).\n\nAs you approach it, the Shade of the Kaldorei (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=34584) will spawn to continue his story.\n\nShade of the Kaldorei approaches the moonwell slowly, a familiar, thoughtful look upon its face.\nShade of the Kaldorei says: Over time, Staghelm only grew more disconnected from our people.\nShade of the Kaldorei says: Some pose that he blames us, his people, for the loss of his son, long ago during the War of the Shifting Sands.\nShade of the Kaldorei says: Others cite rumors of his escalating conflicts with Tyrande Whisperwind, the shining light of our people, our leader in Darnassus.\nShade of the Kaldorei says: But many druids of the Cenarion Circle stand firm that he wants only what is best for all of the Kaldorei, and serve him unerringly towards that end.\nShade of the Kaldorei says: Fandral Staghelm carries the burden of our sins and our follies, and in so doing deserves the respect of us all.\nThe Shade of the Kaldorei closes its eyes and fades away.\n\nThere are five of these lore quests in total.\n\nTeldrassil: Crown of Azeroth (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28729)\nTeldrassil: Passing Awareness (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28731)\nTeldrassil: The Refusal of the Aspects (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=929)\n[Teldrassil: The Burden of the Kaldorei\nTeldrassil: The Coming Dawn (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=933)",
            date = "2010-12-02T23:31:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7383#comments:id=1203164",
        },
        {
            id = 1403407,
            score = 13,
            author = "sadalsuud",
            text = "Found the moonwell fine but can't find the quest giver. There's the yellow question mark at the crossroads where he should be but he isn't there. I even went back to Dolanaar.\n\nEdit: Made like I was going into Darnassus but didn't go all the way in, ran back, and there he was. It's not like he wanders the paths so I'm not sure why he wasn't there. Stopped and smelled the peaceblooms must be.",
            date = "2011-04-28T22:49:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7383#comments:id=1403407",
        },
    },
    [7385] = {
        {
            id = 14203,
            score = 24,
            author = "8825",
            text = "This is how it works. In the Frostwolf village is a small cave just to the left of the blacksmith. The primalist there accepts turnins of Stormpike Soldier's Blood, and once she gets enough she will begin walking towards the middle of the map. She's a level 60+ elite and has an entourage, so she CAN handle herself, but it's important to stay with her and keep her healed, because the Alliance wants her dead. Anyway, once she gets to the middle of the map, she will begin a summoning ritual. Once she and her assistants complete the ritual, a swirly pattern will appear at her feet. Now this is the important part: Ten Horde players must be there when this happens to right-click the swirly thing on the ground and stand still while the ritual completes. Think of it liked a warlock summon, where people have to right click the portal. This works the same way.\n\nIf the primalist makes it to her spot and summons, and if ten Horde players assist her in summoning, she will summon Lok, who basically looks like a pale blue earth elemental. He will go to the center of the map and chill (pun intended) for ten minutes. During that time, he will attack any Alliance that get too close. He's VERY strong, but be careful that you don't let the Alliance kite him away. Each time he defeats an Alliance player, he will grow in size and power. After the allotted ten minutes, he will begin going on a rampage and destroying everything in his path. The Alliance will attempt to kite him, so it's very important that warriors, druids, mages.. anyone with an intercept stays with him. Lok is VERY powerful but he's rather stupid. As soon as one person has aggro from him, he will stay on that person until they're dead no matter where they take him. So, it's important to keep the Alliance from defeating him or letting him get pulled to some random corner of the map.",
            date = "2006-12-12T13:42:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7385#comments:id=14203",
        },
        {
            id = 2851,
            score = 9,
            author = "Dread",
            text = "In the Frostwolf Keep (Horde HQ in AV), there is a cave with a number of shamans inside.  The head shaman has a repeatable quest in which you turn in Blood gained from killing NPCs and Alliance players.\n\nOnce a certain amount of blood has been turned in, the shamans travel to a ledge overlooking the Field of Strife (middle ground in AV) and begin to summon Lok'ohlar the Ice Lord, a huge, hulking boss.  A significant number of players need to help with the summoning, however.\n\nIt is better to wait for a certain time and then everyone with blood travel back and turn it all in at once.",
            date = "2006-11-04T20:00:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7385#comments:id=2851",
        },
        {
            id = 215845,
            score = 8,
            author = "24391",
            text = "In addition to the Frostwolf and Orgrimmar rep, you get +19 rep to each of the other horde cities.(+2 if you only turn in 1 Blood)\nDoes not show in the combat log.",
            date = "2008-01-09T20:16:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7385#comments:id=215845",
        },
        {
            id = 774724,
            score = 8,
            author = "Kalkran",
            text = "This is actually giving me 75 rep with Orgrimmar (and 18.75 rep with the other horde capitals) when handing in now.\nNot having to click through the quest givers gossip options is great as well.. They should add that for other rep turn-ins too.",
            date = "2009-07-11T11:09:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7385#comments:id=774724",
        },
        {
            id = 11974,
            score = 6,
            author = "7343",
            text = "In patch 2.0.1 you  get rep with Silvermoon city for handing in the blood. You can't see it in your combat log, but you actually get a bit.",
            date = "2006-12-09T03:07:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7385#comments:id=11974",
        },
    },
    [7386] = {
        {
            id = 18998,
            score = 5,
            author = "swotam",
            text = "There is a limit to how many of these can be turned in before the druids stop accepting more of them. If you are planning to loot these items, be sure to turn them in regularly or risk missing your chance. Once the maximum number has been reached, the druids will head off to summon Ivus, and that's the last you will see of them.",
            date = "2007-01-01T18:04:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7386#comments:id=18998",
        },
        {
            id = 137567,
            score = 5,
            author = "77681",
            text = "They summon a lvl ?? boss giant to help the alliance.",
            date = "2007-08-14T02:57:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7386#comments:id=137567",
        },
        {
            id = 408519,
            score = 4,
            author = "230660",
            text = "I used to get +19 alliance, now I only get +19 exodar.  Why?",
            date = "2008-10-16T17:30:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7386#comments:id=408519",
        },
        {
            id = 1702641,
            score = 3,
            author = "Ravenei",
            text = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7386 is one of the repeatable quests used to turn in https://www.wowhead.com/item=17423s in order to summon https://www.wowhead.com/npc=13419; this quest is used to turn the https://www.wowhead.com/item=17423 in (5) at a time.\n[hr]\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=17423s are obtained through the looting of the insignia's of enemy players or units killed in [zone=2597] and will be removed from your inventory when the battleground ends.\n\nThey are used to summon https://www.wowhead.com/npc=13419\nThey can be turned into https://www.wowhead.com/npc=13442 in stacks of (1) via the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6881 or in stacks of (5) via the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7386.\n\nFor quick turn ins I use and suggest the following macro.\n/script SelectGossipAvailableQuest(2)\n/script CompleteQuest()\n/script GetQuestReward()\nYou simply need to place this macro into a keybound slot, right click https://www.wowhead.com/npc=13442, press the keybind a couple times (rinse and repeat). You need only to change the \"(2)\" to a \"(1)\" if you would like to turn in the https://www.wowhead.com/item=17423s in stacks of (1) as the above macro is meant to select the second quest (i.e. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7386).\n\n200 https://www.wowhead.com/item=17423s are required to summon https://www.wowhead.com/npc=13419.\n\nAfter 200 https://www.wowhead.com/item=17423s have been turned into https://www.wowhead.com/npc=13442 (in a single match) then the Druids will begin to head south towards a destroyed ballista located in the Fields of Strife next to the Stonehearth Bunker.\n\nOnce they have reached the Fields of Strife they will dismount and summon a Circle of Calling.\n\nTen Players must click the Circle of Calling.\nThe Circle of Calling will bug out quite often.\n\nPrimarily: If the Druids are attacked at any point after they've placed the Circle of Calling then instead of continuing to channel after killing the target, they will stand around aimlessly and https://www.wowhead.com/npc=13419 will not be able to be summoned.\n\nIt's also suggested that players only click the Circle of Calling \"once\" and make sure not to accidentally begin channeling and end channeling by clicking multiple times (If your player does nothing after clicking the stone, wait a tad, if your not purple and channelling then move closer and try again, you were likely too far away).\n\nAll in all, the process (especially the end) for summoning https://www.wowhead.com/npc=13419 can be very buggy; Blizzard has indeed known of this issue for quite some time (years); one can only hope at this point for a fix.\n\nBest of Luck to all of You!",
            date = "2012-08-21T13:13:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7386#comments:id=1702641",
        },
        {
            id = 1688891,
            score = 1,
            author = "1014931",
            text = "The reputation gained as of now is +21 alliance (if you're already exalted with stormpike and ironforge). The amount of crystals needed to summon Ivus the Alliance boss is 200. When the 200 are handed in the arch druids will run to the field of strife on their mounts and kill any horde along the way. Once they reach the middle of the map (field of strife) you will then be able to summon Ivus which takes 10 people to click on the summoning platform. Ivus will be summoned within 10 seconds of 10 people channeling the summon. He will spawn in the middle of Field of Strife and he will kill anything in his way. He will stay within the field of strife for 5 minutes. Once the 5 minutes have ended he will start proceeding to drek. Obviously now that the game has reinforcements and its not like before...getting this all done is extremely difficult, easier to accomplish in lower level AV's since people like to turtle. Enjoy.",
            date = "2012-07-16T18:33:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7386#comments:id=1688891",
        },
    },
