        },
    },
    [7838] = {
        {
            id = 304901,
            score = 56,
            author = "Vayus",
            text = "This was how I accomplished this quest for my level 19 gnome twink, without any help from friends or multiple accounts:\n\n1. First, I moved my 70 main and twink out to the arena in STV.\n\n2. Secondly, I logged out my main on the edge of the arena so that he was not in neutral mode and could not be attacked by members of the same faction. I logged out my twink in the center of the arena.\n\n3. I set an alarm for every 3rd hour when the arena starts.\n\n4. Approximately five minutes before the arena started, I logged in my main and sweeped the edges of the arena with perception to catch any horde in the area before the arena even started.\n\n5. When the chest was dropped, I ran into the arena and immediately began opening the chest. If there were any stealthers or other 70s nearby, they would challenge me and I would kill them (most of the time, anyway). After clearing all visible opposition, I opened the chest and took all items but the trinket itself.\n\n6. I jumped on top of the chest and force quit WoW (Alt+f4). This had the advantage of leaving my 70 in the arena for approximately 45 seconds (your main will actually be in-game during step 7), deterring any ninjas or late arrivals from taking the chest. Simply logging out will leave ninjas with an easy grab.\n\n7. I restarted wow and logged onto my twink. Having the advantage of being a tiny gnome female, I was able to actually log inside the chest, being invisible from the outside. If you are a different race, this may be more difficult, but hopefully your 70 main will be enough of a deterrent to allow you enough time to grab the trinket.\n\n8. I logged out my twink, moved my main up to the edge again and waited another 3 hours to do it all over again.\n\nUsing this method, I was successful 12 of 14 tries, which is an incredible success ratio considering the amount of competition from both 70s and lowbies. Happy hunting!",
            date = "2008-06-14T14:27:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7838#comments:id=304901",
        },
        {
            id = 220893,
            score = 5,
            author = "alanoid",
            text = "Just wondering do you turn in one arena master to get this quest or just turn in 12 arena masters to get the trinket?",
            date = "2008-01-19T23:35:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7838#comments:id=220893",
        },
        {
            id = 1849482,
            score = 5,
            author = "RealTalk",
            text = "Is this still active? I have tried for the 3rd time and still the chest does not appear. I get there a few minutes early, and wait for about 10 minutes after the hour, and always on either 3 or 6 am. I am standing in the arena itself, is this where you are supposed to be? I'm a level 24 if that makes any difference.",
            date = "2013-05-03T03:09:53-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7838#comments:id=1849482",
        },
        {
            id = 250750,
            score = 4,
            author = "132322",
            text = "I can collect 24 green ones and make 2 blue ones.\nIf i am level 1 i will get 50% dodge :)",
            date = "2008-03-09T15:47:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7838#comments:id=250750",
        },
        {
            id = 3309739,
            score = 4,
            author = "deepspace8",
            text = "This quest is unique because you have to loot and turn in 12 of the same exact trinket, which are all also quest-starters, the quest of which you do just once.\n\nAs a level 60 Shadowlands mage, I only ran into problems when there was competition in the arena of players my own level, which happened maybe once or twice.  I mostly got these when most people were sleeping, so there weren't as many people online.  That's what I'd recommend if you're a squishy class.",
            date = "2021-03-19T02:06:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7838#comments:id=3309739",
        },
    },
    [7848] = {
        {
            id = 1293335,
            score = 265,
            author = "33682",
            text = "Directions on getting there (without swimming through the Lava, I always got lost doing that).\n\nEnter BRD. Go left through the wrought-iron door which is now permanently unlocked. Open another wrought-iron door to your right. Then open another steel door in the wall, just ahead. This should take you into the Garrison.\n\nOperate a big mechanism in the garrison room that you're in. Then go up the flight of stairs, hang a left, and follow that passage until you come to the Manufactory. There is only one way out of the manufactory, and it leads to the Grim Guzzler.\n\nIn the Grim Guzzler, buy Dark Iron Ale from Plugger and turn all of it in to Private Rocknot. Then go stand by Phalanx, a small event happens and Phalanx opens the door. Exit the door that he just opened and go left, and left again. Pass ambassador flamelash in the Chamber of Enchantment to the left. This should take you into the Mold Foundry, a big place with forges and golems.\n\nThere's only one way out of here, and it leads to the Chamber of the Seven. Talk to the ghost, defeat 7 ghosts, and exit the chamber through the door that just opened. The next passage will have a right turn almost immediately; it's easy to miss, but leads to a molten bridge with sets of 3 fire elementals. (If you reach the lyceaum you went the wrong way. ) Past the fire elementals you'll see a large green raid instance portal, and the Core Fragment should be in a glowing rock just next to it. If you're in a raid group, you won't be able to see or pick up the fragment.\n\nI hope that helps. Though it would have been more pertinent 5 years ago, maybe now that I've typed it and passed it on, I can get the useless information out of my brain!",
            date = "2011-01-14T10:23:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7848#comments:id=1293335",
        },
        {
            id = 1497183,
            score = 54,
            author = "Hairband",
            text = "Takes 3 minutes using my shortcut to get attuned, no running for the bar, getting lost or directions:\n\nHOW DO I GET INTO BRD?:  Get the quest from Lothos Riftweaver and enter the instance.  BRD is a little hard to find but if you really don't know where it is, it's the doorway next to Lothos's tiny room.  Enter that doorway and go right and you should see some stairs into a zone with Dark Iron Dwarves working called \"The Grinding Quarry.\"  I usually look for a large nut/bolt looking rock on the right, and turn right between the large nut/bolt rock and a flat table looking rock down a hallway.  This will be \"The Masonary.\"  At the end of that hallway I go right into the instance.\n\nNOW I'M IN BRD, HOW DO I GET TO THE CORE FRAGMENT QUICKLY BY SWIMMING?:\n\nEDITED FOR 4.0: The mole machine has been added.  Click \"just past the Grim Guzzler.\"  You will be transported to a half circular balcony above a bridge with some rooms up ramps behind you.  On the bridge, you see Lord Incendius.  Jump down onto the bridge, kill him, and then jump into the lava WEST of him.  Swim NORTH to the first island (there will be fire elementals on that island).  Swim to the second island (same thing, fire elementals on it).  Keep swimming North, and swim under the bridge which is like a metal grate with fire elementals roaming around.\n\nIS THERE AN ALTERNATE WAY TO REACH LORD INCENDIUS? If you a different route, use the \"Dark Iron Highway\" (which is accessed via the gate on the left, straight ahead, and when you see some Dark Iron pats and a fire elemental, you will go to the right.  You don't need to pull any of the little mobs if you are careful.  So if you look up at the end of this large hallway, you will notice the rock walls pictured are the same as the loading screen.  Past the gap in the rock walls you enter \"Shadowforge City.\"  You will see a bridge and fire elemental guards.  Keep walking down that bridge until you see the boss Lord Incendius (who is standing by something called The Black Anvil).  Then, kill him, jump to the left side (West, if that is easier for you) where you came in, swim to the edge of the lava pool and you'll see an island you can stand on (no need to pull aggro), then swim to the next island which is very close.  Looking north, you should see the bridge, fire elementals and a ramp under the bridge.\n\nI SEE THE MOLTEN BRIDGE, WHERE DO I GO? When you see the bridge, you will see one or more rock ramps.  This zone is called \"The Molten Bridge\".  The quickest way up is right under the bridge but don't panic if you went around.  The Dark Forge, where you smelt Dark Iron, is located on the bridge metal framework and you'll see a fire elemental by it.  Anyway, you are going to go up and around until you turn left and you see 3 fire elementals.  Kill them.  Past them there are 3 more fire elementals but you can just zerg the core fragment with a quick cog click (no cast to interrupt) and jump through the Molten Core whirly entrance.  You should be notified you are in Molten Core at this point (may need a raid to jump thru the portal).  If you simply exit the way you entered, you'll be right at Lothos.  TURN IN or you may forget you have it.\n\nHAIRBAND, YOU TALK TOO FAST, COULD YOU BREAK IT DOWN A LITTLE?\n\nOLD ROUTE:\n\n1. Enter the instance.  You will see some NPC's.  Ignore them and go left to a gate.  Open it.\n\n2.  Past that will be a large open hallway leading to another hallway.  The zone here is \"Dentention Block\" but if you go straight, where you will see Dwarves on patrol,dogs patting, and on the right a brazier.  This is called \"The Dark Iron Highway.\" Go right.  I usually jump around the brazier and just frogger my way past any mobs patrolling.\n\n3. Looking up, you will see the ugly faces of the rock walls in the loading screen for BRD.  The doors are open.  Just walk on through and past the fire elementals standing on a bridge until you get to Lord Incendius.  It is kind of a long bridge.  Now you can kill him or just jump to the left.\n\n4.  After jumping, aim kind of to the edge and you will see the island on the left where there are some fire elementals is where you will swim to.  Past that is another similar island.  From that 2nd island you will see \"The Molten Bridge\" made out of stone, and below it, you will see a ramp.\n\n5. Just swim to that ramp and walk under the bridge.  Straight ahead is the Dark Forge if you need to smelt any Dark Iron and have the skill from Gloom'rel.  Do a hairpin left to 3 elementals which you may kill, and at the end, kill 3 more.  Or you can just zerg the core fragment which is left and is clickable, no time cast.\n\n6.  ONLY when you have the core fragment in hand, walk through the giant (and obvious) whirly gate and enter Molten Core.  Now leave the whirly gate the same way you came in and you will be at Lothros Riftwalker to turn in your quest.  Don't forget.\n\n4.0 ROUTE:\n\n1.  Enter the instance.\n\n2.  Use the Mole Machine and hit \"Just Past the Grim Guzzler.\"\n\n3. Jump onto a balcony where Lord Incendius and The Dark Anvil is located.  Kill or skip him, and jump WEST into the lava.\n\n4. - 6.  SEE ABOVE.",
            date = "2011-08-17T16:09:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7848#comments:id=1497183",
        },
        {
            id = 1808770,
            score = 31,
            author = "123744",
            text = "Swimming to MC revised.\n\n1. Take the mole machine Past the Grim Guzzler,\n2. Walk down the stairs to your right around (or through) Ambassador Flamelash (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=9156).  You can now see the Bridge to MC straight ahead from the back of the platform.\n3.  Swim just past the bridge and hop up on the rock by the fallen metal walkway.\n4. Cross the bridge to your left.\n5. Click the shiny rock on the left of the raid entrance.\n\n(p.s.  This is the swimming only method.  If you want to know how to get out again see Necarie's post.  Otherwise continuing down that hallway past Flamelash you can just kill the 7 dwarfs and be able to walk back out to take the portal back up to the entrance to turn in the quest.)",
            date = "2013-02-03T20:16:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7848#comments:id=1808770",
        },
        {
            id = 1503745,
            score = 22,
            author = "zylya",
            text = "To make it as simple as possible:\n\n1. Enter BRD\n2. On your right, take the mole machine to \"just past the grim guzzler\"\n3. Jump down to the Black Anvil\n4. Swim N/NW\n\nThe dungeon maps make finding the direction to swim completely trivial.",
            date = "2011-08-26T08:07:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7848#comments:id=1503745",
        },
        {
            id = 1695919,
            score = 19,
            author = "958208",
            text = "ok, easiest way to the core fragment/molten core; soon as you enter BRD take the mole machine on your left to \"just past the grim guzzler\", then jump over the side onto lord incendius' platform then jump off just to your right, keep swimming until you see a bridge with a few fireguard destroyers on it on the left hand side of the bridge there is a little ramp going up out of the lava , up the ramp and onto the bridge the core fragment/raid entrance is at the other side of the bridge. Also the black forge is on a little bridge leading off of the main one.\n\nNote you will need a reasonable amount of health to get through the lava\n\nhope this helps\n\nEdit: spelling mistakes :)",
            date = "2012-08-04T08:03:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7848#comments:id=1695919",
        },
    },
