            author = "Evenuel",
            text = "This quest has been updated to the 4.3 Darkmoon changes...\nDoes this mean that if somebody did this quest's old version, he/she cannot get it now? (at least I can't see it :(  )",
            date = "2011-12-03T18:16:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7905#comments:id=1588330",
        },
        {
            id = 2519590,
            score = 7,
            author = "piraka810",
            text = "Here's a list of all sources of [currency=515] currently in-game.\n\n8 [currency=515] per day per character from the following daily quests.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=29463\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=29436\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=29438\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=29434\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=36481\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=29455\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=37910\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=37911\nThe https://www.wowhead.com/item=93724 rewarded from these quests can be mailed between characters, allowing you to farm 8 tickets per-character per-day.\n\n15 [currency=515] per day from the two account wide pet battle quests.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=32175: Rewards 5 tickets.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=36471: Rewards 10 tickets.\n\n5 [currency=515] every 3 hours in the PvP chest.\nAt 12:00, 3:00, 6:00, and 9:00 server time, the https://www.wowhead.com/object=209620 spawns in the Darkmoon Death match, containing 5 tickets. Only 1 player can loot the tickets each time.\n\n80 [currency=515] per month from monthly quest items.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=71953: 5 [currency=515]\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=71951: 5 [currency=515]\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=71952: 5 [currency=515]\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=71635: 10 [currency=515]\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=71636: 10 [currency=515]\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=71637: 10 [currency=515]\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=71638: 10 [currency=515]\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=71716: 10 [currency=515]\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=71715: 15 [currency=515]\nThese can be found in battlegrounds and dungeons with the https://www.wowhead.com/item=71634, or bought on the Auction House.\n\n20 [currency=515] per month from Monthly profession quests.\nPrimary profession quests.\n\nAlchemy: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29506 4 [currency=515]\nBlacksmithing: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29508 4 [currency=515]\nEnchanting: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29510 4 [currency=515]\nEngineering: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=2951 4 [currency=515]\nInscription: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29515 4 [currency=515]\nJewelcrafting: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29516 4 [currency=515]\nLeatherworking: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29517 4 [currency=515]\nTailoring: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29520 4 [currency=515]\n\nSecondary profession quests.\n\nArchaeology: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29507 3 [currency=515]\nCooking: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29509 3 [currency=515]\nFishing: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29513 3 [currency=515]\nFirst Aid: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29512 3 [currency=515]\n\nSince you can only do 2 primary and 4 secondary profession quests, this yields a total of 20 [currency=515] per month.\n\n20 [currency=515] per month from monthly quests\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=33354 started from https://www.wowhead.com/item=105891 for killing https://www.wowhead.com/npc=71992 the first time each month.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=29433 completed by killing 250 creatures that yield experience or honor.\n\n100 [currency=515] from a one-time treasure hunt.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=38934 started by buying https://www.wowhead.com/item=126930 for 100 https://www.wowhead.com/item=124669\n\nAll told, you can make 281 [currency=515] per month from doing the daily and monthly quests, plus an additional 8 per character per day from alts. Also, 5 [currency=515] every 3 hours if you win the deathmatch, and finally 100 [currency=515] from the 1 time fishing quest.",
            date = "2017-09-05T00:44:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7905#comments:id=2519590",
        },
    },
    [7926] = {
        {
            id = 1588640,
            score = 37,
            author = "Blackspirit",
            text = "It looks like this quest was not reset for patch 4.3, so if you did it already you'll be out 5 tickets. This also means you must manually get the Guide from either the faction-locked mob in the area outside the portal or Selina Dourman at the entrance of the Faire across from the token vendor.",
            date = "2011-12-04T01:09:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7926#comments:id=1588640",
        },
        {
            id = 80785,
            score = 20,
            author = "48429",
            text = "When it is in Mulgore - coords are 35.34, just near Thunder Bluff.",
            date = "2007-05-10T07:48:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7926#comments:id=80785",
        },
        {
            id = 550486,
            score = 11,
            author = "160394",
            text = "This quest counts towards 3000 Quests Completed (http://www.wowhead.com/?achievement=978).",
            date = "2009-01-06T20:57:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7926#comments:id=550486",
        },
        {
            id = 324171,
            score = 10,
            author = "40483",
            text = "We often have horde visit the faire in Goldshire on Lightbringer. They are usually peaceful and enjoy the faire more on Alliance side since it seems none of the horde want to visit the faire. Occasionally, someone visits to stir up trouble and are quickly put down but most players on both sides frown upon pvp'ing in what's supposed to be a carnival atmosphere. As an Alliance player I quite often come to Thunderbluff because the horde hardly play.\n\nThe main thing to avoid is trying the human cannonball. It's very risky to get to the cannon in the first place and the landing zone is much narrower than the alliance lake. If you miss the target in Stonebull Lake you either lose major health or just flat out die. It's very shallow as well. Landings almost have to be perfect. Also, there's the long trek back from there to Thunder Bluff.\n\nIn short, only do the TB cannonball as an alliance IF you can survive a trip up the lift, to the cannon, a landing in a shallow pond and don't mind travelling so far back to go again.\n\nI have heard, however, that the Horde can't visit the faire when it is in Elwynn Forest; it seems that it is too close to Goldshire and they get attacked by the guards -- can anybody confirm this?\n\nIt's pretty much false. The problems with guards may arise from chasing the little boy for the frog because he does run a pattern down the middle of the street where the npcs will attack. Leave the frogs for Thunder Bluff and it should be safe enough. O, one more npc that might attack, there is a guard kneeling behind a tree that the horde may not know about. You'll pass him on the trip back from the human cannonball. It's easy to avoid him and it's not necessary to engage in battle with him. Just run in circles till he gets tired of chasing you. He's part of an alliance quest so he's permanently fixed there. Not much to do but beware of his location.\n\nBasically stay on the faire side of the fence and away from the wagons on the side of the road. Horde should have no problems enjoying the faire in Goldshire... unless they come for battle. >:-(",
            date = "2008-07-11T00:57:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7926#comments:id=324171",
        },
        {
            id = 1588439,
            score = 7,
            author = "363043",
            text = "I couldn't find this NPC, but there I got the quest from a Darkmoon Faire Mystic Mage, a bloodelf NPC on the upper section in the middle of Orgrimmar near the flight master.\nShe gave me the quest, and could also teleport me  to the area.",
            date = "2011-12-03T20:11:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=7926#comments:id=1588439",
        },
    },
    [8260] = {
