            date = "2010-11-28T09:52:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8784#comments:id=1192967",
        },
        {
            id = 1105746,
            score = 72,
            author = "553717",
            text = "The quest says to talk to dragons, but they looked and sounded like gnomes to me.  Inside the instance, up the stairs on the left, behind the first boss, The Prophet Skeram.  Go down the first flight and bear left back into a room, where you will find 3 NPC's, talk to the little gal on the left, she'll tell you you're tall...",
            date = "2010-08-22T14:21:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8784#comments:id=1105746",
        },
        {
            id = 15707,
            score = 58,
            author = "9600",
            text = "You should save them until 2999/3000 neutral, as you only get rep for killing C'thun and Emps from that point and then turn all in.",
            date = "2006-12-15T00:30:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8784#comments:id=15707",
        },
        {
            id = 15587,
            score = 35,
            author = "IW00Bruiser",
            text = "This quest is from a low random drop, Ancient Qiraji Artifact, off the mobs inside of AQ40.  Turning this in to the Brood of Nozdormu at the start of the instance rewards you with 1000 rep as stated above, which makes the effort to getting to exalted much easier.\n\nIt is a very low chance to drop, but has a chance on practically every mob in the instance aside from bosses.  You can have none drop, or as many as 3 drop, which happened to my guild one time, made everyone very happy.",
            date = "2006-12-14T16:45:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8784#comments:id=15587",
        },
        {
            id = 596704,
            score = 26,
            author = "Maddoks",
            text = "The NPC is in AQ40. You have to kill the first boss to get to her. You cannot stealth past as she is behind a locked door that cannot be targeted. Of course, at lvl 80, it wouldn't take much to run past the trash and kill the boss.",
            date = "2009-02-05T14:11:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8784#comments:id=596704",
        },
    },
    [8789] = {
        {
            id = 2373090,
            score = 83,
            author = "Zaronji",
            text = "If you're filling out your wardrobe, I would strongly recommend doing this quest on a warrior if you can as you'll be able to unlock all four items at once and won't need to do the quest again on another character.",
            date = "2016-08-24T22:33:12-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8789#comments:id=2373090",
        },
        {
            id = 4773,
            score = 53,
            author = "Zanarkand",
            text = "Note that the War Axe and the Pugio aren't \"unique\", and the quest is also repeatable, so you can dual-wield either if you're lucky enough with the Armamaments.",
            date = "2006-11-27T07:17:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8789#comments:id=4773",
        },
        {
            id = 1626465,
            score = 26,
            author = "faeofwind",
            text = "For those wondering where to pick this quest up, Arygos is located just outside of C'Thun's lair. This means you must be able to defeat the Twin Emperors: Vek'lor & Vek'nilash to gain access to him.",
            date = "2012-02-14T17:16:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8789#comments:id=1626465",
        },
        {
            id = 625483,
            score = 20,
            author = "27865",
            text = "For those looking to boost their Brood rep, this turn-in is worth 500 rep (550 Human); full rep is awarded at Lv80.",
            date = "2009-02-27T16:53:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8789#comments:id=625483",
        },
        {
            id = 1004270,
            score = 19,
            author = "297533",
            text = "It doesn't count towards total amount of completed quests (so no Loremaster credit either).",
            date = "2010-03-24T13:14:59-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8789#comments:id=1004270",
        },
    },
    [8790] = {
        {
            id = 3685,
            score = 46,
            author = "6100",
            text = "This quest is given to you by one of the three NPCs in the last chamber before C'Thun in the Ahn'Qiraj Temple.\n\nThe quest is repeatable.",
            date = "2006-11-15T06:32:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8790#comments:id=3685",
        },
        {
            id = 2522238,
            score = 36,
            author = "Dwebbris",
            text = "Something to take note of when doing this now that there's a wardrobe and all:\nYou don't need to repeat the quest to get all the transmogs if you think smart. Use a class that can use all weapons types you get from it, and they will all be saved in your wardrobe upon completion, whether it says you can only choose one of the rewards or all 3.\n\nFor example, completing the quest with a Warrior would get you both the staffs and the hammer transmog, but completing it on a mage, which can't use maces, you'd only get the staffs.\n\nThis should save you some time farming Elementium Ingots and, in some cases, even the time to get the Regalia to drop on several characters.",
            date = "2017-09-11T09:39:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8790#comments:id=2522238",
        },
        {
            id = 1761277,
            score = 14,
            author = "Queendom",
            text = "This quest rewards caster weapons and tank mace, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8789 rewards melee weapons and shield and requires https://www.wowhead.com/item=21232.\n\nBoth staves have unique models, while the mace does not.",
            date = "2012-11-12T06:29:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8790#comments:id=1761277",
        },
        {
            id = 1004272,
            score = 13,
            author = "297533",
            text = "It doesn't count towards total amount of completed quests (so no Loremaster credit either).",
            date = "2010-03-24T13:15:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8790#comments:id=1004272",
        },
        {
            id = 2470813,
            score = 13,
            author = "Xexji",
            text = "Seems rather obvious, but you can draw the required Elementium Ingots from your bank as you can with all crafting reagents.\n\nSo if you're like me and have ~20 sitting gathering dust in your bank, you don't have to go back and get them to complete the quest.",
            date = "2017-02-08T14:25:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8790#comments:id=2470813",
        },
    },
    [8791] = {
        {
            id = 2544893,
            score = 45,
            author = "deathlavitz",
            text = "If you have done this since killing Argus the Unmaker, you will need to find Zidormi at cords 78,22 to go back to show the zone before the wound.",
            date = "2018-01-10T01:29:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8791#comments:id=2544893",
        },
        {
            id = 2546732,
            score = 24,
            author = "Harkzul",
            text = "Since 7.3.5, Cenarion Hold got destroyed, but you still can complete this quest if you talk to Zidormi (78,21) and she will transport you to \"old\" silithus. There you wil be able to turn in the quest :)",
            date = "2018-01-18T11:43:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8791#comments:id=2546732",
        },
        {
            id = 362233,
            score = 22,
            author = "Jagger1",
            text = "On completing this quest, I got 1000 rep for Cenarion Circle, and 500 rep for Brood of Nozdormu (as well as 11,450xp at 66), Mar'alith also does a nice emote:\n\nCommander Mar'alith yells: Soldiers of Kalimdor! Heroes of Silithus! One among you has dealt a vicious blow to our mortal enemies! Aiathonalt and his allies have relieved the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj of its merciless leader! Ossirian the Unscarred, scourge of Silithus, has finally been destroyed and his armies wholly dismantled!\n\nI'm told by people who did this Pre-BC, that 60's and under will get a zone-wide-buff from this...",
            date = "2008-08-26T04:30:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8791#comments:id=362233",
        },
        {
            id = 438318,
            score = 22,
            author = "haoma",
            text = "This quest does count toward the Loremaster of Kalimdor Achievement",
            date = "2008-11-11T06:42:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8791#comments:id=438318",
        },
        {
            id = 1595753,
            score = 0,
            author = "Tylersmith112",
            text = "Kinda cool to randomly hear back then.",
            date = "2011-12-13T22:02:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8791#comments:id=1595753",
        },
    },
    [8801] = {
        {
            id = 752642,
            score = 100,
            author = "IbFeeshin",
            text = "They realize it's just going to respawn next week so they just give you a pat on the back and tell you good job.",
            date = "2009-06-20T19:14:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8801#comments:id=752642",
        },
        {
            id = 1870367,
            score = 61,
            author = "ktoth04",
            text = "First off, on your map this turnin looks like it is outside the gate of AQ40 in silithus. This is wrong.\n\nThis turn in is next to C'thun's room in AQ40.\n\nTo get to C'thun, you have to navigate to Twin Emps (the triangle shaped room) and kill them. Then a door opens inside of that room. This door leads down another long hallway. At the end of this hallway is C'thun's room. Good luck.",
            date = "2013-06-25T02:03:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8801#comments:id=1870367",
        },
        {
            id = 597223,
            score = 41,
            author = "INvShika",
            text = "It is recommended to turn this quest in AFTER you hit 2999/3000 neutral (at which point all mobs in AQ40 cease giving rep) along with your https://www.wowhead.com/item=21229 and https://www.wowhead.com/item=21230\n\nEdit: And the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8791 (begun by https://www.wowhead.com/item=21220) should be saved till max neutral, as it gives 500 brood rep.",
            date = "2009-02-05T22:38:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8801#comments:id=597223",
        },
        {
            id = 922597,
            score = 32,
            author = "Dusktide",
            text = "Counts towards Loremaster of Kalimdor",
            date = "2009-12-19T01:57:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8801#comments:id=922597",
        },
        {
            id = 1854168,
            score = 15,
            author = "555435",
            text = "Unfortunately Caelestrasz is in a room next to C'Thun's chamber at the very END of the raid.  If you space and hearth out before turning the quest in, you will have to run all the way through the place again to get to the end to turn it in.  (If you do forget and have to go back through, still best to do it while it's cleared.  Much better than forgetting until the next week and having to clear the whole place again just to turn a quest in.)",
            date = "2013-05-18T20:44:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=8801#comments:id=1854168",
        },
    },
