    [9151] = {
        {
            id = 2881065,
            score = 24,
            author = "jerodast",
            text = "Weirdly I got a low-pitched \"failure sound\" after turning in this quest with a warning \"You don't meet the prerequisites for that quest\". Presumably it tried to give me a followup quest but couldn't. But, I could still pick up the next one in the chain - although it's given by a different NPC standing nearby. Perhaps an alternate version of the follow-up that didn't quite have the kinks worked out :)\n\nI wasn't playing on a Blood Elf, maybe that made a difference.",
            date = "2019-04-10T00:22:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9151#comments:id=2881065",
        },
        {
            id = 3232089,
            score = 19,
            author = "GibbleFenwick",
            text = "Currently when you hand in this quest, you'll immediately get an error indicating you don't meet requirements for a quest.\nYou don't get any indication which quest failed.\n\nAfter some investigation I've pieced together what is happening:\n\n The scripting for this quest attempts to automatically offer a follow-up quest.\n However, the prerequisites for that quest apparently changed in 7.3.5 (see comments on https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9220).\n As the quest is offered, validation kicks in and aborts the offer. Leaving us naturally somewhat confused and possibly a little worried we may have missed something.\n\nIn order to gain access to the followup, you first need to complete a little \"diversion chain\". Pick up https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9282 at the ground floor of the Sanctum. This chain will send you on a run-around until you've done https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9176. Then you'll be able to pick up the two quests that https://www.wowhead.com/npc=16204 offers.\n\nTo be fair, the changes do provide better continuity for the story. They add context for the https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9220.\nOn the other hand, it's abundantly clear that these quests as a whole lack cohesion. The oversight on this questing zone must have been shockingly poor back in the day.\n(In my case I had already completed everything else at the Farstrider Enclave before this diversion chain came up, so the diversion felt more like an annoyance. And some of the quest text in the chain implies I shouldn't have been there yet. Instead of the chain providing links between areas as part of the exploration, it just had me revisiting places I'd already \"cleared\".)\n\nTo be honest, part of me is happy that some effort was put into maintaining the old content. And another part of me is bitterly disappointed at the complete lack of diligence. The fact that scripting auto-offers an unavailable quest should have been easy to avoid, and even easier to fix if it had been tested appropriately. The lack of care simply creates unnecessary confusion.",
            date = "2020-09-22T10:26:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9151#comments:id=3232089",
        },
        {
            id = 2552390,
            score = 18,
            author = "kirnsten",
            text = "As of 8.2.5 you can start this quest at honored with Tranquillien as Blood elf or revered as other race after completing prerequisite quests, which you can see in quest info.",
            date = "2018-02-13T03:30:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9151#comments:id=2552390",
        },
        {
            id = 1029969,
            score = 10,
            author = "Kyouko",
            text = "This is an optional lead in quest, and becomes unavailable if you are on, or complete \"War on Deatholme (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=9220)\".",
            date = "2010-05-01T02:55:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9151#comments:id=1029969",
        },
        {
            id = 41634,
