            text = "I experienced a low droprate on the CatLord Claws. The rest had a high droprate.\n\nLocation 68,51.",
            date = "2007-02-24T14:18:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9214#comments:id=41627",
        },
        {
            id = 1144717,
            score = 8,
            author = "kowboi83",
            text = "If you also happen to be doing [quest=9158 domain=www], the Catlords pets are  [npc=16348 domain=www] (the felines you need) :D",
            date = "2010-10-16T20:16:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9214#comments:id=1144717",
        },
        {
            id = 229710,
            score = 7,
            author = "120303",
            text = "50 Shadowcasters later, still on 2/3.  I'm not kidding :(",
            date = "2008-02-05T02:40:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9214#comments:id=229710",
        },
        {
            id = 258046,
            score = 7,
            author = "138902",
            text = "The Catlords and the Hexxer are found at Zeb'nowa. The Shadowcasters and the Headhunters are found at Zeb'Tela. The shadowcasters have probably the lowest drop rate in this quest, but everyone elses is allright.",
            date = "2008-03-23T12:48:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9214#comments:id=258046",
        },
    },
    [9215] = {
        {
            id = 21440,
            score = 26,
            author = "8358",
            text = "You can find him at 65, 79 at the top of the building. He's tough to solo but you can do it if you interrupt his casting by moving out of his LOS every time he starts to cast chain lightning or shrink.",
            date = "2007-01-18T17:27:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9215#comments:id=21440",
        },
        {
            id = 2552103,
            score = 14,
            author = "Sharwyn",
            text = "For some reason quest is not available anymore its either linked with reputation or something like that, i have also noticed that lots of quests in Ghostlands are now linked with reputation with Tranquilien and i couldn't get lots of them till i got Honored/Friendly with them\n\nEdit : it becomes avaiable after finishing Attack on Zeb'Tela",
            date = "2018-02-11T13:53:13-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9215#comments:id=2552103",
        },
        {
            id = 162548,
            score = 10,
            author = "20486",
            text = "Just solo'd as a 19 mage ... the 'run behind the pillar' technique works flawlessly. I did have to use one healthpot, and i bandaged once, but luckily, he pauses long enough before chasing after you that you have more than enough time to do stuff like that.\n\nhe actually pauses momentarily once he comes around the pillar and becomes Line of Sight again, too.",
            date = "2007-10-03T20:51:53-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9215#comments:id=162548",
        },
        {
            id = 140135,
            score = 9,
            author = "409",
            text = "His main attack is lightning bolt.  If you just run around the middle part of the structure you will be out of line of sight and his spell will fail, I took very little damage soloing him this way.",
            date = "2007-08-18T14:14:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9215#comments:id=140135",
        },
        {
            id = 261307,
            score = 7,
            author = "Baerce",
            text = "On my lvl 19 BE priest I did the following:\n\nPrepare thoroughly: Make sure you have all your buffs up (this includes touch of weakness and mana tap stacked up 3 times)\n\nThe fight:\n- Shield yourself (I use a macro that shields me if I don't target a friend)\n- Pull with Mind Blast\n- Apply Shadow Word: Pain\n- Now keep sw:p up all the times while you are running around the pillar. If you see him running towards you, turn around and run the other way. Heal (with Renew) and shield yourself if needed.\n- I used arcane torrent once when my mana become too low and kept on using mana tap if it was up.\n\nIf you do this and keep on running, he will die after a few minutes. Other classes with dots may be able to beat him the same way. If you have no dots or are a melee class, you probably need a friend on this quest.",
            date = "2008-03-27T16:35:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9215#comments:id=261307",
        },
    },
    [9216] = {
