    [9624] = {
        {
            id = 2500192,
            score = 27,
            author = "Mike21daisu",
            text = "This is a common quest that people wanna do to get that chest piece as a transmog, so I might as well explain everything from scratch.\n\nHow to get to this quest from Stormwind: Take the boat in [zone=1519], it is a pirate-looking boat (yellowish colour), which is the very bottom one if you open the Stormwind map. This boat will take you to [zone=141] (If you have the flight paths opened just simply talk to the flight master and take the flight to Blood Watch, Bloodmyst Isle, or if you don't have that flight path opened then take the flight path to Azure Watch, Azuremyst Isle). If you don't have any of the flight paths opened or just want to take the boat then continue reading. Now, there are 3 boats here, you are in the middle, the right boat is inactive. Take the left boat, it should take you to [zone=3524]. Now just make your way to [zone=3525], follow the road to the crossroads in the middle at the flight master (Azure Watch), then go to the North (up on the map), don't go into the cave, go around it and cross the bridge which will get you to the Bloodmyst Isle.\n\nYou need to be lvl 9 to take the quest, you can do it on any class (alliance). You don't need to do any other quests in order to take this one.\n\nLegs that goes really well with the plate chest piece that you get from this quest https://www.wowhead.com/item=26032.\nHands that goes really well with the plate chest piece that you get from this quest https://www.wowhead.com/item=120951.\nWrists that goes really well with the plate chest piece that you get from this quest https://www.wowhead.com/item=26040.",
            date = "2017-06-12T04:54:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9624#comments:id=2500192",
        },
        {
            id = 50304,
            score = 19,
            author = "25495",
            text = "The are small little fruit that grow in the ground next to the trees.",
            date = "2007-03-12T22:08:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9624#comments:id=50304",
        },
        {
            id = 2615675,
            score = 16,
            author = "pokii",
            text = "As a lvl 112 newly boosted toon (BFA) I wanted this chest for my Belf Warlock but she’s horde so decided to follow the guide in the comment section but it’s outdated. The journey is actually much simpler.\n\n1. Level any new Alliance character to 10. I couldn’t talk to the NPC at lvl 9.\n\n2. Make your way to Stormwind City.\n3. Travel to Stormwind Harbor where the boats are. Find the First boat on the left-most side if you are facing the ocean. Head to the dock but do not ride the boat.\n\n4. You will see a Portal to Darnassus at the end of the dock near the boat. Use it. It will take you to Teldrassil.\n5. Once you are at Teldrassil, find a dock that has a Portal going to the Exodar. Use it. It will take you to Azuremyst Isle.\n\n6. Once you are at Azuremyst Isle follow the road north of your map. Go around Stillpine Hold (cave) till you cross Fairbridge Strand. its the bridge going to Bloodmyst Isle.\n\n7. Straight ahead is the NPC you are looking for. You should be there by now. Enjoy!",
            date = "2018-09-16T14:55:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9624#comments:id=2615675",
        },
        {
            id = 75872,
            score = 14,
            author = "44462",
            text = "55,85 do with http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9634",
            date = "2007-05-01T03:57:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9624#comments:id=75872",
        },
        {
            id = 329652,
            score = 8,
            author = "79687",
            text = "if your a dwarf, you can use track treasure to find the pears.",
            date = "2008-07-18T20:13:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9624#comments:id=329652",
        },
    },
    [9625] = {
        {
            id = 1314976,
            score = 20,
            author = "183073",
            text = "yes if you pick up the Hero's call: Bloodmyst Isle you will not be able to complete this quest I abandon Hero's call right beside the quest giver and he finally showed a quest mark",
            date = "2011-01-29T21:17:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9625#comments:id=1314976",
        },
        {
            id = 114717,
            score = 12,
            author = "56275",
            text = "This quest is a play on \"This is serious business\" Or \"The Interwebs is serious business\" The phrase often being used on the World of Warcraft forum shows that Blizzard isn't out of the loop :D",
            date = "2007-07-03T01:04:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9625#comments:id=114717",
        },
        {
            id = 38105,
            score = 9,
            author = "13574",
            text = "North of Stillpine where the road forks.. go North to the new zone.",
            date = "2007-02-18T11:18:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9625#comments:id=38105",
        },
        {
            id = 1426224,
            score = 7,
            author = "Califree",
            text = "I can confirm the above for patch 4.1 (level 12 draenei warrior alt):\nHero's Call: Bloodmyst Isle! pays only 85 xp.\nElekks Are Serious Business pays 220 xp plus 1 silver.\n\nI also abandoned the Hero's Call quest right beside the Elekks questgiver and was able to pick up the more profitable quest.",
            date = "2011-05-24T10:58:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9625#comments:id=1426224",
        },
        {
            id = 2455552,
            score = 7,
            author = "TheFharaoh",
            text = "For some Hero's Call quests you can complete the Hero's Call quests and the other breadcrumb quest if you pick the Hero's Call quest FIRST and turn it in, but don't accept any other quests in the new zone. You can then go back and pick the other breadcrumb quest. That way you can complete both breadcrumb quests.\n\nThat does not work with this breadcrumb quest though. I tested it with two characters. You can only complete one of the breadcrumbs so I suggest you take this quest and ignore Hero's Call: Bloodmyst Isle! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28559/heros-call-bloodmyst-isle#comments:id=2455551) since this one gives more experience and reputation.",
            date = "2016-12-21T14:20:23-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9625#comments:id=2455552",
        },
    },
    [9626] = {
        {
            id = 154404,
            score = 24,
            author = "cookiecake",
            text = "To get to Orgimmar, talk to a guard and ask him where the 'Zeppelin Master' is, then exit Undercity through the sewers ('The Sewers' labeled on the Undercity map) into Tristfal Glades then head to the red flag on your map.\n\nClimb up the stairs till you see a bunch of goblins on your left. Wait where they are till a Zeppelin (airship) arrives and board it.\n\nOnce you arrive in Durotar, run down the stairs and talk to one of the guards. Ask them where the 'Shaman Trainer' is. Run to the red flag on your map.\nWhen you get there, Thrall is in the next room.\n\nHope this helped. :)",
            date = "2007-09-17T21:21:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9626#comments:id=154404",
        },
        {
