    [9706] = {
        {
            id = 366159,
            score = 13,
            author = "10502",
            text = "The pre-quest isn't http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9578 - I went there and completed that quest and couldn't accept the book quest - I later went there again to complete http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9703 and found that the quest was then available. At a guess I'd say the pre-chain to this quest is http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9779",
            date = "2008-08-31T14:20:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9706#comments:id=366159",
        },
        {
            id = 580266,
            score = 12,
            author = "Camthra",
            text = "This questline seems odd to me, like it was abruptly cut off. Over and over Blizzard refers to an \"abomination\" that the blood elves made, and from what I can tell, you were supposed to face off with this monster around the same time you blow up the Vector Coil.\n\nFrom what I can gather, it looks like the Blood Elves used a combination of brainwashing, fel magic, and torture to change Vindicator Saruan into some kind of terrible demon whose only purpose was to wreak havoc on Blood Watch.\n\nMatis even eludes to my theory while under inquisition after you capture him.\n\nI was actually looking forward to fighting Saruan when I was leveling my first draenei.\n\nI guess Blizz does cut off a LOT of questlines though. Maybe it'll be finished one day, but looking at almost EVERY other questline they've left hanging, it's not likely. (The only questline I can think of that they've fixed was the Shady Rest Inn questline in Dustwallow.",
            date = "2009-01-25T13:57:10-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9706#comments:id=580266",
        },
        {
            id = 1414910,
            score = 7,
            author = "572194",
            text = "The pre-quest is NOT Searching for Galaen (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=9578) neither Intercepting the Message (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=9779).\nThe pre-quest is Blood Watch (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=9694) , checked today (i can pick this quest without have Intercepting the Message (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=9779) and just after complete Blood Watch).",
            date = "2011-05-10T12:38:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9706#comments:id=1414910",
        },
        {
            id = 110400,
            score = 3,
            author = "Dianora",
            text = "The pre-requisit quest seemed to be http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9578 Searching for Galaen, which is offered by Morae at Blood Watch.",
            date = "2007-06-24T14:53:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9706#comments:id=110400",
        },
        {
            id = 5188450,
            score = 1,
            author = "Azaelyn",
            text = "Since it turns out you never get to see the \"abomination\" that Saruan was allegedly turned into, two things could have happened:\n\n1. Sironas never actually succeeded in corrupting him. She had started to maybe, and hyped it up to her underlings, but still ultimately failed. Maybe Saruan had died from resisting Sironas's corruption before it could be completed. What the Captured Sunhawk Agent says about the abomination when you are talking to them could just be things they were told or overheard, and they never actually saw it. This seems supported by [item=144275 domain=www]\n\n2. Saruan had actually been turned into the abomination and everything the Captured Sunhawk Agent said was true. One of those things was \"Any attacks against the Vector Coil will most certainly result in failure as long as that abomination is around.\" But then, when you raid and destroy the Vector Coil, the abomination isn't around. So before you made it up there to destroy the Coil, maybe Saruan was able to break free from the corruption for a moment and kill himself so that he would not stand in the way of the Draenei defeating the Blood Elves. That, or since the Sunhawk Agent described the abomination as being \"full of rage,\" it either had no loyalty or control and went rogue and started killing Blood Elves, or Saruan was able to regain some free will and turned against them on purpose, either way resulting in them having to kill him.",
            date = "2021-05-31T02:36:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9706#comments:id=5188450",
        },
    },
