            score = 9,
            author = "71674",
            text = "Soloed this with an 18 warrior, but it certainly wasn't worth the effort.\n\nFirst: there's a rare stealthed assassin running around.  Make sure she dies before you attempt soloing others.  The assassin is not elite, only silver.\n\nSecond: just because it looks like there's only one mob there from one angle doesn't mean that there's actually only one.  There are a couple points where they spawn in a straight line on the path most travelled, most notably the very first set as you start heading up the hill.\n\nThird: if you aren't a hybrid class, this is going to be rough.  Healing is a major perk if you're dealing with elites.  What I knew would be a trivial exercise in patience on my druid turned into a major, delicate task on my new warrior.\n\nAs for my specific strategy: If you pass the first group of two elves over the hills on the left, you'll come to a saboteur.  These don't have ranged attacks.  Make sure you're all clear (see above note on assassin), pull it with a crossbow, then just go to work.  Keep battle and demoralizing shouts up, thunder clap, sunder armor, rend--anything you can do to balance out the elite advantage without slowing your attacks.  If you're soloing, heroic strike isn't the best use for your rage until near the end of the fight.  Use Gift of the Naaru before you're on death's doorstep.  It's not like you're going to be able to save it for next fight if you have no other healing skills.  Wait for Gift to come off cooldown, then look to the agent straight up the hill past where you pulled the saboteur.  Agents have bows, so you have to charge that one and hope that the patrol from further up the hill doesn't see you.  Once in melee range, the fight is exactly like the saboteur, just different skills that you can't do much about coming at you.",
            date = "2007-10-16T23:14:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9761#comments:id=170074",
        },
        {
            id = 274018,
            score = 8,
            author = "72744",
            text = "If you're trying to \"solo\" this quest with the assistance of Demolitonist Legoso, you need to do a certain percentage of damage to the mob in order to receive credit for the kill.  If you are a low-burst damage class, your best choice is to let Legoso bumble his way into a pair of mobs and attack the target Legoso is not.  He's a very odd NPC, as he will sometimes feel the need to heal you.\n\nAs a prot paladin, I ended up with 5 agents and 3 saboteurs dead before Legoso left, and was able to amble around the mountains avoiding pairs to find single mobs to kill.",
            date = "2008-04-18T21:53:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9761#comments:id=274018",
        },
    },
    [9762] = {
        {
            id = 1613483,
            score = 123,
            author = "877612",
            text = "It seems that this is only pointed out in replies to other comments, so I'd like to make a note of it on its own.\n\nYou have to be a draenei in order to get this quest. I was working on the Bloodmyst Isle quests on my night elf for https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7520, and I got stuck at 57/60. I came here to Wowhead and saw this quest with a tabard as a reward, but even after doing all of the Bloodmyst Isle quests and being Exalted with Exodar, Velen didn't give me the quest, and it wasnt until then that I really started reading through the comments and replies to see that only a draenei can do this quest, and get the tabard.\n\nLucky draenei. =P",
            date = "2012-01-19T11:25:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9762#comments:id=1613483",
        },
