        },
        {
            id = 281417,
            score = 5,
            author = "146503",
            text = "you should do with \"natural enemies\",the giants drop the bog lord tendril",
            date = "2008-05-03T01:45:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9783#comments:id=281417",
        },
        {
            id = 106064,
            score = 4,
            author = "63155",
            text = "Enter Dead Mire in the northeast part of Zangermarsh and you are there. The Withering Giants are all along the edge. :D\nIf you are currently on the Gathering the Reagents quest; you can go to 77,45 in Dead Mire and kill Sporewing each time he spawns for a Spore Bat Eye. I had gotten a 75% droprate. Doubletasking is fun.",
            date = "2007-06-17T15:36:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9783#comments:id=106064",
        },
        {
            id = 37860,
            score = 3,
            author = "24835_",
            text = "Coords correct. They're all over the inner parts of The Dead Mire, entrance at 80,53.",
            date = "2007-02-18T00:42:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9783#comments:id=37860",
        },
        {
            id = 182230,
            score = 3,
            author = "47329",
            text = "Go to 80,38 by the demolished little bridge.  Almost no adds and the re-spawn rate is slow enough to keep you from getting ganked while resting, eating or eating.  I also was able to pick up a Withered Basidium that started a turn-in quest for a super easy 10,500 exp.  All told, 21,000 exp, 2g40s 250 Exodar rep and a resale of 2g14s for the Vindicator's Cinch made this an awesome quest.",
            date = "2007-11-11T04:08:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9783#comments:id=182230",
        },
    },
    [9784] = {
        {
            id = 1495225,
            score = 111,
            author = "865566",
            text = "There are clearly not enough pins on this map",
            date = "2011-08-15T00:07:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9784#comments:id=1495225",
        },
        {
            id = 191749,
            score = 47,
            author = "Katalaka",
            text = "Be sure you save any Uncatalogued Species you get, while the plant parts will stop giving rep after honored the Uncatalogued Species still will.",
            date = "2007-11-26T16:15:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9784#comments:id=191749",
        },
        {
            id = 139193,
            score = 42,
            author = "bnetgamer77",
            text = "Shocking how no one mentions a fine area to farm these.\n\nIt's true most, if not all mobs have an average of 20-25% chance to drop these...but I found out that the most annoying of Zangarmarsh creatures hold the key to gaining many Unidentified plants.\n\nIf you've ever done an instance in Zangarmasrh, you know of the lake to swim through has a plentiful amount of Mudfin frenzys' that every so often shoot up at you.\n\nTurns out these buggers each have a 20-25% chance to drop an Unidentified Plant, and being they are all 1/4 of a regular mob, to AoE them down in a sense technically quadruples your chance of finding an Unidentified Plant.\n\nI farmed these guys in bear form with no hassle and hit some mobs of 4 with no drops, to tanking a mob of 8 getting 7 drops...the odds are in your favor if you're out for the Grinding of Unidentified Plants.\n\nBest of luck, and good fishing!",
            date = "2007-08-16T21:27:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9784#comments:id=139193",
        },
        {
            id = 1392433,
            score = 36,
            author = "720645",
            text = "Be sure to turn them in before you hit honored, i did this mistake and now im stuck with 80 plants :(",
            date = "2011-04-16T06:19:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9784#comments:id=1392433",
        },
        {
            id = 18082,
            score = 21,
            author = "Lustral",
            text = "There is also a small chance that you'll get an uncataloged plant in the bag, which you can turn into Lauranna for additional Cenarion Expedition rep.\n\nIt's worth hanging onto extra unidentified plant parts if for only that reason, after you've completed the quest.",
            date = "2006-12-27T09:39:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9784#comments:id=18082",
        },
    },
    [9785] = {
        {
            id = 7473,
            score = 42,
            author = "6934",
            text = "You don't have to slay the ancients, not sure why that says that up there.  Just talk to them(they're giant trees standing/walking within the town), get the blessing, and return to Windcaller Blackhoof.  You can continue to pick the buffs up from here on out.\n\nAshyen - Mark of Lore - Increases spell damage/healing by 18 for 30 min.\n\nKeleth - Mark of War - Increases attack power by 30 for 30 min.",
            date = "2006-12-06T14:44:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9785#comments:id=7473",
        },
        {
            id = 110577,
            score = 41,
            author = "32041",
            text = "Note that according to the quest, \"These boons will become more powerful as your renown among us increases,\" indicating an increase dependent on your reputation with Cenarion Expedition. These buffs also only work while in Zangarmarsh and are very helpful for doing the first part of Coilfang instances.\n\nThe following reputation levels grant the following boons:\n\nFRIENDLY\nMark of Lore - Damage and healing done by your spells by 18 for 30 min\nMark of War - Attack power by 30 for 30 min\n\nHONORED\nMark of Lore - Damage and healing done by your spells by 30 for 30 min\nMark of War - Attack power by 50 for 30 min\n\nREVERED\nMark of Lore - Damage and healing done by your spells by 45 for 30 min\nMark of War - Attack power by 70 for 30 min\n\nEXALTED\nMark of Lore - Damage and healing done by your spells by 60 for 30 min\nMark of War - Attack power by 100 for 30 min",
            date = "2007-06-24T21:13:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9785#comments:id=110577",
        },
        {
            id = 546482,
            score = 21,
            author = "Teldarsterallnes",
            text = "Is there a prequest to this?",
            date = "2009-01-04T14:07:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9785#comments:id=546482",
        },
        {
            id = 281578,
            score = 12,
            author = "Hacardos",
            text = "The blessings are obtainable after the quest is done, i was a little worried about that ;)",
            date = "2008-05-03T09:13:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9785#comments:id=281578",
        },
        {
            id = 153239,
            score = 9,
            author = "56517",
            text = "Mark Of Lore.\nMark of War.\n\nBoth can you find in Cenarion Refuge.\n\nLore (Ashyen) are at 81.63. All you need to do: Talk to him and then wait a minute. Complete.\nDo the same to War (Keleth). He is at 79,67\n\nDid notice they walk around a bit. But in Cenarion Refuge.\n\nGood Luck!",
            date = "2007-09-15T07:16:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9785#comments:id=153239",
        },
    },
    [9786] = {
        {
            id = 109254,
            score = 74,
            author = "Sixotoo",
            text = "The comments here are confusing. The actual location for the quest to complete are 45,68. It is not a hut, It is the temple built into the side of the mountain south of Feralfen Village. There are 4 guards leading to the entrance and 1 elite inside the temple which you will not agro if you step in just far enough to complete the quest.",
            date = "2007-06-22T11:23:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9786#comments:id=109254",
        },
        {
            id = 20982,
            score = 37,
            author = "11591",
            text = "Location is 45,66. The quest completes once you enter the hut in the far south of the ruins.",
            date = "2007-01-17T06:07:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9786#comments:id=20982",
        },
        {
            id = 17725,
            score = 31,
            author = "Expunge",
            text = "The Boha'mu Ruins are located in the south central part of the zone, directly south of Feralfen Village.",
            date = "2006-12-21T14:07:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9786#comments:id=17725",
        },
        {
            id = 1332093,
            score = 19,
            author = "Jolster",
            text = "Note to anyone having problems with this Quest.\n\nYou have to enter the temple building thing to complete the explore part of this quest. just flying over the building will not work. you actually have to enter the building.\n\n*edited for spelling mistake that has been bugging me for 7 years :D",
            date = "2011-02-11T16:17:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9786#comments:id=1332093",
        },
        {
            id = 264906,
            score = 12,
            author = "cyborg99",
            text = "Elder Kuruti does not attack you unless you attack him first, so don't worry about creeping up to him.\n\nEDIT: Sending a screenshot for proof soon.\n\nEDIT2: Since WoWhead must have rejected my screenshot...\nhttp://img132.imageshack.us/img132/7412/bohamuzz7.jpg",
            date = "2008-04-02T02:45:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9786#comments:id=264906",
        },
    },
    [9787] = {
        {
            id = 18079,
            score = 73,
            author = "Lustral",
            text = "Though there are more spawn points of the idols scattered around Feralfen Village, I found the best place to collect them was south of Feralfen on the stairs leading up to the The Boha'mu Ruins (tall tower on the map).\n\nThe idols are tiny, wooden statues that look like falcons, and because their respawn is so fast, you can kill the 4 mobs leading up to the Ruins and pick up all 6 required in very little time, rather than running throughout the village and having to kill loads of mobs.",
            date = "2006-12-27T09:29:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9787#comments:id=18079",
        },
        {
            id = 21435,
            score = 34,
            author = "Frei",
            text = "44,65 <-- Thats the cords for the stairway. I have also submitted a screen for those. Cheers.",
            date = "2007-01-18T17:15:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9787#comments:id=21435",
        },
        {
            id = 25401,
            score = 13,
            author = "16507",
            text = "The lazy mans way of doing it is stand at (44,67) and wait until it respawns every 30 secs and you are done the quest in 3 mins without ever havin to run anywhere.",
            date = "2007-01-26T23:27:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9787#comments:id=25401",
        },
        {
            id = 21142,
            score = 11,
            author = "dreanna",
            text = "One idol at the top and one at the bottom of the stairs, it was great - the respawn timer is really fast. Only had to kill a couple of mobs!",
            date = "2007-01-17T20:17:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9787#comments:id=21142",
        },
        {
            id = 79878,
            score = 5,
            author = "Drexxis",
            text = "I timed the idols to be on an approximated 35 second re-spawn timer. So if you like you can sit by the windmill in the (51,61) area and spawn loot the idol on the east side of it. There's no enemies by it so it's quite easy.",
            date = "2007-05-08T15:00:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9787#comments:id=79878",
        },
    },
    [9788] = {
        {
            id = 7906,
            score = 256,
            author = "6934",
            text = "Found at 70, 97 in the cave (entrance coords: 74, 90) take a right after entering the cave and follow the path for a while.  It's resting on a rock near two sporeloks.",
            date = "2006-12-06T19:21:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9788#comments:id=7906",
        },
        {
            id = 38510,
            score = 151,
            author = "8195",
            text = "From entrance you go right & follow the ledge as it curves around to the left.  Once that curve is done you have a sharp curve to the right & the path starts to go down.  At the bottom on that first down ramp you hit a hairpin like turn left & down more.  The box is in that hairpin corner and it's small.  Very easy to miss.  Looks like the little toolboxes from newbie Horde quests.",
            date = "2007-02-19T03:48:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9788#comments:id=38510",
        },
        {
            id = 2348920,
            score = 47,
            author = "Metzae",
            text = "coordinates inside the cave: 70.53, 97.90",
            date = "2016-07-06T23:36:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9788#comments:id=2348920",
        },
        {
            id = 33736,
            score = 35,
            author = "702",
            text = "You can do two other quests at the same time.\n\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10096\n\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9894",
            date = "2007-02-10T19:03:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9788#comments:id=33736",
        },
        {
            id = 1792409,
            score = 29,
            author = "325313",
            text = "Once inside the cave, go [ins]right[/ins] at the first hairpin turn [ins]slight upgrade[/ins] then follow it [ins]downgrade[/ins], turn [ins]left upgrade[/ins], just before you get to the top of this upgrade will be another [ins]right[/ins] turn with a  [ins]short upgrade[/ins] leading into a [ins]slight downgrade[/ins] leading into a [ins]steep downgrade[/ins] and [ins]just at the bottom[/ins] of this steep downgrade will be the flat rock with the [ins](small)[/ins] box on the flat rock behind that mob of 1 Marsh Dredger.\n\nHope this helps!",
            date = "2013-01-04T10:39:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9788#comments:id=1792409",
        },
    },
    [9789] = {
        {
            id = 26900,
            score = 22,
            author = "13182",
            text = "That means around 65, 47.",
            date = "2007-01-29T04:52:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9789#comments:id=26900",
        },
        {
            id = 676614,
            score = 17,
            author = "night1090",
            text = "The number of Clefthoofs needed has been dropped from 30 to 12.",
            date = "2009-04-14T21:36:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9789#comments:id=676614",
        },
        {
            id = 65535,
            score = 8,
            author = "Nerissa",
            text = "I looked at the number required and died a little inside. 3 times the number required for the earlier STV chain. (Which is structured the same way)",
            date = "2007-04-11T13:29:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9789#comments:id=65535",
        },
        {
            id = 12535,
            score = 5,
            author = "6934",
            text = "Head down to the grassy area just North of the Ring of Trials and you'll find the best area to get quick kills.  The area is also rich with Windroc's -- I suggest pairing the quest with http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9854.",
            date = "2006-12-10T01:29:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9789#comments:id=12535",
        },
        {
            id = 172562,
            score = 5,
            author = "93908",
            text = "I like to try and get as many quests done as possible at each area, so I stayed in the area just west over the road from the Burning Blade Ruins (69,71 is the middle of the small area I was doing this) while here I completed:\n\nClefthoof Mastery - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9789\nTalbuk Mastery - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9857\nI Must Have Them - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10109\nThe Tortured Earth - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9819\nA Head Full of Ivory - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9914 (although the Wild Elekk's dont come by often its easy enough with the kill list you have from the other quests)\n\n5 Quests in 1 small area meant some great XPph once all complete and hand ins done.",
            date = "2007-10-21T07:10:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9789#comments:id=172562",
        },
    },
    [9790] = {
        {
            id = 21635,
            score = 38,
            author = "13105",
            text = "These drop off the stingers, needlers, and bleeders.",
            date = "2007-01-19T15:54:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9790#comments:id=21635",
        },
        {
            id = 70618,
            score = 24,
            author = "10415",
            text = "Do this quest along with http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9830 .",
            date = "2007-04-21T18:22:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9790#comments:id=70618",
        },
        {
            id = 25361,
            score = 17,
            author = "16485",
            text = "There are plenty south of Orebor Harborage and on the east end of Hewn Bog.\n\nI suggest doing the initial Angor'mosh and Daggerfen quests together with this one. They're good quests to grind in one general area.",
            date = "2007-01-26T21:50:15-06:00",
