            score = 21,
            author = "darkrebel08",
            text = "The exact spawn rate is 2mins 5secs.",
            date = "2007-01-21T22:38:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9901#comments:id=22590",
        },
        {
            id = 183194,
            score = 11,
            author = "43216",
            text = "Simple quest, Sporewing is a lvl 62, non-elite, easily soloable.\n\nAs for rewards, picking the stack of \"Scroll of Strength V\" (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=27503) would be your best option from a gold-making perspective.\n\nThe scrolls are relatively hard to come by and sell very nicely in the AH since Blacksmiths need two of these scrolls to make Ragesteel Shoulders: (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=33173)",
            date = "2007-11-13T02:50:51-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9901#comments:id=183194",
        },
        {
            id = 225821,
            score = 5,
            author = "64177",
            text = "All the scrolls rewarded by this quest are of limited availability. They are all purchasable from the first two vendors in limited supply with strength, stamina, agility and spirit sold by the third, also in limited supply.:\n\nField Repair Bot 110G (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=24780)\nProfessor Thaddeus Paleo (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=14847)\nSahaak (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=23363)\n\nYou can only buy from Sahaak vendor when doing the quest A Shabby Disguise (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11029)\n\nScrolls stack with elixirs of the same stat bonus but not single stat player buffs. In other words scrolls of stamina, intellect and spirit wont stack with PW:F, Divine Spirit or Arcane intellect and are of little use in a raid.\n\nScrolls of agility and strength *do* stack with shaman totems buffing that stat and are highly sought after. I suggest choosing these either for personal use when raiding at level 70 or to sell on the AH. I choose the agility scrolls and sold them for 10g on Defias Brotherhood - EU\n\nThe scrolls of protection stack with elixirs and player buffs but don't tend to be so popular.",
            date = "2008-01-28T16:56:23-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9901#comments:id=225821",
        },
        {
            id = 20832,
            score = 2,
            author = "12426",
            text = "Can be found at or near 76,45",
            date = "2007-01-16T14:34:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9901#comments:id=20832",
        },
    },
    [9902] = {
        {
            id = 146769,
            score = 37,
            author = "CharlzO",
            text = "You must be Neutral with the Kurenai to pick up this quest",
            date = "2007-08-30T17:14:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9902#comments:id=146769",
        },
        {
            id = 17785,
            score = 34,
            author = "10162",
            text = "Terrowclaw - in the small island (tloc 22,46)",
            date = "2006-12-22T02:49:09-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9902#comments:id=17785",
        },
        {
            id = 34474,
            score = 20,
            author = "22683",
            text = "Be sure to kill surrounding mobs, terrorclaw will fear you into them. I found out the hard way",
            date = "2007-02-12T04:07:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9902#comments:id=34474",
        },
        {
            id = 103488,
            score = 9,
            author = "61150",
            text = "Terrorclaw spawns at the small island in Marshlight Lake, together with 7 mobs. (22,46) .\nBe aware that Terrorclaw fears you, so be sure to kill all of his mobs before you pull him.\nAs a BM hunter this was a pretty easy quest, cleared one side of the island and then pulled him, Bestial Wrath ( unable to be feared ) and his dead within a sec.",
            date = "2007-06-13T05:18:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9902#comments:id=103488",
        },
        {
            id = 855870,
            score = 7,
            author = "462476",
            text = "The gemmed quest rewards are very good with cheap northrend gems, and this quest is super easy with flying mount.\n\nIf you only do a few quests in Zangarmarsh, do this one.",
            date = "2009-09-30T10:05:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9902#comments:id=855870",
        },
    },
    [9903] = {
        {
