            text = "There are 2 caves in this area, Corki is in the southern cave mid-way up the hill, after talking to him you have to go to the north cave to kill Cho'war the Pillager to recieve the key to free Corki, good luck!",
            date = "2008-04-04T00:04:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9954#comments:id=266028",
        },
        {
            id = 28926,
            score = 26,
            author = "Flyv",
            text = "This quest is soloable by higher levels. You can either stealth in to Corki or work your way in. Next to Corki is Warmaul Chef Bufferlo (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18440#00Rzc), a level 66 elite who isn't too difficult.\n\nThe next step of this quest (Cho'war the Pillager) involves killing an elite who is significantly more difficult.",
            date = "2007-02-01T12:28:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9954#comments:id=28926",
        },
        {
            id = 993706,
            score = 25,
            author = "167663",
            text = "I'm just going to say what everyone is thinking: screw this kid.",
            date = "2010-03-08T21:20:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9954#comments:id=993706",
        },
    },
    [9955] = {
        {
            id = 196943,
            score = 134,
            author = "JKane",
            text = "The back door entrance is at 27,11 if you just want to fly there and skip half of the ogres.",
            date = "2007-12-06T13:14:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9955#comments:id=196943",
        },
        {
            id = 1321495,
            score = 74,
            author = "Arcinde",
            text = "I found it a bit difficult to find the guy, so here's some directions:\n\nGo into the north cave of Warmaul Hill at 27.0, 18.9.\nKeep going north until you reach a northern exit at 28.4, 13.6. Then you'll have to walk outside for a bit - keep to the left wall and you'll see another entrance at 27.3, 11.5.\nNow you'll be on the second story of the same cave. Just keep to the path and don't fall off (turn right at the fork at 25.5, 14.4), and you'll reach Cho'war on a little platform at the top.",
            date = "2011-02-04T11:10:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9955#comments:id=1321495",
        },
        {
            id = 262141,
            score = 73,
            author = "133362",
            text = "I love it how you have 50 people telling you have to kill the guy but not how to finish the quest.  This listing is for the quest, not the NPC.  You kill the NPC in the quest but still have more to do.\n After you get key from killing Cho'war, corki is in middle cave all the way in back, 29,26.  Then return to Arechron.",
            date = "2008-03-28T18:10:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9955#comments:id=262141",
        },
        {
            id = 112023,
            score = 27,
            author = "siggboy",
            text = "This is how you can solo it on a hunter:\n\nFirst, turn on \"Aspect of the Viper\" and turn off \"Growl\" and all damaging special attacks on your pet.  You want \"Viper\" because it's a lenghty fight and no special abilities so you can aggro him easier.\n\nClear the entire area immediately before the attempt.\nRun up, send in the pet (with \"Growl\" turned off) and activate \"Mend Pet\" right away (apart from making sure that your pet won't die, this will aggro him towards you in case he's out of sight after you have jumped down).\nPut the pet on \"Stay\" and jump down the ledge.  Chances are he'll already be following you because of the aggro from \"Mend Pet\".  If not, wait until he does or start shooting right away if you have an LoS to him.\nBe careful not to fall down the ledge to your right.  When he gets close, feign death.  He will not reset but run back towards your pet which is conveniently parked at his spawn location.  Rinse, repeat until dead.\n\nIf your pet dies, you lose because he'll reset to full health as soon as you FD.  The video posted above will help you getting familiar with the setup, but I think it's pretty clear anyway when you're at the location yourself.\n\nThis is actually a prime example how to exploit pathing to effectively solo difficult mobs with a hunter.  Ironically non of the quest rewards are especially appealing to us ;-).",
            date = "2007-06-27T19:38:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9955#comments:id=112023",
        },
        {
            id = 23574,
            score = 24,
            author = "13769",
            text = "Keep going through the northern cave. He's on top.",
            date = "2007-01-24T08:40:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=9955#comments:id=23574",
        },
    },
    [9956] = {
