            id = 21644,
            score = 204,
            author = "Wikki",
            text = "Trachela is at 43, 51",
            date = "2007-01-19T16:04:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10035#comments:id=21644",
        },
        {
            id = 21479,
            score = 108,
            author = "13008",
            text = "After killing Trachala, take his carcass to the scarecrow at (27,55) and summon the elite. Easy with 3 people at level 63.",
            date = "2007-01-18T20:19:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10035#comments:id=21479",
        },
        {
            id = 1844349,
            score = 59,
            author = "LeaHavoc",
            text = "Some people are still confused, so I'll make this as simple as possible...\n\n1. You must first kill Trachela (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=21515), then Loot Trachela's carcass.\n2. Go to Terokkar Forest (where the quest arrow leads you), look for Torgos Bane (http://www.wowwiki.com/Torgos%27s_Bane) \"the big scarecrow\" , it has a blue light underneath it.\n3. Once you have located the scarecrow, right click Trachela's carcass that is in your bag (this will bring Torgos to you).\n3. Kill Torgos and loot.\n\nTada! Quest complete!",
            date = "2013-04-17T17:59:12-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10035#comments:id=1844349",
        },
        {
            id = 2459695,
            score = 32,
            author = "Boxofbeer",
            text = "Find https://www.wowhead.com/npc=21515 at 43.2 51.6 (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=21515#map) coordinates, it's a giant grey carrion bird floating above a big pile of bones, slay it and loot https://www.wowhead.com/item=30618 from it's corpse.\nWhen you done, make your way to 26.9, 55.7 point, where you'll find Torgos' Bane, use https://www.wowhead.com/item=30618 to call down https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18707.\nTomTom:\n/way Terokkar Forest 43.2 51.6 Trachela spot\n/way Terokkar Forest 26.9 55.7 Torgos spot\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10035 — https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CQ37_-gieG4",
            date = "2017-01-06T00:27:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10035#comments:id=2459695",
        },
        {
            id = 17701,
            score = 30,
            author = "9877",
            text = "This quest is a follow-up to the Wanted Poster found in Allerian Stronghold.",
            date = "2006-12-21T10:58:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10035#comments:id=17701",
        },
    },
    [10036] = {
        {
            id = 4023,
            score = 228,
            author = "ace22b",
            text = "Trachela is at 43.2, 51.7.\n\nScarecrow you need has blue hue and is at 27.0, 55.6.",
            date = "2006-11-22T20:41:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10036#comments:id=4023",
        },
        {
            id = 59454,
            score = 104,
            author = "Eskimio",
            text = "First: You kill Trachela, a 62-63 buzzard, to get her carcass.\nTrachela is on top of the highest hill at Carrion Hill, south of Stonebreaker Hold (Coords are at 43, 52).\n\nThen: You bring the carcass to a large scarecrow, which glows blue, in the far north-western corner of the Bone Wastes (Coords are at 27, 56).\n\nOnce the carcass has been lain, a 65 elite buzzard named Torgos spawns.\n\nI, a level 64 Elemental Troll Shaman, and my friend, a level 64 Arms Orc Warrior, took him easily.",
            date = "2007-03-29T23:02:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10036#comments:id=59454",
        },
        {
            id = 187552,
            score = 35,
            author = "53189",
            text = "Note that if you set out the carcass and die, you'll have to go get another one.",
            date = "2007-11-19T09:26:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10036#comments:id=187552",
        },
        {
            id = 748691,
            score = 30,
            author = "35921",
            text = "I can't be the only person to find this quest morally repugnant can I? It's basically:\n\nWe want to kill this bird guy.. so you kill his wife, take her mangled corpse and put it on a rock, and as he comes down to mourn, kill him.\n\nThat's a little sick, even by my standards.",
            date = "2009-06-16T22:07:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10036#comments:id=748691",
        },
        {
            id = 1659703,
            score = 20,
            author = "TimeTraveler",
            text = "Just to clarify for some folks, the carcass is not given to you when you pick up the quest.  The quest takes you to two places. First you kill her to get the carcass to lure him down.  She is in north bone waste area, a little bigger than all the other blue flyers, then you take her carcass west (watch the markers on your map to see where) and look for a blue light around one of the scarecrow looking markers.  This is where you put her carcass and he will come down to fight you.  Good comments on here about stepping back after you drop the carcass as he does come down right on top of it.",
            date = "2012-04-28T05:58:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10036#comments:id=1659703",
        },
    },
    [10037] = {
        {
            id = 36935,
            score = 117,
            author = "23914",
            text = "Ironically you can't get the Eel's by fishing, I tried for about 20 mins and none came up. Ah well, still good fishing skill-ups.",
            date = "2007-02-16T11:04:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10037#comments:id=36935",
        },
        {
            id = 11853,
            score = 79,
            author = "6934",
            text = "These eels are located just to the Northeast of Shattrath, in Silmyr Lake (looks more like a long pond to me). They're very weak for their level (went down in 3 non crit frostbolts for me) and they drop the scales 1 out of every 3 kills or so. Easy xp, don't skip this by any means.",
            date = "2006-12-08T23:23:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10037#comments:id=11853",
        },
        {
            id = 21935,
            score = 53,
            author = "13257",
            text = "Coords: 40, 12  In the lake easy to kill (shadow priest  -3 non cirts)  lvl 62-63 drop is low but you need only 8.",
            date = "2007-01-20T05:47:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10037#comments:id=21935",
        },
        {
            id = 114484,
            score = 25,
            author = "66167",
            text = "For those horde-side, Nat Pagle's Extreme Angler FC-5000 (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=19022) is a better alternative. It doesn't have the +51 stamina (who needs that on a fishing pole, anyway?) but it has +25 fishing. For the Alliance, however, this is a perfect fishing pole.\n\nAs for the actual mob, they're quite easy to kill. Took me maybe 10 seconds to kill one, maybe less. They also drop Motes of Water pretty easily (I got one almost every kill), so good to farm if you're looking for Primal Water.\n\nDrop on the quest item sucked for me, though. About 1 in eight.\n\nEDIT: The Nat Pagle's Extreme Angler FC-5000 was actually nerfed years later in Wrath of the Lich King patch 3.1. It now only gives +20 fishing, meaning it is now equivalent to this fishing pole. Horde players no longer get an advantage in fishing skill. It also, for some reason, is now no longer disenchantable and only sells to vendors for an entire 7 copper.\n\nI really wonder what must go through the minds of the people working at Blizzard to think almost four years after a fishing pole was added that they need to nerf it.\n\nEDIT 2: Nat Pagle's Extreme Angler FC-5000 was changed, again. It now sells for 2g85s80c and is disenchantable again.",
            date = "2007-07-02T14:36:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10037#comments:id=114484",
        },
        {
            id = 159316,
            score = 12,
            author = "Shivacode",
            text = "What's sad is the level 70s grinding this lake have access to mobs with better droprates on mote of water. At the very least they should be spending time grinding Muck Spawns in Nagrand, barely any HP and vulnerable to frost like these guys plus good droprate on water motes.\n\nAnyways, new char on a low-pop server, did this at 2AM, just me in the lake. Got a primal in the process. While the droprate for the quest item is just about as bad as the Zangarmarsh eel grind fest, since you actually get items of value (particularly water motes) from these guys you aren't as buggered.",
            date = "2007-09-27T09:32:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10037#comments:id=159316",
        },
    },
