            text = "This is the repeatable quest for Halaa research tokens.\n\nYou can only turn this in if your side controls Halaa.\n\nThe token rewards are obviously currency, along with the Halaa Battle Token (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=26045)s which are a reward for killing enemy forces in the area.\n\nBoth stacks max out at 100 but you can have as many stacks of these tokens as you desire.",
            date = "2008-05-14T09:50:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10077#comments:id=288036",
        },
        {
            id = 334969,
            score = 6,
            author = "hypehuman",
            text = "Oshu'gun Crystal Powder Sample does not drop for players until level 64.  I killled about two hundred ogres and elekks in Nagrand before while I was grinding out the last few bubbles of level 63, and I didn't get a single one until I hit level 64.",
            date = "2008-07-24T12:46:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10077#comments:id=334969",
        },
        {
            id = 945868,
            score = 5,
            author = "Zephyras",
            text = "Please note that Add-ons (Such as EveryQuest) and the Wowhead Profiler do not count this quest as completed even if you have done it. This is because it is one of the ~Pick up and hand in with one click~ style quests, or one of the special repeatables which are scattered around the world which don't actually seem to treat themselves as real repeatables. Even if you query the blizzard servers for your completed quests, this quest registers as incomplete.\n\nMaybe this will change in future, but is valid as of the posting date.",
            date = "2010-01-12T18:42:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10077#comments:id=945868",
        },
        {
            id = 324451,
            score = 2,
            author = "118286",
            text = "even at lvl 70 completing this quest says i have received 8750 experience and 2g 90s",
            date = "2008-07-11T11:54:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10077#comments:id=324451",
        },
    },
    [10078] = {
        {
            id = 20891,
            score = 87,
            author = "Nimchip",
            text = "56,46 - central eastern thrower\n59,47 - eastern thrower\n54,48 - central western thrower\n53,48 - western thrower\nthey are catapults along the horde side of the Path of Glory",
            date = "2007-01-16T20:45:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10078#comments:id=20891",
        },
        {
            id = 838256,
            score = 17,
            author = "Mergy",
            text = "I found the easiest way to do this quest. If you have your flying mount, fly to the top of the siege engine, unmount, and burn. It works wonders, and mobs won't attack.",
            date = "2009-09-12T04:20:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10078#comments:id=838256",
        },
        {
            id = 130386,
            score = 11,
            author = "viejo",
            text = "I had a tough time with this one, mainly because I elected to cross the road to glory instead of going east out of Honor Hold and around that way. There are a bunch of lvl 63 shattered hand captains, and their minions which are lvl 62 hanging around on the road. I did manage to battle my way through, but it was TOUGH. Now once you're up the hill on the other side, carefull pulling. There are lvl 61 hellboars and one 61 elite orc running around near the catapults. So map out your killing field bearing this in mind. Once you get a clear space anywhere near the catapults, use the torch and back away. The flame effect is pretty cool. On my way back, rather than battle accross the road yet again, I took the long way around :)",
            date = "2007-08-01T09:32:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10078#comments:id=130386",
        },
        {
            id = 417651,
            score = 9,
            author = "205357",
            text = "If you left the torch in the bank when you run off to do this quest, don't think abandoning it and then accepting it again from Dumphry will get you another torch.  I tried twice and still ended up having to fly back to Shatt to get the torch out of the bank.  Unlike most quests, abandoning this one won't get rid of the torch quest item in your bank.",
            date = "2008-10-23T14:47:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10078#comments:id=417651",
        },
        {
            id = 216935,
            score = 5,
            author = "Fyurae",
            text = "The 61 Elite, Tagar Spinebreaker, paths all the way around to the ridge southeast of Hellfire Citadel (around 49, 58), so you can wait for him to move out of the area and it will be quite a while before he comes back. You might want to watch out for the Fel Reaver that patrols the road to Thrallmar. I did this with my 59 hunter. Very rewarding quest for how simple it is.",
            date = "2008-01-11T19:09:51-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10078#comments:id=216935",
        },
    },
