            score = 7,
            author = "141915",
            text = "Forge Camp: Rage also houses the Gan'arg servants, so if you are looking for Razorsaw, make sure you are in Forge Camp: Mageddon. I spent like 10 minutes waiting for him to spawn before I realized I was in the wrong camp. Right mobs, wrong place.\n\nRazorsaw is a very easy kill; he died before he had time to attack me. [61 fire mage]. He also drops Burning Legion Missive, which begins http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10395.\n\nGood luck!",
            date = "2008-05-22T13:07:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10390#comments:id=292685",
        },
        {
            id = 1637642,
            score = 5,
            author = "14690",
            text = "Do yourself a favor and simply clear everything you see in the quest area. Makes it much easier when going for the servant mobs which cluster around the cannons.\n\nOnly the little servant mobs give you points towards finishing it, but those guys will be swarmed with demons and cannons. Considering the level of the quest, it's one of the harder ones. Most pulls were 2 or 3 guys and usually had a wandering mob join in. Not impossible but definitely a curious ramp up in difficulty for a level 60.",
            date = "2012-03-10T01:37:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10390#comments:id=1637642",
        },
        {
            id = 128217,
            score = 3,
            author = "Athene",
            text = "Do mind the fast respawnrate in this area. Even Razorsaw respawns something like every 1 or 2 minutes. I got attacked by up to 3 mobs at a time due to surprising respawnrate.",
            date = "2007-07-28T11:27:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10390#comments:id=128217",
        },
    },
    [10391] = {
        {
            id = 105252,
            score = 26,
            author = "49206",
            text = "Destroying the cannons at the Mageddon camp also works.",
            date = "2007-06-16T03:26:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10391#comments:id=105252",
        },
        {
            id = 24617,
            score = 18,
            author = "15585",
            text = "58, 31 is the location of this base, it's surrounded by Forge Camp Legionnaire's",
            date = "2007-01-25T19:12:30-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10391#comments:id=24617",
        },
        {
            id = 23283,
            score = 14,
            author = "12690",
            text = "Wow, so, are you telling me I could have just clicked a firepot and had them explode? Because I just ran up and beat the heck out of them, and that did the trick.\n\nSo, I guess for anyone that is wondering, killing them the old fashioned way works just fine. :)",
            date = "2007-01-23T13:19:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10391#comments:id=23283",
        },
        {
            id = 246269,
            score = 4,
            author = "Solution",
            text = "This can be a tough one to solo.  Forge Camp: Rage is way too crowded-- kill the cannons back at Mageddon where the first part of the chain was.\n\nI found that sitting on the edge of the cliff near the left-most cannon was the best way to get this done.  At this location you're safe from patrols and you'll only ever have to fight two mobs at once.  The cannon and servant will spawn at the same time-- kill them both and by the time your health has filled back up a respawn should come shortly.  Rinse and repeat.\n\nSee the screenshot for positioning.",
            date = "2008-03-01T15:30:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10391#comments:id=246269",
        },
        {
            id = 382816,
            score = 3,
            author = "kaze950",
            text = "The hardest part about this quest isn't the cannons, but all the mobs in the area! Don't be  surprised getting ganged up by 3 or 4 servants. Watch out for those Forgefiends as well.",
            date = "2008-09-21T01:58:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10391#comments:id=382816",
        },
    },
    [10392] = {
        {
            id = 20828,
            score = 58,
            author = "dJe781",
            text = "Takes place north of Thrallmar.\nThe key loots from Arix'Amal (53,26) and has to be used on the Burning Legion Gate (53,28).\nHe doesn't hurt that hard but he strikes pretty fast.",
            date = "2007-01-16T13:50:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10392#comments:id=20828",
        },
        {
            id = 62621,
            score = 34,
            author = "24033",
            text = "Leads to Cruel's Intentions\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10136",
            date = "2007-04-05T15:12:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10392#comments:id=62621",
        },
        {
            id = 22511,
            score = 22,
            author = "2759",
            text = "The gate is a little hard to see- you actually have to stand inside the big portal thing to be able to see/activate it once you have the key.",
            date = "2007-01-21T18:30:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10392#comments:id=22511",
        },
        {
            id = 39011,
            score = 11,
            author = "13128",
            text = "Arix had a very fast respawn time (like 1 min or less) when I had the place to myself, so be careful.  Other mobs had pretty fast respawn too.",
            date = "2007-02-20T01:44:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10392#comments:id=39011",
        },
        {
            id = 179837,
            score = 9,
            author = "88582",
            text = "This quest sucks. this sucks bad. the mobs are crowded in the place, they respawn almost instantly you kill them, the patrols seem to be everywhere you are etc etc etc etc etc. I got to the boss with some luck and when I got to him, it seemed as an easy fight, only one add, but at halfway of the battle, surprise surprise the respawned patrol attacked me and pulled fourth mob to me also! :D whatta nice place I say. So I decided to wait my friends to come online and boost me this !@#$ing annoying quest.",
            date = "2007-11-05T23:45:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10392#comments:id=179837",
        },
    },
    [10393] = {
        {
            id = 21106,
            score = 0,
            author = "491",
            text = "This is a drop off of Razorsaw at approximately 64.32\n\nOnly one person in my party could loot it at a time, although it was only two of us.. could have been a bug.",
            date = "2007-01-17T17:25:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10393#comments:id=21106",
        },
    },
    [10394] = {
        {
            id = 29315,
            score = 49,
            author = "19387",
            text = "ok let's make it short!\n\nField Marshal Brock - 68,28\nMageddon - 65,31\n\ngo finish it!",
            date = "2007-02-02T06:30:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10394#comments:id=29315",
        },
        {
            id = 53185,
            score = 9,
            author = "29917",
            text = "Very easy quest, Targets are directly behind quest giver.\n\n65,29",
            date = "2007-03-18T13:43:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10394#comments:id=53185",
        },
        {
            id = 182708,
            score = 6,
            author = "vexis58",
            text = "Razorsaw has a crazy respawn rate. I think I could probably kill him 10 times before rounding up enough of the little guys.\n\nOnce, he aggroed on me when I was fighting one of the little guys. I had just killed him, so wasn't expecting it. Killed Razorsaw again right as another add aggroed on me. Before that add was halfway dead, Razorsaw respawned right where I was standing and I had to run for it.\n\nHe patrols the whole camp, so watch out! He can sneak up behind you really easily.",
            date = "2007-11-12T04:42:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10394#comments:id=182708",
        },
        {
            id = 130197,
            score = 5,
            author = "StubMcBean",
            text = "Easiest (but slowest) way to complete this is to kill the four Servants closest to Honor Point and let them respawn. This keeps your back clear to run away if you aggro too many other mobs. Razorsaw wanders in close too and is a pretty easy fight for lvl 62.\nIf you are impatient and go through the camp to kill mobs, watch out for the Fel Canon MK1 (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=22461#00Rzc) on the southern and western edges of the camp - they blend in with the other background stuff and  were firing on me before I knew it. They're not worth taking out either since they only drop junk worth a few silver. You fight these in the next part of the quest chain so why bother now?",
            date = "2007-08-01T02:12:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10394#comments:id=130197",
        },
        {
            id = 325902,
            score = 3,
            author = "Xhougnaamn",
            text = "This is a part of a 12 quest chain which you can start by talking to Force Commander Danath Trollbane (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=16819) in Honor Hold. Here is the whole chain.\n\n¤ The Legion Reborn (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10141)\n¤ The Path of Anguish (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10142)\n¤ Expedition Point (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10143)\n¤ Disrupt Their Reinforcements (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10144)\n¤ Mission: The Murketh and Shaadraz Gateways (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10146)\n¤ Shatter Point (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10340)\n¤ Wing Commander Gryphongar (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10344)\n¤ Mission: The Abyssal Shelf (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10163)\n¤ Go to the Front (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10382)\n» Disruption - Forge Camp: Mageddon (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10394)\n¤ Enemy of my Enemy... (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10396)\n¤ Invasion Point: Annihilator (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10397)",
            date = "2008-07-13T19:00:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10394#comments:id=325902",
        },
    },
    [10395] = {
        {
            id = 21989,
            score = 8,
            author = "13354",
            text = "Dropped by Warbringer Arix'Amal at  53,26",
            date = "2007-01-20T09:20:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10395#comments:id=21989",
        },
        {
            id = 75429,
            score = 8,
            author = "Innervate",
            text = "Got the letter doing \"Go to the front\" chain (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10382). It drops from named NPC you have to kill for the last quest (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10397) and unlocks (can anyone confirmed this?) Overlord (elite: http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10400) from Force Commander Danath Trollbane in Honor Hold.",
            date = "2007-04-30T11:04:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10395#comments:id=75429",
        },
        {
            id = 84302,
            score = 7,
            author = "46362",
            text = "I just got the letter that starts this quest.  It dropped from Warbringer Arix'Amal, as noted by others.\n\nI was not on any of the quests in that area and had not done any of them yet.  There does not apear to be any requirement.  Just go to the spot, kill him, loot.  I got it while at level 58.",
            date = "2007-05-16T22:40:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10395#comments:id=84302",
        },
        {
            id = 136789,
            score = 4,
            author = "Kastaje",
            text = "Turning in The Dark Missive (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10395) unlocks\n\nThe Heart of Darkness (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10399)\nOverlord (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10400)",
            date = "2007-08-13T00:50:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10395#comments:id=136789",
        },
        {
            id = 21619,
            score = 3,
            author = "13105",
            text = "This is dropped off of Warbringer Arix'Amal.",
            date = "2007-01-19T15:34:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10395#comments:id=21619",
        },
    },
    [10396] = {
        {
            id = 42057,
            score = 19,
            author = "26957",
            text = "The cannons have a LOT less HP than the servants do that are working on them. Also, the cannons deal more damage. If you take out the cannon first, its smooth sailing.\n\nAs a rogue, if you are having trouble with these, kill the cannon as fast as you can and then vanish without killing the servant... Amounts to about 1 kill per 5 minutes :p\n\nALSO, they have a 4-5 minute respawn timer while the servants working on them have a 15+ minute respawn timer, so if you are having trouble soloing, just camp 1.",
            date = "2007-02-25T10:55:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10396#comments:id=42057",
        },
        {
            id = 325904,
            score = 10,
            author = "Xhougnaamn",
            text = "This is a part of a 12 quest chain which you can start by talking to Force Commander Danath Trollbane (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=16819) in Honor Hold. Here is the whole chain.\n\n¤ The Legion Reborn (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10141)\n¤ The Path of Anguish (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10142)\n¤ Expedition Point (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10143)\n¤ Disrupt Their Reinforcements (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10144)\n¤ Mission: The Murketh and Shaadraz Gateways (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10146)\n¤ Shatter Point (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10340)\n¤ Wing Commander Gryphongar (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10344)\n¤ Mission: The Abyssal Shelf (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10163)\n¤ Go to the Front (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10382)\n¤ Disruption - Forge Camp: Mageddon (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10394)\n» Enemy of my Enemy... (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10396)\n¤ Invasion Point: Annihilator (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10397)",
            date = "2008-07-13T19:00:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10396#comments:id=325904",
        },
        {
            id = 982849,
            score = 8,
            author = "JamesThePaladin",
            text = "Clearly, Alliance is the bad guys after doing this quest.",
            date = "2010-02-22T12:07:10-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10396#comments:id=982849",
        },
        {
            id = 92733,
            score = 7,
            author = "Enclature",
            text = "Rogues: if you attack the servant and use blade flurry it won't hit the canon. But if you attack the canon and blade flurry it WILL hit the servant. At least in my experience. YMMV.",
            date = "2007-05-28T20:54:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10396#comments:id=92733",
        },
        {
            id = 193743,
            score = 7,
            author = "45143",
            text = "This was a pain and a half to solo with a 60 Fury warrior, as both camps are add city and there is no way to attack one of these with out at least one servant attacking you, if not two. On top of that various other demons spawn rapidly around you and generally make life difficult.",
            date = "2007-11-30T04:05:30-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10396#comments:id=193743",
        },
    },
    [10397] = {
        {
            id = 26002,
            score = 22,
            author = "704",
            text = "There are a lot of mobs patrolling the area, and you can avoid most by staying to the Western side.\n\nArix'Amal (53,26) will drop the Gate Key, which you'll then need to use to shut the gate just a few meters away (53,27).",
            date = "2007-01-27T21:28:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10397#comments:id=26002",
        },
        {
            id = 27365,
            score = 20,
            author = "9160",
            text = "Besides the key, Arix'Amal also drops Burning Legion Missive(It looks like a note/envelope) that starts quest The Dark Missive.",
            date = "2007-01-29T19:57:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10397#comments:id=27365",
        },
        {
            id = 66771,
            score = 15,
            author = "WARBOSZ",
            text = "The Burning Legion Gate is north of Thrallmar - exit to the east and go north past the various demons. It's much easier to get to Warbringer Arix'AmalStick if you stick to the right side (with the mountains - east side) because you can avoid the MKI cannons.\n\nMobs spawn fast and there's lots so don't linger too long.\n\nKill Warbringer Arix'Amal to obtain the Burning Legion Gate Key. He is located behind (north) of the actual Burning Legion Gate. You have to then grab the key and go back to the south side of the Burning Legion Gate (it's the glowing thing in the centre which the other towers are feeding magical energy to.",
            date = "2007-04-13T17:28:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10397#comments:id=66771",
        },
        {
            id = 325905,
            score = 13,
            author = "Xhougnaamn",
            text = "This is a part of a 12 quest chain which you can start by talking to Force Commander Danath Trollbane (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=16819) in Honor Hold. Here is the whole chain.\n\n¤ The Legion Reborn (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10141)\n¤ The Path of Anguish (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10142)\n¤ Expedition Point (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10143)\n¤ Disrupt Their Reinforcements (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10144)\n¤ Mission: The Murketh and Shaadraz Gateways (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10146)\n¤ Shatter Point (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10340)\n¤ Wing Commander Gryphongar (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10344)\n¤ Mission: The Abyssal Shelf (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10163)\n¤ Go to the Front (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10382)\n¤ Disruption - Forge Camp: Mageddon (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10394)\n¤ Enemy of my Enemy... (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10396)\n» Invasion Point: Annihilator (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10397)",
            date = "2008-07-13T19:01:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10397#comments:id=325905",
        },
        {
            id = 106670,
            score = 11,
            author = "45703",
            text = "In case you get lost on the same thing I did; to close the gate in question, you'll need to use the key (right-click on it) on the glowing sphere in the middle of the gate structure. So you never actually activate the whole gate or anything, just the core of it.",
            date = "2007-06-18T19:47:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10397#comments:id=106670",
        },
    },
    [10399] = {
        {
            id = 21638,
            score = 24,
            author = "murakaz",
            text = "You can do this quest along with The Pools of Aggonar (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9426), and get two birds with one stone!",
            date = "2007-01-19T15:57:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10399#comments:id=21638",
        },
        {
            id = 21621,
            score = 19,
            author = "13105",
            text = "The Pools of Aggonar entrance is at 38, 44.",
            date = "2007-01-19T15:38:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10399#comments:id=21621",
        },
        {
            id = 246259,
            score = 5,
            author = "75650",
            text = "These guys have an ability called \"Fel Flames\" that is about a 2-3 second cast. Get a dot off and BACK UP to avoid it. Once they start casting they can rotate around in 360 degrees but cannot move so if you move back you can avoid it. After they are done with Fel Flames they also get off an AOE lightning attack that I do not know the name of. But if you back up for the Fel Flames you won't get hit with that one either!\n\nAlso a little cool thing the quest named \"The Heart of Darkness\" (imho) refers to the book by Joseph Conrad. It would make sense since these pools are kind of like the river in the book.\n\nAnyway fun questing to ya!",
            date = "2008-03-01T15:08:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10399#comments:id=246259",
        },
        {
            id = 21993,
            score = 4,
            author = "13354",
            text = "Yes Pools of Aggonar but further to the back of it so 39, 30.",
            date = "2007-01-20T09:22:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10399#comments:id=21993",
        },
        {
            id = 228128,
            score = 1,
            author = "brock",
            text = "Although this quest only requires level 58, the quest item it is derived from requires level 61 to drop.",
            date = "2008-02-02T03:56:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10399#comments:id=228128",
        },
    },
    [10400] = {
        {
