            text = "The bloodmauls are right below the mountain.  Use the powder to shrink the wolves and they become friendly for a while.",
            date = "2007-01-24T14:51:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10506#comments:id=23787",
        },
    },
    [10507] = {
        {
            id = 1505470,
            score = 206,
            author = "Aths",
            text = "If you're an level 85 (Or higher), like me, who just flew up there and killed him and then suddenly wonder why you only got 1 out 3 parts of the quest, then you need to simply loot the satchel in your inventory.\n\nAt least that worked for me, flew up there, killed him, looted the satchel, and flew back.",
            date = "2011-08-28T15:54:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10507#comments:id=1505470",
        },
        {
            id = 1963073,
            score = 48,
            author = "Ozlem",
            text = "Because it's not written I'm writing a little post about HOW to get this quest. With Heirlooms and other EXP boost doodads this quest is normally skipped because you out level zone so fast and if you're like me and want a item that is a quest reward for completing this quest (like https://www.wowhead.com/item=30375 to complete the enchanted thorium set) trying to find your way to get this quest isn't quite so.... linear.\n\nFirst you need to be aligned with [faction=934], and by that I mean you need to make it official, you need to have completed https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10552. I wanted to rush this so I just started turning in https://www.wowhead.com/item=29739 and hit Honored and the quest lines in Netherstorm never opened up. Once I stopped being a nuff-nuff and finished https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10552 and became \"officially aligned\" the quests needed opened up.\n\nAfter you're affiliated with The Scryers you need to talk to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19468 and https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19469 located in Netherstorm, Area 52 Inn.  You will then need to complete https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10204 and then all quests from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19468 leading up to the completion of https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10330. Once you complete https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10330 and turn it in https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19469 will start giving you the quests needed to lead you up to this quest!\n\nIn order:\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10341\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10202\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10432\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10508\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=10509\nand then finally https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10507!\n\nSo yeah after wasting time flying between Netherstorm and Shattrath City trying to find a way to get this quest I figure someone else out there may be like me one day and hopefully this post will help you out!\n\n(Also I have no idea why but on some wowhead pages there are Alliance symbols next to the first two https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19469 quests, as a horde I was slightly confused with this to begin with but both Horde and Alliance, as long as you're with the Scyers, will be given these quests, it's not alliance only - just FYI)",
            date = "2014-05-04T06:20:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10507#comments:id=1963073",
        },
        {
            id = 143964,
            score = 25,
            author = "Xarlequin",
            text = "36,18 in Netherstorm.",
            date = "2007-08-25T17:29:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10507#comments:id=143964",
        },
        {
            id = 124686,
            score = 22,
            author = "22114",
            text = "Soloable as a shadow priest. Because of the increased damage you also get increased mana regen and health. I can heal to full and maintain mana easily against him while damaging him.\n\nHe will resist a lot. So reapply vampiric embrace as much as possible because it wore out on me sometimes and I almost died. I used two super mana pots and a shadowfiend though I could have done it with just 1 mana pot. The shadowfiend will also get extra damage and your mana bar will fill in just a few hits.\n\nClear the mobs around the throne so you can get maximum fighting space. I only cleared the path leading to the platform, but it didn't work out so well... I eventually ended up on the edge of the island kiting him back and forth. Don't kite him too far at the start or he'll deaggro, just kite him back and forth between his casts. He'll occasionally knock you back which makes things easier (or harder if he knocks you somewhere you don't want to be). As for his anti-magic shield you should be running as soon as he casts that to let some of the time wear off on it, but for the most part you just need to tank his damage for awhile and heal back up with VE.\n\nHere is a video of me doing it:\nhttp://video.google.com/videoplay?docid=7590111643202432132",
            date = "2007-07-21T20:07:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10507#comments:id=124686",
        },
        {
            id = 26238,
            score = 21,
            author = "woyy",
            text = "http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10409 Aldor counterpart here. Very fun fight, the item you use on him makes him take 300% damage.",
            date = "2007-01-28T07:55:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10507#comments:id=26238",
        },
    },
    [10508] = {
        {
            id = 44191,
            score = 46,
            author = "25828",
            text = "Enslavable.\n\nI just enslaved it, cleared the whole camp with him and dismiss him when he's at about 5% hp. Deathcoil shadow bolt and he's dead. Loot.",
            date = "2007-02-28T19:18:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10508#comments:id=44191",
        },
        {
            id = 31134,
            score = 42,
            author = "AzGuL",
            text = "The First and Second Half of Socrethar's Stone drops from level 69 elites with around 30,000 HP. (fear and stunable)\n\nForgemaster Morug: 36, 27\nSilroth: 40, 19",
            date = "2007-02-05T08:12:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10508#comments:id=31134",
        },
        {
            id = 26505,
            score = 24,
            author = "13643",
            text = "This is the Scryer version of this quest. The Aldor version can be found here ( http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10407 )",
            date = "2007-01-28T16:25:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10508#comments:id=26505",
        },
        {
            id = 62913,
            score = 4,
            author = "homiebrah",
            text = "All done as a 70 Demo Lock, solo.\n\nFirst Half\nForgemaster Morug can be found at 37,28.  I cleared the area to the southeast, dropped CoA and Corruption and kited him to the ecodome.  One there, reapplied DoTs, feared him off, and used Drain Life.  Felguard never got below 50% health the whole time.\n\nSecond Half\nSilroth can be found at 41,20.  I cleared the bowl that the demon sits in and used the same strategy as above.  No kiting needed.  Just DoTs, fear, Drain Life, repeat as necessary.\n\nNeither elite is immune to fear, so at least for Locks, this should be easy for a 70.",
            date = "2007-04-06T11:57:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10508#comments:id=62913",
        },
        {
            id = 224998,
            score = 4,
            author = "106886",
            text = "Very, very easy as a 70 BM Hunter.\nMisdirect> Aimed Shot, Distracting Shot on your pet, chain mends, and go to town. Both were very simple tank and spank, and I'm pretty sure my pet never went below 80% on either fight.",
            date = "2008-01-27T09:39:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10508#comments:id=224998",
        },
    },
    [10509] = {
        {
            id = 28648,
            score = 50,
            author = "Minthus",
            text = "Despite the vague quest text, you just need to talk to Voren'thal the Seer in Shattrath City. You do not need to have Socrethar's Teleportation Stone.",
            date = "2007-01-31T23:48:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10509#comments:id=28648",
        },
        {
            id = 949250,
            score = 9,
            author = "empfeix",
            text = "Does not count for the Into the Nether (http://www.wowhead.com/?achievement=1194) achievement oddly enough, but its follow up quest does.",
            date = "2010-01-16T21:49:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10509#comments:id=949250",
        },
        {
            id = 563672,
            score = 2,
            author = "Kirtash",
            text = "Its both alliance and horde quest.",
            date = "2009-01-15T10:52:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10509#comments:id=563672",
        },
        {
            id = 232530,
            score = -4,
