    [10586] = {
        {
            id = 32242,
            score = 103,
            author = "11539",
            text = "Go to the first cave entrance (39,40) where you found Flanti's pack. Make your way over the large bridge and on the left side you'll see a gate where you can use the Deathforge key. Warbringer (69 non-elite demon) is at the end of the smaller cave behind the gate.\n\nSoloed as level 70 frost mage, piece of cake.",
            date = "2007-02-07T12:37:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10586#comments:id=32242",
        },
        {
            id = 33530,
            score = 48,
            author = "Flyv",
            text = "This quest is in the middle of a long chain that for Alliance, starts at \"Besieged!\" (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10562).",
            date = "2007-02-10T09:49:23-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10586#comments:id=33530",
        },
        {
            id = 2300253,
            score = 15,
            author = "Aurleis1",
            text = "Video Guide: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JJ7cAcs9qew\n\n1.  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10586\n•\009Accept the quest, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10586, from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=21471 at coords 40.4, 41.2 (Deathforge).\n•\009Travel north, and enter the Deathforge at coords 40.1, 38.3.\n•\009Follow the passage to coords 37.4, 42.7.\n•\009Open the Heavy Iron Portcullis, and follow the passage to coords 39.0, 46.6.\n•\009Kill https://www.wowhead.com/npc=21287, and loot https://www.wowhead.com/item=30689 from his corpse.\n•\009Exit The Deathforge.\n•\009Travel south, to Wildhammer Stronghold, to coords 39.4, 53.6.\n•\009Turn in the quest to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=21357.",
            date = "2016-01-20T14:21:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10586#comments:id=2300253",
        },
        {
            id = 33596,
            score = 7,
            author = "Flyv",
            text = "This quest is easily stealthable. The locked door is out of aggro range of all mobs if you're level 70, so just sneak up to it, open the door, then restealth. I cleared one warrior and one pathing warlock before killing the Warbringer himself.",
            date = "2007-02-10T13:15:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10586#comments:id=33596",
        },
        {
            id = 66136,
            score = 7,
            author = "23388",
            text = "After killing him, I went north to what seemed to be a fake stone wall. I hovered my mouse over it and saw \"Doodad_BlackRockCellDoor01\"\n\nI wonder where it goes :D\n\n(coords for door are: 39, 45)",
            date = "2007-04-12T16:12:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10586#comments:id=66136",
        },
    },
    [10587] = {
        {
            id = 156125,
            score = 33,
            author = "16691",
            text = "This is the start of the Aldor version of the Book of Fel Names chain.  As well as reputation with your chosen faction, if you complete it you can choose from:\nCeremonial Kris (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31013) (+heal dagger)\nSlayer's Axe (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31010) (2H +str axe)\nSunfury Legguards (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30948) (+AP mail pants)\nHauberk of Karabor (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30933) (+AP leather chest)\nSummoner's Blade (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31002) (+dmg sword)\nWildcaller (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31009) (feral staff)\n\nAs with the Medallion of Karabor (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10707) line, this chain starts different depending on whether you're Aldor (A) or Scryer (S).  All the quests are rated level 70 - though the chain is available at level 68, it sends you to the Shadow Labyrinth (http://www.wowhead.com/?zone=3789) to kill Blackheart (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18667), which you might want to hold off on until level 70.\n\nAldors pick it up from Exarch Onaala (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21860) at the Altar of Sha'tar:\n1. (A) Karabor Training Grounds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10587)\n2. (A) A Necessary Distraction (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10637)\n3. (A) Altruis (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10640)\n\nScryers need to visit Larissa Sunstrike (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21954) at the Sanctum of the Stars:\n1. (S) Karabor Training Grounds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10687)\n2. (S) A Necessary Distraction (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10688)\n3. (S) Altruis (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10689)\n\nHere the chains converge on your old friend Altruis the Sufferer (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18417) in Nagrand.  He gives out three quests that need to be completed (in any order) before you can continue:\n4a. Against the Legion (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10641) - Netherstorm\n4b. Against the Illidari (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10668) - Shadowmoon Valley\n4c. Against All Odds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10669) - Zangarmarsh\nHaving gone around the world killing stuff, you can now return to Altruis and receive:\n5. Illidan's Pupil (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10646)\nwhich leads directly into\n6. The Book of Fel Names (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10649)\n\nNow it's time for a venture into the Shadow Labyrinth to kill Blackheart (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18667)!  Once that's done that and his body has been looted for the book, it's back to Altruis where again the chains diverge depending on your allegiance.\n\nAldor:\n7. (A) Return to the Aldor (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10650) - back to Altar of Sha'tar\n8. (A) Varedis Must Be Stopped (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10651)\n\nScryer:\n7. (S) Return to the Scryers (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10691) - back to Sanctum of Stars\n8. (S) Varedis Must Be Stopped (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10692)\n\nVaredis Must Be Stopped is the final part.  It's a 5-man group quest that sends you to the terrace outside the Black Temple to kill four elites: Varedis (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21178), Netharel (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21164), Theras (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21168) and Alandien (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21171).  Look them up  for co-ordinates and tips on killing them - they're pretty straightforward, really.\n\nWhen they're dead it's a simple matter of returning to the questgiver to choose a prize.",
            date = "2007-09-21T09:46:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10587#comments:id=156125",
        },
        {
            id = 828622,
            score = 11,
            author = "Alamandaros",
            text = "Would anyone know why I'm unable to grab this quest from her? I'm friendly with Aldor, yet there's no quest being offered.",
            date = "2009-08-31T22:55:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10587#comments:id=828622",
        },
        {
            id = 73671,
            score = 9,
            author = "35629",
            text = "As a feral druid, I simply cast Faerie Fire (Feral) on one Supplicant in a pair.\n\nOnce they reach 49% they will cease their duel and aggro you.\n\nExtremely easy to kill them after that.\n\nIf you have any sort of ability that puts you on their aggro list but doesn't do (enough) damage to aggro them off their sparring partner, cast it on them and just wait for their duel to finish.\n\nWhen one of the pair is low on HP and uses Evasion (\"Demon Hunter Supplicant begins intensely dodging incoming attacks\"), just switch to the other one. Once that one Evades, the buff should have worn off on the first one.",
            date = "2007-04-27T04:36:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10587#comments:id=73671",
        },
        {
            id = 50183,
            score = 6,
            author = "32804",
            text = "The supplicants cast evasion on themselves at about 20% health, so they are very tough for a melee to kill past that point.  The initiates are squishy and can be easily killed.\n\nEverything in the area seems to be able to see through stealth.",
            date = "2007-03-12T16:46:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10587#comments:id=50183",
        },
        {
            id = 25192,
            score = 4,
            author = "16133",
            text = "66,46   go to the top of the ramp until you get to the temple.  Theyre all around there. Average drop rate",
            date = "2007-01-26T16:05:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10587#comments:id=25192",
        },
    },
    [10588] = {
        {
            id = 30553,
            score = 468,
            author = "marskid2",
            text = "The Cipher of Damnation is an extremely long quest line in Shadowmoon Valley.\n\"*\" Indicates quests with rewards.\n\nQuest Line\n1[A] - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10680 - \"The Hand of Gul'Dan\"\n1[H] - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10681 - \"The Hand of Gul'Dan\"\n2 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10458 - \"Enraged Spirits of Fire and Earth\"\n3 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10480 - \"Enraged Spirits of Water\"\n4* - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10480 - \"Enraged Spirits of Air\"\n5 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10513 - \"Oronok Torn-Heart\"\n6* - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10514 - \"I Was A Lot Of Things...\" - Most annoying quest ever implemented in World of Warcraft.\n7 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10515 - \"A Lesson Learned\"\n8 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10519 - \"The Cipher of Damnation - Truth and History\"\n\nAt this point, the quests diverge into three separate lines (which can be done in any order) for each of Oronok's three sons who will in turn help you obtain the three Fragments of Damnation.\n\nQuest Line I - First Fragment of Damnation\n1 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10521 - \"Grom'tor, Son of Oronok\"\n2 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10522 - \"The Cipher of Damnation - Grom'tor's Charge\"\n3* - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10523 - \"The Cipher of Damnation - The First Fragment Recovered\"\n\nQuest Line II - Second Fragment of Damnation\n1 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10527 \"Ar'tor, Son of Oronok\"\n2 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10528 - \"Demonic Crystal Prisons\"\n3 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10537 - \"Lohn'goron, Bow of the Torn-heart\"\n4 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10540 - \"The Cipher of Damnation - Ar'tor's Charge\"\n5* - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10541 - \"The Cipher of Damnation - The Second Fragment Recovered\"\n\nQuest Line III - Third Fragment of Damnation\n1 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10546 \"Borak, Son of Oronok\"\n2 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10547 - \"Of Thistleheads and Eggs...\"\n3 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10550 - \"The Bundle of Bloodthistle\"\n4 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10570 - \"To Catch A Thistlehead\"\n5 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10576 - \"The Shadowmoon Shuffle\"\n6 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10577 - \"What Illidan Wants, Illidan Gets...\"\n7 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10578 - \"The Cipher of Damnation - Borak's Charge\"\n8* - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10579 \"The Cipher of Damnation - The Third Fragment Recovered\"\n\nAfter completing the quests for the three Fragments of Damnation, the lines converge and you need to kill one last boss.\nFinal* - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10588 - \"The Cipher of Damnation\"\n\nRewards:\n\nEveryone gets http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31074 - Fire Resist Neck\n\nChoose one of the following:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31036 - Caster Staff\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31038 - Healer Staff\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31062 - Paladin/Shaman 2H Axe\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31071 - Tanking 1H Axe\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31072 - Bow\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31073 - Melee Dagger\n\nAfter completing the quest, you will get a message in the mail from Khadgar.  If you go to Shattrath, he will tell you to talk to A'Dal, who unlocks the the three Trials.",
            date = "2007-02-04T11:56:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10588#comments:id=30553",
        },
        {
            id = 24875,
            score = 287,
            author = "Combine",
            text = "You start the quest near 42,45.\n\n1. Use totems on the fire and earth elementals surrounding the immediate area.\n2. Use totems on air elementals near Netherwing Fields. 62,57\n3. Use totems on water elementals near 47,22\n\nThen you go up north to talk to the NPC.  54,23\n\nHe then asks you to use a whistle on whipper tubers.  Note:  A boar must be alive and near for it to work.  They tubers are around 52,20\n\nThen He asks you to destroy some eggs,  They are just north of him down the cliff.\n\nOnce you have done those two quests he will ask you to find his 3 Sons.\n\nThe sons are located...\n\nArtor: 30,50\nWill ask you to slay the main mistress which is up the stairs and to the right.  Then you will have to grind those demons to find a quest item.  Then you will have to escort a NPC up the hill.  Once up the hill the NPC will summon a non elite you must kill.   Loot that mob and your 1/3rd done.\n\nGromtor: 45,24\nTalk to him and he will ask you to find something.  The item you need is locked randomly in a chest that the naga hold.  Go kill some naga and they will randomly drop keys.  Open the chests and eventually youll get the quest item.\n\nBorak: 47,57\nAsks you to do a multitude of things.  The confusing ones involve finding an egg.  Which there are some located in the bird people village just near the NPC.  It will take quite some tries to find the correct one.  He should then ask you to bring it to someone in Shattarah.\nAlso you will end up having to kill some blood elves Eclipse point for armor scraps.  Then you will use a Blood ELf disguise to infiltrate the camp.  Talk to the big guy at the back of camp.  Careful the firehawk beasts see threw the disguise and if you get knocked out of it you must return to the SOn to get a new costume.\n\nThen he will ask you to kill an Elite.  This elite is 61 and can be killed with a tank, healer, and dps.  Once you kill this Dual Thunderfury badass you fight his pet.  Although the item you need is on the guy.\n\nAfter killing this guy return to the son.  Then return with all 3 of the quests completed to the father at 54,23.\nRewards from this part are:\n\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=30951\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=30939\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=30967\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=30962\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=30925\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=30944\n\nHe will then tell you to fight the big green golemagg.\n\nUsing the stone of damnation head to 45,46 (the place you started with the purple aura).  Using the stone at the altar will spawn the boss, and the 3 Sons will fly in to help.  Talk to them when ready and they will begin the fight.  NOTE: These 3 sons will tank the boss  pretty well as long as you dont pull aggro to early.  The boss is a straight forward fight.  You basically need to do 300k damage in a few minutes before the NPC's die, otherwise you'll end up tanking.  Can be done with a decent 5man group.\n\nRewards from killing this guy are pretty sweet...\n\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31073\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31036\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31038\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31062\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31072\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31071\n\nPlus you also get a fire res neck:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31074\n\nI have only gotten this far, according to V head back to the father in the north and you start the key quest.\n\n--have fun.",
            date = "2007-01-26T07:11:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10588#comments:id=24875",
        },
        {
            id = 1277721,
            score = 173,
            author = "docallens",
            text = "I just solo'd this is a level 70 balance druid.  I, too, was confused as to why I could not attack the summon monster.  Then I realized I had to talk to the 3 NPCs behind me to tell them I was ready to go.  During the fight, the NPCs held aggro the whole time, despite my almost constant casting.  They died by the time Cyrukh the Firelord had roughly 20k health, but I easily finished him off.  Note: even though the NPCs died, I could still complete the quest just fine.",
            date = "2011-01-04T20:48:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10588#comments:id=1277721",
        },
        {
            id = 2189492,
            score = 79,
            author = "lizardo",
            text = "If you are having trouble with this quest being \"bugged\". (It's just not very well scripted)\nTry these steps:\n\n-Cyrukh must be despawned. (Much of the time players summon him then think the quest is bugged and then leave him there) You must wait around 10 minutes for him to despawn and make sure nobody else uses the item to summon him during this time.\n\n-Once everything is clear, and reset. Use the item to summon.\n\n-Gul'dan will summon him, and then after a few seconds the brothers will come in on flying mounts. (this is where people mess it up) You must wait for them to land, and then you have to talk to the middle one to start the encounter, otherwise Cyrukh will not be attackable.\n\n-They will run up the side of the hill to the right (make sure you kill the earth spirit there so they aren't stopped) Once they get up there, Cyrukh will face them and become attackable.\n\n-Quest will complete, enjoy",
            date = "2015-06-01T16:08:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10588#comments:id=2189492",
        },
        {
            id = 20152,
            score = 75,
            author = "11877",
            text = "Quest rewards:\n\nChoose from:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31073\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31036\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31038\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31062\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31072\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31071\n\nPlus you also get a fire res neck:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31074",
            date = "2007-01-11T03:39:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10588#comments:id=20152",
        },
    },
    [10589] = {
