            text = "This quest title might be another one of Blizzard's real life references. It sounds like the title of a book I was forced to read once, Zen and the Art of Motorcycle Maintenance.",
            date = "2007-06-21T10:20:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10611#comments:id=108573",
        },
        {
            id = 282994,
            score = 4,
            author = "143861",
            text = "He's a level 69 Undead. Confirmed - he's at the bottom of the hill where the quest giver stands and his chest is just to the right of him by the hill.",
            date = "2008-05-05T18:07:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10611#comments:id=282994",
        },
        {
            id = 232860,
            score = 2,
            author = "31177",
            text = "Man this quest is annoying as a restro shaman solo.  I keep getting 3 things aggroe'd on me at once and i cant even get My earth elemental to tank enough to get the chest open'd",
            date = "2008-02-10T16:28:05-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10611#comments:id=232860",
        },
    },
    [10612] = {
        {
            id = 33855,
            score = 56,
            author = "20659",
            text = "I completed this quest within the time given for it (5 minutes) and when i returned, the quest giver and the guards nearby were gone, so i failed the quest. If this happens, run down the slope to the point when the sky turns purple and run back up. Theyll be there. Also, as a hunter, you can't have your pet out or the control panel will not work.",
            date = "2007-02-11T01:18:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10612#comments:id=33855",
        },
        {
            id = 105594,
            score = 27,
            author = "60815",
            text = "This quest confused me a bit at first until I got the hang of it.\n\nThe  controls are three little boxes just down the hill from the quest giver.  Click on one and you will become the machine.\n\nOne time the control bar never showed up for me - the other time it did.  Don't know if this is a known issue or not.\n\nWalk down the stairs/ramp and there will be more infernals to kill.  Right click on the buff to get  back to the control box and then go up the hill to turn in quest.",
            date = "2007-06-16T18:20:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10612#comments:id=105594",
        },
        {
            id = 1378109,
            score = 26,
            author = "733706",
            text = "Fun?  This has got to be one of the most irritating quests I have come across so far.    It makes me wonder who tested this crap. First of all, as others have mentioned, clicking on the control consoles didn't always work.  I was only able to use the one on the right.\n\nSecond, I had a great deal of difficulty against the 70 elite mobs who were wacking the crap out of the reaver while the weapons I had did very little against them. This was worsened by the irritatingly slow cool-down times of the stuff I had to work with.\n\nThird, I started to run out of little guys to kill! The big mobs, that I couldn't kill, followed me around wacking the crap out of me while I tried to find more of the little guys I was supposed to be after.\n\nThe questgiver tells you that you have 5 minutes to kill 60 of the mobs before your reaver dies.  This is not true.  If it dies, you can get another one and continue with the quest, but the little controller that shows you how much time you have left resets to 5 minutes, but you no longer have five minutes, you are still operating with the original amount of time, which you can no longer see. If you complete the quest, you must jump out of the reaver to turn it in.  It took me over 10 times to complete this quest. Wrote a ticket.",
            date = "2011-03-28T06:07:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10612#comments:id=1378109",
        },
        {
            id = 51897,
            score = 25,
            author = "22320",
            text = "To complete the quest you need to remove the buff from your character to give up control of the reaver.\n\nAlso, if for some reason you have low health, do not start this quest before healing. The quest was bugged (maybe it's intentional) and 2-3 mobs will run up the hill and attack your character while you control the reaver. I repeated this 2 more times to be sure, and I was attacked each time.\n\nThis bug occured March 16, 2007 for those who didn't check the time stamp.",
            date = "2007-03-16T02:02:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10612#comments:id=51897",
        },
        {
            id = 63011,
            score = 23,
            author = "25228",
            text = "If you die : the teleporter can still be used as a ghost to get back to your body! Otherwise there seems to be no path.",
            date = "2007-04-06T17:10:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10612#comments:id=63011",
        },
    },
    [10613] = {
        {
            id = 28200,
            score = 98,
            author = "nura",
            text = "If you're a warlock and are having trouble taking the control, try dismissing your pet, that worked for me, and the other warlock i did it with :)",
            date = "2007-01-31T09:50:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10613#comments:id=28200",
        },
        {
            id = 29585,
            score = 63,
            author = "3217",
            text = "After accepting the Q, walk down the slope and you will see 3 Fel reaver control consoles. Click on 1 of them to control a Fel reaver then use the first ability after the attack key to destroy the elementals. Remember that you have to destroy 60 of them and return in 5 mins, not just killing 60 of them in 5 mins. I killed 60 of them in 4 minutes, but then i played around with the fel reaver and failed the Q :(",
            date = "2007-02-02T17:35:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10613#comments:id=29585",
        },
        {
            id = 150067,
            score = 28,
            author = "84457",
            text = "The fel reaver sentinel which you're controlling has 4 abilities, besides the usual Attack command (sorry I forgot their names):\n\n1. Launches a salvo of missiles that destroy multiple infernals. No target required. From what I remember, this is the only ability to destroy infernals.\n2. Fires something which resembles a railgun on the chosen target. Also damages anything between you and the target.\n3. AOE stun that does great damage. Great for killing trash mobs.\n4. Speed boost.\n\nTip: Run around the area quickly, and use the first ability as often as you could while you're among a bunch of infernals. When there are too many mobs on you, use the AOE stun then use railgun on the furtherest mob for maximum effect.\n\nSometimes mobs will go directly after you and you lose control of the fel reaver. RUN. Run towards the questgiver and the guards will take one or two off you, but you have to fight the rest. Pray none of them are elites. After killing the mobs you may continue with the quest.",
            date = "2007-09-06T23:01:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10613#comments:id=150067",
        },
        {
            id = 29261,
            score = 27,
            author = "11612",
            text = "Very fun quest! You must dismiss your pet if you are a hunter or warlock.\n\nThis quest gives you a felreaver to control as your pet! It is very fun, but you can get agro on yourself and you may die. If you do just run back and use the transporter and you can get back to your body",
            date = "2007-02-02T02:07:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10613#comments:id=29261",
        },
        {
            id = 1729915,
            score = 19,
            author = "960163",
            text = "I'm on patch 5.0.5 - Mists of Panderia.\n\nYou may recall that the quest begins by telling us that the only way to the quest area is via the teleporter.\n\nMy 67 Undead DK died while doing this quest and although other comments here indicated that the teleporter (@26,35) works while you're in ghost form (dead), that seems not to work anymore.\n\nI have tried running every which way -- in ghost form -- to find a path back to my body but so far it seems that there is no path to be found (which agrees with the original premise of the quest: the only way is to teleport).\n\nI feel like I have no choice but to take rez sickness in order to use the teleporter.\n\nI. Am. Bummed.\n\nIf anyone has better insight about how to recover your corpse in the quest area, please do share here. I spent too much time trying to find my way to my corpse and maybe some tips here will save others a lot of wasted time doing the same.\n\n(Edited to add teleporter coordinates, confirming that I was at the correct one).",
            date = "2012-10-03T11:10:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10613#comments:id=1729915",
        },
    },
