    [10626] = {
        {
            id = 40346,
            score = 53,
            author = "marskid2",
            text = "The Illidari-Bane questline is a series of quests that leads to some cool anti-demon weapons.  It involves entering many level-70 instances, so you probably want to do the prerequisites before then.  David Wayne is also rumored to be Mograine of the Ashbringer.\n\nQuest Line\n1 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10621 - Illidari-Bane Shard - Drops from Overseer Ripsaw.\n2 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10626 - Capture the Weapons - Soloable as a warlock with banish.\n3[A] - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10662 - The Hermit Smith\n3[H] - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10663 - The Hermit Smith\n4 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10664 - Additional Materials\n\nAfter returning Additional Materials, he offers you two quests which can be completed in any order.\n5 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10665 - Fresh From the Mechanar - The Mechanar in Tempest Keep\n6 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10666 - The Lexicon Demonica - Shadow Labyrinth in Auchindoun\n\nAfter returning both of these quests, he offers you the second pair which can be completed in any order.\n7 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10670 - Tear of the Earthmother - Shattered Halls in Hellfire Citadel\n8 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10667 - Underworld Loam - The Steamvault in Coilfang Reservoir\n\nAfter finishing all these, you can get your new weapon!\n9 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10676 - Bane of the Illidari\n10 - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10679 - Quenching the Blade\n\nThe rewards are:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=30788 - Melee 1H Sword\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=30789 - Melee 2H Sword\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=30787 - Caster Dagger\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31745 - Melee Dagger\n\nCombined with the http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30756 that started the quest chain, you will have a lot of extra attack power or spell damage versus demons.",
            date = "2007-02-22T06:26:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10626#comments:id=40346",
        },
        {
            id = 42201,
            score = 23,
            author = "fletch",
            text = "you can find Makazradon at 22,30\nMorgoron at 23,41\n\nhe walks around so just fly/run and find them.",
            date = "2007-02-25T15:40:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10626#comments:id=42201",
        },
        {
            id = 5669952,
            score = 20,
            author = "jcam",
            text = "If you've come here wondering if the coordinates have changed or why you can't find either of them - the circles are in the right place, but the respawn time is longer than it should be. Either I am very unlucky, or these have respawn times of at least 15 minutes.",
            date = "2023-08-20T19:13:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10626#comments:id=5669952",
        },
        {
            id = 189769,
            score = 6,
            author = "53308",
            text = "both are immune to enslaving, mak is immune to fear and banish as well.  mor is not immune to banish, didnt try fear.\n\nedit: this was as of 11-23-07, patch 2.3",
            date = "2007-11-23T03:09:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10626#comments:id=189769",
        },
        {
            id = 219997,
            score = 5,
            author = "43121",
            text = "As of yesterday, both these are immune to Enslaving and Fear as I discovered!\n\nIt pays to read comments to the end, especially since Blizzard have changed so much in 2.3 patch",
            date = "2008-01-18T04:01:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10626#comments:id=219997",
        },
    },
    [10627] = {
        {
            id = 40637,
            score = 23,
            author = "25550",
            text = "Morgroron is around 24,40.\n\nMakazradon walks from 21,36 to 25,35. Make a /target Makazradon macro it'll make it easier to spot him.\n\nx)",
            date = "2007-02-22T15:54:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10627#comments:id=40637",
        },
        {
            id = 145898,
            score = 14,
            author = "83130",
            text = "As a caster you can try to kite Morgroron at that place:\nhttp://img249.imageshack.us/img249/5439/kiteii4.jpg\n\nHe can only walk over the ramp. :)\n(Worked quite good for me with mindflay)",
            date = "2007-08-29T08:26:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10627#comments:id=145898",
        },
        {
            id = 69857,
            score = 10,
            author = "44705",
            text = "Just soloed as holy paladin. Both are annoying to melee but can be doable if you can self-heal. I didn't have any problem with adds at all, flew in there and killed 1 add at each spot before pulling the elites.\n\nMorgroron: 23.6, 38.3 - This is within pull range of a spot where he paus in his small circular patrol. A terrorfiend (watch his fear) stand at this spot. Kill him, pull Mor, stand with back against the wall for Mor's knockbacks.\n\nMakazradon: 20.8, 33.6 - This is as far west as he patrols, a wrathwalker stand on a small hill here. Kill him, pull Mak when he walks by. There's also a nice spot far east, near the road (around 26.34), depends where you find him on his route.\n\nYou want a little room when you chose to melee these guys. They use an AoE rain which deals alot of dmg, espec when you have the debuff that deals extra dmg from magic. This can be avoided by moving around them in a circle, don't have to clear mobs. Mor has a knockback tho, the wall helps. Neither has very much hp so I bet you can just nuke them down fast as well.",
            date = "2007-04-19T22:52:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10627#comments:id=69857",
        },
        {
            id = 39332,
            score = 6,
            author = "stylewalker",
            text = "Morgroron is immune to all slowing and fear effects. He can however be kited anyway by a warlock that keep's dots up. Did it solo at lvl 69, affli lock.",
            date = "2007-02-20T12:31:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10627#comments:id=39332",
        },
        {
            id = 44051,
            score = 6,
            author = "27951",
            text = "I tried soloing Mor in bear form; maybe I'm just a weakling, but I couldn't do it.  So i put on my max +int gear and went kiting.  I just made sure they both had moonfire on them the whole time, and brought them down to Shadowmoon Village, where the guards eat them up good.  Only problems I had was stray mobs on me (it's a good idea to clear some first, for an easier kite path), an alliance ganker, and them evade bugging (gotta attack 'em every 5-10 seconds).  Pretty simple for anyone that has some sort of ranged attack!",
            date = "2007-02-28T14:49:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10627#comments:id=44051",
        },
    },
    [10628] = {
        {
            id = 38597,
            score = 86,
            author = "16691",
            text = "The process of attunement to the Black Temple begins in Shadowmoon Valley with a very long quest chain that requires trips to the Arcatraz, Serpentshrine Cavern, Mount Hyjal and finally the doorstep of the Black Temple itself.  Even if you're not planning on raiding just yet, the chain does offer some nice blue rewards half way through.  It starts differently depending on whether you're Aldor (A) or Scryer (S):\n\nAldors pick up the line from Anchorite Ceyla (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21402) in the Altar of Sha'tar:\n1. (A) [70] Tablets of Baa'ri (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10568)\n2. (A) [70] Oronu the Elder (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10571)\n3. (A) [70] The Ashtongue Corruptors (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10574)\n4. (A) [70] The Warden's Cage (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10575)\n\nScyers get it from Arcanist Thelis (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21955) at the Sanctum of Stars:\n1. (S) [70] Tablets of Baa'ri (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10683)\n2. (S) [70] Oronu the Elder (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10684)\n3. (S) [70] The Ashtongue Corruptors (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10685)\n4. (S) [70] The Warden's Cage (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10686)\n\nAt this point the chains converge for both factions:\n5. [70] Proof of Allegiance (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10622)\n6. [70] Akama (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10628)\n7. [70] Seer Udalo (Dungeon) (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10705)\n\nHere, you have to venture into the Arcatraz (which requires a Rogue with 350 lockpicking or somebody to open the door who's completed the Arcatraz Key chain (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10262), which requires trips to the Mechanar and the Botanica respectively) to the room just before the final boss.  Sadly it's impossible to solo-stealth to.  Finding Udalo leads to:\n\nTalk to Akama:\n8. [70] A Mysterious Portent (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10706)\nKill waves of nonelites, 3 elites and a boss (5-man) on a terrace outside the Black Temple:\n9. [70] The Ata'mal Terrace (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10707)\nFinally, deliver the medallion to A'dal in Shattrath City:\n10. [70] Akama's Promise (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10708)\n\nThe chain ends here, and you're granted a choice of rewards:\nAkama's Sash (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30932) (cloth DPS belt)\nBloodwarder's Rifle (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31000) (gun)\nSpellbreaker's Buckler (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30984) (spelldamage shield)\nAshtongue Blade (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30999) (phsyical DPS dagger)\nVerdant Gloves (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30943) (feral leather gloves)\nStaff of the Ashtongue Deathsworn (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31417) (healing staff)\nHowever, if you now go into Serpentshrine Cavern (http://www.wowhead.com/?zone=3607) and kill Karathress (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21214), you'll be able to talk to Seer Olum (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=22820) who'll continue the quest chain for you:\n\n1. [70] The Secret Compromised (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10944)\nGo back to Warden's Cage in SMV and talk to Akama (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21700).\n2. [70R] Ruse of the Ashtongue (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10946)\nUsing the Ashtongue Cowl (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31946) provided, kill Al'ar (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=19514) in Tempest Keep (http://www.wowhead.com/?zone=3842) while disguised as a member of the Deathsworn.\n3. [70R] An Artifact From the Past (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10947)\nYou need to be attuned to Mount Hyjal (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10445) for this.  Simply kill Rage Winterchill (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=17767) and loot his phylactery (what is it with liches and their phylacteries?), then deliver it to Akama...\n4. [70R] The Hostage Soul (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10948)\n...then return to Ad'al (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18481) in Shattrath City...\n5. [70R] Entry Into the Black Temple (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10949)\n...then go back to Shadowmoon and talk to Xi'ri (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18528) on the road leading to the Black Temple.  He'll ask you to help with\n6. [70] A Distraction for Akama (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10985)\n...but once you tell Xi'ri you're ready (talk to him after accepting the quest), you can watch a scripted sequence that you do not actually have to help with in any way.  After this is finished, talk to Xi'ri again for your Medallion of Karabor (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=32649)) and the completion of Black Temple attunement.  Congratulations, you can now waltz in to Illidan's latest bachelor pad!\n\nBut before you go, the chain continues from Xi'ri with:\n7. [70R] Seek Out the Ashtongue (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10958)\nTime to start exploring the Black Temple (http://www.wowhead.com/?zone=3959)!  When you find the Deathsworn, they'll give you\n2. [70R] Redemption of the Ashtongue (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10957)\n...which requires you to kill the Shade of Akama (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=22841).  Finally you're given\n3. [70R] The Fall of the Betrayer (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10959)\nYup, kill Illidan (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=22917).  No problem.  Then you're done.",
            date = "2007-02-19T08:15:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10628#comments:id=38597",
        },
        {
            id = 813945,
            score = 12,
            author = "DuBzY",
            text = "you go down the tunnel from the quest giver then turn right when u see water around the corner. get into the water and swim under the wall!",
            date = "2009-08-16T21:02:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10628#comments:id=813945",
        },
        {
            id = 27415,
            score = 10,
            author = "Kyrra",
            text = "If you see Vagath (a Deathguard type creature) with 2 bodyguards in the same room as Akama, then you cannot talk with Akama.  I sat around for about 5 minutes and the demons stayed around.\n\nI came back 3 hours later, Vagath was gone and I was able to talk with Akama and complete the quest.",
            date = "2007-01-29T22:09:51-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10628#comments:id=27415",
        },
        {
            id = 55256,
