        },
    },
    [10637] = {
        {
            id = 24515,
            score = 105,
            author = "12909",
            text = "Kill Warlocks in the area, not neccessarily the ones fighting Azaloth, until you get a http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30811 (Scroll of Demonic Unbanishing). Use the scroll on Azaloth.",
            date = "2007-01-25T15:50:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10637#comments:id=24515",
        },
        {
            id = 141559,
            score = 38,
            author = "61749",
            text = "Two things to add:\n\nThe Warlocks that are summoning Azaloth DO drop the scroll.  (i actually found killing the 6 or so Warlocks in this area and then waiting for them to respawn the easiest way to get the scroll).\n\nSecond, I found out the hard way that if you have killed all the Warlocks summoning him, he will not have anything to attack, except you.  I died before the elite demon hunter could show up.  If you've killed them all it might be worth waiting for some of the warlocks to respawn in order to see the whole show and avoid death.",
            date = "2007-08-21T05:18:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10637#comments:id=141559",
        },
        {
            id = 27626,
            score = 33,
            author = "Sizzla",
            text = "Location 69, 51",
            date = "2007-01-30T06:59:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10637#comments:id=27626",
        },
        {
            id = 163710,
            score = 25,
            author = "92055",
            text = "You can also lvl ranged weps on him when hes banished",
            date = "2007-10-06T11:14:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10637#comments:id=163710",
        },
        {
            id = 38753,
            score = 15,
            author = "Dianora",
            text = "The scroll drops off both warlock and summoner.  You DO NOT have to kill any of the warlock next to Azaloth.  Hell, I just landed from the air and activate the scroll, and walk away.  fly out and look at the firework.",
            date = "2007-02-19T14:46:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10637#comments:id=38753",
        },
    },
    [10639] = {
        {
            id = 38576,
            score = 205,
            author = "16691",
            text = "This chain begins differently depending on whether you're Alliance (A) or Horde (H):\n\nAlliance - starts in Wildhammer Stronghold from Zorus the Judicator (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21774):\n1. (A) [69] A Ghost in the Machine (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10642)\n2. (A) [69] Harbingers of Shadowmoon (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10643)\n3. (A) [70] Teron Gorefiend - Lore and Legend (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10644)\n\nHorde - starts in Shadowmoon Village from Chief Apothecary Hildagard (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21772):\n1. (H) [69] A Haunted History (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10624)\n2. (H) [69] Spectrecles (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10625)\n3. (H) [70] Teron Gorefiend - Lore and Legend (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10633)\n\nAt this point the chain splits into three parts which can be done in any order (and by both factions):\n4a. [70] Divination: Gorefiend's Cloak (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10635)\n4b. [70] Divination: Gorefiend's Truncheon [2 players] (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10636)\n4c. [70] Divination: Gorefiend's Armor [5 players] (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10634)\n\nAfter collected Gorefiend's stuff and returned it to the spirit (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21797), you will get:\n5. (A) [70] Teron Gorefiend, I am... (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10645)\n5. (H) [70] Teron Gorefiend, I am... (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10639)\n\nFor this final quest, Gorefiend becomes your \"pet\" and you control him using a pet bar.  Having used him to kill Karsius, you return to Zorus or Hildagard to claim your reward.  Choose from:\nEvoker's Helmet of Second Sight (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31104) (cloth DPS headpiece)\nStealther's Helmet of Second Sight (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31109) (leather melee headpiece)\nDruidic Helmet of Second Sight (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31110) (leather magical headpiece)\nStalker's Helmet of Second Sight (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31106) (mail +AP headpiece)\nShamanistic Helmet of Second Sight (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31107) (mail +dmg headpiece)\nOverlord's Helmet of Second Sight (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31105) (plate DPS headpiece)\n\nEdit: converted to new tag format (http://www.wowhead.com/?help=comment-formatting) to fix URL overload problem.",
            date = "2007-02-19T07:47:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10639#comments:id=38576",
        },
        {
            id = 97612,
            score = 146,
            author = "40710",
            text = "Be sure to dismount or you won't be able to attack",
            date = "2007-06-03T20:38:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10639#comments:id=97612",
        },
        {
            id = 132959,
            score = 91,
            author = "4361",
            text = "Took a few tries, but here's what worked best for me (and my group):\n\n1. Start with the AoE/DoT spell.\n2. Follow immediately with the lifesteal spell.\n3. Use Unholy Armor and lifesteal spell everytime they become available.\n4. Done.\n\nI found that aside from opening the fight the AoE/DoT costs too much time. And I recommend using the lifesteal spell right at the beginning for a reason: not to heal yourself, but to do a good deal of damage.\n\nIf you lose the fight, simply abandon the quest and retake it.\n\nGood luck!\n\n(If you found my comment useful, please rate it. Thank you.)",
            date = "2007-08-06T03:42:12-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10639#comments:id=132959",
        },
        {
            id = 1597290,
            score = 47,
            author = "641887",
            text = "I just recently found out about a bug which has yet to be mentioned here\n\nProblem: If you have Karsius the Watcher targeted before you pull, you will bug out making the NPC simply impossible to kill\n\nSolution: After the pull, target the elemental behind Karsius, then Re-target Karsius and start attacking again.\n\nI wasn't able to finish this quest until I found out about the bug and tried the solution, so hopefully this helps those in need.\n\nGood luck!",
            date = "2011-12-16T12:25:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10639#comments:id=1597290",
        },
        {
            id = 53282,
            score = 42,
            author = "23503",
            text = "Realize that when you accept this quest it will start in about 5-10 seconds. Just enough time to mount and fly away (as I did not realize lol) so then it whips ya off your mount and back to the spot where you begin fight. When its over it put you back where you were... in my case mid-air with no mount. *grin*",
            date = "2007-03-18T16:48:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10639#comments:id=53282",
        },
    },
    [10640] = {
        {
            id = 156127,
            score = 89,
            author = "16691",
            text = "This is part of the Aldor version of the Book of Fel Names chain.  As well as reputation with your chosen faction, if you complete it you can choose from:\nCeremonial Kris (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31013) (+heal dagger)\nSlayer's Axe (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31010) (2H +str axe)\nSunfury Legguards (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30948) (+AP mail pants)\nHauberk of Karabor (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30933) (+AP leather chest)\nSummoner's Blade (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31002) (+dmg sword)\nWildcaller (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31009) (feral staff)\n\nAs with the Medallion of Karabor (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10707) line, this chain starts different depending on whether you're Aldor (A) or Scryer (S).  All the quests are rated level 70 - though the chain is available at level 68, it sends you to the Shadow Labyrinth (http://www.wowhead.com/?zone=3789) to kill Blackheart (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18667), which you might want to hold off on until level 70.\n\nAldors pick it up from Exarch Onaala (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21860) at the Altar of Sha'tar:\n1. (A) Karabor Training Grounds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10587)\n2. (A) A Necessary Distraction (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10637)\n3. (A) Altruis (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10640)\n\nScryers need to visit Larissa Sunstrike (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21954) at the Sanctum of the Stars:\n1. (S) Karabor Training Grounds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10687)\n2. (S) A Necessary Distraction (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10688)\n3. (S) Altruis (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10689)\n\nHere the chains converge on your old friend Altruis the Sufferer (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18417) in Nagrand.  He gives out three quests that need to be completed (in any order) before you can continue:\n4a. Against the Legion (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10641) - Netherstorm\n4b. Against the Illidari (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10668) - Shadowmoon Valley\n4c. Against All Odds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10669) - Zangarmarsh\nHaving gone around the world killing stuff, you can now return to Altruis and receive:\n5. Illidan's Pupil (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10646)\nwhich leads directly into\n6. The Book of Fel Names (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10649)\n\nNow it's time for a venture into the Shadow Labyrinth to kill Blackheart (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18667)!  Once that's done that and his body has been looted for the book, it's back to Altruis where again the chains diverge depending on your allegiance.\n\nAldor:\n7. (A) Return to the Aldor (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10650) - back to Altar of Sha'tar\n8. (A) Varedis Must Be Stopped (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10651)\n\nScryer:\n7. (S) Return to the Scryers (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10691) - back to Sanctum of Stars\n8. (S) Varedis Must Be Stopped (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10692)\n\nVaredis Must Be Stopped is the final part.  It's a 5-man group quest that sends you to the terrace outside the Black Temple to kill four elites: Varedis (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21178), Netharel (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21164), Theras (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21168) and Alandien (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21171).  Look them up  for co-ordinates and tips on killing them - they're pretty straightforward, really.\n\nWhen they're dead it's a simple matter of returning to the questgiver to choose a prize.",
            date = "2007-09-21T09:48:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10640#comments:id=156127",
        },
        {
            id = 667838,
            score = 31,
            author = "dremex",
            text = "Turning in this quest and the following three helped me complete my Nagrand Slam (http://www.wowhead.com/?achievement=1273) achievement.",
            date = "2009-04-06T15:04:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10640#comments:id=667838",
        },
        {
            id = 26546,
            score = 18,
            author = "6850",
            text = "After this he gives you three follow up quests to complete before giving you the information you seek:\n\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10641\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10668\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10669",
            date = "2007-01-28T17:40:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10640#comments:id=26546",
        },
        {
            id = 44054,
            score = 18,
