    },
    [10645] = {
        {
            id = 106226,
            score = 172,
            author = "53340",
            text = "Make sure you dismount before accepting the quest, if youre mounted you cannot attack and cant be attacked thus just wasting time and causing you a headache.",
            date = "2007-06-17T22:51:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10645#comments:id=106226",
        },
        {
            id = 38575,
            score = 114,
            author = "16691",
            text = "This chain begins differently depending on whether you're Alliance (A) or Horde (H):\n\nAlliance - starts in Wildhammer Stronghold from Zorus the Judicator (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21774):\n1. (A) [69] A Ghost in the Machine (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10642)\n2. (A) [69] Harbingers of Shadowmoon (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10643)\n3. (A) [70] Teron Gorefiend - Lore and Legend (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10644)\n\nHorde - starts in Shadowmoon Village from Chief Apothecary Hildagard (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21772):\n1. (H) [69] A Haunted History (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10624)\n2. (H) [69] Spectrecles (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10625)\n3. (H) [70] Teron Gorefiend - Lore and Legend (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10633)\n\nAt this point the chain splits into three parts which can be done in any order (and by both factions):\n4a. [70] Divination: Gorefiend's Cloak (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10635)\n4b. [70] Divination: Gorefiend's Truncheon [2 players] (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10636)\n4c. [70] Divination: Gorefiend's Armor [5 players] (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10634)\n\nAfter collected Gorefiend's stuff and returned it to the spirit (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21797), you will get:\n5. (A) [70] Teron Gorefiend, I am... (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10645)\n5. (H) [70] Teron Gorefiend, I am... (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10639)\n\nFor this final quest, Gorefiend becomes your \"pet\" and you control him using a pet bar.  Having used him to kill Karsius, you return to Zorus or Hildagard to claim your reward.  Choose from:\nEvoker's Helmet of Second Sight (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31104) (cloth DPS headpiece)\nStealther's Helmet of Second Sight (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31109) (leather melee headpiece)\nDruidic Helmet of Second Sight (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31110) (leather magical headpiece)\nStalker's Helmet of Second Sight (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31106) (mail +AP headpiece)\nShamanistic Helmet of Second Sight (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31107) (mail +dmg headpiece)\nOverlord's Helmet of Second Sight (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31105) (plate DPS headpiece)\n\nEdit: converted to new tag format (http://www.wowhead.com/?help=comment-formatting) to fix URL overload problem.",
            date = "2007-02-19T07:46:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10645#comments:id=38575",
        },
        {
            id = 38024,
            score = 69,
            author = "1318_",
            text = "When you accept the quest you'll get to control Teron Gorefiend and a pet action bar pops up. He has 4 spells he can cast (Haste, Unholy armor, Touch of Darkness, Death and Decay). Start the fight with turning on Haste and Unholy armor. Cast Death and Decay on Karsius and auto attack him in the Death and Decay cloud. After that just keep auto attacking him and recast every spell once they have cooled down.",
            date = "2007-02-18T09:31:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10645#comments:id=38024",
        },
        {
            id = 26921,
            score = 40,
            author = "10524",
            text = "Event bugs if you allready have a pet, dismiss it first\nand if you have a funky UI that hides pet bar, might want to enable it",
            date = "2007-01-29T05:55:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10645#comments:id=26921",
        },
        {
            id = 1602149,
            score = 40,
            author = "Ludovico",
            text = "This quest is still bugged, but now differently.  This was on a Feral Druid:\n\nIn caster form,\nNot Mounted,\nNo pets,\nDefault Blizzard UI on.\n\nAuto-attack was on a side-bar, but it would not function.  Button #1 did not function and I got a message saying: \"You can not attack the target while pacified\".  Tried various tricks and died several times, but finally discovered a work-around.\n\nGet right up to Karsius and then target him, try to initiate a melee attack by right-clicking on him.  If you do not swing at him, untarget and repeat. You need to do this quickly or he will de-spawn.  Eventually, you will take a swing at him and then the buttons seem to work as advertized.",
            date = "2011-12-26T08:45:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10645#comments:id=1602149",
        },
    },
    [10646] = {
        {
            id = 156129,
            score = 72,
            author = "16691",
            text = "This is part of the Book of Fel Names chain.  As well as reputation with your chosen faction (Aldor/Scyer), if you complete it you can choose from:\nCeremonial Kris (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31013) (+heal dagger)\nSlayer's Axe (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31010) (2H +str axe)\nSunfury Legguards (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30948) (+AP mail pants)\nHauberk of Karabor (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30933) (+AP leather chest)\nSummoner's Blade (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31002) (+dmg sword)\nWildcaller (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31009) (feral staff)\n\nAs with the Medallion of Karabor (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10707) line, this chain starts different depending on whether you're Aldor (A) or Scryer (S).  All the quests are rated level 70 - though the chain is available at level 68, it sends you to the Shadow Labyrinth (http://www.wowhead.com/?zone=3789) to kill Blackheart (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18667), which you might want to hold off on until level 70.\n\nAldors pick it up from Exarch Onaala (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21860) at the Altar of Sha'tar:\n1. (A) Karabor Training Grounds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10587)\n2. (A) A Necessary Distraction (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10637)\n3. (A) Altruis (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10640)\n\nScryers need to visit Larissa Sunstrike (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21954) at the Sanctum of the Stars:\n1. (S) Karabor Training Grounds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10687)\n2. (S) A Necessary Distraction (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10688)\n3. (S) Altruis (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10689)\n\nHere the chains converge on your old friend Altruis the Sufferer (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18417) in Nagrand.  He gives out three quests that need to be completed (in any order) before you can continue:\n4a. Against the Legion (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10641) - Netherstorm\n4b. Against the Illidari (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10668) - Shadowmoon Valley\n4c. Against All Odds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10669) - Zangarmarsh\nHaving gone around the world killing stuff, you can now return to Altruis and receive:\n5. Illidan's Pupil (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10646)\nwhich leads directly into\n6. The Book of Fel Names (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10649)\n\nNow it's time for a venture into the Shadow Labyrinth to kill Blackheart (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18667)!  Once that's done that and his body has been looted for the book, it's back to Altruis where again the chains diverge depending on your allegiance.\n\nAldor:\n7. (A) Return to the Aldor (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10650) - back to Altar of Sha'tar\n8. (A) Varedis Must Be Stopped (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10651)\n\nScryer:\n7. (S) Return to the Scryers (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10691) - back to Sanctum of Stars\n8. (S) Varedis Must Be Stopped (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10692)\n\nVaredis Must Be Stopped is the final part.  It's a 5-man group quest that sends you to the terrace outside the Black Temple to kill four elites: Varedis (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21178), Netharel (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21164), Theras (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21168) and Alandien (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21171).  Look them up  for co-ordinates and tips on killing them - they're pretty straightforward, really.\n\nWhen they're dead it's a simple matter of returning to the questgiver to choose a prize.",
            date = "2007-09-21T09:50:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10646#comments:id=156129",
        },
        {
            id = 1011719,
            score = 15,
            author = "entropicdragon",
            text = "Altruis's Story (Spoiler alert!)\n\nHere is the tale Altruis tells of Illidan's Pupil.\n\nTell me about the demon hunter training grounds at the Ruins of Karabor.\n\nAs a reward for his years of service, Illidan allowed Kael'thas to send him five warriors to train under him. It would be the first time blood elves would be allowed to train as demon hunters.\n\nThe training was brutal. Illidan put Kael's warriors through trials that would defeat most fully capable demon hunters.\n\nThree of Kael's elves died in training - another went mad.\n\nOne succeeded.\n\nI'm listening.\n\nVaredis was his name. To Illidan's surprise, not only did he succeed in the excruciating rites of passage that are part of the training; Varedis was already displaying better command over his powers than many veteran demon hunters.\n\nIllidan sensed the potential in Varedis and assigned three master demon hunters to train him further in their ways.\n\nGo on, please.\n\nWithin a year of training under Illidan's best three demon hunters, Varedis had surpassed them.\n\nNo longer content with the training they had to offer, Varedis infiltrated the Shadow Council where he learned of a powerful relic known as the Book of Fel Names. He secretly read from this book, committing each passage to memory.\n\nInteresting.\n\nKnowledge of a demon's true name is rumored to give a certain amount of power over that demon.\n\nThe Book of Fel names is said to contain the true name of every demon ever to have existed. By memorizing the passages in te book, Varedis had found a source of power to rival Illidan's own drinking from the Skull of Gul'dan.\n\nAt Illidan's request, Varedis now runs the training grounds at the Ruins of Karabor - along with the three masters that mentored Varedis.\n\nThat's quite a story.\n\nIt is not surprising that a blood elf's potential for power as a demon hunter is so high. After all, the sin'dorei do not have the natural aversion to demonic magic that night elves do.\n\nHowever, I do not expect many to succeed. Most of them, Varedis included, pursue power for its own sake. That power will consume them, for they are not driven by the pure fire that burns inside a true demon hunter's heart.\n\nThere was something else I wanted to ask you, Altruis. (This returns you to the first dialog page.)",
            date = "2010-04-03T15:14:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10646#comments:id=1011719",
        },
        {
            id = 109998,
            score = 9,
            author = "rodmin",
            text = "Altruis explains in this quest that Illidan once authorized 5 blood elves to undertake training by his fellow demon hunters. Of the five students, 3 have died, one has gone mad (possibly Leotheras the Blind - http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21215#z0z - it explains why he was imprisioned in SSC) and one has succesefully passed all the trial, namely Varedis (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21178).",
            date = "2007-06-23T18:12:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10646#comments:id=109998",
        },
        {
            id = 128686,
            score = 5,
            author = "68834",
            text = "lol, i noticed that the story he tells sounds an awful lot like the story \"the wizard of earthsea\" where A boy named ged memorizes all the \"real names\" of the elements and such, therefor being able to control him, this was a series, very entertaining to see it refrenced",
            date = "2007-07-29T13:27:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10646#comments:id=128686",
        },
        {
            id = 1638033,
            score = 3,
            author = "963466",
            text = "How come I cant get this quest? I have done up to Forge Camp: Annihilated then it stopped giving me quest I am 5 quest away for that area could someone help me?",
            date = "2012-03-11T01:19:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10646#comments:id=1638033",
        },
    },
    [10647] = {
        {
            id = 89580,
            score = 6,
            author = "41976",
            text = "This guy is no longer kite-able IMO in patch 2.1 - he now moves at about the speed of a non-epic mount.  Even in Druid Travel Form (+40% speed) he caught up to me quickly.   Not sure if slowing effects work though, even so you'd have to be bookin it to stay ahead of this guy.",
            date = "2007-05-24T13:34:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10647#comments:id=89580",
        },
        {
            id = 1608803,
            score = 6,
            author = "Kaiserin",
            text = "http://eu.battle.net/wow/en/blog/3038916#general (http://eu.battle.net/wow/en/blog/3038916#general) Patch 4.3 notes.\n\nMany Group quests in Outland and Northrend have been re-tuned to allow players to complete them solo. They are no longer labeled as Group quests.\n\nThis, unfortunately, does not apply to this quest..\n\nStill a 4 man group quest.. As a 68 hunter, I was able to solo him using a tank pet, made sure he held aggro at least 75% of the time.. Slows will not work on this fellow as well, kiting does, however. Nearly died, had about 300 health left when he bit the dust, and my tank pet took one for the team.\n\nEdit to clarify patch #.",
            date = "2012-01-08T16:19:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10647#comments:id=1608803",
        },
        {
            id = 58756,
            score = 5,
            author = "4257",
            text = "He resets now, if you go too far.",
            date = "2007-03-28T18:32:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10647#comments:id=58756",
        },
        {
            id = 95916,
            score = 5,
            author = "57392",
            text = "Confirmed.  Non-kitable.  Immune to slowing effects and fears.  In short, no longer solo-able.",
            date = "2007-06-02T10:45:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10647#comments:id=95916",
        },
        {
            id = 1249394,
            score = 4,
            author = "740240",
            text = "I just soloed it with my 67 protection pally when it's 70.\nSo it is doable, and my gear is only average.\nDone without any foodstuffs etc, only normal pally buffs.",
            date = "2010-12-21T01:49:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10647#comments:id=1249394",
        },
    },
