    [10651] = {
        {
            id = 156124,
            score = 57,
            author = "16691",
            text = "This is the conclusion to the Aldor version of the Book of Fel Names chain, which gives Aldor/Scryer rep as well as some nice blue rewards.  If you complete it, you can choose from:\nCeremonial Kris (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31013) (+heal dagger)\nSlayer's Axe (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31010) (2H +str axe)\nSunfury Legguards (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30948) (+AP mail pants)\nHauberk of Karabor (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30933) (+AP leather chest)\nSummoner's Blade (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31002) (+dmg sword)\nWildcaller (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31009) (feral staff)\n\nAs with the Medallion of Karabor (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10707) line, this chain starts different depending on whether you're Aldor (A) or Scryer (S).  All the quests are rated level 70 - though the chain is available at level 68, it sends you to the Shadow Labyrinth (http://www.wowhead.com/?zone=3789) to kill Blackheart (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18667), which you might want to hold off on until level 70.\n\nAldors pick it up from Exarch Onaala (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21860) at the Altar of Sha'tar:\n1. (A) Karabor Training Grounds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10587)\n2. (A) A Necessary Distraction (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10637)\n3. (A) Altruis (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10640)\n\nScryers need to visit Larissa Sunstrike (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21954) at the Sanctum of the Stars:\n1. (S) Karabor Training Grounds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10687)\n2. (S) A Necessary Distraction (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10688)\n3. (S) Altruis (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10689)\n\nHere the chains converge on your old friend Altruis the Sufferer (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18417) in Nagrand.  He gives out three quests that need to be completed (in any order) before you can continue:\n4a. Against the Legion (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10641) - Netherstorm\n4b. Against the Illidari (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10668) - Shadowmoon Valley\n4c. Against All Odds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10669) - Zangarmarsh\nHaving gone around the world killing stuff, you can now return to Altruis and receive:\n5. Illidan's Pupil (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10646)\nwhich leads directly into\n6. The Book of Fel Names (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10649)\n\nNow it's time for a venture into the Shadow Labyrinth to kill Blackheart (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18667)!  Once that's done that and his body has been looted for the book, it's back to Altruis where again the chains diverge depending on your allegiance.\n\nAldor:\n7. (A) Return to the Aldor (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10650) - back to Altar of Sha'tar\n8. (A) Varedis Must Be Stopped (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10651)\n\nScryer:\n7. (S) Return to the Scryers (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10691) - back to Sanctum of Stars\n8. (S) Varedis Must Be Stopped (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10692)\n\nVaredis Must Be Stopped is the final part.  It's a 5-man group quest that sends you to the terrace outside the Black Temple to kill four elites: Varedis (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21178), Netharel (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21164), Theras (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21168) and Alandien (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21171).  Look them up  for co-ordinates and tips on killing them - they're pretty straightforward, really.\n\nWhen they're dead it's a simple matter of returning to the questgiver to choose a prize.",
            date = "2007-09-21T09:44:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10651#comments:id=156124",
        },
        {
            id = 33846,
            score = 51,
            author = "11279",
            text = "Actually it wasnt too bad, each of them had a different ability\n\nVaredis: Flame Wave, fire dot on the ground\nTheras: Spell Reflect\nAlandien: Shadowfury, about 10 yard radius aoe knockback+damage\nNetharel: (sorry cant remember, dont think anything significant though)\n\nI'm also pretty sure all of them had a random target Mana Burn spell, Evasion, and Metamorphosis. (but the book only works on Varedis' Metamorphosis spell)\n\nVaredis has the most HP out of all of them so he will be the toughest to fight. I'd recommend fighting him first, and if your group can kill him then the other guys will be a breeze.",
            date = "2007-02-11T01:03:30-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10651#comments:id=33846",
        },
        {
            id = 37440,
            score = 46,
            author = "Mysteeq",
            text = "Alandien is at ... 69; 53\nNetharel is at 69; 53\nVaredis is at 72; 53\nTheras is at 72; 49\n\nJust a little help in finding them",
            date = "2007-02-17T09:07:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10651#comments:id=37440",
        },
        {
            id = 38557,
            score = 26,
            author = "covenant",
            text = "Using the book takes quite a while so be prepared for that.",
            date = "2007-02-19T06:26:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10651#comments:id=38557",
        },
        {
            id = 64049,
            score = 22,
            author = "41366",
            text = "Possible to solo this entire quest as a hunter.\n\nYou must take advantage of the railing on the stairs that is between Alandien and Varedis.  The key feature of it is the rocky formations at one end of it that allows mobs to run up onto the railing structure and the downward stairs at the opposite end of the rocky part.  When you get the demon hunter near the railing with that feature it is possible to kite them back and forth by jumping onto the rail and then down, making the demon hunter run all the way around to reach you.\nBasicly, the stairs that lead towards Varedis from Alandien has a railing that holds three braziers, has an end where mobs can walk onto it and another, downward stair case where you can jump up onto it and thanks to pathing limitations mobs must run around.\n\nAlandien is the easiest as the railing I used is right above her, just shoot her and shes basicly in position.\n\nNetharel is out of reach of this and I happened to luck out when there was a bunch of farmers to the point where I could simply just kite him out the front of the ruins.\n\nVaredis and Theras can be reached by clearing a path towards the railing you use and kiting them to it.\n\nFor Varedis it was really tricky as near 50% he becomes invulnerable until the book is used on him, which has like an 10 second cast.   To over come this I almost let him catch up to me on the bottom, jumped up onto the ledge and used the book.  By the time he reached me I was just barely able to pull it off.  After that its a straight forward kite back and forth\n\nHandy video that details the basic strategy: http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=emgOdXT6WJE\n\nEdit(Patch 2.3.3) : Visited the location and seems that blizzard changed the terrain, as now both sides of the Railing are path-able by mobs, it is still possible to execute the kite, but it is MUCH harder and complicated.",
            date = "2007-04-08T20:12:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10651#comments:id=64049",
        },
    },
