            text = "I can't interact with the NPC after discovering the area and getting him down to me :(",
            date = "2007-03-16T17:50:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10772#comments:id=52276",
        },
        {
            id = 5154052,
            score = 10,
            author = "Jaycoub",
            text = "It seems like the coordinates for quest completion vary for different people. I ran all over the spot marked by Blizzard's UI before meeting the quest requirement at coordinates 51,62.",
            date = "2021-04-16T18:22:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10772#comments:id=5154052",
        },
    },
    [10773] = {
        {
            id = 32232,
            score = 9,
            author = "6850",
            text = "Obviously, the mobs are all on The Path of Conquest. Good place to fight mobs is 55,69, where the path starts on the back side. Holy Paladins can solo this (I did), but expect to take about 5 minutes per Son of Corok.",
            date = "2007-02-07T12:26:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10773#comments:id=32232",
        },
        {
            id = 2300271,
            score = 9,
            author = "Aurleis1",
            text = "Video Guide: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7zw1ujCiLo\n\n1.  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10773\n•\009Travel to the Path of Conquest, in [zone=3520].\n•\009Use the https://www.wowhead.com/item=31310, that was given to you by https://www.wowhead.com/npc=21773, at Wildhammer Stronghold (coords: 36.2, 56.8).\n•\009Accept the quest, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10773, from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19382.\n•\009Travel to the Path of Conquest in the area of 51.5, 62.5 (and further south)\n•\009Kill 20 https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22016, 5 https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19824, and 10 https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22018.\n•\009Use the https://www.wowhead.com/item=31310, and turn in the quest to the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=19382.",
            date = "2016-01-20T14:40:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10773#comments:id=2300271",
        },
        {
            id = 895770,
            score = 5,
            author = "483297",
            text = "Can I give in the quest in any other way because I wasn't provided with a Flare Gun and Thane Yoregar won't give me another ?",
            date = "2009-11-20T09:24:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10773#comments:id=895770",
        },
        {
            id = 1717671,
            score = 5,
            author = "Thebe2",
            text = "This is one of the most miserable grinds in this game to this L69 point. Would recommend the bottom of the lower path at about 55, 70 to start and work your way thru the soldiers, then the ostriches, or whatever they are. Would do the Sons of Corock rock things last. All of these mobs aggro together, so do them individually.",
            date = "2012-09-23T17:58:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10773#comments:id=1717671",
        },
        {
            id = 2497040,
            score = 4,
            author = "1134646",
            text = "FYI- you cannot use the flare gun to call in/complete the quests unless you are *on* the path. I've tried it from a spot of safety on a rock halfway up the cliff wall and it won't work- have to go down to the path.",
            date = "2017-05-28T14:21:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10773#comments:id=2497040",
        },
    },
    [10774] = {
        {
            id = 39250,
            score = 21,
            author = "20805",
            text = "They are standing together at 53;70.",
            date = "2007-02-20T10:32:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10774#comments:id=39250",
        },
        {
            id = 2554488,
            score = 13,
            author = "jermbug1",
            text = "Anyone coming back to this because you somehow missed the quest or whatever can pick up another Wildhammer Flare Gun, sorry about no links, and call the Wildhammer Gryphon Rider and start wherever on the quest chain you are.",
            date = "2018-02-23T07:14:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10774#comments:id=2554488",
        },
        {
            id = 154441,
            score = 7,
            author = "18663",
            text = "You can kill one and die, then come back for the other.  I soloed it this way on my feral druid.",
            date = "2007-09-17T23:30:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10774#comments:id=154441",
        },
        {
            id = 35760,
            score = 3,
            author = "marmal",
            text = "Can be soloed as a hunter.\n\nYou pull them by concussion shooting the blood elf. She will be behind from this point. Then you concentrate your fire on the giant and pull him down the hill on the east side (you lose about 7000 HP from falling down), through the netherwing pass past the air elementals, and up through netherwing fields and then out on the road.\n\nThe giant is simple, just normal kiting (except that the terrain makes it difficult), but the blood elf is very hard. If your pet is full arcane resistance spec you should be able to kill her after you kite the giant down. Kiting the BE was difficult because she has a 30 yard range on her arcane missiles, while my gun has a 35 yard range, so you gotta stay out of her range, while still getting off a shot at her now and then. I think it's easiest to let the pet tank her once the giant is down.\n\nAlso, when you kill the giant, you can then FD and return to her spawn point and kill only her.\n\nI didn't solo the BE, because my pet had the wrong spec, but I think it should be doable.",
            date = "2007-02-14T08:09:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10774#comments:id=35760",
        },
        {
            id = 1960647,
            score = 3,
            author = "333762",
            text = "This was not easy at all for my level 69 mage.  I finally came here to wowhead after failing repeatedly at the quest.  I sent my pet after the blood elf and counter-spelled her frost-bolted her and used mirror image until she died.  Then the big rock guy killed me.  I  back from the graveyard as quickly as could.  I didn't loot the blood elf in the hopes that this would keep her from re-spawning.  I don't know if this was a good thing to do or not, but she did not respawn!  Then I sent the pet after Corok, froze him, used mirror image, used lots of bandages and health pots.  I survived and completed the quest.  Finally!",
            date = "2014-04-23T12:25:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10774#comments:id=1960647",
        },
    },
    [10775] = {
        {
            id = 31956,
            score = 20,
            author = "Pedala",
            text = "It looks like every elf there can drop...\nKilled 10 soldiers, got 10 tabbards",
            date = "2007-02-06T23:19:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10775#comments:id=31956",
        },
        {
            id = 246181,
            score = 3,
            author = "28031",
            text = "This quest is easier with 3 but is completely do-able solo at level 68-70) if you go to the very bottom of the ramp (loc. 54,68) and kill the two mobs (3 each) across from each other then wait for respawn. Drop rate was 100% for me and the Cavalier dropped one also...just gotta time the mob kills with the Cavalier and the Son of Corok that roams close to that loc. Finished this in 10 minutes.",
            date = "2008-03-01T12:17:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10775#comments:id=246181",
