    [10781] = {
        {
            id = 27197,
            score = 107,
            author = "16547",
            text = "This is easy as long as you have the right group make up, everyone's on the ball, know what to do, and have at least five rather than four. I did this with a feral druid tank, arms warrior tank, tree druid, enhancement shaman healer, and a warlock. I really reccomend having at least two tanks and two healers for this. It might be doable with one healer if everyone plays smart. The warlock was also nice for the first wave because he could enslave one of the demons.\n\nThe first wave is pretty simple. A bunch of demons and blood elves spawn and you basically take them down. As far as I know they are not CC'able, with exception to enslave.\n\nThe second wave is two eyes which do a mean mind flay. Interrupt them when they do that as soon as possible to help save the healer's mana.\n\nThe third wave has four fire lords which are blood elf npc's who have a ton of hp and cast flamestrike. This is the fight you have to be on the ball on. It is preferable to have each tank on two of the npc's. Whenever one of the npc's start to cast flame strike, the tank on them and any melee DPS on them need to MOVE. This is pretty universal for any flamestriking mob, but since flamestrike is a ground target spell, its possible to dodge it if you get out of its area of effect (the center of its target when it starts casting, the area of the effect will not follow the person if they move after the cast begins) before it finishes casting. If everyone can dodge the flame strikes, this wave is fairly easy.\n\nThe last wave, the final boss is a simple straight up fight. He will occasionally do an ae damage/knockback, this is another one that can be dodged by moving away when he does it. The casting animation looks like he's casting a shadow spell, so its fairly easy to spot. If you managed to do the third wave though, this one should be no problem, even if you eat the ae's from the boss.\n\nEnjoy your blue ring reward and flashy new tabard.",
            date = "2007-01-29T14:13:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10781#comments:id=27197",
        },
        {
            id = 1622654,
            score = 90,
            author = "901135",
            text = "If you are 85 and just want to do the Twenty-Five Tabards achievements, go and kill Val'zareq the Conqueror (he is walking around the zone), he will drop The Journal of Val'zareq then you give it to the Crystal Prison, it will give you Battle of the Crimson Watch, start the event, finished it and then go to Shattrath City to get you tabard. You will get Green Trophy Tabard of the Illidari or Purple Trophy Tabard of the Illidari. Both tabards are random and they will be in the Offering of the Sha'tar.\nIf you want both tabards you can do this: before you loot the tabard. Remove your auto loot, look inside the Offering of the Sha'tar see what color of tabard you got (dont take the tabard) go and speak to Garyl in Orgrimmar tell her that you lost your tabard of the Illidari, choose a different color of tabard that you have and then loot the Offering of the Sha'tar box. And you will have them both green and purple. It is simple and quick.\nHope this helped.",
            date = "2012-02-06T13:20:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10781#comments:id=1622654",
        },
        {
            id = 2354628,
            score = 45,
            author = "paladinnr1",
            text = "As of Legion you now get both tabards upon completion of the quest.",
            date = "2016-07-21T18:59:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10781#comments:id=2354628",
        },
        {
            id = 70281,
            score = 32,
            author = "44953",
            text = "Managed to 3-man the quest after 2 tries.\nSetup was Prot Warrior, Holy Priest and Rogue. Remember to Shadow Resist Buff.\n\nFirst Wave\nMixed spawn of melee mobs that comes in 2 forms, Humans and Demon forms. Basically tank ran in and grab aggro while healer waits till tank has a sunder on each mob. They don't hit too hard. Meanwhile the rogue would start peeling off the Demonkins first as we noticed they have about 2k less HP then the humanoid version and they're pretty big so we wanted to get better vision as well. Once ya down to the last mob, let healer regen back mana before killing it to trigger the second wave.\n\nSecond Wave\nThis is the wave that gave us the most problems. Spawns 2 x Demons that does a mean mind flay and fears. Key to this fight is to interupt as many mind flays as possible, they can be stunned so thats a huge plus. Rogue would Kick / Kidney Shot / gorge, while warrior Concussion Blows / shield bash. Also to note, as we were 3 manning it, the warrior tanked them similiarly to Onyxia style, getting berzerker rage up as often as possible to avoid fear. If warrior is feared, priest would get all the aggro, just keep healing as the fears don't last too long. Concentrate DPS and take one down asap, then move on to the other. Don't use them to regen mana, as a badly time fear could be a wipe. Quickly move on to the third wave.\n\nThird Wave\n4 x humanoid caster style that has quite a good amount of HP and casts FlameStrike for about 2k damage. For this, we got priest to stand in middle while the warrior would tank 3 of them on one side of the priest while the rogue tanked the 4th one on the other side of the priest. Basically we wanted all of us to spread out to avoid FS. Simple fight, rogue quickly kill his while warrior tanks the 3, when you guys see the casting animation, simply just move away from where u're standing as that would be the FS location. Key to this is to not let priest aggro and move out of FS range when ya see the casting animation. Once rogue is done with his, just join the warrior and finish up the remainder.\n\nLast Boss\nCake.. Has a spell reflect that looks like a counterspell animation, and cast a 1k++ shadow damage knockback. Tank him in the middle, when he casts knockback, we just run out of range.. quite alot of HP, classic tank and spank..\n\nNotes\nBasically as long as priest does not get aggro and warrior is comfortable with multi tanking, 3 manning is very possible. Priest used alot of binding heals for the fight and had pretty decend mana per second to last the waves. Ideally for all the waves except the second one, possible to tank the last mob while healer gets back mana.",
            date = "2007-04-20T23:04:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10781#comments:id=70281",
        },
        {
            id = 2369341,
            score = 18,
            author = "Kenzirey",
            text = "The quest now rewards both https://www.wowhead.com/item=31405 and https://www.wowhead.com/item=31404, no need to go to a tabard vendor and ask for the one you did not recieve from the https://www.wowhead.com/item=31408.",
            date = "2016-08-17T02:35:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10781#comments:id=2369341",
        },
    },
