            text = "Must have complete \"Wanted: Worg Mater Kruush\" for horde (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10809) starts at a wanted poster at Stonebreaker Post in Hellfire Peninsula",
            date = "2007-01-18T17:30:09-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10792#comments:id=21441",
        },
        {
            id = 1293090,
            score = 24,
            author = "757690",
            text = "This quest toke a lot of time for me, as i didnt knew where to light the torches.\nIf anyone is \"in the same boat\", then read here:\n\nStading in front of the main gate of this \"town\". You should see 2 guards on each side of the enstrance. After killing them, and entering the \"town\", you need to head left. The building all the way to the left is the \"forge\", where you can light the touches. It has a \"bowl\" filled with fire/something hot, in the middle. This place is located at the most north/eastern part of the town.\n\nTHANK YOU! this is the only useful comment on this post. EVERYONE JUST KEEP REPEATING THE SAME THINGS, THIS IS FOR HELP,  NOT TO HAVE CONVERSATIONS THAT EVERYONE HAS TO WASTE TIME READING THROUGH YOUR POINTLESS COMMENTS.",
            date = "2011-01-14T05:48:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10792#comments:id=1293090",
        },
        {
            id = 154922,
            score = 22,
            author = "Raziel",
            text = "Locations of all buildings http://www.wowhead.com/?maps=3483:690689690702694763672763685732",
            date = "2007-09-18T23:24:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10792#comments:id=154922",
        },
    },
    [10793] = {
        {
            id = 1622643,
            score = 115,
            author = "901135",
            text = "If you are 85 and just want to do the Twenty-Five Tabards achievements, go and kill Val'zareq the Conqueror (he is walking around the zone), he will drop The Journal of Val'zareq then you give it to the Crystal Prison, it will give you Battle of the Crimson Watch, start the event, finished it and then go to Shattrath City to get you tabard. You will get Green Trophy Tabard of the Illidari or Purple Trophy Tabard of the Illidari.  Both tabards are random and they will be in the Offering of the Sha'tar.\nIf you want both tabards you can do this: before you loot the tabard. Remove your auto loot, look inside the Offering of the Sha'tar see what color of tabard you got (dont take the tabard) go and speak to Garyl in Orgrimmar tell her that you lost your tabard of the Illidari, choose a different color of tabard that you have and then loot the Offering of the Sha'tar box. And you will have them both green and purple. It is simple and quick.\nHope this helped.",
            date = "2012-02-06T13:07:30-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10793#comments:id=1622643",
        },
        {
            id = 24233,
            score = 30,
            author = "Eliska",
            text = "51 72 he is a crystal .. :P\n\nfollow to Battle of the Crimson Watch",
            date = "2007-01-25T07:18:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10793#comments:id=24233",
        },
        {
            id = 2372387,
            score = 18,
            author = "exxyjj",
            text = "Completed this today as a Level 100 Demon Hunter to get my Illidari tabard. It was fairly straightforward; made a macro to target https://www.wowhead.com/npc=21979 and flew around the area where he spawns until I found him. Murdered the Betrayer https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22917's ally, brutally, then completed the quest. Easy peasy! :) For anyone who isn't sure of the macro, I used this:\n\n/tar Val'zareq the Conqueror\n\nAdditionally, https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18481 now gives you both the https://www.wowhead.com/item=31404 and https://www.wowhead.com/item=31405, which some of the top comments don't mention, as I believe it's a more recent change. Happy hunting! :D",
            date = "2016-08-23T03:29:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10793#comments:id=2372387",
        },
        {
            id = 266296,
            score = 16,
            author = "61232",
            text = "For those with a flying mount, the quest itself is incredibly easy. Flew in overhead, flew behind the crystal, and got just close enough to talk to General Auralion (the guy in the crystal) and complete the quest.\n\nDon't forget - by accepting his next quest, you start a long battle that will require a group. That's why this one is marked as a 4-man.",
            date = "2008-04-04T12:08:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10793#comments:id=266296",
        },
        {
            id = 256837,
            score = 14,
            author = "82411",
            text = "You can get Val'zareq to run away from his guards with a flying mount. He's ranged, the adds aren't. Just pull him in a relatively peaceful area, fly low and Val'zareq will attack you. His melee guys will run around a bit. Move away a bit, and the patrol will move on and you can attack Val'zareq without adds. :)",
            date = "2008-03-21T07:02:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10793#comments:id=256837",
        },
    },
