    [10804] = {
        {
            id = 32677,
            score = 147,
            author = "greengoo",
            text = "How to get Neutral with Netherdrake (Netherdrake Epic Mount Quest Starter)\nA list by Greengoo\n\n1. Kindness\n- Kill 8 Rocknail Flayers, Use Carcasses to Feed 8 Dragons (don't move!). Also make sure to travel a bit when laying the meat, as the same drakes won't eat twice in a row.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10804\n\n2. Seek Out Neltharaku\n- Fly on your mount and find Neltharaku, he patrols slowly around Dragonmaw about a few hundred feet up. You'll have to be about 5 yards UNDER him to talk to him.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10811\n\n3. Neltharaku's Tale\n- Listen to story.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10814\n\n4. Infiltrating Dragonmaw Fortress\n- Kill 15 of any type of orcs in the fortress.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10836\n\n5.To Netherwing Ledge!\n- Find 12 Crystals from the floating island SE of the mainland.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10837\n\n6. The Force of Neltharaku\n- Free 5 Dragons by using the item on them, then killing the orcs they agro.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10854\n\n7. Karynaku\n- Find Karynaku, she's the second story of the fortress.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10858\n\n8. Zuluhed the Whacked\n- Kill Zuluhed and recover the key. I recommend pulling him inside so as to avoid the archers, and kill him BEFORE he summons his add. Use the key he drops to free Karynaku.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10872\n\n9. Ally of the Netherwing\n- Return to Mordenai, you will immediately gain 42,000 rep and become neutral.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10870\n\n10. ????\n- Blizzard has announced that next patch they will be introducing a continuence of this quest line, including the ability to get exalted and purchase or receive through extensive questing an EPIC netherdrake mount. You will need epic training to use it however, so save your gold!",
            date = "2007-02-08T13:55:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10804#comments:id=32677",
        },
        {
            id = 24616,
            score = 99,
            author = "13088",
            text = "Kill the bigger Rocknails in order to get an entire carcass. Otherwise, the smaller ones drop an item that you need 5 of to combine into a carcass.",
            date = "2007-01-25T19:09:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10804#comments:id=24616",
        },
        {
            id = 75305,
            score = 82,
            author = "Aisenfaire",
            text = "Trivia:  The dragons will eat the carcass and then tell you, \"Belan shi karkun\", which is apparently Draconic for \"Thank you, mortal.\"",
            date = "2007-04-30T06:07:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10804#comments:id=75305",
        },
        {
            id = 1605433,
            score = 47,
            author = "884231",
            text = "Seems like many people have had the problem of find Mordenai after they have completed the \"Kindness\" quest. And like many of you I got frustrated,expecially after I found there's a 17hr + waiting list for a ticket. Anyway,I decided to search through WoWhead a little bit and found some people had found him in spots other than where he gave you the quest. Personaly,I found him at 62,60. So befor getting upset.Take some time and fly around eventually you WILL find him.",
            date = "2012-01-01T20:29:51-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10804#comments:id=1605433",
        },
        {
            id = 29599,
            score = 37,
            author = "19282",
            text = "If you save up all the meats to place down one after another, make sure you don't put them down in the same spot.  The drakes get a \"full\" debuff and no nearby drakes will come down to eat, so you'll waste meat doing that.",
            date = "2007-02-02T18:05:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10804#comments:id=29599",
        },
    },
    [10805] = {
        {
            id = 26320,
            score = 30,
            author = "15586",
            text = "The mobs start at 62, 22 and are all elites. Almost all are single pulls and could probably be soloed, I would not recommend it. Its a lot of mobs and most have 24k hps+. Firegrom is really no different from any of the battle mages, just named. Pretty simple, just long if you solo.",
            date = "2007-01-28T10:51:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10805#comments:id=26320",
        },
        {
            id = 1066137,
            score = 19,
            author = "aawow",
            text = "Fingrom can be found on the first floor (i.e., one level above the ground floor) of the building at 66,20. Simply climb up the incline and enter the room. The room is occupied by Fingrom and one Bladespire Enforcer.",
            date = "2010-06-25T18:08:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10805#comments:id=1066137",
        },
        {
            id = 90316,
            score = 15,
            author = "novacurse",
            text = "I don't know if this changed after patch 2.1, but the mobs definetley aggro when feared into, especially the ravagers. At least, they all did for me several times.",
            date = "2007-05-25T13:49:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10805#comments:id=90316",
        },
        {
            id = 127123,
            score = 11,
            author = "Eldariel",
            text = "Do yourself a favor; Get a group to do this with you. Also you can use the group to do the next follow-up: Showdown ( http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10806 ) He will be easy and can be two manned if played properly.",
            date = "2007-07-26T11:05:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10805#comments:id=127123",
        },
        {
            id = 1790342,
            score = 11,
            author = "ramrad",
            text = "Doing this quest is so weird after having completed the Ogri'la chain ([quest=11000 domain=www]) to become the king/queen of ogres. All mobs are neutral to you and when you kill them they say something that makes you feel like a horrible leader...  >.<",
            date = "2012-12-31T20:17:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10805#comments:id=1790342",
        },
    },
    [10806] = {
        {
            id = 43947,
            score = 260,
            author = "7485",
            text = "The alter can be found at 64,18 near Gruul's lair",
            date = "2007-02-28T11:40:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10806#comments:id=43947",
        },
        {
            id = 2548812,
            score = 92,
            author = "Chipcaray",
            text = "Coordinates of the stupid alter of stupid Goc are 64.15, 18.51  A little rectangle. Very alter-esque.",
            date = "2018-01-27T19:32:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10806#comments:id=2548812",
        },
        {
            id = 1632501,
            score = 43,
            author = "anteract",
            text = "It needs to be said at this late date, if you wear mail armor of any kind and you finish this quest, take the https://www.wowhead.com/item=31547 as the reward, and don't throw it away, ever.  Its one of a kind in game.",
            date = "2012-02-27T13:22:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10806#comments:id=1632501",
        },
        {
            id = 1639366,
            score = 43,
            author = "806196",
            text = "I spent at least an hour and a half over 3 days trying to find Goc's Altar so I am going to describe in tedious detail how to find it.\nAt this point I assume you have found Gruul's Lair and that it shows on your mini-map.\nDirectly N of the ul in the Gruul's Lair label, there is a marking of a small hut and\ndirectly N of that hut is another slightly larger hut with another building to its E.\nIf you place yourself just S of that NW hut in Gruul's Lair and are pointing due N, to your left/W you will see Goc's Altar; it's small and tucked kinda in an inconspicuous corner.\nIt may be difficult to find - you need to be fairly close to see it - it might not show during a quick fly-by. You should look for the \"banner\", but be aware that there are several similar banners near by.\nOnce I finally find it, I had no problems (Level 68 Tauren Hunter).\nThere is already a screenshot of the altar fairly close up; I have submitted a screenshot farther away to help you locate its position. The screenshot should be published @3/16 or 17.\nP.S. Goc appears S of the alter.",
            date = "2012-03-14T08:18:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10806#comments:id=1639366",
        },
        {
            id = 25861,
            score = 24,
            author = "16848",
            text = "Worked for me last night (01/27/07), 2 manned easily by a druid and priest. The Altar is in the compound to the north, around 63, 20.",
            date = "2007-01-27T17:14:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10806#comments:id=25861",
        },
    },
    [10807] = {
        {
            id = 27012,
            score = 6,
            author = "Chudz",
            text = "@57,36 all arround this location you will all 3 mobs",
            date = "2007-01-29T09:19:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10807#comments:id=27012",
        },
        {
            id = 44107,
            score = 4,
            author = "defektunge",
            text = "Combine this with Tablets of Baa'ri if you're going to do it.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10683\n\nI *hate* those ruins more than any other area in the entire game though, and if I could go back in time I'd just say \"screw the Deathsworn\" and skip the whole thing. Wherever you go you get a million adds crawling out of the walls to kill you, and a hundred elephants kicking you around so you can't do anything (and causing you to get even more adds, of course).",
            date = "2007-02-28T16:28:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10807#comments:id=44107",
        },
        {
            id = 1695941,
