            score = 79,
            author = "Lustral",
            text = "Captive children are freed from Veil Skith Cages at the Skith camp south of Shattrath by using Veil Skith Prison Keys.  The keys drop from both the Dreadhawk's and Windrippers at the camp, at about a 20-25% rate.\n\nThere are four cages at the camp, two on the ground (one on the east side another on the west side toward the  western tree tower), and two up in the trees (one on each tree top).  The ground cages free 2 children each and the tree cages free 4 each, so it's more efficient to use keys on the tree cages whenever the children have respawned inside those.",
            date = "2006-12-29T14:10:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10852#comments:id=18462",
        },
        {
            id = 201146,
            score = 72,
            author = "PirateNipple",
            text = "How do you explain to these kids that you aren't going to open their cage because there's not enough kids locked inside of it?  :(",
            date = "2007-12-14T12:04:30-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10852#comments:id=201146",
        },
        {
            id = 22098,
            score = 67,
            author = "Jessi330",
            text = "You cannot get this quest until you complete one from Rilak the Redeemed in Shattrath City.",
            date = "2007-01-20T13:55:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10852#comments:id=22098",
        },
        {
            id = 24335,
            score = 40,
            author = "Chudz",
            text = "Loc: 31.41",
            date = "2007-01-25T10:33:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10852#comments:id=24335",
        },
        {
            id = 22681,
            score = 24,
            author = "4119",
            text = "Kids will add up in a cage over time, its not random. However many kids are in the cage is how much you get.",
            date = "2007-01-22T03:57:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10852#comments:id=22681",
        },
    },
    [10853] = {
        {
            id = 122918,
            score = 232,
            author = "71267",
            text = "if you are out of totems ... STOP ... don't abandon the quest\njust go back and talk with the quest giver and he'll give you what you need ^^",
            date = "2007-07-18T17:03:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10853#comments:id=122918",
        },
        {
            id = 336050,
            score = 214,
            author = "148209",
            text = "For those wondering, setting netherwing at war and killing the drakes doesn't hurt your rep.",
            date = "2008-07-25T13:56:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10853#comments:id=336050",
        },
        {
            id = 670561,
            score = 93,
            author = "347254",
            text = "Please note for the final time that this quest *can* be done by players who have done the quest chain that makes toons Neutral with the Netherwing faction.\n\nSimply go to your Reputation tab and left-click the Netherwing tab.  Select \"At War.\"\n\nYou will incur NO Reputation penalties for either selecting At War or attacking the Drakes.  After you are done, just un-select the option and you are finished--both with the quest and the worries.\n\nGood luck with Loremaster, everyone.",
            date = "2009-04-09T04:39:22-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10853#comments:id=670561",
        },
        {
            id = 1645914,
            score = 35,
            author = "470888",
            text = "As of 3/28/12, if you are exalted with Netherwing, and mark yourself \"at war\" you CAN attack the drakes. Also, I don't appear to be losing rep with them either. Good to know, although I don't believe you lose the ability to summon the drakes once you learn them.",
            date = "2012-03-28T21:49:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10853#comments:id=1645914",
        },
        {
            id = 24882,
            score = 34,
            author = "14217",
            text = "The netherdrakes can be found at 60,76 in singing ridge",
            date = "2007-01-26T07:14:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10853#comments:id=24882",
        },
    },
    [10854] = {
        {
            id = 27527,
            score = 79,
            author = "Kyana",
            text = "I just stayed at a distance, then used the crystal on the drake. The drake turned green and started attacking the orc. I helped the drake kill the orc to free it (if you don't help, there's a good chance the orc will kill the drake).\n\nThe crystal have a long range, so you can stand pretty far away.",
            date = "2007-01-30T02:26:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10854#comments:id=27527",
        },
        {
            id = 40733,
            score = 43,
            author = "18643",
            text = "What no one has mentioned is that after you use the crystal on the drakes they take a good 2 seconds to turn green...so you must wait that amount of time before attacking.",
            date = "2007-02-22T19:00:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10854#comments:id=40733",
        },
        {
            id = 32683,
            score = 35,
            author = "greengoo",
            text = "How to get Neutral with Netherdrake (Netherdrake Epic Mount Quest Starter)\nA list by Greengoo\n\n1. Kindness\n- Kill 8 Rocknail Flayers, Use Carcasses to Feed 8 Dragons (don't move!). Also make sure to travel a bit when laying the meat, as the same drakes won't eat twice in a row.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10804\n\n2. Seek Out Neltharaku\n- Fly on your mount and find Neltharaku, he patrols slowly around Dragonmaw about a few hundred feet up. You'll have to be about 5 yards UNDER him to talk to him.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10811\n\n3. Neltharaku's Tale\n- Listen to story.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10814\n\n4. Infiltrating Dragonmaw Fortress\n- Kill 15 of any type of orcs in the fortress.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10836\n\n5.To Netherwing Ledge!\n- Find 12 Crystals from the floating island SE of the mainland.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10837\n\n6. The Force of Neltharaku\n- Free 5 Dragons by using the item on them, then killing the orcs they agro.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10854\n\n7. Karynaku\n- Find Karynaku, she's the second story of the fortress.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10858\n\n8. Zuluhed the Whacked\n- Kill Zuluhed and recover the key. I recommend pulling him inside so as to avoid the archers, and kill him BEFORE he summons his add. Use the key he drops to free Karynaku.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10872\n\n9. Ally of the Netherwing\n- Return to Mordenai, you will immediately gain 42,000 rep and become neutral.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10870\n\n10. ????\n- Blizzard has announced that next patch they will be introducing a continuence of this quest line, including the ability to get exalted and purchase or receive through extensive questing an EPIC netherdrake mount. You will need epic training to use it however, so save your gold!",
            date = "2007-02-08T14:03:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10854#comments:id=32683",
        },
        {
            id = 33796,
            score = 30,
            author = "18312",
            text = "The drakes are around the 68,60 area. The crystal can't be used if you are in combat. If you use the crystal and there are more orcs around the drake, it will aggro those orcs, so you need to kill them all before the quest will accept the drake as being freed. Kill orcs around the drake that aren't linked to it before using the crystal if you can. I also had a bug where the drake simply ran across the entire orc camp after I used the crystal. It aggroed all of the orcs, who killed the drake at the end of the camp, and then came to kill me afterwards. Be ready to run out of the camp if this happens.",
            date = "2007-02-10T21:49:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10854#comments:id=33796",
        },
        {
            id = 2435741,
            score = 29,
            author = "Aletto",
            text = "This info might only be useful for a short time, but I figured it might help at least one person.\n\nCurrently this quest seems to be bugged. When you use the Enchanted Nethervine Crystal on the enslaved nether drake, it immediately attacks you alongside its orc captor. Killing the orc captor and waiting around doesn't seem to do anything. And obviously, killing the hostile nether drake doesn't count as freeing it.\n\nThe way to finish this quest now is to use the crystal on the drake, kill only the orc, and then run away from the nether drake until it leashes back to its spawn point. At that point is when it will turn friendly and then randomly attack one of orcs nearest to it. Kill THAT orc, and the drake will once again return to its spawn point and finally be freed. :]",
            date = "2016-10-27T13:47:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10854#comments:id=2435741",
        },
    },
    [10855] = {
