            score = 92,
            author = "27894",
            text = "To continue with this questline, first get your 300 riding (epic flying) skill and talk to Mordenai in Netherwing fields. he will send you to talk to the general of the Dragonmaw orcs at the Netherwing encampment. This encampment is located right on the first E of Netherwing Ledge.\nThere you will get several quests 2-4 daily quests based on how many gathering professions you have, and 1 repeatable quest. Daily quests can be repeated once a day, but you can do no more than 10 of their type a day.\n\nNEUTRAL to FRIENDLY:\n\nA Slow Death (Daily) 250 rep\nGet 12 Fel Glands from the nether rays on netherwing ledge, use these along with the quest item you received to poison the orcs working all around the ledge.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11020\n\nNetherdust Pollen (Daily) 250 rep\nThis is the quest for herbalist, simple enough gather 40 pollens from the netherdust bushes found around the ledge.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11017\n\nNetherwing crystals (Daily) 250 rep\nCollect 40 Netherwing crystals, these drop off of the flayers on the ledge and any mobs in the mines south of the encampment.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11015\n\nNot so friendly skies (Daily)\nGet 10 Netherwing relics from the Dragonmaw transporters flying between Netherwing ledge and the Dragonmaw Fortress. Land on one of the floating islands between the island and the mainland and use ranged attacks to pull the transporters to you.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11035\n\nGreat Netherwing egg hunt (Repeatable) 350 rep first turn in, 250 subsequent turn ins\nThis is the only completely repeatable quest there is, and it's to turn in a netherwing egg. These eggs can come from anywhere herbs, mining, mob drops, there are even eggs that spawn along the ridge that you can click on to loot. Sadly though, the drop rate on these is incredibly low.\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11049\n\nRepeat these quests until you get to Friendly which opens up the quests to get to honored. (see more posts below)",
            date = "2007-05-23T12:54:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10870#comments:id=88453",
        },
        {
            id = 88463,
            score = 63,
            author = "27894",
            text = "Netherwing HONORED to REVERED/EXALTED:\n\nBuilding a Soul Cannon 500 rep\nBring the guy at camp 2 felsteel bars, 1 adamantite frame, 1 khorium power core, and one quest item. You get the quest item in terrokar forest in the area above the horde base that you can only get to with a flying mount. There's a guy there who will summon 5 elementals of each element one at a time, after you kill each of them you get the item, all easily soloable.\n\nThis leads to :\n\nSubduing the Subduer 500 rep\nYou have to channel a spell from your mount onto xxx the subduer a 73 elite in twilight ridge in nagrand. What you have to do is keep far enough back from him, and dodge his bolts to eventually drain his life down, I found it easier to train him around the center of the camp keeping across the center from him at all times (note: height has nothing to do with melee range so don't try to just fly high enough that he won't melee you). Be careful not to die too far in the air. Once you win you get to choose between 4 green quest rewards, none of which are very overwhelming.\n\nDisrupting the Twilight Generator (Daily) 500 rep\nKill any 20 of the mobs at the same place as the above quest.\n\nRace quests 500 each for first 5, 1000 for 6th\nAt this level you also unlock the Race quests. Basically this is a series of 6 quests where you try to fly behind each of the riders and not get knocked off by the bombs/magic/meteors they throw at you. The first 5 aren't too bad once you learn how to avoid their attacks. The final race is either really rough or bugged at the moment, because if you aren't right on top of the guy he'll despawn. The others you could get a little range to dodge at least. Also a riding crop/pally aura makes this a lot easier since he's faster than you, reward is a +10% mount speed trinket.\n\nThis opens up at REVERED:\n\nThe greatest trap ever (Daily) (3 man group)- 500 rep\nYou are told that you need to lead a group of dragonmaw to attack the aldor(scryer) base, once there you talk to a few npc's then start an attack. You will have 8 non elite npc's assisting you and 1 elite npc, your goal is to keep the elite npc alive while fending off all the dragonmaw. There are several waves of these guys so just try to dps them down as best you can. The battle takes place literally 3 steps from the graveyard so it isn't hard to just walk over and rez if you die.\n\nRepeat these until exalted and enjoy your mount :)",
            date = "2007-05-23T13:05:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10870#comments:id=88463",
        },
        {
            id = 24382,
            score = 36,
            author = "15682",
            text = "The rewards for this, in addition to the rep, are:\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31493\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31494\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31490\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31491\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31492",
            date = "2007-01-25T12:26:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10870#comments:id=24382",
        },
        {
            id = 22090,
            score = 32,
            author = "nine",
            text = "You need to do the quest chain to free Karynaku before you can do this quest.",
            date = "2007-01-20T13:41:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10870#comments:id=22090",
        },
    },
    [10871] = {
        {
            id = 24212,
            score = 5,
            author = "15581",
            text = "Apparently this Faction has not yet been fully implemented into TBC.\nAs of now it only seems possible to attain neutral status by doing the following chain of quests in Shadowmoon Valley:\n\nKindness\n\nSeek out Neltharaku\n\nNeltharaku's Tale\n\nInfiltrating Dragonmaw Fortress\n\nTo Netherwing Ledge!\n\nThe force of Neltharaku\n\nKarynaku\n\nZuluhead the Wacked\n\nAlly of the Netherwing",
            date = "2007-01-25T06:09:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10871#comments:id=24212",
        },
    },
    [10872] = {
        {
            id = 44723,
            score = 26,
            author = "zacke10",
            text = "The easiest way to kill this boss is to first clear both rooms of mobs. Then one in your party start the quest while the rest is inside one of the rooms. At the time you start the quest, run as fast as posseble inside the room where your party is.\n\nWhen you are inside, the tank should get ready to taunt the boss, since it will run after you. When the warrior got agro, DPS him as much as posseble. When you see him cast a portal, the whole group must run into the other room very fast. If you do this, the boss will follow and the portal will not summon any hard elite mob. If you do not change room, you will have to face Arcubus, level 68 elite mob. He hits very hard and you will most likely whipe if he shows up.\n\nAt low health he will change form and hit much harder. But it should not be any problem at all if you keep DPSing, because he will die soon after he changes form. After he dies, loot the key and run back to the dragon. Release him and you will fly away with him to the dragon from the sky and Mordenai. He will reward you with one of the following items:\n\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31493\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31494\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31490\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31491\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=31492\n\nTo sum this up:\n1. Clear the rooms\n2. Group gather in one of the room and one of you start the quest.\n3. Run inside the room your mates are in\n4. Tank get agro\n5. DPS him as much as posseble.\n6. When he casts portal - Change room quickly!\n7. Watch out when he is low hp. Changes form and doing heavy damage.\n8. Kill him, loot the key and fly away with the dragon and get your reward!",
            date = "2007-03-01T17:55:42-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10872#comments:id=44723",
        },
        {
            id = 26566,
            score = 13,
            author = "14639",
            text = "You can avoid having to deal with the archers if you clear one of the huts on the left or right of the courtyard gateway.\n\nPull Zuluhead inside one of those huts and out of LOS of the archers.\n\nZuluhead does not do much melee damage, as a shadow priest, I was able to keep our tank topped off with just vamp embrace.  somewhere around 20 pct he'll transform into a demon and start hitting harder, so be ready for that.\n\nNote that the most important part is to kill him before demons start popping through the portal he creates.  dps dps dots dots etc etc",
            date = "2007-01-28T18:14:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10872#comments:id=26566",
        },
        {
            id = 34521,
            score = 6,
            author = "covenant",
            text = "The quest chain starts here: http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10804",
            date = "2007-02-12T07:01:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10872#comments:id=34521",
        },
        {
            id = 189370,
            score = 6,
            author = "Nemari",
            text = "Good news: You can now help a friend, even if you are exalted with the Netherwings.\n\nI was just asked to help and expected that I could only heal, but Zuluhed was red, so I could help with damage.",
            date = "2007-11-22T09:13:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10872#comments:id=189370",
        },
        {
            id = 477340,
            score = 4,
            author = "131458",
            text = "Soloed it as a 74 feral druid in several Northrend blues, and the rest Karazhan level epics. It took two tries, but with careful planning, barkskin + shifting out to heal once, and liberal use of cooldowns, trinkets and other consumables it was doable.\n\n I cleared both of the rooms, and pulled him into the first one. After he cast his first summon, I moved to the second, and when he cast another, I moved outside. By this time, the archers had disappeared. He cast a third summon as well, so I had to move to the balcony. Got a shaman add somehow, which made his dragonkin form very difficult. I ended with about 10% health, but I'm sure someone in better gear than me would find it much easier to solo. Good luck to anyone else looking to get a netherdrake post-70!",
            date = "2008-11-29T04:34:05-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10872#comments:id=477340",
        },
    },
