        },
        {
            id = 2298886,
            score = 1,
            author = "Aurleis1",
            text = "Video Guide: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WftCLjFrzmE\n\n1.  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10878\n•\009Accept the quest, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10878, from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22370 at coords 37.2, 50.6 (Refugee Caravan).\n•\009Travel south, to the area of coords 40, 55.\n•\009Kill 8 https://www.wowhead.com/npc=21661, 4 https://www.wowhead.com/npc=21902, and 2 https://www.wowhead.com/npc=21907.\n•\009Travel north, to the Refugee Caravan, to coords 37.2, 50.6.\n•\009Turn in the quest to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22370.\n\nNOTE: If you haven't already completed https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10880, you probably have this in your inventory, to begin the quest.",
            date = "2016-01-16T10:25:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10878#comments:id=2298886",
        },
    },
    [10879] = {
        {
            id = 32132,
            score = 78,
            author = "TheUz",
            text = "About the Encounter:\nIt is important to note that you have a limited area in which you are allowed to fight.  If you walk too far from the quest giver you will fail the quest.  This means limited kiting.  I would say you should try to stay within a 20 yard radius of the quest giver.   This is a multiple wave event and you will have 5-10 seconds of rest between each wave.\n\nThe Opponents:\n\nThere are 4 waves of enemies:\n\nWave 1:\n2 Birds 1300-1700 health – Melee attacks for 350-700 on 0-1k armor\nWave 2:\n 2 Birds 1300-1700 health – Melee attacks for 350-700 on 0-1k armor\nWave 3:\n 3 Birds 1300-1700 health – Melee attacks for 350-700 on 0-1k armor\nWave 4:\n 1 Bird 10k-12k health – Melee attacks for 1200-2500 on 0-1k armor\nThis bird also has a pushback ability with about 2 seconds of cast time.\nThe pushback does no damage\nMultiple pushbacks can lead you far enough from the quest giver to fail the quest\n\nMy Experience:\nI soloed this quest as an elemental mage at 70.  I would rate the encounter as moderately difficult because of the limited area in which to fight.  Still, I would strongly suggest that this quest be done in a group.\n\nI was able to use all of my crowd control abilities including Polymorph, Blast Wave, Frost Nova, Frost Bolt, and Cone of Cold.  Having cold snap with three ice barriers made a huge difference as well.  I fought him with 6800 health (add 3 ice barriers for nearly 10k).  I did pop a potion mid battle but it turned out to be unnecessary, his attacks while very large were not fast enough to make his DPS as scary as his crits.\n\nI would suggest that any mage who wants to fight him solo open on him with a polymorph to prep a larger damage spell as an opener.\n\nBe prepared that all CC seems to break about 50% quicker on the big bird.  Expect 6-9 seconds on Polymorph, and 5 seconds on Frost Nova.",
            date = "2007-02-07T08:35:51-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10879#comments:id=32132",
        },
        {
            id = 23572,
            score = 36,
            author = "Humbaba",
            text = "You must complete Veil Shalas: Signal Fires and a quick follow up trip to Shattrath in order to start this. It was easily done with an enhance shaman and a warrior as well as with an enhance shaman and a frost mage.",
            date = "2007-01-24T08:37:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10879#comments:id=23572",
        },
        {
            id = 22210,
            score = 12,
            author = "13521",
            text = "3 wave of birds, like 2k hp each.\nThen a the boss bird, chillable and rootable so I was able to solo as frost mage.  Melee crit me for 2k, plus some sort of ranged attack that tickles.",
            date = "2007-01-20T18:12:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10879#comments:id=22210",
        },
        {
            id = 26178,
            score = 11,
            author = "swotam",
            text = "This is not an easy one to solo unless you have decent crowd control available. The regular spawns are easy, but take a little time to get down. The boss who spawns hits very hard, so if you are still clearing the regular spawns when he shows up you will have trouble unless you trap him or immobilize him. Best bet is to get someone to assist you as it only takes a couple of minutes to complete.",
            date = "2007-01-28T04:53:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10879#comments:id=26178",
        },
        {
            id = 106242,
            score = 8,
            author = "Ziir",
            text = "Soloed this as a 68 affliction warlock so I didn't have Felguard like the one above me. Took me a few tries but it was easy when I figured it out.\n\nIt hasn't been mentioned yet but the waves are timed. That means the next wave and the avatar WILL spawn whether or not you've cleared the previous wave.\n\nBefore the fight, have a healthstone and voidwalker. Yes, I know he sucks but you need him for the shield. Having netherweave bandages are very helpful as well.\n\nOn the first wave, send voidwalker to one of the birds and just dot it with corruption and then drain tank the other bird. They die fast so don't bother with UA, just corruption and CoA was enough. The drain tanked one will die fast and just as you are finishing off the other, the next wave should spawn.\n\nAgain, same tatics. On this wave, I couldn't kill off the second bird because I wasn't as fast about it as the first time, so when the third wave spawned I have three at full health and one nearly dead.\n\nThey hit kinda hard for having such low hp, so I instant HoT the four and the low health one died. Stick corruption on all three and then I feared one, voidwalker on another and drained the last. Voidwalker was nearly dead so I sac'd him.\n\nThen the avatar spawned so I feared him. DC one bird, shadowburn the other and drained the last one down and healthstoned. Feared avatar again and hit it with corruption and bandaged myself to life tap cause I was low on mana. Then from there on it was just simple fear and dot.\n\nIt was challenging but it's also a great example of being able to use all of your skills to beat an encounter. As you can kinda tell, I panicked when I had the avatar spawn and three birds coming towards me so I did what I could to burn them down asap.",
            date = "2007-06-17T23:39:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10879#comments:id=106242",
        },
    },
