    },
    [10885] = {
        {
            id = 64573,
            score = 35,
            author = "10796",
            text = "Make sure you do this quest in heroic instances as stated in the objectives",
            date = "2007-04-09T17:49:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10885#comments:id=64573",
        },
        {
            id = 107153,
            score = 23,
            author = "Navaash",
            text = "With today's annoucement by Blizzard that there will now be no attunement required to enter The Eye, it is no longer necessary to do this quest:\n\nhttp://forums.worldofwarcraft.com/thread.html?topicId=110637185\n\nHowever the quest will remain in game; the same post also implies they may add a reward in the future for those who have fully completed this questline.",
            date = "2007-06-19T12:23:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10885#comments:id=107153",
        },
        {
            id = 1809032,
            score = 6,
            author = "Calentor",
            text = "This quest does not count towards [achievement=1272 domain=www]",
            date = "2013-02-04T10:45:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10885#comments:id=1809032",
        },
        {
            id = 1863594,
            score = 4,
            author = "mizzes",
            text = "Heh, turned this quest in to A'dal today (June 2013) and immediately got the achievement Heroic: The Steamvault (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=677).  Clearly I had gotten Kalithresh's Trident before the achievement system was implemented, and not done H-SV on this character since.\n\nYou just don't expect to get heroic dungeon achievements while standing in the middle of Shattrath!",
            date = "2013-06-06T20:55:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10885#comments:id=1863594",
        },
        {
            id = 97057,
            score = 2,
            author = "45745",
            text = "This Quest isn't THAT hard. Just a bit time consuming.\nI did a heroic Shadow Labs which was surprisingly easy.\n\nOur group make up:\nProt Pally: Karazhan/ Heroic epics.\n2 Fire mages: Crafted/ Heroic/ Karazhan epics.\nHoly Priest (me): Crafted/ Heroic/ Karazhan Epics.\nEnhancement Shaman: Karazhan / Blue Gear\n\nThe key to shadow labs is good CC. only time I ever couldnt solo heal the tank is when we had a nine pull. 6 in the room before the boss + 2 on the side(fear) and 1 assassin. It was ugly.\n\nGoodluck getting attuned for the eye. Make SURE u have CC in this instance otherwise it could be HARD.",
            date = "2007-06-03T09:46:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10885#comments:id=97057",
        },
    },
    [10886] = {
        {
            id = 37850,
            score = 17,
            author = "13857",
            text = "We got harbinger to 20% and wiped. The next time we tried it Millhouse would not spawn. I'm not sure if it's a bug or if that's what supposed to happen but just be aware. We petitioned and the gm said to soft reset (meaning we had to clear trash again). Anyway, here is what we had when it worked:\n\nFirst boss was the imp who threw 3k fireballs every once in awhile. Quite easy especially with the break for Millhouse to spawn.\n\nSecond boss was the air elemental who did the AOE lightning that hit for quite alot, probably ~4k I would say every 10-15 seconds. It's not bad with some aoe heals but you have to watch out the a curse he does which is 100% more damage.\n\nThird boss was the broodlord type of guy, nothing much just a knockback. Quite easy.\n\nHarbinger's \"mind flay\" is upgraded to 2000 a tick for 4 ticks. I don't recall anything different from the normal version other than that.  He does it a little bit more often than the regular version as well.",
            date = "2007-02-18T00:17:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10886#comments:id=37850",
        },
        {
            id = 47921,
            score = 10,
            author = "striderevale",
            text = "If you do not have a decurser and get the wind elemental during final boss event, you gotta have very good healing, but it is possible.\n\nMake a /target millhouse macro to check heals on the NPC but he should be ok unless he tries to tank the boss splits.\n\nWarning: Millhouse will nuke MCd players! To prevent millhouse killing your party members, don't let anybody get too low on health, and scatter shot MCd people asap!",
            date = "2007-03-07T21:39:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10886#comments:id=47921",
        },
        {
            id = 107156,
            score = 10,
            author = "Navaash",
            text = "With today's annoucement by Blizzard that there will now be no attunement required to enter The Eye, it is no longer necessary to do this quest:\n\nhttp://forums.worldofwarcraft.com/thread.html?topicId=110637185\n\nHowever the quest will remain in game; the same post also implies they may add a reward in the future for those who have fully completed this questline.",
            date = "2007-06-19T12:24:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10886#comments:id=107156",
        },
        {
            id = 239211,
            score = 9,
            author = "129603",
            text = "http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10680 - for alliance\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10681 - for horde\n\nthe quest is \"The hand of Gul'dan\" where the whole series starts, really long chain",
            date = "2008-02-19T05:07:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10886#comments:id=239211",
        },
        {
            id = 51142,
            score = 6,
            author = "1966",
            text = "It is possible for a group to kill the Harbinger under Heroic difficulty and shuffle players into the instance to talk with Milhouse and complete the quest. This is similar to how it used to be possible to shuffle players into an instance to retrieve the key fragments for Karazhan.\n\nI recommend doing it as soon as you can before Blizzard 'fixes' it. ^_^",
            date = "2007-03-14T14:43:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10886#comments:id=51142",
        },
    },
    [10887] = {
        {
            id = 1639491,
            score = 35,
            author = "680985",
            text = "For those of you who don't care how many people \"Soloed him as ___!, yay!\" The entrance to the tunnel you find Akuno in is at coords 31.2, 52.6, the Shadow Tomb. As soon as you exit the hallway to the main room he is to the left.",
            date = "2012-03-14T13:06:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10887#comments:id=1639491",
        },
        {
            id = 31321,
            score = 25,
            author = "Illimin",
            text = "I was able to solo this as a 64 mutilate rogue - incredibly challenging. You can't let him tank one as he dies within ~15 seconds of doing so, so tank and kill both as best you're able. If you clear from him to outside and run back, you can just get him to skip the first spawn.\n\nMobs you need to clear:\n2 - Interrogator next to him and the mob closest to the Interrogator (pull it carefully so you don't get its neighbour)\n2 - the mobs in the next (second) room (one patrolling, one next to the doorway)\n1 - the mob in the third room\n2 - outside, the mobs on either side of the entrance\n\nThis is as far as I could clear and still have time to get back to him and get him to walk and not snag the newly-spawned. Then, walking with him, you fight:\n\n0-2 mobs in the first room, depending on whether you get back fast enough\n2-4 mobs in the third room, depending on whether he aggroes the ones on the sides (two spawn here)\n2-5 outside - two more spawn here and there are 3 patrollers in the area as well. How many you fight depends on their pathing.\n\nGood luck! This is extremely gratifying to solo, especially if you overcome unexpected adds.",
            date = "2007-02-05T15:30:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10887#comments:id=31321",
        },
        {
            id = 363791,
            score = 7,
            author = "146819",
            text = "Pretty easy for an escort quest IMO. Akuno's Chain Lightning hits like a truck (can easily blast off half a mob's health bar), and you rarely get more mobs than you can handle. He does have low health though, and since you can't heal or buff him you need to make sure you can down the mobs before he dies (odd that a Shaman-type NPC wouldn't have at least a Lesser Healing Wave...). He also falls into the group of NPCs involved in escape-type escort quests who don't seem to understand that escaping is easier if you RUN instead of WALK....\n\nUp until the ramp leading out of the tomb, you only have to worry about respawns. Once you get to the bottom of the ramp, two mobs spawn (both were Cabal Skirmishers (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21661) for me, but they might be random); kill them and leave the tomb. The two Skirmishers by the entrance probably respawned by now, so take them out. After you get a certain distance away from the tomb (30-45 yards, I'd say), there's another ambush of two mobs. You might run into a problem here, since you might aggro the patrol (the 2 mobs riding Felsteeds that for some reason constantly run back and forth between Auchindoun and the Shadow Tomb). If you don't run into them, you should be fine.",
            date = "2008-08-28T08:00:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10887#comments:id=363791",
        },
        {
            id = 858711,
            score = 7,
            author = "427484",
            text = "I just don't understand.. why blizzard but 2 of the same rewards (Mekeda's Gift) and (Unearthed Orb).. they do have the same attribute.",
            date = "2009-10-03T20:52:12-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10887#comments:id=858711",
        },
        {
            id = 320304,
            score = 4,
            author = "162777",
            text = "I had an interesting escort with him, I cleared the whole path and in the middle of the hallway and turns around and Chain Lightning's one of the mobs in the other room for no reason.\n\nYeah, I couldn't heal, buff, or do anything to help him. He can however handle one mob alone succesfully with his overpowered Chain Lightning.",
            date = "2008-07-05T03:21:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10887#comments:id=320304",
        },
    },
    [10888] = {
        {
            id = 36265,
            score = 120,
            author = "15108",
            text = "This is the final step in the quest line to obtain the key for The Eye, which is the raid wing of Tempest Keep.\n\nIn reference to the Phoenix-Fire Band quest reward, the final boss of The Eye is Kael'thas Sunstrider who is well renowned for his use of fire magic (WC3: TFT).",
            date = "2007-02-15T05:25:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10888#comments:id=36265",
        },
        {
            id = 217670,
            score = 97,
            author = "Vlad",
            text = "The chain to get the key (though not required, you get \"Champion of the Naaru\" title):\n\n1. Q: The Hand of Gul'dan (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10680)\n2. Q: Enraged Spirits of Fire and Earth (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10458)\n3. Q: Enraged Spirits of Water (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10480)\n4. Q: Enraged Spirits of Air (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10481)\n5. Q: Oronok Torn Heart (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10513)\n6. Q: I was a lot of things (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10514)\n7. Q: A Lesson Learned (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10515)\n8. Q: The Cipher of Damnation - Truth and History (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10519) (3 quests below:)\n\n8.1. Q: First Fragment of Damnation (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10527) (Map (http://www.wowhead.com/?maps=3520:300500))\n8.1.a. Grom'tor Son of Oronok\n8.1.b. The Cipher of Damnation - Gromtors charge\n8.1.c. The Cipher of Damnation - The first fragment recovered\n\n8.2. Q: Second Fragment of Damnation (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10546) (Map (http://www.wowhead.com/?maps=3520:480570))\n8.2.a. Ar'tor, Son of Oronok\n8.2.b. Demonic Crystal Prisons\n8.2.c. Lohn'goron, Bow of the Torn-heart\n8.2.d. The Cipher of Damnation Ar'tor's Charge\n8.2.e. The Cipher of Damnation - The Second Fragment Recovered\n\n8.3. Q: Third Fragment of Damnation (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10521) (Map (http://www.wowhead.com/?maps=3520:440230))\n8.3.a. Borak, Son of Oronok\n8.3.b. Of Thistleheads and Eggs...\n8.3.c. The Bundle of Bloodthistle\n8.3.d. To Catch A Thistlehead\n8.3.e. The Shadowmoon Shuffle\n8.3.f. What Illidan Wants, Illidan Gets...\n8.3.g. The Cipher of Damnation - Borak's Charge\n8.3.h. The Cipher of Damnation - The Third Fragment Recovered\n\n9. The Cipher of Damnation (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10588)\n\nAnd the hardest part:\n10. Received mail from Khadgar\n11. Trial of the Naaru - Mercy (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10884) (Shattered Halls Heroic)\n12. Trial of the Naaru - Strength (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10885) (Shadow Labyrinth Heroic and Steamvault)\n13. Trial of the Naaru - Tenacity (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10886) (The Arcatraz heroic)\n14. Trial of the Naaru - Magtheridon (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10888) (Duh..)\nYou recieve: [The Tempest Key] (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=31704)",
            date = "2008-01-13T09:26:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10888#comments:id=217670",
        },
        {
            id = 107157,
            score = 41,
            author = "Navaash",
            text = "With today's annoucement by Blizzard that there will now be no attunement required to enter The Eye, it is no longer necessary to do this quest:\n\nhttp://forums.worldofwarcraft.com/thread.html?topicId=110637185\n\nHowever the quest will remain in game; the same post also implies they may add a reward in the future for those who have fully completed this questline.\n\nSo don't worry, you can still get your Phoenix-fire Band. =)",
            date = "2007-06-19T12:24:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10888#comments:id=107157",
        },
        {
            id = 211125,
            score = 37,
            author = "Corgyll",
            text = "Just confirmed by talking to a gamemaster that you HAVE to complete the attunement-quest to Serpentshrine Cavern AND Trial of the Naaru: Magtheridon to get the title \"Champion of the Naaru\".\nIt's stated in the latest patchnotes but most people miss it.",
            date = "2008-01-01T17:20:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10888#comments:id=211125",
        },
        {
            id = 1335567,
            score = 18,
            author = "Netspook",
            text = "For those using the wowhead client/profiler:\n\nThis is the OLD version of the quest, with 10888 as the quest ID. If you didn't do it when the title was available, you will NEVER be able to do it, UNLESS you still have the old version in your quest log.\n\nThe new version of the quest, has 13430 as quest ID, and can be found here:\n\nTrial of the Naaru: Magtheridon (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13430)\n\nDo note that regardless of what version you did, wowhead profiler will show one quest as complete, and the other as INcomplete, and both will have the same name. So, to clear up the mess, mark the incomplete quest in your profile, and hit the Exclude button.",
            date = "2011-02-14T04:20:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10888#comments:id=1335567",
        },
    },
