    [10911] = {
        {
            id = 26709,
            score = 193,
            author = "16172",
            text = "Very difficult. Takes 7 shots... so many adds.... tough quest bring a friend.\n\nYOU NEED YOUR PET BAR, MAKE SURE IT'S SHOWN!\n\nNorthern Cannon: 61, 60\nSouthern Cannon: 65, 68",
            date = "2007-01-28T22:06:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10911#comments:id=26709",
        },
        {
            id = 707956,
            score = 90,
            author = "362388",
            text = "Okay, I guess I'm the slow one on this quest... I read all the comments and tried to do this in-game and took FOREVER standing-around trying to figure out what I was supposed to do, and I couldn't figure-out how to get my cannon to fire once I took-it under control. I kept reading comments above about imps and I was saying to myself \"What Imps? I don't see any imps!\".. so if anyone else is a bit slow like me, here's what you do:\n\n1) take-over the cannon (if you can't figure this out, you're slower then me!)\n2) you'll get a \"pet action bar\" over your own bar (I somehow missed this)... don't summon any pets after taking-over the cannon or you'll lose the cannon!\n3) don't use \"attack\"... for those who use pets, that's not what you use!  I sat around for seemingly 10 minutes trying to get my cannon to \"attack\" once I realized there was a pet-action bar!\n4) there's two seperate attack modes on the pet action bar that you do use to attack... kinda colored green and blobish looking... use those to start the attack!\n5) once you get-off the first shot, imps will start coming out of the teleporter to attack (suicide bomb) your fel cannon... kill them as quick as you can by any means necessary... they don't have much health but come fast... any area-effect weapons should do quite well here... I used my Death and Decay AoE as a Death Knight... worked quite-well at wiping-out multiple imps.\n6) wait for the \"cooldown\" of the fel cannon and hit it again (and again, and again)... it will take multiple shots to destroy the portal, all while imps try to kamikaze into your fel cannon... kill the imps at all costs.\n\nThat's pretty much it... I had a hard time figuring out what I was supposed to do for this quest, so if you're like me, I hope the above helps out!",
            date = "2009-05-06T20:22:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10911#comments:id=707956",
        },
        {
            id = 26960,
            score = 72,
            author = "17633",
            text = "Actually this is soloable by the melee classes, using my tip!\nSimply walk slightly backwards as you hit the imp, and you wont get the damage when he dies, just some very small damage from the imp attacking you.\nI activated the cannon, and just used artillery whenever it came up. I kept meleeing the imps (walking back as i hit each one) and after 6 the dog came out. I just tanked him with evasion while i kept hitting imps and one more cannonball did it.",
            date = "2007-01-29T07:44:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10911#comments:id=26960",
        },
        {
            id = 5839002,
            score = 54,
            author = "piediddly",
            text = "If you are trying to complete your Loremaster Achievement, coming from Dragonflight xpac, lemme explain how I completed this quest.\n\nGo to one of the fel cannons, right-click the ammo which will be located in your bag.  If you look on the left side above your topmost action bar, you'll find an extra 'pet' bar now visible.\nOnly one button matters to us, & that is the artillery button, which will destroy the transporter.\nAt the northern cannon, the demons will appear from the left side of the transporter, so stand to the left of the fel cannon.  At the southern cannon, the demons appear from the right side of the transporter, so stand to the right of the fel cannon.\nYou're gonna want to use any AoE to down the demons that will arrive to destroy your cannon.  Simply kill the demons yourself, while waiting for the fel cannon's artillery CD (12 seconds, I think) to finish then just fire the cannon's artillery.  It will take seven shots to destroy each transporter.\n\nEZ-PZ, lemon-squeezy, your quest should now be completed.  I hope this helps!",
            date = "2024-04-23T22:32:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10911#comments:id=5839002",
        },
        {
            id = 22197,
            score = 42,
            author = "11170",
            text = "Northern Cannon: 61,60\nSouthern Cannon: 65,68\n\nJust use your Naturalized ammunition, and kill all the imps. Very low hp.Void terrors will spawn too but they shouldnt be too hard.\n\nCannon tooltip says 7 shot to kill, so now you know what to do.\nUse your Druid signal and your done",
            date = "2007-01-20T17:49:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10911#comments:id=22197",
        },
    },
    [10912] = {
        {
            id = 26315,
            score = 59,
            author = "15365",
            text = "As a heads up for any tanks choosing a reward, a later quest (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10365) yields the same exact neck piece as \"Natasha's Battle Chain\".\n\nIf you don't mind waiting for a level, go ahead and get one of the dps necks to help you solo.",
            date = "2007-01-28T10:39:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10912#comments:id=26315",
        },
        {
            id = 22827,
            score = 46,
            author = "13511",
            text = "This quest is doable by both factions, as I am a horde and was able to complete it. This part of the quest is soloable as well, you'll note the quest doesn't suggest more then one player and you certainly don't need anyone else.\n\nThe houndmaster, who is in fact elite, doesn't really put up much of a fight towards the ancients you summon to help. During the fight, he will yell \"Release the hounds!\", much like the old scarlet named in the library. This summons one non-elite void hound which didn't help him much.",
            date = "2007-01-22T14:06:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10912#comments:id=22827",
        },
        {
            id = 36773,
            score = 37,
            author = "24265",
            text = "Remember to not delete the Evergrove Wand. You'll have to re-do the end part of the quest if you do.",
            date = "2007-02-16T03:55:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10912#comments:id=36773",
        },
        {
            id = 62821,
            score = 33,
            author = "15216",
            text = "Don't throw away your wand after you kill him.",
            date = "2007-04-06T01:12:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10912#comments:id=62821",
        },
        {
            id = 29462,
            score = 31,
            author = "1171",
            text = "If you don't hold aggro on the Hound-master, and let the treants tank, you will not get kill credit for the quest.\n\nIn the event that this happens, make sure you signal the druid NPC _before_ you abandon to reattempt - as of a few patches ago, abandoning a quest will destroy all associated quest items, and the flare is counted as a component for this quest so you won't be able to summon the druid to reinitiate the quest. (Yea I found out the hard way.)",
            date = "2007-02-02T12:37:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10912#comments:id=29462",
        },
    },
    [10913] = {
        {
            id = 18407,
            score = 36,
            author = "Lustral",
            text = "For whatever reason, the bodies on the ground are not actually labeled as initiates and guardians.  Auchenai warriors and vindicators are the only corpses in the area, and using your Sha'tar Torch will burn them, giving you credit for what it thinks are initiates and guardians.\n\nThe corpses can be found at (35, 75), southwest of Auchidoun, just below the 'A' in Auchidoun.",
            date = "2006-12-29T01:31:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10913#comments:id=18407",
        },
        {
            id = 24701,
            score = 17,
            author = "15982",
            text = "Location confirmed. The quest has been changed to require you burn warriors and vindicators.",
            date = "2007-01-25T21:53:23-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10913#comments:id=24701",
        },
        {
            id = 233499,
            score = 11,
            author = "112741",
            text = "There's a good way to find out if the bodies are burnable:\n\nTarget the corpse and if they appear as neutral towards you, they can be burned.\nThey spawn dead unlike the other mobs. Also The Sha'tar warriors that burn can be\nfound with Slain -infront of their their name. Hope this helps!",
            date = "2008-02-11T11:55:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10913#comments:id=233499",
        },
        {
            id = 135016,
            score = 8,
            author = "76136",
            text = "Additional note, you can only target the corpses that spawn on the ground as corpses.  The Sha'tar warriors and the poor mobs that respawn to fight them specifically cannot be burned.  I tried, but wouldn't let me.\n\nIf a body is at a Sha'tar's feet, no good.  Go for the ones just lying in the open.",
