    [10916] = {
        {
            id = 130274,
            score = 126,
            author = "47987",
            text = "As of today, I found the item at\n54.63\nI was looking into buying the Fei Fei treat and while searching for the Master leatherwork to buy the \"Silken Thread\" I stumbled with a mount on the ground.\nThis is just outside the inn on the back.",
            date = "2007-08-01T04:44:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10916#comments:id=130274",
        },
        {
            id = 1765669,
            score = 91,
            author = "1057028",
            text = "I had a bit of trouble figuring this one out, as it was nothing like the (mind you, outdated) comments here told me. Here's what you have to do:\n\n1) Go to the Leatherworking Trainer, Brumman, at 54,63 and buy a https://www.wowhead.com/item=4291 from him.\n\n2) Next, go to around 56,62, where you'll find both Fei Fei and Warrant Officer Tracy Proudwell. The dog should have a blue question mark over it's head. Talk to the Warrant Officer and exchange your https://www.wowhead.com/item=4291 for a https://www.wowhead.com/item=31799.\n\n3) Once you have the said item, you should be able to complete a quest to Fei Fei, after which the dog would start skittering around different places and digging the ground but will be 'unsatisfied with this hiding spot' for a couple of times, before eventually leading you to a place where he'll bury the treat, making the object Fei Fei's Cache (so, a pile of dirt) appear and you'll be able to dig up the beads.\n\n4) Once you have the https://www.wowhead.com/item=31795, just return to Assistant Klatu inside the inn and ta-da -- quest complete!\n\nI hope this helps.",
            date = "2012-11-21T07:17:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10916#comments:id=1765669",
        },
        {
            id = 372573,
            score = 27,
            author = "Megami",
            text = "Everyone who keeps saying you don't need to feed the treat is half wrong and half right. If someone has recently done the quest the mound will be there, if no one has done it recently the mound will not be there and you will spend 10 min running around searching. If you don't see a mound behind the inn with sparkles than you have to feed the treat.",
            date = "2008-09-09T14:39:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10916#comments:id=372573",
        },
        {
            id = 238652,
            score = 26,
            author = "Infernus",
            text = "Do not purchase the dog treat or follow him around, read the posts above, go behind the inn, you'll see a mound, mouse over it to see \"Fei Fei's Cache\". Open it, done & done",
            date = "2008-02-18T10:56:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10916#comments:id=238652",
        },
        {
            id = 62077,
            score = 25,
            author = "darkangelstrike",
            text = "The phrase \"Klaatu barada nikto\" originates from the 1951 Cold-War-era science fiction film The Day the Earth Stood Still. The phrase \"Gort! Klaatu barada nikto!\" was used to stop Gort, the robot in the film, from destroying the world.\n\nThere is no known translation for the phrase, although \"Klaatu\" is the name of the humanoid alien protagonist in the film, while nikto means nobody in Russian.\n\nIn World of Warcraft: The Burning Crusade, two NPCs exist together named Klaatu and Barada. One named Nikto hasn't been sighted yet.\n\nFrom: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Klaatu_barada_nikto",
            date = "2007-04-04T15:18:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10916#comments:id=62077",
        },
    },
    [10917] = {
        {
            id = 34264,
            score = 59,
            author = "22576",
            text = "It's easiest to do this quest while working on these others for the fastest overall progress, reputation, and XP. I found that all the enemies for and around these other quests dropped the feathers adequately enough.\n\nFor the Horde:\nStymying the Arakkoa (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9987)\nThe Eyes of Skettis (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10847)\nArakkoa War Path (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10868)\n\nFor the Alliance:\nStymying the Arakkoa (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=9986)\nThe Eyes of Skettis (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10847)\nThin the Flock (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10869)",
            date = "2007-02-11T19:14:51-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10917#comments:id=34264",
        },
        {
            id = 213666,
            score = 29,
            author = "Brmonkey",
            text = "That is exactly what they are modeled after. The Skeksis from The Dark Crystal.",
            date = "2008-01-06T05:57:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10917#comments:id=213666",
        },
        {
            id = 118556,
            score = 21,
            author = "4130",
            text = "It should be noted here that the random-suffix BOE blues and rares rewarded from Arakkoa feather turn-ins and from minibosses in Skettis have a slightly different, more class-specific set of random suffixes.\n\nof the Mind <- mage-centric\nof the Vision <- priest-centric\nof the Nightmare <- warlock-centric\n\nof the Grove <- druid-centric\nof the Shadow <- rogue-centric\n\nof the Hunt <- hunter-centric\nof the Ancestor <- shaman-centric\n\nof the Battle <- warrior-centric\nof the Crusade <- paladin-centric\n\nOf course the stats of these suffixes benefit other classes as well, but these suffixes have a more specific design than, say, Bandit or Sorceror.",
            date = "2007-07-10T11:46:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10917#comments:id=118556",
        },
        {
            id = 320778,
