            score = 9,
            author = "Aurleis1",
            text = "Video Guide: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jzT7KTSJU9I\n\n1.  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10957\n•\009Accept the quest, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10957, from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=23158, at the Sanctuary of Shadows, inside the [zone=3959] (Outland).\n•\009Travel southwest, to the Reflectory and enter the room.\n•\009Speak with a stealthed https://www.wowhead.com/npc=23191, as you enter the room, and select \"I'm with you, Akama.\"\n•\009https://www.wowhead.com/npc=23191 will begin channeling a spell at the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22841.  This will make the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=23215, that surround the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22841 killable.\n-\009-\009Kill the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=23215.\n•\009The https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22841 will move closer to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=23191 and they will begin to fight.  Help out your buddy, https://www.wowhead.com/npc=23191, and slay the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22841.\n•\009Exit the room and return to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=23158, at the Sanctuary of Shadows to turn in the quest.\n\nFull Guide (http://www.wowhead.com/item=32757/blessed-medallion-of-karabor#comments:id=2249836) to obtain https://www.wowhead.com/item=32757.\n\nIf you're unsure about which stage of the quest line you are in to obtain the https://www.wowhead.com/item=32757, enter the following script into the chat box (special thanks to Vlad for the script):\n\n[faction=932]\n/run local y={568,571,574,575,622,628,705,706,707,708,944,946,947,948,949,985,958,957,959}print\"The Aldor:\"for i,q in ipairs(y)do q=\"10\"..q print(i,\"\\124cffffff00\\124Hquest:\"..q..\"\\124h[\"..q..\"]\\124h\\124r\",IsQuestFlaggedCompleted(q)and YES or NO)end\n\n[faction=934]\n/run local y={683,684,685,686,622,628,705,706,707,708,944,946,947,948,949,985,958,957,959}print\"The Scryers:\"for i,q in ipairs(y)do q=\"10\"..q print(i,\"\\124cffffff00\\124Hquest:\"..q..\"\\124h[\"..q..\"]\\124h\\124r\",IsQuestFlaggedCompleted(q)and YES or NO)end",
            date = "2015-09-11T00:34:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10957#comments:id=2250099",
        },
        {
            id = 2111489,
            score = 8,
            author = "1428060",
            text = "Another Blizzard fail.  Positioning of the quest giver should have been more obvious, so you couldn't fail to pick it up if eligible.",
            date = "2015-02-19T17:25:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10957#comments:id=2111489",
        },
    },
    [10958] = {
        {
            id = 858520,
            score = 139,
            author = "269629",
            text = "Make sure you do this BEFORE fighting Akama's Shade.\n\nWe knew that defeating Akama's Shade made the Broken friendly, which we figured would then let us talk to the questgiver--but, unless you're required to come here twice just for that (which seems incredibly redundant), you have to talk to the Broken first.\n\nWe defeated the Shade only to get a quest telling us to defeat the Shade... fun times.  Thanks, Blizzard.",
            date = "2009-10-03T15:50:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10958#comments:id=858520",
        },
        {
            id = 1570540,
            score = 72,
            author = "Teiwazgod",
            text = "You need to go see https://www.wowhead.com/npc=23158 ignore what quest tells you",
            date = "2011-11-12T15:28:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10958#comments:id=1570540",
        },
        {
            id = 98896,
            score = 28,
            author = "19650",
            text = "This is a quest involved in the Black Temple Attunement Chain:\n\nThe Black Temple attunement starts at The Altar of the Sha'tar for Aldors, and the Sanctum of the Sun for Scryers. Both are in Shadowmoon Valley.\n\nAldors start attunement from Anchorite Ceyla (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21402) at the Altar of Sha'tar in Shadowmoon Valley:\n1. [A] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10568 [70] Tablets of Baa'ri\n2. [A] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10571 [70] Oronu the Elder\n3. [A] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10574 [70] The Ashtongue Corruptors\n4. [A] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10575 [70] The Warden's Cage\n\nScyers start attunement from Arcanist Thelis (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21955) at the Sanctum of Stars:\n1. [Sc] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10683 [70] Tablets of Baa'ri\n2. [Sc] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10684 [70] Oronu the Elder\n3. [Sc] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10685 [70] The Ashtongue Corruptors\n4. [Sc] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10686 [70] The Warden's Cage\n\nAfter that, the chain comes together for Aldor and Scryer.\n\n5. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10622 [70] Proof of Allegiance\n6. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10628 [70] Akama\n7. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10705 [70] Seer Udalo\n\nSeer Udalo is found in the Arcatraz (http://www.wowhead.com/?zone=3846) just before the last boss.\n\n8. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10706 [70] A Mysterious Portent\n9. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10707 [70] The Ata'mal Terrace\n10. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10708 [70] Akama's Promise\n\nAfter you finish this chain, you get to pick from some rewards and the chain seems like it ends. It continues however, inside Serpentshrine Cavern (http://www.wowhead.com/?zone=3607) from an NPC called Seer Olum (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=22820) who you can speak with after killing Fathom-Lord Karathress. He starts the next part of the Black Temple Chain by offering the quest:\n\n1. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10944 [70] The Secret Compromised\nFor this quest you just return to Akama.\n2. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10946 [70] Ruse of the Ashtongue\nIn this quest, you must use the costume Akama provides, and kill A'lar in Tempest Keep: The Eye while wearing the Ashtongue Cowl. Attunement for The Eye is a whole different chain.\n3. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10947 [70] An Artifact From the Past\nIn this, you need to gain access to The Battle of Mount Hyjal in Caverns of Time, and slay the first boss, Rage Winterchill. Attunement for this involves killing Lady Vashj and Kael'Thas Sunstrider.\n4. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10948 [70] The Hostage Soul\nFor this you must speak with A'dal in Shattrath city.\n5. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10949 [70] Entry into the Black Temple\nFor this, just speak with the naaru Xi'ri in front of Black Temple.\n6. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10985 [70] A Distraction for Akama\nUnknown what this quest asks of you, most likely you need to defend Xi'ri and make your way into Black Temple. At the end, you become attuned to enter and are granted The Medallion of Karabor (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=32649)\n\nAt this point, you are attuned and can enter Black Temple, although the chain continues and you can soon upgrade your medallion. It continues with:\n\n1. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10958 [70] Seek Out the Ashtongue\nYou just need to find Seer Kanai (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=23158) inside Black Temple.\n2. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10957 [70] Redemption of the Ashtongue\nThis involves entering Black Temple, and killing the boss the Shade of Akama (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=22841).\n3. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10959 [70] The Fall of the Betrayer\nAfter killing the Shade of Akama and returning to Seer Kanai, he asks one last thing of you. Kill Illidan The Betrayer. After doing so, you are granted the Blessed Medallion of Karabor, an upgraded version of your original medallion, and allows teleportation to the Black Temple.",
            date = "2007-06-05T18:29:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10958#comments:id=98896",
        },
        {
            id = 1497477,
            score = 23,
            author = "legumious",
            text = "A bit of a \"$%^& you\" from Blizzard on this one. \"Find Akama's Deathsworn\"=Find Seer Kanai. He's the one located completely out of Akama's sight way at the back of the room no one clears out until after Akama's shade is dead. Puts a bit of a grinding halt to the quest line when you have to wait a week.",
            date = "2011-08-18T02:47:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10958#comments:id=1497477",
        },
        {
            id = 1802833,
            score = 17,
            author = "1039410",
            text = "Having only briefly checked the Wowhead page, I was confused as how to complete this quest. I did the Akama encounter and then realized that was part of the next quest. So make sure you go to where the vendor is in the back of the big room and THEN kill the boss. Looks like I get to wait another week!",
            date = "2013-01-23T06:41:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10958#comments:id=1802833",
        },
    },
    [10959] = {
        {
            id = 98725,
            score = 319,
            author = "Taemojitsu",
            text = "You do not kill Illidan. After getting him to a certain percentage in the fight (with the assistance of Akama), Maiev comes to finish him off. As he dies, Illidan utters this line of dialogue:\nhttp://www.invictuswow.com/pics/BLACK_Illidan_16.wav\n\nIllidan may be dead (at least until we get tired of killing him), but his legacy lives on. His actions during his life will forever leave an imprint in our memories, as despite his eventual fall into darkness, Illidan Stormrage DID save the world. Multiple times.",
            date = "2007-06-05T14:05:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10959#comments:id=98725",
        },
        {
            id = 98898,
            score = 230,
            author = "19650",
            text = "This is a quest in the Black Temple attunement chain.\n\nAldors start attunement from Anchorite Ceyla (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21402) at the Altar of Sha'tar in Shadowmoon Valley:\n1. [A] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10568 [70] Tablets of Baa'ri\n2. [A] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10571 [70] Oronu the Elder\n3. [A] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10574 [70] The Ashtongue Corruptors\n4. [A] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10575 [70] The Warden's Cage\n\nScyers start attunement from Arcanist Thelis (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=21955) at the Sanctum of Stars:\n1. [Sc] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10683 [70] Tablets of Baa'ri\n2. [Sc] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10684 [70] Oronu the Elder\n3. [Sc] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10685 [70] The Ashtongue Corruptors\n4. [Sc] http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10686 [70] The Warden's Cage\n\nAfter that, the chain comes together for Aldor and Scryer.\n\n5. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10622 [70] Proof of Allegiance\n6. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10628 [70] Akama\n7. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10705 [70] Seer Udalo\n\nSeer Udalo is found in the Arcatraz (http://www.wowhead.com/?zone=3846) just before the last boss.\n\n8. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10706 [70] A Mysterious Portent\n9. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10707 [70] The Ata'mal Terrace\n10. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10708 [70] Akama's Promise\n\nAfteryou finish this chain, you get to pick from some rewards and the chainseems like it ends. It continues however, inside Serpentshrine Cavern (http://www.wowhead.com/?zone=3607) from an NPC called Seer Olum (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=22820)who you can speak with after killing Fathom-Lord Karathress. He startsthe next part of the Black Temple Chain by offering the quest:\n\n1. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10944 [70] The Secret Compromised\nFor this quest you just return to Akama.\n2. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10946 [70] Ruse of the Ashtongue\nInthis quest, you must use the costume Akama provides, and kill A'lar inTempest Keep: The Eye while wearing the Ashtongue Cowl. Attunement forThe Eye is a whole different chain.\n3. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10947 [70] An Artifact From the Past\nInthis, you need to gain access to The Battle of Mount Hyjal in Cavernsof Time, and slay the first boss, Rage Winterchill. Attunement for thisinvolves killing Lady Vashj and Kael'Thas Sunstrider.\n4. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10948 [70] The Hostage Soul\nFor this you must speak with A'dal in Shattrath city.\n5. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10949 [70] Entry into the Black Temple\nFor this, just speak with the naaru Xi'ri in front of Black Temple.\n6. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10985 [70] A Distraction for Akama\nUnknownwhat this quest asks of you, most likely you need to defend Xi'ri andmake your way into Black Temple. At the end, you become attuned toenter and are granted The Medallion of Karabor (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=32649)\n\nAtthis point, you are attuned and can enter Black Temple, although thechain continues and you can soon upgrade your medallion. It continueswith:\n\n1. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10958 [70] Seek Out the Ashtongue\nYou just need to find Seer Kanai (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=23158) inside Black Temple.\n2. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10957 [70] Redemption of the Ashtongue\nThis involves entering Black Temple, and killing the boss the Shade of Akama (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=22841).\n3. http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10959 [70] The Fall of the Betrayer\nAfterkilling the Shade of Akama and returning to Seer Kanai, he asks onelast thing of you. Kill Illidan The Betrayer. After doing so, you aregranted the Blessed Medallion of Karabor, an upgraded version of youroriginal medallion, and allows teleportation to the Black Temple.",
            date = "2007-06-05T18:31:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10959#comments:id=98898",
        },
        {
            id = 863690,
            score = 94,
            author = "111622",
            text = "Man I really wish they'd bring back things like this, chain quests for Raids, Attunements, Reputations, but right now it's all just about Loot and Achievements...",
            date = "2009-10-10T14:43:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10959#comments:id=863690",
        },
        {
            id = 1143906,
            score = 64,
            author = "splunge",
            text = "If you delete your Medallion of Karabor, and need it to complete this quest, talk to Xi'ri outside Black Temple to get a replacement.",
            date = "2010-10-16T01:03:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10959#comments:id=1143906",
        },
        {
            id = 162439,
            score = 42,
            author = "71903",
            text = "The Item you Gain, has a 15min CD and teleports you to just outside Black Temple, very useful just like a 15min CD hearthstone to Outlands.",
            date = "2007-10-03T15:56:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10959#comments:id=162439",
        },
    },
    [10969] = {
        {
            id = 194182,
            score = 57,
            author = "Tyrsenus",
            text = "There are no prerequisite quests.  This is a \"breadcrumbs\" quest, similar to how other quests send you to the next zone when you reach a certain level.  The prerequisites for this quest are as follows:\n\nYou must be level 67.\nYou must be honored with the Consortium.\nYou must not be currently on or have completed any quests that start from Commander Ameer (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=20448).\nYou must not have completed any quests that end at Commander Ameer.\n\nThe game assumes that you don't need to be sent to Commander Ameer if you're already doing (or have done) his quests and therefore have already met him.",
            date = "2007-11-30T22:01:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10969#comments:id=194182",
        },
        {
            id = 87892,
            score = 24,
            author = "37314",
            text = "Location of Ameer is 59.32",
            date = "2007-05-23T01:20:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10969#comments:id=87892",
        },
        {
            id = 2195930,
            score = 21,
            author = "Vlad",
            text = "Here is my experience summarized on how to get this item. I just did it on one of my characters to prepare for Timewalking in patch 6.2.\n\nBefore you start you might consider purchasing the required materials that will be required further into the quests. It can help reduce farm and speed up completion. At some point you'd need to turn in 10xhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=29460, but in addition you'd need one extra to continue the quest chain. So if I were you, buy at least 10 of these from the Auction House. Though this is not required, just saves you perhaps an hour of farm in total (if unlucky like me.)\n\nAnyway start by doing these quests in the following order:\n1. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10969 (requires Honored)\n2. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10970\n3. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10971 (repeatable, do once)\n4. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10973 (requires Revered)\n5. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10974\n6. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10975 (repeatable, do once)\n7. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10976\n8. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10977\n9. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10981 (repeatable, do once)\n10. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982 (requires Exalted)\n\nOne tip to greatly increase the speed of the farm is to actually enter Heroic [zone=3792] because you can farm the last boss indefinitely. He will first spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18431 and these mobs will spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18430 and these give 10 rep in Normal, and 21 rep in Heroic. If you have 4 hours to kill spamming one macro, basically create this:\n/cleartarget\n/targetexact Ethereal Apprentice\n/use [harm,nodead] ABILITYTHATCANBESPAMMEDTOKILLSTUFF\n/stopattack\n/tar player\n/use Battle Standard of Coordination\nI've included the https://www.wowhead.com/item=64399 to speed up the process. Also helps you not forget to spawn it once it is off cooldown and the old one despawns.\n\nOnce Exalted you can go to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22919 and complete the final quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982 (only requires Exalted, nothing else) for https://www.wowhead.com/item=32092 and you can spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22930 each time you visit the instance - no need to farm keys for one time use consumables.",
            date = "2015-06-20T07:07:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10969#comments:id=2195930",
        },
        {
            id = 89321,
            score = 8,
            author = "Lotara",
            text = "You get this quest at 45.36 in Netherstorm. Questgiver is \"Protectorate Advisor Rahim\". He is standing in the main room at Stormspire.",
            date = "2007-05-24T08:19:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10969#comments:id=89321",
        },
        {
            id = 6267956,
            score = 4,
            author = "Atno",
            text = "As of Patch 12.0.0 Midnight Prelaunch you need to have completed this quest chain in to get the key https://www.wowhead.com/item=32092 to summon Yor to get credit for the Endeavor \"Defeat Yor\" which gives 150 Endeavor Progress 150 House XP and 30 Community Coupons. I should add the NPC's you have to kill in this quest chain are Pre-launch level 80. They are easy but worth noting.\n\nEdited to add additional notes:\nWhen you get to the quest: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10977 Go to Mana Tombs. Make sure you running the dungeon in Heroic Dungeon mode. This is BC dungeon level so you can one shot everything. Kill the first boss Pandemonius  and enter the next room. To the left as you enter is a prison bubble. Go use the key on it and a friendly NPC will appear. He'll tell you to return to the Image of Commander Ameer back in Blade's Edge. This will complete the quest. Do what he says without completing the Dungeon. If you complete it you'll have to wait until Daily Reset before running it again.\nWhen you return to the Image of Commander Ameer turn in the quest. The quest text reads \"Word has gotten back of your heroics {name}. Haramad and I both that what you've done deserves a great reward. Though... Nevermind, you've done enough. I cannot in good conscience ask anything more from you.\" (This assumes you are Exalted). The https://www.wowhead.com/item=32092 quest will be available. Complete it and you'll immediately get https://www.wowhead.com/item=32092.  Then go back and complete mana-tombs, remembering to spawn Yor before killing the Nexus Prince.\nThis will complete the Endeavor.",
            date = "2026-01-23T06:27:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10969#comments:id=6267956",
        },
    },
    [10970] = {
        {
            id = 95386,
            score = 49,
            author = "19037",
            text = "Requires Honored with the Consortium to get this quest.",
            date = "2007-06-01T13:24:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10970#comments:id=95386",
        },
        {
            id = 87771,
            score = 48,
            author = "19634",
            text = "Unfortunately, I can't add much right now. The key dropped for me on my first kill, a Shocktrooper. Talking to some friends, it looks to be a random drop off of any etheral in the Etherium Staging Grounds (didn't check the new mobs they just added). Drop rate seems to be fairly high, of course this might be a biased opinion since I only killed one guy for it.\n\nThe completion of this quest leads to http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10971",
            date = "2007-05-22T22:46:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10970#comments:id=87771",
        },
        {
            id = 88083,
            score = 26,
            author = "54505",
            text = "mobs around 56 39, random drop. take me about 20kills",
            date = "2007-05-23T06:15:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10970#comments:id=88083",
        },
        {
            id = 2195931,
            score = 13,
            author = "Vlad",
            text = "Here is my experience summarized on how to get this item. I just did it on one of my characters to prepare for Timewalking in patch 6.2.\n\nBefore you start you might consider purchasing the required materials that will be required further into the quests. It can help reduce farm and speed up completion. At some point you'd need to turn in 10xhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=29460, but in addition you'd need one extra to continue the quest chain. So if I were you, buy at least 10 of these from the Auction House. Though this is not required, just saves you perhaps an hour of farm in total (if unlucky like me.)\n\nAnyway start by doing these quests in the following order:\n1. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10969 (requires Honored)\n2. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10970\n3. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10971 (repeatable, do once)\n4. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10973 (requires Revered)\n5. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10974\n6. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10975 (repeatable, do once)\n7. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10976\n8. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10977\n9. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10981 (repeatable, do once)\n10. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982 (requires Exalted)\n\nOne tip to greatly increase the speed of the farm is to actually enter Heroic [zone=3792] because you can farm the last boss indefinitely. He will first spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18431 and these mobs will spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18430 and these give 10 rep in Normal, and 21 rep in Heroic. If you have 4 hours to kill spamming one macro, basically create this:\n/cleartarget\n/targetexact Ethereal Apprentice\n/use [harm,nodead] ABILITYTHATCANBESPAMMEDTOKILLSTUFF\n/stopattack\n/tar player\n/use Battle Standard of Coordination\nI've included the https://www.wowhead.com/item=64399 to speed up the process. Also helps you not forget to spawn it once it is off cooldown and the old one despawns.\n\nOnce Exalted you can go to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22919 and complete the final quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982 (only requires Exalted, nothing else) for https://www.wowhead.com/item=32092 and you can spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22930 each time you visit the instance - no need to farm keys for one time use consumables.",
            date = "2015-06-20T07:08:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10970#comments:id=2195931",
        },
        {
            id = 1027310,
            score = 8,
            author = "107862",
            text = "As said above, this quest requires you to be Honored with the Consortium.\n\nAlso, after you complete this quest, you will be able to loot Ethereum Prison keys from any Outland ethereal that's not a part of the Consortium.  The follow-up actually requires these very same key in order to get the ID tag.\n\nAfter this point you can now loot these keys for Consortium rep as well as a few other BC reps.  In the past, I've freed Cenarion Expedetion and Sporregar NPCs from the chambers and got a bonus to those reputations, and there are other reps you can farm via the statis chambers.\n\nA list of ethereum which drop keys (but is not limited to just these areas) is below:\n\nMana-Tombs\nAny ethereum in Netherstom\nBashir Landing in Blade's Edge\nAnd possibly, though I haven't confirmed it, around Oshu'Gun in Nagrand.",
            date = "2010-04-26T23:42:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10970#comments:id=1027310",
        },
    },
    [10971] = {
        {
            id = 116430,
            score = 117,
            author = "Punkeh",
            text = "Before you start farming the mobs to get the key, look for this guy ;) he drops it 100%!\n\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?npc=23008#M0z",
            date = "2007-07-06T09:53:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10971#comments:id=116430",
        },
        {
            id = 1594528,
            score = 80,
            author = "dakota3",
            text = "To help clear up some of the apparent confusion on how to get these keys and what to do with them once you have them (assuming you're farming Consortium rep).\nThere are a couple of ways to get https://www.wowhead.com/item=29460.\n\n1. Camp out in the prescribed area in the quest and kill mobs until it drops. This option is a grind.\nWowhead lists the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=23008 as having a 95% drop rate for the item, but he's a reasonably rare spawn, so you could be waiting a long time before you find him.\nThe next best drop rate is about 7% off other mobs in the quest zone.\nEither way it's painful unless you get lucky.\n\n2. Run Heroic [zone=3792]. One run should give you approximately 4 to 6 https://www.wowhead.com/item=29460. Since you will be getting rep anyway, killing mobs in the instance - this seems a preferable option if you're farming rep with the Consortium.\n\nNext, fly to the quest area and find the Ethereum Staging Grounds. Location 54.6 / 46.5 should put you in the right spot. Use the key(s) to open one of the pink bubble Ethereum prisons.\nThe mob that comes out of the prison will drop a https://www.wowhead.com/item=31957 with about a 98% drop rate.\n\nComplete quest.\nOnce you hand in the quest it will turn into a repeatable quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10972, which will give you approx 300 rep per turn in and also unlock the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10973.",
            date = "2011-12-11T15:14:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10971#comments:id=1594528",
        },
        {
            id = 87789,
            score = 58,
            author = "19634",
            text = "This seems to be a quest thats meant to be done as you do all the other quests in this area as the drop rate is, for me, significantly smaller than the last quest.\nIf you are just starting out in this area, make an effort to turn the salvaged key in right away so you can grab this quest and soften the blow of this grind.\n\nAs a side note, since wowhead doesn't mention it, the precursor to this quest is http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10970",
            date = "2007-05-22T23:07:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10971#comments:id=87789",
        },
        {
            id = 2349740,
            score = 40,
            author = "CzechCloud",
            text = "For anyone dumb as me, you are supposed to drop [item=29460 domain=www] instead of a I.D. Tag.\n\nYou will use this key to open a prison at 54 , 40 and voila.",
            date = "2016-07-10T04:32:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10971#comments:id=2349740",
        },
        {
            id = 87763,
            score = 34,
            author = "13874",
            text = "Repeatable reputation quest, grants 250 rep with the Consortium at level 70.\n\nIn my opinion, if your goal is to simply grind Consortium rep, farming Zaxxis Insignias is still much more effective. Times may vary for different people, but it took me a long time of pretty steady killing to get 1 key for an ID tag.",
            date = "2007-05-22T22:34:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10971#comments:id=87763",
        },
    },
    [10972] = {
        {
            id = 93863,
            score = 21,
            author = "56968",
            text = "Answering my own question here.  Apparantly once you hit revered consortium this opens up a new quest with the keys.  You can continue to complete this one at 250 consortium a pop until then, not sure if you can continue afterwards as well though.",
            date = "2007-05-30T19:06:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10972#comments:id=93863",
        },
        {
            id = 89242,
            score = 17,
            author = "46539",
            text = "250 consortium rep per turn in",
            date = "2007-05-24T06:56:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10972#comments:id=89242",
        },
        {
            id = 1512483,
            score = 15,
            author = "dylacat",
            text = "I just solo'd Mana Tombs & got 8 keys in a 1/2 hour...much quicker than grinding those mobs.  :)",
            date = "2011-09-07T23:45:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10972#comments:id=1512483",
        },
        {
            id = 115684,
            score = 11,
            author = "MoonLite",
            text = "Once you have picked up the key, I higly recommend opening a prison with a full group with different classes.\n\nNot because you have a tough fight, but because the creature that comes out of the prison can drop a very nice Rare item with RANDOM enchantments on it, but it is BIND ON PICKUP, so it could go to waste if you can't use it yourself.\n\n(for me (as warlock) it dropped a Manaforged Sphere of the Prophet (lvl70 offhand +17int +17spi +39healing http://www.wowhead.com/?item=32520\nwhich, was a total waste on me >_< but is very nice for a healer)",
            date = "2007-07-04T20:14:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10972#comments:id=115684",
        },
        {
            id = 356060,
            score = 11,
            author = "Xarlequin",
            text = "There's a prequest for I.D tags to drop, here's how to do it:\n\nComplete this quest chain: (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10339).\nThis will give you a follow up quest: (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10970)\nAfter completing that quest you will get a new followup (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10971) telling you to get a I.D tag.\nAfter completing the followup quest you are able to loot I.D tags from all the monsters you release and kill by using the ethereal keys (ofcourse unless you end up with a friendly reputation guy instead of a monster).\n\n(My friend who I was experimenting on hit honored at the same time, so I don't know if that has anything to do with it, it might have).\n\nSincerely, Xarleen - Darksorrow EU",
            date = "2008-08-18T11:00:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10972#comments:id=356060",
        },
    },
    [10973] = {
        {
            id = 88264,
            score = 137,
            author = "Asfaril",
            text = "This quest requires that you are revered with Consortium",
            date = "2007-05-23T09:44:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10973#comments:id=88264",
        },
        {
            id = 88521,
            score = 84,
            author = "22801",
            text = "So you got this far and you're probably wondering \"what next?\"\n\nWhen I got here, the quests weren't filled in, so here is what happens:\n\n1) You've already done the prequests and started on your keys.  Key drop is low as stated above.  5% sounds right.\n\n2) All ethereals drop them, but the ones around mana forge ultris seem to have the best drop rate.\n\n3) They are SELLABLE.  Do not make these cheap as they are a pain in the ass, as below...\n\n4) You hand in your first key and get your follow up.  5 Keys.\n\n5) Hand in 5 keys, and go to Bashir's Landing in BEM (North)\n\n6) Open Stasis Chamber Alpha and fight an 80,000 hp Gronn.  Does a knockback attack (probably aggro wiping, but i dont know...) and a daze attack, but hey Blizzard:  If you're going to make a quest say \"5 man\" dont make the mob fearable.  Solo'd the mob with a mage friend taking out repops.  8 minute fight :P\n\n7) Hand in the Gronn's drop and take the next quest.  It took several re-reads of the quest, but essentially...\n\n    Get 5 Keys\n    Hand in 5 keys for 1 bashir's landing prison key\n    Open prison and beat up mob\n    Mob has a CHANCE to drop Mark of the Nexus-King\n           Enjoy :P\n\n8) Hand in mark for key to open stasis chamber in heroic mana tombs.  I think this will iether be a new room with new boss and a whole lot of treasure.  Enjoy phat loots.",
            date = "2007-05-23T14:07:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10973#comments:id=88521",
        },
        {
            id = 109960,
            score = 60,
            author = "34592",
            text = "I highly recommend farming Zaxxis Stalker and Raider at The Heap, 30,77.\n\nIt's easier to do an AoE farm there and they also drop Zaxxis Insignia =)\n\nAfter less than 45 minutes I got 50 Zaxxis Insignias and 6 Ethereum Prison Keys.",
            date = "2007-06-23T16:24:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10973#comments:id=109960",
        },
        {
            id = 157325,
            score = 34,
            author = "swotam",
            text = "If you are working on Consortium rep this quest isn't the best use of your keys. This quest and the follow-on grant 1000 rep total. Using the 5 keys and turning in 5 Prisoner ID Catalogue's will get you 1250 rep so all things being equal you are better to skip this and keep turning them in for 250 rep each. Of course, once you hit exalted with them then it's a different story :-)",
            date = "2007-09-23T19:05:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10973#comments:id=157325",
        },
        {
            id = 140717,
            score = 21,
            author = "15689",
            text = "This quest won't show up until you've completed Ethereum Secrets",
            date = "2007-08-19T17:41:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10973#comments:id=140717",
        },
    },
    [10974] = {
        {
            id = 111224,
            score = 32,
            author = "65562",
            text = "You have to turn it in to the Image of Ameer at 52, 15 in Blade's Edge not the image in Netherstorm.",
            date = "2007-06-25T20:52:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10974#comments:id=111224",
        },
        {
            id = 89146,
            score = 29,
            author = "19148",
            text = "coords 51, 12\n\nThuk the Defiant spawns. He is a level 70 elite. He is crowd controllable.  Traps, stuns, snares etc all work.\n\nI recommend 2 people at least for him.\n\nFollow up quest http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10976",
            date = "2007-05-24T04:44:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10974#comments:id=89146",
        },
        {
            id = 496582,
            score = 27,
            author = "78212",
            text = "Counts towards On the Blade's Edge Loremaster achievement.",
            date = "2008-12-07T20:57:42-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10974#comments:id=496582",
        },
        {
            id = 291522,
            score = 16,
            author = "BujuArena",
            text = "This may be a surprise: Soloed as an undead holy priest.  It took me 3 attempts.\n\nMy stats during the fight were:\n8571 health\n10020 mana\n230 mp5 (mana per 5 seconds) inside the 5-second rule\n636 mp5 outside the 5-second rule\n822 bonus damage\n2252 bonus healing\n1630 armor\n\nMy gear is pretty good.  I don't think I could have done it with much worse gear.  I also had some consumable buffs on (Elixir of Healing Power (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=22825) and Golden Fish Sticks (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=27666)).\n\nThis was my spec: 20/41/0 (http://www.wowhead.com/?talent=bxT0zhxZfbxcf0qVuVo).\n\nMy strategy was to keep Shadow Word: Pain (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=25368) and Touch of Weakness (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=25461) up the whole time while \"tanking\" him the best I could.  Inner Fire (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=25431) wasn't much use since he got 20 hits on me way too fast for it to be mana-efficient to recast it.  Well, maybe not.  I'm not sure.  Anyway, I didn't keep Inner Fire up.\n\nI didn't use Power Word: Shield (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=25218) (except to prevent dazing when initially running to my spot) because it costs too much mana and he'd break it in one hit anyway.\n\nI kept myself alive mainly with rank 1 Greater Heal (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=2060) and top rank Renew (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=25222), because of their mana-efficiency.  Whenever I was at about half health, I'd use top rank Greater Heal (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=25213) to catch up, and if I was close to death, Prayer of Mending (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=33076) (one charge of which is actually more mana-efficient than a Flash Heal (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=25235) at my +healing, believe-it-or-not) and top rank Greater Heal (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=25213) after.\n\nTo keep my mana up, I used my Earring of Soulful Meditation (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=30665) on cooldown and Shadowfiend (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=34433) twice.  On my winning attempt, I found Super Mana Potion (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=22832)s weren't necessary, but I'm sure they would have been if my gear wasn't as good as it was.  You may end up having to chug potions if you attempt this with worse gear.\n\nOn my first attempt, all was going well until he started giving me Mortal Wound, which is a stacking physical debuff which decreases healing by 5% per stack.  I found I could get rid of it and prevent it from stacking too high by casting Psychic Scream (http://www.wowhead.com/?spell=10890) on cooldown.  For this to be safe and not pull respawns from where he starts, I had to fight him on a spikey rocky thing pretty far north of where he spawns.  It seems dangerous, but his \"knockback\" ability just knocks you vertically and can't knock you off to your death.\n\nIt's tricky, but doable as a holy priest.  I'm not sure about shadow.  I don't think I can do the quest again as shadow to test it out, though.  Good luck, holy priests, and don't be too discouraged about your class' weaknesses!  Honestly, I didn't think this would be possible when I read the quest or spawned him the first time.  A clever priest is a powerful thing.",
            date = "2008-05-20T11:32:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10974#comments:id=291522",
        },
        {
            id = 1098634,
            score = 14,
            author = "217387",
            text = "You also NEED to have completed the quest \"A thousand worlds\" ([quest=10973 domain=www]), otherwise you won't be able to get it.",
            date = "2010-08-10T14:51:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10974#comments:id=1098634",
        },
    },
    [10975] = {
        {
            id = 932508,
            score = 34,
            author = "Tyrsenus",
            text = "This quest is repeatable (not noted at the time of this comment).",
            date = "2009-12-30T09:43:05-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10975#comments:id=932508",
        },
        {
            id = 105919,
            score = 16,
            author = "60129",
            text = "You know, as nice as it would be to be \"keyed\" for Yor in heroic mana-tombs, I cringe every time I get one of these keys made. You get 250 rep for every cage you open with a key, or combine 5 of them together, complete this quest and get 500 rep. 1250 > 500.\n\nMaybe I should wait until I'm exalted when rep doesn't matter so much.",
            date = "2007-06-17T09:47:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10975#comments:id=105919",
        },
        {
            id = 2195935,
            score = 14,
            author = "Vlad",
            text = "Here is my experience summarized on how to get this item. I just did it on one of my characters to prepare for Timewalking in patch 6.2.\n\nBefore you start you might consider purchasing the required materials that will be required further into the quests. It can help reduce farm and speed up completion. At some point you'd need to turn in 10xhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=29460, but in addition you'd need one extra to continue the quest chain. So if I were you, buy at least 10 of these from the Auction House. Though this is not required, just saves you perhaps an hour of farm in total (if unlucky like me.)\n\nAnyway start by doing these quests in the following order:\n1. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10969 (requires Honored)\n2. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10970\n3. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10971 (repeatable, do once)\n4. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10973 (requires Revered)\n5. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10974\n6. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10975 (repeatable, do once)\n7. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10976\n8. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10977\n9. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10981 (repeatable, do once)\n10. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982 (requires Exalted)\n\nOne tip to greatly increase the speed of the farm is to actually enter Heroic [zone=3792] because you can farm the last boss indefinitely. He will first spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18431 and these mobs will spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18430 and these give 10 rep in Normal, and 21 rep in Heroic. If you have 4 hours to kill spamming one macro, basically create this:\n/cleartarget\n/targetexact Ethereal Apprentice\n/use [harm,nodead] ABILITYTHATCANBESPAMMEDTOKILLSTUFF\n/stopattack\n/tar player\n/use Battle Standard of Coordination\nI've included the https://www.wowhead.com/item=64399 to speed up the process. Also helps you not forget to spawn it once it is off cooldown and the old one despawns.\n\nOnce Exalted you can go to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22919 and complete the final quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982 (only requires Exalted, nothing else) for https://www.wowhead.com/item=32092 and you can spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22930 each time you visit the instance - no need to farm keys for one time use consumables.",
            date = "2015-06-20T07:08:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10975#comments:id=2195935",
        },
        {
            id = 93076,
            score = 12,
            author = "16947",
            text = "The prerequisite for this quest is Stasis Chambers of Bash'ir (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10974)",
            date = "2007-05-29T11:09:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10975#comments:id=93076",
        },
        {
            id = 1905431,
            score = 6,
            author = "1137079",
            text = "Since you need to be Revered for this quest, it could be considered simpler to farm the land by Manaforge B'naar.\n\nYou'll pick up Zaxxis Insignia while you do it, which makes for a repeatable Turn In with the Consortium guy in Area 52 in the Netherstorm.",
            date = "2013-10-04T10:20:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10975#comments:id=1905431",
        },
    },
    [10976] = {
        {
            id = 1650765,
            score = 248,
            author = "Hairband",
            text = "I have this quest on my log and unfortunately, none of the helps here explain what this quest is all about.  I have plenty of addons to tell me where it is, or how to kill him, what are the prerequisites, now that it's patch 4.3.  This entire topic at this day seems so outdated, so basically if nothing here is helping you read further.\n\nFirst, the purpose of this quest is not for Loremaster--I don't believe that it counts toward that, based on what others have said as I already have it.  It is a quest chain to open up a certain heroic mode boss in Mana Tombs (Auchindoun) named Yor (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=22930).  He drops what would have been good rings at lvl 70.  He also drops some transmogrifiable green set gear.  Nothing fantastic but possibly fun to collect.\n\nWhat you are supposed to do is basically grind your Ethereum Prison Keys.  You need 5 keys then you convert them through the questgiver (Ameer--he's the guy on Bash'ir's Landing) to Ethereum Stasis Chamber Key (http://www.wowhead.com/item=29750/ethereum-stasis-chamber-key).\n\nOnce you have 1 of the Ethereum Stasus Chamber Keys, you get to open up an Ethereum Stasus Chamber.  So you're looking at a 5 to one ratio for every Status Chamber Keys you want, you need 5 of those Ethereum Prison Keys which is quite a hassle to begin with.  But there's further annoyance--each Ethereum Stasus Chamber may or may not contain a \"boss\" you need who will drop the Mark of the Nexus-King.  In other words, sometimes the Etherium Stasus Chamber contains a friendly NPC who gives you nothing (maybe a buff?) and thanks you for releasing him or her, plus maybe rep (I recall one being a Night Elf and giving me Cenariun Circle rep).  So you may get a boss OR you may get a friendly.  Who knows what percentage of the time you get a friendly versus a boss.\n\nSo, say you are lucky enough to get a boss.  These bosses appear to be Ethereum Prisoners (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=20889).  (If you check that link, it says the Marks of the Nexus-King item is actually a 24% drop rate at this point in time.)\n\nOne problem is that Wowhead does not have an ID number for the Ethereum Stasus Chambers--just the Prisoners contained inside.  So it's impossible to tell for me right now what percentage of what type of mobs that spawn from those chambers once you convert 5>1 keys from Ameer.  So it's a RNG in an RNG, whether you get a boss or a friendly, and IF you get a boss, what  % of the time the boss drops a Mark of the Nexus King.",
            date = "2012-04-08T16:14:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10976#comments:id=1650765",
        },
        {
            id = 314442,
            score = 106,
            author = "167649",
            text = "[70] Seek Out Ameer (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10969)\n\n[70] A Mission of Mercy (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10970)\n\n[70] Ethereum Secrets (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10971) (Repeatable)\n\n[70] A Thousand Worlds (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10973) (Only available at Revered)\n\n[70] Stasis Chambers of Bash'ir (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10974)\n\n[70] Purging the Chambers of Bash'ir (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10975) (Repeatable)\n\n[70] The Mark of the Nexus-King (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10976)\n\n[70] Stasis Chambers of the Mana-Tombs (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10977)\n\n[70] Nexus-Prince Shaffar's Persona lChamber (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10981) (Repeatable)\n\n[70] The Eye of Haramad (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10982) (Only available at Exalted)",
            date = "2008-06-26T22:44:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10976#comments:id=314442",
        },
        {
            id = 89283,
            score = 78,
            author = "noxx",
            text = "You have to give 5 [Ethereum Prison Key] to the Image of Commander Ameer at Bash'ir's Landing to get a key for one stasis chamber.\n\nAfter opening one of those chambers you have to fight a level 70 elite. I only did it once and i failed because i tried to solo it (lvl 70 warlock). It was immune to fear and its shadow bolts hit quite hard so I died at 75%. It could be possible with 3-4 people though.\n\nAccording to a comment on the item [Mark of the Nexus-King], it doesn't drop every time. In his case he killed 6 bosses and it didn't drop.\n\nAs it is a green item I also think that only one group member is able to loot it.",
            date = "2007-05-24T07:40:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10976#comments:id=89283",
        },
        {
            id = 102720,
            score = 59,
            author = "13869",
            text = "http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10969 starts the quest chain that leads you through a chain of quests before you can get this quest.\n\nHere's the chain:\n\n[70] Seek Out Ameer\n\n[70] A Mission of Mercy\n\n[70] Ethereum Secrets (Repeatable)\n\n[70] A Thousand Worlds (Only available at Revered)\n\n[70] Stasis Chambers of Bash'ir\n\n[70] Purging the Chambers of Bash'ir (Repeatable)\n\n[70] The Mark of the Nexus-King\n\n[70] Stasis Chambers of the Mana-Tombs\n\n[70] Nexus-Prince Shaffar's PersonalChamber (Repeatable)\n\nThe Eye of Haramad (Only available at Exalted)",
            date = "2007-06-11T22:16:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10976#comments:id=102720",
        },
        {
            id = 5755095,
            score = 42,
            author = "DarkKuno",
            text = "Don't waste time farming keys for this.  Just buy the https://www.wowhead.com/item=31941 from the Auction House and save yourself a lot of time and headache of potential bad RNG.",
            date = "2023-12-23T23:39:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10976#comments:id=5755095",
        },
    },
    [10977] = {
        {
            id = 92099,
            score = 65,
            author = "56015",
            text = "Stasis Chamber is beyond the room of the first boss Pandemonius in Mana-Tombs Heroic. An npc spawns when you open it. Return to Bash'ir Landing to complete quest. Now you need to grind another Mark of the Nexus-King to be able to open the final Stasis Chamber in Nexus-Prince Shaffar's room.",
            date = "2007-05-28T00:04:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10977#comments:id=92099",
        },
        {
            id = 92878,
            score = 59,
            author = "54503",
            text = "If you are exalted with them he'll give you shafar's chamber key without asking for another nexsus mark.",
            date = "2007-05-29T04:59:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10977#comments:id=92878",
        },
        {
            id = 6053331,
            score = 33,
            author = "IslaBonita",
            text = "The stasis chamber is located after the first boss, on the left side of the next room.",
            date = "2025-01-23T17:31:10-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10977#comments:id=6053331",
        },
        {
            id = 1121703,
            score = 30,
            author = "Keidric",
            text = "I can confirm the above posts. (Which are nearly 2.5 years old.)\n\nI found this whole process a bit confusing so I hope this helps.\n\nThis is how I got my rep:\n1) Every so often when I felt up to it, I collected [Zaxxis Insignia] from Netherstorm.  I held onto the [Ethereum Prison Key]'s (And even bought a couple cheap) until I got restless from the grind.\n\n2) I'd turn in the [Zaxxis Insignia] in A52.\n\n3a) Then I would fly over to Blades Edge and turn in the 5 [Ethereum Prison Key] for 1 [Ethereum Stasis Chamber Key] and 500 rep.  **Note:** I only did this (3a-3b) because I wanted the permanent key to open the Yor prison in mana-tombs. (Which ill mention in step 6.)  If you only care about maximizing reputation gain this step will cause you to loose up to 750 rep each time.  (This is because a person can *usually* turn in one key for 250 rep by means of the I.D. Cards in Netherstorm. Meaning 5 prison keys == 1,200 rep vs. the 500 for this quest.)\n\n3b) Each time I got a [Ethereum Stasis Chamber Key] I would go open one of the Blade's Edge chambers and hope the mini boss would drop the [The Mark of the Nexus-King.] (See previous quest.) It's about a 20% drop, and you only need get it once!  So if you choose to \"waste rep\" for the Yor Key, make sure to minimize the potential loss by getting only one stasis key at a time.\n\n3c) If you don't care about the Yor key ([The Eye of Haramad]) Just use the [Ethereum Prison Key] on the Netherstorm prison cells and loot the I.D. Cards.  You'll probably get 250 rep for each one and just skip the rest of this.  (I think they changed what comes out, I never saw a random faction non-hostile.)\n\n4) Once I got my [The Mark of the Nexus-King.] I went ahead and turned it in. Then I did this quest, finished it, and turned it in.\n\n(This is the part I was worried about, and a main reason I wrote this.)\n5) At this point I still wasn't exalted, so I simply did not accept the follow up quest that asked for yet another [The Mark of the Nexus-King.]  Instead I went the faster route using my remaining [Ethereum Prison Key]'s in Netherstorm, on the orb prisons, and then turned in the I.D Cards that I looted off the mini bosses there.\n\n6) Once I hit exalted, a new quest appeared in Blades Edge that required nothing but the rep.  It awarded the permanent Yor key. [The Eye of Haramad] Note: (The old repeatable quest that required [The Mark of the Nexus-King.] was still there so don't freak... Just ignore it.)\n\nCan also do the old BC dailies, one of them even gives a prison key.  Or run heroic mana-tombs.",
            date = "2010-09-16T10:53:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10977#comments:id=1121703",
        },
        {
            id = 92701,
            score = 22,
            author = "7240",
            text = "Easy to solo as a druid or rogue. If you're a druid just cast Sooth Animal on the nearest Mana Leech and you should be able to open the Chamber without agroing them. If you are a rogue you might have to use one of those items that reduce your agro radius before you attempt to open it.",
            date = "2007-05-28T19:50:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10977#comments:id=92701",
        },
    },
    [10981] = {
        {
            id = 127087,
            score = 42,
            author = "33682",
            text = "This quest requires you to farm keys after keys after keys, and get groups together to take down the Blades Edge stasis chamber bosses, praying for a Mark of the Nexus King to drop. Alternately you can just use those keys to open the 'easy' stasis prisons in Netherstorm, get prison ID tags, and get rep. When you reach exalted he'll hand over The Eye of Haramad which will summon Yor every run. The Stasis Chamber key from this quest only summons Yor once.\n\nIt's less stressful to just grind exalted and get the Eye of Haramad than to ever do this quest.",
            date = "2007-07-26T09:45:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10981#comments:id=127087",
        },
        {
            id = 2195938,
            score = 29,
            author = "Vlad",
            text = "Here is my experience summarized on how to get this item. I just did it on one of my characters to prepare for Timewalking in patch 6.2.\n\nBefore you start you might consider purchasing the required materials that will be required further into the quests. It can help reduce farm and speed up completion. At some point you'd need to turn in 10xhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=29460, but in addition you'd need one extra to continue the quest chain. So if I were you, buy at least 10 of these from the Auction House. Though this is not required, just saves you perhaps an hour of farm in total (if unlucky like me.)\n\nAnyway start by doing these quests in the following order:\n1. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10969 (requires Honored)\n2. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10970\n3. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10971 (repeatable, do once)\n4. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10973 (requires Revered)\n5. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10974\n6. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10975 (repeatable, do once)\n7. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10976\n8. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10977\n9. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10981 (repeatable, do once)\n10. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982 (requires Exalted)\n\nOne tip to greatly increase the speed of the farm is to actually enter Heroic [zone=3792] because you can farm the last boss indefinitely. He will first spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18431 and these mobs will spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18430 and these give 10 rep in Normal, and 21 rep in Heroic. If you have 4 hours to kill spamming one macro, basically create this:\n/cleartarget\n/targetexact Ethereal Apprentice\n/use [harm,nodead] ABILITYTHATCANBESPAMMEDTOKILLSTUFF\n/stopattack\n/tar player\n/use Battle Standard of Coordination\nI've included the https://www.wowhead.com/item=64399 to speed up the process. Also helps you not forget to spawn it once it is off cooldown and the old one despawns.\n\nOnce Exalted you can go to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22919 and complete the final quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982 (only requires Exalted, nothing else) for https://www.wowhead.com/item=32092 and you can spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22930 each time you visit the instance - no need to farm keys for one time use consumables.",
            date = "2015-06-20T07:08:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10981#comments:id=2195938",
        },
        {
            id = 2559963,
            score = 28,
            author = "Eommus",
            text = "This quest becomes unavailable if you do https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982.",
            date = "2018-03-27T11:32:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10981#comments:id=2559963",
        },
        {
            id = 215711,
            score = 26,
            author = "vexis58",
            text = "\"This quest requires you to farm keys after keys after keys, and get groups together to take down the Blades Edge stasis chamber bosses, praying for a Mark of the Nexus King to drop.\"\n\nYou don't get the Eye of Haramad automatically from reaching exalted with Consortium. You must first complete Stasis Chambers of the Mana-Tombs (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10977) which would require you to get 1 Mark of the Nexus King anyway. Unless you buy the Marks from the AH or something, you're going to have to kill the bosses in Blade's Edge anyway.",
            date = "2008-01-09T16:01:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10981#comments:id=215711",
        },
        {
            id = 6266235,
            score = 2,
            author = "Fragilicious",
            text = "Okay, so I bought Mark of the Nexus-King from the AH.\n\nI have Honoured rep with Consortium.\n\nI go to Image of Commander Ameer in Blades Edge Mountains.\n\nHe has no dialogue options for me.\n\nWhat am I doing wrong? Do I have to go through the whole quest chain?",
            date = "2026-01-21T05:47:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10981#comments:id=6266235",
        },
    },
    [10982] = {
        {
            id = 99073,
            score = 53,
            author = "30943",
            text = "you must be exalted with \"The Consortium\" to get this quest",
            date = "2007-06-06T00:16:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982#comments:id=99073",
        },
        {
            id = 142855,
            score = 45,
            author = "aelfric",
            text = "Note!  You must complete \"The Mark of the Nexus King\" (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10977) before you can get this.\n\nI just hit exalted, but I haven't found a mark, so I can't get the Eye yet.",
            date = "2007-08-23T12:58:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982#comments:id=142855",
        },
        {
            id = 2195939,
            score = 34,
            author = "Vlad",
            text = "Here is my experience summarized on how to get this item. I just did it on one of my characters to prepare for Timewalking in patch 6.2.\n\nBefore you start you might consider purchasing the required materials that will be required further into the quests. It can help reduce farm and speed up completion. At some point you'd need to turn in 10xhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=29460, but in addition you'd need one extra to continue the quest chain. So if I were you, buy at least 10 of these from the Auction House. Though this is not required, just saves you perhaps an hour of farm in total (if unlucky like me.)\n\nAnyway start by doing these quests in the following order:\n1. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10969 (requires Honored)\n2. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10970\n3. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10971 (repeatable, do once)\n4. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10973 (requires Revered)\n5. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10974\n6. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10975 (repeatable, do once)\n7. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10976\n8. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10977\n9. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10981 (repeatable, do once)\n10. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982 (requires Exalted)\n\nOne tip to greatly increase the speed of the farm is to actually enter Heroic [zone=3792] because you can farm the last boss indefinitely. He will first spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18431 and these mobs will spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18430 and these give 10 rep in Normal, and 21 rep in Heroic. If you have 4 hours to kill spamming one macro, basically create this:\n/cleartarget\n/targetexact Ethereal Apprentice\n/use [harm,nodead] ABILITYTHATCANBESPAMMEDTOKILLSTUFF\n/stopattack\n/tar player\n/use Battle Standard of Coordination\nI've included the https://www.wowhead.com/item=64399 to speed up the process. Also helps you not forget to spawn it once it is off cooldown and the old one despawns.\n\nOnce Exalted you can go to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22919 and complete the final quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982 (only requires Exalted, nothing else) for https://www.wowhead.com/item=32092 and you can spawn https://www.wowhead.com/npc=22930 each time you visit the instance - no need to farm keys for one time use consumables.",
            date = "2015-06-20T07:08:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982#comments:id=2195939",
        },
        {
            id = 1091795,
            score = 19,
            author = "427484",
            text = "Don't do my mistake:S\ni clicked that circle south of Manaforge Ultra, and the image showed up, but had no quest.\n\nThe Eye of Haramad (http://www.wowhead.com/item=32092) obtained from  Image of Commander Ameer (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=22919) in Blade's Edge Mountains (http://www.wowhead.com/zone=3522#npcs:100+1)\n\nNot from  Image of Commander Ameer (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=20482) in Netherstorm (http://www.wowhead.com/zone=3523). The map on this page not shown the right loaction.",
            date = "2010-07-29T17:11:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982#comments:id=1091795",
        },
        {
            id = 1699501,
            score = 10,
            author = "Hairband",
            text = "The purpose to getting this key is for the heroic boss, Yor, in Mana Tombs.  It doesn't count toward Loremaster and it doesn't give faction rep.  Therefore IMHO a lot of people have overlooked the quest because getting (1) 5 Ethereum Prison Keys to get (2) 1 Ethereum Stasus key to unlock a prison (3) to get a CHANCE of getting an enemy/boss (or you might get a worthless friendly NPC, maybe a buff or a bit of some other faction rep) and (4) to maybe get a 24% chance to get a Mark of the Nexus King off one of the enemy bosses just is so nuts.  A huge RNG grind to get an RNG mob and RNG loot in the mob... gadzooks!\n\nWhat you would be getting is the option to get a heroic boss, no more no less.",
            date = "2012-08-13T14:19:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10982#comments:id=1699501",
        },
    },
    [10983] = {
        {
            id = 87541,
            score = 35,
            author = "17256",
            text = "It's actually 55, 44",
            date = "2007-05-22T16:11:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10983#comments:id=87541",
        },
        {
            id = 147468,
            score = 34,
            author = "34072",
            text = "This is part of the quest chain to open up the Ogri'la daily quests.  You have to kill five different elite Sons of Gruul.  They are VERY tough and you must have a proper 5-man party to handle them (Tank, Healer, 3 DPS).  You might even want to bring along some extra people that can help out of party.\n\nQuest Chain:\nSpeak with the Ogre (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10984)\n... Mog'dorg the Wizened (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10983)\n...... Grulloc Has Two Skulls (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10995) (Grulloc)\n...... Maggoc's Treasure Chest (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10996) (Maggoc)\n...... Even Gronn Have Standards (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10997) (Slaag)\n......... Grim(oire) Business (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10998) (Vim'gol the Vile)\n............ Into the Soulgrinder (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11000) (Skulloc Soulgrinder)\n.............. Speak with Mog'dorg (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11022)",
            date = "2007-09-01T05:03:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10983#comments:id=147468",
        },
        {
            id = 89785,
            score = 14,
            author = "9020",
            text = "Follow-ups after completing this quest:\n\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10995\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10996\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10997\n\nThose are 5 men elite quests.",
            date = "2007-05-24T18:32:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10983#comments:id=89785",
        },
        {
            id = 718061,
            score = 4,
            author = "Kaliopae",
            text = "I spent a while trying to get this quest unsuccessfully. I was fairly sure I'd done 'Speak with the Ogre' but I couldn't get this follow on. It turns out that I had The Trouble Below (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11057) in my quest log, which also sends you to Mog'dorg. I suspect that you can do one OR the other, and that having 'The Trouble Below' locked me out of this one. Can anyone confirm?",
            date = "2009-05-16T14:06:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10983#comments:id=718061",
        },
        {
            id = 924217,
            score = 3,
            author = "438545",
            text = "Circle of Blood\nBlades Edge Mountains",
            date = "2009-12-20T21:53:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10983#comments:id=924217",
        },
    },
    [10984] = {
        {
            id = 110870,
            score = 45,
            author = "33985",
            text = "If you can't take the quest, that means you already spoke to the ogre Grok and took/finished his quest.\n\nI had the same problem with 2 of my friends when we were trying to do the chain, and it turns out that was the problem",
            date = "2007-06-25T10:09:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10984#comments:id=110870",
        },
        {
            id = 147465,
            score = 30,
            author = "34072",
            text = "This starts the quest chain to open up the Ogri'la daily quests.  You have to kill five different elite Sons of Gruul.  They are VERY tough and you must have a proper 5-man party to handle them (Tank, Healer, 3 DPS).  You might even want to bring along some extra people that can help out of party.\n\nQuest Chain:\nSpeak with the Ogre (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10984)\n... Mog'dorg the Wizened (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10983)\n...... Grulloc Has Two Skulls (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10995) (Grulloc)\n...... Maggoc's Treasure Chest (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10996) (Maggoc)\n...... Even Gronn Have Standards (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10997) (Slaag)\n......... Grim(oire) Business (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10998) (Vim'gol the Vile)\n............ Into the Soulgrinder (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11000) (Skulloc Soulgrinder)\n.............. Speak with Mog'dorg (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11022)",
            date = "2007-09-01T05:00:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10984#comments:id=147465",
        },
        {
            id = 87726,
            score = 13,
            author = "shadowgiant",
            text = "he's at 65,68",
            date = "2007-05-22T21:51:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10984#comments:id=87726",
        },
        {
            id = 1244146,
            score = 4,
            author = "Hipster",
            text = "Didn't know I had to start here for the Winter's Veil achievement Fa-la-la-la-Ogri'-la ... figured I was doing something wrong, after doing almost all the quests in Ogri'la.",
            date = "2010-12-18T20:22:48-06:00",
