        {
            id = 1555237,
            score = 8,
            author = "Akaeya",
            text = "Yeah, the Vial of the Sands was my original issue, too. I had to run out, mount using a different mount, and then fly around the area until all the npc's turned green for me. Then I could continue with the quest.",
            date = "2011-10-27T14:47:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11013#comments:id=1555237",
        },
    },
    [11014] = {
        {
            id = 1977564,
            score = 5,
            author = "Naexkyrnn",
            text = "\"...You'll be required to fill your work orders once per day.\n\nYeah, it's a bunch of crap jobs but even the ascendants started out as peons.\"\n\nSomebody give this daily quest giver an award for up front honesty! I must commend his straightforwardness.",
            date = "2014-07-03T22:09:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11014#comments:id=1977564",
        },
        {
            id = 3222643,
            score = 4,
            author = "DoctorShades24",
            text = "Are there any requirements for this to pop other than going in the quest line?\n\nNot showing up for me.",
            date = "2020-08-12T08:00:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11014#comments:id=3222643",
        },
        {
            id = 3249040,
            score = 3,
            author = "betsystoner",
            text = "Saw the quest marker on my map, but nobody was around to give it. This sometimes happens when you have to kill someone for a drop to start the quest. I got it on a whim by killing Arvoar the Rapacious.",
            date = "2020-11-14T14:26:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11014#comments:id=3249040",
        },
        {
            id = 3246976,
            score = 1,
            author = "robcjacob",
            text = "Commenting here for people in the 9.0 pre-patch looking for answers as to why there are no more quests for your Shadowmoon Valley (Outlands) Loremaster. I did have to get 310 flying for the next \"!\" exclamation point/quest marker to pop on the map. I did all the possible quests on the map that were marked (last one was where you rescue the green drake). I then tried and killed the Arvoar dude 2 times and never got any quest drop. The second I got 310 flying, the quest marker popped up. GLHF",
            date = "2020-11-09T09:16:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11014#comments:id=3246976",
        },
        {
            id = 6084064,
            score = 1,
            author = "Augmentum",
            text = "To get this quest, you need to start a quest chain, starting with the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10804.\n\nAfter that, the enemy troops in that territory will become friendly and you will be able to take quests there.",
            date = "2025-03-18T03:59:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11014#comments:id=6084064",
        },
    },
    [11015] = {
        {
            id = 88375,
            score = 42,
            author = "Toabo",
            text = "Based on my first night of farming, this was the quest seemed the biggest time sink of the Neutral ->Friendly, but your results may vary.  (And if you're determined to be first on your block to be Exalted, you'll have to grit your teeth and power through it regardless.)\n\nThese crystals drop from essentially any mob on Netherwing Ridge.  Above ground, you'll find nether rays lurking around the edges of the Ridge and flayers on the mountains further in.  The flayers are more densely packed for easy farming, but that also makes them popular with your fellow grinders.  The nether rays tend to be less over-farmed and the respawn rate is decent enough to keep a solo player from having too much downtime.  Only risk is that some of the nether ray packs are near paths of the patrolling elite drakonids.  These guys have ~100K health and hit hard, so best just to avoid them.\n\nI found less competition in the underground mine, though that may change when more folks may find out about it.  On the other hand, it's much less convenient to get to since you can't fly, so maybe folks won't bother.\n\nYou'll have to go fairly deep into the mine to find mobs.  You'll see slimes and worms mostly in the central tunnel as you enter.  Further in you'll get access to some side tunnels which feature flayers and ravagers.  Way in the back you'll find murkbloods (hostile, unlike the friendly ones at the mine entrance).  I was with a skinner, so we focused mostly on the flayers and ravagers and had decent results.\n\nYou can only turn in 40 Crystals per day, but you can collect as many as you can carry.  Thus, you can get a jump on the next day's turn-in by farming longer.",
            date = "2007-05-23T11:31:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11015#comments:id=88375",
        },
        {
            id = 234815,
            score = 37,
            author = "Skosiris",
            text = "Only requires 30 crystals (down from 40) in patch 2.4.",
            date = "2008-02-13T02:13:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11015#comments:id=234815",
        },
        {
            id = 118734,
            score = 32,
            author = "21378",
            text = "Bloody hell....  At a roughly 33% drop rate, this quest will require mindlessly grinding out an average of 120 kills...and since it is a \"collect X bear asses\" style quest, you can't speed it up by grouping.\n\nYou'd better really really want that shiny dragon mount if you want to work hard enough to turn this one in every day.  Otherwise, just turn it in less frequently than daily, as you get the crystals from your other activities on the ledge.",
            date = "2007-07-10T19:04:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11015#comments:id=118734",
        },
        {
            id = 100314,
            score = 20,
            author = "24587",
            text = "Our good friends at wowwiki have a listing of all the quests at http://www.wowwiki.com/Netherwing\n\nHowever, detailed information isn't exactly there, so you'll want to keep wowhead up for your specific browsing..\n\nThis is a standalone daily quest, one of the first you can get. Aside from the daily limit of 25 daily quests, no other quests will prevent you from doing this (assuming you're neutral with Netherwing).\n\nCrystal's ONLY drop on/in Netherwing Ridge. You can have an Unlimited(?) number of these crystals, and can farm for them before, during, and after accepting the quest. So done with quests for the night? Farm some extras for tomorrow so you can save time the following day.\n\n-Pseudo",
            date = "2007-06-07T17:00:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11015#comments:id=100314",
        },
        {
            id = 88103,
            score = 14,
            author = "28853",
            text = "These can be farmed very nicely in the mine below the Dragonmaw encampment (entrance southeast of the camp) on Netherwing ledge. There were lots of mobs in there and it was not as heavily farmed as the surface above.",
            date = "2007-05-23T06:34:22-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11015#comments:id=88103",
        },
    },
    [11016] = {
        {
            id = 150698,
            score = 28,
            author = "durid4lief",
            text = "Note that if you have both herbalism and skinning, you are only able to choose this quest OR the one for Netherdust Pollen (http://wowhead.com/?quest=11017), but not both during the same day. You can, however, always get the quest for Netherwing Crystals (http://wowhead.com/?quest=11015).",
            date = "2007-09-08T19:11:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11016#comments:id=150698",
        },
        {
            id = 749891,
            score = 19,
            author = "yarko",
            text = "Dear god. If you have skinning and herbalism, DO THE NETHERDUST QUEST. The drop rate for the hides is horrible.\n\nEDIT: The hides drop even if you don't have the quest for them. So, always do the netherdust quest until you collect 35 hides while doing the other quests. Then turn in the hides instead of doing the netherdust one day.",
            date = "2009-06-18T00:18:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11016#comments:id=749891",
        },
        {
            id = 88728,
            score = 11,
            author = "39880",
            text = "Nethermine Flayer Hides are skinned from the Nethermine Flayers located within the Netherwing mines. There are two entrances into the mine, though both entrance paths join together in the mines. While in the mines keep your eyes peeled for glowing Netherwing eggs\n\nEntrance 1: 65.2 90.2\nEntrance 2: 62.9 87.9\n\nThe Flayers are located towards the back of the mine, when you enter, follow the mine cart tracks on the left and you will eventually come to a junction in the tracks, you can stay left to find a few flayers, or go right and follow the track that loops north, into the main area full of dead miners and flayers.\n\nAlso, kill the blood of draenor mobs as they drop encrusted objects that can be opened that can sometimes contain flayer hides, netherdust pollen, and other stuff that's mostly useless.\n\nFor skinners the drop rate of the hide is quite low, my average rate was roughly 12-18%, sometimes in the 20's if I was lucky. On the plus side flayers drop plenty of Netherwing crystals and the occasional Netherwing egg along with cloth and coin.",
            date = "2007-05-23T18:05:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11016#comments:id=88728",
        },
        {
            id = 88469,
            score = 8,
            author = "Wolfchild",
            text = "One of the early daily quests for the continuation of the Netherwing faction rep grind. Introduced in patch 2.1\nThis one is for skinners.  There are variations for miners and herbalists, as well.\nIt's a little mis-leading, with the reference to the crystal formations, as I've yet to find any flayers outside of the mine south of the fel orc camp where you pick up the quest.\nDrop rate for the hides is...eh.  Got 25 in about 2 hours; need 35 for the turn in.  250 rep per turn-in.\nDefinetly pick up the nethermine crystals quest (for the same rep grind) before you head to the mine, as they crystals drop relatively frequently from all the creatures inside.",
            date = "2007-05-23T13:10:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11016#comments:id=88469",
        },
        {
            id = 627325,
            score = 7,
            author = "287195",
            text = "I found one of my hides from the sludge things in the mine. it was in a slude-covered object -- just a thought. (That's why I looked this page up in the first place.)",
            date = "2009-03-01T10:15:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11016#comments:id=627325",
        },
    },
    [11017] = {
        {
            id = 150699,
            score = 31,
            author = "durid4lief",
            text = "Note that if you have both herbalism and skinning, you are only able to choose this quest OR the one for Nethermine Flayer Hides (http://wowhead.com/?quest=11016), but not both during the same day. You can, however, always get the quest for Netherwing Crystals (http://wowhead.com/?quest=11015).",
            date = "2007-09-08T19:15:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11017#comments:id=150699",
        },
        {
            id = 115417,
            score = 9,
            author = "66632",
            text = "While it grows all over the ledge, you risk being battered by dragonmaw ascendants while picking it.\n\nHowever, it also grows on the mainland around Dragonmaw fortress.  Your orc disguise is active there, too.  So the entire fortress is non-hostile and you can pick risk-free.  There aren't quite enough locations to get your 40 (unless you get real lucky) but if no one else is mopping it up you can probably get half your daily take there without worry.",
            date = "2007-07-04T09:07:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11017#comments:id=115417",
        },
        {
            id = 417139,
            score = 7,
            author = "205445",
            text = "These can also be looted from the mob Black Blood of Draenor (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=23286) if they drop Sludge Covered Objects (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=32724).",
            date = "2008-10-23T04:39:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11017#comments:id=417139",
        },
        {
            id = 1287950,
            score = 6,
            author = "672889",
            text = "everything drops for everyone, but you can't do the quests unless you have the profession",
            date = "2011-01-10T18:12:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11017#comments:id=1287950",
        },
        {
            id = 2796206,
            score = 4,
            author = "1937069",
            text = "Tried to farm Herbalism to open this quest, when I realized that each expansion has their own gathering skill. I was only getting herbalism skills up on some of the plants in the outlands, until I bought \"Outland Herbalism.\" I farmed skill from the plants around the Dragonmaw Island, and this quest unlocked at [50 Outland Herbalism].",
            date = "2018-11-06T20:16:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11017#comments:id=2796206",
        },
    },
    [11018] = {
        {
            id = 904114,
            score = 24,
            author = "230138",
            text = "The entrance to the mines is at 65, 90. Without co-ords: on the main map, there is a blue crystal under the 'N' in 'Netherwing'. It's at the base of that blue crystal, a little left off-centre.",
            date = "2009-12-01T06:45:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11018#comments:id=904114",
        },
        {
            id = 89541,
            score = 14,
            author = "54976",
            text = "The quest for this and the skinning/herbalism drops (which can also be looted from the sludge covered objects mentioned above) are only available if you have those professions.",
            date = "2007-05-24T12:44:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11018#comments:id=89541",
        },
        {
            id = 1424857,
            score = 9,
            author = "717646",
            text = "It seems you cannot do this quest if you didn't have the required mining skill when you first started (Neutral to Friendly).\nI had 81 Mining skill when I first started. Worked on it to get it up to 275, now Friendly with Netherwing, and I can't get this quest. Only quest I can get is the crystals. The gathering quests seem to be \"locked\" after talking to the taskmaster for the first time.\n\nSo, be sure you have at least 275 (not 350) mining before you talk to the taskmaster. Don't screw up like I did. :P\nGood thing is you can sell the ore quite profitable in the AH, depending on your server and faction's economy, and how lazy people are to not just mine the Nethercite on their own.",
            date = "2011-05-22T17:22:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11018#comments:id=1424857",
        },
        {
            id = 223564,
            score = 8,
            author = "29281",
            text = "As an extra note, the loot table on this ore is quite interesting.  Not only is there a chance you will get a netherwing egg, you can also collect:\n\nEternium ore (1)\nMote of fire (1-2)\nMote of earth (1-2)\nUncommon Gem (1)\nRare Gem (1)\n\nYes, that's right.  I had the fortunate luck to mine TWO rare gems from nethercite ore deposits inside 10 minutes.  (one per node)  Mind you, I have been mining the ore for weeks and never had one drop, so I expect that this was just blind luck.\n\nHowever, the motes alone make it worthwhile mining.  If you have to choose between the ore or the herb, the ore is a much better deal for the effort.",
            date = "2008-01-24T18:39:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11018#comments:id=223564",
        },
        {
            id = 89480,
            score = 5,
            author = "54934",
            text = "You can also kill the Black Blood of Draenor mobs--they drop sludge-encrusted objects that occasionally contain the ore (I got one drop of 4 ore last night, though I'm not a miner).",
            date = "2007-05-24T11:34:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11018#comments:id=89480",
        },
    },
    [11019] = {
        {
            id = 98860,
            score = 7,
            author = "Gargon",
            text = "This is the goblin at the camp on Netherwing Ledge.\n\nHe will offer the Netherwing Egg quest aswell as the netherwing relics and the peon poisoning quests.",
            date = "2007-06-05T17:33:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11019#comments:id=98860",
        },
        {
