    [11035] = {
        {
            id = 88327,
            score = 94,
            author = "45734",
            text = "There's a small alternative then the floating rocks. 72.3, 64.3\nIt's just SE of Dragonmaw Fortress, The dragons fly past there and I (as a holy priest) couldn't always keep up with the rate in which they came. and there's no competition :)",
            date = "2007-05-23T10:40:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11035#comments:id=88327",
        },
        {
            id = 88436,
            score = 41,
            author = "Toabo",
            text = "My friend and I did our farming at the wooden ramp on the northern edge of the Ridge towards the east side.  (Not sure on coordinates, but I'm sure someone else has mentioned it above.)  Transporters take-off and land here frequently, so it's a good farming spot (if you can get to it first).\n\nThere are two elite drakonids guarding the platform who can and will crush you if aggroed.  Attacks on any Transporter on the platform will aggro the drakonids.  For this reason, I recommend recommend ignoring arrivals and focusing on departures.  The incoming Transporters are tricky to target and hit before they get too close to the guards.\n\nThe departing Transporters are fairly easy once you learn their routine.  They'll spawn at the back of the platform, walk to the northern edge, pause slightly, and then take off.  As soon as the Transporter is airborne, you can safely pull them without aggroing the guards.\n\nThe Transporter moves fairly quickly, so you'll need to be ready to get aggro before he gets out range.  Don't worry; the timing is pretty easy to master.  My rogue friend never had a problem hitting him with a thrown knife.  As a mage, I found Fire Blast didn't give me sufficient range, but Scorch or Fireball worked just fine.  (Fireball is a little trickier because of the longer cast time, but solution is to start casting Fireball before the Transporter is airborne.)\n\nOne last issue for long-range nukers:  be careful not to overdo it while the Transporter is airborne.  It is possible to kill the Transporter in mid-air and, given your proximity to the edge, the corpse may not be lootable.\n\nThe best part about this location:  a new Transporter spawns every ~25 seconds, so you're assured a steady stream of mobs (plus a stack of corpses at your feet).  As a mage, I personally never had to move from my pulling spot.  Target, nuke, nuke, nuke, loot, wait for next.  Very simple.",
            date = "2007-05-23T12:39:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11035#comments:id=88436",
        },
        {
            id = 88337,
            score = 28,
            author = "22738",
            text = "You have to drop 10 Netherwing Relic http://www.wowhead.com/?item=32509 and they only drop from Dragonmaw Transporters http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=23188.\n\nThere are three spots: the place where they land, and 2 little flying islands where they pass over.. Only in these 3 places you are able to pull them and it's around 74,76. They spawn always on the same place so just take your position and keep it. They will respawn fast so it's kinda a sequent pull.\n\n(Best place where i did this quest is 74.6,75.7 - screenshot coming as soon as approved)\n\nP.S: Aimed shot hit cloths for 2.5k, rarely crit for 4/5k. If you nuke them fast they won't use it.",
            date = "2007-05-23T10:49:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11035#comments:id=88337",
        },
        {
            id = 1682468,
            score = 15,
            author = "Damonra",
            text = "Simple walk-thru, if you're high enough (and maybe if you're not):\n\nGo to the Netherwing Ledge at 76.19 81.20.  Its at the NE corner of the island you got the quest from.  There's a dock there with 2 huge NPCs there.  Kill them to make the rest of this easier.\n\nThe Orcs you will be looking for will be taking off & landing at this dock on Netherwing Drakes.  Kill them as soon as they are in range, then loot an repeat.\n\nAt level 85, this took me less than a minute to get all 10 Netherwing Relic (http://www.wowhead.com/item=32509)s.",
            date = "2012-06-29T08:26:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11035#comments:id=1682468",
        },
        {
            id = 3195974,
            score = 9,
            author = "Marklyft",
            text = "If you stand at 75.75, you can just stand still and have a mob spawning every 10 seconds or so.",
            date = "2020-03-24T07:26:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11035#comments:id=3195974",
        },
    },
