    [11058] = {
        {
            id = 88415,
            score = 315,
            author = "Meeuw",
            text = "Allright, there is a lot of confusion related to this so I will try to explain this quest for you all.\n\nFirst off, you must gather one Apexis Shard (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=32569). Then you need to locate an Apexis Monument. Around this monument, you will find 4 Apexis Relics. Go to one of them and stand on the white globe in the middle of the relic (Under the crystal). This way you will make sure you are in reach of all 4 buttons.\n\nClick the Apexis Relic and you will be asked to use your Apexis Shard. After a few seconds a beam from the relic will hit one of the buttons around it. When the beam has hit a button, you simply push the button it hit.\n\nNext level, the relic will hit two buttons. When that is done, you must push the buttons in the order the relic showed you. Continue this untill the quest is complete. I think it completed for me at level 5.\n\nTo make this easier, have a second computer with a text editor. Asign a number for each of the buttons from 1 to 4. I.e.: You get this order: 1, 1, 4, 3, 1, 2. Type this in your text editor while the beam hits. Relax, and push those buttons in WoW while you look at your text editor for the order. If you dont have a secondary computer, try a cell phone. Good luck!",
            date = "2007-05-23T12:06:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11058#comments:id=88415",
        },
        {
            id = 1456836,
            score = 156,
            author = "754550",
            text = "I read through every single comment here and still couldn't figure this out. I didn't understand what on Earth people meant when they said \"click the button\", \"click the crystal\", \"click the bubble\" or \"press the correct number\".\n\nTo start with, position yourself at one of the smaller floating crystals. Rotate your camera so you are looking straight down, zoom in, and move your pet off to one side.\n\nYou will see that each of the smaller floating crystals has a large bubble in the center directly under the crystal and four smaller bubbles that form the corners of a square. These smaller bubbles are what you click. They are initially all white, but when you right-click the smaller crystal and activate it they turn faint shades of yellow, red, blue and green. The crystal will make some sounds and flash, then the center bubble will generate a colored spark to the smaller bubble of the same color. You right-click the smaller bubble that the spark goes to, it plays a happy sound, then it starts a second sequence.\n\nThe Ogri'Lazy addon is helpful because you can use hotkeys to record the order of the sparks then go back through and click them. Note that you still have to click on the bubbles on the ground. The shortcut keys or macros are only for Ogri'Lazy or whatever other method people are using to keep track of the order. Those do not have anything at all to do with completing the quest.\n\nAs a side note, while this is clearly inspired from the old Simon game, it has a significant difference: the pattern resets every time. If Simon started with Yellow, the first color for the rest of your game is Yellow. In this quest the sequence could start with Blue, then the second iteration could start with Yellow. If you were expecting it to build on itself you're in for a surprise.",
            date = "2011-07-01T08:11:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11058#comments:id=1456836",
        },
        {
            id = 1890034,
            score = 67,
            author = "Rocknight",
            text = "I'm adding my explanation to quite a lengthy list, but hopefully it will be useful and I will try to pull together some of the useful points others have made.\n\n1. To start, go to around (33,51) where one of the Apexis Monuments stands.  You'll see a big shard in the middle, with four other shards around the edges.\n\n2. Choose any one of the four shards around the edges and clear any nearby mobs.  Kite them slightly away from the shard so their corpse doesn't get in the way of your view during the 'game'.\n\n3. Stand on the shard and adjust your camera so you're looking straight down.  Around the edge of the shard's platform (right by your feet) are four white circles.  These will be what you click during the game.  Decide for yourself on a numbering system for these.  For example, I decided on top left = 1, top right = 2, bottom right = 3, bottom left = 4.\n\n4. Read the rest of this guide before starting, so you know what to expect.  But when you're ready, click the shard to begin.\n\n5. First of all I am going to say forget about the colours, and forget about the large shard in the middle.  Just focus on the smaller shard you're standing on, and the four white circles.\n\n6. The first thing that's going to happen is a beam of light will appear between your shard and one of the four little circles that you've numbered 1 to 4.  That is the opponent having his first turn.  All you need to do, to take your turn, is to click on that same circle.\n\n7. Now the opponent will take its next turn.  This time it's going to send a beam of light to one of the circles, and then another beam of light to another circle.  Note that it might choose the same circle twice, so watch carefully.  You'll hear an accompanying buzz each time as well if your sound is turned on.  When it has done BOTH beams, it is your turn to click those same circles, in the same order.  You'll see that you also create beams when you click.\n\n8. Each turn from now on will see the opponent doing an additional beam, so the third time it will do three beams, the fourth time it will do four beams and finally...... five beams.\n\nIf your short-term memory is good, then again just repeat what it is doing.  If your short-term memory is bad, then this is where your numbering system comes in useful...\n\nGrab a pen and paper and write down the sequence that your opponent has done.  For example if he beams the top left circle twice and then the bottom right, you'll write down 1-1-3.  (assuming you're using my numbering system).   Always WAIT until the opponent has completed all his beams.  You'll need to remember what round you're on (e.g. I am now on the round where he will do three).  You have plenty of time to then click your circles and create the beams of your own.\n\n9. Once you've successfully repeated the sequence of five, your quest is complete.  When you hand it in you will be given a Daily Quest to go and play again.  Note that on the daily you will need to do eight rounds.  So if you were feeling smug about being able to remember five numbers without pen and paper..... I'd grab that pen and paper now ;)\n\n10. While the daily does not count towards the Loremaster achievement for this zone, it does award 15 Apexis Shards, so will save you a few minutes of farming for one of your other quests in the Loremaster chain.  Assuming you succeed within the first 14 attempts that is.\n\nAside: I actually failed the daily the first time because instead of a 1-4 numbering system I'd used North East South West (as suggested by someone else in this thread).  Unfortunately my writing is terrible and I couldn't tell whether I had written W or N lol.\n\nHope this helps someone out :)",
            date = "2013-08-25T09:30:22-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11058#comments:id=1890034",
        },
        {
            id = 89654,
            score = 65,
            author = "31938",
            text = "This game is a variant of a handheld game called \"Simon Says\" The difference is that \"Simon Says\" would keep the same initial pattern and just add onto the end.\n\nIf you liked this, go pick one up from a toy shop. Tons of fun in long car rides and helps your brain :)",
            date = "2007-05-24T15:27:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11058#comments:id=89654",
        },
        {
            id = 102046,
            score = 56,
            author = "19196",
            text = "Located at 31,61",
            date = "2007-06-10T18:33:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11058#comments:id=102046",
        },
    },
    [11059] = {
        {
            id = 1883321,
            score = 152,
            author = "DarkSyn",
            text = "Ok, I just did this quest on my 90 hunter for the Blade's Edge quest achievement.  I farmed the required 35 shards, went to the crystal (the big one in the exact center of the circle) clicked it - it asked for the shards, and then I stood back as the 'game' began, doing absolutely nothing until the Guardian showed up.  Killed him, quest completed.   At no time did I attempt to play this stupid 'game'.  So, there you have it.  Have your 35 shards, click crystal, give the shards over, let game begin.  Don't have to play to complete.  Hope that helps anyone having troubles.",
            date = "2013-08-02T15:21:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11059#comments:id=1883321",
