            author = "163409",
            text = "I found staying above him was the best strategy. Easy to outmaneuver the aoe bombs. Need to watch out for the skybreakers though",
            date = "2008-06-18T08:15:59-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11067#comments:id=306866",
        },
    },
    [11068] = {
        {
            id = 91340,
            score = 51,
            author = "11718",
            text = "Leads to: http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11069",
            date = "2007-05-26T21:36:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11068#comments:id=91340",
        },
        {
            id = 595599,
            score = 38,
            author = "287195",
            text = "I love how this NPC can hit himself multiple times with bombs, stopping dead in the air, and NOT fall off his mount. If an NPC does this, it should be an automatic completion for the player.",
            date = "2009-02-04T16:20:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11068#comments:id=595599",
        },
        {
            id = 236618,
            score = 36,
            author = "94623",
            text = "Here's a strategy that worked for me. Paladin with Crusader Aura engaged. Not sure if that will matter....\n\nI got above him right away. Held down both mouse buttons (which acts as move forward) and pointed down towards him. In this way, I was always \"diving\", and I could watch him at all times.\n\nI would then hit the space bar to climb whenever I got near him. So I was making vertical up and down zig-zags. I would make sure I started climbing with space bar every time he throws skulls, and when I had a good handle on where the skulls were going, I let off the space bar to dive around them.\n\nI failed several times before trying this strategy, and it worked the first time.",
            date = "2008-02-15T10:19:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11068#comments:id=236618",
        },
        {
            id = 5233919,
            score = 16,
            author = "dawn22868",
            text = "Accidentally found a way to complete this quest within the first few seconds (as a druid in flightform).\n\n- Fly right into your target when he takes off and keep the distance minimal.\n- When he casts his special ability, let it hit you.\n- He should be hit by it too when you were flying right inside of him, which causes him to abort the race and fly back to base.\n\nYou should receive the quest completion note immediately or after he's back at base.\nWorked for all of the races, except the first (didn't try bc it was short anyways) and last one (tried, but was too hard to pull of).\n\nThis might also work on a flying mount. I didn't bother to test it though.",
            date = "2021-08-08T16:09:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11068#comments:id=5233919",
        },
        {
            id = 837787,
            score = 9,
            author = "267801",
            text = "The Dragonmaw racing quest chain:\n[70] Earning Your Wings... (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11063) (just a prerequisite)\n[70] Dragonmaw Race: The Ballad of Oldie McOld (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11064) (350 rep)\n[70] Dragonmaw Race: Trope the Filth-Belcher (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11067) (350 rep)\n[70] Dragonmaw Race: Corlok the Vet (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11068) (500 rep)\n[70] Dragonmaw Race: Wing Commander Ichman (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11069) (500 rep)\n[70] Dragonmaw Race: Wing Commander Mulverick (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11070) (500 rep)\n[70] Dragonmaw Race: Captain Skyshatter (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11071) (1000 rep + Skybreaker Whip (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=32863))\nTotal rep: 3200",
            date = "2009-09-11T13:14:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11068#comments:id=837787",
        },
    },
    [11069] = {
        {
            id = 89841,
            score = 70,
            author = "12021",
            text = "His text is a reference to the constant whining of the Horde in Alterac Valley regarding the bridge to Dun Baldar.",
            date = "2007-05-24T20:04:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11069#comments:id=89841",
        },
        {
            id = 100462,
            score = 47,
            author = "gazhkull",
            text = "The names \"Ichman\" and \"Mulverick\" are references to the characters of the movie Top Gun \"Iceman\" and Maverick\". I guess having Ichman say: \"You are still dangerous... you can be my wingman anytime\" after you defeat him would have been too obvious...",
            date = "2007-06-08T00:28:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11069#comments:id=100462",
        },
        {
            id = 116303,
            score = 28,
            author = "15038",
            text = "This guy is really fast. The best way to beat him is to stay above him. He likes to fly low to the group and trick you into aggro'ing the flayers. Fly above him, as soon as you see the fireball appear,  fly a little higher and you'll be out of its range. You'll be safely ahead of the explosions by the time the fireball splits. Like the last guy, don't let him get too far ahead.",
            date = "2007-07-06T03:36:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11069#comments:id=116303",
        },
        {
            id = 837790,
            score = 26,
            author = "267801",
            text = "The Dragonmaw racing quest chain:\n[70] Earning Your Wings... (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11063) (just a prerequisite)\n[70] Dragonmaw Race: The Ballad of Oldie McOld (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11064) (350 rep)\n[70] Dragonmaw Race: Trope the Filth-Belcher (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11067) (350 rep)\n[70] Dragonmaw Race: Corlok the Vet (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11068) (500 rep)\n[70] Dragonmaw Race: Wing Commander Ichman (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11069) (500 rep)\n[70] Dragonmaw Race: Wing Commander Mulverick (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11070) (500 rep)\n[70] Dragonmaw Race: Captain Skyshatter (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11071) (1000 rep + Skybreaker Whip (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=32863))\nTotal rep: 3200",
            date = "2009-09-11T13:17:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11069#comments:id=837790",
        },
        {
            id = 110844,
            score = 22,
            author = "45422",
            text = "Easist way for me to get all these done was to use Alt + Z while having the person I'm racing targeted while being naked in case I died.. It helps because you dont have to look at your UI while flying and can concentrate just on what he's trying to throw at you..",
            date = "2007-06-25T09:19:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11069#comments:id=110844",
        },
    },
    [11070] = {
        {
            id = 147552,
            score = 194,
            author = "4361",
            text = "Fun fact: it takes 1:40 mins for Mulverick to to trot into position, slowly fly over the airfield strip, and actually start the race.\n\nMindnumbing.",
            date = "2007-09-01T08:19:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11070#comments:id=147552",
        },
        {
            id = 91464,
            score = 90,
            author = "limitgenesis",
            text = "dispite fustration ive found the full proof stradegy for this guy\n\nk all u have to do is stay above him really far up but not to far then make sure ur straightend out and use left click to look down stay at that camera angel and steer left and right and go up when u need to just watch out where he is or u might go to high\nthere is one trouble point near the end where he takes a drop down near that dock looking thing with the 2 elite guards so folow him down with right mouse click camera angle then straighten out and go birds eye view again.\nlong as u stay directly above him no probs with the bolts.\ngl",
            date = "2007-05-27T02:42:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11070#comments:id=91464",
        },
        {
            id = 210974,
            score = 75,
            author = "Magiras",
            text = "To the person who failed once because he looped around the tower you should have seen that one coming, Maverick ALWAYS buzzed the towers in Top Gun. If he didn't I would have been disappointed.",
            date = "2008-01-01T12:18:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11070#comments:id=210974",
        },
        {
            id = 181047,
            score = 61,
            author = "axellemaelstrom",
            text = "A.W.O.L. = absent without official leave\n\nso just another way of saying AFK",
            date = "2007-11-08T14:09:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11070#comments:id=181047",
        },
        {
            id = 218054,
            score = 52,
            author = "104126",
            text = "This is imho the most difficult of all the racing quests.  I believe the following observations should make it easier:\n\nMy view is that the lighning bolts do not actually track you as some comments suggest.\n\nInstead, what happens is that the lightning bolts expand in a circular way after they have been launched.  It almost works like a circular \"net\" or \"web\" that increases in size as it goes on.  If you get caught in the \"net\", you are dismounted.\n\nAs a countermeasure what you should do is this:  Imagine a cone-shaped area behind Mulverick.  This is the \"danger zone\".\n\nSo if you are very close to Mulverick, there is a smaller chance of being caught.\nIf you are further behind him, the area covered by the bolts are larger and you are in more danger.\n\nHe launches the lighning bolts more or less in your direction, but \"circle of bolts\" then expands the further it goes.  This therefore creates the impression that the bolts actually do track you.\n\nThe strategy that ultimately worked best for me was this:\n\nI flew right behind Mulverick (as close as I could) all of the time.  Perhaps just a little to the side.  Whenever I see a bolt, I hit spacebar and try to go \"over\" it.  If you just keep spacebar in you should be safe.  The closer you are to Mulverick, the easier to dodge the bolts this way.\nWhat also works like a charm here is to cut his corners.  If you are next to (or ahead of) Mulverick, you are safe.  So if he turns, turn sharply into his turn and stay next to him.\n\nFinally, you'll have to get to know his flight path in order to stay close.  Most likely you'll end up doing the quest about 10 times to get the hang of his path, but if you persevere you'll get it.  (Or just memorise it from youtube!)  This dude has one loooong flight path.\n\n(The most frustrating thing here is lag... even with a latency of 500-700ms you'll sometimes find that Mulverick suddenly \"disappears\" in front of you.  If you don't know the flight path, this can be quite frustrating.  Look for him right behind you if this happens.  I think his \"stunts\" are sometimes because of small lag spikes rather than actual stunts?)",
            date = "2008-01-14T06:17:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11070#comments:id=218054",
        },
    },
    [11071] = {
        {
            id = 89158,
            score = 145,
            author = "Mirei",
            text = "I think I spent a good hour working on this quest before finally completing it.\n\nGet used to his yell, \"Prepare a funereal pyre!   has challenged Skyshatter!\"\n\nThe trick here is to remain within range of him (which I think is no greater than 15 YDs, MUCH less than the others), while avoiding a bombardment of 'meteors' that shower around him.\n\nIf you remain rather close to him the entire time (He must have 280% flight speed...  I could NEVER duck and dodge without him getting too far ahead), he'll end up soaking up most of the meteors, himself.  Not to be corny, but trust your instincts.  He'll lead you to victory.  His flight is much shorter than Mulvericks, but about three times as annoying.\n\nGood luck, potential Skybreakers.\n\nCompleting this quest nets you 1000 rep, as well as what is listed, above.",
            date = "2007-05-24T05:04:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11071#comments:id=89158",
        },
        {
            id = 105362,
            score = 81,
            author = "euebi",
            text = "I just did this race and I had a hell of a lot of tries and never really got into the path since I seemed to fall down shortly after I cam into a new area. Therefore I began to search for a video in the web and found this nice little vid:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Rq87HikhdNo\n\nFor everyone that have trouble with Skyshatter, watch this video and you get a clue of the path. After a couple of tries you will get better and better and will defeat him in the end.\n\nGood luck!",
            date = "2007-06-16T09:20:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11071#comments:id=105362",
        },
        {
            id = 223322,
            score = 66,
            author = "117990",
            text = "An interesting fact: this race is exactly as long as the song \"Danger Zone\" from the movie Top Gun.",
            date = "2008-01-24T09:14:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11071#comments:id=223322",
        },
        {
            id = 99139,
            score = 57,
            author = "Nedio",
            text = "I find that hiding all the UIs on screen temporarily for the race helps a lot, easier to race on a clean screen with less distraction.  If you aren't sure which key does this, go to your key bindings and locate the \"Toggle User Interface\" key, hope this would improve fellow racers who are still trying to defeat him =)",
            date = "2007-06-06T03:03:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11071#comments:id=99139",
        },
        {
            id = 784724,
            score = 47,
            author = "Mattboy",
            text = "I hope whoever thought this god-awful quest at Blizzard got fired.\nI can practically hear the pitch.\n\nIdiot: \"Hey guys, lets have a racing mission with flying mounts!\"\nBlizz team: \"Ok. Sounds pretty fun.\"\nIdiot: \"Now, lets have the npc opponent throw objects that can hurt the player... better yet, dismount them!\"\nBlizz team: \"O... k. Sure! A little challenge is just what we need.\"\nIdiot: \"Now, lets have the projectiles spawn from random points in the sky... and explode!\"\nBlizz team: \"Like meteors?\"\nIdiot: \"Exactly! And, uh, we can make some explode as soon as they spawn, to mix it up!\"\nBlizz team: \"Al...right...\"\nIdiot: \"Yeah! and the player will have to follow npc exactly, so he cant see them well.\"\nBlizz team: \"I don't know... thats a little unforgiving.\"\nIdiot: \"Nah! Unforgiving would be where we make them stay within 15 yards or they lose. HEY, lets do that!\"\nChris Metzen: \"We'ren't you the same guy who suggested making a faction of mushroom men?\"\nIdiot: \"Yeah! You liked that?\"\nChris Metzen: \"You're fired. Make sure the Lich King dev team never meets that guy.\"",
            date = "2009-07-21T18:16:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11071#comments:id=784724",
        },
    },
    [11072] = {
        {
            id = 88071,
            score = 62,
            author = "54500",
            text = "The follow-up quest to Adversarial Blood involves taking the Time-Lost Offering to the island in the centre of Skettis, and using it to summon Terokk himself.\n\nTerokk is a giant, ghostly arrakoa, and he has quite a lot of health. You will need a 5 man group with a tank and at least one healer with a considerable mana pool.\n\nDuring the fight, Terokk will become immune to all damage, at which point the tank will need to drag him to one of the four purple crystals around the edge of the green runic circle from which you summon him. This will shatter his immunity, at which point your group can carry on attacking him. Apart from that, it's a simple tank and spank fight.\n\nTerokk drops a BoP blue like each of the four named mobs you summoned during the 'Adversarial Blood' part of the chain. He dropped a blue 1h mace for my group with strangely enough, both +damage and healing and +healing on it, as seperate stats.\n\nUpon finishing the quest to destroy Terokk, you get a choice from four rewards.\n\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?item=32832 is one of them, I can't remember the names of the other three, and they're unsearchable on wowhead at the moment, but I remember there being a polearm with 60 stam and a lot of AP, a staff, as well as a wand with +damage and healing.\n\nI hope this helped someone :>",
            date = "2007-05-23T05:58:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11072#comments:id=88071",
        },
        {
            id = 117614,
            score = 39,
            author = "50453",
            text = "Entire quest 2manned by a dark pact/ruin warlock and holy paladin. Imp was used, warlock did the tanking. You require 10 scrolls per boss per person (the two of us required a total of 80 time lost scrolls). We got 10 scrolls per 15 minutes, so 8 elixirs were needed (48 shadow dust). Only warlock used shadow elixirs (healers don’t need to see undead to loot them). Took about half an hour for the shadow dust, and another 2 and a half hours of farming scrolls/killing bosses. When farming scrolls, it’s best to do a boss in between each elixir to allow for respawns.\n\nAll bosses are immune to fear/stun/etc. After summoned, you have about 5 seconds before they aggro. They each have special abilities.\n\nKarrog – Approx. 73,000 hp. Hits for about 1900-2500 on cloth. “Fixates” on a target, drastically reducing his move speed and increasing his damage to about 5500 on cloth. When he fixates, just kite and damage him, no healing should be needed if you just run (he walks REALLY slow).\n\nGezzarak the Huntress – Approx. 59,000 hp. Hits for about 1500 on cloth. Casts “warped armor” debuff, reduces armor to 0. Will “focus” on a target, then warp to them, dropping aggro.\n\nDarkscreecher Akkarai – Approx 47,000 hp. Does a frostbolt attack, 2.5 second cast, for around 1000 frost damage. Every few frostbolts, he will do a fire blast for around 1600 fire damage. Will also summon adds around every 20 seconds. They come 3 at a time, they are birds that don’t hit for much, have about 5000 hp. The pally gathered them up while the warlock burned Akkarai down, then after he died the birds were killed with seed of corruption (only needed 4).\n\nVakkiz the Windrager – Approx. 59,000 hp. Hits for about 1500 on cloth. Does a chain lightning with around 2000 initial damage for the first 50%. At 50% hp he switches to a bone form, and begins to cast “Bone Spray”. Initially hits cloth for around 500. Each time he attacks, it adds a stack to a debuff he puts on you which increases damage taken by 5% per stack. He casts this around every 2 seconds. Save all your cooldowns for 50%.\n\nEach boss will drop 1 of their quest item that gets rolled on. They also each drop 1 BoP blue item with a random enchant on it. Despite WoWhead’s info, their quest item is a 100% drop (people who don’t need the quest that kill the bosses get no drop, which alters WoWhead’s information).",
            date = "2007-07-08T19:05:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11072#comments:id=117614",
        },
        {
            id = 89421,
            score = 38,
            author = "42987",
            text = "leads to\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11073",
            date = "2007-05-24T10:22:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11072#comments:id=89421",
        },
        {
            id = 88653,
            score = 25,
            author = "27187",
            text = "Afew things to note:\n\n1. Only one person can loot the mob item.\n2. It takes 10 scrolls to summon each mob. So a total of 40 per each person.\n\nThey are elite mobs LVL 72 so bring a decent party with you.\n\nSo its gunna take awhile to finish this quest at the least.\nI got a BOP Blue off of Gezzarak. Healing Neclace.",
            date = "2007-05-23T16:35:59-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11072#comments:id=88653",
        },
        {
            id = 265424,
            score = 24,
            author = "revoked",
            text = "If you have this quest, drop it and pick it up again! In 2.4 they changed it to just needing the kill, not the drop! see here: http://wowhead.com/?quest=11885",
            date = "2008-04-02T22:40:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11072#comments:id=265424",
        },
    },
    [11073] = {
        {
            id = 89316,
            score = 144,
            author = "15429",
            text = "At 20% Terokk becomes Immune to all attacks, and you'll see a blue flare shortly afterward, where a bomb will drop down. Drag Terokk into the flame to break his shield. He'll become enraged but you'll be able to kill him.\n\nThe Ancient Skull Pile respawns after roughly ~15 minutes following a party killing Terokk.",
            date = "2007-05-24T08:15:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11073#comments:id=89316",
        },
        {
            id = 276479,
            score = 63,
            author = "127121",
            text = "Learned this the hard way...the summoner of Terokk MUST remain in the circle for him to not fade away right after you summon him.  Blew the jar, what a waste.",
            date = "2008-04-23T20:09:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11073#comments:id=276479",
        },
        {
            id = 96603,
            score = 45,
            author = "29921",
            text = "This quest gives 1000+ reputation with Sha'tari Skyguard.\nTerokk gives 200+ reputation when killed.\n\n1200+ reputation from one quest aint bad :)",
            date = "2007-06-03T06:20:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11073#comments:id=96603",
        },
        {
            id = 2446647,
            score = 44,
            author = "Jakel0111",
            text = "The pile of skulls is on a 15 minute cooldown. You do not need the elixir of shadow to see it.",
            date = "2016-11-20T14:57:05-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11073#comments:id=2446647",
        },
        {
            id = 1566059,
            score = 37,
            author = "Exixo",
            text = "If you plan on repeating the quest, the 15 min respawn time on the skull pile to re-summon Terokk may seem like a long time, but you need to re-gather 40 https://www.wowhead.com/item=32620 to get:\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=32715\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=32716\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=32717\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=32718\n\n(and the 6 https://www.wowhead.com/item=32388 to make your https://www.wowhead.com/item=32446 if you need it).\n\nThen hand them all in for another https://www.wowhead.com/item=32720 before you can even summon him. Doing all this in 15 mins is no easy task, so unless you stockpile the items you probably won't have any downtime when grinding the boss.",
            date = "2011-11-08T00:50:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11073#comments:id=1566059",
        },
    },
    [11074] = {
        {
            id = 1250210,
            score = 33,
            author = "740666",
            text = "can someone plz hlp me? ive been trying to get this quest for a while now but when i goto the guy that gives the quest he doesnt have it available... i see the guy but not the quest, I ca however do the fires over skettis quest though",
            date = "2010-12-21T11:08:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11074#comments:id=1250210",
        },
        {
            id = 832470,
            score = 17,
            author = "379616",
            text = "Confirmed, quest is repeatable. If you complete it once, you can stack the four items needed for the quest up to four times. By that I mean you can kill all four mini-bosses four times each, and turn in the quest four times all at once for a total of 1400 rep instead of 350 rep.",
            date = "2009-09-05T09:21:07-05:00",
