    [11506] = {
        {
            id = 1553924,
            score = 14,
            author = "733706",
            text = "Just a bit of clarification.  Since this quest is a daily, you can acquire it anytime, once a day. But you can't complete the quest if the timer is running. When the timer runs out and the words \"Towers Controlled\", followed by a number, appear you can complete the quest, and can cap a tower even if the other faction already has it.\n\nAnother thing that confused me when I first attempted this quest: The towers are not visible on the in-game map unless they are available for capture. In other words, you can't see them (on the map) if the timer is running. They are just barely visible on the mini-map, they are small light green-grey circles. Once the timer runs out a grey icon for each tower pops up on the map.\n\nIt has already been mentioned that your faction gets a buff when you have captured all the towers. I don't think anyone mentioned the fact that spirit shards (used to buy trinkets, etc.) also become available to that faction. They drop from bosses in the Achindoun dungeons.",
            date = "2011-10-26T05:20:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11506#comments:id=1553924",
        },
        {
            id = 1076294,
            score = 11,
            author = "617575",
            text = "This does not count toward Terror of Terrokar.",
            date = "2010-07-08T19:21:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11506#comments:id=1076294",
        },
        {
            id = 321619,
            score = 10,
            author = "IronVeins",
            text = "Converting a Tower to Horde is 1 minute's worth of work.\n1) Flag for PvP by rt clicking on your picture and click enable. On a PvP server you don't have to do anything different.\n2) Stay within 20yds or so of the tower while flagged and it will begin converting to your side. If you are flying, you MUST land. You can land on top of the tower and get credit, but it can be tricky.\nThis process takes roughly 1 minute but the time reduces by 50% for every other Horde player standing in range and flagged. Any Horde player of any level (I've had a 57 do it) will convert the tower.\nIf an alliance player is alive and in range while flagged the conversion will stop until he leaves range or is dead. This operates the exact same way as the Towers in EotS battleground.\nIf you can get all 5 converted you get the 5% XP buff and Horde can gather Spirit Shards from bosses inside the dungeons. And yes only 1 tower is needed to complete this quest. You will have to wait for the entire 6 hours to finish counting down to attempt it again.\n\nEasiest way is to gather 10 players together, put 2 on each a few minutes before the timer expires and boom they are all yours 30 seconds afterwards.\n\n-Keonka the Mangler",
            date = "2008-07-07T02:26:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11506#comments:id=321619",
        },
        {
            id = 261301,
            score = 9,
            author = "141000",
            text = "This quest can be completed in a raid group, so ask in General if anyone else is working on it, it'll make it a lot easier. LONG LIVE WORLD PVP!\n\nIf you're interested in world PvP, you might also like In Defense of Halaa ( http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11502 ).",
            date = "2008-03-27T16:25:22-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11506#comments:id=261301",
        },
        {
            id = 281113,
            score = 4,
            author = "82227",
            text = "Copied the following from the Alliance side version of this quest.\n\nThere are five spirit towers visible around Auchindoun when the sixhour counter runs out - they are roughly 10 o'clock, 12:30, 2, 4 and 6 o'clock positions. There is a buff if you cap all 5. You can be in bird form (druid) or in your flying mount but you have to be touching the ground to cap - 10/80/10 is the alliance/gray/horde breakdown for the slider.\n\nOnce we capped all five a six hour timer popped up and there were no more capturing possibilites.\n\nThe buff is called Blessing of Auchindoun - \"Experience gain increased by 5 % Damage increased by 5 % Allows the capture of Spirit Shards\"\n\nFor the Horde! :)",
            date = "2008-05-02T12:33:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11506#comments:id=281113",
        },
    },
    [11513] = {
        {
            id = 261731,
            score = 77,
            author = "Kastaje",
            text = "Bash'ir Landing is around [51,16] (http://www.wowhead.com/?maps=3522:515161) in Blade's Edge Mountains.\nEvergrove is the closest flight path there.\n\nKill mobs until you find the Bash'ir Phasing Device (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=34248).\nThen use the item and you will get phased out (you can compare it to mages invisibility spell but you can use spells).\nThen you will be able to find crates (you are able to see one in the screenshot, they are pink/purple) which contains Smuggled Mana Cell (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=34246#objective-of).\nWatch out so that the Phase Wyrms (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=24917) Don't kill you as you will lose the phase buff.\nWhen you are done with the quest just right click on the buff and turn it in at shatt.\n\nGood Luck!\n\nEdit: Added a little more information.",
            date = "2008-03-28T06:09:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11513#comments:id=261731",
        },
        {
            id = 260900,
            score = 34,
            author = "52844",
            text = "The way this works is that you kill Etherum until the Bash'ir Phasing Device drops. When you use it, you become invisible to the Ethereals in the area and can only see mana cells and wyrms. Generally, it's one wyrm to one cell. Unlike mage invisibility, you can use all your abilities as normal (even mount!) and not aggro the ethereals. The buff has no time limit. but will fade once you leave Bash'ir Landing. The next time you want to do the quest, you will need to kill ethereals until you get another phasing device.",
            date = "2008-03-27T06:12:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11513#comments:id=260900",
        },
        {
            id = 236555,
            score = 26,
            author = "Bamahut",
            text = "You need the \009Bash'ir Phasing Device! (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=34248) to able to see the mana cells. The Bash'ir Phasing Device drop from any ethereal, it also drops from the elementals.",
            date = "2008-02-15T08:32:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11513#comments:id=236555",
        },
        {
            id = 262523,
            score = 20,
            author = "Miyari",
            text = "Upon completion of the Sunwell Portal (a portal from Shattrath City (?zone=3703) to the Isle of Quel'Danas (?zone=4080)) during phase 2, this quest is replaced by Maintaining the Sunwell Portal (?quest=11514), and has the same objective but is a permanent daily quest that can be completed for reputation and reward, and will always be available once it is unlocked.\n\nFor more information regarding the Shattered Sun Offensive (http://www.wowhead.com/?faction=1077) daily quests and the \"phases\" of reclamation, check out this guide (http://www.wowhead.com/?forums&topic=17960#p155565) on the Wowhead forums! :)",
            date = "2008-03-29T10:36:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11513#comments:id=262523",
        },
        {
            id = 261181,
            score = 14,
            author = "95950",
            text = "If you are killed (Opposite faction or a wrym) - you lose the buff, and must get another device.",
            date = "2008-03-27T13:49:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11513#comments:id=261181",
        },
    },
    [11514] = {
        {
            id = 5332051,
            score = 116,
