            text = "Upon recovering the Sun's Reach Sanctum (completion of phase 1), this quest is replaced by Further Conversions (?quest=11525), which has the same objective but is a permanent daily quest that can be completed for reputation and reward, and will always be available once it is unlocked.\n\nFor more information regarding the Shattered Sun Offensive (http://www.wowhead.com/?faction=1077) daily quests and the \"phases\" of reclamation, check out this guide (http://www.wowhead.com/?forums&topic=17960#p155565) on the Wowhead forums! :)",
            date = "2008-03-29T10:27:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11524#comments:id=262513",
        },
        {
            id = 261319,
            score = 6,
            author = "Lorielle",
            text = "This quest is pretty simple once you understand what you need to do.\n\nOnce you pick up the quest go right, you should just see a big field with some mobs spread out.\nThe  Arcane Sentries are pretty large mobs, not hard. They look like the elite Sentries in netherstorm, who patrol the manaforges.\nMake sure and LOOT before you use the crystal in your bag. Right now there is a bug which will cause it not to count.\nThey tend to drop some grey trash, sells for pretty good if you gather enough, and some motes of mana.\n\nOverall, this is a very easy quest that shouldn't take you more then 10 minutes to complete unless there is quite a few people out there.\n\nAs of today on my server, Detheroc, we completed phase 1 and moved into the second one. We are able to still do the first dailies so I imagine they are here to stay!\nEasy gold which helps me since I'm saving for my epic flyer! =)\n\nAlexendra ~ BE Spriest~",
            date = "2008-03-27T17:00:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11524#comments:id=261319",
        },
        {
            id = 259992,
            score = 5,
            author = "140329",
            text = "I had trouble with this quest at first because I wasn't getting credit for converting the sentries.  On my first 3 or 4 tries I used the core on the sentry before looting it and I didn't get any credit.  After that I looted every corpse before using the core and they all gave me credit.  I don't know if this is intentional or a bug, but if you're having trouble try looting the corpse before using the core on it.",
            date = "2008-03-26T08:18:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11524#comments:id=259992",
        },
        {
            id = 234902,
            score = 3,
            author = "blizzae",
            text = "Run around behind the quest givers all up the side near the sunwell you can see the sentrys (They look like the golems from mech).\nKill them and then use the Attuned Crystal Cores on them, Once you have 3 simple run to Sun's reach sanctum (48.0, 36.2) and the quest should complete if you go in or very close to the building",
            date = "2008-02-13T04:50:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11524#comments:id=234902",
        },
        {
            id = 260926,
            score = 2,
            author = "Oktex",
            text = "You have to kill Erratic Sentry mobs. You can find them in Sunwell Plateau.\n\nAfter you killed it target the mob and use your Attuned Crystal Cores.\n\nVery easy!",
            date = "2008-03-27T07:14:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11524#comments:id=260926",
        },
    },
    [11525] = {
        {
            id = 261352,
            score = 15,
            author = "15585",
            text = "The Erratic Sentries are found scattered all over the place. Level 70's non-aggressive, so mistakenly aggro'ing one isn't an issue.\n\nThey only have about 5600 health so they go down pretty easily too.\n\nFor this quest all you have to do is \"kill\" them, then use the Attuned Crystal Cores provided. They will turn into a Converted Sentry for about 10 seconds and then despawn.\n\nRight now they have a very high respawn rate so what I did and recommend is finding one or two close together in a semi remote location and go to town. By the time you kill one, tame it, kill the second and tame it the first will have respawned. Takes under 10 minutes with this method.",
            date = "2008-03-27T17:41:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11525#comments:id=261352",
        },
        {
            id = 262515,
            score = 14,
            author = "Miyari",
            text = "Upon recovering the Sun's Reach Sanctum (completion of phase 1), this quest replaces Erratic Behavior (?quest=11524), and has the same objective but is a permanent daily quest that can be completed for reputation and reward, and will always be available once it is unlocked.\n\nFor more information regarding the Shattered Sun Offensive (http://www.wowhead.com/?faction=1077) daily quests and the \"phases\" of reclamation, check out this guide (http://www.wowhead.com/?forums&topic=17960#p155565) on the Wowhead forums! :)",
            date = "2008-03-29T10:28:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11525#comments:id=262515",
        },
        {
            id = 2880686,
            score = 13,
            author = "jzkalika",
            text = "The Converted Sentries are not within the quest highlight area, I found a bunch of them in north of Dawnstar village near the water! Simply kill them, and use the quest item.",
            date = "2019-04-07T14:36:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11525#comments:id=2880686",
        },
        {
            id = 263179,
            score = 6,
            author = "Lighter",
            text = "Note that if you use your Attuned Crystal Core (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=34368) before you loot you will loose the loot.\n\nAlso trying to use your Core on an Erractic Sentry (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=24972) killed by another player will not work, as it is tagged to them. If they go out of range it will be available for you to use.",
            date = "2008-03-30T11:13:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11525#comments:id=263179",
        },
        {
            id = 442347,
            score = 4,
            author = "245477",
            text = "After the WotLK, gold reward now 3g 40s, 9500xp",
            date = "2008-11-14T05:32:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11525#comments:id=442347",
        },
    },
    [11526] = {
        {
            id = 235472,
            score = 68,
            author = "andyf",
            text = "Using the scroll at the portal teleports you to Outland, Hellfire Peninsula, near where Kazzak spawns.\n\nThe quest text doesn't mention this although the tooltip on the scroll does. Be warned, there's no instant way of getting back to the Isle of Quel'Danas if you take this quest, the portal does not let you return.",
            date = "2008-02-13T18:28:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11526#comments:id=235472",
        },
        {
            id = 260092,
            score = 53,
            author = "Jamo",
            text = "This quest appears to be unrepeatable. Meaning, the second and subsequent days you must actually travel to HFP.",
            date = "2008-03-26T10:15:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11526#comments:id=260092",
        },
        {
            id = 251423,
            score = 23,
            author = "134734",
            text = "The point of this quest is to show you that there are 2 new daily quests found at the Throne of Kil'jaeden. Perhaps fitting given that the final boss of BC is the badass demon himself.\n\nJust be aware that Kazzak is still there and you may run into guilds attempting to take him down for the cheap (or expensive, depending how you look at it) BOE epics.",
            date = "2008-03-10T20:42:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11526#comments:id=251423",
        },
        {
            id = 259844,
            score = 20,
            author = "wingman",
            text = "Leads to 2 daily quests, http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11515 and http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=11516\n\nIt will teleport you thru to Throne of Kiljaeden in Hellfire Peninsula (near where kazzak is) when you use the scroll. The 2 daily quests are quite nearby.",
            date = "2008-03-26T03:22:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11526#comments:id=259844",
        },
        {
            id = 260201,
            score = 19,
            author = "carfo",
            text = "I'm almost positive if you don't have the flight training you can't get this quest",
            date = "2008-03-26T12:34:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11526#comments:id=260201",
        },
    },
    [11532] = {
        {
            id = 240998,
            score = 39,
            author = "40132",
            text = "Part of the Dragonhawk's flight path takes you near where Brutallus, the 2nd boss in the Sunwell Plateau, is standing.\n\nAmusingly enough, if you throw bombs at him he shrugs it off and yells at you to try again \"with 24 of your friends\", poking fun at the hard-capped 25-man raid sizes.",
            date = "2008-02-21T17:59:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11532#comments:id=240998",
        },
        {
            id = 236982,
            score = 29,
            author = "58807",
            text = "Ayren can be found where you landed at Sun's Reach Harbour, easily spotted by the two Dragonhawks protecting him and to the north of the town. You talk to him for the air raid.\n\nTook me more than one run on my first go at the quest. The Pit Lords took about 3 hits from full health to take down, luckily the bombs have a short cooldown roughly similar to GCD.",
            date = "2008-02-15T23:02:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11532#comments:id=236982",
        },
        {
            id = 261338,
            score = 27,
            author = "Lorielle",
            text = "This quest tends to be a bit tougher because at least right now, everyone is doing it too.\nAs stofffer said, You will find Ayren Cloudbreaker at 48, 25 or for those of you without coords. Its the person standing beside the flight master. Not hard to find!\nMy advice would be to group up with people and all try and take off roughly at the same time, you will get credit.\n\nThe flight isn't long and once you are able to use your bombs, do so.\nAll three types of mobs you must kill are large so don't waste your bombs on the small guys standing around.\nThe sorcerers and pit overlords both take more then one hit to kill which is why grouping is a bit faster, atleast until everyone isnt doing them all at the same time or you can just keep repeating until you have them all killed. ( I completed it in 3 tries althought I was bombing the small guys who melee at first. )\n\nYou cannot get this quest until your realm has completed phase 1 which is why some of you guys aren't able to talk with Ayren or get the quest.\nThe more people doing their dailies the faster your realm completes the phases.\n\nAlexendra ~ Detheroc BE Spriest ~",
            date = "2008-03-27T17:25:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11532#comments:id=261338",
        },
        {
            id = 250900,
            score = 24,
            author = "Teer",
            text = "Make sure that no one is leaving just ahead of you as they will probably tag all the mobs just before you and you will just help to kill them for him.",
            date = "2008-03-09T21:08:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11532#comments:id=250900",
        },
        {
            id = 246094,
            score = 21,
            author = "86526",
            text = "These mobs are \"tagged\" similar to other mobs, in that only the player who first damaged a Pit Overlord or Eredar Sorcerer can get credit for the kill.",
            date = "2008-03-01T09:17:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11532#comments:id=246094",
        },
    },
    [11533] = {
        {
            id = 238352,
            score = 48,
            author = "nilbog",
            text = "the npc to get on a mount is next to the boat near where you land from the flightpath from silvermoon city for horde",
            date = "2008-02-17T22:45:09-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11533#comments:id=238352",
        },
        {
            id = 272229,
            score = 41,
            author = "45715",
            text = "You actually get to see Brutallus during this quest. If you throw an Arcane Charge at him, he will yell:\n\"What is this pathetic magic? How about you come back with twenty.four of your best friends and try again, !\n\nIs that a hint to raid him or what?! :D",
            date = "2008-04-15T12:22:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11533#comments:id=272229",
        },
        {
            id = 275589,
            score = 22,
            author = "145646",
            text = "Pretty simple quest really, but its certainly my preference of the dailys in Quel Danas. Get the quest and then talk to Ayren Coudbreaker at 48,25 (next to the normal wind rider master). Select \"I've been ordered to undertake an air strike\" and so long as your not mounted you start the flight. I find it really easy to kill all the required mobs in one pass. The best way i can find to do it, is to assign a key binding to the Arcane Charges and then Alt+Z the screen so you get a nice wide angle of view with no obstructions. Then you just spam the bound key - target over some mobs and click.... I made a vid with ZD softwares game recorder and stuck it on youtube if anyones as bored as I am atm and wants to see it.....\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xPzjZOQvQvc",
            date = "2008-04-22T04:25:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11533#comments:id=275589",
        },
        {
            id = 262531,
            score = 20,
            author = "Miyari",
            text = "Upon recovering the Sun's Reach Armory (completion of phase 2), this quest replaces Distraction at the Dead Scar (?quest=11532), and has the same objective but is a permanent daily quest that can be completed for reputation and reward, and will always be available once it is unlocked.\n\nFor more information regarding the Shattered Sun Offensive (http://www.wowhead.com/?faction=1077) daily quests and the \"phases\" of reclamation, check out this guide (http://www.wowhead.com/?forums&topic=17960#p155565) on the Wowhead forums! :)",
            date = "2008-03-29T10:41:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11533#comments:id=262531",
        },
        {
            id = 307986,
            score = 17,
            author = "163646",
            text = "you can actually do this quest on foot but there really no reason to do it this way. At least you can do it as a ranged class.",
            date = "2008-06-19T21:33:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=11533#comments:id=307986",
