    [12480] = {
    },
    [12513] = {
        {
            id = 308493,
            score = 382,
            author = "107485",
            text = "This is pretty funny, and obvious but I thought I'd give it mention.  Don Carlos sends you back in time to beat his former self up to get his hat for him, and in return creates a time paradox so to speak.\n\nDon Carlos is walking around in Old Hillsbrad, gets jumped by 1-5 guys and has his hat stolen! Some years in the future he's in Tanaris and gets the bright idea of having 1-5 guys go back in time for him and get his hat back. 1-5 guys go back in time, beat up young Don Carlos, takes his hat and brings it back to old Don Carlos.\n\nPretty clever on Blizzard's part.",
            date = "2008-06-20T13:02:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12513#comments:id=308493",
        },
        {
            id = 430924,
            score = 189,
            author = "109726",
            text = "An important thing your party needs to know is that this quest needs to be done before going to rescue Thrall. To find him, make a right from the cave till you hit the road then turn left. You will see him on his mount escorted by his pet. This of course means you will not be taking the dragon flight express straight to Durnholde Keep if you have this quest.\n\nI tried doing this quest after helping Thrall first and ended up searching in vain for an hour. When I reset and came back, there he was causally riding past Hillsbrad. He has 70k health, a mean dog, and a c0cky attitude. He is also annoyingly good at throwing his net.\n\nAs for the story line, now that I thought about it, it is actually hilarious because Don Carlos has no idea you can go back in time. Most likely he does not know the Caverns of Time exists. Remember, the quest is not his \"instruction\", but an \"idea\" Blizzard puts into your toon's head because your toon just happens to be taking a trip to the past. Poor Don Carlos thought no one would ever bring evidence of his one time defeat.",
            date = "2008-11-04T13:14:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12513#comments:id=430924",
        },
        {
            id = 308618,
            score = 146,
            author = "164807",
            text = "He patrols on the road from the keep to SS.\n\nAlso, if you kill him in heroic mode, he drops a blue version of the hat that summons his wolf until you take it off.\n\nWe ran heroic 5 times in a row to get the blue version for everyone. The instance doesn't save because he isn't a boss mob.\n\nThis is all on PTRs and subject to change.",
            date = "2008-06-20T16:42:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12513#comments:id=308618",
        },
        {
            id = 2012463,
            score = 80,
            author = "restopresto",
            text = "Ok straight to the point,\n\npick the quest up in Gadgetzan, then go to the Caverns of time.\n\nGo all the way to the bottom and pull up your map and enter the dungeon for Escape from Durnholde; its at the 10 o'clock from the middle of the map where Anachronus and Zaladormu are lying.\n\nAfter you enter the instance go all the way to the top and exit the cave and you will see Erozion the blood elf and Brazen the dragon. You don't to interact with either of these.\n\nGo due south (down) to the road and then go east (right). You should run into him. I smoked him on a 90 toon and got the quest item as well as his famous hat (blue) which allows you to summon an incorporeal spirit.\n\nHappy hunting!",
            date = "2014-10-13T21:00:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12513#comments:id=2012463",
        },
        {
            id = 319059,
            score = 68,
            author = "112652",
            text = "I don't think hes challenging you to go back and get his hat for him - I think he was simply bragging that he was not beaten, and the player's characters simply decided to go defeat his past self. I think this for a few reasons:\n\n\"Don Carlos has inadvertently challenged you to defeat his younger self in Old Hillsbrad. Afterwards, bring Don Carlos' Hat to him in Tanaris as proof. \"\nInadvertantly: without knowledge or intention - thus, an accident.\n\n\"My... my hat! But... how did you...?\n\nWell... no matter. So, now you know my secret. I WAS beaten... once. Here: take this hat, in return for mine. You've earned it. \"\n-turnin text, from wowwiki - this also suggests it was an accident that he sent you back, and did not expect it.",
            date = "2008-07-03T13:36:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12513#comments:id=319059",
        },
    },
    [12515] = {
        {
            id = 1150293,
            score = 16,
            author = "451796",
            text = "Don't have the dragon fly you to Old Hillsbrad directly, instead mount up and head down the road. I found him a short distance in front of his wolf, however, the wolf will assist as soon as you attack him.",
            date = "2010-10-22T11:34:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12515#comments:id=1150293",
        },
        {
            id = 1716754,
            score = 6,
            author = "Sarepthora",
            text = "Just finished the dungeon on Heroic after which I started looking for young Don Carlos and couldn't find him anywhere.\nSwitched to Normal and re-entered and found him on the road walking his lion.\nSo either hes only there on Normal or you shouldn't do the whole instance first.\nAnyways, as for his whereabouts, walk out of the cave south to the road and make a left, Don Carlos will be patrolling from the first fork in the road to the bridge over the river.\nI can also confirm it doesn't count as a quest for the Loremaster achievement",
            date = "2012-09-21T13:57:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12515#comments:id=1716754",
        },
        {
            id = 631438,
            score = 5,
            author = "332464",
            text = "This quest counts for the Loremaster of Kalimdor.",
            date = "2009-03-04T18:17:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12515#comments:id=631438",
        },
        {
            id = 1535238,
            score = 5,
            author = "784684",
            text = "I don't know why it says this quest is no longer available. I just did it earlier tonight. And no it does not count toward loremaster, like Stjimmy mentioned.",
            date = "2011-10-05T00:27:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12515#comments:id=1535238",
        },
        {
            id = 880035,
            score = 4,
            author = "476008",
            text = "Hat drops in any mode.  His dog will try to help defend him.  While Don is immune to polymorph, the dog is not.  So if you are a mage the dog is easily taken out of the equation.\n\nDon can be found wandering the main road between South Shore and the river bridge.",
            date = "2009-11-01T01:05:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12515#comments:id=880035",
        },
    },
    [12616] = {
        {
            id = 421751,
            score = 41,
            author = "163235",
            text = "In case you get this quest through a share, like I did, it gets turned in at Light Hope Chapel in EPL.",
            date = "2008-10-27T07:06:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12616#comments:id=421751",
        },
        {
            id = 421000,
            score = 30,
            author = "97145",
            text = "What is a man? A miserable little chamber of secrets! But enough talk, have at you!",
            date = "2008-10-26T14:58:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12616#comments:id=421000",
        },
        {
            id = 419706,
            score = 23,
            author = "Calidus",
            text = "You find him above Attumen's room, past the blacksmith and up the stairway.\nWhen you reach the top, go left through the doorway and you'll see the Chaimber doors ahead.\nMirkblood engages as soon as you open the door.\nHe spawns lots of adds that deal significant damage, so make sure to move the boss before the spirit adds activate.\nDrops a pet for everyone in the raid, as well as badges and an ilvl 115 item.",
            date = "2008-10-25T15:11:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12616#comments:id=419706",
        },
        {
            id = 419933,
            score = 21,
            author = "lunamoonraker",
            text = "Don't forget to pick up the scroll on the table in his room after killing him!, in order to get the quest 'Complete' message in quest log.\n\nThe quest does say:\n\ninvestigate Mirkblood's chamber, and return with any information you might find.\n\nThe scroll's title (and screenshot linked to help you) is:\n\n'Orders from the Lich King' (http://i365.photobucket.com/albums/oo96/lunamoonraker/ordersforthelichking.jpg)\n\nEasy to forget after a pretty hard battle. You do not receive any item, just the complete message.\n\nAs other suggest kiting is the secret. We just got tankadin to tank him back the way we came to avoid orbs. He dropped two badges, Arcanite Ripper and the Bat Pet for us.",
            date = "2008-10-25T18:19:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12616#comments:id=419933",
        },
        {
            id = 501425,
            score = 20,
            author = "40254",
            text = "Email From Blizzard:\n\n\"Thank you for contacting the World of Warcraft Game Master Department.\n\nPetition: I was wondering if I am still able to turn in the quest \"Chamber of Secrets\"? The npc is no longer where I originally got the quest.\n\nAnswer: Unfortunately, this quest was only available during the Scourge Invasion event before the release of Wrath of the Lich King, you may not be able to turn in this quest anymore if the quest NPC is no longer there.\n\nFor information on quests, you can visit the quest forums at http://forums.worldofwarcraft.com.\"\n\nConclusion: /cry & abandon quest",
            date = "2008-12-10T04:56:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12616#comments:id=501425",
        },
    },
    [13408] = {
        {
            id = 752300,
            score = 25,
            author = "Miro",
            text = "This should be helpfull to know.\n\nTo be able to get this quest in the first place u need to complete http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10143\n\nWish some1 had told me...",
            date = "2009-06-20T11:50:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13408#comments:id=752300",
        },
        {
            id = 928497,
            score = 21,
            author = "366972",
            text = "Simple quest. Just run inside of each of the three forts and stand there until it says that you've captured it. The amount of time that this take varies. Two things to note are:\n\n1) You can only capture them if they are neutral or are controlled by the other faction. If they are controlled by the other faction, they will first turn neutral after you standing there for a while. Keep standing there and you will soon capture it.\n\n2) If you are on a PvE server, you will have to be flagged for PvP in order to capture any of the forts.\n\nGood luck.",
            date = "2009-12-25T16:23:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13408#comments:id=928497",
        },
        {
            id = 837704,
            score = 13,
            author = "340831",
            text = "stealthing does not seem to move the progress bar of capping the point in your favor. just tried it on my rogue and whenever i stealthed, the progress bar would disappear and stop, till i unstealthed myself. so just a note to you guys out there, dont be standing around for 10 minutes in stealth waiting for something to happen.",
            date = "2009-09-11T11:06:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13408#comments:id=837704",
        },
        {
            id = 406924,
            score = 8,
            author = "VanCleef",
            text = "New quest in patch 3.0.2! You get this quest from Warrant Officer Tracy Proudwell (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=18266) in Honor Hold. It's probably the easiest way to get an Insignia of the Alliance.\n\nI'm not entirely sure what the level requirement is, but I could do it on my level 65 warlock.",
            date = "2008-10-15T13:38:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13408#comments:id=406924",
        },
        {
            id = 697911,
            score = 7,
            author = "345118",
            text = "It seems that the reward for this quest does not count for Freedom of the Alliance (http://www.wowhead.com/?achievement=701).\n\nEdit: Logged in the next day after the small 3.1.x update and the reward counted.",
            date = "2009-04-28T17:58:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13408#comments:id=697911",
        },
    },
    [13409] = {
        {
            id = 717940,
            score = 20,
            author = "366972",
            text = "Simple quest. Just run inside of each of the three forts and stand there until it says that you've captured it. The amount of time that this take varies. Two things to note are:\n\n1) You can only capture them if they are neutral or are controlled by the other faction. If they are controlled by the other faction, they will first turn neutral after you standing there for a while. Keep standing there and you will soon capture it.\n\n2) If you are on a PvE server, you will have to be flagged for PvP in order to capture any of the forts.\n\nGood luck.",
            date = "2009-05-16T11:25:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13409#comments:id=717940",
        },
        {
            id = 542248,
            score = 11,
            author = "288598",
            text = "You need to have completed the quest: http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=10124 before this quest will open up.  I also read somewhere that you need to be friendly.",
            date = "2009-01-02T03:19:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13409#comments:id=542248",
        },
        {
            id = 908072,
            score = 8,
            author = "493627",
            text = "Indeed, this quest is quite simple and quick for the XP & items rewarded and all three buildings are on a road so there are no monsters in addition to possible players. You do NOT however actually need to PK (player kill) if you are opposed to PvP to complete the tasks. You can simply go elsewhere if other opposing players are present. In fact, doing so is the smart move to complete this task quicker for each side.\n\nYou can only capture a structure if it is currently neutral or opposing controlled. Otherwise the status bar does not progress to capture.\n\nAs you enter a structure right click your portrait and under player-vs-player toggle 'Enable'. You must leave this setting on to complete each capture; toggling PvP immediately for 'Disable' to start your 5 minute countdown to PvE seems to stop the capture.\n\nWhile inside each perimeter and flagged for PvP a status bar appears on your screen; Alliance blue to the left and Horde red opposite. A vertical white line appears and then an arrow to indicate progress. When the line reaches your faction symbol the building's flags change and your log updates. You do not have to capture all three structures in sequence or on the same day for the base quest.\n\nAs mentioned in other comments this quest is also repeatable from the quest giver for coin and xp. Each capture rewards a further mark which can be used to buy PvP style items such as rings and socketable gems from the same NPC. Most items run about 10 marks.\n\nEach PK inside the structures also rewards a mark. However, be prepared for this fact as ruthless 70-80s who lack the courage to play on a full time PvP server occasionally gank much lower players given that excuse.",
            date = "2009-12-06T22:24:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13409#comments:id=908072",
        },
        {
            id = 566048,
            score = 6,
            author = "Discombobulator",
            text = "Confirming that the first completion of this quest does  count towards the quest achievement total for To Hellfire and Back.",
            date = "2009-01-17T03:30:50-06:00",
