    [13569] = {
        {
            id = 1084601,
            score = 348,
            author = "troelala",
            text = "The essence to use is in front of the quest giver. After activation the surroundings will become blur and you will see the three spirit around you with an exclamation mark. You will have to choose on of them.",
            date = "2010-07-19T18:08:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13569#comments:id=1084601",
        },
        {
            id = 1078308,
            score = 233,
            author = "Visil",
            text = "You can choose one of three buffs from the great spirits as a resultant of this quest. these are:\n\nThistlebear gives a 10% Reduction in damage taken\nMoonstalker gives a 10% haste bonus, and\nStag gives a 10% increased movement speed\n\nPlease bear in mind these effects are only active in the Darkshore region.",
            date = "2010-07-11T16:19:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13569#comments:id=1078308",
        },
        {
            id = 1682274,
            score = 178,
            author = "FuseinaOokami",
            text = "So I just wanted to bring all the information gathered here in one post:\n\nFirst off, the quest item that you need to right click is sitting at the questgiver's feet.\n\nSecond, you can only choose ONE of the three spirits. Here are the benefits of each spirit.\nStag - Grants 10% increase with movement speed (does not stack with druid forms with increased speed, does stack with Darkflight and Nightstalker), Become friendly with all Stags in Darkshore (there are very few stags in the area now)\nMoonstalker - Grants 10% increase in haste, Become friendly with all Moonstalker (cats) in the area (mainly in the southern area)\nBear - Grants 10% Damage reduction, Become friendly with all bears in the area (everywhere)\n\nThird, bear in mind that once chosen that the buff will persist even after you level past this area, but only in Darkshore, and you will not get a second chance at choosing.\n\nMy Opinions:\nIf you want to level quickly, choose BEAR. You actually travel a lot in Darkshore by Nightsaber provided by the Nightsaber Riders. There are far more bears in the Darkshore than any other creature. Plus the less damage will help in case that involves getting hit by a large group of mobs.\nIf you ever foresee yourself need to gather herbs from this area, or fish... or whatever else you can do here.... and you really don't care about the buffs, STAG will by your best choice. While there are little stags in Darkshore itself the increased movement speed will help out when running around and gathering nearby herbs or dig sites.\nIf your a druid or you can care less about speed and armor, then MOONSTALKER is your choice. Haste increases all extremely important stats.\nI will say this however: On PvP realms it should be noted that Horde may use Darkshore to get to Darnassus or as a refuge from a failed attempt on Darnassus. Thus making Moonstalker's effect a lot more wanting since it's usable at a higher level. Bear would also help in this case as well.\n\nMy choice, ironically, is Moonstalker. As a hunter on a PvP realm, that is high enough level to make this quest green, I really could care less about where mobs are. But the haste rating will help quickly killing my opponents. Every bit counts, and no one has confirmed that the Stag buff stacks with Aspect of the Cheetah.\n\nFinal note: Please don't vote mine down if you feel like it's repetitive (it's supposed to be just a place where to find ALL the information gathered) or if you disagree with what I'm saying, unless you feel that I am totally wrong about a mechanic of something. If that is the case please state why as a reply.",
            date = "2012-06-28T19:38:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13569#comments:id=1682274",
        },
        {
            id = 2879294,
            score = 62,
            author = "1963158",
            text = "There is an incense burner at Keeper Karithus feet.  It is a little hard to see, it blends in with his hooves.  Click it and the screen will go all blurry and three exclamation marks will pop up on your mini map.  Go over to each one, click and read the description.  Choose the one you want and return to Karithus.",
            date = "2019-03-28T22:31:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13569#comments:id=2879294",
        },
        {
            id = 1275877,
            score = 48,
            author = "264227",
            text = "Spirit of the Moonstalker quest text:\nI share these forests willingly, accepting night elf kind into my home, and on occasion calling them friend. Though they have been tainted greatly in recent memory, I can see in you the same strength, honor, and spirit that first endeared them to me.\n\nIf you place value in the ferocity necessary to overcome all odds, then I am willing to call you my champion. Know now that if you side with my kind, the other spirits will not accept you, so consider your choice carefully.\n\nSpirit of the Stag quest text:\nI am the caretaker for my kind, leading not through force, but through wisdom and swift action. Wisdom is what carries us into the deeper forest when danger beckons and swiftness is what leaves our enemies basking in our absence.\n\nIn this wisdom, I see through to your true intentions, and I know that you are deserving of my blessing, the blessing of my swiftness. It can be yours, but know that the other spirits will not welcome you once you proceed - consider this carefully before accepting my boon.\n\nSpirit of the Thistle Bear quest text:\nFor countless ages I have walked these forests and lived in these mountains. Through snow and fire, I have watched civilizations crumble and nature press on. Now, the very earth turns against us, and it becomes very apparent that we must fight if our legacy is to continue.\n\nYour heart is true, and I would choose you as our champion. If you value the thick hide and resilience of my kind, then accept my boon. Know that the other spirits will not accept you once this choice is made, so choose wisely.",
            date = "2011-01-03T20:45:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13569#comments:id=1275877",
        },
    },
    [13570] = {
        {
            id = 1179564,
            score = 622,
            author = "sunsmoon",
            text = "In order to get this quest, you must complete:\nInformation located in parenthesis are notes about the quest, such as quests you can skip.  Quests preceded by dashes are part of a direct chain started by the above quest.\n\n1a.) The Last Wave of Survivors (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13518)\n1b.) Threat from the Water (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13522)\n\n2a.) The Boon of the Seas (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13520)\n2b.) Buzzbox 413 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13521)\n----- No Accounting for Taste (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13527)\n----- Buzzbox 723 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13528)\n\n3a.) A Cure in the Dark (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13554) (Run back to town after you get this quest and get 3b.)\n3b.) The Corruption's Source (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13529)\n3c.) A Troubling Prescription (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13831) (SKIPPABLE)\n3d.) Bearer of Good Fortune (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13557) (SKIPPABLE)\n\n4a.) A Love Eternal (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13563) (SKIPPABLE)\n4b.) A Lost Companion (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13564)\n4c.) The Final Flame of Bashal'Aran (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13562) (SKIPPABLE)\n4d.) Solace for the Highborne (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13561) (SKIPPABLE)\n\n5a.) Unsavory Remedies (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13598)\n5b.) Twice Removed (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13565)\n5c.) Ritual Materials (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13566)\n----- The Ritual Bond (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13569) (If you are leveling through, I'd recommend getting the STAG buff for 10% movement speed.)\n\n6a.) Grimclaw's Return (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13599)\n6b.) An Ocean Not So Deep (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13560) (SKIPPABLE)\n6c.) The Shatterspear Invaders (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13589)\n\n7a.) Remnants of the Highborne (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13505)\n7b.) Shatterspear Laborers (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13504)\n7c.) Reason to Worry (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13506) (SKIPPABLE)\n----- Swift Response (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13508) (SKIPPABLE)\n----- One Bitter Wish (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13511) (SKIPPABLE)\n\n8a.) Denying Manpower (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13507) (can be completed alongside Swift Response)\n8b.) War Supplies (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13509) (can be completed alongside Swift Response)\n8c.) Timely Arrival (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13510) (can be completed alongside Swift Response, SKIPPABLE)\n\n9a.) On the Brink (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13513)\n9b.) Strategic Strikes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13512)\n9c.) Looting of Althalaxx (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13844) (SKIPPABLE)\n\n10a.) The Front Line (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13590)\n------- Ending the Threat (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13515)\n10b.) The Ancient's Ire (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13590) (SKIPPABLE)\n10c.) Disturbing Connections (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13591) (looted off of the objective for Ending the Threat)\n\nAfter turning in Disturbing Connections (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13591), Cerellean is now standing next to the Druid Trainer outside the Inn, next to Grimclaw, and will now allow you to do Remembrance of Auberdine (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13570).\n\nThanks whitehusky, Xaleen, LightsRAWR, flonne, suffragette, and Mykal for the help!",
            date = "2010-11-23T23:13:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13570#comments:id=1179564",
        },
        {
            id = 1981219,
            score = 25,
            author = "Grayy",
            text = "So I noticed that there are a lot of Quest lists that show how to get to Disturbing Connections (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13591). They pretty much list all the quests in the zone. I don't want to do all the quests so, I'm going to clear up what unlocks what and what is needed to finish this chain.\n\nTo start I'm on a druid that has only done the quest Writings of the Void (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28529/writings-of-the-void). This is a pretty easy quest and awards two achievements, going down and Ghosts in the Dark (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=5453).\n\nNext I did The Last Wave of Survivors (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13518). When I finished there were no new quests so I did Threat from the Water (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13522) and that unlocked Buzzbox 413 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13521). After finishing  Buzzbox 413 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13521) do the follow ups: No Accounting for Taste (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13527) and Buzzbox 723 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13528).\n\nNow do The Corruption's Source (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13529) and A Cure In The Dark (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13554).\n(A Cure In The Dark (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13554) might not be reqired because it didn't unlock anything when I finished it.)\n\nDoing The Corruption's Source (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13529) unlocks The Final Flame of Bashal'Aran (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13562), A Love Eternal (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13563) and A Lost Companion (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13564).\n\nTurning in A Lost Companion (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13564) unlocks Twice removed (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13565), Unsavory Remedies (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13598) and Ritual Materials (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13566). Do all three.\n\nThe next step is The Ritual Bond (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13569). To do this quest you need to pick an animal. That animal will give you a preeminent buff that you will have when ever you are in Darkshore.\n\nYour choices are:\nIf you choose Moonstalkers you get Blessing of the Moonstalker (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=64340)\nIf you choose the Bears you get Blessing of the Thistle Bear (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=64329)\nIf you choose the Stags you get Blessing of the Stag (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=64341)\n\nThen I did Grimclaw's Return (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13599) but I dont think it's required because The Shatterspear Invaders (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13589) was unlocked before I turned it in.\n\nDo The Shatterspear Invaders (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13589) and you are now where you want to be. Do the follow up quests Remnants of the Highborne (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13505) and Shatterspear Laborers (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13504). Now do Denying Manpower (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13507) and War Supplies (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13509).\n\nSide note on Denying Manpower (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13507). In my opinion, the reward from this quest, Tysha's Chestguard (http://www.wowhead.com/item=52597), is the best black leather you can get from quests at lvl 20 and that makes it good F2P mog gear.\n\nNow do:\nOn the Brink (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13513) and Strategic Strikes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13512).\n\nPick up The Front Line (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13590). Go over to the night elf mounted on a dark saber. She can give you a ride to your quest turn in.\n\nThe Ancients' Ire (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13514) is not needed but it gives you a ride to the next step as well as an easy way to clear the path.\n\nNow pick up Ending the Threat (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13515). You will need to talk to the quest giver again so she shoots Jor'kil and makes him weak for you. Make sure you loot Jor'kil as he drops Hellscream's Missive (http://www.wowhead.com/item=46318). The Missive starts the quest Disturbing Connections (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13591).\n\nRemembrance of Auberdine (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13570) opens up after this quest and rewards Withers (http://www.wowhead.com/item=46325).",
            date = "2014-07-16T18:58:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13570#comments:id=1981219",
        },
        {
            id = 1179660,
            score = 17,
            author = "Anaro",
            text = "There is one specific quest you need, it appears. This is an item-based quest from Jor'kil the Soulripper (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=32862) found in the cave at the top of the Shatterspear Vale, who is the end target of Ending the Threat (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13515).\n\nI missed this due to doing this quest at 80 and not bothering to loot the corpse. As soon as you turn it in you will see Cerellean Whiteclaw have the quest ! pop up.\n\nedit:\n@sunsmoon: Can you double check this for me? ;)",
            date = "2010-11-23T23:59:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13570#comments:id=1179660",
        },
        {
            id = 1178868,
            score = 10,
            author = "33829",
            text = "I have not been able to locate this npc, does anybody happen to know if he/she was moved?\n\n*edit* I have located him just outside the inn, but I did not see him until I finished the first few quests in the area.  It took me doing 33 quests in the zone for it to show up, so just do all of the first quests that take you all the way over to the Shatterspear Vale quest line, once that finishes you head back to town and turn in for your withers! :D",
            date = "2010-11-23T18:31:30-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13570#comments:id=1178868",
        },
        {
            id = 1085271,
            score = 6,
            author = "179247",
            text = "New pet! Trent that withers away unless you get him close to water. Awesome Blizz!",
            date = "2010-07-20T15:24:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13570#comments:id=1085271",
        },
    },
