            score = 96,
            author = "CleonanTehGnome",
            text = "Parts 1 through 6 guide (I'll post it on all quests)\nThe objective of each quest is to speak with a NPC in Thelsamar, Loch Modan.\nEach quest is acquired from a scroll object laying on the ground.\n\nPart l:\nLocation: (36.8, 61.2)\nDescription: Inside a cave, up the mountain south of Thelsamar, next to both a campfire https://www.wowhead.com/npc=33456 (Objective of https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13648)\n\nPart ll:\nLocation: (41.3, 39.1)\nDescription: Inside the Central-East area of the crater where \"The Loch\" used to be. You will see a dwarven in-ground house entrance with a fishing trainer and a half-buried dock in the sand. The scroll will be slightly under the right side of the dock (Looking away from the house), next to one of its small support pillars.\n\nPart lll:\nLocation: (61.6, 73.1)\nDescription: At the bottom of a crate, to the left of a cave entrance which occasionally houses a rare spider: https://www.wowhead.com/npc=14266.\n\nPart lV:\nLocation: (68.1, 66.0)\nDescription: This scroll is towards the center of Ironband's Excavation Site. To know if you're on the right track if you stumble upon a wooden plank path. At the end of that path, to the left, will be the quest.\nNOTE: This is not near the quest givers, it is behind the huge green wall.\n\nPart V:\nLocation: (53.7, 38.2)\nDescription: If you look at your Loch Modan map, towards the center of the dried up lake, there is a somewhat large patch of water. In the upper right area of that general region, near most likely to be the largest tree, will be the scroll.\n\nPart Vl:\nLocation: (73.1, 35.9)\nDescription: Directly south of Mo'Grosh Stronghold, there is a troll statue near the first line of trees, will be part 6 of the quest.\n\nThe Final Part:\nAfter completing ALL SIX of the scroll quests, you will be offered one final quest entitled \"Heartfelt Appreciation\" which still entails you talking to the same NPC as always, but gives a bit more EXP than the other six.\n\nGood luck!\n(Rate up!)",
            date = "2011-06-16T21:38:38-05:00",
