    [13881] = {
        {
            id = 1428628,
            score = 4,
            author = "835729",
            text = "I've had problems too.  I've accepted the quest, killed the consumed Thistle bears and saw the \"Consumed Thistle Bear slain: x/6\" and the tracker along the right side simply does not account for it.  After killing all 6, I return to the quest giver and cannot complete.  I had abandined, re-accepted, and re-done the quest several times now and the same thing happens.\n\nI've had this problem once or twice before, on other quests, and at some point even though the objectives tracker does not list it as finished, I was able to turn in the quest anyway (I don't remember where it was because it has been a while).\n\nI don't know if it matters, but I am an 85 human Warlock.  My pet is not active, so that's not the issue, as sometimes in the past if my pet kills the mob before I can aggro it I don't get the credit.  Does killing them with one shot somehow mean that the tracker does not recognize the kill?\n\nIf you are wondering why an 85 is questing this, I'm trying to earn the Darkshore Quests achievement towards the Loremaster of Kalimdor achievement.",
            date = "2011-05-27T08:38:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13881#comments:id=1428628",
        },
        {
            id = 1183642,
            score = 3,
            author = "365125",
            text = "The \"well\" is actually a pond:  45.1, 79.2",
            date = "2010-11-25T02:39:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13881#comments:id=1183642",
        },
        {
            id = 2584348,
            score = 3,
            author = "ChadCloman",
            text = "If it's July/August 2018 and you're doing the War of the Thorns (http://www.wowhead.com/event=959/war-of-the-thorns) quest chain as part of the BFA leadup, you probably cannot complete this quest. It's an old quest. The area is now phased, and the old quest may be impossible to complete.\n\nLikewise you may have similar problems with https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13892 and https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13525, which can both be safely ignored.\n\nTemporarily turning off \"trivial quest\" detection (via the magnifying glass icon on the mini-map) will prevent you from seeing these quests.",
            date = "2018-07-25T00:14:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13881#comments:id=2584348",
        },
        {
