            score = 5,
            author = "Tirasmol",
            text = "The flight is automatic so all you have to do is aim the large green target on the ground and fire away.  Yes, the bird is flying somewhat quickly and over the trees, making it really hard to spot the animals, but you can take the flight more than once if needed.  You'll fly north first - aim for the stags, there are usually several small deer around them so you get credit for multiple targets even if you never see them.  When you go west, aim for the Moonstalkers.  Look for bears as you fly south.",
            date = "2010-11-27T20:25:09-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13885#comments:id=1191526",
        },
        {
            id = 1235958,
            score = 4,
            author = "321842",
            text = "The bears are the hardest, because of the tree canopy. I recommend a combination of:\n\n1) Spamming the target reticle as fast as possible, somewhat randomly\n2) Targeting clumps of trees, as the bears seem to hide in them\n3) Occasionally looking behind you to see bears, especially as you approach Master's Glaive.\n\nIf you're lucky, or good you ought to finish this in one pass. Twice around should be enough for the rest of us to complete this quest.",
            date = "2010-12-15T14:11:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13885#comments:id=1235958",
        },
        {
            id = 2090197,
            score = 2,
            author = "Random0532",
            text = "You'll be given the temporary mount https://www.wowhead.com/npc=34375 (https://www.wowhead.com/spell=65384), and have one ability: https://www.wowhead.com/spell=65373. Use it to cleanse eight (8) of the following types of animals (usually appears in the following order):\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=34318 or https://www.wowhead.com/npc=34396\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=2070 or https://www.wowhead.com/npc=2071 or https://www.wowhead.com/npc=2237\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=2165",
            date = "2015-01-17T14:39:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13885#comments:id=2090197",
        },
    },
    [13886] = {
        {
            id = 1224834,
            score = 50,
            author = "Laitarne",
            text = "I had the same problem, after trying it a couple times I think I narrowed it down to the quest being bugged so that if the periodic damage from Vortex Vengeance kills him you are not properly credited for the kill.\n\nMy final time, I slowly worked him to death with Sky Lightning after weakening him enough with Vortex Vengeance and was properly credited.",
            date = "2010-12-11T13:41:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13886#comments:id=1224834",
        },
        {
            id = 1200302,
            score = 14,
            author = "Whiterock",
            text = "Pre-quests: Hot Lava (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13880) and Put Out The Fire (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13884).",
            date = "2010-12-01T13:44:51-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13886#comments:id=1200302",
        },
        {
            id = 1393669,
            score = 6,
            author = "Gasparus",
            text = "I had the exact opposite happen.  Killed him five times with Sky Lightning with no DOT on him.  Then I tried letting the DOT kill him and got credit.  If it's bugged for you, might want to try it both ways.",
            date = "2011-04-17T16:47:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13886#comments:id=1393669",
        },
        {
            id = 1193246,
            score = 5,
            author = "622488",
            text = "Very easy quest.  After accepting the quest, talk to the vortex again and he will turn you into a cyclone and swap out your skill bar.  You will automatically fly up to the boss and, after defeating him, will be automatically flown back down.  In battle, throw the DoT spell on him (#2) and then hit on refresh, optherwise spamming the tiny damage spell (#1).  Damage text will scroll when you have the Lordly  Immolation on you and just immediately cleanse it with #3.  As long as you keep it cleansed (comes every 15 seconds or so) you will have no problems.",
            date = "2010-11-28T11:55:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13886#comments:id=1193246",
        },
        {
            id = 1708738,
            score = 5,
            author = "1028336",
            text = "First tried using both Sky Lightning and Vortex Vengence: No kill credit.\nNext tried using only Sky Lightning as final kill strike, no DoT: No kill credit.\nTried using only Sky Lightning throughout the fight: no kill credit.\nFinally tried using only Vortex Vengence throughout the fight: Kill Credit! Yay!",
            date = "2012-09-03T12:57:53-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13886#comments:id=1708738",
        },
    },
    [13887] = {
        {
            id = 813948,
            score = 11,
            author = "46481",
            text = "Toxic Tolerance (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13850) leads to the quest Venomhide Eggs (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13887)\n\nToxic Tolerance (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13850) is a very annoying quest because you have to be doing damage to the Venomhide Ravasuare for it to be able to bleed on you. The higher level you are the harder of a time you will have with this quest.\n\nOnce you do compelte the Toxic Tolerance (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13850) quest you will then continue o to Venomhide Eggs (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13887)\n\nVenomhide Eggs (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13887) is a very easy quest. Just got to the egg piles that you went to for the Lar'korwi (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=9684) quest The Scent of Lar'korwi (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=4291)\n\nOnce you are done that you will receive the quest They Grow Up So Fast (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13906). This quest gives you a non combot pet that takes up bag space that you summon that will give you a daily quest. Completeing the daily quest will give you a venomhide baby tooth (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=47196).\n\nTo complete They Grow Up So Fast (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13906) you will need the following\n\nVenomhide Baby Tooth x20\nRunecloth x20\nRugged Leather x20\nGold x80\n\nand then presto you have yourself a Venomhide Ravasaur Mount",
            date = "2009-08-16T21:04:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13887#comments:id=813948",
        },
        {
            id = 800763,
            score = 8,
            author = "Windriver",
            text = "As a bonus, this quest DOES count for Loremaster of Kalimdor.",
            date = "2009-08-06T10:04:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13887#comments:id=800763",
        },
        {
            id = 798695,
            score = 7,
            author = "reallydead",
            text = "Being a Skinner really helps for this chain too, as more and more people were killing ravasaurs, then again killing the diemetredons/pterrordons and such, i just ran behind them all and skinned them while i was on the same quest. i got all the rugged leathers i needed from diemetredons and more than enough gold for the runecloth and to pay for my saddle selling the rest.",
            date = "2009-08-05T04:10:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13887#comments:id=798695",
        },
        {
            id = 804643,
            score = 7,
            author = "419768",
            text = "Found the Venomhide Eggs at (62, 80) (62, 65) (60, 72) (58, 78)\n\nMap: http://www.wowhead.com/?object=195022",
            date = "2009-08-09T05:07:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13887#comments:id=804643",
        },
        {
            id = 767816,
            score = 6,
            author = "165675",
            text = "Run around the same area as where you had the venom splashed on you (from the previous quest) and there will be mounds of dark eggs scattered on the ground. Some will have light colored eggs. Collect four and ta-da!",
            date = "2009-07-04T16:31:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13887#comments:id=767816",
        },
    },
    [13888] = {
        {
            id = 1371898,
            score = 29,
            author = "523682",
            text = "The bug appears to be with the DOT damage.  If the quest boss dies to dot damage you may not get credit.\n\nI did the abandon+retry after each failed attempt just to be sure...and I tested it with Lightning Kill , DOT Kill and Manual Kill (flying up and killing it)\n\nOnly way I ever got credit was from Lighting Kill...so widdle him down to 10% then just kill with Lighting Attack (1 on Vehicle bar)",
            date = "2011-03-20T16:00:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13888#comments:id=1371898",
        },
        {
            id = 1192330,
            score = 15,
            author = "Constantinehl2",
            text = "Just did it.Used Vortex Vengence all the time till i got him to 300HP and than only Sky Lightning.Got my kill with the first time.",
            date = "2010-11-28T04:08:42-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13888#comments:id=1192330",
        },
        {
            id = 1194402,
            score = 10,
            author = "Aphileon",
            text = "Prereq to this starts in Hellscream's Watch called Thunder Peak (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13879)",
            date = "2010-11-28T20:56:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13888#comments:id=1194402",
        },
        {
            id = 1968640,
            score = 7,
            author = "Tommyboypsp",
            text = "To obtain this quest you need to do a few quests in Hellscream's Watch, starting with Tweedle's Dumb, until Broyk can give you a quest named Thunder Peak. Then you have to do both quests for the other two elementals before you can accept this one.",
            date = "2014-05-30T05:41:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13888#comments:id=1968640",
        },
        {
            id = 1183163,
