            text = "I dropped the quest and picked it up again and I got credit for killing him, I also waited to attack him until attack 1 was available, not sure what fixed it.",
            date = "2010-11-24T22:37:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13888#comments:id=1183163",
        },
    },
    [13889] = {
        {
            id = 799983,
            score = 24,
            author = "Coldflame78",
            text = "Simply just kill any Dinosaurs in Un'goro to Receive [Fresh Dinosaur Meat].\n\nThen feed it to your little bud.\n\nEDIT: Except for Raptors. They will not drop it.",
            date = "2009-08-05T22:31:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13889#comments:id=799983",
        },
        {
            id = 771848,
            score = 15,
            author = "207575",
            text = "Hungry, Hungry Hippos (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hungry_Hungry_Hippo)! ...er...Hatchling!\n\nEDIT: Oh, and as for the drawing bit, Bliz has been very strongly hinting that Azerothian raptors are far from just simple beasts. They wear feathers and beads, steal things (http://ptr.wowhead.com/?quest=3281) and some live in mud huts (a small settlement in the Barrens). When you add in that many raptors live near humanoids whom they could observe, it's not inconceivable that the race could begin to make some technological advances sometime in the near future. Probably not in WoW, there would be a lot of gameplay complications, but perhaps in a future game...?",
            date = "2009-07-08T14:29:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13889#comments:id=771848",
        },
        {
            id = 803608,
            score = 8,
            author = "Asadro",
            text = "Go to the t west part of Un'goro  There is a lot of dinosaurs there=)",
            date = "2009-08-08T09:46:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13889#comments:id=803608",
        },
        {
            id = 1176087,
            score = 5,
            author = "621632",
            text = "This quest is painfully easy. The hard part is flying there from Orgrimmar. You can collect more than 15 pieces of meat, but it disappears with the quest so don't try to stock up(like you can for the netherwing dailies). Carbonite's coordinates are quite off, but you can find Pterrordaxes/frenzied and diemetradons/frenzied's all around the bottom half of Un'Goro. It will take around 5 minutes of your time if you are level 80. This quest does not count towards Loremaster, but the quest to actually get the raptor does. This quest does count towards your daily daily quests completed.",
            date = "2010-11-20T17:09:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13889#comments:id=1176087",
        },
        {
            id = 829823,
            score = 4,
            author = "Spac3Rat",
            text = "You'll have to do this quest 20 times to get the 20 Venomhide Baby Tooth (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=47196) for the quest They Grow Up So Fast (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13906), which will allow you to ride your new mount with Whistle of the Venomhide Ravasaur (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=46102).\n\nThis all starts at Mor'vek (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=11701) when he gives you the quest Toxic Tolerance (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13850).\n\nThe full chain quest is:\n- Toxic Tolerance (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13850)\n- Venomhide Eggs (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13887)\n\nThen the following quests for 20 days (it's a random quest each day)\n\n- Hungry, Hungry Hatchling (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13915)\n- Gorishi Grub (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13903)\n- Poached, Scrambled, Or Raw? (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13904)\n- Searing Roc Feathers (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13905)\n\nAnd finally you will finish They Grow Up So Fast (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=13906) and get your new raptor mount.",
            date = "2009-09-02T08:51:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13889#comments:id=829823",
        },
    },
    [13890] = {
        {
            id = 1076812,
            score = 110,
            author = "447186",
            text = "For this quest you will need to kill 10 Mystlash Hydra (http://cata.wowhead.com/npc=3721#comments). They will drop Mystlash Hydra Blubber. You will find a lot of them in the waters to the west of Zoram'gar Outpost starting about 9,33. When you have your 10 go back to the forge (11,35). It's inside the building. Melt your blubber into oil at the forge and make your way over to the lighthouse at  (6,28). Climb the stairs to the top, use your oil on the Lighthouse Fire and your done.\n\nLance\nBeta tester for;\nWrath of the Litch King\nCataclysm",
            date = "2010-07-09T16:07:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13890#comments:id=1076812",
        },
        {
            id = 2602390,
            score = 34,
            author = "1765217",
            text = "You're here because you ran straight to the lighthouse like a mindless peon, caring to read the quest description only in front of that fire that you clicked ten times in vain. How do I know? I did exactly the same thing.\n\nSo, here's what you need to know: Mystlash Hydra Oil (https://www.wowhead.com/item=46366/mystlash-hydra-oil) is created by combining 10 https://www.wowhead.com/item=46365, that are dropped by Mystlash Hydras (https://www.wowhead.com/npc=3721/mystlash-hydra). You can find them approximately where you have to pick up the scrap metal for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13883.\n\nJust head there, pick up the blubbers,go back to the forge to melt the oil and finally you can go back to the lighthouse to lit the fire.",
            date = "2018-08-23T12:59:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13890#comments:id=2602390",
        },
        {
            id = 1612721,
            score = 28,
            author = "917229",
            text = "By \"Forge\" they mean \"Anvil.\"",
            date = "2012-01-17T14:52:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13890#comments:id=1612721",
        },
        {
            id = 1294056,
            score = 11,
            author = "764824",
            text = "In Zoram'gar  you go to the building with the anvil in it... it's glowing red.  Then right click on the blubber by the anvil and it will make the oil.",
            date = "2011-01-14T20:14:23-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13890#comments:id=1294056",
        },
        {
            id = 2565067,
            score = 11,
            author = "Wilaeus",
            text = "One of the worst quests in the game.\n\nFighting ten creatures at the bottom of the sea: Check\nBacktracking to town without being able to turn in every quest in the area at once: Check\nDistinct lack of map markers and the need to consult Wowhead if you haven't done this quest already: Check\n\nIf you're don't care about completing Ashenvale, SKIP THIS QUEST",
            date = "2018-04-30T00:20:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13890#comments:id=2565067",
        },
    },
