    [13963] = {
        {
            id = 1092715,
            score = 92,
            author = "Nulgar",
            text = "Talking to the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=34523 gives 5 options:Who sent you!\n\nObviously, the first option gives you only a  or \"I say nothing\"\nThe second and third options, being brutal, at first only meet resistance as well, but after a time or a certain combination of beatings and kicks (or just random, couldn't figure that out yet) will get the quilboar to sayYou waste your strength! Tortusk train us warriors never to talk.\nOh - I've said too much!which completes the objective.\nHowever, you can also choose the fourth and fifth option, which will get the quilboar to blab immediately:Mnn,  why you cook this meat? Tortusk tells us meat taste best when stolen and raw.Haha -  ha - heee!  Haha no stop haha   Hee hee! Battlemaster Tortusk never prepared us for this!each followed by \"Oh - I've said too much!\" of course.\n\nThe brutal options will buff you with [spell=65629 buff=true], increasing your attack power and magical damage done by 8 for 20 minutes. Using one of the brutal options hide the nice options, but you can click off the Nasty buff to see those again.\nBeing nice buffs you with [spell=65628 buff=true], increasing your health regeneration by 3% for 20 minutes - which, at this level, is rather uninteresting, since you still have a huge HP regen out of combat anyway, compared to your HP.\nIf you don't manage to beat it out of the quilbar to complete the objective and receive the Nasty buff, simply be nice to him once to complete the quest, click off the Saintly buff, then kick him again.\n\nSpeaking of clicking off, having the Saintly buff prevents you from seeing any option whatsoever. If you happen to choose tickling first, thinking it to be some random funny meaningless thing, but want to check out the other options as well, don't try and abort the quest, this will get you nowhere :P Just click off the buff. Took me a while to figure this out, so I better share this with you, to save you the humiliation.",
            date = "2010-07-31T05:03:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13963#comments:id=1092715",
        },
        {
            id = 1194699,
            score = 54,
            author = "348590",
            text = "compared to the morally questionable prisoner torture I had to do in Wrath, it was much more fun to tickle this quillboar!",
            date = "2010-11-29T00:21:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13963#comments:id=1194699",
        },
        {
            id = 1433797,
            score = 29,
            author = "57893",
            text = "You can continue punching/kicking him in the face after he talks.\n\nDon't give me that look, you wouldn't have picked that option if you didn't enjoy it.",
            date = "2011-06-04T02:01:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13963#comments:id=1433797",
        },
        {
            id = 1379716,
            score = 24,
            author = "Nulgar",
            text = "It's a general phrase/metaphor, not a movie/series quote.\n\nhttp://www.phrases.org.uk/meanings/by-hook-or-by-crook.htmlMeaning\nBy whatever means necessary - be they fair or foul.\n\nOrigin\nIt is sometimes suggested that 'by hook or by crook' derives from the custom in mediaeval England of allowing peasants to take from royal forests whatever deadwood they could pull down with a shepherd's crook or cut with a reaper's billhook. [...] Another commonly repeated suggestion is that the phrase comes from the names of the villages of Hook Head and the nearby Crooke, in Waterford, Ireland. Hook Head and Crooke are on opposite sides of the Waterford channel [...] A third suggestion is that the phrase derives from two learned judges, called Hooke and Crooke, who officiated during the reign of Charles I (born 1600 - died 1649) and who were called on to solve difficult legal cases. Hence, the cases would be resolved 'by Hooke or by Crooke'.",
            date = "2011-03-30T02:16:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13963#comments:id=1379716",
        },
        {
            id = 1601890,
            score = 23,
            author = "354783",
            text = "Important: If you attempt to abandon the quest in order to get the other buff that you didn't get, you have to right-click the old buff to get rid of it before you get the dialog options to get the new one.",
            date = "2011-12-25T16:37:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=13963#comments:id=1601890",
        },
    },
