    [14318] = {
        {
            id = 1186273,
            score = 509,
            author = "TheBobZ",
            text = "Upon acceptance of this quest talk to the quest giver to \"ride him\" as a mount, otherwise you will not be able to interact with the Fatherstone.",
            date = "2010-11-25T23:41:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=14318#comments:id=1186273",
        },
        {
            id = 1189327,
            score = 73,
            author = "668287",
            text = "Note that your action bar is replaced with an ability to use the spear. If you don't notice this, you'll do as I did, and ride the centaur back to the glen; talk to the quest giver again and get another ride over and use #1 this time...",
            date = "2010-11-27T01:51:51-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=14318#comments:id=1189327",
        },
        {
            id = 1205927,
            score = 49,
            author = "32903",
            text = "I did not get this to follow-up on Breakout (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14314).\n\nHad to do Cenarion Property (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14316) for this to become available.",
            date = "2010-12-04T11:23:30-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=14318#comments:id=1205927",
        },
        {
            id = 2009964,
            score = 44,
            author = "Zaynah",
            text = "I did this quest for Loremaster (achievement=7520) and, probably because of ignorance, being at a much higher level, I got this wrong a couple of times. Here is a summary of what to do / not to do...\n\nStep 1:\nDo not fly or ride to the quest marker on the map. You will not be able to interact with the Fatherstone in any way.\n\nThe only way to place the Spear of the Kolkar Khan (item=49166) is to talk to the quest giver Khan Leh'Prah (npc=36056) and accept a ride to the Fatherstone. You will basically enter a \"vehicle\" called Khan Leh'Prah (npc=36056) and ride on his back to the quest location. This will take a while but there is no way around it.\n\nStep 2:\nDo not try to use the quest item Spear of the Kolkar Khan (item=49166) from your inventory in any way. Do not exit the \"vehicle\" that is Khan Leh'Prah (npc=36056) - this will basically cancel the quest attempt and he will take you all the way back to the start location, which takes just as long as getting to the Fatherstone.\n\nThe only way to place the Spear of the Kolkar Khan (item=49166) is to use ability 1 of the \"vehicle\" Khan Leh'Prah (npc=36056) when you reach the Fatherstone.\n\nStep 3:\nYou have to defend the location, Spear of the Kolkar Khan (item=49166). Friendly mobs spawn around the location who help you against the attackers. It is four defenders vs four attackers if I remember correctly.\nAfter three waves of attackers, Khan Kammah (npc=36163) will spawn and you can turn in the quest.",
            date = "2014-10-04T23:16:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=14318#comments:id=2009964",
        },
        {
            id = 2578239,
            score = 44,
            author = "Seonsha",
            text = "And once again I get caught up by the basics. I am so used to accepting a questing, immediately clicking accepting then running/flying to a circle to kill whatever mob is there.\n\nSo unsurprising this quest caught me out for a second time when I brought my most recent toon through there. I clicked for the quest and immediately clicked accept. Mounting up and running there to the gold circle only to find out I had to ride the NPC to destination, lol. Needless to say I had to run back which was annoying.\n\nLesson of the day for me: these are legacy quests. Quests designed for a time when people would read every quest dialogue once minimum, maybe 2 to 3 times before even daring to hit the WASD on the keyboard. How times have changed and how the old content shows the simplicity I am used to with newer content.",
            date = "2018-07-03T19:40:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=14318#comments:id=2578239",
        },
    },
