    [24430] = {
        {
            id = 1667488,
            score = 29,
            author = "992405",
            text = "I can't control this crazy thing! Most annoying UI quest problems I've ever had. Finally figured it all out:\n\n1. Mount the flying lion (\"grounded wind rider\") right next to the quest-giver.\n\n2. Fly it around:\n\nSPACE-BAR goes upwards,\nX goes downwards,\notherwise forward / backwards / L / R / strafe-L / strafe-R are the same.\n\nThe strafe-L or -R is very useful (usually Q and E on your key-bindings) as is the \"/\" SLASH-KEY on number-pad. (Strafe moves you sideways. Slash toggles walking / running pace.)\n\n3. Targeting:\n\nFly way way way up. I flew to max. Change your camera perspective so that you are looking way way way down (but you can continue to include yourself in the image if you wish). Locate the teeny-tiny white targeting circle, which is straight ahead of you on the ground some distance away. Move the lion so that your targeting circle is exactly on a target and then hit the bomb button. Wait a long time and you will see a teeny bomb finally drop and kaboom the target's gone.\n\nTargets fade out, but maybe you can still kill them. Sometimes the Glaive Throwers seem to disappear if you wait too long, but I bombed an empty spot where a Glaive Thrower used to be and got credit for killing a Glaive Thrower anyway.\n\nThe Command Center is a building next to the bridge. It's square and has crossed peaks on its roof that form an X. Target the X.\n\nNow that you've bombed 'em, look around. You can see a Golf Course (somebody's \"Pleasure Palace\" as mentioned?) next to a rocket pad. This quest gives you the chance to look 'round so you can drool in envy about the abilities and destinations that you can only access once you've levelled to where you have flying ability.\n\nQuickest way to return is to jump off the lion and fall  to the ground. The graveyard is right next to the quest-giver. >:)\n\nOr you could use the X key to lower your altitude until you get to the ground. Low flying near enemies means damage (a Glaive flying at you from a Glaive Thrower is kinda cool but you're probably dead if you see one, the lion doesn't move very quick). You can just stay out of their range 100% of the time you're targeting them.",
            date = "2012-05-16T12:05:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24430#comments:id=1667488",
        },
        {
            id = 1193682,
            score = 25,
            author = "298516",
            text = "Just in case anyone else is a dumbass like me (I sat there for 10 minutes attacking the tower from every possible angle) it is the small building right next to the bridge which is the command center!",
            date = "2010-11-28T15:10:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24430#comments:id=1193682",
        },
        {
            id = 1417902,
            score = 18,
            author = "176962",
            text = "Keep hitting the space bar until you are quite quite high above the glaives.  Make sure your perspective does not show you or your mount at all...you must be able to see the tiny targeter, which is not very easy to manipulate.  Target a glaive and keep pounding #1 key until its been bombed out of existence.  Watch your health meter to make sure you havent been hit with their flying blades.  If you have, you can go back and get a new mount.",
            date = "2011-05-13T17:20:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24430#comments:id=1417902",
        },
        {
            id = 1180467,
            score = 16,
            author = "463376",
            text = "You can use this mount to fly over and visit Galliwix's Pleasure Palace which is otherwise unreachable at the moment without a lot of messing around jumping from rock to rock (look on youtube for video's on how to get there on foot).",
            date = "2010-11-24T06:21:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24430#comments:id=1180467",
        },
        {
            id = 2583676,
            score = 14,
            author = "TheRealGiovanni",
            text = "This thing was hard to fly and there are no lessons.\n\nThe only way I could get it to work was to hold the right mouse click and use my WASD keys. Spacebar didn't work to raise the altitude.\n\nSpam 1 (which is the cannonball) and aim like its coming out of the Wind Riders mouth.\n\nBest of luck!",
            date = "2018-07-23T00:09:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24430#comments:id=2583676",
        },
    },
    [24433] = {
