    [24449] = {
        {
            id = 1231717,
            score = 52,
            author = "106241",
            text = "This appears to be the main quest vain for the zone, so be prepared for a long trip. I'll update as more information comes to light or changes. Please post replies for corrections.\n\nWhile you don't need it to start the chain, you may as well start in the beginning.\n\nWarchief's Command Board (http://www.wowhead.com/object=206109) Quest: Warchief's Command: Azshara! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28496)\n-or-\nGarrosh Hellscream (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=39605) Quest(Goblin): Report to the Labor Captain (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25275) (Goblin, step 6 of chain She Loves Me, She Loves Me Not! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25243))\n\n1. Quest Hub: Orgrimmar Rear Gate (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=16:265774)\nLabor Captain Grabbit (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=35086) starts with the Quests: Runaway Shredder! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14129) & The Captain's Logs (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14134) & Up a Tree (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14135).\nCompleting Unlocks Quest: Report to Horzak (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14162).\n\n2. Quest Hub: Orgrimmar Rocketway Exchange (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=16:295673)\nHorzak Zignibble (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=35091/horzak-zignibble) gives the Quests: Basilisk Bashin' (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14161) & Stone Cold (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14165).\nCompleting Continues the Stone Cold Chain: The Perfect Prism (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14190), Prismbreak (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14192), Refleshification (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14194).\n\nAt his quest hub you must also complete the quests given by Foreman Fisk (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=35085): A Quota to Meet (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14197).\n\nPrivate Worcester (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=36752) now gives the Quest: Another Warm Body (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14468) which send you to...\n\n3. Quest Hub: Forlorn Ridge (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=16:291572)\nHere Commander Molotov (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=36749) gives you the Quest: Hand-me-downs (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14469).\n\nYou must also finish the other quests at this hub given by Glix Grindlock (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=36744) (Military Breakthrough (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14470), and later In The Face! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14472)) & Xiz Salvoblast (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=36746) (First Degree Mortar (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14471)).\n\nMolotov now has the Quest: Profitability Scouting (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=24452) & Private Chat (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=24453).\n\n4. Quest Hub: Bilgewater Harbor (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=16:560506)\nAt this point you can head to Bilgewater Harbor and find a Wrenchmen Recruitment Poster (http://www.wowhead.com/object=201578) for the Quest: Operation Fishgut (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14478), leading to Rapid Deployment (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=24455), and There Are Many Like It (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14479).\n\n5. Quest Hub: The Shattered Strand (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=16:408545)\nNow that you're on The Shattered Strand seek out Lieutenant Drex (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=36920) for the Quest: Mop Up (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=24435). You must also finish the quest of nearby Sergeant Hort (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=36921/sergeant-hort) (Halo Drop (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=24436)).\n\nDrex now offers the Quest: Field Promotions (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=24448) sending you to...\n\n6. Quest Hub: Ruins of Eldarath (http://www.wowhead.com/maps)\nPick up every quest at the hub, from Captain Tork (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=36745) (Still Beating Heart (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14487)), Sergeant Zelks (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=36895) (Extermination (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14480), Head of the Snake (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14484), Ticker Required (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14485)), and Tora Halotrix (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=36894) (Handling the Goods (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14486)).\n\nOnce these are finished, Tork offers the Quest: Shore Leave (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=24449), a simple turn in.",
            date = "2010-12-13T23:11:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24449#comments:id=1231717",
        },
        {
            id = 1202752,
            score = 12,
            author = "710509",
            text = "Simple, just a \"go to this person\" quest\nNote: You do not have to run or swim back, just jump into the copter behind the quest giver",
            date = "2010-12-02T18:37:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24449#comments:id=1202752",
        },
        {
            id = 1405253,
            score = 6,
            author = "Aquifel",
            text = "If you want a faster path to your blue items, the quest Mutiny, Mon ( [quest=14063 domain=www] ), has almost identical rewards (gun replaced with a dagger, sorry hunters) and is part of a very short chain.",
            date = "2011-04-30T16:01:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24449#comments:id=1405253",
        },
        {
            id = 1967356,
            score = 3,
            author = "853632",
            text = "After escaping the Wandering Isle, I went looking for the best gear available for my level 13, Twink Panda Mage.  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24449 had the lowest level requirements for rare quality boots, https://www.wowhead.com/item=53428.  Although https://www.wowhead.com/quest=14063 offers a basically identical reward, that quest may not be available until at least level 14.  I turned off my xp and progressed toward my goal without leveling at all past level 13.\n\nIdeally I didn't want to do more quests than necessary to complete Shore Leave.  As I worked on quests in the zone, I kept checking in with Captain Tork to see if his quests had become available.  I skipped the quests at the Orgimmar's rear gates, and went straight for the quests at the Orgrimmar Rocketway Exchange.  Once I had completed the quests there and at Forlorn Ridge, I was sent on the rocket to the Southern Rocketway Terminus, at that point the breadcrumb quest for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=14478 became available at Billgewater Harbor.  So I skipped the quests at the Southern Terminus.\n\nFrom there it was onward to the Shattered Strand quests and then finally the Ruins of Eldarath.  I turned in https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24449 with just 30 quests completed in Azshara.  Although there may still be a more efficient path to completing Shore Leave than what I was able to find, if you follow my steps you can shave around 20 quests off your mission for low level blues. Enjoy.",
            date = "2014-05-23T19:07:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24449#comments:id=1967356",
        },
        {
            id = 2337320,
            score = 1,
            author = "Vayall",
            text = "where do you go after you have handed this in, I can't find any quests?",
            date = "2016-06-05T15:00:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24449#comments:id=2337320",
        },
    },
    [24452] = {
        {
            id = 1260515,
            score = 14,
            author = "kyio",
            text = "The heart is at 32,50.\n\nIf you're trying to get there but keep losing the stealth, there is a path you can follow through the minefield, down the middle, starting at 27,54.  at the bottom, just avoid pats and walk around the buildings to the Naga statue.",
            date = "2010-12-26T18:09:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24452#comments:id=1260515",
        },
        {
            id = 1210729,
            score = 13,
            author = "306101",
            text = "Doing this quest as a Tauren is probably the closest you'll ever get to playing a Tauren Rogue. As a bonus, they tip-toe as their stealth motion.",
            date = "2010-12-06T19:53:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24452#comments:id=1210729",
        },
        {
            id = 1182872,
