    [24478] = {
        {
            id = 1076035,
            score = 71,
            author = "533061",
            text = "This quest should be nick named the Trial of Patience. Recklessness and rushing will most likely push back any progress you've gained on your buff stack.\n\nThe goal is to run around collecting the floating frost orbs until you have a stack of 20. There are 3 very large frost spheres that shoot out a stream of frost (Frostburn) in a rotating manner. Each time Frostburn hits, you lose 1 from your stack, and it hits very quickly.\n\nYou need to run around the spheres dodging the streams, but keep in mind they turn slightly faster than you can run around them. The way around this is to keep distance, the area is sufficiently large enough to out-range the stream by running to the edges (Don't fall off).\n\nThe blue runes on the ground will be a bane to your progress, as stepping on them launches you in the air, causing you to most likely get stuck in Frostburn.\n\nLastly, underneath the 3 large spheres is a patch of ice, stepping on it will severely slow you down and can easily wipe away your whole stack once Frostburn starts hitting you.\n\nThe easiest thing to do is be patient and take open opportunities to collect a frost orb or two safely while keeping safe distance from the spheres, trying to blitz through it will inevitably cause you to get trapped and lose a major chunk of your stack. Each time you collect an orb it resets the stack duration to a minute, which is a very long duration to play it safe and collect the orbs worry free.",
            date = "2010-07-08T11:43:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24478#comments:id=1076035",
        },
        {
            id = 1204153,
            score = 55,
            author = "Strayer",
            text = "Easiest way to do this is to simply mount, and then run around the outer rim of the island.",
            date = "2010-12-03T12:51:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24478#comments:id=1204153",
        },
        {
            id = 1418022,
            score = 51,
            author = "Grimij",
            text = "You know, if you're gonna make a low-level quest hard to do, make sure the f*^&n dynamics work properly for low level toons trying to complete it. Sometimes the rune traps make you jump, sometimes they don't. Some times the burn gets you some times it doesn't. Hard to figure out a puzzle when nothing's consistent. This is the most annoying quest line I've ever tried and almost makes me want to quit playing the game for good. A big F-U to the programmer who thought these up and the supervisor who gave them the go ahead. I never thought I could get as pissed-off at a game as those people in the gameflix commercials, but this quest line has proven me wrong. I may need a new monitor and cast for my fist.",
            date = "2011-05-13T20:55:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24478#comments:id=1418022",
        },
        {
            id = 1188025,
            score = 22,
            author = "223108",
            text = "It is advised not to attempt this quest while there are more than one or two people doing the same.  Patience is all well and good, but sadly there is a time limit on how long you can stand in a safe zone and wait to grab another orb (59 seconds).  When someone else grabs an orb, you have to wait for it to respawn all over again, so if you are taking the \"Stand in a safe zone and grab the nearest ones as they spawn\" route, you will not manage it while there are other people grabbing the orbs.\n\nI'm not sure about anyone else, but I for one do NOT find this quest enjoyable in the slightest.  In my opinion, trying over and over and over and over and over and over and over again to complete a quest is not fun at all.  But then, that's just my opinion.  Many others may find this sort of thing amusing.",
            date = "2010-11-26T15:16:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24478#comments:id=1188025",
        },
        {
            id = 1179891,
            score = 19,
            author = "420211",
            text = "This is part of a quest chain in which the player aids Kalecgos (the new blue dragon aspect) in finding Azuregos and protecting him from the black dragonflight. It spans much of the land of Azshara and is composed of many quests, several of which are completely original in their concepts.\n\n1.)Azshara Blues (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14407)\n2.)Friends Come In All Colors (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14130)\n\nHelping out Ergll:\n3.)A Little Pick-me-up (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14131)\n4.)Absorbent (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14323)\n---5.)Full of Hot Water (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14324)\n6.)That's Just Rude! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14132)\n\nFinding Archmage Xylem:\n7.)The Way to a Mage's Heart (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14133)\n8.)Wash Out (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14345)\n9.)Dressed to Impress (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14340)\n\nHelping Xylem and his Apprentices:\n10.)Shear Will (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14249)\n11.)Waste of Thyme (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14263)\n12.)Renewable Resource (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14250)\n\n13.)Manual Labor (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14230)\n14.)Trouble Under Foot (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14226)\n\nGetting to Xylem's Trials\n15.)The Pinnacle of Learning (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14413)\n16.)Watch Your Step (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14296)\n\nXylem's Trials\n17.)The Trial of Fire (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14300)\n---Achievement: Glutton for Fiery Punishment (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=5448)\n18.)The Trial of Frost\n---Achievement: Glutton for Icy Punishment (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=5546)\n19.)The Trial of Shadow (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=24479)\n---Achievement: Glutton for Shadowy Punishment (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=5547)\n\nFinding Azuregos\n20.)Xylem's Asylum (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14299)\n21.)Wasn't It Obvious? (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14389)\n22.)Easy is Boring (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14390)\n23.)Turning the Tables (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14391)\n\nThe Final Battle\n24.)Fade to Black (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=24467)",
            date = "2010-11-24T01:32:51-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24478#comments:id=1179891",
        },
    },
    [24479] = {
        {
            id = 1227153,
            score = 30,
            author = "56952",
            text = "I've had a few run straight over the runes without anything happening.\n\nQuite annoying really, its not like they were just clipping them, they went straight though the middle.",
            date = "2010-12-12T09:37:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24479#comments:id=1227153",
        },
        {
            id = 1207804,
            score = 18,
            author = "fordman7795",
            text = "The way I did this was start the event and mount up.  Once the ghosts start chasing you, head to the front near where they spawn and sit there on your mount.  Let them keep spawning until you have around 20 beating on you.  Then take off on your mount in circles until they blow up.  First pack i got 14 in one portal then finished off the couple stragglers.",
            date = "2010-12-05T08:33:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24479#comments:id=1207804",
        },
        {
            id = 1177160,
            score = 14,
            author = "Jaymacibe",
            text = "Either this quest is a little buggy or something.\nI lead some of the mobs right on top of the circles and they go right in the middle and it doesn't kill them.",
            date = "2010-11-21T20:21:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24479#comments:id=1177160",
        },
        {
            id = 1130375,
            score = 12,
            author = "344141",
            text = "The 'circle shadow' generates from under your character feet and it shoots out to the portal, so the closer you are to the portal the faster the shades will come.\n\nThe best to do this is to stay by the starting crystal as it gives you the longest distance from the portals and allow you more time to position yourself\n\ncheck out my video below for the example.\n\nThe Trial by Shadow Video (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N9FmFcMWDHo&hd=1)\n\nThe Trial by Fire Video (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N9FmFcMWDHo&hd=1)\n\nThe Trial by Frost Video (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RTz0adLgUjQ&hd=1)",
            date = "2010-09-28T21:41:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24479#comments:id=1130375",
        },
        {
