    [24564] = {
        {
            id = 956183,
            score = 46,
            author = "gatygun",
            text = "k this can be confusing:\n\nthis is what you need to do.\n\nDo not make a raid to enter sunwell, if you do that the quest wont compleet. What you need to do is talk to a guard infront of the entrance he will port you inside.\n\nonce inside, walk down the long stairs past some big robot npc and turn left to the middle. You are standing now infront of some big red light..\n\nUse your quest item there, and you are done.",
            date = "2010-01-25T04:54:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24564#comments:id=956183",
        },
        {
            id = 911076,
            score = 38,
            author = "45234",
            text = "Here's the entire quest chain, with simple descriptions and quest links for the Horde versions.\n\nThe Battered Hilt (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24554)\nBring the Battered Hilt to Myralion Sunblaze at Quel'Delar's rest, south of the Argent Tournament Grounds.\n\n2. What The Dragons Know (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24555)\nSpeak to Krasus at the top of Wyrmrest Temple.\n\n3. The Silver Covenant Scheme (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24557) (Alliance version is called \"The Sunreavers' Plan)\nObtain the Orders by killing an NPC in the Dalaran Sewers.  Make sure you kill the right one.\n\n4. A Suitable Disguise (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24556)\nObtain a Borrowed Tabard from Shandy Glossgleam; He is upstairs in the Threads of Fate: if you are standing in front of the stairs with the Violet Citadel to your back, it is to the right (to the left is the toy store).\n\n5. An Audience With The Arcanist (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24451)\nRetrieve the Ancient Dragonforged Blades tome from Arcanist Tybalin. Use the disguise and go in the Alliance section of Dalaran.\n\n6. Return To Myralion Sunblaze (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24558)\nBring the Ancient Dragonforged Blades to Myralion Sunblaze at Quel'Delar's Rest.\n\n7. Reforging The Sword (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24559)\nObtain 5 Infused Saronite Bars and the Forgemaster's Hammer and use them to make the Reforged Quel'Delar. (AKA: Run the Pit of Saron.  The infused bars are near the entrance; don't forget you have to kill the boss, too.)(It appears this can be done on Normal Difficulty.)\n\n8. Tempering The Blade (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24560)\nTemper the Reforged Quel'Delar in the Crucible of Souls. (AKA: kill the final boss of Forge of Souls; use the quest item nearby.)(It appears this can be done on Normal Difficulty.)\n\n9. The Halls Of Reflection (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24561)\nBring your Tempered Quel'Delar to Sword's Rest inside the Halls of Reflection.  (AKA, obviously, run Halls of Reflection.)(It appears this can be done on Normal Difficulty.)\n\n10. Journey To The Sunwell (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24562)\nSpeak with Halduron Brightwing at the entrance to the Sunwell Plateau on the Isle of Quel'Danas.\n\n11. Thalorien Dawnseeker (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24563)\nVisit Thalorien Dawnseeker's Remains and obtain his blessing to wield Quel'Delar.  (Go around behind SWP to the Dead Scar (southern end of Isle of QD zone, not in the SWP raid instance) and kill a bunch of mobs.)\n\n12. The Purification of Quel'Delar  (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24564)\nImmerse your Tempered Quel'Delar in the Sunwell. Speak to a Warden of the Sunwell when you are ready to enter the Sunwell Plateau. (Possibly different versions of this for sword/mace?)\n\n13. A Victory For The [Sunreavers/Silver Covenant] - (sword (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24801) or  mace (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=24798))\nBring the Restored Quel'Delar to the NPC at the Violet Citadel in Dalaran.\n\nA lot of this info came from comments people left on the various quest pages. Thanks to all those who posted useful tips!",
            date = "2009-12-09T15:39:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24564#comments:id=911076",
        },
        {
            id = 936503,
            score = 17,
            author = "294523",
            text = "If it doesnt complete, abandon qeust and retake from the guy near entrance Sunwell.\n\nStand near the natural NPC and \"use\" the Quel qeust item (inside and near Sunwell)\n\nIt will trown it in and the event starts again, wait till its over and then u have to \"use\" the Quel'Delar u see sticking in the Sunwell.\n\nDone, go to Aethas to have a little chat about it <3",
            date = "2010-01-03T14:23:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24564#comments:id=936503",
        },
        {
            id = 1085146,
            score = 15,
            author = "topmen",
            text = "Dialogue :\n\nSunwell Honor Guard says: Can that really be Quel'Delar?\nLor'themar Theron says: We shall see.\nGrand Magister Rommath says: Look at it, Lor'themar. It is certainly Quel'Delar.\nLor'themar Theron says: It is indeed Quel'Delar. I had not thought I'd live to see the day when Thalorien Dawnseeker's legendary sword would be restored to us.\nLor'themar Theron says: You are a hero and an inspiration to the sin'dorei, *name*, a symbol of our endurance in the face of tragedy and treachery.\nGrand Magister Rommath says: The regent speaks truly, *name*. Thalorien's sacrifice could not prevent the fall of this very Sunwell.\nGrand Magister Rommath says: When you found the sword, it was broken and abandoned, much like Silvermoon after Kael'thas's betrayal.\nGrand Magister Rommath says: Let Quel'Delar be a sign that we will never give up, that we will face any enemy without fear.\nCaptain Auric Sunchaser says: Quel'Delar is not held in high esteem by the sin'dorei alone. It holds a place in the heart of all children of Silvermoon.\nCaptain Auric Sunchaser says: This blade has been returned to us for a reason, my lords. Now is the time to rally behind the bearer of Quel'Delar and avenge the destruction of Silvermoon and the Sunwell.\nGrand Magister Rommath says: Reclaim the sword,*name*, and bear it through that portal to Dalaran. Archmage Aethas Sunreaver will be waiting to congratulate you.",
            date = "2010-07-20T12:28:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24564#comments:id=1085146",
        },
        {
            id = 2152913,
            score = 11,
            author = "Lostelf",
            text = "For non-blood elves Lor'themar will die upon reaching for the sword, whereas before he was simply knocked back and lost a large chunk of health. It seems the damage the sword deals didn't get nerfed along with everything else in the game (Lor'themar's health did however get nerfed a lot).",
            date = "2015-04-03T21:06:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24564#comments:id=2152913",
        },
    },
