    [24572] = {
        {
            id = 1309137,
            score = 31,
            author = "669102",
            text = "While doing this quest, I couldn't help myself....\n\nI killed every single Taurajo Looter.\n\nEvery.\nSingle.\nOne.\nOf.\nThem.\n\nThe music played in this area was perfect...\n\nGreat quest.",
            date = "2011-01-25T07:49:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24572#comments:id=1309137",
        },
        {
            id = 1185021,
            score = 20,
            author = "665594",
            text = "You might have noticed while doing this quest, that there's still is a working tauren-themed mailbox in the middle of the destroyed Camp Taurajo. I bet the postman isn't too excited to deliver the mail now that the place is crawling with hostile Taurajo looters.",
            date = "2010-11-25T14:01:10-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24572#comments:id=1185021",
        },
        {
            id = 1382673,
            score = 20,
            author = "810976",
            text = "When I got to town, the looter in the middle called out \"Have we cleaned out the inn yet? Burn the rest of it when you're done.\"\n\nHe never spoke again because I shoved a blade in his belly.  The rest got the same.\n\nCongratulations, Blizzard.  This is the first quest I've ever done where I didn't stop when I hit the objective.  Because my objective was \"Every filthy looter in this town must die.\"",
            date = "2011-04-02T20:15:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24572#comments:id=1382673",
        },
        {
            id = 1412502,
            score = 18,
            author = "512576",
            text = "I kill them all. Whenever I fly over this place, I kill them all. On my death knight, I no longer raise just any old dead for my ghoul pet. I specifically go to Taurajo and raise these miserable maggots into the unending torment of unlife so that they might serve the Horde.",
            date = "2011-05-07T20:24:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24572#comments:id=1412502",
        },
        {
            id = 1204221,
            score = 8,
            author = "366821",
            text = "funny an orc calling the alliance a renegade band of butchers.\nEspecially when there are gems of Horde quests such as Parts-is-Parts (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=24619) -- in the same zone, no less.",
            date = "2010-12-03T13:23:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24572#comments:id=1204221",
        },
    },
    [24573] = {
        {
            id = 1422501,
            score = 73,
            author = "Rankkor",
            text = "@Marathan on southshore just about everyone escaped, considering how fenris island is FULL of survivors, to the point that on this (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27232) quest and this (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27097) quest shows just how many of them left, wich is pretty much the whole damn town.\n\non Silverpine, there were no children, or inocents. That was a war front. The alliance invaded horde lands, and the horde repelled them, simple as that. Mess with the bull and you get the horns.\n\nthere were no \"inocents or childrens\" of the alliance on gilneas simply because at the moment of the horde invasion, Gilneas was NOT a part of the alliance. I should remind you that their jerkass leader said this gem of a quote to Terenas shorly after the second war was over:\n\n[quote Genn Greymane]Damn the orcs, damn the Alliance, and damn you! The last thing Gilneas needs is sponges from other nations drawing from our resources, Dalaran wizards meddling with our affairs, and someone else's enemies killing our soldiers! Gilneas is its own nation and it always will be. This is the last time I'll ever talk to you, Terenas, so I hope you were listening (Taken from Genn's article on wowpedia)\n\nso this was simply the horde attacking a nation with a considerable military presence, and a rather dangerous enemy of the forsaken (worgens have been a threat to the forsakens for the past 6 years) rather than them attacking a nation of the alliance. The gilneans rejoined the aliance AFTER this invasion.\n\non New Andorhal there were no children either. The alliance and horde were trying to conquer the zone and they had only military presence there to push the other away. This was simple combat, where soldier fought soldier, that's war and in war there are casualties. Its not the same as attacking a civilian town full of non-combatants.\n\non ashenvale theres silverwing refuge, wich was the main base of operation of the sentinels, again another military target, as oposed to a civilian outpost.\n\non the broken front, indeed that was very dishonorable ( I hate that quest) but again those were soldiers, not civilians, and the commanding officer (Sky-reaver Krom) was chewed out by Garrosh and the Warchief, as well as demoted of his command after the northrend campaign.\n\nStonetalon was also dishonorable but the druids in the grove were neutral (there were tauren druids as well as night elven ones) and even then, the guy responsible was harsly punished (with his life)\n\nwich leads us back to: Taurajo\n\nA civilian town, with children, and lots of non-combatants. Primarily a hunter's camp, full of (duh) hunters that brought food and natural resourses to the rest of the tauren tribes. Attacked cowardly at night, with siege tanks, drunk wildhammer griphon riders (Don't question me on the \"Drunk\" part, this quest (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27752) shows that wildhammers love to fight dead-drunk) and ex-convicts, during the night, while the hunters were out, and the only people in the town were civilians who coudn't fight back.\n\nking's honor my ass.",
            date = "2011-05-19T11:15:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24573#comments:id=1422501",
        },
        {
            id = 1178904,
            score = 68,
            author = "506816",
            text = "After leveling more toons than I can count through the Barrens, this quest actually got me a bit teary eyed, especially Omusa's comments.",
            date = "2010-11-23T18:48:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24573#comments:id=1178904",
        },
        {
            id = 1194012,
            score = 63,
            author = "255458",
            text = "This is probably the most emotional quest I've done as a player of many Tauren characters. When you use the funeral totem, each spirit relives its last few moments when it was alive. Having played through the barrens roughly six times, I remember all these NPCs.\n\nOmusa (the old Flight Master)\nOmusa's Spirit says: No, stay with the others. Escort them north, away from the fighting. I will stay here with the wyverns and cover your escape. Go!\nOmusa's Spirit says: ...wait, it is over? I've been run through... Ah. Of course. I understand now. I am expected elsewhere.\n\nYonada (Tailoring Supplier)\nYonada's Spirit says: Alliance - they've surrounded the camp! What are they doing here? Why are they attacking Taurajo? Get the children - run! RUN!\n\nDranh (Leatherworking Trainer)\nDranh's Spirit says: I can feel the embrace now of all living things, the Earthmother's eternal peace. Thank you.\n\nKrulmoo (Skinning Trainer)\nKrulmoo's Spirit says: I ran to wake up the others when the attack hit. Were they able to escape? I tried to fight off the soldiers with a skinning knife...\n\nI've deleted my Alliance characters since.",
            date = "2010-11-28T17:10:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24573#comments:id=1194012",
        },
        {
            id = 1188849,
            score = 53,
            author = "315138",
            text = "This has got to be the saddest quest I've done on the Horde.\n\nAs many times as I've caught a wind rider flight from Omusa Thunderhorn - it was very sobering to find him dead and deliver his last respects.  Downright inspirational to learn he stayed behind to cover the retreat.\n\nLok'Tar A'gar!  I will avenge you!\n\nI think my new PVP battlecry will be \"Remember Camp Taurajo!\"",
            date = "2010-11-26T20:59:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24573#comments:id=1188849",
        },
        {
            id = 1201524,
            score = 49,
            author = "141924",
            text = "God this quest was sad. Reading about the self-sacrifice in everyone's last words before they finally depart into the spirit world... very, very sad. Really nice quest done up by Blizzard. Don't miss it. (Chances are if you're reading this though, you haven't missed it.)",
            date = "2010-12-02T02:55:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24573#comments:id=1201524",
        },
    },
    [24574] = {
        {
