    [24594] = {
        {
            id = 928741,
            score = 28,
            author = "barbeque",
            text = "You do not need to be in a raid to do this portion of the quest. Once you have accepted the quest, talk to any of the NPCs around the quest giver to be teleported into the Sunwell Plateau raid instance. When you are inside, you should see the Sunwell, down at the bottom of the spiral slope (you really can't miss it). Just go down, and click your tainted blade next to the Sunwell. It will kind of suspend there in mid-air.\n\nAt this point, the two NPCs will start a dialogue, and at the end of the dialogue, you can click on your suspended sword to pick it up again. There's actually a port to Dalaran available at the side of the circular area, so don't bother hearthing. You do, however, need to fly back to the Argent Tournament area to turn in the quest before coming back to Dalaran again, though.\n\nThe phasing of this portion of the quest is very interesting, as most of the isle has been taken back. Except the naga along the coast line, who were left to torment the murlocs there.",
            date = "2009-12-26T00:17:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24594#comments:id=928741",
        },
        {
            id = 911002,
            score = 20,
            author = "159117",
            text = "Note that this quest comes from the end of a long chain asking you to go everywhere and do everything. Always.\nIt starts with a Battered Hilt, which is a drop off of mobs in either of the Icecrown Citadel 5-man instances.\n\nEDIT: added a link Battered Hilt (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=50380)",
            date = "2009-12-09T14:45:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24594#comments:id=911002",
        },
        {
            id = 954149,
            score = 12,
            author = "Bengesko",
            text = "This seems to have different scenarios for different races. I just completed this on my blood elf hunter who was welcomed to the Sunwell and cheered as he purified the blade, and hailed as the one who would avenge the fallen of Quel'thalas.\n\nGuildie of mine just finished it on her troll hunter and as soon as she got close to the Sunwell she was frozen in place and Loth'remar tried to claim the blade from her, but was unable to as the blade chose her.\n\nInteresting differentiation of events.",
            date = "2010-01-22T17:23:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24594#comments:id=954149",
        },
        {
            id = 2100053,
            score = 6,
            author = "1440372",
            text = "This is the blood elf version of the quest, which has a different scene play out than that of the other races. Here is the dialogue:\n\nSunwell Honor Guard says: Can that really be Quel'Delar?\nLor'themar Theron says: We shall see.\nGrand Magister Rommath says: Look at it Lor'themar. It is certainly Quel'Delar.\nLor'themar Theron says: It is indeed Quel'Delar. I had not thought I'd live to see the day when Thalorien Dawnseeker's legendary sword would be restored to us.\nLor'themar Theron says: You are a hero and an inspiration to the sin'dorei, , a symbol of our endurance in the face of tragedy and treachery.\nGrand Magister Rommath says: The regent speaks truly, . Thalorien's sacrifice could not prevent the fall of this very Sunwell.\nGrand Magister Rommath says: When you found the sword, it was broken and abandoned, much like Silvermoon after Kael'thas's betrayal.\nGrand Magister Rommath says: Let Quel'Delar be a sign that we will never give up, that we will face any enemy without fear.\nCaptain Auric Sunchaser says: Quel'Delar is not held in high esteem by the sin'dorei alone. It holds a place in the heart of all children of Silvermoon.\nCaptain Auric Sunchaser says: The blade has been returned to us for a reason, my lords. Now is the time to rally behind the bearer of Quel'Delar and avenge the destruction of Silvermoon and the Sunwell.\nGrand Magister Rommath says: Reclaim the sword, , and bear it through that portal to Dalaran. Archmage Aethas Sunreaver will be waiting to congratulate you.\n\nOther races will see a different version of this dialogue, which can be found in lovelywaz's comment here: [quest=24553 domain=www]#comments\n\nAlso, Rommath is a dirty dirty liar. You take the portal back to Dalaran but then have to go to the Argent Tourney grounds to turn the quest in to Myralion Sunblaze, after which you go BACK to Dalaran, and only then do you meet Aethas Sunreaver and get your congratulations and your awesome sword. :)",
            date = "2015-02-06T00:21:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24594#comments:id=2100053",
        },
        {
            id = 924097,
            score = 3,
            author = "Sygmoral",
            text = "You don't need to have ever been to the Sunwell Plateau raid.\n\nYou will end up in a 'phased' version of the instance, and will only be able to walk around in a limited region of it: the hallway running up to the actual Sunwell, which is now* a place of pilgrimage for Blood Elfs. You won't need to fight anything.\n\n*: only for the people being at this specific part of this quest chain...",
            date = "2009-12-20T18:34:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24594#comments:id=924097",
        },
    },
    [24595] = {
        {
            id = 968069,
            score = 30,
            author = "281567",
            text = "If you take too long to pick up the Resored Quel'Delar (when the little \"event\" has taken place and you can once again move) you don't have to panic (as I did and rushed for the GM ticket). What you do is very simple. Go back out to Halduron Brightwing, abandon the quest, and re-take it. You'll get to see the little chat again in Sunwell, and then you've learnt from your previous misstake and pick the restored sword up before it disappears again.\n\n.../Seasha\nLevel 80 Shaman - Argent Dawn (EU)",
            date = "2010-02-06T21:01:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24595#comments:id=968069",
        },
        {
            id = 911729,
            score = 22,
            author = "437058",
            text = "At this point you will want to talk to one of the guards outside of Sunwell called Warden of the Sunwell.  DO NOT just go into Sunwell.  Talking to the guard transports you into a solo version of Sunwell Plateau with all green NPC's.  They will not attack you and you won't need to get a raid together in order to complete this.  After a brief encounter (no combat involved) with the NPC's around the sunwell you will get your Restored Quel'Delar and your mace will be practically in hand.  Enjoy!",
            date = "2009-12-10T01:06:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24595#comments:id=911729",
        },
        {
            id = 932782,
            score = 10,
            author = "220068",
            text = "wel this is the encounter you wil sie\n\nRandomly, Liadrin makes a statement to some gathered Pilgrims:\n\nLady Liadrin says: My brothers and sisters, words cannot describe what I felt upon seeing the Sunwell rekindled.\nLady Liadrin says: In that moment, the Light revealed to me the truth of the terrible things I had done.\nLady Liadrin says: Our people had walked a dark path and miine was among the darkest of them all.\nLady Liadrin says: But the Light showed me that I was not lost. It helped me to find the strength to survive in spite of all that had happened and all the evil I had wrought.\nLady Liadrin says: It is a strength that we sin'dorei all share. It is a strength we will need to free ourselves of the addiction ravaging our people.\nLady Liadrin says: It will be the most difficult battle we have ever faced, but our resolve and the power of the Sunwell will sustain us until we have been restored to our greatness.\nBlood Elf Pilgrim says: Well said, my lady. We sin'dorei will be free and we shall be great again!\nUpon throwing in the sword on the southeast side of the Sunwell:\n\nSunwell Honor Guard says: Can that really be Quel'Delar?\n\nLor'themar Theron says: We shall see.\n\nGrand Magister Rommath says: Look at it, Lor'themar. It is certainly Quel'Delar.\n\nLor'themar Theron says: So it is. You have my thanks, , for restoring\nQuel'Delar to its rightful owners.\n\nTheron walks up to the blade and grabs it. He is thrown across the room by the blade, knocking him to roughly half-health.\n\nSunwell Honor Guard yells: My Lord Regent! What have they done to you?\n\nRommath freezes the player in an Icy Prison and guards approach from all directions.\n\nGrand Magister Rommath says: What is the meaning of this treachery?\n\nSunwell Honor Guard says: Drop your weapon and surrender, traitor.\n\nCaptain Auric Sunchaser says: This is not my doing, Rommath. There is no treachery here.\n\nCaptain Auric Sunchaser says: Call off your men. Lor'themar's own foolishness caused his injuries. Quel'Delar is not chosen; it chooses its master.\n\nGrand Magister Rommath says: It seems the captain is correct. Quel'Delar is not to be ours after all.\n\nGrand Magister Rommath says: Guards, return to your posts.\n\nThe Icy Prison fades\n\nGrand Magister Rommath says: You will have what you have come for, . Take the sword and begone. And you, Auric, have a care for what you say in this sacred place.\n\nCaptain Auric Sunchaser says: Carry the sword back to Dalaran through that portal, . You have done what many quel'dorei have dreamt of for years. Quel'Delar has been restored at last.\n\ntaken from wowwiki (http://www.wowwiki.com/Quest:The_Purification_of_Quel%27Delar_(Alliance))",
            date = "2009-12-30T15:46:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24595#comments:id=932782",
        },
        {
            id = 932099,
            score = 2,
            author = "Elknot",
            text = "I talk to the npc, and it gives me the \"Additional instances cannot be launched, please try again later\" message...\nanyone else having this problem? I've been trying for over 1 hour now, still no luck......",
            date = "2009-12-29T21:42:06-06:00",
