        },
        {
            id = 1079547,
            score = 2,
            author = "Lindentree",
            text = "Unfortunatly swords have always been iconic as noble weapons and many stories that are used as the basis for WoW's ideas for legendary weapons involve swords. True enhance shammies have gotten the nerf bat when it comes to legendaries, since there havent been any 1h dps legendaries that havent been swords\n\nDuring most of vanilla, enh shaman used 2-handed maces, so Sulfuras was an enh weapon :). They got a pretty equal shot at getting it, too, as there was at the time no class which could wield 2-handed maces and was also primarily melee DPS in raids. (Warriors were tanks; druids, paladins, and shaman were healers; death knights didn't exist yet).\n\nThe people who have really been left out of the Legendary loop are the offensive spellcaster trees of healing classes, i.e. boomkin, ele shaman, and spriests. These specs have never had a legendary weapon. (When it was relevant, the priest Atiesh only buffed healing power, since this was before the spell power merge). Technically frost DKs are out of the loop as well, as Thunderfury was before their time. You could also make a case for prot paladins, as unlike Sulfuras Thunderfury was usable by warriors and rogues for their main roles in raiding.\n\nBlood DK: Shadowmourne\nFrost DK: none\nUnh DK: Shadowmourne\nBoomkin: none\nFeral druid: Sulfuras\nResto druid: Atiesh, Val'anyr\nHunter: Thori'dal\nMage: Atiesh\nHoly paladin: Val'anyr\nRet paladin: Sulfuras\nProt paladin: none\nShadow priest: none\nDisc/Holy priest: Atiesh, Val'anyr\nRogue: Thunderfury, Warglaives of Azzinoth\nEle shaman: none\nEnh shaman: Sulfuras\nResto shaman: Val'anyr\nWarlocks: Atiesh\nArms warriors: Sulfuras, Shadowmourne\nFury warriors: Warglaives of Azzinoth, Shadowmourne\nProt warriors: Thunderfury\n\nAll that said, I have no idea why you're bringing up legendaries, as Quel'delar is definitely not one.\n\nWhen you get to choose your reward it will determine what you want to use it as: 1H DPS, 2H DPS, caster dps, tanking, or healing.\n\nThis is unfortunately not true: there is no Quel'delar for warrior or paladin tanking.\n\nThis is most likely a lore nod to the fact that Quel'delar is Quel'serrar's sister blade. Quel'serrar is a one-handed tanking sword; so Quel'delar complements it by doing everything else.",
            date = "2010-07-13T09:44:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24598#comments:id=1079547",
        },
        {
            id = 1087649,
            score = 1,
            author = "632979",
            text = "where is the quest dude at i can never find him even with the help of this website",
            date = "2010-07-23T21:43:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24598#comments:id=1087649",
        },
    },
