    [24707] = {
        {
            id = 1497981,
            score = 205,
            author = "Wimbleton",
            text = "It ought to have an \"often bugged\" disclaimer. Never knew about the armor and there obviously was no #3 button. Absolutely baffled after 15 minutes of trotting around, being chased by the mother of all devilsaurs and in the process also aggroing 275 dimetradons, a dozen oozes, 700 Macedonian warriors, the entire population of Broken Bow, Oklahoma and the London Philharmonic. What they were all doing in the Crater was a mystery to me.\n\nAfter realizing that all this rock throwing was only annoying the big girl, I hopped off. Naturally Wonder Boy disappeared and I had to face off against Gekko Girl, who is a 55 Elite. Luckily my 57 Holy Priest could self-heal and had a pretty good mana pool because the biggest problem was not so much Big Green as it was the other oozes, dimetradons, spirit creatures and what I can only assume was the Second Bassoonist, all of which together kept one-shotting my shield. I got lucky and whacked the dino with my wand just as I went OOM. How annoying to be killed by trash mobs, I thought but at that moment they all disappeared. Nobody was more surprised than me.\n\nSo luck plays a role, as it always does. But be prepared to be buggered, or bugged, or both.",
            date = "2011-08-18T16:53:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24707#comments:id=1497981",
        },
        {
            id = 1089190,
            score = 58,
            author = "327155",
            text = "Best quest chain ever.",
            date = "2010-07-25T23:22:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24707#comments:id=1089190",
        },
        {
            id = 1193786,
            score = 54,
            author = "Calidus",
            text = "Hillarious quest line! Here's the transcript of the final fight:\n\nMaximillian of Northshire says: I see the dragon up ahead.  She is larger than I had first anticipated.\nMaximillian of Northshire yells: Dragon!  Hear me out!  I am Maximillian of Northshire, and I have come to deliver you.  Your blood shall fill...\nMaximillian of Northshire yells: Great Uther's ghost, it's chasing after us!  Squire, do something!  Throw rocks at it!  I have no plan!\nMaximillian of Northshire whispers: Wait, I have an idea!  Here, throw my Light-blessed shield at the beast!\nMaximillian has handed you his shield.  Throw it at the Devilsaur!  Er... dragon!\nMaximillian of Northshire whispers: That shield-toss worked remarkably well.  Quickly, hurl my holy shoulder-plate!\nMaximillian of Northshire whispers: I have managed to remove my gloves.  You may lob them at our foe.\nMaximillian of Northshire whispers: The ironclad heel of my armored boot should prove to be quite destructive.\nMaximillian of Northshire whispers: Eat my other shoulder-plate, vile lizard!\nMaximillian of Northshire whispers: If you can heft my breastplate, then throw it!  Throw it for Doloria!\nMaximillian of Northshire whispers: This is quickly becoming humiliating... and drafty.  Hopefully my legplates shall deal the deathblow.\n\nMaximillian will also heal you up as you get low on life:\nMaximillian of Northshire says: Your health is faltering.  Allow me to help.",
            date = "2010-11-28T15:41:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24707#comments:id=1193786",
        },
        {
            id = 1094961,
            score = 49,
            author = "Vlad",
            text = "One could argue if this or the \"punch Deathwing in the face (http://cata.wowhead.com/search?q=the+day+that+deathwing+came)\" is more funny, I myself prefer Maximilian!\n\nGreat Uther's ghost, it's chasing after us!  Squire, do something!  Throw rocks at it!  I have no plan!\n\n(Want to do this epic quest chain and slay the Queen? This is the location of Max (http://cata.wowhead.com/maps?data=490:310510). I've uploaded a video of this quest on Youtube (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8JxxLvDGh7g&fmt=37).)",
            date = "2010-08-03T14:54:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24707#comments:id=1094961",
        },
        {
            id = 1197583,
            score = 38,
            author = "473253",
            text = "After killing the Queen and reading the posts here, I reckoned I'd make a neat list of the most important tips for this fight:\n\n- make sure you have bagspace before you start, like 2-3 slots, because you'll need it for the rocks (gathered by stomping [button 1], stack in lots of 200) and the pieces of Max's armour\n\n- when you accept the quest and find yourself mounting up for the auto-ride to the Queen's lair, stomp a few times on the way there. This will give you a couple of rocks from the start, which will speed up the kill\n\n- once the fight commences, spam 'throw rock' [button 2] until you either run out or the Queen comes too close\n\n- stomp on every cd, both to gather more rocks and to keep the Queen at bay\n\n- at some point during the fight, Max will start stripping off his armour and handing it to you so you have extra 'weapons' [button 3]. Make sure you throw these as soon as they become available, for they do quite some damage\n\n- when the Queen has died, you won't automatically dismount at the campsite. Use the 'leave vehicle' arrow to dismount and head back to the campsite",
            date = "2010-11-30T10:27:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=24707#comments:id=1197583",
        },
    },
    [24708] = {
        {
            id = 1181051,
            score = 36,
            author = "166836",
            text = "Click the item you get, it will turn you in the direction you need to go for a fossil. Additionally it tells you in the chat pane how close you are \"You are very close\". At some point it startet turning me always around when I used the item and after about 3 times turning on the spot it said \"you should dig here\" and a big bone appeared wich was lootable. The Fossil-Finder thing works when mounted.",
