        {
            id = 1642024,
            score = 13,
            author = "scharky",
            text = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=56885  A great reference to the Ides of March, and Caesar's death by stabbing on that day  o.0",
            date = "2012-03-20T23:06:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25065#comments:id=1642024",
        },
        {
            id = 1277606,
            score = 5,
            author = "spriint",
            text = "meatface is at 53;89",
            date = "2011-01-04T19:22:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25065#comments:id=1277606",
        },
        {
            id = 3300163,
            score = 1,
            author = "Saakaf36",
            text = "So... these items are -still- available, but, often (and if you're playing a spec that it isn't their main weapon) they will not show up as a reward, or actually -give- you the item as a reward.\n\nThis is also part of a moderate quest chain that starts from the gnome apprentice up in Gadgetzan, who sends you out to kill sea giants and collect equipment boxes.\n\nAfter killing pirates and saving surviving goblins via a blimp, you are sent to find Kelsey Steelspark at her -first- encampment, making war on other pirates.\n\nAfter completing her quest-chains, you are sent to bootlegger post.\n\nAfter completing -these- quest chains, you are sent to Kelsey once again at lands end to begin the quest-line.\n\nNOTE: Let it be known that you apparently have to be able to USE said items for them to be added to your roster. IE: If you do the quest chain on a hunter, the 2h mace will NOT be added to your appearance log.",
            date = "2021-02-12T00:16:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25065#comments:id=3300163",
        },
    },
    [25067] = {
        {
            id = 1291950,
            score = 50,
            author = "754947",
            text = "... This is laughable... My searing totem killed the Ginormus and the promoter said: ''Dr. Dealwell yells: The Ginormus has fallen! Searing totem looks like she's ready for more!'' I did not know that wooden sticks had sexes. =O",
            date = "2011-01-13T10:45:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25067#comments:id=1291950",
        },
        {
            id = 1270721,
            score = 24,
            author = "163282",
            text = "Forget the 3-man tag.  All of these \"bosses\" are wimps that hit maybe about as hard as two normal mobs.  All were easy solos as a 47 enhance shaman in quest gear...didn't even need to heal myself.  Easy xp and a free blue.  Have fun.",
            date = "2011-01-01T03:36:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25067#comments:id=1270721",
        },
        {
            id = 3224328,
            score = 20,
            author = "Heathmonn",
            text = "For anyone getting the message \"You don't meet the requirements for that quest\" when trying to pick this quest up it is likely because you have War Mode disabled. Go turn War Mode on and you should now be able to pick up and complete these quests. I do not know the full extent of this bug but it is definitely not intended and turning on War Mode definitely works as of my writing of this (Confirmed on my 120 Warrior). This bug is probably caused by the fact that the dome itself used to flag you for PvP automatically and no longer does so when War Mode is turned off.\n\nStill doesn't explain why the questgiver sends you to the Amphitheater of Anguish though... I mean, it isn't even the same NPC in Northrend that gives the quest... Anyway...\n\nTL;DR Turn on War Mode if you are having difficulty picking up this quest!\n\n- - -\n\nEdit: As a result of my experimenting, I did complete The Amphitheater of Anguish: Yggdras! (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12932/the-amphitheater-of-anguish-yggdras) and had The Amphitheater of Anguish: Magnataur! (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=12933/the-amphitheater-of-anguish-magnataur) in my log when I finally completed the quests by turning War Mode on. Though I am still confident having War Mode on is all you need to do to fix this bug.",
            date = "2020-08-20T00:29:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25067#comments:id=3224328",
        },
        {
            id = 1270819,
            score = 16,
            author = "99400",
            text = "This fellow is a nod to Mad Max 2's The Humungus. looks exactly the same. The Thunderdrome is also a reference to a Gladiatorial arena in the same movie franchise, which if i can recall, is in the 3rd movie.",
            date = "2011-01-01T05:47:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25067#comments:id=1270819",
        },
        {
            id = 1609742,
            score = 10,
            author = "624617",
            text = "If you're having trouble seeing this quest to start the chain:\n\nThere's a lead-in quest given by Flinn (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=38578) at Gustan's Dig, the southern-most flight point in Tanaris. See if it's available to you.\n\nTry completing Kelsey Steelspark (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=38535)'s quest chain, (ending with You Too, Brute? (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25065)). She is involved in the last Thunderdrome quest, and I'm guessing being part way through her chain may interfere with picking up the first Thunderdrome quest. (The last one can't be picked up at all until You Too, Brute? is complete.)\n\nIf you still can't see it, someone else's recent Thunderdrome attemps may have messed it up; try checking in later or after a server reset.\n\nEdit: And for those of the Horde persuasion: Sherm (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=44374) for the lead-in, Megs Dreadshredder (www.wowhead.com/npc=38534)'s quest chain, ending with Sandscraper (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25001).",
            date = "2012-01-10T12:59:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25067#comments:id=1609742",
        },
    },
    [25068] = {
        {
            id = 1189109,
            score = 6,
            author = "117905",
            text = "You can complete this quest pre-cata if you don't stray too far into Uldum. As long as you don't leave the hallway leading into the large room you should be able to kill enough of these guys to finish the quest.",
            date = "2010-11-26T23:32:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25068#comments:id=1189109",
        },
        {
            id = 1334329,
            score = 4,
            author = "785664",
            text = "The enterance to the Uldum is 37.75,80.62. Watch out for the giant Guardian that comes out after you turn in the quest at the chest.",
            date = "2011-02-13T07:17:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25068#comments:id=1334329",
        },
        {
            id = 2456793,
            score = 3,
            author = "ghostwolf82",
            text = "Enter the Ruins of Uldum (37.7/78.9) and kill the white mobs (Sandstone Earthen) kneeling along the edges of the entrance path (along the walls). They will drop the Earthen Jewel needed to complete this quest. You will sometimes have the ability to loot the mobs, but get the message that there is no loot. Found this to be quite odd, as if there is no loot, then the loot mouseover shouldn't even appear.",
            date = "2016-12-26T13:21:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25068#comments:id=2456793",
        },
    },
    [25069] = {
        {
            id = 3190770,
            score = 105,
            author = "jowo",
            text = "if anyone is having an issue getting to the chest in patch 8.3 make sure u go to uldum and talk to zidormi to set uldum to past version\ncheers",
            date = "2020-02-17T07:15:23-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25069#comments:id=3190770",
        },
        {
            id = 1264739,
            score = 6,
            author = "263353",
            text = "If you are using a leveling guide like wow-pro, which I'm using, the tomtom takes you into Uldum...this is a no no.  Uldum is level 84.  To get to the quest, make sure your back is toward Andoren Dawnwise.  Get on your mount and bear right.  Head towards the building on your map that looks like two pillars...you will need to get past some Sandstone Golems.  Then you get to the entrance...\n\nA couple of things...there's a quest called the Crumbling Past.  Get this quest before you go there.  Otherwise, you end up going back and forth.\n\nThe quest is inside the building.  Keep going until you see a table.  Pick up quest to complete.  There is a follow on quest immediately thereafter.  Pick up quest.  The Antechamber Guardian will appear immediately.  Kill guardian and complete quest.  Return to Andoren Dawnwise to turn in quests.\n\nHope this helps...",
            date = "2010-12-28T19:49:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25069#comments:id=1264739",
        },
        {
            id = 1178793,
            score = 5,
