    [25152] = {
        {
            id = 1398656,
            score = 18,
            author = "819875",
            text = "The beginning of a promising Orc's adventure.",
            date = "2011-04-24T16:30:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25152#comments:id=1398656",
        },
        {
            id = 1842511,
            score = 7,
            author = "Gadoink4",
            text = "Sadly we never do get to find that great dragon or demon and strangle it with our bare hands :(",
            date = "2013-04-13T05:59:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25152#comments:id=1842511",
        },
        {
            id = 3291985,
            score = -5,
            author = "2201631",
            text = "Here is the full storyline quest text, played as a Nightborne Mage.\n\nStoryline Overview:>https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25152\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=25126\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=25172\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=25127\n\nLocation: [zone=6451]\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=10176:Finally, you are of age, ... of age to battle in the name of the Horde. To conquer for the glory of the Warchief.\n\nYes...\n\nYou will do nicely.\n\nNo doubt you wish to find a great dragon or demon and strangle it with your bare hands, but perhaps it would be wise to start on something less... dangerous.\n\nReport to Gornek, he should be able to assign a task better suited to a young . You will find him seated at the fire behind me.\n\n[Speak with https://www.wowhead.com/npc=3143.]\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=3143:Another one of Kaltunk's recruits, hm?\n\nA sorry state of affairs we find ourselves in if this is the best the Horde can produce. No matter. By the time we think you're ready to leave the Valley, you'll be a proud warrior of the Horde.\n\nThe first order of business will be to put a little strength in your backbone. I could send you out to the Barrens to hunt kodo, but well, in all honesty, you're more useful to us alive than dead.\n\nI believe you'll be of more use to us slaughtering the boars you'll find in the farms to the north and northeast of here.\n\n[Slaughter 6 https://www.wowhead.com/npc=3098s.]\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=3143:Hmmm, not bad, . But don't let it get to your head...you'll fight tougher than boars in your career.\n\nNonetheless, you've proven yourself well, and your next trial will be against a considerably more dangerous opponent, so you'll need some extra protection.\n\nYou're not just another grunt - you seem to be a serious . Good, because that's exactly what I need.\n\nTry not to let the word out, since I don't want to cause a panic... but there have been reports of more humans nearby. This is an egregious betrayal of the peace that we negotiated with that miserable Jaina Proudmoore! We can't allow humans here in Durotar, and especially not here in the Valley.\n\nYou will find them to the south. Slay them quickly, before their numbers increase any more.\n\n[Slay 7 https://www.wowhead.com/npc=39317s.]\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=3143:Executed with quickness and discretion.  A job well done.\n\nI must send you back into the fields again, . You will find large numbers of scorpids northwest of here. Bring me eight of their tails.\n\nThe antidote for their sting is actually made from venom extracted from their stingers. We keep large quantities of antidote for scorpid venom on hand to heal young bloods just like you...\n\nBut I'm sure you won't be needing any of that, will you?\n\n[Obtain 8 https://www.wowhead.com/item=4862s.]\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=3143:The carapace of a scorpid isn't so thick that the strength of a determined warrior will be deterred. Strike strongly and without doubt, and the scorpids should prove easy prey.\n\nThere is an important lesson that you must take away from fighting scorpids. The smallest or largest of opponents can still send you to your doom. In fierce combat, any number of things can prove your downfall.\n\nI have no more to teach you, . You have done well, and I will watch your progress with interest.",
            date = "2021-01-17T21:10:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25152#comments:id=3291985",
        },
        {
            id = 2331613,
            score = -7,
            author = "BloodveinHD",
            text = "Here's a demonstration of the quest being done:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t0ujzC7wd5Y (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t0ujzC7wd5Y)",
            date = "2016-05-16T21:08:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25152#comments:id=2331613",
        },
    },
    [25153] = {
        {
            id = 1644739,
            score = 52,
            author = "joker102877",
            text = "Yes, there is a small prerequisite chain.  Never fear, it is relatively painless.\n\nDigsite Status (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25104) --> Hands Off Me Dig! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25106), Feegly the Exiled (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25108) --> Marley's Final Flight (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25120) -->Bael'Dun Rescue (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25153)\n\nRate this comment up so others may benefit.",
            date = "2012-03-25T21:56:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25153#comments:id=1644739",
        },
        {
            id = 1190078,
            score = 30,
            author = "kuruma",
            text = "Remember to follow the directions in the quest and use the \"fire valves\" to quell the flames else your gonna get burned, literally.  I didn't and just ran in there trying to be a hero but ended up dieing to the flames.  They're small red valves with what seems to be steam coming out of them at the entrance to Bael'dun just before you enter to rescue the survivors, located on the sides of the walls.  They will give you a 30 second buff called \"Emergency Fire Ward\" making you immune to fire damage within the keep.\n\nEdit: Also, careful with dieing in the keep.  As of this patch it seems that you will die again upon ressing even close to the flaming entrance of Bael'dun.  So remember to rebuff yourself with Emergency Fire Ward before it runs out.  There are many other valves scattered throughout the keep.",
            date = "2010-11-27T09:51:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25153#comments:id=1190078",
        },
        {
            id = 1195884,
            score = 11,
            author = "204380",
            text = "This was the first time I can remember, that I kept clicking past the ten required survivors on my way out of the fortress.  The animation on the trapped victims is a little too good.  This quest chain is traumatic!",
            date = "2010-11-29T14:20:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25153#comments:id=1195884",
        },
        {
            id = 1668935,
            score = 9,
            author = "dayoodin",
            text = "There is no need to go really deeply into the building! This is a really easy quest, it's just hard to keep a straight head with the klaxon wailing, all the injured dwarves flailing around, having to get the buff due to the various fires, etc.\n\nTip:  Turn off your sound for this quest if the klaxon is too distracting and distressing!\n\nThis is how I would do it now that I know better:\n\nGet buff outside. (Buff lasts about 30 seconds and there are plenty of nozzles, so just keep an eye on the timing and refresh appropriately, as necessary.)\nTo get the Horde body, go in through the right entrance. Once in, go left, rescuing dwarves as you run across them. The body of Weezil Slipshadow is right there with the question mark over his head. Complete quest there, then run back out the way you came in, again rescuing dwarves as you see them.\nOnce outside again, take a deep breath, refresh buff, if necessary.\nTo get the keg, now enter through the left entrance, take a right and just go straight ahead, rescuing dwarves along the way. Keg is straight ahead in a little eatery area.\nOnce you have the keg, go back out the way you came in, refreshing your buff as necessary and rescuing dwarves along the way.\n\nTip: After the \"Activating\" gauge shows you that you've turned the handle successfully, remain still! There is a little lapse between after it's activated and when the buff actually comes streaming out. Be sure to stay until the stream of air has come out, as that is what gives you the buff--otherwise you'll run off thinking you have the buff when you don't and you'll die quickly.",
            date = "2012-05-20T08:59:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25153#comments:id=1668935",
        },
        {
            id = 2582509,
            score = 4,
            author = "Tassit",
            text = "The fire does about 450 damage a second now in 8.0, as a level 34 I last about 3 seconds (and the immunity buff doesn't actually work!)",
            date = "2018-07-19T21:37:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25153#comments:id=2582509",
        },
    },
    [25163] = {
        {
