    [25627] = {
        {
            id = 1186288,
            score = 59,
            author = "629371",
            text = "Entrance to the cave at 91.79, 82.78.\n\nThrow the treasure at the whompers and they will turn friendly.\n\nFollow the cave path around to the left until you find Tony. He is a 42 elite, but easy enough to solo. Quite a fun fight, he jumps into the chests behind him and pops up into another chest, with a spawn or two (which you don't really have to worry about). He does send some parrots at you but they're simple to take down with a bit of aoe.",
            date = "2010-11-25T23:48:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25627#comments:id=1186288",
        },
        {
            id = 3118642,
            score = 17,
            author = "OneMoreBook1268",
            text = "Cave entrance  /way 91.88 83.04\nStay to the right all the way around and you'll jump in behind Two-Tusk.\nToss the coins to the Ogres if you're low level/don't want to fight.\nKill Two-Tusk (on my 120 it was a 2 shot)\nStay to the right once again to get out of the cave.",
            date = "2019-04-15T13:44:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25627#comments:id=3118642",
        },
        {
            id = 1278610,
            score = 14,
            author = "750237",
            text = "**Info found on www.wowhead.com\n\n\"This can actually be quite a tricky one to find (don't follow the skull on your map). Due south of the questgiver (about a hundred yards), you will find a cave with ~L41 elite ogres within. Use the quest item given to you to bribe them; they should then despawn [become green or non-aggressive], giving you an easy run out of the cave.\n\nBear left constantly while in the cave to find Two-Tusk.\n\nThe fight with Two-Tusk is an interesting one; periodically he will jump into a treasure chest and then something will happen: either the other chests will spawn weak pirates, or (very) weak parrots, while he himself appears or disappears. The fight appears to be a DPS race as he doesn't attack you directly, so if you can concentrate on him, I would. He has around 45K health.\"\n\nTIP:  As a Hunter, I found that my Hunter's Mark was a great tool to use on Tony in order to know in advance which chest would have Tony Two-tusk inside.",
            date = "2011-01-05T10:32:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25627#comments:id=1278610",
        },
        {
            id = 1205185,
            score = 11,
            author = "46662",
            text = "It is a fun fight, and not hard at all. Don't let the elite status fool you, as he doesn't really ever attack you directly. Once you engage him, he jumps into the chest behind him. The chests all spin around and he emerges in a different one, with other mobs spawning in other chests.\n\nFirst are guys with essentially flamethrowers. Second time will be guys who throw explosive charges at you. Third spawn will be several parrots with minimal health. Fourth was an engineer; you'll get an emote telling you to kill him before he can set off his weapon. Easy to kill, I don't even know what the weapon would've been. If you keep going the sequence will repeat.\n\nNone of these do all that much damage. Each time Two-Tusk pops up, just start attacking him until he disappears back into the chest.\n\nThis glitched the first time through for me. After he died, he glittered as all lootable objects do but it wouldn't let me loot (the cog-wheel wasn't visible when I moused over him). He respawned after a minute or so and I went through it again. Second time through I could loot with no problem.",
            date = "2010-12-04T00:01:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25627#comments:id=1205185",
        },
        {
            id = 1468355,
            score = 11,
            author = "836406",
            text = "The entrance to the \"Admiral's Den\" is a cave to the south and east of the location of the quest giver, near a windmill. An ogre may be standing on guard. Coordinates approximately 91.81, Southsea holdfast. Toss the treasure to any ogre you encounter and they will take it and go away.\n   Once inside the cave, bear to the left. Tony Two-Tusk is standing around 4 or 5 large chests. When you attack him, he will hide in them. I marked him with the Hunter's Mark, so I never lost track of him and had my pet attack. He summons minions to attack you from these chests. Some with flame-throwers, sometimes savage parrots.\n   As a hunter, I found the quest interesting and mildly challenging. Cloth and leather armor wearers may have to rely on heavy hits dealt fast to take him down, or bring a friend or two to help.",
            date = "2011-07-12T20:42:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25627#comments:id=1468355",
        },
    },
    [25628] = {
        {
            id = 1180458,
            score = 138,
            author = "Whollyunholy",
            text = "This can actually be quite a tricky one to find (don't follow the skull on your map). Due south of the questgiver (about a hundred yards), you will find a cave with ~L41 elite ogres within. Use the quest item given to you to bribe them; they should then despawn, giving you an easy run out of the cave.\n\nBear left constantly while in the cave to find Two-Tusk.\n\nThe fight with Two-Tusk is an interesting one; periodically he will jump into a treasure chest and then something will happen: either the other chests will spawn weak pirates, or (very) weak parrots, while he himself appears or disappears. The fight appears to be a DPS race as he doesn't attack you directly, so if you can concentrate on him, I would. He has around 45K health.\n\nNear the end of the fight an engineer will spawn, \"casting\" a very slow gunshot aimed at you. I haven't been hit by it but I would assume it hurts. You are prompted via a Blizzard raid warning to kill the engineer before she can get the shot off, but killing Two-Tusk causes her to despawn, so check his health at this point and see which you prefer.\n\nSoloed first time as a L44 shaman (elemental spec). Shouldn't cause you much trouble. Melee characters may find the pirates more troublesome; as a caster, I didn't seem to be in range for them to aggro on me.\n\nGood luck.",
            date = "2010-11-24T06:17:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25628#comments:id=1180458",
        },
        {
            id = 1182547,
            score = 129,
            author = "505525",
            text = "Cave around 91,82.",
            date = "2010-11-24T18:14:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25628#comments:id=1182547",
        },
        {
            id = 1186682,
            score = 24,
            author = "64801",
            text = "If you of a higher level that you can kill him before he even gets into a box don't. I had this quest bug out to where I could not loot him after he died. If you have DoTs just hit him with one and let it work for a bit then take him out. Seems to glitch if you kill him too fast.",
            date = "2010-11-26T04:01:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25628#comments:id=1186682",
        },
        {
            id = 1273565,
            score = 22,
            author = "Jeryn",
            text = "Entrance to the den at: 92,83\n\nStick to the path on the left once you are inside.",
            date = "2011-01-02T15:44:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25628#comments:id=1273565",
        },
        {
            id = 1386249,
            score = 21,
            author = "770905",
            text = "If anybody like me is completely directionless and can't follow the \"south\" or \"west\" instructions on this page for how to find the cave entrance, it is a little bit back and to the right of the house that is directly next to the quest giver. Just walk past the house and then a little bit further. When in the cave, hang left, and just keep flinging treasure. I guess I killed him too quickly the first time, because while sparkly, he wasn't lootable. Next time I didn't throw quite so much dps, and waited for the engineer to come out, and then it worked.",
            date = "2011-04-07T12:21:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25628#comments:id=1386249",
        },
    },
    [25640] = {
        {
            id = 1184310,
            score = 7,
            author = "708409",
            text = "Completing this will also unlock Windshear Mine Cleanup (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25646) if you have done\nHellscream's Legacy (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25616).",
            date = "2010-11-25T09:10:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25640#comments:id=1184310",
        },
        {
            id = 1208473,
            score = 3,
            author = "Whiterock",
            text = "CHASING THE BOMB Quest Tree From Whiterock\n[pre]\n1)They Took Our Gnomes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13913)*\n ||\n || 1)Ze Gnomecorder (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25607)* 1)The Goblin Braintrust (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13979)*\n ||__||_________________||\n ||\n2)Do Yourself a Favor (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25613)\n2)The Only Way Down is in a Body Bag (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25614)\n1)Return to Stardust (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25615)-->2)Hellscream's Legacy (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25616)\n ||\n2)Field Test: Gnomecorder (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25621)\n2)Burn, Baby, Burn! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25622)\n2)Bombs Away: Windshear Mine! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25640)\n ||                     ||->2)Don't Look Them in the Eyes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25642)\n2)Illegible Orc Letter (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25647) ||->2)Windshear Mine Cleanup (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25646)\n2)Minx'll Fix It (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25649)\n2)Orders from High Command (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25650)\n2)Commandeer That Balloon! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25652)-->2)Just Ask Alice (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25673)\n ||->1)Gerenzo the Traitor (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25729)    2)Mr. P's Wild Ride (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25728)\n ||\n2)Free Our Sisters (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25662)              1)BEWARE OF CRAGJAW! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25730)\n2)Rumble in the Lumber... Mill (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25669)\n ||  ||               ||->3)Preparations for the Future (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25741)\n ||  ||               ||\n || 3)Arcane Legacy (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25766) 3)Capturing Memories (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25767)\n ||  ||              /\n || 2)Fallowmere Beckons (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25769)\n || 4)Bombs Away: Mirkfallon Post! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25768)\n ||  ||                    ||->4)Schemin' That Sabotage (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25878)\n || 4)Gnome on the Inside (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25875) ||->4)The Lumbering Oaf Problem (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25879)\n || 4)It's Up There! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25876)\n || 4)No Time for Goodbyes! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25877)\n || 1)Warn Master Thal'darah (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25880)\n || 6)Save the Children! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25889)\n || 6)Last Ditch Effort (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25891)\n ||  ||->5)Back to the Depths! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25914)\n ||  ||->5)Putting Them to Rest (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25913)\n ||  ||->5)Seen Better Days (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25912)        Help for Desolace (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25938)*\n ||  ||\n || 1)Thal'darah's Vengeance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25925)\n ||  ||                   ||->7)Hungry Pups (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25935)\n || 7)Ascending the Vale (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25930) ||->7)World First: Gnomegen (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25934)\n || 7)Brood of Seldarria (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25931)\n ||\n ||\n3)If the Horde Don't Get You... (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25739)\n1)Tell 'Em Koko Sent You (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25765)\n8)The Deep Reaches (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25793)\n ||_________________________________________\n ||                 ||                      ||\n8)Shuttin Her Down (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25811) ||        8)Leave No Man Behind! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25809)\n ||                /                       ||\n || 8)They Put the Assass in... Never Mind (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25806) ||\n || 8)Is This Thing On? (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25808)                    ||\n ||___||____________________________________||\n ||\n1)A Special Kind of Job (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25821)\n1)Death by Proxy (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25834)\n1)A Proper Peace Offerin' (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25837)\n9)Sating the Savage Beast (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25844)\n1)Terms of Service (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25845)-->8)The Unrelenting Horde (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25823)\n ||\n8)Armaments for War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25822)\n9)Grundig Darkcloud, Chieftain of the Grimtotem (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25846)\n9)Grimtotem Supremacy (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25847)\n9)Downfall (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25848)\n1)Dances with Grimtotem (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25851)\n1)All's Clear (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25852)\n\nD)Thinning the Horde (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25671)(Not aviable?)\nHero's Call: Stonetalon Mountains! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28539)(WTB info)\nThey Set Them Up The Bomb! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=13981)(Ashenvale quest)\nQuest zones:\n1)Unique zones_____2)Windshear Crag+Windshear Mine_____3)Ruins of Eldre'thar+Webwinder Hollow_____4)The Sludgewerks_____5)Stonetalon Peak_____6)Thal'darah Grove_____7)The Charred Vale_____8)The Deep Reaches+Unearthed Grounds_____9)Camp Aparaje+Grimtotem Post\nD)Daily_____G)Gluing Separate Questlines\n*Click to see more info about that quest-line.\nStonetalon Mountains(Alliance) is done! Leave your comments/sugestions at my comment in Stonetalon Mountains zone (http://www.wowhead.com/zone=406). Thanks everyone who helped me to make it via comments on wowhead and in-game pre-quest tracking. Special thanks to Ravenhurst (http://www.wowhead.com/user=Ravenhurst).\n\n[/pre]",
