    [26115] = {
        {
            id = 1273321,
            score = 173,
            author = "Mumpley",
            text = "Besides Garrosh's unexpected change of heart, this quest -- more specifically, quest line -- centered around The Bomb is actually quite fascinating.\n\nAs a Goblin character in Kezan, you had to do the quest Waltz Right In (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14123) for Slinky Sharpshiv. In it, you had to steal Trade Prince Gallywix's prized possessions with the hopes of reselling them and making big moolah. The 3 possessions were Maldy's Falcon (http://www.wowhead.com/item=48937), The Goblin Lisa (http://www.wowhead.com/item=48939) and... The Ultimate Bomb (http://www.wowhead.com/item=48941)? Hold on a second... a super secret bomb being worked on by Hobart Grapplehammer? That sounds awfully familiar.\n\nFurther down the line while in Azshara, you have to deliver an unstable Azsharite Core from Hobart's Secret Lab to his assistant, Greely, in the quest Segmentation Fault: Core Dumped (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=14310). Being the decent Goblin he is, Dr. Grapplehammer manages to weaponize the unstable core and then gives you the task of delivering it to Bilgewater Harbor in the quest A Hello to Arms (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=24458). Assuming Hobart is trying to finish his work from Kezan, the Armed Azsharite Core (http://www.wowhead.com/item=49705) is the continuation of his \"Ultimate Bomb\".\n\nLo and behold, after a pit stop in Ashenvale, failed interventions from the Alliance and a refueling session, this bomb is finally dropped over Thal'darah Grove in this very quest. So basically, Hobart Grapplehammer built a nuke out of Cliff Giant poop, sent it to an insane Overlord who then  used it to destroy a grove full of innocent Druids. Oh, how I love Blizzard.",
            date = "2011-01-02T13:34:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26115#comments:id=1273321",
        },
        {
            id = 1467053,
            score = 133,
            author = "150475",
            text = "Garrosh: Do I look like a murderer?\n*throws off cliff*",
            date = "2011-07-11T09:50:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26115#comments:id=1467053",
        },
        {
            id = 1196799,
            score = 130,
            author = "146438",
            text = "The quote \"Honor, no matter how dire the battle, never forsake it\" comes from Overlord Saurfang after defeating his son Deathbringer Saurfang in ICC",
            date = "2010-11-30T00:10:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26115#comments:id=1196799",
        },
        {
            id = 1104362,
            score = 112,
            author = "621098",
            text = "Was simply epic. I even came to respect Garrosh, too bad that i lost my rank of General :(",
            date = "2010-08-20T11:25:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26115#comments:id=1104362",
        },
        {
            id = 1406741,
            score = 89,
            author = "Blackboy0",
            text = "Overlord Krom'gar says: Watch now, Cliffwalker, as this battle comes to its glorious conclusion.\nHigh Chieftain Cliffwalker says: You are about to cross a terrible threshold, Krom'gar. may the Earth Mother have mercy on your soul.\nOverlord Krom'gar says: Look upon the world, Cliffwalker, and see the might of the Horde!\n*The Ultimate Bomb is dropped on Thal'darah Grove*\nOverlord Krom'gar says: Warchief! I… I was carrying out your command!\nGarrosh Hellscream says: My command?\nGarrosh Hellscream says: Was my command to murder innocents, Krom'gar?\nOverlord Krom'gar says: Warchief… Sir… I…\nGarrosh Hellscream says: Am I a murderer, Krom'gar?\nOverlord Krom'gar says: No, Warchief!\nGarrosh Hellscream says: Then I ask you again: WHAT HAVE YOU DONE!\nGarrosh Hellscream says: I sent you into Stonetalon Mountains with an army. Your orders were to secure this land for the Horde.\nGarrosh Hellscream says: Instead, you laid waste to the land. Murdered innocents. Children even…\nGarrosh Hellscream says: I spent a very long time in Northrend, Krom'gar. I learned much about the Horde in that time.\nGarrosh Hellscream says: While there, a wise old war hero told me something that I would carry with me forever…\nGarrosh Hellscream says: \"Honor\", Krom'gar, \"No matter how dire the battle… never forsake it.\"\nGarrosh Hellscream says: Overlord Krom'gar, you have disgraced the Horde.\nGarrosh Hellscream says: You have brought shame to us as a people.\nGarrosh Hellscream says: By my right as Warchief, I hereby relieve you of duty.\n*Garrosh Hellscream picks Overlord Krom'gar up by the neck and walks to the edge*\nGarrosh Hellscream says: YOU ARE DISMISSED.\n*Garrosh Hellscream lets go and Overlord Krom'gar falls to his death*\nGarrosh Hellscream says: And you, !\n*Garrosh Hellscream turns to the player*\nHigh Chieftain Cliffwalker says: Wait, Warchief! Please!  was the hero responsible for uncovering this corruption. He tried to stop Krom'gar!\nHigh Chieftain Cliffwalker says: Have mercy, Warchief.\nGarrosh Hellscream says: Mercy… Your wife and child were murdered. Your kin wiped out. Your home burned to the ground.\nGarrosh Hellscream says: Mercy… Chieftain, on this day I learn from you.\nGarrosh Hellscream says: , Krom'gar's army is no more. Your rank no longer has meaning. If you wish to truly help the Horde, your considerable power could be used in Desolace or in the Southern Barrens.\nGarrosh Hellscream says: The choice is yours to make.\nGarrosh Hellscream says: Let honour guide you, . Do not forget that Hellscream's eyes are always upon you.",
            date = "2011-05-01T21:44:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26115#comments:id=1406741",
        },
    },
    [26116] = {
        {
            id = 2141825,
            score = 30,
            author = "linda535",
            text = "Kinelory is an idiot who shouldn't be allowed outside. This quest is pretty hard because Kinelory doesn't avoid ANY of the enemies and usually walks right to or through them.",
            date = "2015-03-22T11:41:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26116#comments:id=2141825",
        },
        {
            id = 1375753,
            score = 23,
            author = "Abiwho",
            text = "You have to protect Kinelory as he makes her way around the farm (counter-clockwise inside the cliffs) to the house on the opposite side where you have to defeat the undead Apothecary Jorell. I would strongly recommend taking out as many of the mobs outside the house as possible before allowing Kinelory enters; she doesn't pull the mobs as she walks past them (at least she didn't for me) but they come running once the fight starts. Apothecary Jorell is an easy fight alone, but it's very difficult to keep Kinelory alive against Jorell and three other mobs.\nOnce Jorell is slain Kinelory collects items from the house and then runs (and I mean RUNS) back to Quay around the upper rim of the cliffs (clockwise). There are only a few scattered orcs on the way back, but she really books it so \"stay on your paws\" :-)\nIf Kinelory dies, abandon quest, run back to Quay and wait for Kinelory to respawn (about 5 min for me).\n\nEdit: can't spell to save my life",
            date = "2011-03-25T12:09:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26116#comments:id=1375753",
        },
        {
            id = 1530032,
            score = 12,
            author = "Infiniti",
            text = "\"Watch my rear!\"",
            date = "2011-09-28T13:54:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26116#comments:id=1530032",
        },
        {
            id = 1548073,
            score = 11,
            author = "Kayaku",
            text = "Abiwho already indicated that once you kill Jorell Kinelory will run back to Quae quite fast, but i want to add that if you let her get too far ahead you will fail the quest.\n\nSo you might wanna get a bit of headstart while she's busy collecting the items inside of the house. (Altough not too far, because this will also count as failure...)\n\nAlso, while running, don't bother fighting mobs if she doesn't or she'll get away.\n\nIf you fail nonetheless and you're a guy who's all about perfect statistics you do not need to abandon the quest. She will respawn after 5-10 Minutes and you'll have the chance to try again, without the quest counting as \"abandoned\".\n\nHope this helps.",
            date = "2011-10-19T06:21:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26116#comments:id=1548073",
        },
        {
            id = 2562412,
            score = 7,
            author = "Cyjon",
            text = "Those of you thinking of skipping this terrible quest, be warned: it is a requirement of the Arathi Highlands Quests (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=4896/arathi-highlands-quests) achievement. Took me three tries: she died the first time, disappeared the second, and I barely managed to survive the third.",
            date = "2018-04-11T21:48:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26116#comments:id=2562412",
        },
    },
    [26117] = {
        {
            id = 1686677,
            score = 13,
            author = "Princeofchaos",
            text = "Nice and simple. These are quests you must complite to get this one:\n\n1. [quest=26113 domain=www]\n2. [quest=26110 domain=www]\nCourier is 27 lvl ud, so not a problem, really. Patroling from farm to Hammerfall.\n3. [quest=26114 domain=www]\nStand near Quae, just need to speak with her :)\n4. [quest=26116 domain=www]\nJust another escort quest. Keep her safe and youll be ok. After escort ends you will get your quest. Good luck and have fun.",
            date = "2012-07-10T09:43:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26117#comments:id=1686677",
        },
    },
    [26118] = {
