    [26171] = {
        {
            id = 1186545,
            score = 81,
            author = "Magion",
            text = "The person you are looking for is an ethereal ghost to the northwest of the mountain in the Rise of the Defiler (not in the cave).  He is standing by a purple glyph on the ground.  Cords: 46,21",
            date = "2010-11-26T02:33:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26171#comments:id=1186545",
        },
        {
            id = 1418747,
            score = 75,
            author = "705621",
            text = "There is a way down. On the north side of the rise, there is a platform. On the platform is a blue rune called The Rune of Return. You must drop down (don't jump or you will take more damage) to the platform where the rune is and move onto the rune. It will instantly teleport you to the bottom of the Rise of the Defiler. Hope this helps. Happy gaming. :)",
            date = "2011-05-14T16:25:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26171#comments:id=1418747",
        },
        {
            id = 1192475,
            score = 38,
            author = "Vizime",
            text = "This quest was a bit annoying since I didn't get credit for Destroying his body. After several times trying a hunter (level 57) came. I just let him dps Razelikh and finally it worked. If you dps him too fast you won't get the credit for destroying his body and you will 'bug' the quest.\n\nSo when ur level 80 and doing this quest, don't dps too much! =)",
            date = "2010-11-28T05:34:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26171#comments:id=1192475",
        },
        {
            id = 1495769,
            score = 37,
            author = "violetta",
            text = "I told that bloody gnome that I should use my jumper cables but noooo, he has to use the Altar of Storms...",
            date = "2011-08-15T18:40:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26171#comments:id=1495769",
        },
        {
            id = 1800557,
            score = 29,
            author = "819747",
            text = "Ok so for those of you actually looking at completing this quest at the designed level (I'm assuming here that you already know how to get up the mountain here as most of the other comments pertain to how to get there...) here is some information on the actual quest.\n\n1.  While you're fighting against Rakh'likh, he will summon some beasts.  They are thoroughly annoying as they eat away your and the NPC's hp.  However, when he casts the spell that sends you soaring, the beasts disappear until he summons others.\n2.  Make sure you damage Rakh'likh quickly enough because if the NPC dies, you're pretty much screwed and will have to go back down the mountain and teleport back up to reset it.\n3.  You will be provided with a (very minor) continuous healing boost during the fight.\n4.  Once the demon will be down to a quarter of hid HP, the fight will stop and you will get credit for destroying his body.  His soul will then be transferred to the NPC's body.  Then, all you will have to do is eat away at his HP until the NPC prompts you to use the knife.\n\nQuest complete.\n\nOther info:\nI tried to complete this quest too many times to count with a lvl 56 Frost Mage and was unsuccessful as I couldn't keep up with the healing the the quest required.  I managed to complete it in a party with a lvl 57 druid.\n\nIf you die during the encounter, as soon as you release your spirit, you will be in your physical form (ie: not a ghost that needs to find its corpse).  You can go straight back up (you spawn very close to the etheral being that sends you up the mountain) and pick up on the fight where you left off.\n\nBugs:\nI started to fight the demon for what seemed to be the millionth time and noticed a druid watching.  I invited him to a group and we were able to get the demon down to a quarter of his HP.  However, he just disappeared and no credit was given for destroying the body.  Had to go back down and come back up (yet again) to reset the quest.   When the party was formed prior to engaging the demon, no such problem arose.",
            date = "2013-01-18T13:22:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26171#comments:id=1800557",
        },
    },
