    [26317] = {
        {
            id = 1412828,
            score = 45,
            author = "Glowyrm",
            text = "How to obtain the Lashtail Hatchling (http://www.wowhead.com/item=69251) companion as Horde\n\nTo see the Lashtail Hatchling inside the Zul'Gurub instance after killing Bloodlord Mandokir (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=52151) you must first complete a series of small quest lines in Northern Stranglethorn.\n\n*SPOILERS Start at step 7 for Horde - You can stop right before those steps if you want to see the main meat of the story unfold yourself*\n\nAs a member of the Horde this entire ordeal starts with The Defense of Grom'gol: Raptor Risk (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26278) given by Commander Aggro'gosh (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2464) in Grom'gol.\n\nAfter completing that quest, you will automatically receive the quest A Lashtail Hatchling (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26317) and the Lashtail Raptor Egg Fragment (http://www.wowhead.com/item=58165).\nReturn with the hatchling to Far Seer Mok'thardin (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2465) in Grom'gol (If your bags were full check your Mail for the Egg Fragment).\n\nNext he will send you on a quest called I Think She's Hungry (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26321) to feed the baby raptor murloc meat. Make sure your raptor is summoned so she can take bites out of the corpses as you kill them.\n\nNow take the hatchling to the Bal'lal Ruins @ 33.7, 37.2 (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=33:338372) where you will find a pile of skulls on the ground, Your hatchling will run up to the pile and grab a skull from it. Now he will give you the quest Favored Skull (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26323) which needs you to return to Nimboya (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2497) in Grom'gol.\n\nThe cauldron near Nimboya will now offer the quest A Nose for This Sort of Thing (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26325).\n\nNext you get the quest Who's a Big Troll? (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26330) then Skullsplitter Mojo (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26332)\n\nAfter completing the above quest line, Bloodlord Mandokir (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26334) will spawn and offer a \"quest\" of the same name. He really just wants to steal the raptor from you because it's special. Do not chase him when he runs off. There is more to do, you must now embark on a chain to try and save your new raptor friend from her fate.\n\nNimboya will now give you a quest to speak to Priestess Hu'rala (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26350).\n\nShe will lead you on a chain to try and save your new raptor hatchling friend from her terrible fate of becoming the Bloodlord's new raptor slave. This is all your fault! But maybe you can do something about it...\n1) Mind Vision (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26351), 2) See Raptor (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26359), 3) Mind Control (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26360), 4) Be Raptor (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26362), 5) Surkhan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26386)\n\nAfter that really cool and fun quest chain from the Priestess you are ready to enter the 85 Heroic Dungeon of Zul'Gurub and face the Bloodlord Mandokir. It's time to undo the mistake you made by bringing him back to life, and you must save your new friend from a world of torture and evil. Once the Bloodlord falls at your hands, you will see An Old Friend (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=29208#comments:id=1408932).\n\nHow to obtain the Lashtail Hatchling (http://www.wowhead.com/item=69251) companion as Alliance (Credit to user: Madwolf (http://www.wowhead.com/user=Madwolf))\n\n*SPOILERS Start at step 8 for Alliance - You can stop right before those steps if you want to see the main meat of the story unfold yourself*\n\nFor Alliance this chain starts with the quest Bad Medicine (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26732) given by Brother Nimetz (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=739) at the Rebel Camp.\n\nUpon completion of Bad Medicine you will automatically obtain the quest Just Hatched (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26738) and the Lashtail Raptor Egg Fragment (http://www.wowhead.com/item=58165). Return to Corporal Sethman (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=1422) at the Rebel Camp with the new hatchling.\n\nHe will then send you on the quest I Think She's Hungry (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26739) to feed the baby raptor some basilisk meat. Make sure you have the hatchling summoned while killing basilisks so she may take bites from the corpses as you kill them.\n\nNext you must do The Fate of Kurzen (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26735) given by Lieutenant Doren (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=469) in the Rebel Camp. Continue on his chain and do Spared from Madness (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26736) next.\n\nAt this point you must log out and in to spawn an NPC that will be required in the next step.\n\nNow take the hatchling to the Bal'lal Ruins @ 33.7, 37.2 (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=33:338372) where you will find a pile of skulls on the ground. Your hatchling will run up to the pile and grab a skull from it. Now he will give you the quest Favored Skull (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26745). Return to Osborn Obnoticus (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=43884) at the Rebel Camp (This is the NPC that you must have logged out then back in to see according to some Alliance players).\n\nOsborn will then give you A Nose for This Sort of Thing (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26746) to start trying to figure out who that skull belonged to.\n\nAfter that do the next quest in the chain, A Physical Specimen (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26747).\n\nAfter completing the above quest line, Bloodlord Mandokir (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26748) will spawn and offer a \"quest\" of the same name. He really just wants to steal the raptor from you because it's special. Do not chase  him when he runs off. There is more to do, you must now embark on a chain to try and save your new raptor friend from her fate.\n\nOsborn will give you a quest to go talk to Priestess Thaalia (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26749) at Fort Livingston.\n\nShe will lead you on a chain to try and save your new raptor hatchling friend from her terrible fate of becoming the Bloodlord's new raptor slave. This is all your fault! But maybe you can do something about it...\n1) Mind Vision (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26772), 2) See Raptor (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26773), 3) Mind Control (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26774), 4) Be Raptor (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26775), 5) Ghaliri (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26776)\n\nAfter that really cool and fun quest chain from the Priestess you are ready to enter the 85 Heroic Dungeon of Zul'Gurub and face the Bloodlord Mandokir. It's time to undo the mistake you made by bringing him back to life, and you must save your new friend from a world of torture and evil. Once the Bloodlord falls at your hands, you will see An Old Friend (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=29208#comments:id=1408932).",
            date = "2011-05-08T07:04:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26317#comments:id=1412828",
        },
        {
            id = 1431020,
            score = 11,
            author = "452042",
            text = "From what I can figure out, the quest chain has you losing the little hatching, only to be reunited with the little bugger after doing Zul'Gurub on heroic (lvl 85).  This means you won't have the little guy as a companion while you are lvl 29 and finishing up your Stranglethorn quests; instead you'll get him back once you reach lvl 85 and do the dungeon.\n\nI, personally, think it is a cool concept that results in tying your early adventuring days to your later end-game adventures.",
            date = "2011-05-30T21:14:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26317#comments:id=1431020",
        },
        {
            id = 1182689,
            score = 8,
            author = "Junyed",
            text = "Just a note, if your bags are full, don't worry, return to grom'gol and you can get the quest from far seer mok'thardin.",
            date = "2010-11-24T19:04:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26317#comments:id=1182689",
        },
        {
            id = 1397200,
            score = 5,
            author = "817177",
            text = "After I fed the raptor and no other quests popped up i went over to the Bal'al ruins and my raptor found a skull and it gave me a quest to go back to the witch docter at Grom'gol and it continued the chain.",
            date = "2011-04-22T18:12:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26317#comments:id=1397200",
        },
        {
            id = 1810128,
            score = 4,
            author = "1070835",
            text = "Really neat effect the hatchling does when you finally get her as a summonable pet - She'll run up to random kills of yours, pick a bone off it, and hold it in her mouth for a few seconds. She'll then toss it aside. Also, holding true to the end quest text, she IS a bit bigger than other hatchling pets. Definitely a worthy endeavor to get her!",
            date = "2013-02-06T23:15:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26317#comments:id=1810128",
        },
    },
    [26318] = {
        {
            id = 1477648,
            score = 4,
            author = "855522",
            text = "every time I go and kill the troggs all the time a elite mob comes up nad kills me all the time can someoen help me?",
            date = "2011-07-23T14:45:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26318#comments:id=1477648",
        },
        {
            id = 1606835,
            score = 2,
            author = "certa0",
            text = "Just level'd a Female Gnome Warrior through this. Brutal, One death upon encountering and trying to slay, another death to get further in and one more death to get out. 3 death total. Not possible to level a gnome thru here without dying unless you're loomd, I was on a new server so no looms.",
            date = "2012-01-05T05:11:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26318#comments:id=1606835",
        },
        {
            id = 1906072,
            score = 2,
            author = "1146401",
            text = "A word of advice on this quest...\n\nSince Cataclysm came and broke the game, there is a Level 6 rare called \"Great Father Arctikus\" which appears to have been left in the cave.  Although he is now level 6, it is still too high a level for the starting gnome area.\n\nHe is also heavily glitched.  Do a /targetexact Great Father Arctikus while in the cave, and 90% of the time you will target him because he is stuck inside the cave walls/floors/ceilings.  It appears that his pathing was never updated with the cave changes.  To make matters worse, he'll frequently blink out of existence as his pathing is bugged, sometimes even temporarily appearing in a hut NW of Kharanos.  Perhaps Blizzard wanted to move him there, but forgot to remove his path from the cave.  That would be my best guess on this utter mess.\n\nUnfortunately for us, the bugged mob has been present for 3+ years and, despite numerous bug reports, Blizzard has not bothered to fix it.  They typically ignore bugs in new player areas and only focus on end game new content.\n\nAll I can advise here is to /targetexact the mob and just wait for it to be gone.  Also, please, please, please open tickets, bug reports, suggestions, whatever with Blizzard on this and ask them to remove or fix this NPC.  Perhaps if there are enough complaints it'll happen.  I doubt it, but worth a try.",
            date = "2013-10-06T10:51:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26318#comments:id=1906072",
        },
        {
            id = 2014314,
            score = 2,
            author = "89813",
            text = "As of today, 10\\16\\2014 all enemies are level 3, saw no elite. Easy.",
            date = "2014-10-16T19:41:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26318#comments:id=2014314",
        },
        {
            id = 1631801,
            score = 1,
            author = "SkeeterEater",
            text = "This one is a little ridiculous. Between the extreeeemely short trogg respawn times and the wandering level 6, this is one of the few quests I would actually like to see getting nerfed. That being said, the strategy i used was to work my way back into the cave as far as i could (while the wandering Great Father guy is near the back), then when he inevitably came along and spanked me, ran back and res'd after he'd wandered further to the front of the cave. Killed the boss, popped the explosives, and repeated the process on the way out.\nNote: https://www.wowhead.com/npc=1260 is no longer Elite, but is definitely still a pain.",
            date = "2012-02-26T01:03:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26318#comments:id=1631801",
        },
    },
