        {
            id = 1889829,
            score = 12,
            author = "jfoobar",
            text = "For those that look at newest comments first, here is something that will keep you from having to dig down into older comments.  Smoot is a goblin that runs at full speed around the village.  Look for the running goblin carrying something.  You will need to get close to him long enough to very briefly sprocket him (sprocket on mouseover) and that will stun him.  After he is stunned for about five seconds, the samophlange appears on the ground next to him.  Loot and win.\n\nApparently this can be done while mounted.  I did it as a hunter in aspect of the cheetah.",
            date = "2013-08-24T15:51:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26361#comments:id=1889829",
        },
        {
            id = 1346444,
            score = 6,
            author = "794450",
            text = "The best way to find this little critter is to use the /target smoot\ni then used Shadow Jade Focusing Gem to track him .  was verry usefull. even though you track him its hard to find him because he runs perty fast and he is soo small.",
            date = "2011-02-22T19:40:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26361#comments:id=1346444",
        },
    },
    [26362] = {
        {
            id = 1098904,
            score = 94,
            author = "18516",
            text = "Very cute quest. If you get caught by trolls you get returned to the starting point, so avoid that big time.  There are only 4 raptors to speak with. On my mini-map they were marked as green dots, but that could have been because I had hunter beast tracking on, though you are in pet/vehicle form during the quest and those abilities shouldn't work....  You start out with a Dash ability (1 button)\n\nFirst raptor teaches you how to break out of nets (2 button). In my experience they captured you again before you could break out of their nets, so pretty much useless.\n\nSecond raptor asks you to get him food from a sleeping guy, so I did a 180 back away from him, hugged the right wall, and went into the back tent to get him food. You have 3 minutes to return with the food. Once you do he teaches you an ability to use get torches from braziers and burn tikis (3 button). If you get caught on the next steps you do not have to get him food again, because you have already learned the burning tiki ability.\n\nYou have to burn three tikis to get to the next raptor. Click the brazier below him and move nearish the tiki next to it, and hit the 3 button.  The guards will move away and attend to the tiki. Going forward do the same with the next brazier, but this time you must be faster. The last brazier is right past where the guards are. Use the brazier and hit dash, click the 3 button as soon as you can at the next tiki, otherwise your torch will burn out, and move forward to the last raptor. I had to do this a few times to get it right.\n\nLast raptor teaches you how to pick up skulls to trip trolls (4 button). I picked up a skull below and put it on the footbridge. If the patrol aggros you he will ignore the skull, so stay back a bit. Once he nears the skull he will trip and fall of the bridge. I repeated this on the next bridge.\n\nLast bit has a triple patrol and a single patrol. I zipped around all of them, used the brazier near the exit, burned the tiki and ran up the stairs to get the complete event.",
            date = "2010-08-10T23:12:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26362#comments:id=1098904",
        },
        {
            id = 1350010,
            score = 32,
            author = "242813",
            text = "Here's a video guide for the quest for those who don't like reading a wall of text: WoW Quest Guide: Be Raptor (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GrR5a0R7G3A)",
            date = "2011-02-25T17:27:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26362#comments:id=1350010",
        },
        {
            id = 2625363,
            score = 29,
            author = "Seonsha",
            text = "An absolutely horrific quest. Easily in the top 10 of worst quests.\n\nNot only is this thing prown to disconnecting you from the game server when a troll captures you (I had a bunch of disconnects during the quest.) The whole design of might of supposed to be fun? Well it failed hard. But the raptor manuevers like the titanic trying to do a u-turn in a one way street. The mobs sometimes ignore the fires and skuls and go straight for you.\n\nThis quest can easily be rage inducing for all those factors.",
            date = "2018-10-22T10:15:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26362#comments:id=2625363",
        },
        {
            id = 1210375,
            score = 21,
            author = "fortnerd",
            text = "Tip: You don't have to go inside the tent at all to steal the food. Stand at the back of the tent, close to the wall and hover the cursor around till you see the loot cursor. Voila, food. And no pesky guards with nets.",
            date = "2010-12-06T14:40:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26362#comments:id=1210375",
        },
        {
            id = 1401934,
            score = 15,
            author = "Khayr",
            text = "For those of you wondering, if you've completed the raptor chain the hatchling drops from Mandokir in the new heroic dungeon.",
            date = "2011-04-27T19:15:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26362#comments:id=1401934",
        },
    },
    [26363] = {
