            text = "Don't  even try to get to the Hinterlands from Hammerfall - instead, go back to the Eastern Tower in the Hillsbrad Foothills, and head for Durnholde Keep. Don't go in, just head North-East of the keep. You'll pass a few rampaging owlbeasts, but you will see a path through the hills that leads you directly to the Hinterlands.\n\nYou'll save a lot of time! (That is if you missed the fact you are supposed to speak to Urda ;) )",
            date = "2013-03-18T11:33:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26430#comments:id=1830636",
        },
        {
            id = 1385868,
            score = -4,
            author = "448957",
            text = "I'm rather annoyed Revantusk Quests don't earn you Darkspear rep, not everyone wants to do dungeons to get rep, they also removed all the cloth quarter masters which I can see no reason for, except for making Rep a grind.\n\nOh well, I guess I'll have to do every single troll quest and end up doing dungeons anyway, *groan* as a level 46 troll myself, I can't just go and do Argent Tournament dailies. (which are also a god damn grind of dailies.)",
            date = "2011-04-07T00:01:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26430#comments:id=1385868",
        },
    },
    [26432] = {
        {
            id = 1388500,
            score = 8,
            author = "tnwizard",
            text = "This is a \"bread crumb\" quest to get you over to Jintha'Alor. If you didn't get it before starting those quests it is impossible to get.",
            date = "2011-04-10T15:51:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26432#comments:id=1388500",
        },
        {
            id = 2201785,
            score = 2,
            author = "Wirenth",
            text = "The Jinth'alor questline would be a lot more fun if higher level Alliance players could find better things to do with their time than constantly kill the quest givers. Every time I take a toon through there, mostly months apart, it's always the same tedious, boring, repetitive story. FGS, guys - go play with the endgame content, will you! PVP is one thing but this kind of griefing is just unacceptable, especially to casual players like myself who don't have time to waste hanging around hoping to get the opportunity to progress their questline.",
            date = "2015-06-27T07:27:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26432#comments:id=2201785",
        },
    },
    [26433] = {
        {
            id = 1766439,
            score = 5,
            author = "168405",
            text = "There is a path leading up to the Nek'mani Wellspring that starts at: 40.89 45.61\nThe spring is at: 43.92 48.96",
            date = "2012-11-22T19:09:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26433#comments:id=1766439",
        },
        {
            id = 1963301,
            score = 2,
            author = "Firelocked",
            text = "I had to go from 41,44 at the end of the bridge. Keep to the left on the path until 41,50, where you see an archway. Go through it, you'll see a bridge that goes straight to the Wellspring.",
            date = "2014-05-05T04:22:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26433#comments:id=1963301",
        },
        {
            id = 6410530,
            score = 1,
            author = "Roxtoni",
            text = "Before Cataclysm, you could complete https://www.wowhead.com/quest=573, a quest that is no longer available in the current version of the game.\nIf your character completed https://www.wowhead.com/quest=573 before Cataclysm, the game will now direct you to https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26590.\nHowever, if your character did not complete https://www.wowhead.com/quest=573 back then, the game will instead direct you to https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26433.\n\nYes, both quests have the same name, but the quest text and context are different. The reason is that a character who completed the original pre-Cataclysm quest is already familiar with the source of the naga threat, so the game gives that character a slightly different version of the storyline.\n\nIt is still possible to complete both versions today, but you need access to an old character that completed https://www.wowhead.com/quest=573 before Cataclysm.\n\nThis is how I managed to do it:\n\nFirst, on your current/main character, pick up and complete https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26433 normally.\nThen, log onto an old character that completed https://www.wowhead.com/quest=573 before Cataclysm and pick up the quest that leads into the old version, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26590.\nNext, use Party Sync with another character from a second account or with a friend. Share the quest with that character, then switch back to your main character and have them share the quest back to you.\n\nAs far as I know, this is the only way to get https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26590 on a character that normally receives https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26433, allowing you to complete both versions of the quest on the same character.\nLuckily, I had a really old character, which made it possible for me to do this!",
            date = "2026-09-02T21:20:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26433#comments:id=6410530",
        },
    },
    [26434] = {
        {
            id = 1189035,
            score = 14,
            author = "665595",
            text = "It seems that the Tigress and Shadowmaw share a spawn point now. If you can't find any tigresses, just kill all the panthers you can find, and wait for respawn. You should get some tigresses.",
            date = "2010-11-26T22:56:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26434#comments:id=1189035",
        },
        {
            id = 1189375,
            score = 6,
            author = "330405",
            text = "Actually, I meant how am i to get eligible to interract with the goblin, in order for me to be offered the quest, in first place. At the moment I am stuck at 57/60 quests done At Cape of ST, and I know this Flem Gizzix holds the last few, but for some reason, he wont be giving them away to the ones who complete Hadwrenched Hideaway quests before visiting Bambala to the North first. Instead, if you let HH q's intact and go to Bambala, at some point the flight master there will offer you a free ride to HH. And when you arrive there, you will find Gizzix ... willing to assign you with the first task, this holy water quest. carefull guys, that's the way it should be done if you wanna get the Cape achievement and not get stuck the way me and few others did. (Still waiting for Blizzard's response on this issue).",
            date = "2010-11-27T02:27:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26434#comments:id=1189375",
        },
        {
            id = 1187890,
