    [26563] = {
        {
            id = 1310962,
            score = 22,
            author = "54288",
            text = "These npcs keep talking over and over while you quest.\n\nJorgensen says: You orcs are gonna be sorry when I get out of here.\n\nMessner says: I think I'm gonna go to Dalaran after this is over. Help'em get that city up and Floating.\n\nKrakauer says: Wait'll these orcs get a load of us. Bravo Compagny BACK IN BUSINESS!\n\nKrakauer says: So whatever happened to that hot little number in Stormwind? Lady Prestor was her name.\n\nJorgensen says: You know, I kept hearing the Blackrock orcs talk about the return of Hellscream to the Horde. What's that all about? Isn't Hellscream dead?\n\nMessner says: I need to use the restroom.\n\nDanforth says: I remember this one time, Keeshan and I were out fishing at the Lakeshire bridge and Keeshan farted. Don't think Oslow ever forgave Keeshan for that one...\n\nDanforth says: You ever notice how sarcastic the people living in Redridge are? Sometimes I feel like I just want to take a blow torch to that jackass Solomon's town hall.\n\nDanforth says: You know, I've always wondered why they call themselves orcs.\n\nKrakauer says: It's weird. My butt hurts. Not sure why.\n\nDanforth says: It's an ugly word, you know? It's a word I'd use to describe defecating. For exemple:\n\nDanforth says: After that Pilgrim's Bounty dinner, I took a huge smelly orc.\n\nMessner says: I really missed you, Danforth.\n\nDanforth says: You know, Keeshan lost his wife to Blackrock orcs. He was never the same after that day. Was like the sun just set on his life. Darkness, man. Pure darkness.\n\nJorgensen says: You ever seen Keeshan kill an orc? It's a sight to behold, man.\n\nDanforth says: They called us the Bravo Vompagny. When things needed killin', we did the spillin'... of blood.\n\nDanforth says: Messner is a master of fire magic. We invite him to all of our barbecues.\n\nMessner says: So what's up with the bridge in Lakeshire? Oslow ever finish building it?\n\nDanforth says: So I hear Varian Wrynn is back. That true? Sorry, I'm a bit out of the loop.\n\nJorgensen says: I feel weak. I mean weaker than normal. Like as if the Light is less powerful this week. Probably just something I ate. Orc food give me the craps.\n\nDanforth says: Jorgensen is real dainty, by the way. He's a paladin, so be careful what you say around him or you're liable to make him cry.\n\nJorgensen says: Real funny, Danforth.\n\nMessner says: These orcs are in for a rude awakening once Bravo Compagny is back and running.\n\nJorgensen says: So I heard Thrall left the Horde. That true?\n\nMessner says: Being a mage has its advantages. but the laundry bills are hell to pay.\n\nJorgensen says: I'm probably the most important member of this team, being a paladin and all.\n\nKrakauer says: Keeshan's a good man, . Any of us would give our lives for him.\n\nKrakauer says: When this is all over, I'm taking a vacation.\n\nMessner says: We all oew our lives to Keeshan. He's saved our hides a hundread times.\n\nJorgensen says: Can't believe we're putting the old team back together. All tanks to you, .",
            date = "2011-01-26T16:36:05-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26563#comments:id=1310962",
        },
        {
            id = 1343195,
            score = 20,
            author = "432617",
            text = "Bravo Company is made up for 4 members. All are level 17 elites. They all self heal after a fight. They are comprised of:\n\nMessner  : Mage - 1750Hp\nJorgensen: Paladin - 1625Hp 357Mana\nDanforth   : Warrior - 1930Hp\nKrakauer  : Warrior - 1930 Hp\n\nBoth Krakauer and Danforth can tank for you. They also cast Battle shout with only the +AP component.\n\nThe mage casts the Flamestrike and firebolts. Also selfbuffs Molten Armour.\n\nThe Paladin has the Concentration aura on  and self buffs Seal of Righteousness.\n\nThey dps  ranges from 22(lvl 18mob) - 67(lvl14 mob) depending on mob level.\n\nThey can follow you around on a lvl 20 mount with ease. However if you happen to agro something they tend to slow down till you lose agro OR stop to fight.\n\nAs the previous poster said you will lose them if you:\n1: Teleport anywhere, instance, hearth, log out etc\n2: Take a flight mount to anywhere.... they can run but not that fast.\n3: If you loose line of sight of them ie  run away while they fight. (which is how l lost them in STV ... so sad)\n\nThey will not randomly agro anything and start a fight. You need to hit the mob first before they join in\n\nThese boys are the best of the best. If you have a &*!@ load of time on your hand then you can have a great deal of fun before you hand this quest in.\n\nThe benefits of keeping them is this, the 2 warriors can tank and boy can they tank.  Take them around and they will do the tanking for you and you can dps from the background.  You just need to make sure you hit the target first and be able to take some initial damage  before the 2 tanks take over. Then sit back and dps em down. If your level 15-20 then this group will be a real great help for your questing. But Under level 20 you will be walking around a lot to get from one zone to another so its up to you if its worth the time and effort :)\n\n1. Use them to level up gathering professions. At lvl 20 you can level your professions to level 225 (not including racial bonuses). You can basically go to a high level zone and do your farming safe  in the fact that you can take on mobs up to level 30.  I never got the chance to go any higher cos l lost them. Just make sure you take on one mob at a time. Any more and you will get agro on other mobs 'cos the Bravo Company can only dps ONE mob at a time.  So if u get more than one be prepared to  deal damage.\n\nOne thing you do need to have is a lot of HIT and Expertise gear 'cos you will be missing all your attacks on anything higher than 4 levels above you.  I had about 28HIT rating at level 21  and 0 expertise, and l was still missing a load of  hits on a lvl 30 mobs. Also remember these are Level 17 Elites so they will be doing minimum damage to a level 30 mob. They are they just to keep agro on the mob while you do the dps. So wear HIT gear.\n\nI took Bravo Company into Stranglethorn Vale via Duskwood. Was a long ride but worth it. I managed to max out my  herb/skinning to  225 and 240(worgan racial bonus)\n\nI went slow killing one mob at a time working my way south to the southern area cos l was not getting many skill ups in the north after lvl 210.\n\n2: Take them around to a AH and get them stand next to the AH  npcs :)\n3: go to where the duelers are and follow one dueler around so the other has a hard time targeting them :)\n4. Take them sight seeing. See how far you can take them. (l'm on my way to taking them to see the IronForge king.)\n5. Use em for quests in nearby zones . Duskwood, Westfall etc heck even at lvl 25+ you can take them into StV\n\nJust posted a pic of them next to King Varian in Stormwind. Heck now l feel like taking em to see the Ironforge king via Westfall, swim to wetlands ride across to Loch Mordan then Dun Mordan... sigh that will be a long swim and ride in. Have fun :)\n\n\"There is no limits but what your mind sets\"",
            date = "2011-02-20T07:40:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26563#comments:id=1343195",
        },
        {
            id = 1196744,
            score = 16,
            author = "363646",
            text = "When you are at this stage of this quest, don't deliver the quest in, because you can take those four boytoys along with you to other areas outside redridge. I went with them to Duskwood and that was really funny, how easy it was killing all that went passed us by. Also remember that mounting by flightpath or porting outside redridge, will make your elites disappear. if that happens just return to redridge and your 4 bodyguards will pop up again.\nFunny is, that they will agro all, so rogues and druids can stay in stealth and you get loads of buffs like aura's, battleshouts and stuff and they keep the agro down. handy for mages:)",
            date = "2010-11-29T23:30:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26563#comments:id=1196744",
        },
        {
            id = 1196816,
            score = 12,
            author = "223389",
            text = "Will these guys help you with PVP?",
            date = "2010-11-30T00:23:13-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26563#comments:id=1196816",
        },
        {
            id = 1416155,
            score = 12,
            author = "Dreddful",
            text = "Once I got these guys, I stopped questing in Redridge and took the group to Darkshire, did all the quests there with their help.  They fought Stitches and Mor'Ladim.  They wouldn't help with Morbent Fel though - they stopped in the root-filled tunnel and wouldn't go into to the room where he was.  They helped me a lot though, quests went very fast, got up to level 28 before I took them back to Redridge.  On the way I stopped in front of Stormwind and challenged a level 28 druid (I'm an arms warrior) to a duel - I hit the guy once and they finished him off.  I love these guys.",
            date = "2011-05-11T17:07:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26563#comments:id=1416155",
        },
    },
    [26566] = {
        {
