            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26573#comments:id=1208891",
        },
        {
            id = 1295309,
            score = 5,
            author = "Jaymacibe",
            text = "Blizzard should have put these items in a different place. It's not logical to go though this place AGAIN for the rescue quests.\n\nKrakauer: \"Help....me!\"\nYou: \"Oh I'm sorry I'll come back for you later after I finish this quest and another.\"",
            date = "2011-01-15T18:31:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26573#comments:id=1295309",
        },
        {
            id = 5717289,
            score = 1,
            author = "Aletto",
            text = "On the last two characters I took through Redridge, I wasn't able to remotely turn in 'Weapons of War' like I remember being able to. Instead the quest would just sit completed in my log until I came back to town after rescuing Krakuer and Danforth to turn everything in - and then Troteman (acting like he's remotely radioing me in the field) would offer 'His Heart Must be in It' which would send me back to the cave I just fought through to open a chest in there.\n\nSo it seems like for now you should probably head back to Lakeshire to turn in 'Weapons of War' in person so you can have the followup quest active when you go through the cave at Render's Camp.",
            date = "2023-11-04T01:36:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26573#comments:id=5717289",
        },
    },
    [26574] = {
        {
            id = 1949612,
            score = 9,
            author = "Gymlea",
            text = "Directions: this camp is covert. That means there is no road to it, nor signs. Indeed it is surrounded by hostile MOBs. There is no way to avoid them except by flying, and, I assume, if you are doing this quest, that you are not level sixty and therefore are not flying. Go east on the road, past the bridge, under the three fallen trees, until you see the Horde Tauran Grimtotem camp on your left.  Now in a ways, on the right if you watch closely you will see a cut in the bank with a log over it, leaving room for someone on foot to go under.  Turn south under the log, and by dead reckoning, travel due south till you reach the Zukk'ash infestation. The Covert Camp is to the northeast. If you have good graphics, and WoW is set to high, you will see the two Alliance Banners that flank the short trail into the camp. If you go around the bend on the road to where you can just see Camp Mojache you have gone just a bit too far. Back up to the cut in the bank.",
            date = "2014-03-09T19:02:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26574#comments:id=1949612",
        },
        {
            id = 1205697,
            score = 7,
            author = "FaustinaDraenor",
            text = "Coords for the Entrance of the Camp are at 76, 57 - just north of the Writhing Deep.",
            date = "2010-12-04T07:55:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26574#comments:id=1205697",
        },
    },
    [26586] = {
        {
            id = 1281708,
            score = 11,
            author = "757883",
            text = "No it is not, it is a direct reference to the Rambo - first blood movie. The names are all the same names from Rambo's squad.\nColonel Troteman = Colonel Troutman from Rambo\nJohn J. Keeshan = John J. Rambo\n\nCoolest quest line in WoW!",
            date = "2011-01-07T03:20:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26586#comments:id=1281708",
        },
        {
            id = 1369307,
            score = 10,
            author = "423583",
            text = "Messner, Jargensen (Jorgensen), Krakauer and Danforth are also identified as members of the Baker Company, which was the name of Rambo's group.  I guess that makes the Redridge Orcs the Vietkong.",
            date = "2011-03-17T13:48:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26586#comments:id=1369307",
        },
        {
            id = 1202585,
            score = 8,
            author = "Ombree",
            text = "EPIC quest chain!",
            date = "2010-12-02T16:32:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26586#comments:id=1202585",
        },
        {
            id = 1208893,
            score = 7,
            author = "wharris",
            text = "Guide to Redridge Quests:\n\nDo these at any time:\nNida's Necklace (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26508)\nAn Unwelcome Guest (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26509)\nLake Everstill Cleanup (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26511)\nWanted: Redridge Gnolls (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26504)\nFranks and Beans (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26506)\nThreat to the Kingdom (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26761) (from Westfall chain)\n\nOptional prequest: Hero's Call: Redridge (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26365) or Hero's Call: Redridge (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28563)\nThen a long chain:\nStill Assessing the Threat (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26503)\nParker's Report (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26505)\nWe Must Prepare!  (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26510) (available earlier)\n        Completing the above enables: Like a Fart in the Wind (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26513)\nTuning the Gnomecoder (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26512)\nCanyon Romp (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26514)\n       A gnoll drops dirt-stained scroll (http://www.wowhead.com/item=58898) which allows for He Who Controls the Ettins (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26519) and Saving Foreman Oslow (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26520)\nThey've Wised Up (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26544)\nYowler Must Die! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26545)\nJohn J Keeshan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26567)\nThis Ain't My War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26568)\nWeapons of War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26571)\n       Accepting this enables  Render's Army (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26570) and Surveying Equipment (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26569)\nHis Heart Must Be In It (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26573)\nIn Search of Bravo Company (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26586)  (I'm not sure what the exact prerequisties are)\nBreaking out is hard to do (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26587)\nJorgensen (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26560)\nKrakauer (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26561)\nAnd Last but not Least...Danforth (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26562)\nReturn of the Bravo Company (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26563)\nThey Drew First Blood (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26607)\nIt's Never over (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26616)\n\nThen do these together:\nBravo Company Field Kit: Camouflage (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26636)\nBravo Company Field Kit: Chloroform (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26637)\nHunting the Hinters (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26638)\nPoint of Contact: Brubake (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26639)r and Unspeakable Atrocities (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26640)\n\n(Main chain Continues)\nPrisoners of War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26646)\nTo Win a War, You Gotta Become War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26651)\nDetonation (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26668)\n    (Shadowhide Extinction (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26692) now available)\nThe Dark Tower (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26693)\nThe Grand Magus Doane (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26694)\nAHHHHH! AHHHHHHHHHHHH! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26708)\nShowdown at Stonewatch (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26713)\nDarkblaze, Bood of the Worldbreaker (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26714)\nTriumphant Return (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26726)\n\nA truly epic chain!",
            date = "2010-12-05T18:41:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26586#comments:id=1208893",
        },
        {
            id = 1275199,
            score = -3,
            author = "753962",
            text = "Is this a battlefield: bad company reference?",
            date = "2011-01-03T13:21:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26586#comments:id=1275199",
        },
    },
    [26587] = {
        {
            id = 1213797,
            score = 68,
            author = "Khark",
            text = "Real easy to get that key. Run in, die, run in as a ghost, resurrect next to key, grab it and walk out.",
            date = "2010-12-08T03:19:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26587#comments:id=1213797",
        },
        {
            id = 1178889,
            score = 32,
            author = "Nui1",
            text = "When i finished this there was no follow up, but when i went to render's camp this npc poped out and starting following you with another quest [quest=26560 domain=www]\n\nedit: seems like he actually spawns on dismount",
            date = "2010-11-23T18:40:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26587#comments:id=1178889",
        },
        {
            id = 1378912,
            score = 24,
            author = "Zoraan",
            text = "Quest title is a reference to oldie goldie Breaking up is hard to do by Neil Sedaka.\nThe fact that this had not been mentioned earlier was quite shocking, but then again, I guess most WoW players don't listen to music from the fifties.",
            date = "2011-03-29T03:45:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26587#comments:id=1378912",
        },
        {
            id = 1467267,
            score = 18,
            author = "733706",
            text = "Well the previous comments pretty much explained the quest so let me add one thing in case you might have been thinking along the sames lines as myself.  My main is a lvl 85 Pally skinner and this quest didn't exist when he was the level for it. When my Warlock alt did the quest, it seemed like this might be a great place for the Pally to get leather, but I tried it-don't bother.\n\nSure, I went in there, aggroed most of the wolves at once and did them in real quick with the Pally's  Divine Storm.  But you can't loot 'em and you can't skin 'em. They just lay there in a white mist for a few moments, then vanish and respawn real quick.\n\nI wasted my time checking on this so you don't have to.  BTW, Neil Sedaka's \"Breaking Up Is Hard To Do\" was released in 1962 and hit number one on the pop charts in August of that year.",
            date = "2011-07-11T14:41:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26587#comments:id=1467267",
        },
        {
            id = 1372709,
            score = 17,
            author = "750237",
            text = "Good grief, it's not hard to do.\n\nThe den is oval shaped and the Den Captain rides up and down the middle.  Just follow his path down the middle and as long as you're not too close to him to aggro him, you'll be fine to walk.  You won't aggro the sleeping worgs.\n\nNo running, no death, no mounting, no lying down.....   just walk.",
            date = "2011-03-21T14:15:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26587#comments:id=1372709",
        },
    },
    [26589] = {
        {
            id = 2005404,
            score = 8,
            author = "1361840",
            text = "You can do both this quest and https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28510.\n1. Get https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28510 and hand it in first.\n2. Don't accept any further quest from Konu Runetotem.\n3. Now you can pick up this quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26589",
            date = "2014-09-23T14:11:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26589#comments:id=2005404",
        },
        {
            id = 1910396,
            score = 4,
            author = "joss002",
            text = "If you have  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28510 in your quest log,this quest wont show up.",
            date = "2013-10-20T08:31:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26589#comments:id=1910396",
        },
        {
