            score = 11,
            author = "wharris",
            text = "Guide to Redridge Quests:\n\nDo these at any time:\nNida's Necklace (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26508)\nAn Unwelcome Guest (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26509)\nLake Everstill Cleanup (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26511)\nWanted: Redridge Gnolls (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26504)\nFranks and Beans (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26506)\nThreat to the Kingdom (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26761) (from Westfall chain)\n\nOptional prequest: Hero's Call: Redridge (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26365) or Hero's Call: Redridge (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28563)\nThen a long chain:\nStill Assessing the Threat (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26503)\nParker's Report (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26505)\nWe Must Prepare!  (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26510) (available earlier)\n        Completing the above enables: Like a Fart in the Wind (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26513)\nTuning the Gnomecoder (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26512)\nCanyon Romp (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26514)\n       A gnoll drops dirt-stained scroll (http://www.wowhead.com/item=58898) which allows for He Who Controls the Ettins (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26519) and Saving Foreman Oslow (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26520)\nThey've Wised Up (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26544)\nYowler Must Die! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26545)\nJohn J Keeshan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26567)\nThis Ain't My War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26568)\nWeapons of War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26571)\n       Accepting this enables  Render's Army (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26570) and Surveying Equipment (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26569)\nHis Heart Must Be In It (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26573)\nIn Search of Bravo Company (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26586)  (I'm not sure what the exact prerequisties are)\nBreaking out is hard to do (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26587)\nJorgensen (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26560)\nKrakauer (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26561)\nAnd Last but not Least...Danforth (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26562)\nReturn of the Bravo Company (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26563)\nThey Drew First Blood (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26607)\nIt's Never over (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26616)\n\nThen do these together:\nBravo Company Field Kit: Camouflage (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26636)\nBravo Company Field Kit: Chloroform (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26637)\nHunting the Hinters (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26638)\nPoint of Contact: Brubake (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26639)r and Unspeakable Atrocities (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26640)\n\n(Main chain Continues)\nPrisoners of War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26646)\nTo Win a War, You Gotta Become War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26651)\nDetonation (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26668)\n    (Shadowhide Extinction (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26692) now available)\nThe Dark Tower (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26693)\nThe Grand Magus Doane (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26694)\nAHHHHH! AHHHHHHHHHHHH! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26708)\nShowdown at Stonewatch (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26713)\nDarkblaze, Bood of the Worldbreaker (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26714)\nTriumphant Return (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26726)\n\nA truly epic chain!",
            date = "2010-12-05T19:07:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26607#comments:id=1208953",
        },
        {
            id = 1319095,
            score = 9,
            author = "Quilan",
            text = "If nothing else gives away what this hole chain refrences, its this quest title:\nThis chain refrences Rambo, the Quest title is ALMOST the movie's name: First Blood. (But we all know blizz hates copy-right [I'm looking at you Lady La-La's necklace >.>]) John J. Keeshan is Rambo (Rambos first name was John and his middle name Initial was J.) And Troteman is refrencing Trautman, Rambo's commanding Officer.",
            date = "2011-02-02T08:06:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26607#comments:id=1319095",
        },
        {
            id = 5444924,
            score = 1,
            author = "glassleo",
            text = "To get this quest, you must complete both https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26573 and https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26563.",
            date = "2022-10-02T16:07:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26607#comments:id=5444924",
        },
    },
    [26609] = {
        {
            id = 1512052,
            score = 44,
            author = "Rhynchelma",
            text = "Researched some more. You have to do at least one of the chains below in order to make this quest available.\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=26599 to https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26601\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=26603 to https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26606\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=26593 to https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26595\n\nThere are no more quests obviously available that could be another trigger but, knowing Blizzard, who knows?\n\nRewritten for today's web syntax.",
            date = "2011-09-07T11:59:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26609#comments:id=1512052",
        },
        {
            id = 1497168,
            score = 30,
            author = "error10",
            text = "I have several level 85 alts who have never set foot in Booty Bay, so I did some experimenting.\n\nOn one alt I picked up https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26599 and did that chain through its end, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26601. I never touched https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26603. When I completed it, I was able to pick up this quest. The quests in this chain granted reputation with Booty Bay and removed reputation from Bloodsail Buccaneers.\n\nOn the other alt I picked up https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26603 and did that chain through its end, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26606. I never touched https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26599. When I completed it, I was able to pick up this quest. The quests in this chain granted no reputation.\n\nTL;DR: To become eligible for this quest, you can do either quest chain. If you're going for Insane in the Membrane, you would be better off with the https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26603 chain.",
            date = "2011-08-17T15:54:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26609#comments:id=1497168",
        },
        {
            id = 1201200,
            score = 7,
            author = "albacore",
            text = "When doing this quest be sure to kill \"Good-Boy\" Bruce (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=43454), who is located right by the Bloodsail Correspondence, and loot Weather-Beaten Coin (http://www.wowhead.com/item=59143) to start the quest An Old Sea Dog (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26617).",
            date = "2010-12-01T22:23:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26609#comments:id=1201200",
        },
        {
            id = 1474499,
            score = 5,
            author = "gtadem",
            text = "I can verify that the Message in a Bottle chain is what unlocks this quest. Odd considering the two are completely unrelated. That said, when doing the captain's chest quest, you're right there on the beach where the bottles are anyways. Don't be like me and run back to BB before doing so. Of course, if you're reading this, chances are you already have.",
            date = "2011-07-19T21:16:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26609#comments:id=1474499",
        },
        {
            id = 1186140,
            score = 2,
            author = "378554",
            text = "First Mate Crazz will offer this quest after completing both of the quests offered by \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2501)",
            date = "2010-11-25T22:37:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26609#comments:id=1186140",
        },
    },
