        {
            id = 1179373,
            score = 89,
            author = "koax",
            text = "Not exactly a prereq but a sub quest for Seeing Where Your Loyalties Lie (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26629).\n\nAlso:\nThe Oversized Pirate Hat (http://www.wowhead.com/item=59148) is available from Narkk (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2663) in the Old Port Authority.\nThe Cow Head (http://www.wowhead.com/item=59147) is from \"Doing to deed\" on Bossy (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=43505), second floor of the building with the Leatherworking Supplier (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2699)",
            date = "2010-11-23T21:57:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26630#comments:id=1179373",
        },
        {
            id = 1195090,
            score = 65,
            author = "366196",
            text = "Bossy, I need to ask something great of you. I need yo cut off your head to prove my loyalty to the bloodsail Buccaneers, so they will allow me to infiltrate their ranks and hopefully discover their true intentions. Booty Bay needs you, Bossy...now more than ever.\n\nMoo.\n\nBoth options let you choose between the following:\n Do the deed. --->Cow head.\nChicken out.----->Bossy breathes a heavy sigh of relief.",
            date = "2010-11-29T05:53:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26630#comments:id=1195090",
        },
    },
    [26631] = {
        {
            id = 1395633,
            score = 10,
            author = "Krater",
            text = "I had this same problem.  Got the quest and then headed over to the ship.  My mini-map had the '?' on it but Capt. Keelhaul didn't.  He was also red but not aggressive and I couldn't attack him or any of the other pirates.  I logged out and then back in and then he had the '?' but was still red to me.\n\nI dropped the quest and got it again, same result.  Did that a couple times, still no change.\n\nI came to this thread and saw the post from a rogue name Erum and he said he logged out and logged back in and the pirates were then friendly.  Others talked about disabling addons and then trying it.\n\nFirst, I disabled my addons and then logged in and out multiple times - and it worked.  The pirates were then friendly to me.  I wondered if it truly was my addons (I don't run anything exotic - bartender, recount, omen, dbm) so I logged out and enabled them again.  On logging back in the pirates were red.  I then logged in and out a couple times and got them to be friendly to me again, so it wasn't my addons.\n\nSo, in summary: if the pirates aren't friendly to you just spam logging out and back in until they are.  Addons don't seem to be causing this.  That's what worked for me.",
            date = "2011-04-20T11:34:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26631#comments:id=1395633",
        },
        {
            id = 1342437,
            score = 9,
            author = "438814",
            text = "After reading whole quest line, i rofled so hard upon laying eyes on the quest item given. \"Yer Papers\" God I love pirates.",
            date = "2011-02-19T15:50:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26631#comments:id=1342437",
        },
        {
            id = 1646512,
            score = 5,
            author = "56301",
            text = "For those who still have the silly reputation bug: Simply grab a mount and fly to the nearest zone, causing you to loose the \"Piracy\" buff. I recommend the southern part of Stranglethorn Vale (The sea where you get fatigue) as that's nearest.",
            date = "2012-03-30T06:19:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26631#comments:id=1646512",
        },
        {
            id = 1207513,
            score = 4,
            author = "488143",
            text = "neither reputation gained nor lost",
            date = "2010-12-05T04:24:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26631#comments:id=1207513",
        },
        {
            id = 1330710,
            score = 3,
            author = "541996",
            text = "I was having the same problem. I tried it again after turning off all of my Addons and logging back into WoW and it work for me. don't know if this will help anyone out or not.",
            date = "2011-02-10T16:19:23-06:00",
