    [26678] = {
        {
            id = 1206158,
            score = 69,
            author = "Henderman",
            text = "The doublerum is in a barrel in a bedroom on the 2nd floor of the Tavern.",
            date = "2010-12-04T13:19:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26678#comments:id=1206158",
        },
        {
            id = 1485830,
            score = 22,
            author = "859950",
            text = "anyone knows why im not phasing when i get Doublerum?\n\nEdit: Found out my problem, you have to turn in Doublerum at the barrel to \"phase out\" (:\nNow i can start to farm Bloodsail rep *-*",
            date = "2011-08-02T18:05:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26678#comments:id=1485830",
        },
        {
            id = 1508681,
            score = 21,
            author = "eskilajnen",
            text = "Reputation gains from killing named NPC's stop at 11999/12000 into honored when you are in this phase.",
            date = "2011-09-02T08:10:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26678#comments:id=1508681",
        },
        {
            id = 1500590,
            score = 9,
            author = "Jollygood",
            text = "I'm one shotting everyone right now. No AoE. Bruisers are still level 35 and give no rep.  Revilgaz took two shots, bless his green heart. Make sure to nail the bruisers first or they shoot you to the point where you can only move away from them. The damage is miniscule, but you can't move except to swim away from them.\n\nETA - after re-reading the discussions, here's a listing. I am only going to list Bloodsail rep gains. Assume the damage to Steamwheedle Cartel reps is 5 times the Bloodsail gain for Booty Bay and 2 or 3 times for the others. Everyone gives you 5 Bloodsail rep points except these guys:\n\nAuctioneers: 0, plus they will mark you for PvP for 5 minutes.\nBaron Revilgaz: 25\nBrashtide Raiders: 0, but they all have loot like fabric, cheese, and so on.\nBruisers: 0, but after my abortive attempts at killing them at 85, it feels kinda good.\nGoldgrubber brothers (2 bankers): 25 each\nGringer, Horde flight master: Will kill you. If you do nail him, 0 rep and marked PvP. Watch your tab targeting on his flight deck.\nGrizzlowe: 25\nWharfmaster Lozgil: 15\n\nIf you want to drop your guild banner, I suggest the plank leading to the bank is the place to do it. You have a 45 yard range and 2 minutes. If you are a caster, you can cast as far as your range and if you are near the banner, you get credit. I was getting 31 on a gnome exalted with the guild for the Goldgrubbers and the Baron. Your key area is the Goldgrubbers at the bank and the Baron. Hit the V key to get the big red health banners over them for visibility. Nail the Goldgrubbers (31)and Joad(6) first, then hit the Baron(31), then Seahorn(6). Keep an eye on the Goldgrubbers and the Baron the whole time. You can also get credit for the guy in the doorway across from Seahorn, the guy next to Gringer the Horde Flight master (watch your tab targeting if you are Alliance!), and the five NPCs in the inn within the radius. But always keep an eye on the Baron. I was lucky enough to get him twice on one go of the banner, which tells me that the respawn rate in the phased area is a little more zesty than in the normal situation.\n\nI started by alternating between Booty Bay and the pirates cove in Tanaris to try to stay at least neutral with the cartel, but realized there is a maximum any faction can hate you, so it is more time efficient to just plow all the way through to exalted with the pirates and totally hated with the Steamwheedle guys, then go over to Tanaris, Venture Bay, whatever, and grind there later. I'm actually going to pony up for a race change to human to do that next month.\n\nA complete side note is that I am doing quests in Netherstorm and the goblins there are not at all related to the Steamwheedle Cartel.",
            date = "2011-08-22T01:09:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26678#comments:id=1500590",
        },
        {
            id = 1530709,
            score = 9,
            author = "Wellard",
            text = "I have the quest and I am phased, all was going well and I had successfully grinded a few k rep, then a level 85 bruiser came out of nowhere and killed me. After I respawned, there were 2 of them. This is making it impossible for me to efficiently grind rep here. Has any one else had this problem?\n\nEdit:\n\nI was told earlier tonight by a GM that as of 4.2 level 85 bruisers will spawn as well as the level 35 bruisers.\n\nEdit 2:\n\nAfter the server shutdown last night, no level 85 bruisers have spawned. So it appears that it was just a bug and the information the GM gave me was false.\n\nOn another note, the rogue trainer Ian Storm (40.5 73.5) appears to be dead, but really he is not! You can still kill him and gain Bloodsail reputation. Those damn sneaky rogues!\n\nI also found that grinding Steamwheedle Cartel reputation was extremely efficient on the boat in the middle of Booty Bay. The Bloodsail Corsairs normally respawn within seconds. You can run around the boat and never have to stop and wait for respawns or move to another location.\n\nEdited on the 15th of July 2012 to fix a few typos.",
            date = "2011-09-29T07:45:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26678#comments:id=1530709",
        },
    },
    [26679] = {
        {
            id = 1571047,
            score = 24,
            author = "804053",
            text = "This quest causes you to be phased. It should be noted that ALL BOOTY BAY BRUISERS in Booty Bay will be level 35 non-elites for the duration of this quest, allowing you to kill the citizens of Booty Bay without fear of being killed.\n\nThis is very advantageous for those going for the https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=2336 achievement (and also https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=871). Just AoE the Booty Bay people (the bruisers will still use their nets on you) and you'll get fast rep.\n\nAlso note that killing any of the pirates attacking Booty Bay will not affect your rep, so feel free to spam AoEs all over.",
            date = "2011-11-13T08:44:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26679#comments:id=1571047",
        },
        {
            id = 1617135,
            score = 22,
            author = "Qoko",
            text = "Everyone that wants to max out both the Bloodsail and Cartel rep to Exalted, do NOT grind your Honored rep during this quest, but continue. Made an overview on the [faction=87] comments.",
            date = "2012-01-26T11:38:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26679#comments:id=1617135",
        },
        {
            id = 1964853,
            score = 22,
            author = "Constantime",
            text = "I had started this quest to get phased so that it would be easier to farm Bloodsail rep.  Once I got to honored (I'm going for the Insane Title), I went looking for the pirates south of Booty Bay to get the quest to get my Bloodsail Admiral Title.  Upon arriving at the ship, the quest giver along with all of the other pirates would phase away.  Because I was now hated with Booty Bay, I could no longer turn in this quest to try and ending the phasing.\n\nI discovered that besides the ship in the Booty Bay Harbor, there is another ship out front of Booty Bay by the island with the large statue, that was not phased for me and had the quest/ quest giver I needed.  Picked it up, did a few small things and got my Achev.\n\nHope this helps for anyone stuck wonder where to get their quest.",
            date = "2014-05-12T10:51:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26679#comments:id=1964853",
        },
        {
            id = 2293070,
            score = 11,
            author = "1099629",
            text = "To be clear (since I spent a while trying to figure out if I could turn this in to finish loremaster), the phasing starts when you turn in the previous quest, and does not end if you turn in this one (the followups involve kicking the Bloodsail out of Booty Bay). You do not need this quest in your log to be phased.",
            date = "2015-12-29T09:09:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26679#comments:id=2293070",
        },
        {
            id = 1609772,
            score = 10,
            author = "858144",
            text = "Killing the low level Booty Bay bruisers while the area is phased no longer gives Bloodsail reputation.\n\nThe booty bay bruisers in the phased area never gave reputation. Reputation comes from the various named NPCs.",
            date = "2012-01-10T14:44:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26679#comments:id=1609772",
        },
    },
