            text = "These humorous quest lines continue because the Bloodsail brought https://www.wowhead.com/npc=43560 to fight, as well.  You can see him floating in the bay, like he's almost guiding the incoming Bloodsail where to attack.  XD",
            date = "2011-11-14T13:21:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26698#comments:id=1572048",
        },
    },
    [26699] = {
        {
            id = 1198681,
            score = 12,
            author = "196807",
            text = "Completing this quest (and killing all the stuff required) does not decrease your reputation with the Bloodsail Buccaneers.\n\nThis might change in the future though. Currently, killing the Bloodsail Raiders doesn't drop rep with BSB, but killing the Bloodsail Corsairs do.",
            date = "2010-11-30T19:44:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26699#comments:id=1198681",
        },
        {
            id = 1522261,
            score = 5,
            author = "gajackson",
            text = "for anyone stopping in BEFORE completing this/choosing a reward:\n\nto the best of my knowledge (and going through threads here & on other sites), Revilgaz's Cutlass is a *unique* cutlass/sword model in game. There are scimitars, rapiers, etc. but ONLY this one looks like this.\n\nSo if you are a sword-wielder, consider that, esp. with 4.3 on the way. I am praying I haven't done the quest yet on my rogue, because I am trying to 'mog him into a cavalier/ city-duelist type - but not a pirate/swashbuckler. This is a perfect main-hand model; I just need some kind of main-gauche and a proper Musketeers-style plumed hat. :)\n\nupdate: I tried checking both Rev & Seahorn, but both only had flavor-text comments. I figured I had just done them a long time ago, and forgot.\n\nThen, I found out there are pre-req quests: you will need to first do \"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley (2 quests) and First Mate Crazz's tasks. Also, while doing these, you will be given a reward option of a Pirate's Musket ([item=61576 domain=www] ; a model you won't see again until lvl 63).\n\nFrom what I can tell, this whole questline has been re-written/re-tuned, so don't get that 'Ugh! Not this stuff again!' feeling, if you did it on another character a long time ago.",
            date = "2011-09-19T23:51:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26699#comments:id=1522261",
        },
        {
            id = 1641628,
            score = 4,
            author = "364030",
            text = "To get this quest you must do all the Bloodsail pirate infiltration quests and trigger the invasion event in BB.\n\nYou need to do all the quests it outlines on the link below, and TURN IN the quest \"Return to Revilgaz\". Soon after, Fleet Master Seahorn will give you \"Turning the Brashtide\".\n\n[guide=183 domain=www]",
            date = "2012-03-19T20:30:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26699#comments:id=1641628",
        },
        {
            id = 1500167,
            score = 2,
            author = "Wormag",
            text = "Probably one of the most fun quests in Booty Bay.\nNote: The guards in this phase seem to be only level 35 which may make it easier to kill them if you're looking to get the Bloodsail title.",
            date = "2011-08-21T12:31:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26699#comments:id=1500167",
        },
        {
            id = 1680264,
            score = 1,
            author = "Plutofour",
            text = "i am trying to figure out the /script for the music during this quest i love it so much. all i seem to be coming up with is this so far\n\n/script PlaySoundFile(\"Sound\\\\Music\\\\Cataclysm\\\\MUS_PiratesSurrender_UU01.mp3\")\n\nit's still pretty awesome sounding but i don't think it's the exact sound file from the actual invasion.\n\nany help would be awesome. Enjoy the first /script XD\n\nTurns out i got the script command correct! XD",
            date = "2012-06-23T15:41:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26699#comments:id=1680264",
        },
    },
    [26700] = {
        {
            id = 1185596,
            score = 30,
            author = "SubjectV",
            text = "Use the ropes on the ground next to Fleet Master Seahorn to swing over. When you want to leave the boat, use the ropes on the deck to swing back. Very easy. :)",
            date = "2010-11-25T17:59:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26700#comments:id=1185596",
        },
        {
            id = 1190513,
            score = 17,
            author = "447611",
            text = "I loved this quest. Was a great story line and you dont get to see Booty Bay blasted very often. To get on the boat, just walk the mast behind the goblin fleet master and kill away. To get off, click on the rope on the deck and you will swing over like Tarzan.\n\nEdit: to get on the ship, there is also the rope just to the left of Fleet Master Seahorn.",
            date = "2010-11-27T13:15:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26700#comments:id=1190513",
        },
        {
            id = 1437142,
            score = 17,
            author = "Vlad",
            text = "If you have https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26700 what I found to be the best way to farm reputation for [faction=21]+[faction=577]+[faction=369]+[faction=470] at once was to stand on the boat in the middle of Booty Bay and simply kill the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=43726 as long as you can, here are my estimations (did this on my feral Druid, note that I had Cat Form and ran at 130% speed, so 30% quicker than other classes):\n\n[pre]    0%                        5 (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=78634)%       1 (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=78635)0 (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=20599)%       1 (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=78634)5 (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=20599)%       2 (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=78635)0 (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=20599)%\n    0.83 rep a second         0.87      0.91      0.95      0.99\n   49.45 rep a minute        51.93     54.40     56.87     59.35\n 2967.38 rep an hour       3115.75   3264.12   3412.49   3560.86\n 5934.76 rep per 2 hours   6231.50   6528.24   6824.98   7121.71\n11869.53 rep per 4 hours  12463.01  13056.48  13649.96  14243.44\n23739.05 rep per 8 hours  24926.01  26112.96  27299.91  28486.86\n\nWith 0% these are the following estimations:\nHonored->Revered: 12000 rep takes roughly  4 hours and 2 minutes\nHonored->Exalted: 33000 rep takes roughly 11 hours and 7 minutes\nRevered->Exalted: 21000 rep takes roughly  7 hours and 4 minutes[/pre]\nMy sample size was 10 minutes of farming like this, constantly running and killing as they spawn, they spawn quite quickly since they are quest mobs.",
            date = "2011-06-08T15:14:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26700#comments:id=1437142",
        },
        {
            id = 1369281,
            score = 16,
            author = "721249",
            text = "Wow, what fun!\n\nBooty Bay in flames! Pirates swarming through the town!\n\nThis Alli Worgen got to fly a Horde Windrider... it doesn't get much better than this.",
            date = "2011-03-17T12:47:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26700#comments:id=1369281",
        },
        {
            id = 1203004,
            score = 6,
            author = "vorlash",
            text = "This is a fantastic way to farm some goblin rep, the corsairs give faction with everything but Booty Bay.  They respawn fast enough that it's a constant stream.",
            date = "2010-12-02T21:19:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26700#comments:id=1203004",
        },
    },
    [26701] = {
        {
            id = 2609970,
            score = 16,
            author = "Maricka",
            text = "You can do both quests, just follow the instructions below:\n\n1) Accept Warchief's Command: Dustwallow Marsh! (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28554/warchiefs-command-dustwallow-marsh) from board.\n2) Turn it in to Krog, BUT DO NOT accept any further quest from him.\n3) Fly back to Ratchet and accept Flight to Brackenwall (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26701/flight-to-brackenwall) from Gazlowe.\n4) Fly back to Brackenwall and turn it in to Krog.\n\nDone!",
            date = "2018-09-04T07:31:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26701#comments:id=2609970",
        },
        {
            id = 1302537,
            score = 7,
            author = "768077",
            text = "This is another of those quests that ties in with the Warchief's Command quests from the Message Boards in the cities....Upon turning that in you will still be able to get \"A Shambling Threat\".",
            date = "2011-01-21T01:48:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26701#comments:id=1302537",
        },
    },
    [26702] = {
        {
            id = 1716558,
            score = 57,
            author = "1034881",
            text = "There is a way to complete the quests after Theramore's Fall Scenario... You have to go out to the long bridge out of Theramore to the west, once you cross the bridge look to the right and talk to the Keeper of Time, her name is Zidormi. She will give you the option to go back into time before the destruction happened, and all the NPC's will be back. You have the option to revisit her and bring Theramore back to present time as well.\n\nHope this helps anyone that was working on Loremaster, and Kalimdor achievements.",
            date = "2012-09-21T02:44:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26702#comments:id=1716558",
        },
        {
            id = 1301552,
            score = 31,
            author = "ahac",
            text = "You won't be able to pick this up (and get the free flight) if you also have https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28552 in your quest log.",
            date = "2011-01-20T08:23:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26702#comments:id=1301552",
