    [26814] = {
        {
            id = 1405121,
            score = 74,
            author = "Emalethx2",
            text = "I found that the quests were not so much bugged, as the npcs were set up to spawn when you enter a certain way ie run through the door. So if you're like me, an 85 after loremaster, or just checking out the new quests, and you try flying over the walls, the npcs don't spawn properly.\n\nJust retrace your steps and voilà, we have NPC takedown :p",
            date = "2011-04-30T13:24:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26814#comments:id=1405121",
        },
        {
            id = 1480432,
            score = 41,
            author = "Apolocyntosis",
            text = "Rope Ladder died.\n\nWat.",
            date = "2011-07-26T22:00:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26814#comments:id=1480432",
        },
        {
            id = 1820621,
            score = 29,
            author = "1103260",
            text = "Since no one else explained this fight in its entirety, here I go.\n\nWalk straight ahead from where the portal deposited you.  You'll see a bunch of critter snakes on the ground and a troll on a stone bed on a raised platform.  That troll's Venoxis.  Zanzil shows up for round 2.\n\nYour job is to kill Venoxis.  Zanzil's job is to heal Venoxis to full, while halfheartedly burning you down and occasionally hiding like a chicken to heal.  First to achieve objective wins.  Venoxis's job is to lie there and be a target.\n\nIf you're high level, don't kill Venoxis until Zanzil's had a few seconds to get going, or you'll bug the quest.  Lowbies don't need to worry about this.\n\nZanzil throws potions at the snakes to turn them into bigger snakes that go up to Venoxis, cast heal, and die.  If you don't want Venoxis healed, then burning down the snakes is a priority.  Burning down Zanzil temporarily removes a damage source and stops the snakes from spawning, but he'll be back.  This is a very difficult fight to solo at level, unless you bring a mage, in which case you just sheep Zanzil and burn (freeze?) Venoxis down with impunity.  Other classes' cc might also work.\n\nNone of this matters.\n\nHexxar shows up when Venoxis is either at 1 hp or at full.  Success or failure means nothing, and you can just hide and twiddle your thumbs while Venoxis gets healed and you'll still be just as good off.  Hexxar grabs you in a strangulation plot-spell, does some \"kill the hero\" bond villain speech, and some questgivers from before whose names we never bothered to memorize show up with an airship and a ladder to pull you to safety before you get killed.\n\nThe ONLY THING you have to do is grab the ladder.  That's all.  That's all it takes to complete the quest.\n\n(Actually, you complete it either way, but grabbing the ladder keeps you from waking up in a 6ft bed with the Angel of Failure wondering how much you had to drink 10 seconds ago.)",
            date = "2013-03-03T19:19:05-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26814#comments:id=1820621",
        },
        {
            id = 1189614,
            score = 26,
            author = "485266",
            text = "Failing to grab the ladder at the conclusion of this quest leads to Jin'do nuking you pretty hard:\n\nShade of the Hexxer's Jin'do's Rage hits for 33466 Shadow. (69312 Resisted) (590338 Overkill)\n\nSo yeah he nukes you for 700k. One wonders why he didn't do that back at level 60!\nNote that dying to this attack still means you've completed the quest, you just have to take an unnecessary 10% durability loss and a short graveyard run.",
            date = "2010-11-27T04:56:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26814#comments:id=1189614",
        },
        {
            id = 2548286,
            score = 23,
            author = "Vafthrudnir",
            text = "Tried this at least 4-5 times today just to see if anything would change, and it looks like it's now actually impossible to grab the ladder at the end. He finishes his cast way before the ladder gets anywhere close to you. There's no way to avoid getting one shotted.\n\nThe quest completes either way and you can use the quest item to teleport directly to the quest giver so it's not a super big deal, just a weird ending to the questline.",
            date = "2018-01-25T09:56:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26814#comments:id=2548286",
        },
    },
