            date = "2011-02-12T07:09:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27000#comments:id=1332885",
        },
        {
            id = 1378620,
            score = 5,
            author = "Trolled",
            text = "Mount horse.\nRun south.\nSmash 1, Smash Tab, Repeat 25 times.\nTurn in quest.\n\nBeautiful.",
            date = "2011-03-28T18:58:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27000#comments:id=1378620",
        },
    },
    [27001] = {
        {
            id = 1193042,
            score = 50,
            author = "Hourglass",
            text = "You also simply tag the spiders with any attack, and kite them up to the NPCs.  Faster that using the horse.",
            date = "2010-11-28T10:25:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27001#comments:id=1193042",
        },
        {
            id = 1194422,
            score = 26,
            author = "32411",
            text = "After you complete the quest, you are allowed to stay on the horse given and ride up to Hearthglen (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27002). Something to note though, is that you can actually ride indoors with it, right up to Highlord Tirion Fordring himself.\n\nI found this to be a comforting tidbit, given that Fordring's dialogue seems to suggest that he has completely forgotten that only three years ago I was there with him when he killed Arthas. Apparently, my slaying of the Lich King makes me a \"promising recruit\".",
            date = "2010-11-28T21:13:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27001#comments:id=1194422",
        },
        {
            id = 1259249,
            score = 22,
            author = "Deltethnia",
            text = "You, people in your party, others in the area regardless of faction; it doesn't matter WHO lures the spiders to the mill. You will get credit for any and ALL spiders lured and killed by the NPCs so long as you are near/at the mill when the spiders are killed. If there is someone else in the area on the quest you can simply accept the quest and sit there and let them lure the spiders for you. Easiest quest EVAR!",
            date = "2010-12-26T02:43:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27001#comments:id=1259249",
        },
        {
            id = 1182132,
            score = 16,
            author = "458239",
            text = "You can't mount the horses while mounted.  Doing so makes the horse disappear.",
            date = "2010-11-24T15:47:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27001#comments:id=1182132",
        },
        {
            id = 1428954,
            score = 13,
            author = "darthveda",
            text = "Why couldn't one just, you know... kill the spiders?  Or hey, we've got four buddies too... we could all kill the whole forest faster than it takes to do this quest...\n\nI guess variety is the spice of life?",
            date = "2011-05-27T21:18:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27001#comments:id=1428954",
        },
    },
    [27002] = {
        {
            id = 1260046,
            score = 34,
            author = "SPF18",
            text = "\"What? You say you killed the Lich King? Oh, and you were involved with redeeming my son? Funny, I don't remember that at all!\"",
            date = "2010-12-26T13:21:09-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27002#comments:id=1260046",
        },
        {
            id = 1199195,
            score = 18,
            author = "302325",
            text = "Apparently being exalted with his Argent Crusade doesn't keep Tirion from calling me young and a \"new recruit\". Hmph!\n\nNathaniel here offers for you to continue on his mustang up to Hearthglen to meet with Tirion, do it, even at level 80+. The mount really is a fast mount, and more importantly, the mount allows you to stay mounted even inside Mardenholde Keep where you will find the Highlord.",
            date = "2010-12-01T01:51:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27002#comments:id=1199195",
        },
        {
            id = 1664083,
            score = 15,
            author = "894609",
            text = "If you're having trouble finding the guy, as you enter Mardenholde Keep, make a right, left, left - go up the stairs in the slightly larger room you're in, turn left, then an immediate right, up a small ramp, and enter the door on your right. He's in that larger room with another quest giver.",
            date = "2012-05-08T00:08:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27002#comments:id=1664083",
        },
        {
            id = 1501603,
            score = 14,
            author = "863449",
            text = "This quest unlocks https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27151",
            date = "2011-08-23T08:51:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27002#comments:id=1501603",
        },
        {
            id = 1243356,
            score = 3,
            author = "487694",
            text = "This is about the only opportunity you'll get to ride around a castle without being dismounted.",
            date = "2010-12-18T13:48:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27002#comments:id=1243356",
        },
    },
    [27011] = {
        {
            id = 1194479,
            score = 7,
            author = "Seprest",
            text = "SHE PLANTED THEM ON THE GNOL......---- (smashed with a bread roller)",
            date = "2010-11-28T21:48:42-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27011#comments:id=1194479",
        },
        {
            id = 1867811,
            score = 5,
            author = "Aardum",
            text = "There's some nice bit of lore here. The progress text says \"Some of the older lumberjacks tell me that the Redpine lived in the area several years ago, but left when the plague arrived.\" Thus, (1) some of the lumberjacks who have returned to this area after the Scourge are original Lordaeronians, now working together with the Argent Crusade, (2) the Redpine Gnoll have managed to avoid the Scourge and survive it somewhere, only to return to the Northridge area later. Nice, and I'm happy for the Lordaeronian survivors, out of the Forsaken's reach as Argent Crusaders :)",
            date = "2013-06-17T22:58:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27011#comments:id=1867811",
        },
    },
    [27012] = {
        {
            id = 1385618,
            score = 12,
            author = "Ithuraen",
            text = "She doesn't want the gnoll's stealing her lumber, but she asks you to steal their weapons. She doesn't want to kill them either... but the only way to get their weapons is to pry it from their cold dead hands.\n\nSounds like your average justification for war throughout history (for both sides).",
            date = "2011-04-06T14:52:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27012#comments:id=1385618",
        },
        {
            id = 1692949,
            score = 12,
            author = "206461",
            text = "I don't want to order some sort of mass gnoll genocide because of a mother's worries.\n\nUhh...yeah...wouldn't want that. I'm gonna go.",
            date = "2012-07-27T21:07:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27012#comments:id=1692949",
        },
    },
