    [27098] = {
        {
            id = 1190106,
            score = 59,
            author = "711068",
            text = "Uploaded a Vid to Youtube of this Epic Quest (And its Pre-Quest)\nFor those that want to view it again, or simply havent done it but like the lore.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QTJ-0kKF0fg&hd=1\n\n1080p is available and Preferable to watch.\n\nEnjoy!",
            date = "2010-11-27T10:02:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27098#comments:id=1190106",
        },
        {
            id = 1186010,
            score = 49,
            author = "106237",
            text = "Honestly, one of the quest i enjoyed most in 6 years of WoW, simple as it is. And let's face it, the way she just shoots a worgen here and there like it's nothing is badass.",
            date = "2010-11-25T21:30:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27098#comments:id=1186010",
        },
        {
            id = 1098566,
            score = 46,
            author = "nihmue",
            text = "On the ride, Sylvanas will narrate her and Lordaeron's story to you in voice, quite spectacular.",
            date = "2010-08-10T12:38:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27098#comments:id=1098566",
        },
        {
            id = 1210606,
            score = 37,
            author = "710728",
            text = "Quest Lordaeron\n\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says:\n\nI have not always been the Banshee Queen.\nAnd my peopel have not always been the forsaken.\nLong ago this land comprised the northern kingdoms of Lordaeron, ruled by King Terenas Menethil.\nTerenas had a son named Arthas.\nArthas... even saying his name makes my body quiver in rage.\nThis man-child, Arthas, took for himself a cursed blade known as Frostmourne.\nThrough Frostmourne, arthas killed his own father and razed this land along with every living creature in it!\nMy own death came at the hands of Arthas when he and his armies sacked my homeland, Quel'Thalas, and murdered my people.\nIn his vast cruelty, Arthas severed my spirit from my body and raised me as a banshee to serve in his Scourage army.\nA similar fate befell all that would die to the Scourage war machine.\nIn death, they were reborn as mindless undead.\nBut Arthas was not invincible! With each passing day his power waned-his grip over the will of the damned loosening.\nIt was when Arthas was at his weakest that I struck!\nand though the hour of his atonement had come, the worm managed to escape his fate, returning to the frozen wastes of Northrend.\nWith Arthas gone, so too was the control he held over the undead masses of Lordaeron. After recovering my body, I freed the remaining Scourage that were left behind.\nFrom the cruelty and mercilessness of Arthas, the man who would be the Lich King, the Forsaken were born.\nOur goal... Our sole purpose was to destroy the Lich King. We threw our lot in with the Horde and began our journey towards redemption.\nNow the Lich King is ead and we have returned.\nThe peopel who called this land their home in life, do so in death as well.\nBut the alliance does not recognize our rights. They claim this land is their own while attempting to invalidate the claims of the founders of this kingdom.\nI will never allow it.... Never!\nLordaeron belongs to the Forsaken - always and forever.",
            date = "2010-12-06T17:48:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27098#comments:id=1210606",
        },
        {
            id = 6260497,
            score = 36,
            author = "NapalmDawn",
            text = "Here's some notes.  If you have the rep with UC, there is a UC quartermaster on the ramparts above the portal area in org.  Essentially, on the upper area of the front door to Org.  If you need to complete the quest, go see Zidormi outside UC.  Ask her to show you the old version of the area and ALL of the area goes back before the blight, not just UC.  You can then go here [npc=1500 domain=www] which has some quests.  Do them until he sends you to \"Speak with Sevren.  Then go do his chain which leads to the Bulwark, Voss and then back to Brill. Do the \"Warchief Cometh\" quest to go to the Forsaken High Command.  Then do all the quests out there.  Eventually you deliver a report to Sylvanas,\n\nThat report is the next set of breadcrumbs.  It leads to the rear guard.  DO the quests there in the boat area and the spider area. You'll also need to do the Ettin quest to.  You then get sent back to Sylvanas. SHe has you go do a few quests on Fenris island When you turn them in, it FINALLY leads to the \"Lordaeron\" quest which gives you the decor.\n\nMy main was able to see the vendor in Org. Some other toons weren't.  My hunter, which had done the Sylvanas transmog chain was able to ask Zidormi for the change back to old UC. Some of my others toons could not get her to offer that.\n\nI can't recall if the vendor was sitting atop Org prior to me doing the chain on my hunter to get the decor but he was there when it was done even with UC being in old mode (no mist).",
            date = "2026-01-11T22:15:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27098#comments:id=6260497",
        },
    },
    [27099] = {
        {
            id = 1423128,
            score = 64,
            author = "faerieevenstar",
            text = "I accidentally skipped the cinematic once on this quest, and panicked wondering how to finish the quest, but if you leave the room and re-enter, they appear all over again for you. Phew.\n\nBut you don't seem to be able to do the quest without watching the cinematic for the bit where Agatha yells \"run!\" and carries you away... she won't carry you away if you didn't watch it!\n\nEDIT: I just saw Androidus's comment. It did work for me just leaving the room and re-entering, so perhaps they fixed the bug. I didn't need to ticket a GM. :)",
            date = "2011-05-20T08:54:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27099#comments:id=1423128",
        },
        {
            id = 1190947,
            score = 60,
            author = "89046",
            text = "The ride back was kinda awkward with the valkyr thong in your face the whole time",
            date = "2010-11-27T16:23:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27099#comments:id=1190947",
        },
        {
            id = 1192249,
            score = 29,
            author = "77279",
            text = "+++9000 to Blizzard for these awesome quests. I love the cutscenes and such a great companion to the Worgen levelling quests on the beta.",
            date = "2010-11-28T03:21:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27099#comments:id=1192249",
        },
        {
            id = 1277347,
            score = 26,
            author = "Sketchie",
            text = "This is what happens when you enter the main room in the Fenris Keep:\n\nYou and Agatha automatically move into position in the room once you enter. Lord Darius Crowley and Ivar are facing towards Magistrate Henry Maleb and several random human NPCs.\n\nAgatha says: This way, . We will take them by surprise.\nLord Darius Crowley says: The Forsaken have broken through your defenses, magistrate.\nLord Darius Crowley says: You are out of time.\nLord Darius Crowley says: A decision must be made!\nLord Darius Crowley says: Die in battle and be raised as a servant of the Forsaken or...\nLord Darius Crowley says: Drink in my blood and reborn as worgen, immune to the depravity of the Forsaken.\nLord Darius Crowley says: Help us destroy the Forsaken and retake Lordaeron for the Alliance!\nMagistrate Henry Maleb says: We would rather die than be turned into worgen, but seeing as how even death provides no relief from the atrocities of this war...\nMagistrate Henry Maleb says: We choose vengeance!\nAll the humans, including Magistrate Henry Maleb, drinks the worgen blood and are transformed into worgen.\nAgatha says: Run...\nAgatha says: RUN!\nAgatha picks you up and flies back to the Banshee Queen quickly.",
            date = "2011-01-04T16:18:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27099#comments:id=1277347",
        },
        {
            id = 2855914,
            score = 25,
            author = "mudplayerx",
            text = "Do not cancel the cutscene or you won't get credit and have to watch it all over again.",
            date = "2018-12-01T23:10:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27099#comments:id=2855914",
        },
    },
    [27103] = {
        {
            id = 2397539,
            score = 27,
            author = "noamchomsky",
            text = "Please see the screenshots. They show what you're looking for at a small tree glowing red behind the final boss in \"Dire Maul - Warpwood Quarter.\" There are 5 of these shards on the ground. Each player should:\n\n1) Pick up one shard only.\n2) Open their inventory.\n3) Right click on \"Reliquary of Purity.\" Then the quest is complete.\n4) Turn in the quest. (Until Blizzard changes the quest turn in location, it's at the beginning of this instance.) So click the green Dungeon Finder icon on the perimeter of your minimap, click \"Teleport Out of Dungeon,\" and then teleport back in which will start you back at the beginning of the instance so you can turn it in easily.",
            date = "2016-09-11T12:23:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27103#comments:id=2397539",
        },
        {
            id = 2152484,
            score = 23,
            author = "AddictedPoi",
            text = "People may screw up the quest for other party members if they pick up a shard, use the reliquary and then pick up another shard. No shard for the one who is not fast enough!",
