            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27154#comments:id=1191617",
        },
        {
            id = 1708168,
            score = 1,
            author = "624027",
            text = "High level hunter... get rid of your pet, if you don't get a shot in, you don't get credit for the kill...\n\nRespawn is now very fast...",
            date = "2012-09-02T12:12:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27154#comments:id=1708168",
        },
        {
            id = 1832622,
            score = 1,
            author = "1108039",
            text = "Here's what's weird, my mage character went to the top of the tower and of course we know he wasn't there, so I wanted to slow fall down and started up my spell.... welp, it didn't stop, ever!  In fact I stayed in the spell cast stance, and could run around at the same time, BUT my running was sped up tremendously.  Which of course I wanted to show and share with others since it looked so silly to be in casting stance and running around in fast forward... but alas nobody was around.\nHas anyone else experienced anything weird there, or this effect at all, or anywhere for that matter?",
            date = "2013-03-22T01:35:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27154#comments:id=1832622",
        },
        {
            id = 1990060,
            score = 1,
            author = "777538",
            text = "Make sure to stand with your back right against the railing around the stairwell when you engage him.  This will prevent him blinking to a position behind you every few moments in the fight.",
            date = "2014-08-09T18:18:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27154#comments:id=1990060",
        },
    },
    [27155] = {
        {
            id = 1255550,
            score = 64,
            author = "109170",
            text = "Cleverly enough you actually dont know there's a quest reward till you turn it in to Tyrion.",
            date = "2010-12-23T20:43:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27155#comments:id=1255550",
        },
        {
            id = 1426611,
            score = 54,
            author = "Apolocyntosis",
            text = "Wait... what? My going after the Magus wasn't Crusade-sanctioned?\nWait... WHAT? I'M GETTING HUNG OUT TO DRY FOR FOLLOWING YOUR ORDERS?\n\nDaria, you sneaky motherless......oh. Tirion's cool with it. Alright, then.",
            date = "2011-05-24T23:41:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27155#comments:id=1426611",
        },
        {
            id = 1673297,
            score = 24,
            author = "Tensaiga",
            text = "I really kinda loved this quest.  Having consequences for your actions, or at the very least, the appearance of consequences is awesome.  You just killed someone known by everyone and in town to boot!  And now you have to fess up the authorities!  Makes sense!",
            date = "2012-06-04T02:47:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27155#comments:id=1673297",
        },
        {
            id = 1634649,
            score = 9,
            author = "Zachs",
            text = "This quest also awards you with your choice of the following three items:\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=62191\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=62190\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=62189",
            date = "2012-03-03T16:26:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27155#comments:id=1634649",
        },
        {
            id = 1953484,
            score = 6,
            author = "855987",
            text = "Your heroism is budding much earlier than even I had anticipated.\n\nAh, Farseer Fordring. I didn't realize the Light served you so. =/\n\nThis is a critique of one line of the writing, not of the action of the questline. The rest of his lines made sense. This one just took me out of the moment.\n\n\"Your heroism is budding\"\nCan you imagine anyone else who speaks like that?\nDoes this sound like the man who fought the Lich King?\n\"much earlier than even I had anticipated\"\nWho else is anticipating this budding?\nWhat was the initial timeline you suspected?\n\n[br]\n\nI know we don't get choices in (almost all of) our quests -- we can't choose a bad man's path like Arthas did -- but it would be nice if the game didn't whack me over the head with how I'm always going to be the hero or in the process of becoming the hero.\n\nLikewise, NPCs have seen their leaders turn evil. Why would they be so keen to label anyone \"hero\" these days? A \"thank you\" is enough. Or better: questioning why I took brute tactics over CCing the mage would have been better -- it would be enough for him to suggest that I must always be mindful of the road my choices take me down.\n\nNote that one of the previous quests in the chain had an NPC chide me for being nosy. In a game where there are no questline choices per se, being chided, being warned, being confronted despite being on rails is better than being acknowledged as the unquestionable, unfailing hero.",
            date = "2014-03-24T16:51:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27155#comments:id=1953484",
        },
    },
