://www.wowhead.com/quest=27311, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28284, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27317 & https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27313: https://www.wowhead.com/item=63596 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63597 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63598 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63599 are side quests during this chain)\n\n37a. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28086\n37b. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28087: https://www.wowhead.com/item=63648 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63649 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63650 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63651\n38. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28088\n39. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28098: https://www.wowhead.com/item=63652 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63653 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63654 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63655\n40. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28124\n\n41a. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28125: https://www.wowhead.com/item=63656 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63657 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63658\n41b.  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28127\n42a. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28136: https://www.wowhead.com/item=63659 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63660 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63661 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63662\n42b. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28139\n43. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28140\n44. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28142\n\n45a. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28157\n45b. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28158\n46. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28159: https://www.wowhead.com/item=63663 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63664 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63665 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63666\n\n47. https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28161: https://www.wowhead.com/item=63673 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63674 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63675 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63676 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63677 https://www.wowhead.com/item=63678\n\n(If I missed something, let me know)\n\n(on a side note: I got https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=4938 while just going for the end quest by doing all it's pre-requisit quests and some side quests that were in the same area. (Also did a chain started with https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28042 but afaik this is not needed.))\n\nNote: 07/11/2011, changed the 1st sentence, it was originally \"An overview of all the quests needed to get there:\" to avoid some confusion as to what this post is all about.",
            date = "2011-10-29T06:58:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27328#comments:id=1556593",
        },
        {
            id = 1755216,
            score = 1,
            author = "VicHolmes",
            text = "Did this as a 44 Tauren Shammy.  The trick is to actually HAVE a level-class healing potion.  Focus on the adds, you take the adds and the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=45278 will tank the main.  When he says take the potion, TAKE the potion and be ready cuz all will focus on you.  You only have to hold them off for about 30 sec without dying (tough but doable).  I also had the Horn of the Traitor (https://www.wowhead.com/item=63633) that calls the Cliff-dweller to fight at my side.  Use it at the beginning so the cooldown starts ticking right off the bat.  You'll need him later to help with the adds if the fight REALLY drags on!\n\nLast, as soon as you kill one add, take another on.  Don't stop to breathe.  Just keep killing till you see the \"mission Complete\" banner where the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=45278 has killed the main.  As near as I can see, the spirit guy only died once during the battle then came back 30 sec later.  After the fight is over, the adds do NOT disappear (I actually had two more pop up as I was walking away), so keep a lookout!  Good luck!",
            date = "2012-11-01T20:39:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27328#comments:id=1755216",
        },
    },
    [27329] = {
        {
            id = 1190140,
            score = 17,
            author = "711077",
            text = "You have to kill the Grimtotem adds that are channeling the shield to him before you can attack him otherwise you're doing 1 damage for each ability you do.",
            date = "2010-11-27T10:11:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27329#comments:id=1190140",
        },
        {
            id = 1198847,
            score = 17,
            author = "218791",
            text = "If he heals to full after you get him down, just run away. You've completed the quest.",
            date = "2010-11-30T21:37:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27329#comments:id=1198847",
        },
        {
            id = 1797408,
            score = 3,
            author = "1057520",
            text = "Was the sentinel supposed to help you here? Mine just stood there.",
            date = "2013-01-12T16:53:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27329#comments:id=1797408",
        },
        {
            id = 1207524,
            score = 2,
            author = "448160",
            text = "Can he still be tamed?",
            date = "2010-12-05T04:35:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27329#comments:id=1207524",
        },
        {
            id = 1866085,
            score = 2,
            author = "Veradas",
            text = "I tried killing the serpent 3 times with my lvl 44 Night Elf Hunter.  Even with my pets, it is an impossible task, my toon keeps getting killed every time!  Not one Grimtotem shaman appeared to heal the serpent before I died!  Even potions don't help!  This quest needs some serious rework.  I don't mind quests being challenging, what I do mind is them being impossible!",
            date = "2013-06-13T07:20:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27329#comments:id=1866085",
        },
    },
    [27330] = {
        {
            id = 1219799,
            score = 13,
            author = "sjones321",
            text = "In case you don't notice them like I didn't for a long time, you need to kill the guys channeling into Arikara's shield before you can do any real damage.",
            date = "2010-12-09T20:32:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27330#comments:id=1219799",
        },
        {
            id = 1207737,
            score = 9,
            author = "82411",
            text = "No need to kill the serpent. It goes back to full health and completes the quest. You can just walk away.",
            date = "2010-12-05T07:52:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27330#comments:id=1207737",
        },
        {
            id = 1819989,
            score = 6,
            author = "wowheadfunky",
            text = "Be aware that Freewind Brave does not always fight with you - he didn't with me. I did it as a 44 Hunter with a bear pet, I concentrated on killing Arikara and spamming Mend Pet so my bear didn't die. As soon as I saw any of the ancestral grimtotem's I set them as my target and kept the bear on Arikara. I did this because I saw the quote mentioned in another comment.\n\nI found it quite ironic that this big powerful 'helper' would help kill all the mobs leading up to this but not a thing on this.",
            date = "2013-03-02T09:51:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27330#comments:id=1819989",
        },
        {
            id = 1450588,
            score = 4,
            author = "437066",
            text = "It took me awhile to figure out about the guys on the side healing the serpent as well, but after catching on I killed them as they appeared. Problem was, after killing the serpent it instantly came back to life at full health. There was a message that said Arikara's Revenge - so I whittled him down again, and he re-spawned again at full health. At this point I walked away as I was tired of fighting, out of mana and potions, and low on health. I did receive credit for the quest, but I think it is still bugged as of this writing.",
            date = "2011-06-25T19:34:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27330#comments:id=1450588",
        },
        {
            id = 1524451,
            score = 3,
            author = "FamousAtomicBoy",
            text = "It's definitely bugged, but I managed to get it to work - sort of - after a few attempts. After I \"beat\" Arikara and it was restored to full health, I ran across the bridge to reset it. I ran back, used the https://www.wowhead.com/item=61043 to start it over, and finally got the Twilight Hammer script to play just as the four spirits reappeared and healed it again:\n\nArikara yells: Stop! You have bested my wind serpent.\nArikara yells: I have been taken prisoner by the Twilight's Hammer.\nArikara yells: I'm not certain where. Start with their western base overlooking Highperch.",
            date = "2011-09-22T04:16:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27330#comments:id=1524451",
        },
    },
    [27336] = {
        {
            id = 1192385,
            score = 178,
            author = "Maahk",
            text = "For this quest, you have to get the killing blow on the mob while it is under the debuff from the totem.\nThis restriction includes hunter pets - I had to put my pet on passive to be sure I got the killing blow and to make this quest bearable.\n\nThey did make the cooldown on the totem short and also made the debuff last longer vs. pre-cata, making this a bit less frustrating than before.",
            date = "2010-11-28T04:40:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27336#comments:id=1192385",
        },
        {
            id = 2543244,
            score = 25,
            author = "Wyr3d",
            text = "Pretty much as others have said. This quest is bugged for characters with pets (namely hunters and warlocks) You should dismiss your pet before attempting this quest, or it will take you forever (something like 1/10 kills before I realised the pet damage was fudging the quest on my warlock)\n\nOnce you put your pet away, you'll have no problem.",
            date = "2017-12-30T18:39:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27336#comments:id=2543244",
        },
        {
            id = 1286947,
            score = 24,
            author = "464014",
            text = "If you're having trouble with this quest, check the following:\n\nYou have to get the killing blow on the crocs. If your pet gets the last hit you will not get credit for the \"totem test\".\nThe totem debuff MUST be on the croc at the time of the kill. The debuff lasts for about 6 seconds and reapplies after a split second. It is entirely possible to kill the croc within this split-second and if this happens you will not get credit.\n\nIf you are still having trouble make sure you have the right crocs and have the totem down when the kill occurs with the deuff currently on the croc when you get the killing blow.",
            date = "2011-01-10T04:33:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27336#comments:id=1286947",
        },
        {
            id = 5195910,
            score = 21,
            author = "Alteir",
            text = "I've tested this a bunch on TBC Classic and I've found that the problem isn't having a pet out, the pet doing too much damage, or the pet dealing the killing blow - the problem is that the pet has aggro. That's what hinders quest progression. The crocs HAVE to have aggro on the player character when they die, not the pet.",
            date = "2021-06-14T10:34:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27336#comments:id=5195910",
        },
        {
            id = 2094577,
            score = 15,
            author = "Random0532",
            text = "How to do this quest:\n\nFind either a https://www.wowhead.com/npc=4344 or a https://www.wowhead.com/npc=4345.\nPut down your https://www.wowhead.com/item=33101.\nAttack the mob and drag it to the totem.\nIt'll be affected with the debuff https://www.wowhead.com/spell=42454, only then are you good to kill the mob.",
            date = "2015-01-25T11:45:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27336#comments:id=2094577",
        },
    },
    [27339] = {
        {
            id = 1450457,
            score = 17,
            author = "541032",
            text = "Dear lvl'ers. Please skip this quest. The droprate is very low and with the fast lvling nowadays this quest ain't worth it. The only reason you have for doing this quest should be loremaster.",
            date = "2011-06-25T15:46:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27339#comments:id=1450457",
        },
        {
            id = 1256158,
            score = 6,
            author = "Muse",
            text = "Other people might have more or different luck than I did, but the drop rate for the venom was abysmal to the point of being nonexistent on the noxious shredders. Unless you want to kill them for the sake of killing them, skip those and just kill the darkfang creepers. It will still be plenty grindy, but it drops enough that you won't be wondering if the quest is broken. :-)",
            date = "2010-12-24T05:54:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27339#comments:id=1256158",
        },
        {
            id = 1978201,
            score = 2,
            author = "Lovestorybro",
            text = "Note that this quest item drops off of both the green flying snakes and the orange spiders.  The drop rate is lower than normal (about 40%) which makes the quest annoying.  I guess it was meant to be done while you are doing other quests in the area.  Might as well keep the quest until you leave the zone as you'll probably end up completing it eventually.",
            date = "2014-07-06T08:25:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27339#comments:id=1978201",
        },
        {
            id = 1887898,
            score = 1,
            author = "27eper",
            text = "It seems that the drop rate was fixed (or I'm very lucky).",
            date = "2013-08-17T18:10:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27339#comments:id=1887898",
        },
        {
            id = 3175251,
            score = 1,
            author = "Tyrsenus",
            text = "If you're having trouble getting this quest, talk to Zidormi  (https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63546/zidormi) switch to the \"other\" version of Dustwallow Marsh, then find Apprentice Garion (https://www.wowhead.com/npc=23601/apprentice-garion). For some reason I couldn't get the quest from him until I did that.",
            date = "2019-12-05T20:21:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27339#comments:id=3175251",
        },
    },
