        {
            id = 2132774,
            score = 6,
            author = "Wimbleton",
            text = "There's an interesting little twist to this quest. If you don't turn it in during or at the end of the actual instance you are in, you won't be able to turn it in later. The reason is that when you re-enter the dungeon, there are three elites and a dog guarding the quest giver. Two of them are 57, one is 56 and the dog is 54. If you are level-appropriate, you'll have an interesting time killing all four because you can't pull just one; I've tried all the ways. Even worse, if you run out of the dungeon to escape the mass attack, it doesn't reset but all four mobs respawn, even though the corpses of the one or two that you managed to kill are still there (and lootable, not that they drop much of anything).\n\nI assume it's a glitch and I would never suggest it's poor design work, particularly after WoD, which I think is brilliant. But it is pretty terminal: don't turn it in, you lose it, unless you can convince a higher-level from your guild to swat the mobs around the quest giver.",
            date = "2015-03-07T15:56:30-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27440#comments:id=2132774",
        },
