    [27487] = {
        {
            id = 1208428,
            score = 19,
            author = "648135",
            text = "You have to go through and do all of the quests at Fiona's Caravan to reach this quest.",
            date = "2010-12-05T14:55:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27487#comments:id=1208428",
        },
        {
            id = 1592044,
            score = 14,
            author = "Aradona",
            text = "This quest will throw you for a loop, as it is exceptionally hard. It's Blinding Swarm ability will do MASSIVE damage to you, and running from it simply makes it follow you, while you aren't doing any damage from fleeing. I would strongly suggest you bring a friend to down it.  I have died 4 times on this guy alone. If possible, stun or silence him as soon as he starts the swarm. It is non-interruptable, so this is your best bet, and hit him with all of your cooldowns.  DO NOT count on Taradar to be much help at all, or to take aggro off of you...he will not do so.\n\nAlso, try to repair before going into it...if you die a couple times, you do not want to have to go back and repair.\n\nThe minions are around his location, and are easy to kill.\n\nHe is not a rare or elite, just one of those (!) mobs.  Be warned.\n\nEdit:  Rogues-- As soon as he uses Blinding Swarm, Vanish and get behind him. Taradar will grab the aggro, and you thus avoid it. Ambush when he's done swarming and kill for the win. Just killed him today as a 44 Rogue.",
            date = "2011-12-07T13:43:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27487#comments:id=1592044",
        },
        {
            id = 1204918,
            score = 12,
            author = "710649",
            text = "His blinding swarm ability was taking me down by about 350 per second, so be aware of your health bar.",
            date = "2010-12-03T20:27:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27487#comments:id=1204918",
        },
        {
            id = 1893068,
            score = 11,
            author = "Pastoral",
            text = "After four tries on my 40th level Mistweaver Monk, and ready to give up, I gave it one more try.\n\nPlease ignore the idiots who are claiming that he's not hard...and by implication, that the rest of us are just stupid and incompetent while they in their infinite lack of skill and poor gear, managed to do it like he's just any ol' quest mob.\n\nI didn't save the battle logs for this, but I suspect what was happening is that this mob had help. The surrounding trash, which is also part of the quest, can stun, damage and some have pets and ranged attacks, too. And because of this Quest Mob's size, there's a good chance you didn't even see them.\n\nWhat worked for me was clearing away the trash first, then fighting him on a hill top away from everything else. When he launched his blinding swarm ability, I ran from him in a lateral direction. He can't move when he does the Blinding Swarm, but he can turn to keep it aimed at you. Running away from him seemed to mitigate the damage, and it also gave me time to recover some of my abilities on CD.\n\nHe did go down, with some difficulty. My best guess is that he had some help the first few times I fought him.",
            date = "2013-09-05T12:04:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27487#comments:id=1893068",
        },
        {
            id = 1375304,
            score = 9,
            author = "kalarel",
            text = "Get your pots and heals out for this one. It hits HARD.",
            date = "2011-03-24T21:10:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27487#comments:id=1375304",
        },
    },
