    [27489] = {
        {
            id = 1191587,
            score = 18,
            author = "196807",
            text = "On this leg of the journey, the 3 NPCs continue to discuss their troubles:\n\nTarenar Sunstrike yells: I can't believe I let Gidwin run off like that!\nFiona says: It's not your fault, Tarenar.  He ran off on his own will.  None of us could stop him.\nArgus Highbeacon says: We can't be certain that he was killed.  Maybe he just ran off somewhere.\nTarenar Sunstrike yells: No, he'd never just leave his prayer book behind!  He was always nose-deep in that book, studying.\nTarenar Sunstrike says: He was always studying, always trying to get better.\nArgus Highbeacon says: Even more reason to believe that he's still alive.\nArgus Highbeacon says: A paladin like Gidwin makes a fine death knight.  Any member of the Scourge powerful enough to defeat him would know that.\nArgus Highbeacon says: It's likely that he's being held somewhere, awaiting a death ritual.\nFiona yells: Really?  That's great news!\nFiona says: Well, actually, that's pretty bad news, but considering the alternatives...\nArgus Highbeacon says: If we're to find him, we're headed in the right direction.  It's likely that he was taken to Stratholme, or potentially to the Plaguewood.\nArgus Highbeacon says: Both are places of great evil.  This is the leg of my journey that I shun the most.\nTarenar Sunstrike says: I'm not sure I'm ready to go in there alone.\nFiona says: You're not alone, Tarenar.  You've made allies along the way.  And besides, you're a skilled paladin in your own right.\nTarenar Sunstrike says: Me, skilled?  No, no, Gidwin was the good paladin.  He's the one who stayed up for hours every night practicing...\nFiona says: ...yet it was you that continually kept up with him.  Without practice.\nFiona says: I've watched both of you fight, Tarenar.  You've got natural talent - more than Gidwin ever will.\nArgus Highbeacon says: Perhaps that's why he left without you.\nTarenar Sunstrike says: What do you mean?\nArgus Highbeacon says: Perhaps he felt he needed to prove that he was as talented as you.\nTarenar Sunstrike says: This is all my fault.  I've got to go find him, to set things right.\nArgus Highbeacon says: I wouldn't say that it's your fault, Tarenar.  But don't let that stop you from saving Gidwin.",
            date = "2010-11-27T20:55:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27489#comments:id=1191587",
        },
        {
            id = 1199031,
            score = 9,
            author = "181815",
            text = "Giddy may be a stick-in-the-mud, but when it comes down to it, he can swing the Light like a champion.\n\nSo that's what that book he was studying so hard was...",
            date = "2010-11-30T23:43:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27489#comments:id=1199031",
        },
        {
            id = 1182000,
            score = 8,
            author = "Tristful",
            text = "jumped on her wagon and then was booted off about 20 yards down the ramp from the tower about 5 seconds later. she didn't appear at the new tower and was missing from the old tower. i abandoned the quest in hopes of resetting the phase and still nothing. =(\n\nedit: relogged and the problem was fixed",
            date = "2010-11-24T15:02:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27489#comments:id=1182000",
        },
        {
            id = 1509587,
            score = 7,
            author = "Orcbum",
            text = "This quest pulled by heartstrings :(. Gidwin was a dwarf that aspired to be as great as a paladin as the ones in Light's Hope Chapel, and I always got the feeling Tarenar didn't give a rat's butt as long as he was by his best friend's side.\n\nAnd I always liked the idea that everyone has their flaws and that they are prone to their base humanistic feelings, regardless of friendship. (Gidwin and his jealousy)\n\nIt's even better that they reconciled at the end. :D This quest chain while not as flashy and \"SAVE-THE-WORLD\" type-ish as the other Cataclysm quests, was definitely my favorite. I love the power of friendship.\n\nFRIENDSHIP POWER!",
            date = "2011-09-03T16:00:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27489#comments:id=1509587",
        },
        {
            id = 2556220,
            score = 2,
            author = "Aernath",
            text = "I guess this quest is bugged at the moment, I can't seem to get the ride, I dropped and retake the quest, relogged, nothing worked. I was working for Loremaster and EPL was the last one for my Eastern Kingdoms achievement... QQ\n\nUpdate: Oops... It's because of the Storyline addon, last new choice wasn't showing, if you're also as gullible as I am, resize the window or disable the addon, you'll see the option \"Ride Fiona's Caravan to its next destination\" there... Sowwy :P",
            date = "2018-03-05T01:31:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27489#comments:id=2556220",
        },
    },
