        },
    },
    [27550] = {
        {
            id = 6225854,
            score = 96,
            author = "DCCXVIII",
            text = "So you're trying to figure out how to get the new player housing decor item that this quest rewards.\n\nTurns out this quest is part of a massive 53 quest long chain that spans not 1, not 2, but 3 zones! So you will need to do quests in Silverpine Forest, Ruins of Gilneas and Hillsbrad Foothills to eventually get this quest. But the quest chain starts in Silverpine Forest with [quest=26965 domain=www]. So just start there. Also, make sure you're completing the various ancillary side quests that reveal thesmevles as you progress. A lot of the time these quest are also required for the chain to progress even if they're not directly part of the quest chain itself.",
            date = "2025-11-14T23:30:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27550#comments:id=6225854",
        },
        {
            id = 6257515,
            score = 8,
            author = "Silvansaria",
            text = "Sooo...\n\nThis might not be so easy to figure out *where* you are in the questlines... I went through about 10 pages of info on Wowhead trying to figure out what quest I'm supposed to do in order to pick up this or that and do this or that in order to get the decor item. THEN - I decided to look at my ACHs - under QUESTS - and then under SILVERPINE FOREST.\n\nApparently I have done a lot but stopped on \"The Ruins of Gilneas\"...\nI had to start with the quest: \"The Great Escape\".\n\nIf you look it up - the \" ! \" is to the right of Northern Headlands on the map but MINE - was actually all the way south below the Tempered Reach along the beach there...\n\nYou might have different progress than me - and need to start all this somewhere else but a good place to start your search is the actual \"Silverpine Forest Quests\" and that will list your progress, and then you can look THAT up to find out exactly where you are in the quest chain and what you need to do NOW.\n\n**some people have stated how long the questlines are and how tedious and is it worth it and all that other crap... If you REALLY have to ask that or say that - maybe you should stop playing World of Warcraft. These questlines, even the super low ones, are really fun even at max level (and funny if you actually read the dialogue) and absolutely worth doing.\n\nHope this all helps and good luck!",
            date = "2026-01-04T18:32:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27550#comments:id=6257515",
        },
        {
            id = 1271521,
            score = 4,
            author = "virgo664",
            text = "For those that are having problems getting this quest (ie level 85 players) get off your mount and walk over to the front lines. The quest givers will appear and you will have three more quests to attend to.",
            date = "2011-01-01T14:53:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27550#comments:id=1271521",
        },
        {
            id = 1429664,
            score = 3,
            author = "Liri",
            text = "Lord Godfrey says: Through fire we purge this land of its impurities.\nLord Godfrey says: Reduced to ashes... Soon nothing will be left of Gilneas or the worgen taint.\nLord Godfrey says: Some people only want to watch the world burn. Others want to be the ones responsible for burning it...",
            date = "2011-05-28T21:23:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27550#comments:id=1429664",
        },
        {
            id = 1943041,
            score = 3,
            author = "HotRats",
            text = "Contrary to what wowhead states, this quest's series does not start with this quest or https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27542 . Given the lore (as I remember it) I suspect you have to start with quests at the Forsaken High Command  (in northern Silverpine Forest)",
            date = "2014-02-13T16:56:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27550#comments:id=1943041",
        },
    },
    [27551] = {
        {
            id = 1181263,
            score = 18,
            author = "Nifel",
            text = "Done most of the quests in here, got the drop and it says I don't meet the requirements. Bug? Any other suggestions?\n\nEDIT: Found the problem. I started the EP quests from Light's Hope Chapel and worked my way towards Stratholme. Turns out you have to do the Caravan questline which starts at the border WP/EP until the part where you go look for Tarenar Sunstrike on the road close to Stratholme. There you get the quest Guardians of Stratholme (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27525) which involves killing Omasum Blighthoof (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=45867) and Karthis Darkrune (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=45868) for the item which starts this quest (http://www.wowhead.com/item=61378). If you kill them prior to this it will be useless and just take up inventory space.",
            date = "2010-11-24T11:19:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27551#comments:id=1181263",
        },
        {
            id = 1182888,
            score = 11,
            author = "221009",
            text = "I believe you have to have completed Blind Fury to be able to activate the item that gives this quest.  No idea why you can get the drop before then.",
            date = "2010-11-24T20:21:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27551#comments:id=1182888",
        },
        {
            id = 2621637,
            score = 4,
            author = "Shadow12000",
            text = "Just a note since none of the other comments mention it. Unlike other items that start quests, this wont start automatically upon looting it. This is because you need to have completed the quest to kill the death knights that actually drop the item first before being able to accept the quest. This also means that until you accept the quest, it'll have a marker on your world map that a quest is at one of the ziggurats, even if you have the item in your inventory. Overall, it was an odd choice to make this quest start from a drop, rather than just making the \"kill the death knights\" quest end with you turning in the missive as some objective of its own like \"Learn Gidwin's Location\".",
            date = "2018-10-06T15:06:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27551#comments:id=2621637",
        },
        {
            id = 3197106,
            score = 3,
            author = "Xithriial",
            text = "Just an FYI, This wouldn't let me accept it until I had done the repeatable quest from behind lights hope chapel. Annals of the Silver Hand (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28755/annals-of-the-silver-hand) from Lord Raymond George (https://www.wowhead.com/npc=49856/lord-raymond-george)",
            date = "2020-03-31T00:39:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27551#comments:id=3197106",
        },
        {
            id = 5753955,
            score = 3,
            author = "auvii",
            text = "Starting this quest requires \"The Baroness' Missive\" that drops from Omasum Blighthoof (https://www.wowhead.com/npc=45867/omasum-blighthoof) and Karthis Darkrune (https://www.wowhead.com/npc=45868/karthis-darkrune) during the Guardians of Stratholme (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27525/guardians-of-stratholme) quest.\n\nOnce looted the item automatically gives you the option to accept the new quest if you are using the Quest Objectives",
            date = "2023-12-21T09:29:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27551#comments:id=5753955",
        },
    },
    [27555] = {
        {
            id = 1182763,
            score = 44,
            author = "412275",
            text = "as you progress through her quests through the zone, her caravan advances with more/different riders. its just the maps way to help you remember where you are and how far you have left. it also helps you track the related achievement a little. if yet to see the caravan anywhere other than the wpl/epl border without starting her quests\n\nand in relation to this buff, it becomes available after finding and returning with her first 2 paladin traveling companions tarenar sunstrike (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=45429) and gidwin goldbraids (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=45428)\n\nits actual effect is to cause hidden stash (http://www.wowhead.com/item=61387#dropped-by) to drop off of mobs which has a small chance to contain Mr. Grubbs (http://www.wowhead.com/item=66076)\n\ntl:dr - find fiona, do her 2 quests, do the 2 pallys quests, recieve buff, grind for pet",
            date = "2010-11-24T19:36:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27555#comments:id=1182763",
        },
        {
            id = 1186765,
            score = 16,
            author = "lawngnomejack",
            text = "So, I can confirm that the charm does remain even if you log out, so if you get fed up after grinding for an hour and want to quit for a while don't worry.  Thing is, after getting Mr. Grubbs I tried right clicking the charm and that does not make it come off, which I am not complaining about, but I do not know if there is a time limit on the charm.\n\nAs for grinding, the best area is Zul'Mashar in North-Eastern EPL with all those troll graves.  Tons of bodies to loot, especially if you have area spells and can kill lots at once.  The respawn is a little slow but you can kill the other trolls in the small area while you wait.  It is the best place because there are lots of mobs  to kill and minimum travel.\n\nAlas, even with all those mobs I was still there for at least an hour and half, and didn't get very many stashes in all that time.  Some people get lucky and get it after two loots but those are rare, happy stories.  The best thing to do with an item that is a semi-rare drop is to assume it will take some dedication, decide whether or not you want to spend the time, and then be surprised if you get it early, or not surprised if you're there for 2 days.\n\nFun thing for me is that I looted 2 stashes from a group of the trolls and opened them one after the other; they both had Mr. Grubbs in them lol.  It's too bad they are BOP.",
            date = "2010-11-26T04:51:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27555#comments:id=1186765",
        },
        {
            id = 1183884,
            score = 9,
            author = "Ipfree549",
            text = "This charm can be obtained after by doing the 2 quests offered by Fiona in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nThe charm used to get the pet Mr. Grubbs (http://www.wowhead.com/item=66076) which is found in  Hidden Stash (http://www.wowhead.com/item=61387) that drop from the level 40-45 mobs in the Eastern Plaguelands.",
            date = "2010-11-25T04:44:13-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27555#comments:id=1183884",
        },
        {
            id = 1186691,
            score = 8,
            author = "lawngnomejack",
            text = "Just wondering: if I log off will the charm still be on me when I log back in?  And if I somehow lose the charm can I simply get it again from Fiona's Caravan?\n\nIt appears that I should be able to, what with the blue question mark and all, but I just want to make sure not that I log off without getting the pet and essentially screw myself.",
            date = "2010-11-26T04:09:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27555#comments:id=1186691",
        },
        {
            id = 1631297,
            score = 8,
            author = "Eillesthis",
            text = "Farming for https://www.wowhead.com/item=66076 under the effect of https://www.wowhead.com/spell=85612, I killed 257 https://www.wowhead.com/npc=12261s, and got 22 https://www.wowhead.com/item=61387, for a drop rate of 8.6%.  That's of course a much smaller sample pool than wowhead has, and the drop rate for all npcs may not be the same, but wowhead stats presumably include kills without the buff, so I wanted a controlled (if small) experiment.\n\nAs for how often those stashes contain what you want, I can't judge from personal experience.  I stopped once I got my first Mr. Grubbs - for even rough statistics I would have to keep going 'till I had 10, which would take forever.  However as others did last year, we may be able to extrapolate from wowhead stats.  As of this date wowhead has seen https://www.wowhead.com/item=61387 drop 319319 times, and has seen https://www.wowhead.com/item=66076 drop 5760 times, so maybe 1.8% of the time it's a good stash.",
            date = "2012-02-24T20:52:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27555#comments:id=1631297",
        },
    },
