    [27600] = {
        {
            id = 1180181,
            score = 88,
            author = "707511",
            text = "This quest in picked up by Crazy Larry.\n\nWalk right outside the camp and Lil' Crazy Larry will be on your right hand side. I will submit a screen shot of him as well. If you talk to him you can choose to have him load you into the cannon. Doing this loads you in, and a few seconds later it will blast you across the water, landing on the ship. Be aware you might take some damage from this. Also, there will be 3 or so Giblins right next to where you land, so be prepared for this.\n\nThere are 3 items you need to pick up from the ship:\nThousand-Thread-Count Fuse\nExtra-Pure Blasting Powder\nStack of Questionable Publications\n\nOne is on the deck of the ship itself, the other two are underneath the deck, in pretty much opposite sides of the ship. There are some mobs around, so be aware if you're leveling.\n\nAfter picking up the 3 items, there is a cannon on the top deck you can \"talk too\" and it will give you the option to load yourself into the cannon. The same thing will happen, and you get shot back to where you started, next to Lil' Crazy Larry.\n\nHope this helps! Feel free to correct me, or add more info if needed :)",
            date = "2010-11-24T03:55:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27600#comments:id=1180181",
        },
        {
            id = 1188156,
            score = 58,
            author = "44621",
            text = "The powder is in the \"captains room\" on the 2nd floor.\nThe fuse is on the deck of the ship, near the mast.\nThe \"Stack of Questionable Publications\" is in the bottom floor, far end from the stairs.\n\nAlso: doing this quest gives you the Going Down? (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=964) achievement from using the cannons.",
            date = "2010-11-26T16:07:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27600#comments:id=1188156",
        },
        {
            id = 2564999,
            score = 33,
            author = "tarc",
            text = "So has anyone ever used the cannon on the ship and had it shoot you not towards land, but instead out into open water? I did that just now, landed in fatigue waters. Not too far into it, but still, was kind of funny.",
            date = "2018-04-29T13:10:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27600#comments:id=2564999",
        },
        {
            id = 1186301,
            score = 28,
            author = "Jaymacibe",
            text = "To note for this quest: Long spawn timer!\n\nIf you get a lot of people expect to be there for awhile.",
            date = "2010-11-25T23:56:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27600#comments:id=1186301",
        },
        {
            id = 2545493,
            score = 24,
            author = "Umiamz",
            text = "Every time I do this quest, the 'Landward Cannon' shoots me in the opposite direction out to sea. Surprised that nobody else has mentioned it...",
            date = "2018-01-14T05:58:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27600#comments:id=2545493",
        },
    },
    [27601] = {
        {
            id = 1277748,
            score = 101,
            author = "Sketchie",
            text = "I've wrote down what happened at the event. Massive spoilers ahead, of course.\n\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: Onward,  We will beat back the Alliance dogs and secure Lordaeron for the Forsaken! For the Horde!\nAccompany Lady Sylvanas Windrunner across the Battlefront.\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner yells: Lay down your arms and surrender!\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner yells: I will leave your cities in dust and your lives in ruin!\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: Look at them, . They scurry like rats, veering headlong to their doom. Surely Crowley and Bloodfang can see the futility in this!\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: To the Greymane Wall! We will force their hand.\n\nYou are given the Song of Sylvanas buff, which makes you stronger and move faster. High Warlord Cromush and Sylvanas' Val'kyr Agatha, Arthura and Daschla will stick with you while Sylvanas charges ahead towards the Greymane Wall. At the gates...\n\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner yells: Crowley, your forces have fallen before my mighty army. You have lost!\n\nLord Darius Crowley and Packleader Ivar Bloodfang approaches the group.\n\nLord Darius Crowley says: It's not over, Sylvanas. Not yet.\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: You frivolously throw away the lives of your people while your own king sits atop his throne of lies, nary lifting a finger to help.\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: Is Gilneas worth the lives that have been lost? The lives that will be lost? You cannot win.\nLord Darius Crowley says: We will die trying!\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: And your daughter? You could have saved her... You could have offered her your blood, and yet you did not. Why?\nLord Darius Crowley says: LORNA? What... Where is she! What have have you done to her!\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: Nothing, yet...\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: I now present you with a choice - a choice that I was never given.\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: I offer you the life of Lorna for your unconditional surrender.\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: Choose your next words wisely, Crowley. Deny me and she will serve me in undeath - forever.\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner yells: Bring her, Godfrey!\n\nBaron Ashbury, Lord Walden and Lord Godfrey approach the group with Lorna over Godfrey's shoulder.\n\nLord Darius Crowley says: GODFREY! You deceitful maggot!\nLord Godfrey says: Hello, old friend!\nLord Darius Crowley says: Lorna... I... Release her. I will sound the retreat.\nPackleader Ivar Bloodfang says: You can't be serious, Crowley. You miserable bastard!\n\nPackleader Ivar Bloodfang retreats back into Gilneas.\n\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: Release her, Godfrey.\nLord Godfrey says: Of course, mistress.\n\nGodfrey releases Lorna, and she runs up to Crowley and sits in front of him.\n\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: Now leave here, Crowley, and never return.\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: Lordaeron belongs to the Forsaken.\nLord Darius Crowley says: Forgive me, daughter...\n\nBoth Lorna and Crowley retreats back into Gilneas. Baron Ashbury, Lord Walden and Lord Godfrey walks behind Sylvanas.\n\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner yells: SOLDIERS OF THE HORDE! WE ARE VICTORIOUS! LORDAERON IS W...\n\nLord Godfrey shoots Sylvanas in the back with a gun and she falls over, dead.\n\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner dies.\n\nHigh Warlord Cromush says: WHAT HAVE YOU DONE, GODFREY!\nLord Godfrey says: Something that should have been done a long time ago, you filthy animal.\nLord Godfrey says: Gilneas belongs to me, and soon will the rest of Lordaeron!\nLord Godfrey says: NOW JOIN YOUR MISTRESS IN DEATH!\n\nYou now have to battle Lord Godfrey, Baron Ashbury and Lord Walden. High Warlord Cromush, Agatha, Arthura and Daschla will assist you. After a while...\n\nLord Godfrey yells: FALL BACK, BROTHERS! TO SHADOWFANG!\nLord Godfrey yells: This land will quiver and shake in the wake of our destruction!\n\nLord Godfrey, Baron Ashbury and Lord Walden retreats, presumably to Shadowfang Keep. Agatha, Arthura and Daschla will surround Sylvanas.\n\nHigh Warlord Cromush says: Fix her... FIX HER!\nAgatha says: We are bound to her, sisters...\nArthura says: It will destroy us, sister...\nDascha says: It is our sacred duty. The pact was sealed, the bargain made...\nArthura says: Then let it be done.\n\nThe sisters all channel their energies into Sylvanas, bringing her back to life. However, it comes with a price as all sisters dies. Sylvanas slowly gets back up while Cromush kneels in front of her.\n\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: I saw... only darkness.\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: And as I drifted towards nothingness, a brilliant light appeared, then another, and another... My dear val'kyr.\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: I know now - beyond a shadow of doubt - that the val'kyr are our future.\nLady Sylvanas Windrunner says: We will never stop fighting for Lordaeron. Never...",
            date = "2011-01-04T21:04:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27601#comments:id=1277748",
        },
        {
            id = 1196971,
            score = 83,
            author = "77279",
            text = "Make sure you are dismounted when you accept this quest!\n\nAnd trying to avoid spoilers: as tempting as it is, try not to engage any mobs while escorting Sylvanas. Cromush bugged out the first time I tried this quest.",
            date = "2010-11-30T02:08:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27601#comments:id=1196971",
        },
        {
            id = 1206634,
            score = 67,
            author = "179142",
            text = "Wow! Playing through SIlverpine Forest was amazing. So much fun. The storyline was brilliant!",
            date = "2010-12-04T18:05:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27601#comments:id=1206634",
        },
        {
            id = 1197978,
            score = 66,
            author = "226304",
            text = "As you're riding to the front, spare a few moments to look around. You'll notice that some of them are named worgen fighting. Them being the former named NPCs of Southshore, having accepted the worgen curse as seen way down earlier in the zone. An interesting touch, at the very least.",
            date = "2010-11-30T14:00:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27601#comments:id=1197978",
        },
        {
            id = 1188709,
            score = 63,
            author = "139511",
            text = "Without spoiling anything...\n\nThat guy has one strong gun.\n\nGreat quest though.",
            date = "2010-11-26T19:56:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27601#comments:id=1188709",
        },
    },
    [27603] = {
        {
            id = 2144201,
            score = 32,
            author = "Bogdanov89",
            text = "My theory (even though it goes a bit strange with the quest's text):\n\nThe players enter the Blackrock City through a cave opening in a slave mine.\nThat is definitely NOT the official entrance used by the Blackrock dwarves (and elemental/giant allies).\n\nThe way all those elite patrols are put between the two gigantic gates (one with the giant boss in front) definitely looks like that \"highway\" is the main path into the city.\nSimilar to how Ironforge has guards paired down the main hall where you enter the city.\n\nTo me the gigantic gate guarded by the giant boss is probably an official way into Blackrock City.\nSimilar to how Ironforge is entered through a gigantic gate - not some small hole in a mining tunnel.\n\nWhile the goblin NPC does seem mystified by the gate, i think that gate is nothing more than one of the gates between Blackrock City and the official exit to the surface world.",
            date = "2015-03-27T11:13:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27603#comments:id=2144201",
        },
        {
            id = 1544412,
            score = 19,
            author = "Wolgan",
            text = "Short answer, you don't open it. The shadowforge gate at the other end of the hall opens, but the one Bael'gar is guarding doesn't. I'd love to see another half  of BRD. Maybe in another expansion they'll open it up like they did with Blackrock Caverns and Blackwing Descent.",
            date = "2011-10-16T12:17:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27603#comments:id=1544412",
        },
        {
            id = 1244828,
            score = 14,
            author = "zingar",
            text = "sadly we dont get to find out whats behind the door :/",
            date = "2010-12-19T03:52:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27603#comments:id=1244828",
        },
        {
            id = 1321011,
            score = 14,
            author = "410384",
            text = "When I went over to kill Bael'Gar I noticed that the gate mentioned in the quest text was not actually a texture, and you could kind of see through the crack in the gate a bit. I kind of assume that this quest is sort of referencing conspiracy theories that people may have had about the gate in vanilla, can any older players confirm this?",
            date = "2011-02-04T00:06:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27603#comments:id=1321011",
        },
        {
            id = 1468854,
            score = 13,
            author = "Vraebel",
            text = "I played in Vanilla and when I first saw this gate, I really thought there was a conspiracy.\nHow do you open it?",
            date = "2011-07-13T12:01:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27603#comments:id=1468854",
        },
    },
