        {
            id = 1204408,
            score = 46,
            author = "Senithil",
            text = "Had a lot of difficulties doing this quest until I noticed that you can move the statues diagonal",
            date = "2010-12-03T14:50:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27693#comments:id=1204408",
        },
        {
            id = 1202901,
            score = 41,
            author = "644871",
            text = "Since the most helpful comment at the moment is just a link that goes to a confusing video with a long technique , I'll try and lend a hand here:\n\nStand in the middle of the ring. Start with any random one, and look which way it's facing. You want to get this one to the right position to face you, so look at the angle it's facing. What at which point on the board (other then the middle) would it look at you.\n\nOnce you've found the spot, move the one on the spot to the middle and put the correct one in that spot. Then do the same thing for the one moved to the middle, till they are all facing you.\n\nTL;DR: So, pretty much, from an over head view, just switch two parts on the board (i.e.  would turn into  (right edge) which would turn into (left edge) >  (center) <)",
            date = "2010-12-02T20:02:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27693#comments:id=1202901",
        },
        {
            id = 1345560,
            score = 39,
            author = "Makhunty",
            text = "Another Video guide. Short and simple ! :)\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gzFM0SP8Jmg",
            date = "2011-02-22T01:47:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27693#comments:id=1345560",
        },
    },
    [27694] = {
        {
            id = 1180230,
            score = 29,
            author = "707511",
            text = "This quest is picked up from Lord Itharius at Temple of Attar' Hakkal. If you walk up the stairs to the temple you will find him easy. He standing in front of the entrance leading to the dungeon.\n\nTo complete the quest you simply have to swim around the temple and pick up these artifacts. You do not enter the temple itself. They can be found all around the temple. I have submitted a screen shot to illustrate it. They can be a bit tricky to see, but other than that an easy and simple quest to do.\n\nWhen done hand it back in to Lord Itharius.",
            date = "2010-11-24T04:24:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27694#comments:id=1180230",
        },
        {
            id = 1293981,
            score = 7,
            author = "493620",
            text = "These things are hard to see. They are small brown clumps and don't glisten like you are probably used to. I just jumped around until I saw a Sawfin Frenzy and went down. You might as well kill the Frenzies in the area, otherwise they become an irritant.\nHere are the coords for your Atasl'ai Artifacts:\n1. 65:52\n2. 65:57\n3. 66:48\n4. 66:54\n5. 73:49\nHope this helps!",
            date = "2011-01-14T19:05:10-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27694#comments:id=1293981",
        },
        {
            id = 1202159,
            score = 6,
            author = "sour33",
            text = "The Temple of Atal Hakkar does not count as being in Swamps of Sorrows and gets rid of the buff from https://www.wowhead.com/item=62795",
            date = "2010-12-02T13:06:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27694#comments:id=1202159",
        },
        {
            id = 1195113,
            score = 5,
            author = "391479",
            text = "The artefacts are much easier to see when one is on the surface looking down into the water, as being submerged within the water itself actually desaturates the glow effect that usually outlines quest objects.",
            date = "2010-11-29T06:18:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27694#comments:id=1195113",
        },
        {
            id = 1254023,
            score = 4,
            author = "718694",
            text = "They're hard to see, but keep close to the floor and you'll see them slightly glistening",
            date = "2010-12-23T05:51:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27694#comments:id=1254023",
        },
    },
    [27697] = {
        {
            id = 1182320,
            score = 10,
            author = "81657",
            text = "This quest becomes available right as you enter Maraudon / Purple Crystals and in order to complete it you just have to click \"Complete Quest\" under the quest description in your quest log, after of course you've killed Lord Vyletongue.",
            date = "2010-11-24T16:43:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27697#comments:id=1182320",
        },
        {
            id = 2069713,
            score = 7,
            author = "Wyr3d",
            text = "Just thought I'd put a note here in case you entered Mauradon through the entrance at Desolace like I did. When you enter from the first glowing portal you come across in there, you may end up in the easy half of the dungeon. Here you are given no immediate quests, but once you take a step, the new \"Mauradon Quest\" interface will popup, and you can kill mobs and bosses at whim.\n\nHowever, by the time you get to the east side of the the dungeon, and arrive at this other entrence, you'll get randomly given this quest to kill Lord Vyletongue. No doubt by this point, the guy is already dead, making this quest a bit \"Johnny come lately.\"\n\nSince you can slip by the guy without killing him, you might want to leave him alive til after you obtain this quest, rather than having to do the dungeon a second time like I have to.\n\nIncidently, this quest wasn't given to me by any NPC - it just auto-appeared when I walked up the path to the entrance portal. You have no choice but to accept it either, as it goes into your log regardless.",
            date = "2014-12-15T13:56:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27697#comments:id=2069713",
        },
        {
            id = 1823487,
            score = 5,
            author = "xEvilsteinx",
            text = "Pretty annoying that while you can enter this section of Maraudon through Dungeon Finder at level 30, this quest requires you to be level 32.",
            date = "2013-03-07T07:10:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27697#comments:id=1823487",
        },
        {
            id = 1302755,
            score = 2,
            author = "29626",
            text = "Its a Alliance quest as well. And yes, you don't need to go all the way to Zaetar's Spirit to turn it in, you complete it through the new Quest popup.",
            date = "2011-01-21T06:56:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27697#comments:id=1302755",
        },
    },
