            score = 8,
            author = "Halajin88",
            text = "Am i the only one who noticed the connection between this cave and the old gods?\n\n1.  It is said that the sea creatures have been called here by something, that something is the guy we have to kill in the quest, Hr'nglth the lost, which is a faceless one. It is a little strange that we do not see any other faceless in swamp of sorrow or the areas around. Also we know the relationship between the old gods and the faceless.\n\n2.  All the creatures that he called in the cave are fish: naga, murlocs, etc. One of the whispers in the puzzle box of yogg'saron says \"The fish know all the secrets. They know the cold, they know the dark\"\n\n3. Hr'nglth the Lost says: \"Hear the call... serve him... join ussssssssssss...\" My first thought was: who is \"him\"? I belive the he was his master, and the masters of the faceless ones are the old gods. Could this be N'Zoth?\n\nWhat was the faceless one doing there? Why did he summon the sea creatures in swamp of sorrow?\n\nWe know from the puzzle box of yogg that an old god is dreaming in a sunken city, is this old god N'Zoth? Did he caused this this event in the swamp? And why?\n\nThe sea creatures, the faceless one, the sunken old god, the swamp, all are connected somehow.\n\nAnyone theories about this?",
            date = "2013-08-06T08:43:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27757#comments:id=1884488",
        },
        {
            id = 1366734,
            score = 5,
            author = "803490",
            text = "When you get into the cave you will quickly come to a section where it splits off into 3 passages.  Most people will want to take the passage on the middle or the right- it doesn't matter which because those passages come back together.  If you go left, you will be able to see Hr'nglth but you will be separated from him by a gap that is too large to jump across unless you're playing certain classes as noted above.  If you have enough ranged dps to kill him before he runs out of range and you don't care about looting him this is actually the fastest way to kill him.",
            date = "2011-03-14T12:01:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27757#comments:id=1366734",
        },
    },
    [27758] = {
        {
            id = 1188340,
            score = 6,
            author = "psxchelly",
            text = "Leads to:\n\nThe Machination\nhttp://www.wowhead.com/quest=27781 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27781)\n\nPS: dont forget to use the transporter thingy to prevent \"some\" running back and forth.",
            date = "2010-11-26T17:26:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27758#comments:id=1188340",
        },
        {
            id = 1179767,
            score = 4,
            author = "quinnallman",
            text = "The remote communication device allowed me to complete each quest without running back to Laine each time, but I could not pick up the follow up remotely. Luckily, there are teleporters that let you jump between certain spots (although I can't seem to be able to to jump from a boss teleporter back to Laine).",
            date = "2010-11-24T00:38:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27758#comments:id=1179767",
        },
        {
            id = 1193864,
            score = 0,
            author = "309256",
            text = "I was running my level 12 Priest through Deadmines with my level 80 Druid. With the Druid, I initially picked up the first quest, The Foreman (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27756), but abandoned it because my Priest was not high enough (level 15 requirement) and figured I would come back and do them both together.\n\nWhen my Priest entered the Mast Room, the quest The Carpenter (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27758) was automatically offered, even though he does not meet the level requirements and does not have the Stormwind Communicator Mk. II (http://www.wowhead.com/item=62334), yet my Druid got no quest.\n\nUpon entering the Goblin Foundary area, the same thing happened with the quest The Machination (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27781); offered to my ineligible Priest just for walking through the door, but not to my eligible Druid.\n\nOnce walking onto the dock in the Ironclad Cove area, I was given the quest The Admiral (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27785), but upon completion, I was NOT given the follow-up quest, The Defias Kingpin (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27790).\n\nI ran through the dungeon again, this time doing the quest line with my Druid, starting from the beginning, and was given every quest normally as I progressed through the dungeon, without incident.\n\nOnce my Priest reached level 15, I zoned back into Deadmines and Lieutenant Horatio Lane (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=46612) offered me both The Foreman (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27756) and The Defias Kingpin (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27790) at once.\n\nTL;DR - Even if you are below level 15, it seems you can still do every quest in this chain except the first and the last.\n\n-- SPECIFIC INFORMATION ABOUT THIS FIGHT --\n\nFor rep farmers: If you kill the Lumbering Oaf the goblin rides on too quickly, you won't get any xp or rep from killing him. If the fight lasts long enough that Helix dismounts while the Oaf is still alive, you will get +300 rep for both.",
            date = "2010-11-28T16:08:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27758#comments:id=1193864",
        },
        {
            id = 5422237,
            score = 0,
            author = "Chaindog",
            text = "SL S4\n\nSOLUTION TO QUEST PROBLEM: Heroic turn-in problem still exists in 2022!\n\n1 - You need to EXIT dungeon,\n2 - RESET to Normal mode,\n3 - re-enter and you'll be able to turn this in to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=46612 not too far inside.\n\nEnjoy your loot!",
            date = "2022-08-23T03:50:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27758#comments:id=5422237",
        },
    },
