    [27829] = {
        {
            id = 1420623,
            score = 6,
            author = "832863",
            text = "this quest is crazy ridiculous. i've died at least 6 times trying to kill kalaran because the other three don't give off enough threat to keep him occupied on them for any amount of time. can anyone give me advice on how to kill this beast?",
            date = "2011-05-16T21:59:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27829#comments:id=1420623",
        },
        {
            id = 1429858,
            score = 6,
            author = "MochaKimono",
            text = "Here's what I did:\n\nSwiftly clicked Eric's Charge > Baelog's Valhalla Shot > Baelog's Warcry > Olaf's Mighty Shout > Olaf's Shield Wall. That way Kal is stunned immediately, then takes a bunch of damage, then Olaf taunts and protects himself. THEN I attacked, and I sometimes halted attacks when my threat overwhelmed theirs.\n\nJust make sure to hit the Shot, Warcry, Shout and Shield Wall whenever they are on cooldown, ignoring you own abilities for a moment if you must. Use the Potion as necessary. You may wish to save the Charge for when Kal is charging up his flame breath, to interrupt it.\n\nI also cleared out the trash nearby first to prevent adds, which is even more critical for The Sorrow and the Fury.",
            date = "2011-05-29T04:30:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27829#comments:id=1429858",
        },
        {
            id = 1303541,
            score = 4,
            author = "62855",
            text = "I had just picked this quest up when I had to log out for a bit.  I logged back on (I had tucked my toon in the inn tent before logging), and found that only Eric is with me now.  Baelog is missing entirely and Olaf is standing in the tent and will not move or follow me.  I tried abandoning and re-taking the quest from each of the toons who can give it to me (Eric, Olaf and Rhea) in turn.  But Olaf does not budge from the tent and Baelog does not re-appear.  This appears to be a bug.  Has anyone else encountered it or discovered a fix?",
            date = "2011-01-21T20:36:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27829#comments:id=1303541",
        },
        {
            id = 1505037,
            score = 4,
            author = "535505",
            text = "After I died the first time, I lost Baelog and have been unable to get him back no matter what I try. They didn't patch in these quests with old noobs in mind. The three of us remaining just keep wiping.",
            date = "2011-08-28T01:20:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27829#comments:id=1505037",
        },
        {
            id = 1323766,
            score = 3,
            author = "anitabeato",
            text = "i had the same problem\nthen i just abandoned the quest, logged out, and log back in\ngot the quest back from one of the three, and the three started following me again\n\nit is important to mention that if you are a hunter you won't have your pet for this quest, since the three of them are your pet",
            date = "2011-02-06T05:39:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27829#comments:id=1323766",
        },
    },
    [27830] = {
        {
            id = 1204280,
            score = 38,
            author = "Squiji",
            text = "Don't actually go INTO New Kargath, or you will find yourself flagged PvP fighting Horde NPCs higher level than you are.  The right-hand path up the hill leads to the town the Horde use.  The left path up the hill leads to the parts where the mobs are you want to kill.",
            date = "2010-12-03T13:50:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27830#comments:id=1204280",
        },
        {
            id = 1391388,
            score = 14,
            author = "764609",
            text = "I always thought a quest in an enemy town would be interesting and fun due to the danger involved.  Leave it to Blizzard to make sure it's not.  Getting chain-ganked by a level 85 guard for entering the area marked on the map as the quest area is about as fun as chewing on broken glass.\n\nTake out the one-shot deaths for stepping in the wrong place and this will be a fun quest.",
            date = "2011-04-14T17:36:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27830#comments:id=1391388",
        },
        {
            id = 1198430,
            score = 8,
            author = "141466",
            text = "You must go up the hill into New Kargath. Moldarr is in the most southern building in the complex. Continue up the hill from this building and there will be a tower. General Jirakka is at the top of the tower.",
            date = "2010-11-30T17:16:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27830#comments:id=1198430",
        },
        {
            id = 1929136,
            score = 4,
            author = "830962",
            text = "What if one of your guys dies?  Is there any way to get him back?",
            date = "2013-12-26T02:58:42-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27830#comments:id=1929136",
        },
        {
            id = 2238502,
            score = 4,
            author = "Ringthane",
            text = "Yet another horrendous Cataclysm quest.  Not only do pet classes have to give up their pets for these useless dwarves, this level 47 quest has us fighting two elites - which I thought is something they didn't want us to have to do any more.  Aside from that, if you die, not all of your dwarves come back when you respawn.  And what's more, thanks to the idiotic \"let's just do as much damage to the terrain as we can\" design philosphy, God help you if you have to find your way back up to the top if you die.  If you don't go the right way, all you have is hills and valleys you can't navigate.\n\nI like to level characters myself instead of using the boost, since I like to experience the story and the different playstyles of different classes, but quests like this make me seriously reconsider just saying \"screw this\" and boosting straight to 90 so I can do some quests that actually make sense.\n\nAnd here's something else I just found out - even if you abandon the quest, you can't get rid of whatever dwarf you have tagging along.  So right now my warlock is trying to do other quests in the zone with a dwarf NPC as his pet, instead of the voidwalker that might actually help him out just a bit.",
            date = "2015-08-26T11:21:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27830#comments:id=2238502",
        },
    },
    [27831] = {
        {
            id = 1206906,
            score = 75,
            author = "564414",
            text = "Terrible quest, bad design. I'm a total keybinder, so trying to click on three different pets' abilities was a clunky nightmare. Whelp respawn rate is way, way too fast. Reminds me of the worst of the Wrath vehicle quests in its clumsiness. Too bad, because I was really enjoying the story up until this frustration.",
            date = "2010-12-04T21:05:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27831#comments:id=1206906",
        },
        {
            id = 1186639,
            score = 35,
            author = "Sagerauru",
            text = "Whenever you do this quest, make sure that you clear a spot out where when you pull Nyxondra from right above your head. This will prevent the NPCs following you from running off and pulling whelps into the fight. Also, it is worth noting that Nyxondra's Bellowing Roar can be interrupted, so interrupt it every time you can to make the fight that much easier.",
            date = "2010-11-26T03:32:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27831#comments:id=1186639",
        },
        {
            id = 1488459,
            score = 30,
            author = "760338",
            text = "I hated this quest until I read the other comments. Here's what you should keep in mind in short:\n\nGet to the northwest area, just behind the little burnt down shack. There's no whelps back there and doesn't despawn your 'vikings'.\nUse Swift's charge to interrupt Bellowing Roar. Will save you lots of time, specially if you don't have your own interrupt.\nCC works. I feared her a few times when the charge was on cooldown.\nIf you do try it elsewhere, do NOT loot the whelps as you kill them. This prolongs the spawn time and you just might notice that you can kill her before those bodies even disappear. Spawn times: Unlooted > looted > skinned.\n\nAs for getting back after you die or back there in general, go to the western area. With some decent WoW jumping skills you should be able to get back there easy enough. There's a way to do it in the south right by the graveyard but it's a bit of a pain.",
            date = "2011-08-06T06:29:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27831#comments:id=1488459",
        },
        {
            id = 1262424,
            score = 12,
            author = "i7Rage",
            text = "This quest is designed to push the solo player to the limit. It's especially difficult as a melee class due to the uneven terrain. The hills here require special attention. You will have to learn where you can and can't go through trial and error and jumping around a bit. It's tricky when you're also negotiating caster mobs you may not be able to attack due to the terrain (if you're a melee). The boss has an aoe fear that extends perhaps 40 yards out and you are forced to take her on with three \"friendly\" npcs. These npcs will scatter in all different directions during the fear drawing several adds, even if you've done a good job clearing the area. The aoe fear has to be interrupted or you're dead.\n\nThe terrain is really the decisive factor here. On even ground this would be a welcome challenge.\n\nUnless you're content to die multiple deaths, just do yourself a favor and skip this one.",
            date = "2010-12-27T17:44:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27831#comments:id=1262424",
        },
        {
            id = 1345601,
            score = 11,
            author = "Jaunter",
            text = "This is a very glitchy quest for quite a few reasons.  I will list them below.\n\n1) There is no reasonable way to get into the area unless you go up the paths to kill the previous two pocket bosses in the chain and literally jump down into the area.\n\n2) The hunter pet in your \"party\", the viking hunter likes to disappear from the party for some odd reason.  This leaves you effectively with only two npc party members to help you out.\n\n3) The respawn rate and density of the whelps is just flat out insane.  Super fast respawn rate and they're packed in very dense.  It almost reminded me of the dailies in the Sunwell area during the heyday of the Burning Crusade expansion.\n\n4) Although the interrupts can be done between your character and Eric's charge, it has to be timed precisely because of cooldowns.\n\n5) The whole quest is just simply over-tuned and leaves very little margin for error.\n\n6) The whole chain was fun all the way up until this final quest.  Then it just turned into an exercise in frustration.  I can see ramping up the difficulty as you get to the end of the chain, but this final one was orders of magnitude much more difficult than the one just before it.  Not sure what the Blizzard developer's rationale was for the insanely ramped up difficulty of this one.",
            date = "2011-02-22T02:55:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27831#comments:id=1345601",
        },
    },
    [27832] = {
    },
