    [27893] = {
        {
            id = 1411803,
            score = 13,
            author = "617575",
            text = "The bars for these guys will REPLACE your pet bar, so hopefully you don't need your pet.\n\nThe awesome part? When I mounted, so did they - on motorcycles! :P",
            date = "2011-05-07T00:33:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27893#comments:id=1411803",
        },
        {
            id = 1893180,
            score = 4,
            author = "Freeboosie2791",
            text = "Took me forever to get these guys to follow me.\n\n1. If you are in any kind of combat they will not follow you.\n2. If you have a pet, you must dismiss your pet and abandon and re-pickup quests to get them to follow you.\n3. If you try to summon your pet after they are following you it will temporarily replace one of them with your pet before dismissing your pet and replacing it with the one that disappeared.\n\n*The reason they take the place of your pet is because they all 3 have abilities which are usable from your pet bar, using each of their abilities is a part of the quests.\n\nAlthough with all of these abilities they are very helpful when going against single targets, it is kind of inconvenient when going against multiple targets due to the fact you cannot direct them to a particular target. This is especially true if youre using a minion as a tank.\n\nThey also do NOT attack at all (with the exception of their abilities, which will be used upon clicking) until you yourself take damage from the enemy. Which can be very frustrating when attacking from ranged. Even if you use the tanks Taunt ability, it will not taunt anything until you have taken damage from the enemy.\n\nOn a brighter note they all ride motorcycles when you mount up, its pretty sweet :). Orc Mercenary Motorcycle Gang FTW!",
            date = "2013-09-06T00:50:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27893#comments:id=1893180",
        },
        {
            id = 5963386,
            score = 3,
            author = "Mowse89",
            text = "With being able to edit your UI, I was really confused with this one. All the comments about pets finally helped me realize that you need to use the Pet Bar to use the items and have them attack a mob. Hope this helps!",
            date = "2024-09-19T19:47:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27893#comments:id=5963386",
        },
        {
            id = 1560790,
            score = 2,
            author = "Schnoodledorfer",
            text = "I was already in combat when I picked up the quests apparently because I got too close to the dragons fighting the grunts near Gorn while picking up his quest. The three mercenaries wouldn't move at all untilI got out of combat, then they suddenly appeared near me. They didn't even help even though one of the dragons even ran into the inn and attacked me right in front of them. They will help if you enter combat after you already have them accompanying you, though.\n\nThe grunts originally fighting the dragons in front of Gorn are the only ones who will aggro on the dragons trying to invade New Kargath, as far as I can tell.",
            date = "2011-11-02T12:09:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27893#comments:id=1560790",
        },
        {
            id = 1928390,
            score = 2,
            author = "zeni7h",
            text = "A possible reference to the polish metal band Behemoth (with lead vocals/guitar Nergal )",
            date = "2013-12-22T18:11:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27893#comments:id=1928390",
        },
    },
    [27894] = {
        {
            id = 1610268,
            score = 4,
            author = "930436",
            text = "This is easily the most frustrating quest I have ever encountered. (I'm trying it with my undead warlock level 47 main, though.)\n\nI literally lost track of how many times I died trying to kill bloody Kalaran. It was at least five. But the guardians aren't completely useless...\n\nWhat I did was stand in an area that was as clear as possible of raging whelps and soldiers, and I mean clear as in all of them would have been out of range had I tried to make a ranged attack. I attacked Kalaran (with a spell; I don't think anyone cares which one) and as soon as he tried to attack me, I told Gargal to do his \"mighty shout\" to draw the dragon's attention and got the hell out of the way. I kept ordering the guardians to attack, and if I ever attacked him myself and drew Kalaran's aggro, I got Gargal to shout again to take the attention off me.\n\nI did get attacked by one of the raging whelps during the successful attempt at the quest (i.e., finally killing Kalaran), but I cast Bane of Agony on it and it ended up fighting with the demon imp the bane summoned and left me alone. If I hadn't been a demonology warlock, I'd have been screwed. This quest is a massive pain in the ass.\n\nZhanniespal, was the Eastern Plaguelands frustrating quest trying to kill Ix'tar, by any chance?",
            date = "2012-01-11T16:31:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27894#comments:id=1610268",
        },
        {
            id = 1594496,
            score = 3,
            author = "921716",
            text = "I did this quest WITH ALL THREE GUARDIANS INTACT and still could not kill Kalaran the Annihilator. I am a level 47 Druid. I could not complete this quest without the help of my son and his level 85.\n\nThree things happened that caused this quest to fail for me several times:\n\n1. While staying on top of it and self healing, I ran out of mana and died anyway.\n\n2.  Darkflight Soldiers and those baby dragons mobbed us in mid attack. Too much to handle.\n\n3. Ok, so then kill the Soldiers and the baby dragons first seemed like a good strategy. But then Kalaran starts to attack just as I am finishing clearing the area and my health and mana are already low. No time to sit and drink Moonberry juice. Yup, die again.\n\nThis exact same thing happened while questing in the Eastern Plaguelands on another quest. Cannot remember which character I was tryng to kill, though.",
            date = "2011-12-11T13:58:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27894#comments:id=1594496",
        },
        {
            id = 1639214,
            score = 2,
            author = "chexmixultimate",
            text = "Here are some tips for using the mercenaries:\n\nWhen using them, my warlock pet went away. Not sure if this applies for hunters as well? You can't have them both out at the same time.\nIf you are a ranged attacker, they'll do their special attacks on command but they won't auto-attack unless you get near the enemy.\nThey disappear in certain areas... I think if you get too far from New Kargath or the quest area.\nIf they die in combat, they will not rez until you've finished fighting, but they'll come back with full health and mana.\nIf you mount up, they hop on motorcycles. (:",
            date = "2012-03-13T22:17:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27894#comments:id=1639214",
        },
        {
            id = 1594779,
            score = 1,
            author = "911066",
            text = "Having problems myself with my level 49 Warlock. Can't believe yours is the only comment here, zhanniespal. Don't think that the 'Guardians' do much more than be a nuisance. Will try this one again tomorrow.",
            date = "2011-12-12T02:53:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27894#comments:id=1594779",
        },
        {
            id = 1622444,
            score = 1,
            author = "944997",
            text = "to anaralah, thnx so much for that little tip of using the shout. i was about to give up on this quest, but by following yer instructions, killed the stupid dragon in a minute. thnx again.",
            date = "2012-02-06T06:18:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27894#comments:id=1622444",
        },
    },
    [27895] = {
        {
            id = 1483261,
            score = 2,
            author = "AudibleKnight",
            text = "After the previous quest return to New Kargath.\n\nMoldarr can be found inside a hut at [15, 48]\n\nYou can find General Jirakka by climbing the ramp at [16, 46]. You will fight through a couple pairs of enemies to reach a tower at [15,42]. The entrance is protected by 3 mobs, and is clear until you find the General at the top of the tower.\n\nFor some reason the default quest helper directed me to General Jirakka first, before Moldarr. Depending on how long it takes you to climb the path and kill everything, the mobs at the beginning of the path may start to respawn on your return down.",
            date = "2011-07-30T14:32:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27895#comments:id=1483261",
        },
        {
            id = 1639240,
            score = 2,
            author = "chexmixultimate",
            text = "Here are some tips for using the mercenaries:\n\nWhen using them, my warlock pet went away. Not sure if this applies for hunters as well? You can't have them both out at the same time.\nIf you are a ranged attacker, they'll do their special attacks on command but they won't auto-attack unless you get near the enemy.\nThey disappear in certain areas... I think if you get too far from New Kargath or the quest area.\nIf they die in combat, they will not rez until you've finished fighting, but they'll come back with full health and mana.\nIf you mount up, they hop on motorcycles. (:",
            date = "2012-03-13T23:39:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27895#comments:id=1639240",
        },
        {
            id = 1874657,
            score = 2,
            author = "735486",
            text = "Well I dont get it, I walked into New Kargath and obviously a horde npc immediately one-shotted me and now my flag is on.  I had thought it might be some kind of instanced fake New Kargath the way they do in a lot of other quests.",
            date = "2013-07-07T22:22:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27895#comments:id=1874657",
        },
    },
    [27896] = {
        {
            id = 1195863,
            score = 65,
            author = "Flitzy",
            text = "Whoever designed a quest with the most unfriendly terrain, a billion respawning caster whelps, and elite dragon that fears every minute, and a potion on a 2 minute cool-down is nothing more than a masochist. >_<",
            date = "2010-11-29T14:10:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27896#comments:id=1195863",
        },
        {
            id = 1387116,
            score = 30,
            author = "813717",
            text = "I made an account just to rant. If you are a class that is pet reliant (hunter, demo lock) then you are gonna have a hard time, as the game doesn't allow you to use it.\n\nIf I could have one wish, it would be to punch the guy that designed this quest in the face.",
            date = "2011-04-08T17:12:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27896#comments:id=1387116",
        },
        {
            id = 1244198,
            score = 28,
            author = "dementiya",
            text = "This quest was too difficult for me, I ended up giving up on it after the seventh time of dying. -_-",
            date = "2010-12-18T21:00:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27896#comments:id=1244198",
        },
        {
            id = 1261950,
            score = 28,
            author = "felicitous",
            text = "I found this an incredibly annoying and difficult quest. It didn't help that when I died, it took me forever to navigate around the hills to get back to the area. I agree that some of these things are designed by masochists!",
            date = "2010-12-27T12:51:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27896#comments:id=1261950",
        },
        {
            id = 1517507,
            score = 9,
            author = "872348",
            text = "I just ran this quest as a level 50 retribution paladin.\n\nThe group of mercenaries make this very, very easy.\n\nAs of this run, the mage's fireball has no range limit.\n\nI aggro'd Nyxondra from (12.42) with the mage's fireball. It took two shots to get her to engage and fly up to our position. This is the tower area where you kill the elite mob from the previous quest.\n\nFrom there it was just keeping the DPS up and using the mercenaries abilities. Fears weren't an issue, because there were no mobs to run into.\n\nAfter that I cleaned up the broodling mobs for the quest, pulling then as I ran out of the area.",
            date = "2011-09-13T22:59:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=27896#comments:id=1517507",
        },
    },
