        {
            id = 1394446,
            score = 11,
            author = "castorjay",
            text = "Is it possible to not turn this quest in and still get the 60 quests completed for this zone?",
            date = "2011-04-18T20:16:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28031#comments:id=1394446",
        },
        {
            id = 1443159,
            score = 7,
            author = "842119",
            text = "To close this quest just look into the boat on the sea surface",
            date = "2011-06-17T05:26:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28031#comments:id=1443159",
        },
        {
            id = 2252882,
            score = 5,
            author = "HobDawgh",
            text = "Here's a little guide on how to get this fun item:\n\nStart off in Feralas with the quest  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25486 and kill 7 mobs.\nAccept the next quest and \"enjoy\" the boat ride.\nFollow the quests\nComplete the quests https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25515, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25517 & https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25524. To complete  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25517, go downstairs to the Innkeeper, Daisy, buy  Bottle of Grog and simply use it on any goblin. To complete https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25524, kill mobs on the sea floor untill they drop  Pirate's Crowbar and use it the \"house\" you took the quest from.\nComplete the questline to and including quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25585\nGo down the boat and accept the quest  https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28031.\nKeep the quest in your quest log and you will keep this item! Have fun.",
            date = "2015-09-16T10:29:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28031#comments:id=2252882",
        },
    },
    [28032] = {
        {
            id = 1630322,
            score = 43,
            author = "817851",
            text = "If you're 85 and just questing to get gear for your transmog set, to get this quest, you need to open it first. Going to Agnes in Iron Summit will only cause you confusion.\n\nThe quest chain starts at Thorium Advance. Don't go to Thorium Point. Go to Thorium Advance. Do all the quests at Thorium Advance (you'll be tickled at what Lunk does). This will unlock the quests to go to Thorium Point. Once at Thorium Point, do the quests. Don't go running off to do the Burning Steppes quests. Once you finish those quests, you'll unlock the quests at Iron Summit.\n\nLearn from my mistake.",
            date = "2012-02-22T11:04:05-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28032#comments:id=1630322",
        },
        {
            id = 1449150,
            score = 19,
            author = "ZNasty",
            text = "\"\n\nYes, very interesting. Very interesting indeed...\"\n\nDark Iron Dwarf research at its finest.",
            date = "2011-06-23T22:44:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28032#comments:id=1449150",
        },
        {
            id = 1452162,
            score = 9,
            author = "faerogue",
            text = "To get this quest to open up you need to complete Thorium Point quests up to Dark Ministry. You will then be sent to Iron Summit to talk to the Mountain-Lord, once you do that you'll be able to get this quest.",
            date = "2011-06-27T17:47:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28032#comments:id=1452162",
        },
        {
            id = 5330460,
            score = 2,
            author = "ScreamOutTears",
            text = "Start with \"A New Master... But Who?\" follow the storyline till \"Dark Ministry\". When u complete this Quest u can take this Quest.",
            date = "2022-02-25T11:17:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28032#comments:id=5330460",
        },
        {
            id = 6142376,
            score = 1,
            author = "Hollyleaves",
            text = "I come from the summer of 2025 during TWW...\nIf you're flying in as a high level and haven't really done any work in Searing Gorge, you gotta start from the start:\n\nFIRST:\nGo to Thorium's Advance, and take the first two quests from Jack Rockleg:\nA New Master...But Who?\nDig-Boss Dinwhisker\n\n(Other quests are available, but if you just want to get to Agnes, just do those two. If stuck take the two quests and complete and Rockleg so he will give you: Thorium Point: The Seat of the Brotherhood. Take it and go to Overseer Oilfist at Thorium Point.\n\nOnce there, talk to Overseer Oilfist, and take and complete:\nRasha'krak (not sure, but might be optional, for me it seemed to open the next NPCs)\nThen after that, talk to Hansel Heavyhands, take and complete:\nHeat That Just Don't Quit\nCure These Fat Fingers\nTalk to Taskmaster Scrange, take and complete:\nRecon Essentials\n\nAfter completing those, talk to Hansel Heavyhands and do:\nDark Ministry\nCompleting it will give you the achievement progress The Seat of the Brotherhood\n\nTake In the Hall of the Mountain Lord to lead you to Iron Summit.\nOnce completed, more quests will crop up, including Agnes!\n\nShe offers Mysteries of the Fire Gizzard.\nIn all, 8 quests to get to her from around the zone.\n\nNOTE: Completing this and subsequent quests to get the Flirtation Regalia will also award you the other armor pieces, so no need to do these on another other characters. All will benefit from one character doing the work.",
            date = "2025-07-13T17:50:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28032#comments:id=6142376",
        },
    },
