    [28196] = {
        {
            id = 1414220,
            score = 15,
            author = "Angelusmorti",
            text = "It is interesting to note that the contents of this journal directly contradict several pre-Cataclysm quests in HIllsbrad that targeted Citizen Wilkes, the Farmers, and the others.",
            date = "2011-05-09T19:22:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28196#comments:id=1414220",
        },
        {
            id = 1858267,
            score = 15,
            author = "1073160",
            text = "I think my only question is; WHY are we giving this journal to Stillwater, which it's pretty much damning?  Shouldn't we give it to like....I dunno, someone who will call Syl?  Seems like some bad stuff is going on here....Bad stuff even the Queen would get ticked off at.",
            date = "2013-05-26T12:24:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28196#comments:id=1858267",
        },
        {
            id = 1821177,
            score = 12,
            author = "Farsoul",
            text = "The quest item that starts this quest drops from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=47789.",
            date = "2013-03-05T08:06:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28196#comments:id=1821177",
        },
        {
            id = 1916724,
            score = 8,
            author = "299678",
            text = "Journal of Clerk Horrace Whitesteed (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2448/)\n\nThe Battle for Hillsbrad\n\n=============\n\nDay 12\n\nWe just received word that Southshore has been lost. The Forsaken (http://www.wowhead.com/race=5) war machine is too powerful. We are no match for their chemical weapons. I will attempt, however futilely, to keep this journal (http://www.wowhead.com/item=63249) updated. I must record these atrocities for posterity.\n\nDay 16\n\nMany of the farmers and residents of Hillsbrad (http://www.wowhead.com/zone=267) fled. Some attempted to venture east to Arathi Hightlands (http://www.wowhead.com/zone=45). They never made it. Slaughtered before they reached Thoradin's Wall. Many went north to seek refuge in Silverpine Forest (http://www.wowhead.com/zone=130). They walked right into the heart of enemy territory! Insane, I know, but they claim that the Worgen (http://www.wowhead.com/race=22) are on our side. Last I heard they made it to Fenris Isle. We lost contact with them after that. Worgen? Could it be true....\n\nDay 19\n\nWe knew our time was limited. We evacuated everyone that we could, but Burnside (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2335) stated that he would go down with Hillsbrad. We all agreed to stand by his side. Magistrate Burnside, Citizen Wilkes (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2449), Blacksmith Verringtan (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2404/) and the farmers, Getz (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2403), Kalaba (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2451), and Ray (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=232) remain here as well as a few dozen farmhands (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=2360/).\n\nDay 20\n\nThe Hillsbrad Fields are no more. Those that did not flee were captured. The Forsaken have declared us all prisoners of war. We are to be laborers at their new plantation.\n\nDay 25\n\nThey incinerated our farms and made us watch. Construction begins tomorrow.\n\nDay 40\n\nConstruction of their plantation is nearly complete. This place resembles no farm or plantation I've ever seen.\n\nDay 41\n\nThe Warden of the plantation, Stillwater (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=47781), arrived today. He lined us all up and gave us medical examinations. Nobody knows what's going on.\n\nDay 45\n\nWe've started laboring in the sludge fields. They grow poisonous mushrooms in fetid water and muck.\n\nDay 50\n\nI hear screams coming from the Warden's manor. People are starting to disappear (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=47859).\n\nDay 52\n\nI overheard some guards talking about the farmers, Ray, Getz and Kalaba. Something terrible (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=47793) has happened to them -- of this I am certain.\n\nDay 60\n\nThose of us that remain are scared for our lives. Some of the farmers claim to have seen ghouls (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=47861) running amok at night.\n\nDay 61\n\nA strange turn of events today: a master apothecary from Tarren Mill arrived. From what little information I am able to gather he is here to supervise the operations. Lydon (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=47900) is his name.\n\nDay 62\n\nMaster Apothecary Lydon was dragged away by Stillwater's guards. He was yelling and screaming that the Dark Lady (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=10181) would have Stillwater's head (http://www.wowhead.com/item=63330/) for this. What is he talking about (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28237), I wonder?\n\nDay 63\n\nI saw them take away Burnside and Verringtan last night. I can only assume that I'm next.",
            date = "2013-11-10T11:27:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28196#comments:id=1916724",
        },
        {
            id = 2501898,
            score = 2,
            author = "Ringthane",
            text = "Make sure you have room for the quest item before you kill the guy.  I didn't have room the first time on one of my alts and it said the quest failed since I couldn't get the drop.  So now I've killed him two more times and nothing.  So once again, here's another situation from Cataclysm where I have two-thirds of a zone to complete, and no quests or any way to get quests to continue the extremely linear quest chains.\n\nI swear, if they said tomorrow \"We're removing Cataclysm content from the game and just pretending it never happened\", no one would miss it.",
            date = "2017-06-17T14:08:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28196#comments:id=2501898",
        },
    },
    [28197] = {
        {
            id = 1180207,
            score = 126,
            author = "viciouser",
            text = "Citizen Wilkes is on top of the little gardens structure with the chem set in it south end of the field in the southern most field.",
            date = "2010-11-24T04:14:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28197#comments:id=1180207",
        },
        {
            id = 1197072,
            score = 26,
            author = "347628",
            text = "If anyone else is as dense as me and didn't find him despite the descriptions above, he's in the field with the screaming humans on top of the minihut most further away from the house.\n\nI guess he's supposed to jump down and attack you or something, but since you won't aggro him at lvl 80 it's very to spot his crouching figure on the top of the hut.",
            date = "2010-11-30T03:20:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28197#comments:id=1197072",
        },
        {
            id = 1666850,
            score = 19,
            author = "942150",
            text = "If you still have trouble finding citizen wilkes, then just go into the same field you found clerk horrace whitesteed in and type /target citizen wilkes into chat. Then turn the target option on for the minimap, and walk to the spot shown on your minimap. Then, look up :D It took me ages as a rogue because i didn't unstealth, and so didn't aggro him when i walked close :)",
            date = "2012-05-14T11:30:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28197#comments:id=1666850",
        },
        {
            id = 1225673,
            score = 15,
            author = "30584",
