        {
            id = 1642339,
            score = 11,
            author = "drend",
            text = "Okay to make this somewhat easier for those of you looking for this item for a rogue twink.\n\nThese are the quests I did to get to this quest:\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=28096 (Skipping the first quest or two)\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=28111\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=28138\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=28192 (Again skipping the first quest or two)\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=28196\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=28197\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=28206\n\nOnly after all of these quests was I able to get this quest.  I am not sure if they are all necessary but I know that you cannot get Little Girl Lost without the prior three.  And I'm pretty sure you cannot see No One Here Gets Out Alive without at least doing Welcome to the Machine.\n\nHope this helps.",
            date = "2012-03-21T20:16:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28209#comments:id=1642339",
        },
        {
            id = 1374889,
            score = 5,
            author = "Varyss",
            text = "In this building, you have Johnny Awesome on the right and Master Apothecary Lydon on the left. The building in question is another site of the repeated strikes made by the Blizzard pop-culture machine. If you take the titles of these NPCs away, you get the name John(ny) Lydon, better known as Johnny Rotten, the singer for the Sex Pistols. ;)",
            date = "2011-03-24T09:45:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28209#comments:id=1374889",
        },
    },
