    [28225] = {
        {
            id = 1411964,
            score = 10,
            author = "617575",
            text = "This quest really ticks me off. I'm Exalted with the Thorium Brotherhood so what, exactly, do I have to prove?\n\nProve yourself, Stebben!",
            date = "2011-05-07T05:22:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28225#comments:id=1411964",
        },
        {
            id = 1262511,
            score = 3,
            author = "wharris",
            text = "Guide to Burning Steppes quests:\n\nOptional breadcrumbs:\nHero's Call: Burning Steppes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28666) or Mouton Flamestar (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28514)\n\nDo anytime before leaving to Chiselgrip:\nDone Nothing Wrong (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28172)\n\nKeeshan is back with either:\n    Burning Vengeance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28416) if you did the Redridge chain or Burning Vengeance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28174) if you did not.\n\nThese three at once:\n  Stocking Up (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28177)\n A Future Project (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28178)\n Mud Hunter (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28179)\n\nThen:\nThe Sand, the Cider, and the Orb (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28180)\n\nThese two at once: Warlocks Have the Neatest Stuff (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28181) and Shadow Boxing (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28182)\n\nThen:\nReturn to Keeshan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28183)\nChiselgrip, the Heart of the Steppes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28184)\n\nEnables these quests, which must be completed before General Thor'izog in the main chain:\nProve Yer Allegiance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28225)\nScrapped Golems (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28226) (leads to Golem Training (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28227))\n\nMain chain continues:\nA Needle in a Hellhole (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28254)\nA Perfect Costume (4 versions) Read the quest carefully. What creature disguise do you need?\n  --->    Orc (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28202) (given to Humans and Dwarves): 2 Hides, 4 muds, 2 thread\n  --->    Goblin (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28204) (given to Gnomes): 1 hide, 3 mud, 4 thread\n  --->    Troll (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28205) (given to Night Elves): 3 Hides, 2 mud, 1 thread\n  --->    Ogre (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28203) (given to Draenei and Worgen): 4 Hide, 1 Mud, 3 thread\n\nThen:\nInto the Black Tooth Hovel (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28239)\nGrunt Work (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28245)\n  Look in your quest log -- Strategic Cuts (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28246) has silently appeared\nThe Kodocaller's Horn (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28252)\nTaking the Horn for Ourselves (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28253)\nUntil Blizzard fixes it, when you turn in this quest, you will get a failed quest sound\n  with \"You don't meet the requirements for that quest\". Don't panic.\n\nYou must by this time have finished Stebben's quests, listed above.\nGeneral Thorg'izog (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28265)\nTrial by Magma (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28266)\nI Am the Law and I am the Lash (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28278) [I think this completing this one is optional]\n  When you accept the above, look for Abuse of Power (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28279) in your quest log\n\nThen:\nEnough Damage for One Day (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28286)\nMorgan's Vigil (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28310)\n\nCompleting that quest allows for these four together:\nSEVEN! YUP! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28415) [rewards Tiny Flamefly (http://www.wowhead.com/item=66080)]\nBlackened Ashes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28311)\nA Heap of Delicious Worg (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28313)\nLatent Demons of the Land (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28312)\n\nThen these three together:\nBlood Tour (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28314)\nDraconic Vanguard (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28315)\nA Deal with a Dragon (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28316)\n\nGiven when third one above is completed: Placing the Pawns (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28326)\n\nThen these three:\nA Delivery for Thorg'izog (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28317)\nA Delivery for Neeralak (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28318)\nA Delivery for Zi'lun (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28319)\n\nAuto-accepted when above three are done:\n Locked and Loaded (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28327)\n\nAnd the epic conclusion:\nAssault on Dreadmaul Rock (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28320)\nGlory Amidst Chaos (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28321)\nThe Spoils of War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28322)",
            date = "2010-12-27T18:10:05-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28225#comments:id=1262511",
        },
        {
            id = 1641233,
            score = 1,
            author = "735207",
            text = "Rep is not 250 as stated; I just did the quest and got 1200 rep with guild and bonus for human, so it appears to be 1000 now if you have no buffs.",
            date = "2012-03-18T18:43:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28225#comments:id=1641233",
        },
        {
            id = 2854807,
            score = 1,
            author = "Aerynsun8449",
            text = "This quest made me laugh. Well, now since Battle for Azeroth is live and we can play Dark Iron Dwarfs I mean. I'm a Dark Iron Dwarf, and this quest wants me to \"prove my allegiance\" by killing. . . Dark Iron Dwarfs. Once again, as with the Highmountain Tauren and Nightborne, Blizzard programmers didn't think things through completely. In legions, after Mayla sends me out to the world as a level 20 Highmountain Tauren to help the Horde, and I come back at level 100 to be told by Oro where Mayla is and exactly who Mayla and Huln Highmountain are. As a Nightborne, after Thalyssra sends me out as a level 20 Nightborne and I return at level 100, not only do I get to learn all about the Nightborne and what they went though, but I also have to wear a masquerade mask when I enter Suramar so I can look like, get this, a Nightborne.\n\nAnd here, as a Dark Iron Dwarf, I have to prove my allegiance by killing my brothers and sisters. No, I'm not a traitor, no I'm not a spy. I'm simply questing to assist the Alliance in their Battle for Azeroth. I think Blizzard programmers need to brush up on World of Warcraft lore before they write these things. Granted, this is OLD content. And at the time we WERE fighting the Dark Iron Dwarfs. But they've updated many things to accommodate the new expansions. Yet, they leave this kind of stuff, both in Legions and now BfA to \"break\" lore. Wow, to say the least.",
            date = "2018-11-24T20:16:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28225#comments:id=2854807",
        },
    },
    [28226] = {
        {
            id = 1181156,
            score = 79,
            author = "Samse89",
            text = "Killing the War Reavers will sometimes spawn a War Reaver Parts next to it that you can loot and choose one of two items that you need.\n\nEDIT: Since people confirms it, ALL of them does it.",
            date = "2010-11-24T10:47:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28226#comments:id=1181156",
        },
        {
            id = 1182662,
            score = 55,
            author = "penguinsane",
            text = "The Stone Power Cores are a \"rare\" drop, indicated by the quest text. If you see one, pick it up! Until then, keep killing War Reavers and checking the War Reaver Parts for it.",
            date = "2010-11-24T18:54:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28226#comments:id=1182662",
        },
        {
            id = 1188889,
            score = 17,
            author = "Tirasmol",
            text = "Just to clarify what the above posters have said -  You must first kill the War Reavers (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=7039) then look on the ground near the body for a mechanical part.  You may have to kill several reavers before you find one of the parts nearby.\n\nYou need to gather three each of the piston, sieve and gearshaft, and one stone power core.  Once you open the piece, it will display only two options for you to select.  Read them carefully so that you can choose a part you don't already have.",
            date = "2010-11-26T21:25:42-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28226#comments:id=1188889",
        },
        {
            id = 1925491,
            score = 9,
            author = "Anedill",
            text = "The parts they drop seem to  spawn at your feet or hooves. :D",
            date = "2013-12-12T16:58:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28226#comments:id=1925491",
        },
        {
            id = 2558507,
            score = 9,
            author = "Heidimus73",
            text = "If you want to be nice to other players, leave the parts, when you have enough of the ones you can choose. This way other players can get the items, instead of you having extras for no use :)",
            date = "2018-03-18T12:25:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28226#comments:id=2558507",
        },
    },
    [28227] = {
        {
            id = 5458520,
            score = 38,
            author = "Cincaid",
            text = "Currently bugged in the Dragonflight pre-patch, at least at level 60. The golems just stay hostile without giving you quest credit, making it impossible to complete the quest. I even tried using the Soft Foam Sword, thinking I bugged it because of too much damage, but no luck.\n\nShame when trying to complete the quests in the area for achievement.",
            date = "2022-10-26T09:24:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28227#comments:id=5458520",
        },
        {
            id = 1188919,
            score = 23,
            author = "Tirasmol",
            text = "Talk to any one of the Chiseled Golems (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=48037) around Chiselgrip to start their training.  The golem will become hostile and attack using basic unarmed skills.  Once defeated, the golem will pause and re-calculate its battle strategy.  Then it will restore its health to full and attack you again, but this time it will use an ability called Heave (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=91314).  Defeat the golem a second time.  The golem will heal itself once more and attack using an ability called Flame Blast (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=91313).  Beat the golem one more time and it will tell you that it has enough training and despawn.  Do this on three more golems to complete the quest.",
            date = "2010-11-26T21:41:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28227#comments:id=1188919",
        },
        {
            id = 1189170,
            score = 18,
            author = "Znuff",
            text = "You can fight more than 1 golem at a time, and you get the correct credit.",
            date = "2010-11-27T00:05:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28227#comments:id=1189170",
        },
        {
            id = 1244356,
            score = 15,
            author = "729828",
            text = "The golems say some fairly amusing things when defeated, such as:\n\n\"Defeated. Shame level: High. Adjusting strategy for future battles.\"\n\"Battle result: embarassing failure. Incorporating new methods into battle regimen.\"\n\"Beatdown recieved. Optimizing strategy for next battle...\"\n\"Pummeling recieved. Adjusting battle parameters...\"",
            date = "2010-12-18T22:48:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28227#comments:id=1244356",
        },
        {
            id = 1262502,
            score = 8,
            author = "wharris",
            text = "Guide to Burning Steppes quests:\n\nOptional breadcrumbs:\nHero's Call: Burning Steppes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28666) or Mouton Flamestar (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28514)\n\nDo anytime before leaving to Chiselgrip:\nDone Nothing Wrong (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28172)\n\nKeeshan is back with either:\n    Burning Vengeance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28416) if you did the Redridge chain or Burning Vengeance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28174) if you did not.\n\nThese three at once:\n  Stocking Up (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28177)\n A Future Project (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28178)\n Mud Hunter (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28179)\n\nThen:\nThe Sand, the Cider, and the Orb (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28180)\n\nThese two at once: Warlocks Have the Neatest Stuff (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28181) and Shadow Boxing (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28182)\n\nThen:\nReturn to Keeshan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28183)\nChiselgrip, the Heart of the Steppes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28184)\n\nEnables these quests, which must be completed before General Thor'izog in the main chain:\nProve Yer Allegiance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28225)\nScrapped Golems (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28226) (leads to Golem Training (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28227))\n\nMain chain continues:\nA Needle in a Hellhole (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28254)\nA Perfect Costume (4 versions) Read the quest carefully. What creature disguise do you need?\n  --->    Orc (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28202) (given to Humans and Dwarves): 2 Hides, 4 muds, 2 thread\n  --->    Goblin (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28204) (given to Gnomes): 1 hide, 3 mud, 4 thread\n  --->    Troll (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28205) (given to Night Elves): 3 Hides, 2 mud, 1 thread\n  --->    Ogre (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28203) (given to Draenei and Worgen): 4 Hide, 1 Mud, 3 thread\n\nThen:\nInto the Black Tooth Hovel (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28239)\nGrunt Work (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28245)\n  Look in your quest log -- Strategic Cuts (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28246) has silently appeared\nThe Kodocaller's Horn (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28252)\nTaking the Horn for Ourselves (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28253)\nUntil Blizzard fixes it, when you turn in this quest, you will get a failed quest sound\n  with \"You don't meet the requirements for that quest\". Don't panic.\n\nYou must by this time have finished Stebben's quests, listed above.\nGeneral Thorg'izog (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28265)\nTrial by Magma (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28266)\nI Am the Law and I am the Lash (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28278) [I think this completing this one is optional]\n  When you accept the above, look for Abuse of Power (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28279) in your quest log\n\nThen:\nEnough Damage for One Day (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28286)\nMorgan's Vigil (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28310)\n\nCompleting that quest allows for these four together:\nSEVEN! YUP! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28415) [rewards Tiny Flamefly (http://www.wowhead.com/item=66080)]\nBlackened Ashes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28311)\nA Heap of Delicious Worg (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28313)\nLatent Demons of the Land (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28312)\n\nThen these three together:\nBlood Tour (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28314)\nDraconic Vanguard (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28315)\nA Deal with a Dragon (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28316)\n\nGiven when third one above is completed: Placing the Pawns (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28326)\n\nThen these three:\nA Delivery for Thorg'izog (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28317)\nA Delivery for Neeralak (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28318)\nA Delivery for Zi'lun (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28319)\n\nAuto-accepted when above three are done:\n Locked and Loaded (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28327)\n\nAnd the epic conclusion:\nAssault on Dreadmaul Rock (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28320)\nGlory Amidst Chaos (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28321)\nThe Spoils of War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28322)",
            date = "2010-12-27T18:08:00-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28227#comments:id=1262502",
        },
    },
