            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28321#comments:id=1808272",
        },
        {
            id = 1202864,
            score = 31,
            author = "218896",
            text = "I'd just like to point out that John J. Keeshan is a huge hinderance to stealth classes, he will follow you and aggro any mobs while you're stealthed not allowing you to restealth untill the said mobs have died.\n\nThis makes what could potentially be a perfect quest for a Rogue/Druid into a huge PITA.",
            date = "2010-12-02T19:44:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28321#comments:id=1202864",
        },
        {
            id = 1661876,
            score = 29,
            author = "982421",
            text = "General Thorg'izog -- Inside Firegut Furnace:  Cave Entrance:    65.0, 46.6\n\nDragon-Lord Neeralak -- Bridge that leads to the top:  64.3, 37.4  Cave Entrance at top:    68.8, 44.1\n\nHigh Warlock Xi'lun -- Inside Skull Warren:  Cave Entrance:    70.8, 38.1",
            date = "2012-05-02T18:09:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28321#comments:id=1661876",
        },
        {
            id = 1194746,
            score = 23,
            author = "Chancakes",
            text = "All of the orcs can be found in the same positions as previously in the questline - the orcs have just swapped posts.\n\nDragon-Lord Neeralak is located in the cave on top of Dreadmaul Rock.\n\nGeneral Thorg'izog is located in the cave on the west side of the mountain.\n\nHigh Warlock Xi'lun is located in the cave on the east side of the mountain.",
            date = "2010-11-29T01:20:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28321#comments:id=1194746",
        },
        {
            id = 2361601,
            score = 15,
            author = "NessieMo",
            text = "Once on the https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28321 or https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28455 quest, the NPCs have moved.\n\nTheir precise locations are as follows for TomTom / Paste users:\n\n/way Burning Steppes 65.27 46.52 Entrance to Firegut Furnace for General Thorg'izog\n/way Burning Steppes 66.48, 40.58.6 General Thorg'izog in Firegut Furnace\n/way Burning Steppes 64.33 37.55 Dragon-Lord Neeralak - Rope bridge, follow twisting path up from here\n/way Burning Steppes 69.01 43.95 Entrance to Dragon-Lord Neeralak's cave\n/way Burning Steppes 70.66 38.33 Entrance to Skull Warren for Xi'lun\n/way Burning Steppes 70.18 47.23 Dragon-Lord Xi'lun (quest marker incorrect)",
            date = "2016-08-04T16:55:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28321#comments:id=2361601",
        },
    },
    [28322] = {
        {
            id = 1262524,
            score = 25,
            author = "wharris",
            text = "Guide to Burning Steppes quests:\n\nOptional breadcrumbs:\nHero's Call: Burning Steppes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28666) or Mouton Flamestar (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28514)\n\nDo anytime before leaving to Chiselgrip:\nDone Nothing Wrong (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28172)\n\nKeeshan is back with either:\n    Burning Vengeance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28416) if you did the Redridge chain or Burning Vengeance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28174) if you did not.\n\nThese three at once:\n  Stocking Up (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28177)\n A Future Project (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28178)\n Mud Hunter (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28179)\n\nThen:\nThe Sand, the Cider, and the Orb (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28180)\n\nThese two at once: Warlocks Have the Neatest Stuff (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28181) and Shadow Boxing (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28182)\n\nThen:\nReturn to Keeshan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28183)\nChiselgrip, the Heart of the Steppes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28184)\n\nEnables these quests, which must be completed before General Thor'izog in the main chain:\nProve Yer Allegiance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28225)\nScrapped Golems (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28226) (leads to Golem Training (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28227))\n\nMain chain continues:\nA Needle in a Hellhole (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28254)\nA Perfect Costume (4 versions) Read the quest carefully. What creature disguise do you need?\n  --->    Orc (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28202) (given to Humans and Dwarves): 2 Hides, 4 muds, 2 thread\n  --->    Goblin (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28204) (given to Gnomes): 1 hide, 3 mud, 4 thread\n  --->    Troll (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28205) (given to Night Elves): 3 Hides, 2 mud, 1 thread\n  --->    Ogre (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28203) (given to Draenei and Worgen): 4 Hide, 1 Mud, 3 thread\n\nThen:\nInto the Black Tooth Hovel (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28239)\nGrunt Work (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28245)\n  Look in your quest log -- Strategic Cuts (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28246) has silently appeared\nThe Kodocaller's Horn (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28252)\nTaking the Horn for Ourselves (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28253)\nUntil Blizzard fixes it, when you turn in this quest, you will get a failed quest sound\n  with \"You don't meet the requirements for that quest\". Don't panic.\n\nYou must by this time have finished Stebben's quests, listed above.\nGeneral Thorg'izog (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28265)\nTrial by Magma (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28266)\nI Am the Law and I am the Lash (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28278) [I think this completing this one is optional]\n  When you accept the above, look for Abuse of Power (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28279) in your quest log\n\nThen:\nEnough Damage for One Day (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28286)\nMorgan's Vigil (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28310)\n\nCompleting that quest allows for these four together:\nSEVEN! YUP! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28415) [rewards Tiny Flamefly (http://www.wowhead.com/item=66080)]\nBlackened Ashes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28311)\nA Heap of Delicious Worg (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28313)\nLatent Demons of the Land (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28312)\n\nThen these three together:\nBlood Tour (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28314)\nDraconic Vanguard (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28315)\nA Deal with a Dragon (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28316)\n\nGiven when third one above is completed: Placing the Pawns (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28326)\n\nThen these three:\nA Delivery for Thorg'izog (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28317)\nA Delivery for Neeralak (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28318)\nA Delivery for Zi'lun (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28319)\n\nAuto-accepted when above three are done:\n Locked and Loaded (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28327)\n\nAnd the epic conclusion:\nAssault on Dreadmaul Rock (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28320)\nGlory Amidst Chaos (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28321)\nThe Spoils of War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28322)",
            date = "2010-12-27T18:12:51-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28322#comments:id=1262524",
        },
        {
            id = 1285940,
            score = 4,
            author = "Werlwind",
            text = "Pretty much spot on :) The NPC hunter you have with you, makes the quests rather easy.",
            date = "2011-01-09T14:01:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28322#comments:id=1285940",
        },
        {
            id = 1952885,
            score = 2,
            author = "gbalkam",
            text = "Again, another needlessly lengthy quest chain to get a gear item that will be of no use by the time you finish the quest chain to get it.   I actually turned my XP off to do this chain to get the mail belt, and only because I was wearing a leather one, with better stats than any mail belt previous to this one.  Around midway, I started thinking.. what the hell am I doing?  I could have xp on, skip this entire chain, and be level 57-58 and using BC items that I can get for nearly nothing from the AH.\n\nOf course, around 60% through I just got plain stubborn and bullheaded and set my mind to get this damn belt even if it took another 3 days.  (playing off and on, as I have a number of other alts to play which take priority over this hunter i am on now).\n\nI admit, I am a bit OCD, like when it comes to chasing prof patterns.. but I gave up chasing lore master after LK came out and all the zones I had finished reset.. and I have no intention of starting over on level 1 quests at level 90. lol.\n\nBTW.. an important note here.. don't log out while wearing the disguise if you are in the caves surrounded by ogres.. it drops off when you log in.",
            date = "2014-03-22T09:56:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28322#comments:id=1952885",
        },
    },
    [28324] = {
        {
            id = 1399561,
            score = 21,
            author = "98367",
            text = "Listen to me Hatcher, you've got to tell them.  The green slimes... they used to be... people!  BLIGHT SLIMES ARE PEOPLE!",
            date = "2011-04-25T20:36:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28324#comments:id=1399561",
        },
        {
            id = 1228746,
            score = 14,
            author = "385619",
            text = "also, more incentive to leave this quest incomplete, samples can be taken from chet, massively reducing his health and damage, making him easily soloable despite Trail of Filth's 2 suggested players.",
            date = "2010-12-12T20:37:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28324#comments:id=1228746",
        },
        {
            id = 1205689,
            score = 10,
            author = "673937",
            text = "If the \"angry-meter\" in the bottom of the screen goes to half full, the Blight Slimes will go hostile.\nThe Slimes will (over time) become less hostile and finally neutral again. That is if you don't let the meter become completely full, then you'll have to suffer the wrath of the Slimes for the rest of the quest.\nThe meter fills when you take samples with the Lethality Analyzer.",
            date = "2010-12-04T07:50:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28324#comments:id=1205689",
        },
        {
            id = 1448460,
            score = 10,
            author = "811184",
            text = "I really love the doodad this puts on my toon's back. Unfortunately, it doesn't render unless you're in HIllsbrad. Still, I refuse to turn in this quest for the time being. :) Just looks too cool.",
            date = "2011-06-23T01:29:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28324#comments:id=1448460",
        },
        {
            id = 1197973,
            score = 8,
            author = "582347",
            text = "Keep this q unfinished until u have defeated Chet from the q \"Trail of Filth\" [quest=28330 domain=www]",
            date = "2010-11-30T13:58:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28324#comments:id=1197973",
        },
    },
