    [28328] = {
        {
            id = 1374892,
            score = 16,
            author = "Zachu",
            text = "This quest is kind of soloable, just get to BRD, take the elevator to the Domicile, then run around and click the books to burn them - its instant click.\nYou will probably die 3-4 times, but it takes less than 20 secs to get back in as the spirit healer is just outside BRD.",
            date = "2011-03-24T09:55:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28328#comments:id=1374892",
        },
        {
            id = 1622336,
            score = 5,
            author = "13930",
            text = "Post-Cata class quest that rewards the T1 helm lookalike.\n\nA list of all classes are as follows:\n\nDeathknight : No T1, no dice.\n\nDruid: Breath of Cenarius (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28343) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Cenarion Helm (http://wowhead.com/item=16834). Both the alliance and the horde gets the quest from the same NPC.\n\nHunter: The Golem Lord's Creations(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28394)/The Golem Lord's Creations(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28461) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Giantstalker's Helmet (http://wowhead.com/item=16846).\n\nMage: The Pyromancer's Grimoire(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28398)/The Pyromancer's Grimoire(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28458) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Arcanist's Crown (http://wowhead.com/item=16795).\n\nPaladin: Weapons of Darkness(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28405)/Weapons of Darkness(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28466)/Weapons of Darkness(Blood Elf) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28473) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Lawbringer's Helm (http://wowhead.com/item=16854), also rewards Blood Elf paladins with the Blood Knight Tabard (http://www.wowhead.com/item=25549).\n\nPriest: Twilight Scheming(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28328)/Twilight Scheming(Blood Elf) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28475)/Twilight Scheming(Goblin) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28478)/Twilight Scheming(Tauren) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28476)/Twilight Scheming(Troll) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28477)/Twilight Scheming(Undead) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28474) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Circlet of Prophecy (http://wowhead.com/item=16813).\n\nRogue: The Dark Iron Army(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28406)/The Dark Iron Army(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28463) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Nightslayer Cover (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16821).\n\nShaman: Slaves of the Firelord(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28401)/Slaves of the Firelord(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28465) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Earthfury Helmet (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16842).\n\nWarlock: Stones of Binding(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28399)/Stones of Binding(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28459) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Felheart Horns (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16808).\n\nWarrior: A Dangerous Alliance(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28393)/A Dangerous Alliance(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28457) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Helm of Might (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16866).\n\nThese rewards are also quite good at their level if you don't have a heirloom helmet for your alt(s). I also have no idea why the horde priests get race specific quests.",
            date = "2012-02-06T02:08:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28328#comments:id=1622336",
        },
        {
            id = 5412834,
            score = 5,
            author = "hungrybrains220",
            text = "Update as of Shadowlands: The quest is now given by Patrice Lancaster at 78.93, 69.78. Inside the house where you go after Exile's Reach. The priests in the Cathedral of Light no longer offer the quest or accept as turn in.",
            date = "2022-08-07T15:30:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28328#comments:id=5412834",
        },
        {
            id = 1376418,
            score = 4,
            author = "733706",
            text = "Well whether you die or not obviously depends on a few things, such as what level you are  and what your spec'd and equipped for.  I didn't pick up this quest until I was a lvl 65 priest (healer) and wondered how successful I would be at doing it solo.\n\nAs was mentioned previously, using the \"mole machines\" to get around inside BRD is really convenient and makes the quest much easier.\n\nThe problem I had was that the mobs in that area are tightly grouped and were \"guarding\" some of the books.  I got mobbed (and killed) once but was able to walk around the room and get enough books to complete the quest without pulling any more of the mobs. There are two books down the stairs to the south that are unprotected.",
            date = "2011-03-26T04:41:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28328#comments:id=1376418",
        },
        {
            id = 1492304,
            score = 2,
            author = "662487",
            text = "Really easy as Discipline. I already had Pain Suppression, shielded and feared them, got it in 3 runs.",
            date = "2011-08-11T05:19:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28328#comments:id=1492304",
        },
    },
    [28329] = {
        {
            id = 1188244,
            score = 22,
            author = "209176",
            text = "The slimes you kill during this quest drop Broken Arrow (http://www.wowhead.com/item=3673)s pretty frequently, which may seem strange unless you're familiar with military terminology. Broken Arrow is US military code for an accident involving nuclear weapons, and the drop is another rather subtle joke from Blizzard.",
            date = "2010-11-26T16:45:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28329#comments:id=1188244",
        },
        {
            id = 1192755,
            score = 15,
            author = "351693",
            text = "When accepting the quest, the caption that shows up underneath the image of the slime reads \"Angry Slime - Perhaps it was beaten as a young slime.\"\n\nIt feels as if the humor that surrounds the Forsaken has gotten much darker with the new quests, something that amuses me to no end.",
            date = "2010-11-28T08:21:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28329#comments:id=1192755",
        },
        {
            id = 1180295,
            score = 9,
            author = "707541",
            text = "This quest is found in a new way added in Cataclysm. Killing an Angry Blight Slime (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=48319) will trigger this quest, allowing you to accept it and kill more.\n\nIn addition, the quest name is a reference to Scrubbing Bubbles cleaning product. It's mascot is a large dome shaped brush with a flat bottom and a smiling face on the front, almost exactly like the mob you kill in the quest.",
            date = "2010-11-24T04:59:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28329#comments:id=1180295",
        },
        {
            id = 1897769,
            score = 7,
            author = "THRobinson",
            text = "Quest Completist indicated that I can only get this quest when doing another quest, so thought I was out of luck. On a whim, I flew over the area (lvl90 at this point) and saw a slime with a red ! over it's head. That started the chain for this quest followed by Trail of Filth (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28330).",
            date = "2013-09-14T10:06:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28329#comments:id=1897769",
        },
        {
            id = 1190340,
            score = 4,
            author = "690735",
            text = "doesnt appear possible to pick this quest up until you have completed studies in lethality. not sure if its a bug or not",
            date = "2010-11-27T11:57:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28329#comments:id=1190340",
        },
    },
    [28330] = {
        {
            id = 1181484,
            score = 28,
            author = "177254",
            text = "I recommend doing this along with the quest Studies of Lethality (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28324) as the quest item debuffs Chet down to 1k hp!",
            date = "2010-11-24T12:33:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28330#comments:id=1181484",
        },
        {
            id = 1169618,
            score = 15,
            author = "FarseerLolotea",
            text = "The objective's name is \"Chet,\" and the phrase \"You're stewed, buttwad!\" appears under his picture when you take the quest.  This is a reference to the 1985 film Weird Science.",
            date = "2010-11-13T03:28:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28330#comments:id=1169618",
        },
        {
            id = 1200990,
            score = 3,
            author = "715868",
            text = "He can be kited to one of the dark rangers, I held the aggro and it registered the kill. Not sure if aggro is needed or not.",
            date = "2010-12-01T20:17:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28330#comments:id=1200990",
        },
        {
            id = 3238714,
