    [28397] = {
        {
            id = 1192874,
            score = 48,
            author = "351693",
            text = "I found that Orkus is much more chatty than Dumass and Johnny Awesome, sometimes spamming me with paragraphs at a time. If you let him stick around for long enough, he'll let you in on some of his secrets.\n\nSome things he says:\n\nI wasn't there, but I heard that Sylvanas died in Silverpine and that her precious val'kyr resurrected her at the cost of their own lives. Know anything about it?\n\n, just between you and me, I never saw the fall of the Lich King. And... well... I've never been to Ulduar. I... well... I am a dungeon explorer. Yes. I prefer exploring dungeons with allies. The pay is excellent and the risk is low.\n\nI liked the worgen better when they were a disorganized mess that you'd run into in small packs. This new Gilnean worgen alliance is much more difficult to deal with.\n\nHillsbrad has changed. Back in my day Hillsbrad was a place of constant battle. The humans and dwarves of Southshore would constantly attack the Horde at Tarren Mill. There were days when you could look out past the intersection at Darrow Hill and see a thousand people battle. Glory days,  - they'll pass you by.\n\nI have heard tale of the Maelstrom itself opening up, threatening to devour the world. Could you imagine such a thing?\n\nI am sorry that I called you puny, . When we first met I thought you were just another one of Darthalia's pawns.\n\nWorgen and dwarves working together... What has the world come to?\n\nVarian Wyrnn... I saw him fight once at Dire Maul. He killed five feral scar yetis with his bare hands. Pretty good for a human, no?\n\nI found Kasha in Icecrown. She was injured and dying. I managed to carry her back to the Shadow Vault where the death knights helped nurse her back to health. We are now the best of friends.\n\nThis place reeks of evil. It must be purged!\n\nIf Ivar Bloodfang is here, where is Darius Crowley?\n\n, you and I are friends.\n\nGarrosh Hellscream: great warchief or greatest warchief?\n\nIf we stop these dwarves and worgen we will be celebrated as great heroes of the Horde!\n\nThe longer you afk with him, the more he has to say it seems : I",
            date = "2010-11-28T09:06:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28397#comments:id=1192874",
        },
        {
            id = 1187337,
            score = 16,
            author = "tmptfate",
            text = "Leads to Heroes of the Horde (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28400) to finish up the quest chain.",
            date = "2010-11-26T10:11:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28397#comments:id=1187337",
        },
        {
            id = 1318590,
            score = 9,
            author = "301240",
            text = "Garrosh Hellscream: great warchief or greatest warchief?\nI think Orkus watches the Colbert Report.",
            date = "2011-02-01T19:55:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28397#comments:id=1318590",
        },
        {
            id = 1554710,
            score = 4,
            author = "Barleduq",
            text = "Since he acts like a pet during this section, I tried just swimming back to shore to see if he'd follow me around and protect me while I did what should be corpse runs to get Halloween candy. Alas, he evaporated about halfway to shore, and didn't show up again till I was back on the island.",
            date = "2011-10-27T00:45:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28397#comments:id=1554710",
        },
        {
            id = 1951829,
            score = 4,
            author = "Morzella",
            text = "For some reason I was rather tickled by how Orkus sometimes reffered to me as quest giver. I wondered if he realised that he was now handing out quests to us. When this quest came up I figured we must appear to Orkus as one of those npc's that will sometimes accompany us. Even worse, I realised due to the nature of how the game works we end up acting like one of those infinetly infurating old school escort npc's. This entier quest Orkus must be think \"Oh Lok'tar why does this idiot keep running ahead of me pulling random things. Just let me pull you!\"",
            date = "2014-03-17T21:01:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28397#comments:id=1951829",
        },
    },
    [28398] = {
        {
            id = 1307833,
            score = 25,
            author = "coedyfaye",
            text = "for those who are having trouble :\n\nfrom the entrance head straight acros the dentention block and upon entering the other side (the halls of law) turn right for an entrance to an arena. complete this event for a special path\nas soon as you reach the top of the ramp out of the Ring of Law immediately turn right twice (turn around) for another ramp up to the ring of law spectators head to the other end for another doorway and turn right and  the end of this hallway is Loregrain along with the 6-8 twilight emissarys\nhope i helped!",
            date = "2011-01-24T10:56:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28398#comments:id=1307833",
        },
        {
            id = 1617955,
            score = 14,
            author = "761762",
            text = "And this is so easy to get to. Go into the main entrance of the instance. Take the mole to the domicile, you are were u need to be. Easie as pie!",
            date = "2012-01-28T10:50:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28398#comments:id=1617955",
        },
        {
            id = 2362644,
            score = 8,
            author = "ladynagini",
            text = "To get to the entrance of black rock depths:\n\nInside blackrock mountain (between searig gorge and buring steppes)  you fly down towards the magma. One of the chains coming from the floating rock in the center leads to a little platform with a blood/high elf character present (those who run MC will recognize him as the npc that takes you straight to molten core). before the little room with the elf, turn right into a cave. At the end of the cave is the entrance to Black rock depths.\n\nOnce inside, take the mole machine to the domicile. there are twilight emissarys all around, and the bridge with all the fire elementals leads in a striaght corridor to the named npc you have to kill.",
            date = "2016-08-07T06:54:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28398#comments:id=2362644",
        },
