            score = 12,
            author = "ladydanielle",
            text = "There are more than 6 of these stones, so you aren't looking for a specific set of items.  You zone in, turn left, go through that gate (remember, they removed the keys a while back, so easy peasy), immediately turn right and go through that gate, then take the door on your left; there's a dwarf standing next to it now.  There is one of the stones in that room, hit the bridge cog in the back of the room, then go up the ramp where the first fireguard paths.  Continue straight into the upper part of the Ring of Law, go around it to the other side, and down that ramp, there will be tons of Twilight humanoids down here, and lots of stones, go right pick up those two, then turn around and go back left and pick up those stones along the way.  Keep going down that left path and you'll cross a bridge  with 2 pairs of Fireguard mobs on each side, once across you'll be in The Domicile, and should be able to grab any remaining Stones you might need.  Hope this helps, once I got in and started wandering around it turned out to be way easier than I thought it would be; enjoy your new mogging piece!",
            date = "2012-04-08T21:30:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28399#comments:id=1650890",
        },
        {
            id = 1313721,
            score = 10,
            author = "775700",
            text = "This quest was solo-able for me as a level 50 Worgen Warlock. I did die three or four times, but my character isn't in a guild so I opted to try it alone instead of using the random dungeon finder.\n\nThat said, the stones as mentioned aren't far into the instance so it's not problematic to get there by yourself. I did have to use howl of terror and the Voidwalker's sacrifice to hit a few of the stones, but that's not too unreasonable considering I'd guess this was intended to be a group affair.\n\nTo sum up the trip, I went in with 100% armor and 0/6 stones captured, and left 53% and ready to turn-in.",
            date = "2011-01-28T21:01:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28399#comments:id=1313721",
        },
    },
    [28400] = {
        {
            id = 1182208,
            score = 169,
            author = "231954",
            text = "Stunning questline. Orkus is the most memorable character in WoW I've ever seen. Such a tragic character and such a bittersweet ending. He almost made me shed a tear.\n\nR.I.P. Orkus.",
            date = "2010-11-24T16:13:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28400#comments:id=1182208",
        },
        {
            id = 2014425,
            score = 163,
            author = "Blitzfeuer",
            text = "This quest is bugged as of 6.0.2\n\nOrkus will leap and kill the Battlemaster and you will not be able to loot the plans. In order to get around this, do the following:\n\n Aggro the bosses by attacking them. They will not deal damage to you\n Speak to Orkus to let him know that you are ready for him to attack.\n Quickly turn and attack the Battlemaster before Orkus can leap to him. Orkus will run to fight the bosses and the Battlemaster will sit in the same spot and regen health making him unkillable for the moment.\n Run over to near where Orkus is fighting and hit the Battlemaster with a ranged attack (you might have to do this twice to get him close enough.)\n Once he's close enough, the battlemaster will no longer regenerate health and you will be able to kill him, loot the plans and complete the quest.",
            date = "2014-10-17T00:47:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28400#comments:id=2014425",
        },
        {
            id = 1494449,
            score = 90,
            author = "81303",
            text = "Q. How do I get this quest?\n\nA. Do the following:\n\nPick up the quest to go to Hillsbrad:\nWarchief's Command: Hillsbrad Foothills! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28089)\nWarchief's Command: Hillsbrad Foothills! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28571)\nDo Welcome to the Machine (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28096)\nGo to Southshore and find Kingslayer Orkus (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=48218) in the water and do:\n*Gurgle* HELP! *Gurgle* (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28345)\nStormpike Rendezvous (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28348)\nKasha Will Fly Again (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28354)\nThe Road to Purgation (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28375)\nThey Will Never Expect This... (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28397)\n\nThen you can do this final quest and get your level 20 twink gear!",
            date = "2011-08-13T23:34:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28400#comments:id=1494449",
        },
        {
            id = 1270466,
            score = 79,
            author = "Sketchie",
            text = "In case if anyone is wondering, here's what happened after you turn in the They Will Never Expect This... quest and accept Heroes of the Horde!. Of course, massive spoilers ahead.\n\nWhen you reach the top of the Purgation Isle, it starts.\n\nKingslayer Orkus says: STOP! GET DOWN, !\nKingslayer Orkus says: Look there, near the map table! The Stormpike Battle Master holds the Alliance battle plans!\nKingslayer Orkus says: I... I have a plan of my own.\nKingslayer Orkus says: I will kill the guard at the table and then I will draw the attention of the trio.\nKingslayer Orkus says: While I have them distracted you get the plans from the guard's corpse. I will call Kasha to pick you up as soon as I see you get the plans.\nKingslayer Orkus says: Do not worry about Orkus, . I... I will be fine.\nKingslayer Orkus says: Tell me when you are ready and we will go!\n\nYou then will have to talk to Orkus and tell him you are ready to go. He will promptly jump at the Stormpike Battle Master and kill him in one shot, and then immediately engage the trio at the tower..\n\nKingslayer Orkus yells: GET THE PLANS AND GO!\nKingslayer Orkus yells: CAN YOU SMELL WHAT THE LOK'TAR IS COOKIN'?\n\nAfter you loot the corpse and get the Alliance Battle Plans...\n\nKingslayer Orkus yells: KASHA, GET  OUT OF HERE!\nKingslayer Orkus yells: FORGET ABOUT ME, KASHA! GO!\n\nKasha will swoop down and pick you up and fly away very briefly before turning back to pick up Orkus. Orkus has rather low health at this point to signify that he is dying. Kasha brings you back to Tarren Mill, and the following happens on the way...\n\nKingslayer Orkus says: K... Kasha... you... came back for me...\nKingslayer Orkus says: You are the best friend that Orkus ever had, . *Orkus coughs*\nKingslayer Orkus says: I... I never knew anyone like you. You saved me, . I... I know it's selfish, but I have something to ask of you.\nKingslayer Orkus says: Please take care of Kasha. Make sure she finds a cold place to live.\nKingslayer Orkus says: Somewhere safe...\n\nKingslayer Orkus dies midflight. Kasha lands in Tarren Mill and High Warlord Cromush approaches you...\n\nHigh Warlord Cromush says: What happened? What have you got in your hands there?\nHigh Warlord Cromush reads the Alliance battle plan.\nHigh Warlord Cromush says: He... He died to get this here?\nHigh Warlord Cromush lifts Orkus' lifeless body up.\nHigh Warlord Cromush says: Do not mourn Orkus. He died with honor... with pride. He died a hero of the Horde.\nHigh Warlord Cromush says: From Lordaeron to Kalimdor, they will know his name and they will sing songs of glory, praising the fallen champion of the Horde.\nHigh Warlord Cromush says: Know that what you did will save hundreds, maybe thousands of lives. You are also a true hero of the Horde, .\n\nBravo, Blizzard, for putting in such an emotional quest that actually bought me to tears.",
            date = "2010-12-31T23:03:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28400#comments:id=1270466",
        },
        {
            id = 1186661,
            score = 75,
            author = "526010",
            text = "I have his quote macro'd to my Blood Fury racial in honor of him.\n\nCAN YOU SMELL WHAT THE LOK'TAR IS COOKIN'?\n\nYou will be remembered Orkus.",
            date = "2010-11-26T03:49:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28400#comments:id=1186661",
        },
    },
    [28401] = {
        {
            id = 1360881,
            score = 19,
            author = "celixi",
            text = "This quest can be soloed as long as you are capable to killing 6k hp elites which are mainly caster mobs (susceptible to interupt). All of them are solo pulls. However, you will need 1 instance reset to get this done.\n\nFirst fireguard - From the instance entrace, go left through a cell door, you will see a fireguard patrolling in circle near a group of anvilrage officers, when it patrols aways from them, you can pull it solo using a range ability and kill it.\n\nSecond fireguard - From where you kill the first fireguard, look for another cell door to the right (not the one you came in from). Past the door you will see a friendly dwarf npc and a door in front of him, go past the door, hugging the right wall, go up the stairs, the mob patrols through this path.\n\nThird fireguard - At the stairs where you killed the second fireguard, go up the stairs to los pull the 3rd fireguard down, where you can kill it in the middle of the stairs, away from groups of mobs.",
            date = "2011-03-08T05:00:51-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28401#comments:id=1360881",
        },
        {
            id = 1271836,
            score = 14,
            author = "752161",
            text = "You need to kill the Fireguards and use the totem on their dead bodies.",
            date = "2011-01-01T18:13:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28401#comments:id=1271836",
        },
        {
            id = 1189598,
            score = 6,
            author = "529539",
            text = "NPC - new coords (patch 4.0.3) 66.31 Dwarwen District",
            date = "2010-11-27T04:48:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28401#comments:id=1189598",
        },
        {
            id = 1178848,
            score = 5,
            author = "CanuckBuck",
            text = "You must first kill them to be able to use the totem on them",
            date = "2010-11-23T18:22:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28401#comments:id=1178848",
        },
        {
            id = 1622328,
            score = 3,
            author = "13930",
            text = "Post-Cata class quest that rewards the T1 helm lookalike.\n\nA list of all classes are as follows:\n\nDeathknight : No T1, no dice.\n\nDruid: Breath of Cenarius (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28343) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Cenarion Helm (http://wowhead.com/item=16834). Both the alliance and the horde gets the quest from the same NPC.\n\nHunter: The Golem Lord's Creations(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28394)/The Golem Lord's Creations(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28461) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Giantstalker's Helmet (http://wowhead.com/item=16846).\n\nMage: The Pyromancer's Grimoire(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28398)/The Pyromancer's Grimoire(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28458) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Arcanist's Crown (http://wowhead.com/item=16795).\n\nPaladin: Weapons of Darkness(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28405)/Weapons of Darkness(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28466)/Weapons of Darkness(Blood Elf) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28473) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Lawbringer's Helm (http://wowhead.com/item=16854), also rewards Blood Elf paladins with the Blood Knight Tabard (http://www.wowhead.com/item=25549).\n\nPriest: Twilight Scheming(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28328)/Twilight Scheming(Blood Elf) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28475)/Twilight Scheming(Goblin) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28478)/Twilight Scheming(Tauren) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28476)/Twilight Scheming(Troll) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28477)/Twilight Scheming(Undead) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28474) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Circlet of Prophecy (http://wowhead.com/item=16813).\n\nRogue: The Dark Iron Army(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28406)/The Dark Iron Army(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28463) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Nightslayer Cover (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16821).\n\nShaman: Slaves of the Firelord(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28401)/Slaves of the Firelord(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28465) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Earthfury Helmet (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16842).\n\nWarlock: Stones of Binding(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28399)/Stones of Binding(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28459) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Felheart Horns (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16808).\n\nWarrior: A Dangerous Alliance(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28393)/A Dangerous Alliance(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28457) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Helm of Might (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16866).\n\nThese rewards are also quite good at their level if you don't have a heirloom helmet for your alt(s). I also have no idea why the horde priests get race specific quests.",
            date = "2012-02-06T02:00:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28401#comments:id=1622328",
        },
    },
    [28405] = {
        {
            id = 1187677,
            score = 20,
            author = "Liri",
            text = "This quest is 'easily' soloable.\n\nGet the weapons off the dwarves outside the instance, enter, use the 'Abandoned Mole machine' to go to the destination 'just past the grim guzzler'.\n\nJump down and start hammering.  The boss will kill you a time or two but the weapon smashing can only be interrupted by his knockbacks.\n\nProfit!",
            date = "2010-11-26T12:58:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28405#comments:id=1187677",
        },
        {
            id = 1378498,
            score = 17,
            author = "Hairband",
            text = "I came here for help and felt some clarification was needed if you're in a group doing BRD anyway.\n\nFirst, I obtained my 5 weapons from the digger NPC's outside the instance's entrance.  Then I went inside and did a full clear.  I did not use a mole machine but if you're going to solo it, that's definitely a nice way, just jump down using the Grim Guzzler option.\n\nThe Dark Anvil is what you're looking for and it is guarded by Lord Incendius and his firelord NPC's.  In order to find him, you have to use the Dark Iron Highway which an area to the left when you first come inside the entrance (use the iron gate immediately to the left of where you enter, and you will see a brick road looking area, with some Dark Iron NPC's and a fire elemental or two and some Dwarven braziers).  It should say \"Dark Iron Highway\" or \"Shadowforge City\" here.\n\nTo the left will be Bael'gar, a magma elemental and to the right will be an open doorway with big ugly faces that looks like the BRD load-up screen.  Follow that pathway killing elementals until you reach the Lord Incendius.\n\nKill him.  Then you just click the weapons from your bag while standing there to break them and they just go away (yay, bag space).  You get credit for your quest, boom, done.\n\nFYI: to get your bearings, beyond the Dark Anvil is the Hall of Crafting where Fineous Darkvire is found.  The Hall of Crafting is a C-shaped spiral that goes to the half-circle hallway and that's connected to the vault room and the Domicile.  So if you find yourself in a party that doesn't do Bael'gar, you can still hopefully navigate this way also. The Domicile is accessible through the Ring of Law, if that's the way you're headed make sure you clear all the way through down to Lord Incendius.",
            date = "2011-03-28T15:53:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28405#comments:id=1378498",
        },
        {
            id = 1342506,
            score = 6,
            author = "473253",
            text = "Just a moderator fyi: when I tried to find this quest to see the reward options, I couldn't find it in the list of Paladin class quests (Database - Quests - Classes - Paladin). Since I didn't know the name of the quest it took me a bit of searching before I finally found it here. Maybe it can be added to the filter? :)",
            date = "2011-02-19T17:00:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28405#comments:id=1342506",
        },
        {
            id = 5467911,
            score = 5,
            author = "krilvyn",
            text = "Wowhead shows the wrong quest giver and coordinates.  It is not Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker.  The quest giver is Ezul'aan in the Training Hall in Stormwind (79,70).  Probably was changed at some point.",
            date = "2022-11-10T08:15:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28405#comments:id=5467911",
        },
        {
            id = 1622347,
            score = 4,
            author = "13930",
            text = "Post-Cata class quest that rewards the T1 helm lookalike.\n\nA list of all classes are as follows:\n\nDeathknight : No T1, no dice.\n\nDruid: Breath of Cenarius (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28343) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Cenarion Helm (http://wowhead.com/item=16834). Both the alliance and the horde gets the quest from the same NPC.\n\nHunter: The Golem Lord's Creations(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28394)/The Golem Lord's Creations(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28461) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Giantstalker's Helmet (http://wowhead.com/item=16846).\n\nMage: The Pyromancer's Grimoire(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28398)/The Pyromancer's Grimoire(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28458) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Arcanist's Crown (http://wowhead.com/item=16795).\n\nPaladin: Weapons of Darkness(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28405)/Weapons of Darkness(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28466)/Weapons of Darkness(Blood Elf) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28473) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Lawbringer's Helm (http://wowhead.com/item=16854), also rewards Blood Elf paladins with the Blood Knight Tabard (http://www.wowhead.com/item=25549).\n\nPriest: Twilight Scheming(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28328)/Twilight Scheming(Blood Elf) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28475)/Twilight Scheming(Goblin) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28478)/Twilight Scheming(Tauren) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28476)/Twilight Scheming(Troll) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28477)/Twilight Scheming(Undead) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28474) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Circlet of Prophecy (http://wowhead.com/item=16813).\n\nRogue: The Dark Iron Army(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28406)/The Dark Iron Army(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28463) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Nightslayer Cover (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16821).\n\nShaman: Slaves of the Firelord(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28401)/Slaves of the Firelord(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28465) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Earthfury Helmet (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16842).\n\nWarlock: Stones of Binding(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28399)/Stones of Binding(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28459) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Felheart Horns (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16808).\n\nWarrior: A Dangerous Alliance(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28393)/A Dangerous Alliance(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28457) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Helm of Might (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16866).\n\nThese rewards are also quite good at their level if you don't have a heirloom helmet for your alt(s). I also have no idea why the horde priests get race specific quests.",
            date = "2012-02-06T02:22:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28405#comments:id=1622347",
        },
    },
    [28406] = {
        {
            id = 1387558,
            score = 16,
            author = "80899",
            text = "There's an easier/faster way to do this than the guides above.\n1. Enter Blackrock Depths.\n2. Walk through the gate on the left.\n3. Immediately turn right, avoid the fire elemental.\n4. Immediately go left, through the door (there's an NPC in front of it).\n5. Poison the sack on the left. If you're low level you will aggro, vanish in combat. Avoid the fire elemental patrol.\n6. Poison the sack on the right. Again avoid the fire elemental patrol.\n7. Go up the ramp completely, poison the sack left from the end of the ramp, avoiding the fire elemental patrol.\n8. Poison remaining sacks lying around guarded by 2 dwarfs. For that Sap one, Blind the other, poison the sack, Vanish. Wait for your Blind and Vanish CD to come back, repeat.\n\nAlso uploaded some screenshots of the item for you :)",
            date = "2011-04-09T10:46:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28406#comments:id=1387558",
        },
        {
            id = 1195121,
            score = 14,
            author = "aryon",
            text = "Pretty easy to solo at level 50 if you don't mind repair costs.\n\nStealth all the way, vanish when you need to, and make sure you're not in the fiery mobs' line of sight.\n\nTo get to the grain sacks go into the instance past the friendly guys, then when you get into the large room go for the first passageway on the left.\nThere's a friendly guy guarding a small door on the right, which is unlocked. Go in and you'll see sacks of grain lying about the place. Find ones that aren't close to the dark iron dwarves and poison them.\n\nWhen you die now it's only a one second corpse run, unlike before patch 4.0.3a when it used to take ages. Thanks Blizzard.",
            date = "2010-11-29T06:29:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28406#comments:id=1195121",
        },
        {
            id = 1506899,
            score = 8,
            author = "Micia",
            text = "This mission almost seems to be designed to be solo'd, given a rogues capabilities. And it suits them too. A secret mission behind enemy lines to poison their foodsupplies.\n\nI wish there were more of these missions.",
            date = "2011-08-30T15:37:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28406#comments:id=1506899",
        },
        {
            id = 1198624,
            score = 5,
            author = "332958",
            text = "Seriously easy to solo (53). Walk into the instance, turn left and go through the door, wait for the fire elemental to pass (stealth makes this easier but isnt needed) and open the second door, go to third door (with the npc named Prospector Seymour) open the door, turn right and use the Fast-Acting Poison on the Grain Ration, turn around and walk along the wall untill you see the second Grain Ration which is to the right by the cannon balls(watch out for the Fireguard patrol) Poison the second Grain Ration, run out, reset, rinse and repeat.",
            date = "2010-11-30T19:08:09-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28406#comments:id=1198624",
        },
        {
            id = 1622332,
            score = 4,
            author = "13930",
            text = "Post-Cata class quest that rewards the T1 helm lookalike.\n\nA list of all classes are as follows:\n\nDeathknight : No T1, no dice.\n\nDruid: Breath of Cenarius (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28343) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Cenarion Helm (http://wowhead.com/item=16834). Both the alliance and the horde gets the quest from the same NPC.\n\nHunter: The Golem Lord's Creations(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28394)/The Golem Lord's Creations(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28461) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Giantstalker's Helmet (http://wowhead.com/item=16846).\n\nMage: The Pyromancer's Grimoire(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28398)/The Pyromancer's Grimoire(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28458) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Arcanist's Crown (http://wowhead.com/item=16795).\n\nPaladin: Weapons of Darkness(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28405)/Weapons of Darkness(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28466)/Weapons of Darkness(Blood Elf) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28473) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Lawbringer's Helm (http://wowhead.com/item=16854), also rewards Blood Elf paladins with the Blood Knight Tabard (http://www.wowhead.com/item=25549).\n\nPriest: Twilight Scheming(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28328)/Twilight Scheming(Blood Elf) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28475)/Twilight Scheming(Goblin) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28478)/Twilight Scheming(Tauren) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28476)/Twilight Scheming(Troll) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28477)/Twilight Scheming(Undead) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28474) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Circlet of Prophecy (http://wowhead.com/item=16813).\n\nRogue: The Dark Iron Army(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28406)/The Dark Iron Army(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28463) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Nightslayer Cover (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16821).\n\nShaman: Slaves of the Firelord(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28401)/Slaves of the Firelord(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28465) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Earthfury Helmet (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16842).\n\nWarlock: Stones of Binding(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28399)/Stones of Binding(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28459) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Felheart Horns (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16808).\n\nWarrior: A Dangerous Alliance(A) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28393)/A Dangerous Alliance(H) (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28457) - Rewards with blue quality lookalike of Helm of Might (http://www.wowhead.com/item=16866).\n\nThese rewards are also quite good at their level if you don't have a heirloom helmet for your alt(s). I also have no idea why the horde priests get race specific quests.",
            date = "2012-02-06T02:05:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28406#comments:id=1622332",
        },
    },
    [28415] = {
        {
            id = 1193256,
            score = 72,
            author = "Nulanna",
            text = "You do not need to be in any other zones. I just started from scratch in Burning Steppes and here are the hubs you need to hit.\n\nFlamestar Post - do all the quests, and in the end it will send you to Chiselgrip\nChiselgrip - Do all the quests in this hub and after Abuse of Power it will send you to Morgan's Vigil\nMorgan's Vigil - As soon as you come here the quest is available to pick up from Oralius\n\nMost of the flameflys can be found if you head towards the Redridge Mountain road - they're all over the place",
            date = "2010-11-28T12:00:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28415#comments:id=1193256",
        },
        {
            id = 1170772,
            score = 52,
            author = "419121",
            text = "Nice to see the Cataclysm hasn't affected Oralius at all, he seems as sane as ever.",
            date = "2010-11-14T11:29:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28415#comments:id=1170772",
        },
        {
            id = 1190675,
            score = 42,
            author = "208337",
            text = "Not Fifty? (For those that don't know, Oralius pre-cat had a quest called \"FIFTY, YEP!\" which had you getting 50 blackrock orc ears, if I recall correctly.\n\n\"Orc is the flavor of the month!\n\nI WILL KILL YOU, WINKY!\"\n\nBest quest giver, ever.",
            date = "2010-11-27T14:27:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28415#comments:id=1190675",
        },
        {
            id = 1262514,
            score = 34,
            author = "wharris",
            text = "Guide to Burning Steppes quests:\n\nOptional breadcrumbs:\nHero's Call: Burning Steppes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28666) or Mouton Flamestar (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28514)\n\nDo anytime before leaving to Chiselgrip:\nDone Nothing Wrong (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28172)\n\nKeeshan is back with either:\n    Burning Vengeance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28416) if you did the Redridge chain or Burning Vengeance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28174) if you did not.\n\nThese three at once:\n  Stocking Up (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28177)\n A Future Project (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28178)\n Mud Hunter (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28179)\n\nThen:\nThe Sand, the Cider, and the Orb (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28180)\n\nThese two at once: Warlocks Have the Neatest Stuff (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28181) and Shadow Boxing (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28182)\n\nThen:\nReturn to Keeshan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28183)\nChiselgrip, the Heart of the Steppes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28184)\n\nEnables these quests, which must be completed before General Thor'izog in the main chain:\nProve Yer Allegiance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28225)\nScrapped Golems (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28226) (leads to Golem Training (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28227))\n\nMain chain continues:\nA Needle in a Hellhole (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28254)\nA Perfect Costume (4 versions) Read the quest carefully. What creature disguise do you need?\n  --->    Orc (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28202) (given to Humans and Dwarves): 2 Hides, 4 muds, 2 thread\n  --->    Goblin (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28204) (given to Gnomes): 1 hide, 3 mud, 4 thread\n  --->    Troll (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28205) (given to Night Elves): 3 Hides, 2 mud, 1 thread\n  --->    Ogre (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28203) (given to Draenei and Worgen): 4 Hide, 1 Mud, 3 thread\n\nThen:\nInto the Black Tooth Hovel (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28239)\nGrunt Work (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28245)\n  Look in your quest log -- Strategic Cuts (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28246) has silently appeared\nThe Kodocaller's Horn (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28252)\nTaking the Horn for Ourselves (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28253)\nUntil Blizzard fixes it, when you turn in this quest, you will get a failed quest sound\n  with \"You don't meet the requirements for that quest\". Don't panic.\n\nYou must by this time have finished Stebben's quests, listed above.\nGeneral Thorg'izog (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28265)\nTrial by Magma (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28266)\nI Am the Law and I am the Lash (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28278) [I think this completing this one is optional]\n  When you accept the above, look for Abuse of Power (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28279) in your quest log\n\nThen:\nEnough Damage for One Day (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28286)\nMorgan's Vigil (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28310)\n\nCompleting that quest allows for these four together:\nSEVEN! YUP! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28415) [rewards Tiny Flamefly (http://www.wowhead.com/item=66080)]\nBlackened Ashes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28311)\nA Heap of Delicious Worg (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28313)\nLatent Demons of the Land (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28312)\n\nThen these three together:\nBlood Tour (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28314)\nDraconic Vanguard (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28315)\nA Deal with a Dragon (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28316)\n\nGiven when third one above is completed: Placing the Pawns (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28326)\n\nThen these three:\nA Delivery for Thorg'izog (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28317)\nA Delivery for Neeralak (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28318)\nA Delivery for Zi'lun (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28319)\n\nAuto-accepted when above three are done:\n Locked and Loaded (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28327)\n\nAnd the epic conclusion:\nAssault on Dreadmaul Rock (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28320)\nGlory Amidst Chaos (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28321)\nThe Spoils of War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28322)",
            date = "2010-12-27T18:11:10-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28415#comments:id=1262514",
        },
        {
            id = 1429184,
            score = 26,
            author = "Vlad",
            text = "To quickly figure out how far you got in the chain for the awesome https://www.wowhead.com/item=66080 companion, simply run this macro (pick the one for [acronym=\"I put both factions on here in case you are visiting the wrong quest on Wowhead.\"]your faction[/acronym]):\n\nAlliance\n/run local i=0 for q in(\"514416172178179177180181182183184254205226225227239246245252253265266278279286310415\"):gmatch(\"%d%d%d\")do q=\"28\"..q i=i+1 print(i,\"\\124Hquest:\"..q..\":0\\124h[#\"..q..\"]\\124h\",IsQuestFlaggedCompleted(q)and COMPLETE or INCOMPLETE)end\n\nHorde\n/run local i=0 for q in(\"417418419420421422423424425426225226227427428432434433435436437438440441442491\"):gmatch(\"%d%d%d\")do q=\"28\"..q i=i+1 print(i,\"\\124Hquest:\"..q..\":0\\124h[#\"..q..\"]\\124h\",IsQuestFlaggedCompleted(q)and COMPLETE or INCOMPLETE)end\n\nI hope this helps you backtrack where to go next! :)",
            date = "2011-05-28T06:41:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28415#comments:id=1429184",
        },
    },
