        },
    },
    [28455] = {
        {
            id = 1193827,
            score = 35,
            author = "528708",
            text = "General Thorg'izog - Western most cave entrance in the back. 66.2, 41.0. Enter cave at 65.0, 46.7.\nDragon-Lord Neeralak - Located on top of Dreadmaul Rock, just inside the cave. 69.1, 44.0.\nHigh Warlock Xi'lun - Eastern most cave entrance (70.8,38.1) Once inside hang a left to 70.1, 47.3.\nOnce completed return to Flame Crest, follow up is a gimme that rewards your choice of two weapons/armor.",
            date = "2010-11-28T15:54:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28455#comments:id=1193827",
        },
        {
            id = 1631390,
            score = 32,
            author = "14690",
            text = "I had an incredibly annoying and possibly (by design?) thing happen at this phase of the quest. While many of the golem and imp mobs were gone en route to Dreadmaul Rock, and I did get to see the green golems guarding the rock, by the time I got close to the Rock, pretty much every mob I didn't kill during the dragon phase was wandering around and could aggro me.\n\nKilling these 3 bosses therefore consisted of me going up the mountain and killing 50+ mobs en route, most of them in packs of 3. Basically, all those mobs that you passed when you were disguised, you now had to kill, plus tons of others. It was nuts!\n\nIt was a tremendous difficulty spike that I don't think was intended. Fortunately I was already level 55 and as a druid I could shift out and heal pretty well. On top of this already long quest chain where you kill literally 500 mobs in Burning Steppes, I was aggravated trying to slog through this last grind of easily 50+ wandering mobs. It look probably 45 minutes of straight pulls and non stop combat to get to these last 3 bosses (who were simple to kill once you reached them), and then fight your way back out.",
            date = "2012-02-25T03:54:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28455#comments:id=1631390",
        },
        {
            id = 2552753,
            score = 12,
            author = "Comradical",
            text = "\"There's three orcs who survived the attack\" My left nut. It really defeats the purpose of all the infiltration, if the last quest is you running past all the mob aggro to assassinate the leader, I could have done that in the first place.\n\nIf I had to guess, I'd say this phase is _supposed_ to be just them, but somebody got lazy/forgot.",
            date = "2018-02-14T20:17:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28455#comments:id=2552753",
        },
        {
            id = 2547352,
            score = 6,
            author = "Chirdis",
            text = "With the new patch 7.3.5 leveling-scaling added, this was horrible.\nIf I still had the option to \"call the dragon\" to clear all the unintended-trash, I totally would.\nI believe the option to hearth-out and return would still work to fix the phasing.\nUnfortunately I learned of that after completing this quest, scarce-fully.",
            date = "2018-01-20T15:37:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28455#comments:id=2547352",
        },
        {
            id = 1554798,
            score = 5,
            author = "Brulath",
            text = "The phasing on this quest will prevent deathwing from killing you, if he decides to visit.  Just leave the phased area and stand in one of the fires that appears to get the achievement.",
            date = "2011-10-27T03:23:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28455#comments:id=1554798",
        },
    },
