        {
            id = 1249558,
            score = 4,
            author = "windstrum",
            text = "If you're Tauren and wondering how you get from Mulgore to Northern Barrens, here's how:\n\n1. Head to the north-western point of Mulgore, called Stonetalon Pass.\n2. Navigate your way past the Grimtotem to the top of the pass. Once at the top, head east along the cliff tops until below you on your left you see Malaka'jin.\n3. Drop down into Malaka'jin, and speak to the flight master to discover the path. Nearby, just to the east, you should see a pathway called The High Road (marked by a sign).\n4. Follow the high road, keeping an eye out on your left for another pathway that leads down to the border between Stonetalon Mountains and Northern/Southern Barrens. The pathway backtracks slightly, so you'll need to look carefully. Head down the path.\n5. Nagivate past the Honor Hold Footmen (level 30 alliance guards). Most of them should be in combat with Horde guards, but you might run into one or two on their own who will attack.\n6. Cut across this area towards Northern Barrens. Once past the Honor Hold Footmen you should be safely in Northern Barrens.\n7. Remember to visit the flight path at the Crossroads. :)",
            date = "2010-12-21T03:49:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28494#comments:id=1249558",
        },
        {
            id = 1681077,
            score = 3,
            author = "BlackMonarch",
            text = "If you've accepted Conscript of the Horde, Preserving the Barrens, and Ak'zeloth, but haven't completed any of them, then \"Warchief's Command: Northern Barrens!\" becomes inaccessible. Once you complete them all, though, it's accessible again. Any idea why?\n\nI'm not sure about what happens if you accept all 3 and only complete some, though...",
            date = "2012-06-25T16:05:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28494#comments:id=1681077",
        },
    },
    [28495] = {
