        {
            id = 1322659,
            score = -2,
            author = "361267",
            text = "If you have The Sands/Dunes Of Silithus (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28859) then this quest is not available...\n\n+\n\nBy Shishire\n\nNote, The Sands/Dunes Of Silithus quest is worth a lot more rep/XP than the Warchief's Command/Hero's Call quest. Since its mutually exclusive, you're better off going with this one. Additionally, since this quest is a continent closer to the zone this gets turned-in in, you should be able to pick this up on your way to the zone.",
            date = "2011-02-05T12:31:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28528#comments:id=1322659",
        },
        {
            id = 1466669,
            score = -3,
            author = "748974",
            text = "This quest should be taken out of the game.  I picked it up in Darnassus and was like \"never done this zone\" before, so I took the boat to Stormwind, the tram to Ironforge, the boat the Theramore, swam across Thousand Needles, hoofed it over Tanaris and Un'goro, and then when I finally arrive....the zone is terrible!\n\nThere are only about 20 quests here and then the main chain ends abruptly and you get the message \"you are not eligible for this quest\" and that's the end of the zone.\n\nTo add insult to injury, the next thing you do is take a portal to Blasted Lands where the first thing the NPC says to you on arrival is \"Silithus not so great, eh?  We get a lot like you.\"\n\nIf the zone doesn't get an update, why send people there only to port them to a better zone on the other side of the world.",
            date = "2011-07-10T22:30:59-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28528#comments:id=1466669",
        },
    },
    [28529] = {
        {
            id = 1194253,
            score = 49,
            author = "Chupathingy",
            text = "The quest explicitly states that being/becoming a Demon Hunter is strongly \"frowned on\" by many of the Night Elves, probably mostly due to Illidan's bad example.\n\nArcane magic is frowned upon by night elves but they can be mages. Demon Hunters are frowned upon because it usually requires the aid of the burning legion to be one.\n\n While unpopularity/hate from the major populace didn't stop other classes to be available (Warlock, Death Knight) I doubt that one single quest involving the ghost of a Demon Hunter foreshades playable Demon Hunters.\n\nwhy? if they haven't announced anything yet, why would they add absurd amounts of foreshadowing? I wonder how many have found their way to him in those ruins is textbook foreshadowing.\n\nBC had you working for an independent one and fight four Demon Hunter trainers, so that doesn't mean much.\nyour right, that doesn't mean much\n\nEven if they are considering a new class after the DK (near-)debacle, a tank class that didn't increase relative tank numbers,\n\nWe still have plans to introduce new Hero classes in the future. (http://www.worldofwarcraft.com/cataclysm/faq/)\nthey are considering it.\n\nwhat would be so unique about a Demon Hunter?\n\nwhat's unique about any class these days? the resource system. i'm sure it wouldn't be that hard to make a good one.\n\nPortions of this lore class have been incorporated into rogues, hunters and warlocks already, so a Demon Hunter as its own class can not really stand out.\n\nso? parts of the death knight existed in the warlock (they even share an ability with the same (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=47541) name (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=6789)) also, hunters haven't taken anything from demon hunters other than the name and tracking demons.\n\nTL:DR\nmy rebuttle to Nathanyel",
            date = "2010-11-28T19:17:23-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28529#comments:id=1194253",
        },
        {
            id = 1276842,
            score = 22,
            author = "387118",
            text = "If you do a 3D view of Illidan and Telarius, you notice some distinct differences side-by-side. Sure, one could chalk up the differences to being \"his demon form\" or something. But take note of the markings. While very similar at first glance, a closer look will show them being very unique of one another. Also, the hair. Telarius's hair is green. Illidan's is black. Ears are slightly different. Again, I suppose this could all be attributed to his demonic influence? But I doubt it.\n\nIMHO: I imagine Telarius was more than likely some poor sap recruit who still had his recruitment flier on him - being that his level is in the mere teens. Especially given the supporting text of this quest. He couldn't hack it, got trapped in the whirlpool or whatever. Died in Deathwing's path and became a ghost, who knows? I'm not the Fact Checker. But it's logical. As for the \"You are not prepared\" bit... hey, it could be the demon hunter motto for all we know.\n\nAlso, Blizz does adore throwing in obscure, but blatant hints. Like the release date of Cataclysm was \"leaked\" intentionally in an obscure reference in-game. Of course, everyone guessed it. This could be a similar not-so-subtle 'hint'.\n\nBlizz has also stated, they do intend on other hero classes, just not \"right now\". I think this was because at the time they were focused on getting Cata launched first. One major catastrophe at a time. heh\n\nPlus, it extends the shelflife of WoW if they can launch one major change at a time, instead of all at once. Then there's all the resources into creating, editing, testing, editing, testing, testing, editing, etcetera, ad nauseum.\n\nDo I believe this to be a hint? Sure! Why not? It's fun to speculate. And if it isn't? So what? I mean, really. You know work doesn't stop when they launch a major expansion. The creators don't sit around and QC what's launched. The thinktanks have already started on the next one, and it's just a matter of time until they unveil what they've decided on. And rest assured, it will have a buggy and rocky start just like every other major upheaval. Besides. They have to have SOMETHING for Blizzcon. I suspect they actually have the next several expansions penciled out, if not more.\n\nUntil then, enjoy the ride. :-)",
            date = "2011-01-04T11:06:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28529#comments:id=1276842",
        },
        {
            id = 1179749,
            score = 21,
