    [28656] = {
        {
            id = 1582986,
            score = 27,
            author = "466885",
            text = "After hunting for this quest for a good 15 minutes on my Holy Paladin, I discovered something that may be of relevance; It appears that you need to be in melee range of the monster to recieve the https://www.wowhead.com/spell=91082 buff.\nI killed several furbolgs (Read: 25+) through ranged means, and didn't get it, however one of them managed to get within melee range of me, and the moment it died I got the buff (and thus the quest).\n\nI have no idea if this is how it actually works, but it might be something you'd wanna try in case you are stuck trying to get the quest and it feels like it's avoiding you somehow.",
            date = "2011-11-29T01:09:48-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28656#comments:id=1582986",
        },
        {
            id = 1583139,
            score = 6,
            author = "Schnoodledorfer",
            text = "When you complete the quest, Witch Doctor Mau'ari tells you to go find \"de E'ko\" on all of the creatures in Winterspring. If you get all seven types of E'ko (depends on the type of creature), you earn the https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=5443 achievement. (If you mouseover that link you can see the seven creature types listed.) This quest (Strange Life Forces) was triggered the first time you got E'ko from one, so you have six more to go after that. Each type gives a different buff, too.",
            date = "2011-11-29T07:06:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28656#comments:id=1583139",
        },
        {
            id = 1270660,
            score = 5,
            author = "110727",
            text = "I got the quest while doing Archeology and figured, \"Why not?\"  Went to go complete it with the doc and he was hostile to me.  So what do I do?",
            date = "2011-01-01T02:29:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28656#comments:id=1270660",
        },
        {
            id = 1875598,
            score = 2,
            author = "sickbox",
            text = "I had been hoping for this quest for quite a bit on my lock.  Came here and found Rexxagon's post which worked wonders.  Killed a Winterfall Totemic at melee range and got the quest immediately... though that only lasted so long.  I dropped the quest and the buff each time, and usually got the quest immediately after a couple of times then nothing for a long long time.  It seems that any of the creatures that will give you a buff for https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=5443 will grant you this quest when the buff is activated.  I think that you can only get the buffs in a certain area X number of times within some kind of time frame, maybe 3 times every 15-20 min. I ditched the Furbolgs after a while and went after Shardtooth bears, the second one gave me https://www.wowhead.com/spell=91992 and the quest popped.\n\nSo at least there is one definite thing: Get the buff; Get the quest.  You just may want to vary your kills between different buff groups if you are taking a bit to get one.  In this case your targets should be: Winterspring Furbolgs, Shardtooth Bears, Frostsabers, Ice Thistle Yeti, Wildkin, Frostmaul Giants, or Chillwind Chimaera",
            date = "2013-07-10T19:59:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28656#comments:id=1875598",
        },
        {
            id = 1583129,
            score = 1,
            author = "Schnoodledorfer",
            text = "You probably need to get the Killing Blow to get the buff that triggers the quest prompt. Pets on passive Locks/Hunters!\nWhy did you conclude that? (ADDED: I found a comments under https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=5443 that said that a pet got a buff that indicates that the E'ko was released, but the hunter didn't get credit. I tested that and saw the same thing happen with the buff one time when I let my hunter's pet kill. It's not clear that a hunter or warlock was even involved in the case of the OP, though.)\n\nEven if you were correct about that, the person that you are replying to said that he didn't want the quest, so your advice would be backwards. Did you accidentally reply to the wrong comment?",
            date = "2011-11-29T06:48:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28656#comments:id=1583129",
        },
    },
    [28666] = {
        {
            id = 1262452,
            score = 19,
            author = "wharris",
            text = "Guide to Burning Steppes quests:\n\nOptional breadcrumbs:\nHero's Call: Burning Steppes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28666) or Mouton Flamestar (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28514)\n\nDo anytime before leaving to Chiselgrip:\nDone Nothing Wrong (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28172)\n\nKeeshan is back with either:\n    Burning Vengeance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28416) if you did the Redridge chain or Burning Vengeance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28174) if you did not.\n\nThese three at once:\n  Stocking Up (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28177)\n A Future Project (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28178)\n Mud Hunter (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28179)\n\nThen:\nThe Sand, the Cider, and the Orb (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28180)\n\nThese two at once: Warlocks Have the Neatest Stuff (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28181) and Shadow Boxing (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28182)\n\nThen:\nReturn to Keeshan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28183)\nChiselgrip, the Heart of the Steppes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28184)\n\nEnables these quests, which must be completed before General Thor'izog in the main chain:\nProve Yer Allegiance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28225)\nScrapped Golems (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28226) (leads to Golem Training (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28227))\n\nMain chain continues:\nA Needle in a Hellhole (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28254)\nA Perfect Costume (4 versions) Read the quest carefully. What creature disguise do you need?\n  --->    Orc (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28202) (given to Humans and Dwarves): 2 Hides, 4 muds, 2 thread\n  --->    Goblin (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28204) (given to Gnomes): 1 hide, 3 mud, 4 thread\n  --->    Troll (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28205) (given to Night Elves): 3 Hides, 2 mud, 1 thread\n  --->    Ogre (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28203) (given to Draenei and Worgen): 4 Hide, 1 Mud, 3 thread\n\nThen:\nInto the Black Tooth Hovel (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28239)\nGrunt Work (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28245)\n  Look in your quest log -- Strategic Cuts (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28246) has silently appeared\nThe Kodocaller's Horn (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28252)\nTaking the Horn for Ourselves (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28253)\nUntil Blizzard fixes it, when you turn in this quest, you will get a failed quest sound\n  with \"You don't meet the requirements for that quest\". Don't panic.\n\nYou must by this time have finished Stebben's quests, listed above.\nGeneral Thorg'izog (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28265)\nTrial by Magma (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28266)\nI Am the Law and I am the Lash (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28278) [I think this completing this one is optional]\n  When you accept the above, look for Abuse of Power (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28279) in your quest log\n\nThen:\nEnough Damage for One Day (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28286)\nMorgan's Vigil (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28310)\n\nCompleting that quest allows for these four together:\nSEVEN! YUP! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28415) [rewards Tiny Flamefly (http://www.wowhead.com/item=66080)]\nBlackened Ashes (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28311)\nA Heap of Delicious Worg (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28313)\nLatent Demons of the Land (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28312)\n\nThen these three together:\nBlood Tour (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28314)\nDraconic Vanguard (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28315)\nA Deal with a Dragon (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28316)\n\nGiven when third one above is completed: Placing the Pawns (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28326)\n\nThen these three:\nA Delivery for Thorg'izog (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28317)\nA Delivery for Neeralak (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28318)\nA Delivery for Zi'lun (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28319)\n\nAuto-accepted when above three are done:\n Locked and Loaded (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28327)\n\nAnd the epic conclusion:\nAssault on Dreadmaul Rock (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28320)\nGlory Amidst Chaos (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28321)\nThe Spoils of War (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28322)",
            date = "2010-12-27T17:57:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28666#comments:id=1262452",
        },
        {
            id = 1845421,
            score = 5,
            author = "syranna",
            text = "wasn't available @lvl53.",
            date = "2013-04-21T04:11:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28666#comments:id=1845421",
        },
        {
            id = 3131471,
            score = 3,
            author = "carsono311",
            text = "I would like to know if it is possible to complete this quest and then accept and complete https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28514 sequentially.  I know some breadcrumb quests can overlap now, so has anyone done/tried this?  Thanks.\n\nAs it turns out, I was able to accept and complete both quests concurrently.  I accepted https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28514 and then https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28666 and was able to keep both in the log and turn them in.",
            date = "2019-06-28T22:13:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28666#comments:id=3131471",
        },
    },
    [28667] = {
        {
            id = 1709444,
            score = 1,
            author = "QuickBASIC",
            text = "List of all the Warchief's Command breadcrumbs and the required level. Remember that none of these count for https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7520 or associated achievements and are unavailable as soon as you start any chain in the zone it indicates.\n\nAs of 5.0.4 though, these quests give 60,000 guild exp (as does any level appropriate quest) so it may be worth while to come back and grab them as you are leveling when they come availible.\n[hr]\n\n[table]\n[tr][td align=left]Quest[/td][td align=left]Level[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28496[/td][td align=left]9[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28560[/td][td align=left]9[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28494[/td][td align=left]9[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28568[/td][td align=left]9[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=26964 (given by https://www.wowhead.com/npc=1515)[/td][td align=left]9[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28493[/td][td align=left]19[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28571[/td][td align=left]19[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28089 (given by https://www.wowhead.com/npc=44640)[/td][td align=left]19[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28572[/td][td align=left]24[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28619 (given by https://www.wowhead.com/object=207279 in Hillsbrad)[/td][td align=left]24[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28688[/td][td align=left]24[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28532[/td][td align=left]24[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28548[/td][td align=left]29[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28549[/td][td align=left]29[/td][/tr]\n[tr][td align=left]https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28704[/td][td align=left]2