    [28733] = {
        {
            id = 1180284,
            score = 112,
            author = "287206",
            text = "For those wondering how to play:\nYou need to gather sun light (the little orbs that fall) to increase your energy. When you gather enough energy, you can place a plant on the field to help your fight against the zom... undead. Sunflowers are used to gather more sunlight that can be collected, spitters are your primary offense in starting.\n\nTo gather sun, you right click them. For some reason I had to do this twice to get it to count per sun. If you find it isn't working, try disabling your addons.\n\nThe bottom will have a bar filled with your current options. When you've gathered enough sun, place your sunflower in one of the blocks that make up the lawn (better to have it in the back [left side], in order to give you more space away from oncoming undead.\n\nSome really good tips here: plant at least 3 sunflowers before any offense. The initial undead are very slow, and can be killed easily. It's best to plant as many sunflowers as you can in this beginning time in order to have enough for the waves later.",
            date = "2010-11-24T04:54:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28733#comments:id=1180284",
        },
        {
            id = 1345817,
            score = 57,
            author = "784024",
            text = "I made videos of the entire chain.  Here's a link on YouTube:\n\nBasic Botany (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wVL5W5UZW9c)\nFlower Power (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fWB1-LgJLXs)\nGhouls Hate My Grains (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MNJBr7kv55k)\nSomeone Setup the Pumpkin Bomb (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ggVoKTaKdII)\nLawn of the Dead (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=929IFjIAliY)\n\nedit: added YouTube links to entire chain",
            date = "2011-02-22T08:19:03-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28733#comments:id=1345817",
        },
        {
            id = 1137347,
            score = 27,
            author = "sjeesen",
            text = "this is the first quest of the plants vs zombies chain.\nbased on the popcap game plants vs zombies.\ncompleting the chain will give you this: Don't Want No Zombies on My Lawn (http://cata.wowhead.com/achievement=5364)\n\nthe name of the achievement comes from the song. clicky (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0N1_0SUGlDQ)",
            date = "2010-10-08T00:27:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28733#comments:id=1137347",
        },
        {
            id = 1202000,
            score = 27,
            author = "716383",
            text = "BEST TACTIC BARNONE LISTEN GUYS\n\nthought of it myself after 3 hours of hell makes me think only if someone posted this earlier\nSF=sunflower\nSP=peashooter\nSFP=freezeshooter\nV=Vines\nR=rockshut nut\nB=Bomb\n\nfirst two rows SF\n3rd row SP\n4th row SFP\n5th row Vines\n6th row R only if your getting pressure if not just build V on this row\nand use the bombs on high level zombies and boss\n\nbuild up as much sf in the beginning thats when youll need to take advantage of the low level zombies and use R if necessary to take advantage\n\nfollow these tactics and itll be smooth sailing\nhope this helps\n\nDargrin\nProudmoore server",
            date = "2010-12-02T09:36:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28733#comments:id=1202000",
        },
        {
            id = 1186069,
            score = 19,
            author = "401437",
            text = "The way i finished the final quest was to make the first two rows all sunflowers, third row spitters, fourth row ice ones (forget the name) fifth row vines, and sixth row rocks. I put pumpkins down whenever big mobs came out.\n\nJust keep putting the same plants back where they should be as they die and you should finish it easily.",
            date = "2010-11-25T22:06:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28733#comments:id=1186069",
        },
    },
    [28734] = {
        {
            id = 1185732,
            score = 41,
            author = "238601",
            text = "You can do this quest after you did Fel Moss Corruption (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28714), but only if you did not do Demonic Thieves (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28715) at the same time.",
            date = "2010-11-25T19:12:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28734#comments:id=1185732",
        },
        {
            id = 5558491,
            score = 17,
            author = "erro3",
            text = "As other commenters have noted - It seems https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28734 is intended as a breadcrumb quests for new players or people who don't notice Melithar is offering a quest nearby.\n\nFor quest completionists looking to scratch this off the list of addons like ATT, take 5 minutes and create a new Night Elf character in Shadowglen. Complete the initial quest of killing nightsabers to be offered https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28714. Accept the quest and make sure to abandon https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28715. Complete https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28714, then at turn in you'll be offered https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28734 as a breadcrumb to accepting the previously abandoned https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28715.\n\nFinally the quest will be marked off your list and you can delete your new toon or continue leveling!",
            date = "2023-03-03T23:38:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28734#comments:id=5558491",
        },
        {
            id = 1703994,
            score = 8,
            author = "ProtossValor",
            text = "So then is there any way possible to get this quest if you do the thieves quest first?",
            date = "2012-08-24T21:44:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28734#comments:id=1703994",
        },
        {
            id = 2579178,
            score = 8,
            author = "EmJii",
            text = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28734 is only available if you abandon https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28715, after you auto-accepted it.",
            date = "2018-07-07T09:54:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28734#comments:id=2579178",
        },
        {
            id = 1640421,
            score = 1,
            author = "GreyMouser",
            text = "I was wrong. This quest is available, but only if you complete Fel Moss Corruption before accepting Demonic Thieves. Turn in Fel Moss and Ilthalaine offers this one as long as Demonic Thieves hasnt been accepted.",
            date = "2012-03-16T22:31:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28734#comments:id=1640421",
        },
    },
    [28742] = {
        {
            id = 1488039,
            score = 14,
            author = "460595",
            text = "Please don't call Shy Rotam an \"IT\" She's not an inanimate object. XD Call her an it, she'll probably look at you funny.\n\n(,,,) =^,-,^= (,,,)",
            date = "2011-08-05T14:47:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28742#comments:id=1488039",
        },
        {
            id = 1178473,
            score = 8,
            author = "299433",
            text = "In case anyone was wondering, this mob seems to have changed genders as of the world shattering.\n\nThe old quest text for HER:\nIn northern Winterspring, great cats assemble around a large landmark called Frostsaber Rock. The leader of these cats is known by the name Shy-Rotam. Defeating the matriarch of the frostsabers would grant you much respect in the eyes of your fellow .\n\nGo again to the harsh wilds, and once there, gather sacred meat from the frostsabers. Find the stone of Shy-Rotam, and place it there. Placing the meat of her kin before her will summon Shy-Rotam, in anger.\n\nBe ready for her fury, and defeat her.",
            date = "2010-11-23T11:51:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28742#comments:id=1178473",
        },
        {
            id = 1765028,
            score = 8,
            author = "galkaia",
            text = "Attention transmoggers! If you're a high level merely after one of the items above for a mog set (I was after Shy Breastplate, for example), you do NOT have to start at the very beginning of this chain. You can start on Fresh Frostsabers.\n\n I noticed the quest when going after two pieces from quest NPCs near this one, but didn't think it through and ignored this one. I could have saved myself the travel time and the annoyance of going into a barrow-den for the beginning few segments...",
            date = "2012-11-19T22:08:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28742#comments:id=1765028",
        },
        {
            id = 1424927,
            score = 4,
            author = "Engrelled",
            text = "Sian-Rotam was around this weekend - I saw him twice, sleeping under the rock behind Shy-Rotam, and killed him twice. He unfortunately only dropped vendor trash, although he was listed as a Rare (and had the silver wreath around his portrait).\n\nKilling him was a bit dicey the first time, since I did not pull him far enough away and Shy-Rotam respawned very quickly so I had to fight both at once.",
            date = "2011-05-22T19:36:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28742#comments:id=1424927",
        },
        {
            id = 1438728,
            score = 4,
            author = "763135",
            text = "tamed both Shy- and Siam-Rotam today. Siam is now laying on the floor next to the rock, he is now longer \"summoned\" by her.",
            date = "2011-06-10T17:42:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28742#comments:id=1438728",
        },
    },
    [28744] = {
        {
            id = 1196064,
            score = 63,
            author = "Astralen",
