    [28747] = {
        {
            id = 1179414,
            score = 162,
            author = "NoSmoking",
            text = "FYI the screen shot shown is a HUGE hint, and makes it really easy once to get the hang of it. But if you don't like puzzles, read on...\n\nCollect Sunpower by right clicking on them.\n\nEarly on, keep the plant Sunflowers on cooldown till you have about 3 made. By then you should be dealing with about 3 Zombies. Rocknut's are your friend (and cheap!), build a few to hold them off.\n\nNext you'll want to plant Spitter's to kill off those 3 Zombies once you have enough Sunpower.\n\nStart planting more Sunflowers, the key to winning is making two full rows of Sunflowers.\n\nBalance making those with a full row of Spitter's and a full row of Freezya's. You should also place a full row of Rocknut's for extra protection.\n\nThen try and stockpile Sunpower for Pumpkin Bombs and Strangler Vines.",
            date = "2010-11-23T22:16:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28747#comments:id=1179414",
        },
        {
            id = 1180986,
            score = 115,
            author = "168407",
            text = "I was having a huge amount of trouble with this one until someone have me a tip. This is what you need:\n\n2 rows of sunflowers\n3 rows of tentacles.\n\nStart planting sunflowers early on, and plant tentacles as needed. Save two rows for all of your sunflowers! Get them up ASAP. One tentacle should have no problem taking down 2 zombies, so don't worry about it. Once all your sunflowers are up, start planting tentacle vines. I ended up with three rows, but you can probably get by with two. With two rows of sunflowers you get so much sunlight that you actually start looking for things to spend it on.\n\nAfter you have the sunflowers and tentacles up, make sure you have enough sunlight for a pumpkin bomb, and plant rocks as needed. Only use the pumpkin bomb on the big purple guys (and anything bigger than that). The tentacles will take care of anything else. If your pumpkin bomb is on cooldown and you have sunlight to pare, plant a few rocks.\n\nOnce I used this strategy this level was very easy. You can use this same strategy on the final level as well. Don't bother with spitters or freezies, just sunflowers and tentacles.",
            date = "2010-11-24T09:58:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28747#comments:id=1180986",
        },
        {
            id = 1180535,
            score = 43,
            author = "mykkenny",
            text = "A tip for everyone that's stuck:\n\nIn the very first 'wave' of zombies, find a lane where there is only one zombie and block him with a wall nut (stone). Keep blocking him until you have two lines of sunflowers and your defenses are shaping up, then kill him and spank the rest with endless sunshine. The next wave shouldn't trigger until you kill that zombie, so this buys you a ton of time to prepare.\n\nGood luck! Got my sunflower pet this morning, gonna go do it again on the DK :)\n\nTarien - Silvermoon.",
            date = "2010-11-24T07:05:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28747#comments:id=1180535",
        },
        {
            id = 1179968,
            score = 39,
            author = "lodion",
            text = "This is bugged for me. I've survived two full waves, no zombies left on hte screen at all, but the progress bar is about 2 pixels short of finished.\n\nNot the first time this has happened to me. So damn frustrating.",
            date = "2010-11-24T02:09:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28747#comments:id=1179968",
        },
        {
            id = 1135922,
            score = 23,
            author = "9945_",
            text = "A reference to the famous Engrish \"Somebody set up us the bomb\" from Zero Wing.",
            date = "2010-10-06T05:37:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28747#comments:id=1135922",
        },
    },
    [28748] = {
        {
            id = 1179599,
            score = 353,
            author = "NoSmoking",
            text = "Early on, keep the plant Sunflowers on cooldown till you have about 3 made. By then you should be dealing with about 3 Zombies. Rocknuts are your friend (and cheap!), build a few to hold them off.\n\nNext is planting Spitters in the rows where the Zombies spawned once you have enough Sunpower.\n\nStart planting more Sunflowers, the key to winning is making two full rows of Sunflowers.\nBalance making Sunflowers with a full row of Spitters and one row of Freezya's. You can even toss in a row of Rocknuts to be safe (Sunpower allowing).\n\n- Strangler Vine's are a bit too expensive and are really not needed, try to avoid planting them early on. However, you can toss in a few just to burn off extra Sunpower!\n\nYour next order of business is stockpiling Sunpower, to keep Pumpkin Bombs on cooldown, but also to replace Plants destroyed by Warden Stillwater's Blight.\n\n4-5 Pumpkin bombs should win the game\n\nGood luck!",
            date = "2010-11-23T23:32:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28748#comments:id=1179599",
        },
        {
            id = 1181095,
            score = 98,
            author = "Adverse",
            text = "Some of the strats on here are very helpful, I used a little from a few of them.\n\nI went with 2 rows of Sunflowers, used some Rocknuts to hold off some of the zombies while I collected enough Sun to put down some Shooters.\n\nOnce I had about a row of shooters I put down some Tentacles and blocked off a few of the harder zombies with Rocknuts.\n\nBy the time the boss appeared the Sun power was dropping quite fast, I just had keep Tentacles and Sunflowers up while waiting for the Pumpkin Bomb to come off cooldown.\n\n---\n\nSF = Sunflowers\nSH = Shooters\nTE = Tentacles\n\nSF SF SH TE\nSF SF SH TE\nSF SF SH TE\nSF SF SH TE\nSF SF SH TE",
            date = "2010-11-24T10:25:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28748#comments:id=1181095",
        },
        {
            id = 1132381,
            score = 57,
            author = "579020",
            text = "@Lmjkdd6   Both wrong and right.\nThis whole questline is based on the game Plants vs Zombies (http://www.popcap.com/games/free/pvz), which originally was going to be called Lawn of the Dead, a spoof on Dawn of the dead. They had to change to Plants vs Zombies due to copyright.\n\nThe reward (Brazie's Sunflower Seeds (http://cata.wowhead.com/item=66067)) teaches you the pet Brazie's Sunflower (http://cata.wowhead.com/spell=93823), who sings :)",
            date = "2010-10-01T12:27:22-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28748#comments:id=1132381",
        },
        {
            id = 5677394,
            score = 45,
            author = "SithJew",
            text = "I cannot get Warden Stillwater to spawn, his message pops up but he never shows up and the game just goes forever. 10.1.7",
            date = "2023-09-06T01:09:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28748#comments:id=5677394",
        },
        {
            id = 2133041,
            score = 40,
            author = "1446900",
            text = "This worked for me:\n\nSF = Sunflower\nSH = Shooter\nFR = Freezya\nRN = Rocknut\nTE = Tentacle\nPK = Pumpkin\n\nSH SF SF FR TE RN RN\nSH SF SF FR TE RN RN/PK\nSH SF SF FR TE RN RN\nSH SF SF FR TE RN RN/PK\nSH SF SF FR TE RN RN\n\nFirst get up about 3 SF, by then, some zombie should be lumbering about half way across field.  Put a RN in it's way and ignore it.  You want it to destroy this RN because you'll plant something else there later, like FR or TE.  If one doesn't get destroyed, you'll be ok, so don't worry.\n\nSecond, spam in the SF and get the shooters in as needed.  Freezyas come in as needed here too.  During this process, thinking ahead, drop in the RN as needed to slow things down.\n\nThird, get the TE up, maintaining the RN, replace any FR or SF that get killed, or wilted.\n\nFourth stage, is maintenance mode.  You should have way more sun coming in than you can click on.  Keep replacing RN, and when your sun is full, or if there is a cluster of bad guys, start dropping pumpkins (if there's a space to do so), to burn off excess sun.  Never waste sun if you can help it.\n\nThe Warden will die pretty soon.  Actually, I found this final battle much easier than the preceding battle.",
            date = "2015-03-08T09:12:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28748#comments:id=2133041",
        },
    },
    [28749] = {
        {
            id = 1204670,
            score = 51,
            author = "Chibchub123",
            text = "Worth mentioning, You CAN'T pick this quest up if you have any of the quests listed on the right side in Quick Facts, I did not test turning one of them in and trying to pick up the quest, but it was unavaliable for me until I dropped Hero's Call:WPL",
            date = "2010-12-03T17:09:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28749#comments:id=1204670",
        },
        {
            id = 1272390,
            score = 37,
            author = "Seriesh",
            text = "This quest is very awesome for those trying to work on Archaeology in Eastern Kingdoms. The portal is initiated by you talking to the quest giver, and is usable as many times as you wish, so long as you don't turn in the quest. You can then fly south from Western Plaguelands and dig up any sites you see. Take the portal at Booty Bay (again) and pop back at the top of the continent.\n\nThis method has saved hours of my time while trying to farm for my staff/sword/soul back. :P\n\nEdit: I don't know if there's a Horde equivalent, but I do this as an Alliance character.",
            date = "2011-01-02T01:14:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28749#comments:id=1272390",
        },
        {
            id = 1205565,
            score = 19,
            author = "218837",
            text = "I can confirm that it is possible to talk to him multiple times to get a portal to Andorhal. The major drawback is that it won't be possible to obtain the follow-up quest Scourge First... Horde Later (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27159) and as a result, obtain Western Plaguelands Quests (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=4893).",
            date = "2010-12-04T06:09:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28749#comments:id=1205565",
        },
        {
            id = 1209164,
            score = 12,
            author = "328410",
            text = "This must be part of the phasing system that Blizz is implementing. When I rode through Andorhal with my 80s to get the new flight paths, I noticed some red-tagged mobs as soon as I entered town, but they almost immediately disappeared. All the NPCs were friendly there for my 80s.\n\nAfter accepting the portal in Booty Bay and then the flightpath, the town is full of faction NPCs battling the last remnants of the Scourge.\n\nI thoroughly enjoyed this quest line. It is not terribly challenging for the level, but the story is rich with lore and helps tell the story of what happened to Andorhal between old world and Cataclysm. You see some old \"friends\" like Araj and Tharassian, kill some new bosses, and see the new post-Cat plague lands.\n\nHave to say \"bravo\" to Blizz.",
            date = "2010-12-05T21:29:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28749#comments:id=1209164",
        },
        {
            id = 1194207,
            score = 7,
            author = "179247",
            text = "When you do this quests, you will be teleported to Andorhal and receive Flight Paths up to Andorhal if you have not received them yet. This is the best way to begin the Andorhal quests.",
            date = "2010-11-28T18:50:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28749#comments:id=1194207",
        },
    },
