    [28751] = {
        {
            id = 1478559,
            score = 39,
            author = "706669",
            text = "Facts:\n\nPopCap released an official Bejeweled add-on in 2008 after a fan created a clone. (source (http://www.wired.com/gamelife/2008/09/bejeweled-comin/)) They followed it up with a Peggle add-on for World of Warcraft in early 2009. (source (http://www.wired.com/gamelife/2009/04/peggle-joins-be/)) These add-ons are notable because they use obfuscated code which is against Blizzard's UI Policy (http://us.battle.net/wow/en/forum/topic/1021053914) but an exception is made due to both companies closely working together. (source (http://wow.joystiq.com/2009/05/04/popcaps-addons-are-obfuscated-blizzard-is-ok-with-that/))\n\nThese are still available to download from PopCap's site right here (http://www.popcap.com/promos/wow).  They are not being maintained but do work (with a few errors) in current WoW.\n\nIn 2009 (after the release of WoW Peggle) Blizzard hired PopCap's VP Greg Canessa. (source (http://news.softpedia.com/news/Blizzard-Hires-PopCap-Exec-World-Domination-Imminent-111335.shtml))\n\nBlizzard started working on the Peacebloom vs Ghouls quest chain before contacting PopCap.  They could have easily released it without any problems even if PopCap complained as it falls within fair use.  PopCap loved it and had Laura Shigihara (PvZ's music composer and voice of the sunflower) to record \"a few extra bits\" for Blizzard to include. (source (http://www.gamepro.com/article/news/216703/popcap-blizzard-has-something-special-for-plants-vs-zombies-cataclysm-quest/)) This was later confirmed to be speech samples for the https://www.wowhead.com/spell=93823, presumably so that Blizzard could redistribute them at any time without needing to clear it with PopCap.\n\nEven after the Electronic Arts buyout of PopCap, their official line is that things like this wouldn't change as PopCap is going to remain mostly autonomous sort of like Blizzard remains mostly autonomous from Activision. (source (http://kotaku.com/5820658/what-does-the-big-ea-buyout-mean-for-popcap-games-and-for-bejeweled-in-world-of-warcraft))\n\nSpeculation:\n\nQuite honestly the Peacebloom vs Ghouls quest chain is fun the first time but it doesn't hold up to the real thing.  I'm sure that if you had to do 15 stages of it in one sitting you would be quite tired of it.  Plants vs Zombies on the other hand is something that you can play for hours and hours.\n\nSo really the only thing stopping you from doing this is that it didn't test well.",
            date = "2011-07-24T16:46:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28751#comments:id=1478559",
        },
        {
            id = 1705883,
            score = 22,
            author = "488359",
            text = "This daily is available again as of 5.04!",
            date = "2012-08-29T18:25:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28751#comments:id=1705883",
        },
        {
            id = 2364296,
            score = 15,
            author = "Musician2111",
            text = "Can anyone tell me what the reward is on doing the repeatable quest? Is it just the 15 gold or so?",
            date = "2016-08-10T03:21:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28751#comments:id=2364296",
        },
        {
            id = 2578153,
            score = 5,
            author = "207078",
            text = "Is it me, or the zombies got more hp after scaling of the world? Before it, I believe the weakest zombie died at half the distance with one shooter.\nEdit. 8.0.1 patch seemingly fixed zombie hp.",
            date = "2018-07-03T10:26:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28751#comments:id=2578153",
        },
        {
            id = 2555348,
            score = 4,
            author = "1847497",
            text = "As of 7.3.5 - this quest and the three predecessors to it are available.  Every quest in the chain including this daily are hit or miss if you will be able to complete them.  If the plants and zombies disappear off of the map you will have to exit the scenario and try again.\n\nIn total it took me approximately 2 hours to complete all of them.  Just before this quest unlocks you'll earn a sunflower minipet\n\nThe daily does not give any achievements or rewards other than those listed in the quest and I got no additional reputation hits besides guild.\n\nI had to re-try this quest once to be able to complete it.  My strategy is:\n\nBuild sunflowers first and consistently until you get your first mobs\nBlock the mobs as high up the field as you can with the stone cairns while still stacking sunflowers from the left side of the map\nOnce you've had to apply a few cairns and the mobs have started catalyzing against your wall, drop a pumpkin to buy more time to build more sunflowers\nContinue this until you have a solid two panels of cairns on the right (but leave the farthest right row empty to drop pumpkins) and 3 rows of sunflowers on the left\nNow that your solar energy flow is infinite - build spitters up in the remaining two rows, put vines on the right most row on the edges and in the middle - leaving two cells in the far right blank to drop pumpkins\nFill in gaps, vines and drop pumpkins on cool down and you will absolutely win every time using this method\n\nGood luck!",
            date = "2018-02-27T21:03:44-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28751#comments:id=2555348",
        },
    },
    [28752] = {
        {
            id = 1291044,
            score = 12,
            author = "466605",
            text = "This quest is the 'free play' mode of the 'plants vs zombies' quests in Hillsbrad. It was in the beta, and though I didn't play beta I recall people mentioning that it was missing. Cata has been out over a month now, no comments, screenshots, and the quick facts box is incomplete.\n\nThis quest didn't make it to live :( I really hope they put in back in because it looks fun!",
            date = "2011-01-12T18:16:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28752#comments:id=1291044",
        },
    },
    [28755] = {
        {
            id = 1206964,
            score = 117,
            author = "718641",
            text = "Here is what I did. I grabbed the quest, then flew to Plaguewood Tower. If you don't have the Flight Path make sure you grab it! I then entered Stratholme.\n\nI cleared the monsters etc. to Balnazzar. Opposite Balnazzar was Instructor Galford. I killed him and took the book from him, which was behind the table.\n\nI exited the instance, then went to Plaguewood Tower. DO NOT RESET THE INSTANCE! I caught a wind rider to Light's Hope Chapel and handed the quest in, getting 2000 Argent Dawn rep.\n\nI grabbed the quest again and did the same as before. Because I didn't reset the instance, there were no mobs to kill; making a clear path for me to follow. The book is still obtainable.\n\nTo get revered to exalted you will need to do this quest 11 times. :)\n\nEDIT: After getting exalted; doing the quest 11 times took me about 3-4 hours. Also, I did this as a level 80 ret pally. Doing it 70+ would be advised.",
            date = "2010-12-04T21:44:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28755#comments:id=1206964",
        },
        {
            id = 1203076,
            score = 95,
            author = "jidders",
            text = "No need to reset the instance.",
            date = "2010-12-02T22:18:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28755#comments:id=1203076",
        },
        {
            id = 1370979,
            score = 55,
            author = "601044",
            text = "To add to Malgeras's post:\n\nTo get the repeatable Argent Dawn quests:\nTo be able to do the quests https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28756 and https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28755 you must first complete the following quests that are initiated by Fiona (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=45941) who is standing at the bridge that connects the Eastern Plaguelands and Western Plaguelands.\n\nTarenar Sunstrike (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27370) -> What I Do Best (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27371) -> A Gift For Fiona (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27372)\nGidwin Goldbraids (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27367) -> Just Encased (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27368) -> Greasing the Wheel (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27369)\n\nOnce these two chains are completed, you can do Onward, to Light's Hope Chapel (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27373) which will take you to 'Crown Guard Tower'. Once there you must complete Traveling Companions (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27381) (he's at the top of the tower) and then complete his quest (Rough Roads (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27382)) before being able to continue on to the next tower via the quest The Trek Continues (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27448). Once there, you can pick up the quest Boys Will Be Boys (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27455) from Fiona. Go to 'Light's Hope Chapel' and complete the following quest line:\n\nA Boyhood Dream (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27463) -> Argent Call: The Trial of the Crypt (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27464)\n\nAfter completing the latter of these two quests, you will be set to revered (+0 reputation if you're already over 0/21000 revered) and Lord Raymond George (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=49856) will appear at the back of the chapel and will provide you with the two repeatable quests that give 2,000 Argent Dawn reputation per hand-in.\n\nBest Grinding Method:\nI have just got to exalted on my protection paladin and found something interesting (I was level 85 and used a flying mount to get around):\n\nWhen doing both quests it took me just over 12 minutes to do, starting from standing in front of Lord Raymond George (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=49856) (the quest giver) and ending in front of him. However, if I only did https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28756, it took me around 5 minutes 30 seconds to complete meaning it's actually quicker to spam Rattlegore kills than to try doing both.\n\nThe best way to complete https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28756 is once you've got to Scholomance, jump down from the 'bridge' and stay as close to the wall as you can (there's a little ledge in the pit below which you'll land on and it will greatly reduce the chance of pulling anything). Then run up the steps and over to the room with whelplings in; once in this room, jump down the hole on your left and then run over and kill Rattlegore. After that there's only really one way back to the entrance. It shaves off about 30 seconds or so taking this route to Rattlegore.",
            date = "2011-03-19T16:07:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28755#comments:id=1370979",
        },
        {
            id = 1189218,
            score = 31,
            author = "divinebaboon",
            text = "2000 argent dawn rep, repeatable.",
            date = "2010-11-27T00:38:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28755#comments:id=1189218",
        },
        {
            id = 2330152,
            score = 28,
            author = "Adelline",
            text = "I didn't start playing until Wrath, so I never did Strath when it was current, and wasn't familiar with the terms 'living side' and 'dead side'.\nThis quest takes place in the section now known as 'Main Gate'. It's the entrance marked 'Stratholme' on the map.",
            date = "2016-05-11T17:48:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28755#comments:id=2330152",
        },
    },
