uest=26008)\n6)Come Hell of High Water (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25884) ├>6)What? What? In My Gut...? (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25885){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=26040)\n6)The Warden's Time (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=27708)       └>6)How Disarming (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25883)\n7)Across the Great Divide (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25471)\n7)The Looming Threat (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25334)\n7)Backed Into a Corner (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25164)\n7)Rundown (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25221)            ┌>9)Slippery Threat (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25220)\n8)Silver Tide Hollow (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25222)─┼>9)Don't be Shellfish (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25219)\n9)The Great Sambino (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25216)  └>8)A Distracting Scent (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25215)\n9)Undersea Inflation (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25218)\n9)Totem Modification (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25217)  9)Crabby Patrons (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25360)\n8)Back In One Piece (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25456)\nG)Toshe's Vengeance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=25359)──>https://www.wowhead.com/quest=25439*\nQuest zones:\n1)Orgrimmar+Stormwind_____2)Legion's Fate+Seafarer's Tomb_____3)Shallow's End+Smuggler's Hole_____4)Gurboggle's Ledge_____5)Skeletal Reef_____6)Deepmist Grotto+The Clutch_____7)Damplight Chamber+Shimmering Grotto_____8)Silver Tide Hollow_____9)Silver Tide Trench\nG)Gluing Separate Questlines_____S)Skippable\n* is another Quest Tree.[/pre]\nIMPORTANT INFO:\nIn order to gethttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=27668 you must completehttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=25944 before acceptinghttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=25946.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=25477 andhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=25371 are NOT needed to takehttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=25587 and followups, however that would make you unable to gethttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=27685.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=55186 have 0% drop chance beforehttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=25459 done and 100% after, however anyone can share you this quest as long as you are 80+lvl.\nAnyone can takehttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=25439 and do it's followups as long as they are 80+lvl. Quests above are NOT needed for it.\n> (http://www.wowhead.com/forums&topic=180241&p=2487503)",
            date = "2011-03-08T14:28:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28827#comments:id=1361278",
        },
    },
    [28828] = {
        {
            id = 1187247,
            score = 4,
            author = "165064",
            text = "looting a egg aggros every chimaeras in a 40 yards radius",
            date = "2010-11-26T09:31:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28828#comments:id=1187247",
        },
        {
            id = 1639729,
            score = 3,
            author = "Barleduq",
            text = "Ok, so what are all the little snow-piles around here? They look like the snowpiles from the dwarf starter zone, when you're picking up artifacts for the guy in Anvilmar. But they're not clickable...",
            date = "2012-03-15T02:33:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28828#comments:id=1639729",
        },
        {
            id = 1871988,
            score = 1,
            author = "D4n13le",
            text = "This quest seems bugged as of 2013/06/29.\nYou can click the eggs, the character \"kneels\", but the loot window doesn't show up.",
            date = "2013-06-29T16:16:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28828#comments:id=1871988",
        },
        {
            id = 1410434,
            score = 0,
            author = "ziggy29",
            text = "I've done this on a few characters now, but one thing I recently noted when leveling my rogue through here is this:  I usually run in subtlety spec, but you lose most of the advantage of that spec in this quest, since any time you loot the eggs you become visible, targeted and can't benefit from ambush.  So as it turns out, I found this easier (and faster to grind through) when I stayed in combat spec.  I did a fair bit more DPS that way (keeping in mind you lose ambush and stuff from subtlety spec) and my energy generation was faster, enabling me to generate combo points more quickly.  When this was done, I went back into subtlety spec to deal with the frostsabers, owls and stuff.",
            date = "2011-05-05T11:50:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28828#comments:id=1410434",
        },
        {
            id = 1604278,
            score = -5,
            author = "SkeeterEater",
            text = "Not a radius issue, One chimaera is spawned and attacks each time you loot an egg.",
            date = "2011-12-30T15:41:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28828#comments:id=1604278",
        },
    },
    [28829] = {
        {
            id = 1257754,
            score = 9,
            author = "Firehoof",
            text = "Poor Orc. He is one unlucky plucker....",
            date = "2010-12-25T04:38:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28829#comments:id=1257754",
        },
        {
            id = 1416254,
            score = 3,
            author = "Blog",
            text = "If you have the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28838 it is best to do that one before this, as The Owlbeasts' Defense leads you to this area to kill the wildkin here.",
            date = "2011-05-11T19:32:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28829#comments:id=1416254",
        },
        {
            id = 3143920,
            score = 2,
            author = "TheSkullpitter",
            text = "\"I tried to steal everything from these things and they hurt me. Isn't that a really sad story?\" No. I would go so far as to say that it's a happy story with an unhappy ending, because you're still alive.",
            date = "2019-07-28T16:18:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28829#comments:id=3143920",
        },
    },
    [28830] = {
        {
            id = 1300505,
            score = 5,
            author = "Anaranjada",
            text = "These guys are right around the gorge and have a nasty knockback. Be careful of your positioning; they're very capable of knocking you off the ledge to your death.",
            date = "2011-01-19T12:57:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28830#comments:id=1300505",
        },
        {
            id = 1589559,
            score = 1,
            author = "Schnoodledorfer",
            text = "In both the initial text and the completion text, Jadrag says the giants on the other side of the gorge are much tougher. https://www.wowhead.com/npc=7428s and https://www.wowhead.com/npc=7429s used to be elite and a little higher level (archived information here (old01.wowhead.com/npc=7428/frostmaul-giant)), but have been nerfed, apparently to make https://www.wowhead.com/quest=5981 easier. Now they are at the same level as https://www.wowhead.com/npc=50258s and no longer elite, so at first glance what Jadrag says seems to be out of date. The \"adult\" giants still start out with much more HP than the Tumblers and they were considerably more work for my Shammy take down, though. Other than hunters trying to farm https://www.wowhead.com/npc=7446, there isn't much of a reason to go to the other side, and it's not easy to do if your character can't fly yet.",
            date = "2011-12-04T17:18:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28830#comments:id=1589559",
        },
        {
            id = 6044594,
            score = 1,
            author = "Renmeker",
            text = "For Loremaster Winterspring I received the Jadrag's Fate step for completing this quest.\n\nI was able to simply accept Quest 49 Razor Beak and Antlers Pointy and did the quests leading up to this quest.",
            date = "2025-01-08T15:49:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28830#comments:id=6044594",
        },
    },
    [28831] = {
        {
            id = 1204888,
            score = 24,
            author = "268722",
            text = "\"Me and Frostillicus go back a long way. I used to share a bathroom with Frostillicus. In fact, I got a real funny story about that! Actually, it's not so much funny as it is long.\"\n\nFrostillicus is a Simpsons reference, episode 4F24 (http://www.snpp.com/episodes/4F24).  Jasper \"cryogenically\" freezes himself in the Kwik-E-Mart freezer so he could see a future where robot wives were cheap and effective. Apu decides to make money off of the frozen man by calling him \"Frostillicus\" and charging admission. The above quote is from Abe (Grandpa) Simpson, who stood by the exhibit and rambled as he is wont to do.",
            date = "2010-12-03T20:05:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28831#comments:id=1204888",
        },
        {
            id = 1338183,
            score = 13,
            author = "787942",
            text = "Also, part of the quest completion text is: \"Whenever the wind whistles through the trees, I will always hear your name.\"  I think this is a subtle reference to yet another Simpsons episode, \"Bart the Lover\" (http://www.snpp.com/episodes/8F16.html).  Bart's final letter to Ms. Krabappel states: \"Any time I hear the wind blow it will whisper the name... Edna.\"",
            date = "2011-02-16T06:46:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28831#comments:id=1338183",
        },
        {
            id = 1420156,
            score = 12,
            author = "stenova",
            text = "The path down is on the west of the gorge. Just in case any other idiots than me run around searching.",
            date = "2011-05-16T08:16:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28831#comments:id=1420156",
        },
        {
            id = 1180832,
            score = 11,
            author = "336870",
            text = "Starts with Jadrag the Slicer (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=50263) at 61,74 after you finish the quest Razor Beaks and Antlers Pointy (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28829).",
            date = "2010-11-24T09:16:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28831#comments:id=1180832",
        },
        {
            id = 1488632,
            score = 11,
            author = "857644",
            text = "Path down to the gorge is at 57.77 near the dun Mandarr camp",
            date = "2011-08-06T12:36:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28831#comments:id=1488632",
        },
    },
    [28837] = {
        {
            id = 1184060,
            score = 31,
            author = "Tenjen",
            text = "Wise from your gwave!",
            date = "2010-11-25T06:50:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28837#comments:id=1184060",
        },
        {
            id = 1294164,
            score = 19,
            author = "746780",
            text = "When you are looking the mobs which drop these don't go to the tunnel. I visited there before I checked some help from here and there was nothing.\n\nMobs you are looking for can be found around the hills not far away from quest giver. They look pretty much like ordinary critters (rabbits, light blue foxes) like Ainasni said.\n\nThis quest also leads to The Owlbeasts' Defense (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=28838).",
            date = "2011-01-14T21:59:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28837#comments:id=1294164",
        },
        {
            id = 2567155,
            score = 19,
            author = "lynnsie",
            text = "If you've looted several and nothing has dropped, just keep going. It isn't a 100% drop rate. I went about 5 in with nothing and was concerned I was wasting my time, turns out they just have no other loot and the brain is not a guarantee.",
            date = "2018-05-12T17:29:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=28837#comments:id=2567155",
        },
        {
            id = 1255100,
            score = 12,
