    [29032] = {
        {
            id = 1400167,
            score = 43,
            author = "390723",
            text = "This is the very first quest to get you started on the 20-day quests to get you your Frostsaber mount.  THis has been recently changed, a welcome one, seeing as the last one had your grind rep for 8 hours while doing the same quest over and over again.\n\n-Accept this quest.  Go around the open patch of land underneath the quest giver, and pick up 8 frostsaber cubs.  They're the small, glittering ones by the rock dens.\n\n-Turn them in, and accept the next quest, They grow up so fast.  Now, for 20 days, doesn't have to be in a row, just 20, you must summon your pet in Winterspring and do one of the offered quests.  You will accumulate whiskers at the end of each quest.\n\n-At the end of the 20 days, take your whiskers back to the quest giver, and collect your mount!\n\n:)",
            date = "2011-04-26T16:15:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29032#comments:id=1400167",
        },
        {
            id = 1356353,
            score = 14,
            author = "TegoZanduba",
            text = "No more rep grind!",
            date = "2011-03-03T13:18:30-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29032#comments:id=1356353",
        },
        {
            id = 1403657,
            score = 14,
            author = "26532",
            text = "You don't have to dismount to collect the cubs.",
            date = "2011-04-29T04:32:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29032#comments:id=1403657",
        },
        {
            id = 1422732,
            score = 13,
            author = "skyfire477",
            text = "For those of you looking for the cub companion there is a vendor in the inn at Everlook, if you go in look at the back left corner her name is Michelle De Rum, the cub costs 50 gold from her.",
            date = "2011-05-19T17:35:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29032#comments:id=1422732",
        },
        {
            id = 1426856,
            score = 11,
            author = "491045",
            text = "Yes, it sounds a little dirty, but considering the amount of political hits a google search (http://www.google.dk/search?hl=da&source=hp&q=get+them+while+they%27re+young&aq=f&aqi=g10&aql=&oq=) gave, I think it's just referencing to the common saying and idea that brainwashing works best on young and innocent minds.",
            date = "2011-05-25T08:54:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29032#comments:id=1426856",
        },
    },
    [29033] = {
    },
    [29034] = {
        {
            id = 1436975,
            score = 92,
            author = "kaiderey4",
            text = "Progression\n\n[50] Get Them While They're Young (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=29032)\n[50] They Grow Up So Fast\n\n[50 Daily] A Cub's Cravings (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=29035)\n[50 Daily] 'Borrowing' From the Winterfall (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=29037)\n[50 Daily] Cub's First Toy (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=29040)\n[50 Daily] Hunting Practice (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=29038)\n\nNotes\n\nA Cub's Cravings\n\nYou will need to feed your Winterspring Cub: Shardtooth Meat (http://www.wowhead.com/item=12622) (6)\nDrops from bears with Shardtooth in their name, most common in the area between Frostsaber Rock and The Hidden Grove.\nAfter being fed a piece of meat, the cub will offer one of the following emotes:\n\nThe Winterspring Cub devours the food.\nThe Winterspring Cub's strong jaws tear into the food.\nThe Winterspring Cub catches the food in its mouth and swallows it in one gulp.\nThe Winterspring Cub quickly finishes the food and glances around for more.\n\n[br]\n'Borrowing' From the Winterfall\n\nYou have to have your Winterspring Cub (http://www.wowhead.com/item=68646) summoned in order to feed the Smoked Meat (http://www.wowhead.com/item=68645) to it.\nThe Smoked Meat stands (http://www.wowhead.com/object=208189) are found in two places:\n\nWinterfall Village at (67, 46)\nTimbermaw Post at (56, 35)\n\n[br]\nCub's First Toy\n\nTo make the cat toy, you need these things:\n\nTough Yeti Hide (http://www.wowhead.com/item=68663) (1)\nDropped by the yeti just south of the Winterfall Village in the cave.\n\nWildkin Feather (http://www.wowhead.com/item=68662#dropped-by) (5)\nDropped by the Owlbeasts in The Hidden Grove.\n\nAfter collecting the hide (http://www.wowhead.com/item=68663) and feathers (http://www.wowhead.com/item=68662), right-click to combine them into the cat toy (http://www.wowhead.com/item=68668). Then right-click the toy to Use it.\nUsing the toy produces a ground targeted area of effect targeting circle. Click the circle to have the cub play with the toy.\nThe Hidden Grove can be found at the north end of Winterspring, due north of Everlook, and is labeled on the game map.\n\n[br]\nHunting Practice\n\nSimply bring your cub close to one of the mounds. The cub will pounce on the mound, and the player will see the emote\nWinterspring Cub pounces on the snow-covered hare burrow (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=51711) (View comments on that page for coordinates to some of the burrows I've found) If you don't have coordinates, most of the burrows are in the middle area between: Frostsaber Rock, The Hidden Grove, and Starfall Village.",
            date = "2011-06-08T11:10:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29034#comments:id=1436975",
        },
        {
            id = 1774736,
            score = 53,
            author = "Symphonius",
            text = "Somewhere along the way of transferring and race changing I lost my https://www.wowhead.com/item=68646.\n\nIf you happen to lose the item, it is safe to abandon the quest and pick it up again to receive another one. You will NOT lose your https://www.wowhead.com/item=68644, as they are not tagged as quest items and will not disappear when the quest is dropped.",
            date = "2012-12-03T12:01:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29034#comments:id=1774736",
        },
        {
            id = 1421866,
            score = 47,
            author = "Norrinir",
            text = "This quest rewards 10 000 reputation (not counting guild perk or human racial). Doing whole line (i.e. starting quest + 20 dailies + this one), gives 43 000 reputation and thus makes you Exalted no matter what you do.",
            date = "2011-05-18T15:14:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29034#comments:id=1421866",
        },
        {
            id = 1353209,
            score = 45,
            author = "dhomeli",
            text = "The new Winterspring Frostsaber quest, which is now very similar to the Horde questline for the Venomhide Raptor.\n\nFirst you do the quest: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29032 which will give you your very own https://www.wowhead.com/item=68646!\n\nEach day you will get dailies from the Winterspring Cub which in turn give you: https://www.wowhead.com/item=68644s.\n\nDo 20 dailies for 20 whiskers (and collect 20 runecloth, 20 rugged leather, and 70g 60s), and you will have your very own Winterspring Frostsaber mount!",
            date = "2011-02-28T13:51:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29034#comments:id=1353209",
        },
        {
            id = 1412075,
            score = 25,
            author = "JalanBax",
            text = "Just got my mount without completing this quest.\n\nI've been grinding the rep on and off for about a year so was midway through revered when I started doing the new cub dailies and getting rep for each one completed.\n\nWhen I got to exalted, I was able to buy the mount directly from Rivern Frostwind for 80 gold without needing to turn in the whiskers, leather and cloth.\n\nFeat of strength achieved!\n\nNow, do I complete the quest anyway for cub's first toy?",
            date = "2011-05-07T09:09:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29034#comments:id=1412075",
        },
    },
