    [29547] = {
        {
            id = 5201408,
            score = 59,
            author = "iSkynette",
            text = "Attention: If you're an upper level character having difficulties initiating this questline and none of the above options have worked, try the following:\n\n1. Go to the Hero board in your city - you're likely going to see 3 completely irrelevant zone missions other than Jade Forest.\n2. Don't panic, you've got this.\n3. Pick up one of the three irrelevant Heroes Call missions anyway.\n4. Check your board again.\n5. Repeat as needed, Jade Forest will appear as an option eventually,\n6. Abandon irrelevant Heroes Call missions.",
            date = "2021-06-22T12:55:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29547#comments:id=5201408",
        },
        {
            id = 1736918,
            score = 37,
            author = "natassja72",
            text = "If you happen to miss this particular quest pop up on your screen and wonder \"how the heck do I get to Pandaria now?\" - check the next quest in the chain - https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29548. It is available just in front of the Stormwind keep entrance.",
            date = "2012-10-09T19:59:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29547#comments:id=1736918",
        },
        {
            id = 1778964,
            score = 28,
            author = "671293",
            text = "If you did a faction change from Horde to Alliance and can't do the intro questline to Pandaria visit Taradormi (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=69157) in Krasarang Wilds and she'll cast a time travel spell (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=136399) to send you back to when the Skyfall arrived in the Jade Forest.\n\nTricked-out DeLorean and 1.21 gigawatts not required.",
            date = "2012-12-10T10:57:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29547#comments:id=1778964",
        },
        {
            id = 1951623,
            score = 14,
            author = "zomgname",
            text = "This quest, as well as the other starting Panderia quest, are auto-completed for you when you boost a character to level 90. There is no way to go and do them, and no way to get the items from them other than the old raids that share the models.\n\nI spoke with a GM that said there would be \"many many\" problems if this was not done. The GM said, despite being able to clearly see the quest were auto-completed and we got nothing from them, they cannot grant the items, \"their system won't allow it\". I was told that \"it sucks but I get a level 90 with 2 max profressions\". I informed the GM that I didn't get max profressions because I boosted from level 1, and they asked me if I had professions at level 1. I had to explain to the GM how their boost system works, and that you only get boosted profressions if you are level 60.",
            date = "2014-03-17T01:17:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29547#comments:id=1951623",
        },
        {
            id = 1925998,
            score = 12,
            author = "ladyofthemasque",
            text = "Since no one has posted this yet, here's a transcript (with some descriptive touches) of the cinematic cut-scene that happens the moment you enter the castle.\n\nThis cinematic can be triggered from either the front courtyard entrance (the moment you enter the castle proper, past/behind the fountain/statue), or by entering via the garden entrance toward the throne room (the moment you leave the grass if you flew in down through the center of the garden square, or if you fly to the walkways and come around from either the library or the other side along the walkway; as soon as you get within a few yards of that part of the atrium walkway, you get pulled into the cinematic).\n\n(You can still enter the library without triggering the cinematic.)\n\n______\n\n*cinematic begins, 3 figures stand around a map table; a human woman, King Varian in his distinctive armor, and a night elf male; on the map near Tanaris are 3 wooden ship markers*\n\nGrand Admiral Jes-Tereth (brunette woman, silve armor, white tabard with gold anchor):  “We’ve made a thorough inspection of the wreckage, Your Majesty. There is no sign of Admiral Taylor, or his ship.”\n\nKing Varian:  “Two hundred ships at my disposal, yet the one carrying my son goes missing!”  *thumps the map table with his left hand between the 3 ships, which fall over* “What of their last message?  Show me whatever you have.”\n\n*Rell Nightwind (male night elf, hot pink hair, dark green armor, SI:7 agent, shows up as a major quest giver later) moves to replay the message in a scrying bowl bubble. King Varian draws near as the message plays.  The Grand Admiral moves up behind him to watch/listen as well*\n\nAdmiral Taylor (blond human male, Stormwind blue-and-gold tabard over his armor, seen from the waist-up in the scrying bubble):  *The recording flickers occasionally*  “We have been drawn off course. - Horde airfleet. - Many casualties. - Shipwrecked on an uncharted isle.  But the White Pawn is accounted for.\"  *thumps fist in hand*  \"Repeat, the White Pawn is safe!”\n\nKing Varian:  “Anduin…”\n\nAdmiral Taylor: *looks away abruptly, the messages flicker and break up*  “Surprise attack!  - Requesting immedi--***--’ve hit it with some sh—”  *message ends*\n\nGrand Admiral Jes-Tereth:  “Sir, the 7th Fleet has already been dispatched.  But it could take weeks before it—”\n\nKing Varian:  “--There’s no time to waste!\" *turns away*  \"We’ll send a small, elite force to secure this new land…and bring back my son!”\n\n*cinematic ends*\n________\n\n...I'd recommend actually watching the cinematic, as it's far better and much more dramatic than this text-based transcript.  But just like the Ancestral Brewmaster jokes when running through the Stormstout Brewery dungeon, or the whispers of Wrathion as you grind (oh that horrible long grind) for those Titan Runestones, people like seeing this stuff written down...so here ya go!\n\n(Also for absolute accuracy...the very last set of lines from Admiral Taylor were very difficult to understand, even cranking the volume and listening to it around 11-12 times, but I have done my best.  Feel free to debate what he was actually trying to say; just keep it polite.)",
            date = "2013-12-14T21:19:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29547#comments:id=1925998",
        },
    },
