        },
    },
    [29662] = {
        {
            id = 1718652,
            score = 9,
            author = "tarc",
            text = "After the quest is turned in;\n\nJoro Ironbrow says: The reeds of the Singing Pools are the hardest in all of the land, but they are as air before my mighty brow.\n\nHe then proceeds to place the reeds in a stack and then smashes through them all with his forehead.\n\nJoro Ironbrow says: Many have tested my claim, and I yet stand proven.\n\nJoro then walks along the pathways to 74,46 and despawns",
            date = "2012-09-25T11:36:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29662#comments:id=1718652",
        },
        {
            id = 1664470,
            score = 4,
            author = "darknesscalls",
            text = "Entire quest description:\n\nGather me reeds from the nearby pools.\n\nHah! If only all quest givers were like this! Straight to the point, no messing around! xD",
            date = "2012-05-08T21:31:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29662#comments:id=1664470",
        },
        {
            id = 1757826,
            score = 4,
            author = "JuliaHB",
            text = "I looked at this quest and https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29661 to see if anyone had mentioned where the \"lore\" comes from; the fact that you turn into a frog if you go into the water (or a skunk when you first go to get the quests from Aysa...).\n\n This is a reference to an manga/anime from the late 80's called Ranma 1/2. In that story, while on a training journey in the Bayankala Mountain Range in the Qinghai Province of China, Ranma Saotome and his father Genma fell into the cursed springs at Jusenkyo. When someone falls into a cursed spring, they take the physical form of whatever drowned there hundreds or thousands of years ago whenever they come into contact with cold water. The curse will revert when exposed to hot water until their next cold water exposure. Genma fell into the Spring of the Drowned Panda (and therefore becomes a giant panda when hit with cold water) while Ranma fell into the Spring of the Drowned Girl (so he becomes a \"she\"!). Many other characters in the story also came into contact with these cursed pools...one turns into a pig, another a cat, and yet another, a duck.\n\nIn the game, we saw the Pool of the Drowned Skunk, and Pool of the Drowned Frog...but if you explored just a little bit, there is also the Pool of the Drowned Crane, Drowned Turtle, and Drowned Baby Crocolisk. ^_^\n\nJust a little fun!\n\nhttp://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ranma_%C2%BD",
            date = "2012-11-05T19:16:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29662#comments:id=1757826",
        },
        {
            id = 1906040,
            score = 3,
            author = "780862",
            text = "dont follow him after the quest, he disappear after 5 minutes of walk :P",
            date = "2013-10-06T09:44:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29662#comments:id=1906040",
        },
        {
            id = 1754999,
            score = 1,
            author = "990608",
            text = "Try and keep out of the water, if you land in the water you get turned into a frog and the cranes will attack you",
            date = "2012-11-01T12:40:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29662#comments:id=1754999",
        },
    },
    [29663] = {
        {
            id = 1657459,
            score = 5,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "Do this quest while at the same time doing \"The Lesson of Dry Fur\".\n\nWhen you get the quest, go under the bridge and stand on the dry land.  This will turn you back into a Panda.  You will see wooden poles in front of you.  When you mouse over them, you will note that the green action arrow appears on the poles close enough for you to jump to.\n\nClick on a pole and you can jump from pole to pole.  The poles around the stone where the bells are will throw you up onto the stone.  Once on the poles you cannot fall off unless killed.\n\nYou will encounter the Tushi monks on the poles.  One you tap one - they will throw rocks at you.  Down 6 and you are done.\n\nYou can do this while going to the Bell for the The Lesson of Dry Fur.\n\nTo exit the pole maze, there are poles on the shore next to the bridge.  Jump to them and you can walk off the poles.",
            date = "2012-04-22T16:50:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29663#comments:id=1657459",
        },
        {
            id = 1883614,
            score = 1,
            author = "Merkilan",
            text = "It is expedient to do this at the same time as \"Lesson of dry fur\", however there is the extra danger of being turned into a toad and attacked by a crane when knocked off.  The balancing monks don't have to 'kill' you to knock you off.  There are two pools to the east of this one that won't curse you and have cranes try to eat you when you fall off if a lesser challenge is wanted to complete this quest.",
            date = "2013-08-03T13:07:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29663#comments:id=1883614",
        },
        {
            id = 1884075,
            score = 1,
            author = "Ryawy",
            text = "Rogues and Warriors can use their https://www.wowhead.com/spell=121733 (or https://www.wowhead.com/spell=122475) to hit trainees from a range, instead of needing to jump up to them.\n\nPriests, Mages, and Hunters are generally ranged anyway.",
            date = "2013-08-05T04:44:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29663#comments:id=1884075",
        },
    },
    [29664] = {
        {
            id = 1654912,
            score = 5,
            author = "jaquis",
            text = "This quest has become horrible and the false macro is making it worse.  I just completed it with a little graphics trick.  Set your graphics to lowest setting, and then switch to ultra.  It can help to bog system with loading some browser windows.  It took me 3 tries, but it does work.  You need to bog down your graphics card a bit so the other players load slowly.  Since they are last in priority and features are higher up... the brazier will appear before they will.  Some folks are logging, but the same effect can be achieved with a ui reload too.\n\nIf you have an incredible gaming machine... try it on an old machine...",
            date = "2012-04-16T14:29:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29664#comments:id=1654912",
        },
        {
            id = 1657441,
            score = 4,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "This quest is not a well designed quest but is not as miserable as everyone is making it out to be.\n\nIn the same room as the quest giver are four fires.  The first one is the Challenger which is right next to the quest giver.  The remaining fire pits light up at the corners of the water pool.\n\nLight the Challenger fire first - then the rest start to sparkle.\n\nThe torch was given to you and is in your bag.",
            date = "2012-04-22T16:07:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29664#comments:id=1657441",
        },
        {
            id = 1654506,
