    [29681] = {
        {
            id = 1681437,
            score = 8,
            author = "Eillesthis",
            text = "This quest is automatically offered, from no one in particular, once you turn in https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29675.  Under https://www.wowhead.com/npc=18481's portrait:\nBe careful, he is very powerful.\nand upon completion:\nTheir capabilities are most unsettling.\n\nAs for why two of the rewards are the same, they weren't originally, back when they were rewards from the now replaced https://www.wowhead.com/quest=10882.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=31747 was originally spell damage, then spell power, and now intellect.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=31749 was originally healing, then spell power, and now intellect.",
            date = "2012-06-26T15:21:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29681#comments:id=1681437",
        },
        {
            id = 1592700,
            score = 6,
            author = "Villager720",
            text = "Confirmation that Skyriss is in fact working for the Old Gods, and thus, the Old Gods are a galactic force of chaos, not unique to Azeroth!",
            date = "2011-12-08T14:26:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29681#comments:id=1592700",
        },
        {
            id = 1631199,
            score = 4,
            author = "Pypode",
            text = "I entered as Level 85 mage.  You will pick up two quests inside this dungeon.  At the end, after you kill the bosses in Stasis Block: Maximum, you will find a small doorway near the doorway from which you entered.  Go through this passage which will take you to Stasis Block: Trion. This is where you will complete the quest Maximum Security Breakout.  Very pretty zone. Take time later to look at it.\n\nThere are a couple of mobs in the beginning but The Protean Horrors almost did me in. They just don't quit. I finally ran through the hall into the next room, then the next small area and killed the ones who followed me. I do not recommend stopping to fight these creepy things.  Protean Spawn-slug-things will attack you in the hallways. Just keep on going, easy to follow the trail.\n\nYou will pass two sentries before you enter a room with two 4-person mobs. One pats the area. You can pull the patrol into the hallway, if you time it right. After they are dead, look at far side of the room to see the corpse of Udalo. (I hope you can hearth back to Shadowmoon Valley cuz thats where u need to go to complete the quest Seer Udalo.)\n\nGargantuan Abyssal can be pulled into this area before you go into the next area which has two huge Hellcallers and two huge Sargerons, all Elite 70s, paired, left and right. Can clear one without pulling the other pair unless you have a clone like mine, which started the second fight before I was ready.\n\nNow you will see three more challenges--Unchained Doombringer, Gargantuan Abyssal, & another Unchained Doombringer. Pull each one separately.\n\nAnd at the far end stands a very wee person...Warden Mellichar, Elite 72. The warden makes a speech before protecting himself with a bubble and sends for help: Phase hunter, Elite 72; then (to our surprise) Millhouse Manastorm, 70 elite, who says he will help. Third the Lightning Waker(?); Fourth Blackwing Drakonar 72 elite.  Finally Harbinger Skyriss, a huge grasshopperish-looking guy, for a quest.   He splits twice in the fight; I concentrated on the original.\n\nBack to Shadowmoon Valley to finish a very long quest.",
            date = "2012-02-24T14:54:51-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29681#comments:id=1631199",
        },
        {
            id = 1659234,
            score = 0,
            author = "druvirus",
            text = "Does it bother anyone else that the Potent Sha'tari Pendant and A'dal's Recovery Necklace are both the exact same stats?",
            date = "2012-04-27T02:20:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29681#comments:id=1659234",
        },
        {
            id = 2203889,
            score = -5,
            author = "Silden",
            text = "When time-walking this dungeon, the experience drops down to single-digits.",
            date = "2015-06-29T13:53:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29681#comments:id=2203889",
        },
    },
    [29682] = {
        {
            id = 1634070,
            score = 4,
            author = "Pypode",
            text = "I ran thru as Level 85 mage.  In Selin's room there are three mobs: two of six each and two directly ahead. You can attack each without aggroing Selin.  If casters attack first, he takes a few seconds to leave his platform and run down.  He will, during fight, run to green, suspended stone for healing.\n\nTyrith is lying inside the next area, the Halls of Theory. There are a two mobs of wyrms in this hall;  they are normal 70s. You can aggro one bunch at a time.  A keeper will approach to kill you; Vexalis awaits your attack on him. He will create motes of energy to attack you after you aggro him.\n\nThe scrying orb is just around the next wall. It has a short cinematic to preview, I thought, the next part during which you will kill Priestess Delrissa.\n\nKalecgos, of the Blue Dragonflight, will appear in his human form to your right to complete the quest, The Scryer's Scryer. He will give you the quest, Hard to Kill.  Keep on going past Kalecgos to enter the Halls of Theory again and face a rather intimidating mechanical, Level 71 elite who I was able to freeze in place.\n\nThe next area has many mobs of six; the first one includes both a mage and a warlock. Mages, you can Spellsteal here. You get a nice enemy mage-dampening, purple dome that heals and refills mana. The next mob you can steal fel armor and haste. Be warned, my pet started a fight with the next mob before I was ready. Definitely need casters/distance fighters in this area.Stay inside the purple dome whenever it is stolen. It's great. (My pets keep starting fights even when on Defense.)\n\nThe Priestess Delrissa is a many-armed boss surrounded by defenders. Wipe out all the surrounding mobs first, of course. Stupid pets started the boss fight before I cleared all the mobs!  Fortunately, the furthest one wasn't aggroed. Run on thru the next doorway to get to the final boss, Kael'thas and all his mobs.\n\nExarch Larethor shows up to complete outstanding quests. The pink orb up on the platform up the ramp will port you back to the Shattered Sun Staging Area.\n\nThis is a fun and very pretty dungeon.",
            date = "2012-03-02T06:29:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29682#comments:id=1634070",
        },
    },
