        },
    },
    [29692] = {
        {
            id = 1583473,
            score = 35,
            author = "Ashkir",
            text = "In 4.3 this is a repeatable quest (blue questionmark) that is given by T'shu (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=54674) in Underbog. You do not need any prior reputation with Sporeggar (http://www.wowhead.com/faction=970) to do this. Shrubberies are still obtained by normal means, as drops or looted from flowers through the dungeon.",
            date = "2011-11-29T16:56:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29692#comments:id=1583473",
        },
        {
            id = 1680160,
            score = 26,
            author = "ontera",
            text = "Bring me another shrubbery, lest I say \"Ni\"!",
            date = "2012-06-23T11:22:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29692#comments:id=1680160",
        },
        {
            id = 1650899,
            score = 24,
            author = "kulakai",
            text = "This repeatable quest rewards 750 rep instead of 250 as of 4.3.3.  Humans will get more with their racial bonus. You can pick up the quest from T'shu just inside the entrance to the Underbog.  Sanguine Hibiscus drops from the mobs in the instance or can be picked up like an herb. It isn't soulbound, so you can also trade it or buy it from the auction house.",
            date = "2012-04-08T22:03:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29692#comments:id=1650899",
        },
        {
            id = 2317891,
            score = 11,
            author = "Sn0vit",
            text = "Neutral to Exalted in 40 minutes!\n\nTested in WoD patch 6.2.4.\nWorks from atleast Neutral all the way up to Exalted with [faction=970],\ni got 750 rep for each https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29692 turn in on my lvl 100 horde druid.\nEasiest way to do this is to farm [zone=3716] on Normal.\n\nFarm tactic:\nEnter The Underbog on Normal.\nPick up all the https://www.wowhead.com/item=24246 and kill + loot all the mobs, up past Hungarfen until you see the first https://www.wowhead.com/npc=17726, this is where you run out of the instance and reset it.\n\nEach run took around 4 mins, and i got:\nFirst run: 20 x https://www.wowhead.com/item=24246\nSecond run: 29 x https://www.wowhead.com/item=24246\nThird run: 29 x https://www.wowhead.com/item=24246\n\nRep from mob kills:\n[faction=970]: ~1260 rep (21 rep from normal mobs and 210 rep from Hungarfen)\n[faction=942]: ~420 rep (7 rep from normal mobs and 70 rep from Hungarfen)\n\nIf you want to buy the https://www.wowhead.com/item=24246 from AH you will need:\nNeutral to Friendly: 4 quest hand ins = 20 x https://www.wowhead.com/item=24246\nFriendly to Honored: 8 quest hand ins = 40 x https://www.wowhead.com/item=24246\nHonored to Revered: 16 quest hand ins = 80 x https://www.wowhead.com/item=24246\nRevered to Exalted: 28 quest hand ins = 140 x https://www.wowhead.com/item=24246\n\nSummary\nFrom Neutral to Exalted: 56 https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29692 hand ins = 280 x https://www.wowhead.com/item=24246 if you buy them from AH.\nIf you get around 23 https://www.wowhead.com/item=24246 per run + 1260 rep from killing mobs, you need around 8-9 Underbog runs and around 40 mins of your time!\n\nHope this was of any help, good luck! :)",
            date = "2016-03-29T12:09:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29692#comments:id=2317891",
        },
        {
            id = 1700108,
            score = 7,
            author = "1022147",
            text = "While the quest gives 750rep (with no bonuses) I also get 23rep per mob and 237rep from bosses. I am already exhalted with the Cenarion Expedition, so the spillover rep might then be transferred to Sporeggar.\n\nSo farming underbog does not only give these quest items, it also gives rep from killing the mobs.",
            date = "2012-08-15T05:30:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29692#comments:id=1700108",
        },
    },
    [29693] = {
        {
            id = 1656429,
            score = 48,
            author = "926587",
            text = "So if you are a Hunter, shouldn't that mean you should be able to choose from all the items?",
            date = "2012-04-20T08:07:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29693#comments:id=1656429",
        },
        {
            id = 1653783,
            score = 28,
            author = "Zillions",
            text = "General Nazgrim says:\nUngh... Wha?\nMy weapon?\n\nThis quest rewards a dynamic quest reward based on your class.  For example, hunters receive a https://www.wowhead.com/item=80970.",
            date = "2012-04-14T11:47:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29693#comments:id=1653783",
        },
        {
            id = 1657075,
            score = 15,
            author = "OldRatbeard",
            text = "The only problem I see with this is this: Let's say I'm playing a paladin, and I see that there's a quest that gives out the Scavenger's Club and it would look perfect with the transmog set that I'm putting together.\n\nProblem is, the Scavenger's Club isn't available to paladins, because it's got agility on it, and dynamic questing makes it impossible for me to acquire this weapon. The rewards are BoP so I can now never get it. This is lame. I suppose as long as this isn't retroactive, it won't be a problem, but I don't like the idea of being locked out of items I would have otherwise had access to. Getting a cool looking weapon model to transmog might be worth losing the 20g or so I'd get from vendoring it, and maybe my current weapon is good enough.",
            date = "2012-04-22T00:07:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29693#comments:id=1657075",
        },
        {
            id = 1658163,
            score = 13,
            author = "KingSeamus",
            text = "The only real flaw I see is for cloth wearing classes, often on my cloth toons I will pick the plate item because it vendors for more. Yes, until your 90 you might be using some quest items but I am sure most slots will be filled with dungeon gear rather soon.",
            date = "2012-04-24T10:44:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29693#comments:id=1658163",
        },
        {
            id = 1657692,
            score = 4,
            author = "alexko9",
            text = "Honestly this system is a bit weird and I don't like it. Normally while questing as a druid you encounter quests that either give useful agility to you or useful intellect gear. Questing like that provides me with no choice on what item I get and is all dependent on the spec I'm in. So really if I want to gear two different specs at the same time I would have to turn every other quest or look up the quest and change spec before turning in...",
            date = "2012-04-23T07:23:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29693#comments:id=1657692",
        },
    },
    [29694] = {
        {
            id = 1718892,
            score = 20,
            author = "45642",
            text = "Rivett could be a little tricky to find.\n\nHe's hanging from a tree, north of the honeydew village. Between the river and the edge of the world.",
            date = "2012-09-25T15:22:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29694#comments:id=1718892",
        },
        {
            id = 1719899,
            score = 17,
            author = "1031945",
            text = "Shademaster Kiryn  32.0  13.3\nShokia   29.4  8.5\nRivett Clutchpop  30.5  7.2\nSgt. Gorrok  30.6   11.7",
            date = "2012-09-26T09:10:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29694#comments:id=1719899",
        },
        {
            id = 2572091,
            score = 6,
            author = "Skargus",
            text = "In order to get this quest on my 110 goblin shaman (trial toon boosted to 100 originally), I had to turn on track trivial quests while in Orgrimmar, then speak to General Nazgrim in Grommash Hold to get the quest \"The Art of War\".  This quest chain starts the Mist of Pandaria intro scenario.  After about half a dozen quests, you'll finally be given the quest \"Regroup!\"  I was after the Cannonball Dented Shield for my TMog.\n\nOnly after having completed the intro scenario did a portal to Honeydew Village appear in Orgrimmar.  I had never done the MoP scenario on any toon before.  I tried to follow the instructions in the post below, but had no portal initially.  After doing some more internet research did I figure out what I needed to do.",
            date = "2018-06-03T21:50:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29694#comments:id=2572091",
        },
        {
            id = 1718439,
            score = 4,
            author = "Alaticia2012",
            text = "On the minimap the people you need to speak to  are shown by speechmarks. :D",
            date = "2012-09-25T07:50:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29694#comments:id=1718439",
        },
        {
            id = 1718951,
            score = 3,
            author = "Domina",
            text = "Leave Thunder Hold and go back down the staircase into the jungle.\n\nShademaster Kiryn is next to the questgivers at the bottom of the steps (32, 13).\n\nYou'll find the people you're supposed to rescue by looking for the white dialog boxes above them in person and on your minimap around this area.",
            date = "2012-09-25T16:05:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29694#comments:id=1718951",
        },
    },
