    [29733] = {
        {
            id = 5906340,
            score = 101,
            author = "UthrenAN",
            text = "As of this date, there is a bug where Rell dies way too fast. However, here is a workaround:\n\n1. After you talk to Kearnen, run away west (toward the river) far enough to where the hozen will not aggro you (you may have just one aggro you, if so, kill it).\n2. Wait about 30-45 seconds for all the hozen to spawn.\n3. Slowly walk in to edge of the quest area's blue circle on your minimap, barely enough to not aggro them.\nNote: The hozen's position is random. Sometimes you may have to kill to reach the edge of the blue circle. As long as you don't aggro two at at a time or aggro the boss you should be good.\n4. Wait for about 5 minutes, the hozen will automatically die and you will get credit.",
            date = "2024-07-27T10:07:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29733#comments:id=5906340",
        },
        {
            id = 5904853,
            score = 48,
            author = "DarkfireZarandar",
            text = "As of 7/25/2024 (patch 11.0), specifically Remix: Mists of Pandaria in my case, it appears that there is an issue with how much damage the Hozen do. Sometimes it seems normal, but sometimes it is so significant that it KO's you from 70%. Either this is a bug, or their critical hit rates are astronomical. I have tried at least ten times and was knocked out of the \"report\" every time. The last time, I was hit for 67% or more (I was at 67%) and KO'd, and I have been at 80% and knocked down to 2% in one hit.\n\nAnother reason I think this is unintentional is that a couple times I was hit for severe damage, and then healed up most of that damage (from 75% to 3%, then back up to 65% the last time I noted it).\n\nAs an aside, I really wish we could skip the delay from the dialogue in the beginning.",
            date = "2024-07-25T11:52:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29733#comments:id=5904853",
        },
        {
            id = 3182440,
            score = 30,
            author = "Azraenya",
            text = "This is my first time trying this quest, but I am completely unable to do it.  As I understand things, accepting the quest should put me in Rell's body with his skills available, and transfer me to the quest location.  However, no matter what I do, I've never gotten put into the quest \"vehicle\" body.  I've read that pets can cause problems, so I dismissed mine.  I read that UI errors can cause it to mess up, so I disabled my entire setup of addons and just tried with the default WoW UI.  I have been completely unable to use Rell's abilities, or even see his sprite instead of that of my character.  I tried running off to the right like some dwarf is supposed to at some point, and I do see a broken-down airship, but there's no Amber anywhere around it.  On top of the broken airship stands General Rik-Rik, who doesn't respond to me in any way.\n\nI AM getting ported to where the quest is supposed to start...but it never does.  I've abandoned and retaken it close to fifteen times trying different combinations of pet/no pet and addons/no addons, but nothing works.  Help?",
            date = "2020-01-16T01:06:36-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29733#comments:id=3182440",
        },
        {
            id = 1912343,
            score = 23,
            author = "Dariusdracos",
            text = "After doing this a few times, I thoroughly loathe this mini chain. Such a huge pain in the ass.",
            date = "2013-10-26T23:26:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29733#comments:id=1912343",
        },
        {
            id = 1655296,
            score = 16,
            author = "Bethenal",
            text = "Beta Build 15589\n\nWhen you accept the quest, you are transported to Fox Grove as Rell Nightwind to relive the events of Rell’s story.  You are given three abilities:\n\nSure Strike (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=103693) – Strikes at an enemy, dealing Physical Damage (0.85 sec cd).\nMasterful Strike (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=103695 ) – Deals a large amount of Physical damage (5 sec cd).\nTwin Strike (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=103696 )  - Deals an incredible amount of Physical damage, knocking the target down (15 sec cd).\n\nAfter a very short RP lead-in, you are directed to talk to Amber Kearnen (who is on the plane).  After that the Hozen ambush will begin.  You will be attacked by 3x 85 elite Hozen (with 632k health) and then by General  Rik-Rik, another 85 elite (with 1264k health).\n\nThe strat to do this is fairly simple: make sure you use the Masterful Strike and Twin Strike abilities on cooldown.  The Hozen come out one at a time, but you will likely still be dealing with one as the next comes out.  The abilities are single target, so take down each hozen before moving on to the next as the damage from more than one for too long will overwhelm you and you can’t heal or drink health pots.\n\nTip:  If it looks like you are going to die, exit the vehicle which will take you back to the start.  If you die and have to corpse run, you will rez right on top of any elites that are still in that area.\n\nBecause the full quest chain is not showing on WoWHead yet, the quests are in this order:\n1. The Scouts Return (http://mop.wowhead.com/quest=30458)\n2. SI:7 Report: Lost in the Woods (http://mop.wowhead.com/quest=29733)\n3. SI:7 Report: Fire From the Sky (http://mop.wowhead.com/quest=29725)\n4. SI:7 Report: Hostile Natives (http://mop.wowhead.com/quest=29726 )\n5. SI:7 Report: Take No Prisoners (http://mop.wowhead.com/quest=29727 )\n\nEdit:  added full quest chain",
            date = "2012-04-17T10:33:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29733#comments:id=1655296",
        },
    },
    [29743] = {
