        },
    },
    [29779] = {
        {
            id = 1718925,
            score = 2,
            author = "940955",
            text = "The hozen are absolutely hilarious. So much of what they do is funsies and does barely any damage. For example, the ones with the Firework Launcher will occasionally cast \"Shoot ALL the fireworks!\" which.... makes you sparkle for a bit. It's also a reference to the meme 'X ALL the Y', taken from here (http://hyperboleandahalf.blogspot.in/2010/06/this-is-why-ill-never-be-adult.html).",
            date = "2012-09-25T15:40:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29779#comments:id=1718925",
        },
        {
            id = 1657470,
            score = 1,
            author = "329137",
            text = "This is another quest where you have to take care not to pull too many Hozen. This is on the Beta, but the spawn rate is very high (due to how quickly other players are killing them off) and regardless of that, they will swarm you if you get too close to them. Stand back and pull, if possible. Ji Firepaw accompanies and fights alongside you, but he's not all that helpful. Be ready to use Quaking Palm (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=107079) and any other skills you have, to get away at the first sign of trouble.\n\nSome classes will do fine (Hunters especially), Monks and other Ranged classes be OK if you're careful. Others (Warriors, Rogues) need to take great care.\n\nLet the Pandaren corpses littering the ground serve as a warning!",
            date = "2012-04-22T17:25:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29779#comments:id=1657470",
        },
        {
            id = 1659576,
            score = 1,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "From the quest giver, proceed on the path the leads up the hill behind where the quest giver provides you with the quest.  You will have a fighting companion with you - which is a big help on this quest.\n\nAt the top of the hill - there is a path to the left (Do No Evil) and a path to the right (Monkey Advisory Warning).\n\nMake sure to pick up quests - \"Do No Evil\" and \"Monkey Advisor Warning\" and do these two quests at the same time.\n\nThis quest is simple if you are ranged DPS because you can pull the monkeys one at a time.\n\nThe first ones you pull are the two by the totem pole as you approach the village.  You can pick up a quest there at the totem.\n\nNext go to the right and pull the groups along the fence line - one monkey at a time - then go up and loot the fireworks.  Try to do this quickly as the monkeys respawn fast.  Watch out for the wondering monkey going back and forth on the main path.",
            date = "2012-04-27T20:36:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29779#comments:id=1659576",
        },
        {
            id = 1789152,
            score = 1,
            author = "mongrel1999",
            text = "If like me you die on the rocks below the mountain. SS back to training ground and go to the Temple of Five Dawns. R/click on the wirlwind thing. this will take you up in the air to where the path is to get you back to the quests.",
            date = "2012-12-29T14:07:09-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29779#comments:id=1789152",
        },
    },
    [29780] = {
        {
            id = 1728730,
            score = 7,
            author = "druunah",
            text = "As you head up the road toward Fe-Feng Village, you will see \"Jade Tiger Pillar\" standing to the left of the road. Kill the monkeys guarding it and get the quest it provides.\n\nTake the road to the left of where the pillar stood into the small \"valley\" continue to stay to the left. Near the cliff edge you will come to, you will see a large evergreen looking tree with a pale trunk with Ruk-Ruk underneath it. Kill him to complete the quest. You will be aided by Ji Firepaw, so there is no need to be in a group. Ji says \"Lets do this monkeyface!\" \"That all you got?\" \"This monkey's about to get slapped!\" and \"He's down for the count! Good going!\"",
            date = "2012-10-02T12:31:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29780#comments:id=1728730",
        },
        {
            id = 1723716,
            score = 3,
            author = "kerrymayall",
            text = "\"This monkey is about to get slapped\"\n\nI LoL'ed",
            date = "2012-09-28T23:12:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29780#comments:id=1723716",
        },
        {
            id = 1659579,
            score = 1,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "Ruk-ruk can be most easily beaten as a group.  So if someone is standing around waiting for the respawn - invite them to a group.\n\nTo find Ruk-ruk - proceed up the hill to the west of the village.  At the top the road reaches a T-intersection.  In front of you will be a totem that you should have already beaten the two monkeys and collected the quest from.  If not - smack the monkies and collect the quest.\n\nLook out for a wondering monkey who criss-crosses up and down the path.\n\nNext go left (facing the totem) and between the gap there is a small valley.  Go to the far corner and you will find Ruk-ruk.",
            date = "2012-04-27T20:44:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29780#comments:id=1659579",
        },
        {
            id = 1957657,
            score = 1,
            author = "912158",
            text = "See no evil, hear no evil, speak no evil, Do No Evil.",
            date = "2014-04-11T09:00:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29780#comments:id=1957657",
        },
    },
    [29781] = {
        {
            id = 1730841,
            score = 4,
            author = "245224",
            text = "Seems a bug with this quest made it to live from the beta. If you find yourself unable to loot fireworks. Exit wow and delete the itemcache file in the WDB folder within the Cache folder, restart and try again.",
            date = "2012-10-04T06:16:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29781#comments:id=1730841",
        },
        {
            id = 1659578,
            score = 3,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "You should be doing the quest \"The Direct Solution\" while doing this quest.  More detailed directions are posted with that quest.  The summary - go up the hill, turn right (after killing the two monkeys at the totem and gathering that quest), the stick to the mountain next to the totem and pull the monkeys one at a time to you.  Then when clear - run up and click on the jars to get the Stolen Firework Bundle.",
            date = "2012-04-27T20:39:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29781#comments:id=1659578",
        },
        {
            id = 1746763,
            score = 2,
            author = "941372",
            text = "There are a lot of fireworks near https://www.wowhead.com/npc=55634.",
            date = "2012-10-20T22:06:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29781#comments:id=1746763",
        },
    },
    [29782] = {
        {
            id = 1749764,
            score = 24,
            author = "MarsJenkar",
            text = "For posterity, here's what happens after you turn the quest in:\n\nJojo Ironbrow says: This is magnificent!  I've never seen craftsmanship so fine.\nJojo Ironbrow says: There is only one thing to do.  I must smash it!  Once and for all, all shall know the power of my mighty brow.\n[Jojo attempts to smash the pillar, but fails, leaving him dizzy.]\nJojo Ironbrow says: Oh... my head... it hurts so badly!  I've... the pillar must contain enormous power... perhaps stronger even than my brow.\nJojo Ironbrow says: I'm... I'm just going to lie down a while... until this headache goes away.\n\nAnd later on, you see he's wielding the jade pillar as a weapon.",
            date = "2012-10-24T20:22:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29782#comments:id=1749764",
        },
        {
            id = 1718670,
            score = 18,
            author = "1011285",
            text = "Finally, something that will stop that guy's annoying little speeches.",
            date = "2012-09-25T11:52:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29782#comments:id=1718670",
        },
        {
            id = 1926801,
            score = 17,
            author = "Traynwreck",
            text = "Because doctors all agree; the best thing to do after a head injury is lie down and sleep...",
            date = "2013-12-17T12:40:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29782#comments:id=1926801",
        },
        {
            id = 1719433,
            score = 14,
            author = "973043",
            text = "A quest that you must do or it will cause you to be stuck with no lead.",
            date = "2012-09-26T01:09:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29782#comments:id=1719433",
        },
        {
            id = 1731450,
            score = 10,
            author = "akatnel",
            text = "I was glad to get this quest. I'd gotten rather tired of this guy showing off all the time.",
            date = "2012-10-04T16:54:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29782#comments:id=1731450",
        },
    },
    [29783] = {
        {
            id = 1721963,
            score = 8,
            author = "tarc",
            text = "These are the strongest stones across all of Shen-zin Su, yet they are as nothing before my mighty head.\n\nTHWACK.\n\nAny yet who doubt my strength are simply foolish.\n\nThis one despawns on the spot after a few minutes, no walking.",
            date = "2012-09-27T18:23:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29783#comments:id=1721963",
        },
    },
    [29784] = {
        {
            id = 1725684,
            score = 22,
            author = "jabberie",
            text = "Make sure that you do Stronger Than Bone (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=29782) before going back to Aysa on the rope. It's not directly linked to the chain but you need it to be able to get\nDafeng, the Spirit of Air.",
            date = "2012-09-30T06:46:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29784#comments:id=1725684",
        },
        {
            id = 1787317,
            score = 13,
            author = "bowedoak1",
            text = "Although it was mentioned earlier, I want to expand. This quest drove me nuts and even with the walk, strafe etc I still have trouble. Earlier someone mentioned \"use right click to move\"  and I wanted to go into that more bc it's foolproof.\nGo to:\nGame Menu\nInterface\nMouse\nClick to Move.\nMake each pillar your target, right click dead center and your character will walk there and stop. Do the next pillar etc. Three moves and done.",
            date = "2012-12-25T14:58:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29784#comments:id=1787317",
        },
        {
            id = 1722274,
            score = 11,
            author = "JohnPWest",
            text = "Use the right click move-to mechanism and you will not fall off the rope!",
            date = "2012-09-27T23:22:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29784#comments:id=1722274",
        },
        {
            id = 1656316,
            score = 5,
            author = "selvin",
            text = "If you keep falling off the rope what I found to work best was to stand so that your character's head was in the middle of the rope pointing to the next pillar, and then just push the forward arrow key. Overcompensation is what makes you fall off, not waiting too long to correct.",
            date = "2012-04-19T23:59:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29784#comments:id=1656316",
        },
        {
            id = 1729235,
            score = 5,
            author = "259667",
            text = "I.  Hate.  This.  Quest.  Despise it. Revile it. Loathe the thought.  Really don't like it.\n\nI am a keyboard player and, it turns out, a klutz of a Panda.  What should take seconds took hours and was Really Not Fun.\n\nSo, if you are about to cancel your WoW subscription, have already tried the \"auto run\" click and wondered how to get a water-walking potion onto this God-forsaken island, I have a solution.  Stupid? Maybe, but it worked.\n\n1. Turn off \"run\" (that is: hit the / key one time, you should now walk instead of run) and hop onto the first pylon/post.\n2. Rotate your camera view upward until you are looking staight down on your panda-self.\n3. Pan out until you can see 5-10 steps in front of your toon.\n4. Breathe.\n5. As much as possible, line up your toon's nose to the direction of the rope.\n6. Hit the up arrow once per step.  Watch the left-right trends. My Panda, it turns out, leans to the right.  (Must be an alignment issue or below the equator, I dunno.  Whatever.)\n7. As soon as the toon's nose is close to the edge of the rope, strafe in the other direction (one keystroke, \"Q\" made me go one step left, \"E\" one step right)\n8. Breathe.\n9. Repeat 6-8 until you reach a post, then turn, go to step 4 and repeat.\n10. On the final run, keep moving your mouse up to see when you are close enough to turn in this [CENSORED] quest.",
            date = "2012-10-02T22:07:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29784#comments:id=1729235",
        },
    },
    [29785] = {
        {
            id = 1728745,
            score = 26,
            author = "druunah",
            text = "To avoid the winds simply wait for Aysa Cloudsinger (who should be with you) then run when she runs.You should make it across without problems.",
            date = "2012-10-02T12:44:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29785#comments:id=1728745",
        },
        {
            id = 1739783,
            score = 14,
            author = "994996",
            text = "If you're unable to start this quest after finishing Balanced Perspective (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=29784), check to make sure you have done Stronger than Bone (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=29782), which starts from a green totem outside the hozen village. This may allow you to continue your questing.",
            date = "2012-10-12T17:45:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29785#comments:id=1739783",
        },
        {
            id = 1659584,
            score = 9,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "Ok - you ran across the ropes from \"Balanced Perspective\" and you are now on Dafeng, the Spirit of Air.  Aysa will be following you on this journey.\n\nFollow the trail south out of the village.  The trail ends at the Chamber of Whispers.  Do not run in right away or you could potentially die.  Tornadic winds will blow debris out of the building and onto you.  So step back and take cover after Aysa tells you to \"Watch Out\".  If you don't have audio - then step in and back out before you take damage.\n\nOnce the blast subsides - run into the room - across the room and up the stairs.  Another blast will start when you hit the stairs, take cover behind a pillar next to the wall to minimize the damage.\n\nRun into the room, across the room, the wind calms and you can turn in the quest once you reach Dafeng.",
            date = "2012-04-27T20:52:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29785#comments:id=1659584",
        },
        {
            id = 1654443,
            score = 1,
            author = "wgrinolds",
            text = "It's not made clear, but to avoid the damage, while the wind is gusting, move to the sides and wait for the wind to die down.\n\nYou can ignore this mechanic and die - you should only have to die once before reaching Dafeng.",
            date = "2012-04-15T14:45:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29785#comments:id=1654443",
        },
        {
            id = 1656319,
            score = 1,
            author = "selvin",
            text = "Next in chain is Battle for the Skies. (http://mop.wowhead.com/quest=29786)",
            date = "2012-04-20T00:14:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29785#comments:id=1656319",
        },
    },
    [29786] = {
        {
            id = 1765106,
            score = 16,
            author = "Lauraline",
            text = "I hated this quest, dying my though it on my monk, but today helping my daughter on it I finally understood the trick to it.\n\nYou run counter clockwise as said in previous posts.\nBut also you will launch only every other or third launcher you get to...cause this is when the serpent is close enough.\n\nYou stand at the launcher prepaired....and when you se the lightening of his AOE beginning to form and come towards you, (just as it forms like a lightning) you click the launcher\nand, eventhough you cant see if the firework is launched, you run!\nThis is important.\nCause clicking it it feels like \"nothing happened\" and you might be tempted to wait that one millisecond to se it go off and then the AOE will hit you.\n\nJust trust that it will launch at one click and then run.... it will hit him roughly when the AOE hits where the launcher is.....\nwith you at a safe distance on the way to the next spot. (2-3 launchers away)\n\nI got hit only by one AOE doing it this way and also went over the green bubble for a quick heal...so mainly  full health (at this lvl 9 hunter with pet dismissed) when he finally went down.\n\nGood luck on this.",
            date = "2012-11-20T02:52:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29786#comments:id=1765106",
        },
        {
            id = 1731513,
            score = 5,
            author = "Bettievamp",
            text = "THIS IS NOT AN EASY QUEST!  After dying TWICE, what I did was just move as quickly as I could counter-clockwise from one fireworks to another until he came down (avoiding his infernal AOE all the time, mind you) and finally was able to kill this guy. If the next one still has is AOE around it, go to the next one because otherwise you will NOT survive. Hope this helps! Not sure if this matters, but I'm a lvl 9 hunter.",
            date = "2012-10-04T17:43:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29786#comments:id=1731513",
        },
        {
            id = 1678198,
            score = 3,
            author = "943939",
            text = "It would help if he didn't keep evading everything right now. will wait till after the next reset.",
            date = "2012-06-18T22:34:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29786#comments:id=1678198",
        },
        {
            id = 1757123,
            score = 3,
            author = "983937",
            text = "It takes TWO to tango.\nYou can kill the beast if someone else is on the quest at the same time.",
            date = "2012-11-04T16:21:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29786#comments:id=1757123",
        },
        {
            id = 1772581,
            score = 3,
            author = "Wimbleton",
            text = "After dying the second time and inventing some new swear words, I found that you can actually go far enough away to be out of combat, use the bandages you don't have, then run back and your NPC teammate will still be engaging him. He doesn't automatically reset. All else is true - counterclockwise, etc. Fighting him on the ground was amusing but for a monk, fairly meaningless. Kind of like pelting a Bengal tiger with cotton balls.\n\nThe Time-Constrained Player isn't allowed to try a quest twice and I was wondering if abandoning this one was going to cause sequence problems when he finally died. 16 minutes of irritating glitchiness. It's a kind of minor torture, like listening to fourth-graders trying to learn how to play the violin.",
            date = "2012-11-30T21:53:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29786#comments:id=1772581",
        },
    },
    [29787] = {
        {
            id = 1659587,
            score = 7,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "Master Shang Xi leads you north then west along a path leading to a long stairway.  Climb the stairs to the top.  Master Shang Xi tells you that you must defeat the guardian before you can pass.  This is an easy easy fight.\n\nAfter the fight, follow Master Shang Xi up the next set of stairs where he will give you his next quest.",
            date = "2012-04-27T21:02:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29787#comments:id=1659587",
        },
        {
            id = 1796794,
            score = 3,
            author = "Aros",
            text = "Dialog for this quest as Master Shang Xi leads you up to the Wood of Staves.\nMaster Shang Xi says: Come Child. We have one final journey to take together before your training is complete.\nMaster Shang Xi says: Beyond the Elders' Path lies the Wood of Staves, a sacred place that only the worthy may enter.\nMaster Shang Xi says: Of the many ways to prove your worth, I require the simplest of you now. I must know that you will fight for our people. I must know that you can keep them safe.\nMaster Shang Xi says: Defeat the Guardian of the Elders (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=56274), and we may pass.\nMaster Shang Xi says: You've become strong indeed, child. This is good. You will need that strength soon.\nMaster Shang Xi says: And here we are. Help me with a couple small tasks while I prepare, if you would.",
            date = "2013-01-11T17:26:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29787#comments:id=1796794",
        },
    },
    [29788] = {
        {
            id = 1681147,
            score = 27,
            author = "614435",
            text = "Be very careful with these!  It's not uncommon for 2 or 3 scamps to run around together.  If they all decide to attack you and each spawn 2 of their summoned scamps, good night!  Tread very carefully and try to attack one that's alone if you can!",
            date = "2012-06-25T20:34:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29788#comments:id=1681147",
        },
        {
            id = 1659588,
            score = 4,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "You followed Master Shang Xi to this area after beating the Guardian in the previous quest \"Worthy of Passing\".\n\nYou should make sure and pick up the second quest \"Small, But Significant\" and do this quest at the same time.\n\nThe Thornbranch Scamps are both to the north and south in all of the areas where you will be also harvesting the Kun-Pai Ritual Charms for the \"Small, But Significant\" quest.\n\nOne neat trick is when the Thornbranch Scamp is that it will summon two additional scamps.  The two additional scamps (of much lower health, 31 health) will appear and start wailing on you.  All three together can spank you pretty good, so stay focused on the main scamp and kill him quick.  The summon is time based - about 5 seconds was my estimate.  The scamps disappear after about 4 seconds.\n\nWhen you are down to just the two summoned scamps, they are pretty easy to kill one or two hits each - or you can run away and they will dispurse in a few seconds after the scamp who summoned them is dead.",
            date = "2012-04-27T21:16:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29788#comments:id=1659588",
        },
        {
            id = 1836264,
            score = 4,
            author = "945326",
            text = "This requires more patience than anything else.  Once you receive the quest, you'll see quite a few of the sprites.  But don't start attacking just yet.  Just stand there in front of the NPC for a bit and look around you.\n\nYou'll see several pairs of running sprites.   And then, if you look close, you'll see a couple of single sprites, often lounging around on the ground.\n\nNow watch to see the path that the running sprites take.  And how long it takes them to complete a circuit.\n\nNOW, look for a single sprite, and WAIT until any running pairs that path by him have gone by.  Attack the single sprite.  If you are ranged, pull them away from the path of the running pair.  If you are melee, attack and then back up out of range of the running pair when they path back around.\n\nThe two lesser scamps each one summons when about 1/3 heath are very fragile.  Don't worry about killing them.  Kill your main target first.  The two summoned scamps will die on their own seconds after you finish killing the main target.  I often only managed to kill one of them before the other one died on its own.\n\nBut the point is that you'll see lots of sprites/scamps and -- if you're a typical WoW player -- you'll just start in on killing.  That's a good way to die yourself.",
            date = "2013-03-29T13:03:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29788#comments:id=1836264",
        },
        {
            id = 2334602,
            score = 1,
            author = "Caudog",
            text = "Oh, you only need one more mob?  Lucky you, here comes three!",
            date = "2016-05-27T09:30:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29788#comments:id=2334602",
        },
    },
    [29789] = {
        {
            id = 1659589,
            score = 6,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "The Kun-Pai Ritual Charms hang from the trees - the are long red ropes with a ring on the end.  They will be sparkling.  There are often more than one per tree.  There are in two areas, one to the north and one to the south of the quest giver, and also there are a few in the immediate are around the quest giver.\n\nMake sure and pick up the quest \"Unwelcome Nature\" because you will be killing the scamps while you are collecting the ritual charms.  Note in the posting for Unwelcome Nature, that the Thornbranch Scamp summons two additional skamps (31 health) when the scamp reaches one third health.",
            date = "2012-04-27T21:17:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29789#comments:id=1659589",
        },
        {
            id = 6145337,
            score = 1,
            author = "Kaelen",
            text = "It is called Kun-Pai Ritual Charm, which appears randomly on tree branches. I found some at coordinates 18.35, 48.24.",
            date = "2025-07-18T03:03:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29789#comments:id=6145337",
        },
        {
            id = 1662949,
            score = -4,
            author = "asloversgo",
            text = "That's what she said.",
            date = "2012-05-05T09:49:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29789#comments:id=1662949",
        },
    },
    [29790] = {
        {
            id = 1743146,
            score = 44,
            author = "Rankkor",
            text = "If you don't choke up even a little bit, something is wrong with you.\n\nThis is a very sad quest, as your master passes away. The music used in this scene really helps to sell the moment.\n\nKudos, MASSIVE KUDOS to the entire music team. I know every expansion (even the disaster that was cataclysm) has had incredible music, but they really outdid themselves here. This very simple quest has one of the most emotional moments ever due to its very fitting music.",
            date = "2012-10-16T07:11:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29790#comments:id=1743146",
        },
        {
            id = 1718078,
            score = 31,
            author = "Molaca",
            text = "For 3,000 years, we have passed the knowledge of our people down. Elder to youth. Master to student.\n\nEvery elder reaches the day where he must pass on and plant his stave with the staves of his ancestors. Today is the day when my staff joins these woods.\n\nPlayer, our people have lived the wholes of their lives on this great turtle, Shen-zin Su, but not in hundreds of years has anyone spoken to him.\n\nNow Shen-zin is ill, and we all are in danger. With the help of the elements, you will break the silence. You will speak to him\n\nAysa and Ji have retrieved the spirits and brought them here. You are to go with them, speak to the great Shen-zin Su, and do what must be done to save our people.\n\nYou've come far, my young student. I see within you a great hero. I leave the fate of this land to you.\n\nMaster Shang Xi's words as he plants his staff in the ground.",
            date = "2012-09-24T19:35:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29790#comments:id=1718078",
        },
        {
            id = 1659591,
            score = 11,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "Listen to the story - then realize we are living on a turtle.  I Love Being a Turtle!  oh- that is another game.\n\nAnyway, climb the stairs near the quest giver, at the top jog right, then head down the hill toward the Balloon.  Aysa Cloudsinger, will be there to turn in the quest to.",
            date = "2012-04-27T21:29:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29790#comments:id=1659591",
        },
        {
            id = 1718150,
            score = 5,
            author = "294966",
            text = "it is broken for me",
            date = "2012-09-24T23:12:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29790#comments:id=1718150",
        },
        {
            id = 6242088,
            score = 1,
            author = "Deenaria",
            text = "If you return to his resting place during the pandaren heritage armor quest line, you will see that his tree/staff has grown! Its not a whole lot but it made me choke up either way :')",
            date = "2025-12-08T13:50:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29790#comments:id=6242088",
        },
    },
    [29791] = {
        {
            id = 1796827,
            score = 20,
            author = "Aros",
            text = "As you approach the balloon to pick up this quest Aysa Cloudsinger (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=56662) and Ji Firepaw (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=56663) greats you with these words:\n\nAysa Cloudsinger says: We're ready to go whenever you are, .\nJi Firepaw says: Or if you want to wander the woods a while, Aysa and I can hang out here. You know... just the two of us.\nAysa Cloudsinger says: Don't listen to him. We've got work to do.\n\nThen there's a long dialog during the flight with the balloon.\n\nAysa Cloudsinger says: Hop in.\nJi Firepaw says: , where's Master Shang?\nAysa Cloudsinger says: ...Ji, they where in the Wood of Staves. You know where Master Shang is now.\nJi Firepaw says: Bah, let a pandaren hope, would you? I'm going to miss the old man.\nAysa Cloudsinger says: Ji, be respectful when we speak to Shen-zin Su.\nJi Firepaw says: When am I not respectful? You hurt me, Aysa.\nAysa Cloudsinger says: I might, if you embarrass us.\nAysa Cloudsinger yells: Shen-zin Su, we are the descendants of Liu Lang. We've sensed your pain, and we want to help.\nAysa Cloudsinger yells: What ails you Shen-zin Su? What can we do?\nShen-zin Su says: I am in pain, but it warms my heart that Liu Lang's grandchildren have not forgotten me.\nShen-zin Su says: There is a thorn in my side. I cannot remove it.\nShen-zin Su says: The pain is unbearable, and I can no longer swim straight.\nShen-zin Su says: Please grandchildren, can you remove this thorn? I cannot do so on my own.\nAysa Cloudsinger yells: Of course, Shen-zin Su! But your shell is large, and I do not know where this thorn could be.\nShen-zin Su says: It is in the forest where your feet do not walk. Continue along the mountains and you will find it.\nAysa Cloudsinger yells: We will find it, and we will remove it. You have our word!\nShen-zin Su says: Thank you, grandchildren.\nJi Firepaw says: A thorn? And I left my tweezers at home.\nJi Firepaw says: How could such a thing cause pain to something so large?\nAysa Cloudsinger says: We'll know soon enough.\nJi Firepaw says: Are you seeing what I'm seeing? Is that a boat?\nAysa Cloudsinger says: It is a boat... a whole airship! That's a bigger thorn than I was expecting.\nJi Firepaw says: And those aren't pandaren down there. They've got no fur. Aysa Cloudsinger says: Someone has crashed into our island. Removing this thorn may be more complicated than we thought.\nAysa Cloudsinger says:We should let Elder Shaopai and then plan our next move.",
            date = "2013-01-11T18:24:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29791#comments:id=1796827",
        },
        {
            id = 1659604,
            score = 7,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "Ride the balloon and hear the story.  The ride will drop you off on top of a building.  Go down to the first floor, exit and go north up the stairs to Elder Shaopai, turn in the quest.",
            date = "2012-04-27T21:56:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29791#comments:id=1659604",
        },
        {
            id = 1834406,
            score = 7,
            author = "68528",
            text = "I suggest doing this quest with greater than minimum graphics.  I didn't get to see the turtle (sad panda).",
            date = "2013-03-25T20:00:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29791#comments:id=1834406",
        },
        {
            id = 1818293,
            score = 6,
            author = "338621",
            text = "Scumbag Aysa Cloudsinger.\n\n\"Hop aboard hero, you will be the first pandaren to speak to Shen-zin Su in hundreds of years.\"\n\nProceeds to speak with Shen-zin Su by herself.",
            date = "2013-02-26T01:54:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29791#comments:id=1818293",
        },
        {
            id = 1946826,
            score = 5,
            author = "elfiemyrtle",
            text = "From Shang Xi's grave, go up to the umbrella tree (the one with white foliage). Make your way down towards the balloon and speak to Aysa. It is important to get her to come on the flight with you, or else (which has sadly just happened to me) the whole dialogue will not kick in. All you'll get is a silent flight around the turtle's head. The quest can be completed though, just go to the temple after the drop off.",
            date = "2014-02-26T06:41:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29791#comments:id=1946826",
        },
    },
    [29792] = {
        {
            id = 1718684,
            score = 11,
            author = "Spyre",
            text = "Don't take the Uplifting Draft up this time. You don't want to go up there. If you did, and got stuck (like me), you can cross the bridge to the west and jump back down the north side of the cliff there without dying.",
            date = "2012-09-25T12:08:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29792#comments:id=1718684",
        },
        {
            id = 1659606,
            score = 1,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "Head south down the stairs, keep going to you reach the first door.  You will have 3 companions by this time.  Open the door, head for the next door (just follow your 3 NPC companions), each will try and open the door, which finally opens because someone figured out they had a key.  Then progress up the hill to the quest giver for your next quest.",
            date = "2012-04-27T22:00:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29792#comments:id=1659606",
        },
        {
            id = 1782063,
            score = 1,
            author = "1026168",
            text = "Pei-Wu Forest: Pei-Yu!",
            date = "2012-12-15T20:34:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29792#comments:id=1782063",
        },
        {
            id = 1908859,
            score = 1,
            author = "Sketchie",
            text = "What is amusing is that you can actually Blink through the gate leading to Pei-Wu forest if you're a Mage.\n\nI believe you still have to stick around for the NPCs to actually open the gate to get credit, though.",
            date = "2013-10-15T12:58:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29792#comments:id=1908859",
        },
    },
    [29793] = {
        {
            id = 1663898,
            score = 1,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "The Darkened Horrors are around the area of the quest giver.  Make sure and pick up the quest \"Handle with Care\" and do this quest at the same time as the you do this one.\n\nAn easy way to kill the Darkened Horrors is to run down the dirt path to the base of the hill, Darkened Horrors will run in from there.  Hit them with a ranged attack and kite them back to the Horde camp and they will help finish off the beasties.  Others will appear to the east, you can also kite them back to the camp for easy dispatch.",
            date = "2012-05-07T13:33:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29793#comments:id=1663898",
        },
        {
            id = 1694428,
            score = 1,
            author = "455621",
            text = "If you can't find this quest, questgiver is in wrong phase. Leave the area of the camp and return.",
            date = "2012-07-31T10:15:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29793#comments:id=1694428",
        },
        {
            id = 1718968,
            score = -5,
            author = "940955",
            text = "The Darkened Horrors/Terrors are reskinned Worgen. Their movement, idle animations, sound bites, attacks and skeletal frame are all identical.\n\nDisappointing part of an otherwise superb island.",
            date = "2012-09-25T16:22:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29793#comments:id=1718968",
        },
    },
    [29794] = {
        {
            id = 1719994,
            score = 102,
            author = "994442",
            text = "The injured sailors are laying on the ground, they sparkle, can't miss them. The area is littered with them.\n\nOnce you have clicked on one, you will throw them over your shoulder (if you are a female pandaren) or throw them between your arm and your chest (if you are a male pandaren). You then have to run back to the alliance camp with your one injured sailor.\n\nUsing https://www.wowhead.com/spell=109132 to return back to the camp faster is perfectly fine and will not cause you to drop the soldier.\n\nYou cannot carry more than one injured sailor at a time so you must run back to the camp 3 times with an injured sailor to complete this quest.\n\nEdited to include information posted by defektunge about gender difference of animations.",
            date = "2012-09-26T10:27:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29794#comments:id=1719994",
        },
        {
            id = 1721837,
            score = 41,
            author = "307035",
            text = "After rightclicking injured sailor LOOK CLOSELY - you are carrying one on your back. It's hard to see this has happened (especially with wide player models such as pandarens), because there is no animation, just sailor dissapears from the ground. You have to run back to quest giver with sailor on your back.",
            date = "2012-09-27T15:44:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29794#comments:id=1721837",
        },
        {
            id = 1663921,
            score = 5,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "You should also be doing:\n\nMedical Supplies\nFrom Bad to Worse\n\nWhile you are also doing this quest.\n\nThe injured sailors are in the boat to west of the quest giver.  Go inside, approach a sailor laying on the ground, click on him and he will jump onto your back.  Run back and drop him off next to the quest giver.",
            date = "2012-05-07T13:59:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29794#comments:id=1663921",
        },
        {
            id = 1780937,
            score = 4,
            author = "Fatboy334881",
            text = "While you have a sailor on your back, open up the character pane for a good laugh.",
            date = "2012-12-13T20:22:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29794#comments:id=1780937",
        },
        {
            id = 1779499,
            score = 2,
            author = "Twizm",
            text = "Using Roll (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=109132) while rescuing an injured sailor (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=55999)?\n\nIt's called \"safe\" recovery!",
            date = "2012-12-11T08:06:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29794#comments:id=1779499",
        },
    },
    [29795] = {
        {
            id = 2011504,
            score = 3,
            author = "977166",
            text = "The stalks glow at their base where they connect to the ground rather than along their entire length, so its possible to miss them if you are looking afar.  They stand twice as tall as the average Pandarian.  If one is lucky, you may also find them lying on the ground as well.",
            date = "2014-10-10T20:32:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29795#comments:id=2011504",
        },
        {
            id = 1663885,
            score = 1,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "Very simple gathering quest.  Ideally do this quest while at the same time doing the quest \"Preying on the Predators\" which involves killing the Tigers which surround the quest area.",
            date = "2012-05-07T13:14:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29795#comments:id=1663885",
        },
    },
    [29796] = {
        {
            id = 1663908,
            score = 2,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "Pick up all three of the next quests as they all are in the same area.\nNone Left Behind\nMedical Supplies\nFrom Bad to Worse",
            date = "2012-05-07T13:38:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29796#comments:id=1663908",
        },
        {
            id = 1728852,
            score = 1,
            author = "druunah",
            text = "Go southeast toward the Wreck of the Skyseeker. Continue southeast along the path until you come to the Alliance camp and Delora Lionheart near the wreck (also fairly near the waters edge at the coastline. (42.2 86.6)\n\nThere are several mobs of \"Darkened Terrors\" along the way.",
            date = "2012-10-02T14:22:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29796#comments:id=1728852",
        },
        {
            id = 1871369,
            score = 1,
            author = "Coolmama",
            text = "If you go directly to the southwest, you will more than likely encounter more Darkened Terrors and Darkened Horrors than you'd like to. Since most of them are in groups of 2 or 3 these are fights you may want to avoid.\n\nThe easiest way to get to Lora Lionheart is to do the following:\n\n1. Jump at the first Darkened Terror or Darkened Horror you find and get yourself killed :P\n\n2. Since you are only level 10 or below, you can rezz without penalty and/or damage, so do just that.\n\n3. Then follow the path back towards the questgiver untill you come to the bridge.\n\n4. Jump in the water on the left side of the bridge and swim towards the end of the stream\n\n5. Get out of the water, talk to Lora Lionheart and turn in the quest\n\nI did this on 2 chars, and both times I only bumped into 1 Darkened Terror and 1 Darkened Horror.",
            date = "2013-06-27T19:28:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29796#comments:id=1871369",
        },
        {
            id = 1663906,
            score = 0,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "Head southwest away from the quest giver, around the base of the mountain and you will encounter a stone path that will lead you to another camp with a blue banner.   You will find Lora Lionheart there - turn in the quest and she will have a new task for you.",
            date = "2012-05-07T13:37:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29796#comments:id=1663906",
        },
    },
    [29797] = {
        {
            id = 1663920,
            score = 1,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "Also pick up the following quests before you start this one;\n\nNone Left Behind\nFrom Bad to Worse\n\nTo the west you will find the abandoned ship.  Kill the Deep Sea Tormentors (Lizardmen) and gain access to the ship where you will find injured Sailors to heal and crates with a first aid symbol on them to collect for Medical Supplies.",
            date = "2012-05-07T13:56:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29797#comments:id=1663920",
        },
        {
            id = 5548813,
            score = 1,
            author = "soneil",
            text = "If you find it hard to get supply packs because there are too many other people doing a quest then look for a cave entrance in the middle of the quest area. There are plenty down there and I have never seen other players down there.",
            date = "2023-02-12T08:00:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29797#comments:id=5548813",
        },
    },
    [29798] = {
        {
            id = 1794917,
            score = 4,
            author = "xxkelandixx",
            text = "For a single, not in group: It's easiest for melee to stand underneath him while attacking, so that his aoe won't hit you. You'll still get flung, but pandaren are \"bouncy\" so you won't take a lot of damage just from that.\n\nWhen the first set of adds spawn, you can run away from the ship's area to leave combat and eat/drink if you've been taking a lot of damage or need more mana. Make sure that you don't leave combat after the second set of adds spawns though because it won't give you enough time to heal and make it back before he is killed. Therefore, you won't receive credit for the kill and will have to start the fight over.",
            date = "2013-01-08T16:58:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29798#comments:id=1794917",
        },
        {
            id = 1845076,
            score = 1,
            author = "oaninor",
            text = "I'm going for the Ironman challenge with all classes and sadly I don't know how lame are shammies without specialization. specially because the mana run out with just 4 lightning bolts, 2 shocks and one primal strike. all of this barely enough to kill a lvl 9 tiger and my shammie is lvl 14. if you need heal yourself you must choose.\n\nI do this quest before with few pandaren and was hard so, I was afraid of die but reading the other comment I realize that is not necessary to kill the adds.\n\nso, I enter into the fight, I was worried for Aysa but I see that she couldn't die so forget her and care yourself. just stay behind Vordraka.\n\nI use one flame shock for the DOT and one Earth Shock for the debuff, just in case he turns and hit me or Aysa stop healing herself. when the first pack of mobs appear I run but I couldn't eat or drink so I return and stay hitting in the back just single melee hits (white dmg) and occasionally one shock.\n\nthe second pack was tough. I stay hitting just melee, saving the mana for healing surge. stun one of them with the racial and could kill them. I must use healing surge just one time bu I think was the lvl difference which plays in my favor (lvl 9 mobs vs lvl14 me)\n\nthe fight extend for 10 minutes so I can say, only 2 pack of mobs attack and Aysa can't die.\n\nso if you are doing the Ironman or just are too low lvl. you can run from the fight for the first pack of mobs, try to handle the second and the rest is just wait to low the hp of Vordraka between you and Aysa, just remember stay behind him. a fight of resistance.  :)",
            date = "2013-04-19T23:34:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29798#comments:id=1845076",
        },
        {
            id = 1851126,
            score = 1,
            author = "65960",
            text = "For a priest, the best strategy seems to be: just keep your bitty DoT up on Vordraka and stay behind him, then take care of the adds by burning them down. Keep yourself healed, and let Aysa take care of herself, she does fine on her own. First couple of times I did this, I ran out of mana too quickly to be of any real help. This way, I barely got below half. This fight is long, but worry about yourself first, and the Bad Guy will go down soon enough.",
            date = "2013-05-08T08:03:53-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29798#comments:id=1851126",
        },
    },
    [29799] = {
        {
            id = 2587884,
            score = 44,
            author = "Aletto",
            text = "This quest is a bit of a nightmare to solo since the BFA prepatch. If you're lucky enough to have other people around, it's not too bad, but on your own it's a real bear. The saurok mobs hit hard and they love to gang up on you and the NPC healers you rescue. One of the types of Saurok has a sort of channeled claw attack that absolutely shreds the healers. And if you die, there's a good chance all your progress toward healing the wound will reset.\n\nBut there's a way to complete this quest and keep your sanity - if you can heal. Near Ji Firepaw, on the cliffside, there's usually a couple of Alliance priests. One is trapped under some debris and the other is usually fighting a saurok. Save them both, then run over to where Ji and Jojo are standing. Set up shop here.  The two healers will run over to the wound and begin healing. Saurok will start leaping onto them and start hurting them pretty bad. Stay near Ji and heal the priests, which will also pull the mobs away and over to where you are. You could also use taunts or ranged attacks to get their attention too.\n\nJi and Jojo will help you dispatch the saurok. Some nearby alliance soldiers might run over to help you too. Keep the priests healed up, keep pulling the saurok over to the Pandaren, and you'll eventually get there. I don't recommend running off to find more healers to speed things up - the first two priests will probably die quickly without heals or someone to pull the saurok off of them.\n\nAlso keep an eye out for the healing orbs that Ji spawns around himself. You can run through those to keep your own health up, and save your juice for the priest NPCs. You might lose one despite your best efforts, so if that happens, try and wait for a lull in the battle and then go back to the cliff from before. Hopefully by then the priest trapped under the debris has respawned and you can quickly free him and get back to your spot next to Ji.\n\nFor non-healers, I imagine you can still pull the saurok over to Ji and Jojo, but you'll probably have to replace them more frequently.\n\nHope this helps!",
            date = "2018-08-04T21:45:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29799#comments:id=2587884",
        },
        {
            id = 1669933,
            score = 28,
            author = "Stryker666",
            text = "I'm not sure if this is any easier in a group/busy area but this is from me doing this quest alone.\n\nI would recommend you rescue 2/3 healers and then defend them.\n\nIt may say **/12 healers but that doesn't mean you have to make sure 12 healers are doing their jobs at the same time.",
            date = "2012-05-23T12:27:12-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29799#comments:id=1669933",
        },
        {
            id = 1790729,
            score = 17,
            author = "CallMeNoa",
            text = "Did you know! Druids heal by taking the life from soemwhere else. They can't just make new life pop up.\n\nMalfurion healed the red dragon Korialstrasz in the WotA books, and it ended up making all the grass for yards around black and dead.\n\nThe Horde druids healing Shen-zin Su here are sapping life from somewhere else on the island to help him.",
            date = "2013-01-01T14:43:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29799#comments:id=1790729",
        },
        {
            id = 1987874,
            score = 15,
            author = "shanefuqua",
