    [29858] = {
        {
            id = 1655747,
            score = 5,
            author = "blupache",
            text = "Bugged on beta.\n\nIf more than one person goes in at a time, the quest becomes undoable. Most servers have got around this by forming a line & waiting (semi) patiently for the people in front to do it.\n\nSome people try to queue jump due to ignorance or selfishness, but that's just as likely to get the line-jumper deliberately locked out by others jumping in after them to spite them until they give up & log off or join the line. I'd recommend waiting till the line is short instead of trying to queue jump & ending up in a grief-fest, you can do quests in some of the other hubs around the zone.\n\n---\n\nWhen you go into the phased area you get an action bar with a left & right arrow, and a 1-100 energy bar that fades towards 0 (if it's at 1-50ish) or 100 (if it's at 50ish-100).\n\nYou need to press the buttons to try & keep the energy bar around 50.\n\nOccasionally you'll get bonked on the head by the sage. This'll randomly move your energy bar 15-25 points one way or the other. Hence the best thing to do is always try to stay as close to 50 as possible.\n\nAfter about minute of this you'll pass his test, can hand in & the next person in line can do the quest.",
            date = "2012-04-18T12:06:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29858#comments:id=1655747",
        },
        {
            id = 1657039,
            score = -6,
            author = "Chaosrock",
            text = "You don't need to wait in line. Just keep trying it over and over. Finally it worked for me. I think the line is just another troll thing like the '/c interact' BS.",
            date = "2012-04-21T22:23:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29858#comments:id=1657039",
        },
    },
    [29865] = {
        {
            id = 1788607,
            score = 7,
            author = "1057174",
            text = "For any of you who arn't as edumacated as others, the \"Silkwood Road\" is a play on the Asian trade route known as \"The Silk Road\" which connected China and the Roman Empire during that era",
            date = "2012-12-28T12:26:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29865#comments:id=1788607",
        },
        {
            id = 1718587,
            score = 5,
            author = "Kemaria",
            text = "These spiders cast a spell called Ravenous Spiderlings, which gives you a Ravenous Spiderlings debuff that reads: \"Spiders are eating your face, inflicting periodic Physical damage.\"   This lasts for several seconds, to the intense horror of all arachnophobes doing this quest. :)",
            date = "2012-09-25T10:23:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29865#comments:id=1718587",
        },
        {
            id = 5392933,
            score = 1,
            author = "HushGlowie",
            text = "This quest is only obtainable after completing the first four chapters in the Jade Forest main quest line and a couple more breadcrumb quests.\n\nThe Jade Forest quest line is actually the first one you obtain upon entering Pandaria, so this begins in Stormwind with The King's Command (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29547/the-kings-command) which can either be picked up on a character in Pandaria Timewalking (you must be level 1-49 and talk to Chromie (https://www.wowhead.com/npc=167032/chromie) to start this) or you can pick up Hero's Call: Jade Forest! (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=49556/heros-call-jade-forest) from the Hero's Call Board (https://www.wowhead.com/object=206294/heros-call-board) on any character level 50 or higher. If it doesn't show up right away try picking up some other quests from the call board until the one you want appears. You can just discard the extra quests and pick them back up anytime. Once you have that quest you can just simply follow the quest chain up to this one.\n\nYou will need to complete these four chapters:\n\nPaw'don Village\nThe Waterspeaking Ceremony\nThe White Pawn\nPearlfin Village",
            date = "2022-07-07T09:53:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29865#comments:id=5392933",
        },
        {
            id = 1843560,
            score = 0,
            author = "1092085",
            text = "the start of quest lines can go way back in Pandaria.\nthis one starts close to Pearlfin Village with Loremaster Cho.\nAfter you follow all his quest there, and deal with the VIP,\nElder Lusshan will tell you to meet Cho in Dawn's Blossom.\nCho will introduce you to Toya.\nFollow Toya's quest to get this one.\nWhile the cubs surround you, click on them. Even with no\ndialog bubble they each have a different remark. tooo cute.",
            date = "2013-04-15T17:35:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29865#comments:id=1843560",
        },
        {
            id = 2554784,
            score = -3,
            author = "Oldmanpants",
            text = "As for the horde,  here's the entire progression starting in Orgrimmar and taking you through honeydew village and grookin hill to dawn's blossom.  Since ya know, horde can't do pearlfin.\nhttps://wow.gamepedia.com/Quest:The_Art_of_War",
            date = "2018-02-24T15:56:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29865#comments:id=2554784",
        },
    },
