        {
            id = 1728292,
            score = 95,
            author = "owhnoes",
            text = "Summon her BEFORE you zone into the quest zone or else you'll have to rezone to get the credit.",
            date = "2012-10-02T05:04:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29950#comments:id=1728292",
        },
        {
            id = 5903664,
            score = 93,
            author = "Ratpoberson",
            text = "I ran into a weird bug on turn-in.  Li li was still with me, so she didn't show up as the turn in point. The mini map was showing the turn in where I expected it to be, but Li-Li didn't have a quest turn in -- she was still following me around.\n\nTurns out the turn-in point on my mini-map was very high in the air above the quest starting point.  Once I flew up to that point, and flew through the floating \"?\" , it disappeared and all of a sudden Li Li was on the ground at the turn-in point with the quest turn--in icon over her head, and I was able to turn-in the quest normally after that.  It took me quite a while to figure out how to get around this, and I hadn't seen it mentioned anywhere so I wanted to share here in case someone else runs into the same issue.\n\n(I was using Skyriding in the Panderia Remix.  This was within a few minutes of the TWW pre-patch launching. I will be reporting this as a bug with Bizz. )",
            date = "2024-07-24T15:28:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29950#comments:id=5903664",
        },
    },
    [29951] = {
        {
            id = 1714575,
            score = 668,
            author = "Martika",
            text = "I took this quest, tried it a few times and then avoided it like the plague until I came back to it at level 88. The description is terrible and misleading. I thought you had to get enough muddy water into the flask so that if you carried it all the way back to MudMug there would still be some left once you got there. In fact you simply have to move from pool to pool until it is full, at which point it stoppers itself. Then you just turn it in. Once I knew this, it took me 10 seconds to complete.",
            date = "2012-09-16T11:40:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29951#comments:id=1714575",
        },
        {
            id = 1721631,
            score = 244,
            author = "XxiolaA",
            text = "whoever designed this quest should be fired",
            date = "2012-09-27T09:38:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29951#comments:id=1721631",
        },
        {
            id = 1727918,
            score = 109,
            author = "BubbRubb23",
            text = "This quest is horribly explained.  I thought you collected water from a pool, and then had to find the shortest route back to Mudmug.  Yeah, no.  You collect water from multiple pools until it is full, and then you're done, the pools are green in color.  Most of them have 3 or 4 pools to collect from, and then you can easily walk to the next pool and collect another 3-4.  Seriously blizz?  Come on man!",
            date = "2012-10-01T21:02:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29951#comments:id=1727918",
        },
        {
            id = 1728086,
            score = 80,
            author = "829438",
            text = "Bring Li-Li.\n\n\"Are you sure you don't want to keep wading in this gross water?\"\n\"Maybe we can find some more wierd, splashy bottles to fill with mud.\"\n\"My favorite part was when you splashed muddy water in my eyes.\"\n\"I'm being sarcastic, by the way.\"",
            date = "2012-10-02T00:13:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29951#comments:id=1728086",
        },
        {
            id = 1845916,
            score = 72,
            author = "521162",
            text = "Mudmug: Use this leaky vial to get me muddy water!\nMe: Um, ok... By the way, I've got almost 600 alchemy, and I always carry around a couple dozen crystal vials. Any chance I could use one of them instead? I'll even let you keep it!\nMudmug: No, follow the rules. I make everybody use the same vial. It wouldn't be fair.\nMe: You caught the part where it's crystal, right? Everything on this continent seems to be made from yak parts, so you could probably sell this and get five cracked vials! Whattaya say?\nMudmug (/facepalming): Ok, fine. You can use your fancy \"Crystal\" vial... ooooorrr you can can use mine, and i'll throw in a (almost) brand new pair of boots.\nMe: ...are they good boots?\nMudmug: They're quest greens.\nMe: ... just give me your damn vial.",
            date = "2013-04-22T13:46:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29951#comments:id=1845916",
        },
    },
    [29952] = {
        {
            id = 1721471,
            score = 17,
            author = "Sooba",
            text = "I love these kind of quests, where you play someone else in a memory. They're awesome, good job blizzard!",
            date = "2012-09-27T07:41:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29952#comments:id=1721471",
        },
        {
            id = 1772335,
            score = 17,
            author = "spoonman184",
            text = ">I do not want to talk about it.\n>recounts every minute detail about his fights and talks there",
            date = "2012-11-30T15:32:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29952#comments:id=1772335",
        },
        {
            id = 1688036,
            score = 15,
            author = "yjesus",
            text = "Seems to be broken, can't open the door after killing the first mob.",
            date = "2012-07-14T11:47:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29952#comments:id=1688036",
        },
        {
            id = 1760354,
            score = 13,
            author = "Sketchie",
            text = "Chen Stormstout may only have two moves: Stormstout Fu and Drink, but that's pretty much all he needs to defeat the two mobs (Unruly Alemental and Wuk-Wuk).\n\nDrink is pretty much self explanatory, Chen will sit down and drink to restore his health. I believe it restores all of his health if you sit and drink the entire 9-10 seconds, but even then it should only take a couple since Chen doesn't take much damage, providing you spam Stormstout Fu.\n\nStormstout Fu is quite a fun move as it actually picks out from a random pool of Monk-esque moves. The moves are as followings:\n- Tiger Palm. This actually does not trigger the Tiger Strikes buff, however.\n- Blackout Kick. Instead of restoring your health, you will kick back the enemy a short distance.\n- Expel Harm. You restore about 10k health while inflicting the same amount on the enemy.\n- Fists of Fury. The \"buff\" while channeling Fists of Fury is called Hundred Paw-Strikes, and it has an additional benefit of allowing you to use Stormstout Fu while it is being channeled. (Thanks Reignac!)\n\nAgainst the Unruly Alemental and Wuk-Wuk, just spam Stormstout Fu. After the fight, Drink if needed, although even after defeating both of them Chen had about 85% health left. I guess it's there just in case.\n\nEDIT: The \"Beer Elemental\" I had written down is actually \"Unruly Alemental\". Sorry for the mistake.",
            date = "2012-11-10T13:40:13-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29952#comments:id=1760354",
        },
        {
            id = 5905995,
            score = 10,
            author = "zergfest90",
            text = "Broken as of the War Within PrePatch. I'm attempting it on a level 37 Warlock and have found Chen does negligible damage to the first mob, and I repeatedly die.\nIn addition, upon leaving the dream, the mob follows me out, and I have to try to kill the mob in the real world for no XP. Once I had to fight TWO of the first mob in the real world. The quest giver area is littered with other ppl dying as well. Def. broken.",
            date = "2024-07-26T22:25:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=29952#comments:id=5905995",
        },
    },
