        {
            id = 2326729,
            score = 1,
            author = "1031604",
            text = "Several people have asked: \"How to reach \"THE JADE SERPENT\" quest?\"\n\nTo reach \"THE JADE SERPENT\" quest, you got yo do approximatively 42 quests. Unfortunately yes! I explain:\n\nIt start with these two:\nOptional breadcrumb: Alliance: In Search of Wisdom / Horde: Dawn's Blossom\nAnd: Welcome to Dawn's Blossom\n\nThen, when you done \"Welcome to Dawn's Blossom\", there is 14 quests before \"THE JADE SERPENT\" (and 3 more if I calculate the optional quests)\n\nBut, you may ask: \"Mystterious, how to reach \"In Search of Wisdom\" quest?\"\n\nWell,\n\nElder Lusshan  give you that quest.\n\n2 quests lead up to this guy:\n\nQ1- Carp Diem\nand\nQ2- Let them burn\n\n\"Let them burn\" gives you a little orange fish pet in a bubble, named \"Fishy\".\n\nNow, to illustrate, let's reach the quest \"Let them burn\", with the pet \"Fishy\":\n\nI have the pet \"Fishy\" in my pets Journal. I did the quest \"Let them burn\" few weeks after MoP was realized. To reach that quest, I started at the very beginning, with the 3 or 4 quests that lead to Jade Forest. They are on a flying boat for Alliance, near Paw'Down Village. In one of these quests, they asks you to use a parachute to go down on the ground of Jade Forest, do you remember? Once there, after 20-25 quests, I went to \"Let them burn\" where I had my Fishy.\n\nSo, total of quests before \"THE JADE SERPENT\"? 39 to 45, +3 the optional quests I mentioned, if they are necessary.\n\nIt's very long even for a level 100.\n\nConclusion: If you want the reward item from the quest \"THE JADE SERPENT\", ask yourself: Does it REALLY worth a try?\n\nE  _ n _ d!",
            date = "2016-04-28T00:22:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30005#comments:id=2326729",
        },
    },
    [30006] = {
        {
            id = 1737136,
            score = 4,
            author = "sorceressdee",
            text = "The mobs are in a courtyard gathering around some adepts/guardians. You can pull them off the adepts and get credit for killing them even if they aren't at full health. If you're also on the Hidden Power (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30066) quest, those guardians or adepts are the ones you need to deliver the Mantras to.\n\nWhile running down the stairs they do not aggro, but if they reach their spot and don't find anybody to fight, they'll aggro you (assuming you're in range).",
            date = "2012-10-10T02:54:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30006#comments:id=1737136",
        },
        {
            id = 1761438,
            score = 4,
            author = "grimnosh",
            text = "This is a daily quest for the August Celestial faction so you must first get to Revered with the Golden Lotus to unlock it. This is one of 4 diffrent places that the August Celestials have thier dailies, you can either visit all 4 sites (Temples to the Jade Serpent or White Tiger, Cradle of Chi-Ji, and Niuzao Temple) if you have time to waste or you can go to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=64001 (Horde) or https://www.wowhead.com/npc=64032 (Alliance) in the Vale of Eternal Blossoms (Shine of Two Moons and Seven Stars respectively) to see exactly where the daily hub will be at.",
            date = "2012-11-12T13:04:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30006#comments:id=1761438",
        },
        {
            id = 5866616,
            score = 4,
            author = "zenithstorm",
            text = "If you can't see the mobs, try flying out of the area (maybe above the Jade Temple instance) and then flying back in.\n\nI couldn't see any of these sha invaders at first. I flew all around the area looking for them, but saw nothing. It was bright and sunny, and there were lots of calm Pandaren NPCs sitting around. I then flew into the outdoor version of the Jade Temple, saw nothing, came back, and then the scene became darker, and there were a ton of sha creatures right in front of the temple.",
            date = "2024-05-26T12:13:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30006#comments:id=5866616",
        },
        {
            id = 1739142,
            score = 2,
            author = "717646",
            text = "How do you even get this daily? I've helped out a few Adepts and Defenders, but they aren't giving me a quest.",
            date = "2012-10-12T03:19:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30006#comments:id=1739142",
        },
        {
            id = 1787728,
            score = 1,
            author = "Pandecio",
            text = "As far as I've seen, the best place to complete most of the quests in the Jade Temple Grounds is where you can find the sutras for the Saving the Sutras (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30064) quest.\n\nYou can find the Sutras easily in the rocks surrounding the clearing; plus it seems to have an abundance of arrows for Arrows of Fortune (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30065). The three Guardians there can be used for both the Hidden Power (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30066) quest and as tanks/support for The Darkness Around Us (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30006) and Behind the Masks (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30063) quests, specially if they are empowered by the scrolls.\n\nPretty much all daily quests for this particular place can be completed in 4-5 minutes at good pace.",
            date = "2012-12-26T14:30:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30006#comments:id=1787728",
        },
    },
    [30011] = {
        {
            id = 1724271,
            score = 5,
            author = "456634",
            text = "Have tried twice now to complete this quest. No NPC shows up in or near the courtyard once the dungeon is cleared. Not sure if the quest is bugged or if I have to get to the NPC Before clearing the instance... Will update as I make the attempt.\n\nEdit: FINALLY figured it out! To complete this quest, speak to Elder Sage Wind-Yi (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=57242) who stands just to the left of the steps to the entrance to The Temple of The Jade Serpent instance (OUTside in the temple grounds - BEFORE entering the instance!) She offers you an option to enter the temple. This phases you into a phased version of the temple which is NOT a Dungeon run, but the Temple at peace, with NPC's to talk to, including Elder Sage Rain-Zhu (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=56782) who is the quest turn in npc. She's straight ahead of you on top of the steps to the left. Once turned in, don't forget to pick up The Jade Serpent (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30000) quest from Fei  (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=56784) on the right side of the same platform!",
            date = "2012-09-29T08:57:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30011#comments:id=1724271",
        },
        {
            id = 2328592,
