    [30073] = {
        {
            id = 1660264,
            score = 86,
            author = "Billredskin",
            text = "Chen Stormstout says: Very well, . I will need your help making this beer.\nChen Stormstout says: When I yell out the names of ingredients, you throw them in the pot...\nChen Stormstout yells: I am kidding!\nChen Stormstout says: I'm the best brewer that ever lived. I think I can handle this part.\nMudmug yells: Damn straight you can!\nChen Stormstout says: If you wouldn't mind waiting, ... this might take a long time.\nOne fade to black later...\nLi Li says: That DID take a long time!\n\nThe second line is a reference to this quest (quest=12644)",
            date = "2012-04-29T09:17:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30073#comments:id=1660264",
        },
        {
            id = 1725273,
            score = 52,
            author = "923430",
            text = "The location on the map is wrong.  This quest starts and ends in halfhill",
            date = "2012-09-29T23:13:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30073#comments:id=1725273",
        },
        {
            id = 1751729,
            score = 52,
            author = "andreicmello",
            text = "You have to stand near Chen after accepting this quest in order to complete it. So if you're mounted and end up riding away right as you accept it, it will bug out. Just abandon it and take the quest again to fix the problem.",
            date = "2012-10-27T11:22:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30073#comments:id=1751729",
        },
        {
            id = 1747501,
            score = 29,
            author = "Eillesthis",
            text = "https://www.wowhead.com/npc=56138 says: That DID take a long time!\n\nToo funny!",
            date = "2012-10-21T22:32:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30073#comments:id=1747501",
        },
        {
            id = 5772315,
            score = 28,
            author = "jayciejuice",
            text = "Current as of Jan 26 2024 (Dragonflight season 3)\n\nIf you have The Emperor as a quest but you didn't stay at 55, 49 (By the mailbox in halfhill outside the inn) then just go back to 55, 49 and drop the quest. Pick it back up and then stand there and wait, unmounted.\nThis is a really weird quest that doesn't leave an indication that you need to stay and wait for it to complete and it also bugs out if you leave and come back resulting in it needing to be dropped and picked back up.\nGood Luck!",
            date = "2024-01-26T10:00:07-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30073#comments:id=5772315",
        },
    },
    [30074] = {
        {
            id = 1768427,
            score = 15,
            author = "Sketchie",
            text = "Once you accept Knocking on the Door, a scene will occur.\n\nChen Stormstout says: Let's load these barrels up into the chart, shall we?\n\nHe hops off a pile of barrels and then starts throwing all of them into a cart with amazing speed and accuracy, stacking up perfectly. Li Li then hops on the pile while Chen hops into front of the cart, ready to pull it.\n\nChen Stormstout says: Onward to Stormstout Brewery!\nLi Li yells: So long, Halfhill!\nChen Stormstout says: Mudmug, are you coming?\n\nMudmug blushes.\n\nMudmug says: Oh, I dunno. This kinda seems like a family thing you're doin'...\n\nChen Stormstout then hops in front of Mudmug.\n\nChen Stormstout says: It IS a family thing, Mudmug. And I want you to join us.\nMudmug says: No foolin'?\nChen Stormstout says: Of course not! We brewed beer together. That practically makes us brothers.\n\nMudmug then runs up to Chen Stormstout.\n\nMudmug says: Y-yeah! Beer brothers!\n\nChen Stormstout laughs.\n\nLi Li says: Ugh! You guys are gonna make me throw up.\nLi Li says: Seriously, though, Mudmug. Don't be dumb.\nChen Stormstout says: Come on, help me pull this cart.\n\nChen Stormstout and Mudmug then hops in front of the cart, ready to pull it. They then begin to walk towards Stormstout Brewery.\n\nLi Li yells: Is this the fastest you can go? Come on fatsos! Move those legs!\nChen Stormstout says: Very well, I will put my belly into it...\n\nThey then suddenly blast off towards Stormstout Brewery - so fast you will never be able to keep up with them on a ground mount, and you'd probably need 280% or even 310% flying to keep up with them.\n\nI do not know if they say anything if you're actually around by the time you arrive at Stormstout Brewery at the same time with them, though.",
            date = "2012-11-26T22:55:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30074#comments:id=1768427",
        },
        {
            id = 1807412,
            score = 9,
            author = "Eekwibble",
            text = "Additional dialogue once the quest is handed in:\nLi Li says: Huh! Looks like they're closed.\nChen Stormstout says: Yes, strange. This door was not here before.\nMudmug says: Y'all think they're hidin' something inside?\nChen Stormstout says: We will find out. Chen Stormstout yells: Stormstouts, open up! I have returned. And I brought beer!\nLi Li says: Umm... guys...\nChen Stormstout says: Settle down, Li Li. You know that I hate to be interrupted while I'm knocking on doors.\nAfter the dialogue Ook-Ook will arrive and throw barrels on everyone present.\n\nIf you run far enough away you can avoid the barrel-on-head cutscene with no issues and pick up the continuing (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30077) three (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30076) quests (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30075).\n\nYou then get more dialogue:\nLi Li says: I'm going ahead to see if there's anything I can do to help.\nLi Li yells: See you there, Uncle Chen!\nMudmug says: The brewery's got a second entrance, over yonder.\nMudmug says: I suppose I'll be off then. You a-comin', Chen?\nChen Stormstout says: See you on the other side, [@player-name].\nChen Stormstout yells: Li Li, Mudmug, wait up!",
            date = "2013-01-31T20:27:06-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30074#comments:id=1807412",
        },
        {
            id = 1963089,
            score = 8,
            author = "Argentverris",
            text = "Beer brothers, it brought a tear to my eye.  Damn you Blizzard with your emotional quests!",
            date = "2014-05-04T07:35:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30074#comments:id=1963089",
        },
        {
            id = 2004163,
            score = 6,
            author = "Casn",
            text = "Depending on order in which you take followup quests, second part of dialogue will be different. There are possible outcomes:\n\nIf first or second but before Chen:\nLi Li yells: See you there, Uncle Chen!\nIf second after Chen:\nLi Li yells: Hey, you dumb old uncle! You left me behind.\nIf third\nLi Li yells: Hey you old jerks! You left me behind!\n\nIf first:\nMudmug says: I reckon I'll see you over there\nIf second, after Li Li(forgot to check second after Chen) :\nMudmug says: I suppose I'll be off then. You a-comin', Chen?\nIf third:\nMudmug says: Where'd those other two go? Did they leave me behind? Don't nobody care about Mudmug?\n\nIf first:\nChen Stormstout yells: Mudmug, Li Li... follow me!\nIf second, depending on who went first\nChen Stormstout says: I'd better catch up with Mudmug\nChen Stormstout yells: Li Li, wait up!\nIf third:\nChen Stormstout yells: Li Li, Mudmug, wait up!",
            date = "2014-09-19T12:20:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30074#comments:id=2004163",
        },
        {
            id = 1763495,
            score = 3,
            author = "168688",
            text = "This one is available to me just outside of the Inn in Halfhill Market.",
            date = "2012-11-16T19:17:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30074#comments:id=1763495",
        },
    },
    [30075] = {
        {
            id = 1846427,
            score = 16,
            author = "1105894",
            text = "Here is the full quest chain\n\nChen and Li Li\nA seemingly Endless Nuisance\npoor grasp of the basics\nlow turnip turnout\ntaking a crop\nrampaging rodents\npractically perfect produce\nthe fabulous miss fanny\nmeat they'll eat\nBack to the sky\na neighbors duty\nPiercing Talons and Slavering Jaws (Lupello counts as a wolf kill as well)\nLupello\na lesson in bravery\ngreat minds think alike\nLeaders among breeders\nyellow and red make orange\nCrouching carrot hidden turnip\nThe Warren Mother\nThieves to the core\nLegacy\nLi Li's Day Off\nMuddy water\nBroken Dreams\nChen's resolution\nHop Hunting\n    Gardener Fran and the watering can\n    Weed War\n    Enough is ookin' enough\n    Stormstout's hops\nDoesn't hold water\n    The great Water hunt\n     barreling along\nLi Li and the Grain (Gotta love Anamaniacs Narf!)\n    Tast Test\n    out of sprite\n    wee little Shenanigans\n    Quest for a better barley\n    The chen taste test\nThe Emperor\nKnockin on the door\nClear the way\nThe Fanciest Water\nBarrels, Man\nCleaning House\ninto the brewery\ntrouble brewing\n\nI will edit later to add links",
            date = "2013-04-24T02:51:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30075#comments:id=1846427",
        },
        {
            id = 1731746,
            score = 6,
            author = "1040332",
            text = "just kill hozen. when attacked, they will cast barrel toss at you from ranged, and then they will move into melee.\n\nOok-Ook is basically harmless, so don't bother being afraid him or letting him slow your quests down because you're trying not to get close. he won't attack. if you attack him or if he comes near you, he will just turn you into a beer keg and continue on his merry way, and you just click the button to free yourself. also, if you you look up, Hoptallus can be seen hopping around the outer parts of the brewery.",
            date = "2012-10-04T23:34:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30075#comments:id=1731746",
        },
        {
            id = 1862145,
            score = 6,
            author = "Xabidar",
            text = "The dialog of Chen, Li Li, and Mudmug is different, depending on the order you accept these three quests:\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=30075 from Chen\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=30077 from Li Li\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=30076 from Mudmug\n\nThere is a lot of overlap when a character is picked first or third; most of the unique lines are when a character is picked second.\nAfter completing these three quests, this also affects the order of the bosses you fight in the next quest in the chain, https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30078\n\nIf you pick Chen first, Li Li second, Mudmug third:\n\nChen Stormstout says: See you on the other side, .\n/script PlaySoundFile(\"Sound/creature/ChenStormstout/VO_CHEN_EVENT_BONKERS_BREWERY_01.OGG\")\nChen Stormstout yells: Mudmug, Li Li... follow me!\n/script PlaySoundFile(\"Sound/creature/ChenStormstout/VO_CHEN_EVENT_BONKERS_BREWERY_02.OGG\")\nLi Li says: I'm going ahead to see if there's anything I can do to help.\n/script PlaySoundFile(\"Sound/creature/LiLiStormstout/VO_LI_LI_EVENT_BONKERS_BREWERY_01.OGG\")\nLi Li yells: Hey, you dumb old uncle! You left me behind!\n/script PlaySoundFile(\"Sound/creature/LiLiStormstout/VO_LI_LI_EVENT_BONKERS_BREWERY_04.OGG\")\nMudmug says: The brewery's got a second entrance, over yonder.\n/script PlaySoundFile(\"Sound/creature/Mudmug/VO_MUDMUG_EVENT_BONKERS_BREWERY_01.OGG\")\nMudmug says: Where'd those other two go? Did they leave me behind? Don't nobody care about Mudmug?\n/script PlaySoundFile(\"Sound/creature/Mudmug/VO_MUDMUG_EVENT_BONKERS_BREWERY_03.OGG\")\n\nChen first, Mudmug second, Li Li third:\n\nChen Stormstout says: See you on the other side, .\n/script PlaySoundFile(\"Sound/creature/ChenStormstout/VO_CHEN_EVENT_BONKERS_BREWERY_01.OGG\")\nChen Stormstout yells: Mudmug, Li Li... follow me!\n/script PlaySoundFile(\"Sound/creature/ChenStormstout/VO_CHEN_EVENT_BONKERS_BREWERY_02.OGG\")\nMudmug says: The brewery's got a second entrance, over yonder.\n/script Play