            text = "Anyone else find this buggy? I've had it several times where it says I'm looting and I get nothing. If I try again it says object is being used. I do the other eye and same thing happens. So far eventually got them to work but today it's harder than usual.. didn't get any yet",
            date = "2013-03-16T14:03:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30265#comments:id=1829689",
        },
    },
    [30266] = {
        {
            id = 1729029,
            score = 26,
            author = "Midgetpower",
            text = "Instead of worrying about aiming, get in the cannon, turn all the way towards the direction they are coming from and spam fire.  They will be grouped up because of the angle they are flying in at and VERY easy to hit quickly.",
            date = "2012-10-02T17:42:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30266#comments:id=1729029",
        },
        {
            id = 1743672,
            score = 17,
            author = "Lukahna",
            text = "This quest is simple, but potentially a little confusing. Head to the upper (covered) level at (7.07, 70.35) in the Vale. You'll see turrets surrounding the platform. Click to mount one.\n\nYour only targets are the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63973s that are flying fairly far in the distance, not the large packs of mobs on the ground; it almost looks like you can target the ground mobs. When you aim the turret, fire as soon as you see the globe target reticule at the end of the trajectory line. Your shot will connect. Focus on groups, as the shots do splash damage.",
            date = "2012-10-16T23:11:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30266#comments:id=1743672",
        },
        {
            id = 5864491,
            score = 13,
            author = "caroleen",
            text = "Tried cannons on South side of tower, trickier to mount.  One of them I saw swarmers but never got credit for kills, other one there were no swarmers (and yeah, tried logging out and back in.\n\nCannons on North side of tower worked fine, took about 30 seconds to complete quest.",
            date = "2024-05-24T11:51:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30266#comments:id=5864491",
        },
        {
            id = 5876953,
            score = 11,
            author = "utakata",
            text = "cannons work  near setting sun garrison\nOther side phases you out",
            date = "2024-06-08T05:55:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30266#comments:id=5876953",
        },
        {
            id = 1728233,
            score = 8,
            author = "Dreadlack",
            text = "Go to 8 , 44 in Vale of Eternal Blossoms, atop of the temple and mount a cannon.\n\nThe swarmers will be flying around in the air.",
            date = "2012-10-02T03:40:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30266#comments:id=1728233",
        },
    },
    [30267] = {
        {
            id = 1723404,
            score = 21,
            author = "entropos",
            text = "HAVING A HARD TIME WITH THE GLADE GLIMMERS?\nOpen up your keybinds and find the \"interact with target\" setting\n(It's in the Targeting section of the keybinds)\nSet a key for it.\n\nNow create this target macro:\n/tar Glade Glimmer\n\nFind a patch of glimmers, stand in the middle of it and spam your target macro then interact with key until bam you're chock full of glimmer.",
            date = "2012-09-28T18:20:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30267#comments:id=1723404",
        },
        {
            id = 1656077,
            score = 11,
            author = "Khalya",
            text = "Spindly Bloodfeathers drop from Glade Hunters or Glade Sprinters - drop rate seems to be around 25%",
            date = "2012-04-19T09:59:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30267#comments:id=1656077",
        },
        {
            id = 1660380,
            score = 11,
            author = "yoshimo",
            text = "http://mop.wowhead.com/npc=57301#screenshots ,\n\nGlade Glimmer are small yellow critters that can be collected and have a cogwheel symbol on them",
            date = "2012-04-29T12:31:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30267#comments:id=1660380",
        },
        {
            id = 1712525,
            score = 5,
            author = "750725",
            text = "There are groups of these little Glade Glimmers - they look like little fireflies or dragonflies and they are not hostile.  Right clicking them will 'capture' them.\n\nHunters beware, if your pet does an AOE attack on a Glade Hunter (crane) that is standing near a group of these, your pet will kill them and you will not be able to click on them to \"capture\" them after they fall dead to the ground.  Either kite the Glade Hunters out of the group of Glade Glimmers, or turn off the AOE attack on your pet (i.e. Thunder Stomp).",
            date = "2012-09-12T01:42:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30267#comments:id=1712525",
        },
        {
            id = 1683480,
            score = 4,
            author = "Blanckaert",
            text = "Quest is bugged, it NEEDS 18, but half the quest text says 10, you can only get 10, then your icon switches to attack them, instead of 'catch' them.  Tried putting the 10 in the Bank, and tried getting more, but that didn't work.",
            date = "2012-07-01T23:27:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30267#comments:id=1683480",
        },
    },
    [30268] = {
        {
            id = 1677523,
            score = 64,
            author = "darksoul019",
            text = "One of those quests where apparently while they able to bite you they dont have heads, they also drop fangs, which appreantly arent part of a head. Killed around about 25 of these for the 6 heads, sad really blizzard still adopts farming quests like these.",
            date = "2012-06-17T03:12:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30268#comments:id=1677523",
        },
        {
            id = 1725184,
            score = 18,
            author = "Random0584",
            text = "While it's not a mistake everyone will make, be sure you're actually in the water when you attack these things otherwise they have a terrible habit of .\n\nTook me a while to figure this out >.>",
            date = "2012-09-29T21:10:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30268#comments:id=1725184",
        },
        {
            id = 1725732,
            score = 9,
            author = "235214",
            text = "This was nicely parodied by Dark Legacy Comics in the \"Brains (http://www.darklegacycomics.com/107.html)\" episode.\n\nWowhead says the Murkscale Head (http://www.wowhead.com/item=79199) head is a 45% drop rate - was 6/15 (or 40%) when I just did it.",
            date = "2012-09-30T07:46:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30268#comments:id=1725732",
        },
        {
            id = 1838327,
            score = 7,
            author = "219877",
            text = "I hate \"body part\" quests and usually just drop them if they seem to have a low drop rate as this one does. So after getting one head in 4 or 5 kills I did just that. Then after an hour or so of questing I found, although I had done no Red Crane Temple quests, I had no more quests for Krasarang. Could it be that the only way Blizzard can get people to suffer through these really incredibly stupid quests is to make them required to complete a long quest chain? Well I'm not going to do this quest to find out. Off to another area to get to 87 and higher altitudes.\n\n I changed my mind and went ahead and did the quest. Killed 17 to get 6 heads and the follow on quests. 88,000XPs for kills and 17 leather. 35 minutes.",
            date = "2013-04-03T03:30:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30268#comments:id=1838327",
        },
        {
            id = 1865661,
            score = 6,
            author = "nahkhaz",
            text = "Oddly enough, murkscales don't have a poison attack, yet we are sent on a quest to get their venom because they have been poisoning the locals. Puzzlement.",
            date = "2013-06-12T10:12:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30268#comments:id=1865661",
        },
    },
