    [30277] = {
        {
            id = 1744120,
            score = 126,
            author = "ShaunDreclin",
            text = "To deactivate the first and second spirit walls you need to go to the left and right sides of the room and click the little pedestals that have green orbs floating above them.\n\nThe final spirit wall is opened by a pedestal directly to the left as you enter the door to the final room.",
            date = "2012-10-17T14:08:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30277#comments:id=1744120",
        },
        {
            id = 1689262,
            score = 109,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "When entering the Guo-Lai Halls, make note of the symbol at the bottom of the stairs.  Many of the rooms in here have stones with various symbols on them and stepping on those with the same symbol will prevent you from taking damage from various sources.",
            date = "2012-07-17T19:17:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30277#comments:id=1689262",
        },
        {
            id = 5857871,
            score = 37,
            author = "Kryptaria",
            text = "If you're doing this in Remix:\n\nEnter the Guo-Lai Halls (Vale of Eternal Blossoms /way 22.6 27.2 Guo-Lai Halls ).\nGo down the ramp. The green circles will speed you up. There are a lot of mobs, and some of the statues will come to life if you get near them, even in stealth, so watch out.\nWhen you enter the first big room, you'll see one floor tile that looks different from the rest. Remember that tile pattern. That tile is safe. All the others will damage/kill you.\nFrom the big room, turn left. You'll enter another room with more mobs, statues, and rubble. You can make your way around the rubble.\nGo down the hall, turn right, and go down the stairs into the next room. There will be a misty wall up the stairs to your left, and you'll see another misty wall up the stairs ahead and to the right.\nGo right (not ahead and then right) up the stairs. You'll see a Spirit Orb. Kill the mobs and click the orb. This deactivates the misty wall you saw up the stairs to the left (now across the room).\nGo across the room and up the stairs. Kill the mobs and click the second Spirit Orb. This deactivates the misty wall that was beyond this room to the right.\n[Go down the stairs, turn left, go up the stairs, and kill the mobs. Turn right and go down the ramp.\nLook at the floor tiles. If you remembered the tile from the very beginning, you should see a clear path that will eventually get you to the far stairs, which are blocked by a final misty wall.\nLook for another clear floor tile path to a final Spirit Orb. For me, it was directly to the right. Kill mobs, click orb, stay on the path, and go up the stairs.\nClick the quest item. You should also have at least one Guo-Lai Cache Key, so open any chests you can.\nStealth, hearth, or fight your way back along the same path out.\n\nAll the mobs in here do floor things, so keep careful watch. They'll drop runic circles that damage or stun, circular AOE attacks, and shockwaves that stun. Be prepared to move a lot while fighting, but don't step on bad floor tiles.",
            date = "2024-05-17T10:45:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30277#comments:id=5857871",
        },
        {
            id = 2496343,
            score = 31,
            author = "FeyGyrl",
            text = "I came here looking for information specifically referencing the dropping of the spirit wall. After not finding it in the first several posts - their focus seemed to be more on why you shouldn't bother with this quest - I just began scouring the room for anything. Eventually, I found a clickable orb in a corner niche, just inside the main doorway. I found it in the niche to the right, as you look at the spirit wall across the room, from the doorway. Once you click on this first orb, the spirit wall drops & then you can click on the orb needed for the quest.\nAs an aside, be careful approaching the crossing of the room. Look for the gold only designs. The tiles with the stylized wind, motion, & fire designs all do damage & the wind ones also throw you off that tile, usually onto another dangerous one. You can work your way across the room from door to the first orb; then orb to the spirit wall area using only the safe tiles, if you visually scout your route, first. There are spawns that \"come to life\" sometimes, too, as you near them, so just stay aware of your surroundings as you make your way across.\nSince this sometimes helps folks to know...I did this solo, as a 110 ret paladin, with no problems once I figured out how to drop the wall. Running this daily netted me a decent amount of Lotus rep, which I'm working up for the fun of it.",
            date = "2017-05-25T00:24:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30277#comments:id=2496343",
        },
        {
            id = 1750813,
            score = 25,
            author = "940955",
            text = "Fun fact: The statues chasing you take damage from falling rocks.\n\nIf you can kite one into them, don't bother dpsing it. It'll kill itself first.",
            date = "2012-10-26T10:04:12-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30277#comments:id=1750813",
        },
    },
    [30280] = {
        {
            id = 1736996,
            score = 42,
            author = "Caladynus",
            text = "I guess I will be the first one to write a comment on this quest.  You can get this quest at revered from the same quest hub you get \"The Ashweb Matriarch\".  You go into the Hall of the Serpent and you see this big serpent floating up in the air.  This mob has 4.7 million health, but it is not as hard as it seems.\n\nThere is a lower section and an upper section to this room.  When you are in the lower section he does two things.  He will spew lightning breath on a section of the room you are in.  It will cover just about one third of the room.  Simply move to a section it is not on. The other ability didn't seem to do much that I noticed.  He throws a gust of wind that did 20-30k I think.  As long as you are not low, it won't be an issue. As soon as you get a chance, move up the steps to the upper section.  Melee will have to go up here right away as he will not get low enough to the ground in the lower area for you to melee him.  He will just sit there spewing lightning, etc\n\nIt is much simpler to dps him up here.  When you are up here, he will start shooting a bolt of lightning toward the spot on the floor where you are.  You will recognize it by a big black circle under you.  Staying in the pool will cause 20k dmg initially.  I didn't wait around to see what it did after that, but the pools stay around for a little while.  He does this a random number of times in a row, although it was usually four times from what I saw, never less and then you have a period of time where you can dps him before he does it again.\n\nEventually he will hit you with a gust of wind that knocks you back down to the front section of the room.  Again try and get back to the top as quickly as possible as that is the best spot to dps him from.  If you stay down at the bottom, there is very little room to dps him in as he will cover almost the whole ground with massive lightning pools.\n\nRepeat this until he is dead.  There is just one thing to be careful about.  You can go out of line of sight past the pillar that he sits between BUT if you are in the wrong spot, the gust of wind can knock you against the pillar and then you just fall down to your death in some sort of chasm, lol.\n\nAll in all, a fun fight for a quest.",
            date = "2012-10-09T22:20:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30280#comments:id=1736996",
        },
        {
            id = 1749616,
            score = 36,
            author = "1048804",
            text = "For the hallway with the tiles: The colour of the \"safe\" tiles changes but if you look carefully you can see one type of tiles forming a path from the door where you stand - they will often be the safe ones.\n\nas for the fight with Milau: when she hits you with the gust of wind to knock you down to the lower section you can counter it by staying near the railing when she cast the gust of wind. I've managed to stay in the upper area doing that.",
            date = "2012-10-24T15:56:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30280#comments:id=1749616",
        },
        {
            id = 1737079,
            score = 23,
            author = "Ponkana",
            text = "Entrance to Guo-Lai Halls is in 22.5, 27.0 of Vale of Eternal Blossoms.\n\nOne of the requirements for https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7324 . Make sure to not get hit by Milau's lightning pools, and pretty much when you stay on her platform that you won't get hit by lightning breath.\n\nShe does a mass grip when she flies to the middle of the room, then casts a very long spell which would knock you back if ever you're in range. Just move out, wait for her to cast then speed up going back to the platform above. Mulai will do it twice.. every 1/3 of her HP.\n\nPassing through the hall of tiles can be a problem for this also, just try to remember the FIRST tile you see when you enter Guo-Lai Halls, as it is the safe tile to step on so that you don't lose the achievement.",
            date = "2012-10-10T00:53:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30280#comments:id=1737079",
        },
        {
            id = 1902793,
            score = 21,
            author = "1147177",
            text = "OK, seems since 5.4 this is now a whole lot harder.  The room both upstairs and downstairs where you find Milau is now full of other mobs.  Cleared all of them, started battle with Milau as usual and mobs all spawned again by the time I got thrown down the bottom section the first time.  Before I have done this easy enough solo in a clear room but now with all the extra mobs, unless you have a group, probably won't bother with it again.  Managed to get it done on my over 500 equipped mage but died twice trying to get out again.  The 5 Valor points aren't worth the hassle.",
            date = "2013-09-26T00:43:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30280#comments:id=1902793",
        },
        {
            id = 1923347,
            score = 13,
            author = "610726",
            text = "With the changes to Guo-Lai Halls in 5.4, this quest and https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30277 have become more trouble than they're worth. The Halls are filled with mogu that respawn very quickly and aren't AoE-friendly, and the final objective has lots of potential to be aggravating.\n\nHowever.\n\nIt appears the drop rate for https://www.wowhead.com/item=87779 has increased, and the chests are conveniently placed together in one spot, near the quest objectives. They contain JC pet patterns and new Cooking recipes, as well as the usual https://www.wowhead.com/item=90815 and https://www.wowhead.com/item=90816 (which provide a bit more rep too), and https://www.wowhead.com/item=103624.\n\nTurns out if you can handle the mobs enough to farm for keys, you can grind a lot more than 500 rep from all the kills, top it off with the relics (or mail them to alts now), and come away with a respectable amount of harmony, cloth, greens, cooking mats, and vendor trash. My scribe/jeweler also found her final Primal recipes (finally!) and a few of the new glyph recipes, and fought the rares that spawn in there at least three times. Personally I found it easier to run down to Milau's room and back up, than to take the route for the other quest, and I just ignored the quests altogether.",
            date = "2013-12-04T03:23:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30280#comments:id=1923347",
        },
    },
