 of quests each starting from NPC that gave you previous quests.\nOrdo Warbringer have quest that starts via pop-up after Channelers and backup from Taylor/Nazgrim if you abandon first.",
            date = "2012-09-26T15:51:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30594#comments:id=1720438",
        },
        {
            id = 1742059,
            score = 4,
            author = "tpie89",
            text = "FYI if someone else has been attacking the Guardians and they turn back to stone you will not be able to hit them. best to find your own guardians to kill. They come to life and then back to stone again. Easy enough to kill before they change again.",
            date = "2012-10-15T04:39:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30594#comments:id=1742059",
        },
        {
            id = 2557356,
            score = 4,
            author = "qman63",
            text = "Has this been nerfed beyond recognition or was I just lucky?  In the past some percentage of the statues come to life and attack you, often when fighting another one. You have to be on your toes.  The entire time I was in the area, and completed the quest, not one statue ever animated.",
            date = "2018-03-11T16:27:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30594#comments:id=2557356",
        },
        {
            id = 1968783,
            score = 1,
            author = "wowheadizmydaddy",
            text = "Mechanics for it are pretty cool, but they needed to make a screw-up for the player a bit more risky. Like make the dudes hit hard. Anyhow, nice change of pace for a quest.\n\nThe completion text, however, must be from the writer who did the original '10 Rats' quest 30 years ago - it's that inspiring.  >.>",
            date = "2014-05-30T18:44:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30594#comments:id=1968783",
        },
        {
            id = 2223631,
            score = 1,
            author = "Popoki",
            text = "You must do this quest before she will offer you her other quest.",
            date = "2015-08-01T15:58:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30594#comments:id=2223631",
        },
    },
    [30595] = {
        {
            id = 1939961,
            score = 6,
            author = "Mustardisbad",
            text = "His last words were \"Now that you've softened them up, I'm thinking that I might head in. Just a few more relics from around the outskirts. Nothing dangerous.\"\n\nAfter that he was never seen again.\n\nSome say that was the end of his collecting adventure and others say it was just the beginning.\n\nHe shall forever remain a page in the history books of Heroes, but only that.",
            date = "2014-02-01T21:00:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30595#comments:id=1939961",
        },
        {
            id = 1938180,
            score = 5,
            author = "Jaydeetoo",
            text = "A good quest, minimal effort (as in with some luck you will not even have to face a single mob), and the opportunity for a higher reward if you remember to pick up the Treasure of Pandaria achievement item,  Terracota Head (http://www.wowhead.com/item=86427/terracotta-head), worth 100 gold.",
            date = "2014-01-26T17:45:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30595#comments:id=1938180",
        },
        {
            id = 1792645,
            score = 4,
            author = "nabziF",
            text = "Yes Blizzard, let's glamorize the looting of archaeological sites.\n\nNow that I think about it, there are a great many such quests in the game...I guess Bao Jian's manner just struck me as particularly unscrupulous. He'd fit in well with the goblins :-)",
            date = "2013-01-04T19:06:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30595#comments:id=1792645",
        },
        {
            id = 2448516,
            score = 3,
            author = "Tigronn",
            text = "What a scam, he gives you 10 gold for 12 pieces of these, yet, the treasure, a smaller piece of the same statues, sells for 100gold",
            date = "2016-11-26T10:51:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30595#comments:id=2448516",
        },
        {
            id = 5871878,
            score = 3,
            author = "Ignignokt",
            text = "On Remix, the mogu were not spawning in the quest area for me. I flew up to the mountain ridge just north of the quest area (toward the Sha of Anger spawn location) and turned around to look back down, noticing that the area had phased; the mogu had spawned in. I hopped back down the mountain and was able to complete the quest.",
            date = "2024-06-01T21:48:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30595#comments:id=5871878",
        },
    },
    [30596] = {
    },
    [30599] = {
        {
            id = 1665916,
            score = 42,
            author = "Alskonda",
            text = "For this quest, you have to go kill three hozens, loot their bodies and make a sacrifice at each of their respective alters. The sacrifice is made by clicking on the knife, laying on the stone in front of the alter.\n\nThe Burlap Trail (Subzone), south of where you take the quest:\nTak Tak is to the east of the cave, at the other hozen village.\nKo Ko is at the entrance of the cave.\nDak Dak is inside the cave. When you enter it, you can jump down. There are two huge beast corpses down there.",
            date = "2012-05-12T10:15:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30599#comments:id=1665916",
        },
        {
            id = 1747149,
            score = 11,
            author = "Desertcobra",
            text = "Cave entrance 52.85 71.04\nKoKo alter 52.26 71.44\nTak Tak 56.78 70.97",
            date = "2012-10-21T11:34:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30599#comments:id=1747149",
        },
        {
            id = 1721569,
            score = 6,
            author = "Whiterock",
            text = "What is Your 'Luckeydo?' Quest Tree From Whiterock\n[pre][ins]+[/ins])Traffic Issues (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30616) [ins]+[/ins])Oil Stop (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30614) [ins]+[/ins])A Grummle's Luck (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30808)\n       \\          ||         /\n       a)Roadside Assistance (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30617)\n\n   [ins]+[/ins])The Burlap Trail: To Burlap Waystation (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30592)\n   /                 \\\nb)The Rabbitsfoot (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30602)    b)The Broketooth Ravage (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30603)──>c)Breaking Broketooth (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30604)\n ||            ┌───────┤\nc)A Monkey Idol (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30599)      c)No Pack Left Behind (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30600)\n   \\                 /\n   d)Bros Before Hozen (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30605)──>d)Thumping Knucklethump (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30606)\n   /                 \\\nd)The Snackrifice (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30608)    d)Hozen Love Their Keys (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30607)\n                └┬───┬┘\ne)Unleash The Yeti! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30611) e)Grummle! Grummle! Grummle! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30610)\n   \\                /\n   e)The Leader Hozen (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30612)\n   f)The Burlap Trail: To Kota Basecamp (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30692)\n\n[ins]+[/ins])Kota Blend (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30744){ver2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30825)} [ins]+[/ins])Trouble Brewing (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30745){ver2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30826)} [ins]+[/ins])Gourmet Kafa (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30743){ver2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30824)}\ng)A Fair Trade (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30746)\nh)The Burlap Grind (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30747)                         [ins]+[/ins])Shut it Down (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30742){ver2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30823)}\n[ins]D[/ins])The Burlap Grind (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30821)\n\nLegend:\nD means Daily\n+ means Can start anytime, prequests not needed.[/pre]\n\nKota camp have second version of quests, they start from the other side of the mountain.",
            date = "2012-09-27T08:57:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30599#comments:id=1721569",
        },
        {
            id = 1752708,
            score = 4,
            author = "861121",
            text = "Ok, for idiots like me who can't find the cave because they come in from the west and attack Ko Ko first, the cave is not necessarily visible (depending on where you are standing)..\n\nFirstly standing on the hillock where the quest giver is and looking directly south you can actually see the cave entrance - it is straight ahead on the ground level, not one of the many high up caves.\n\nSo if you attack Ko Ko first, go East (left facing Ko Ko) a very short distance and the cave is right there, you will find Dak Dak straight ahead inside the cave. Once you have killed him (the alter is in the bottom of the cave), come back out of the cave and travel further East out of the immediate village area and there is a small path leading upwards to Tak Tak.",
            date = "2012-10-28T16:51:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30599#comments:id=1752708",
        },
        {
            id = 1793267,
            score = 2,
            author = "nabziF",
            text = "Heh another MoP quest with giblets (when idols explode).",
            date = "2013-01-05T19:15:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30599#comments:id=1793267",
        },
    },
