    [30641] = {
        {
            id = 1689263,
            score = 50,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "When entering the Guo-Lai Halls, make note of the symbol at the bottom of the stairs.  Many of the rooms in here have stones with various symbols on them and stepping on those with the same symbol will prevent you from taking damage from various sources.",
            date = "2012-07-17T19:21:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30641#comments:id=1689263",
        },
        {
            id = 1742807,
            score = 30,
            author = "616100",
            text = "This quest is a reference to the famous orchestral piece In the Hall of the Mountain King, composed by Edvard Grieg for the sixth scene of act 2 in Henrik Ibsen's 1876 play Peer Gynt.",
            date = "2012-10-15T20:02:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30641#comments:id=1742807",
        },
        {
            id = 1704088,
            score = 24,
            author = "Karadine",
            text = "Part of a quest chain given by https://www.wowhead.com/npc=59905 at the Golden Pagoda in [zone=5840] upon reaching Revered with [faction=1269].\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=30640 > https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30641 > https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30642",
            date = "2012-08-25T03:02:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30641#comments:id=1704088",
        },
        {
            id = 1756056,
            score = 20,
            author = "edgeblade",
            text = "Make sure you talk to the NPC or else you won't get credit for \"entering\" the Hall of Tiles despite actually going in there on your own. Quest objective should be changed to say \"Talk to NPC and enter the Hall of Tiles\" or something like that.",
            date = "2012-11-03T05:21:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30641#comments:id=1756056",
        },
        {
            id = 1731993,
            score = 16,
            author = "Tharama",
            text = "Ren Firetongue is there waiting for you to assist you on this quest. He says quite a bit during the quest so thought I'd write it up, behind a spoiler as well to make sure I don't spoil people right away, enjoy!\n\n[spoiler]As you go into the now opened middle hallway of Guo-Lai Halls, Ren is there waiting for you in a room of tiles of varying colours but with many matching\n\nRen Firetongue says: Whoa! Careful over there! These tiles have violet tendencies...\nRen Firetongue says: Cloud tile is good.  Other tiles bad.  There was a tile at the bottom of the entrance stairs that tipped me off.  My sharp eyes have saved my delicate features yet again!\n\nAs he mentions, there is a lone tile as you get through the first hallway and into the big room. I assume that is the safe tile for today/this quest but I am not sure.\n\nRen Firetongue says: The mogu, they seem not so good at this game, if their dead bodies are any indication.\n\nThere are some dead mogu on \"bad\" tiles. Dumb mogu. After noticing the mogu, he follows the correct path through a much larger room of good and bad tiles. You can follow him or go ahead safely.\n\nRen Firetongue says: I see, I see.\nRen Firetongue says: Mmmm, shall we?\nRen Firetongue says: I think I would quite enjoy skipping stones down that hallway.  It would be quite the display!\n\nHe says these during the trip through the room, I can't record if it was at any specific moments, except for the final one which he says after going through a large, operable (right-clickable) door.\n\nThe room opens up to an even larger place with huge mogu statues and staircases. The mogu's swing their axes when you get close, making the ground tremble and dealing damage if you stand in it but they do not start moving about like normal monsters As you get further into this larger room, Ren remarks:\n\nRen Firetongue says: Now where's that big mogu baddy that came tramping through here a short bit ago?\n\nAt this moment, Zhao-Jin the Bloodletter appears once more and blocks you from taking the Helm that is floating a little off the floor, two large mogu statues next to it.\n\nRen Firetongue says: He's... so...\nRen Firetongue says: ...ugly!\nZhao-Jin the Bloodletter says: The Battle Helm of the Thunder King...\nZhao-Jin the Bloodletter says: It would seem my guards are useless. I will have to take care of you myself.\nZhao-Jin the Blood yells: There will be no cages this time, I will tear your limbs from your bodies!\n\nAt this point, he engages in combat using two abilities, Decapitating Strike (your usual mogu frontal cone) and Lightning Crash which marks a spot on the ground with a fire runes which is then struck by lightning. (or auto attacks if you intterupt lightning crash) both attacks are able to be dodged and the only problem is that he is A LOT of health. Do not come in as a tank like I did.\n\nHe also starts combat at 40%, wounded somewhat from a previous battle and you only need to bring him to 20% where he attempts to take the helm.\n\nZhao-Jin the Bloodletter yells: You are not as weak as I thought, but the helm is still mine....\n\nHe is stopped however as Ren freezes the Helm in a block of ice.\n\nZhao-Jin the Bloodletter yells: Aaaarrrghhh!  Mage, when we next meet I will seperate your head from your body.\n\nAt which point, he activates two Jade Guardians standing on either side of now frozen Helm and runs away like a sissy girl. The Jade Guardians share health and are killed easily enough.\n\nAfter the guardians die, the helm unfreezes and becomes lootable.\n\nRen Firetongue: Mighty fine hat!  I take it this is what you were looking for?\n\nAfter looting the helm and having completed your mission, Ren runs off and finishes with this one final line:\n\nRen Firetongue: Ta ta for now, friend!\n\nThen you just go back the way you came or hearth or portal or wish yourself to the quest giver and turn in. Thanks for reading![/spoiler]",
            date = "2012-10-05T05:57:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30641#comments:id=1731993",
        },
    },
    [30642] = {
        {
            id = 1736070,
            score = 67,
            author = "Zillions",
            text = "For this quest, you will head to south-central Vale to Mistfall Village.  On the cliffs to the east of the village is the entrance.  Once you get close to the axe, you will become cage in, and start a mini 'event' which has you killing approx 20 https://www.wowhead.com/npc=60297.\nYou are assisted by 2x healing runes and 1x DPS rune (grants the buff https://www.wowhead.com/npc=64928).  Simply kill the mobs that spawn over the course of about 5 minutes, then loot the axe.\n\nMake sure you don't leave the room when done, because you will be turning the quest in to the NPC in the same room!",
            date = "2012-10-08T21:11:12-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30642#comments:id=1736070",
        },
        {
            id = 1704089,
            score = 36,
            author = "Karadine",
            text = "Part of a quest chain given by https://www.wowhead.com/npc=59905 at the Golden Pagoda in [zone=5840] upon reaching Revered with [faction=1269].\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=30640 > https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30641 > https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30642",
            date = "2012-08-25T03:08:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30642#comments:id=1704089",
        },
        {
            id = 1737478,
            score = 31,
            author = "Ellgar3",
            text = "this quest was bugged for me - some sort of phasing issue. I couldn't get past the fence in the Silent Sanctuary.\n\nHowever, i was able to fly over the fence with mount. It's impossible to mount inside the Silent Sanctuary, you have to take advantage of late dismounting after you enter the room.\nEDIT: there's invisible wall at entrance - fly very low to avoid it, and then immediately up over the fence\n- thanks Eatrio, forgot to mention this\n\nafter that i was able to loot the axe, and trial started when i got close to the fence.\n\nQuest giver spawns inside the Silent Sanctuary after you pass this trial, so don't leave the room!\n\nhope this is going to help someone",
            date = "2012-10-10T11:37:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30642#comments:id=1737478",
        },
        {
            id = 1742907,
            score = 24,
            author = "1046450",
            text = "I found a Work-around that doesn't involve disconnecting or using lag.\n\nFind another person on the same quest and group with them.\n\nstand in front of the gate, 1 person abandons the quest, walks past the now phased out gate, and the other shares the quest. repeat for the other person.\n\nGo collect the axe, then move back towards the bars to activate the event.",
            date = "2012-10-15T22:54:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30642#comments:id=1742907",
        },
        {
            id = 1756132,
            score = 17,
            author = "Biffsterr",
            text = "If you're a mana class, you need to conserve your mana.  That is your chief concern.  The jade constructs come alive one at a time and attack you.  As time goes on, they spawn faster and faster so that you have a whole crowd of them on you seemingly at once.  There are three orbs that spawn, two healing orbs on either side of the center one which increases your damage.  When you really need healing, walk through a healing orb.  When you need a lot of damage output, walk through the damage orb.  The orbs respawn after something like 20 or 30 seconds so use them judiciously.  My main is a holy priest, I use shadow for questing, and I had very little trouble doing this quest.  The only real issue I had was keeping my mana up.\n\nThis quest really works against people with little patience.  Don't start out popping all your cooldowns or with all guns blazing.  It starts slowly and takes time to complete so if you lack patience, your frustration will be the thing that kills you.",
            date = "2012-11-03T08:29:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30642#comments:id=1756132",
        },
    },
