! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30619){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30620)    e)Trouble on the Farmstead (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30569){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30570)\n ||                        /     \\\n ||       e)Farmhand Freedom (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30571)     e)... and the Pot, Too!  (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30581)\n ||                       └─┬───┬─┘\n || e)Back to Westwind Rest (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31252)(A) e)Back to Eastwind Rest (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31253)(H)\n ├─────────────────────────┴───┴─┬───────────────────┐\n ||                               ||                   ||\nf)In Tents Channeling (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30652){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30657)        f)Barrels of Fun (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30651){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30656) f)Pandaren Prisoners (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30650){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30655)\nf)The Ordo Warbringer (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30660){A2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30662),H1 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30661),H2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30663)}  ||                   ||\n ||                           └─┬─┴─────────────────┬─┘\nMuskpaw Ranch (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31456){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31457)*              ├>The Shado-Pan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31455){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31453)* ├>The Missing Merchant (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31452){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31451)*\n                               └>Beyond the Wall (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31695)*  └>Cho's Missive (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31460){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31459)*\nLegend:\n+ means Can start anytime, prequests not needed.\n# means Other Zones\n(A)/(H) means Alliance/Horde only.\n{H} means Quest Have Horde Variant, click {H} for it.\n* means another Quest Tree.[/pre]\nAdditionall info:\n\nYes, Shado-pan questline have such weird prequests :D\nAwakened quests have 3 version of quests each starting from NPC that gave you previous quests.\nOrdo Warbringer have quest that starts via pop-up after Channelers and backup from Taylor/Nazgrim if you abandon first.",
            date = "2012-09-26T16:26:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30663#comments:id=1720497",
        },
    },
    [30665] = {
        {
            id = 1842114,
            score = 154,
            author = "OldWolf2",
            text = "To unlock this quest, you only need to complete \"Call Out Their Leader\" at Binan Village. There is no breadcrumb, but once you have done that quest you will find that this quest is now offered.",
            date = "2013-04-12T01:04:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30665#comments:id=1842114",
        },
        {
            id = 1823658,
            score = 57,
            author = "73955",
            text = "This quest is currently bugged as of 5.2 release. None of the Yaungols, near the door nor wandering in the area highlighted in blue on the map, will give credit for a kill. GM ticket opened... will update this comment in 3 days when GMs return my call.\n\nUpdate:\nGm Response: This is a known issue. The only way to complete this quest currently is to engage the packs of 3 Yaungol as they approach the gate, but before they aggro onto the the Shado-Pan defenders at the door. Not every pack will give you credit for the kills, but it only took me 21 kills to get the credit for the 15 I needed.",
            date = "2013-03-07T10:43:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30665#comments:id=1823658",
        },
        {
            id = 1749401,
            score = 36,
            author = "445261",
            text = "On this quest, don't make the mistake I did and kill the mobs at full health wandering the village.  Kill the ones right at the door to the Shado-Pan fallback, fighting the Shado-Pan Guard NPCs.  The NPCs hit like trucks and will do most of your work for you.",
            date = "2012-10-24T10:17:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30665#comments:id=1749401",
        },
        {
            id = 1785267,
            score = 24,
            author = "Barringa",
            text = "Not only is it easier to attack the mobs the NPCs are, you don't even get credit for killing the ones around the village, so there's no point whatsoever in targetting them.\n\nEDIT: I don't know how long this has been the case but this quest has finally been fixed. You do get credit for killing the Yaungol in the village now.",
            date = "2012-12-21T19:24:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30665#comments:id=1785267",
        },
        {
            id = 1724238,
            score = 23,
            author = "Whiterock",
            text = "Sha in the Monastery Quest Tree From Whiterock\n[pre]The Ordo Warbringer (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30660){A2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30662),H1 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30661),H2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30663)}* Barrels of Fun (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30651){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30656)* Pandaren Prisoners (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30650){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30655)*\n                           └──────┼───────────────┘\nCall Out Their Leader (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30457)* [ins]S[/ins])The Shado-Pan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31455){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31453) Hit Medicine (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30460)* All of the Arrows (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30459)*\n ||                  └────┐        ||       /             /\na)Turnabout (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30670)             a)The Defense of Shado-Pan Fallback (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30665)    [ins]+[/ins])Holed Up (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30682)\na)Unmasking the Yaungol (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30690)\nb)To Winter's Blossom (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30699)\n ||                \\\nb)A Line Unbroken (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30715) b)Honor, Even in Death (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30723)\n    \\             /\n    b)To the Wall! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30724)\n    /             \\\nc)Off the Wall! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30750)   c)A Terrible Sacrifice (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30751)\n ||                /\nd)Lao-Chin's Gambit (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30994)\nd)Do a Barrel Roll! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30991)\nd)Finish This! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30992)──────>My Husband... (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30768)*\n ||\nf)Where are My Reinforcements? (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30993)\nf)Unbelievable! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30752)\n[ins]S[/ins])Into the Monastery (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31030){backup version (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31031)}(Shado-Pan Monastery)\n[ins]#[/ins])Lord of the Shado-Pan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30757)(Shado-Pan Monastery)\n\n[ins]#[/ins])The Path to Respect Lies in Violence (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31342)(Shado-Pan Monastery)\n\nLegend:\nS means Skippable\n+ means Can start anytime, prequests not needed.\n{H} means Quest Have Horde Variant, click {H} for it.\n* means another Quest Tree.[/pre]\n\nYes, there are SUCH WEIRD prequests, even more weird that it have breadcumb with other prequests.",
            date = "2012-09-29T08:19:59-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30665#comments:id=1724238",
        },
    },
    [30666] = {
        {
            id = 1742146,
            score = 26,
            author = "aspasito",
            text = "This is the first quest of the Nayeli Lagoon storyline, and as far as I can see there is not a breadcrumb quest to lead us there. If you're an explorer, you will find Jay Cloudfall and the quests.",
            date = "2012-10-15T07:05:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30666#comments:id=1742146",
        },
        {
            id = 1841253,
            score = 3,
            author = "torin23",
            text = "The nearby crocolisks that the fishermen are fighting named Desperate Mortbreath aren't the correct mob and you won't get credit.  You need to go to the beach and kill those.",
            date = "2013-04-10T02:46:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30666#comments:id=1841253",
        },
        {
            id = 2287829,
            score = 1,
            author = "253840",
            text = "There are 12 boots that are part of the Brick Battleplate (Recolor) (http://www.wowhead.com/transmog-set=1503/brick-battleplate-recolor) and nine come from three quests. This comment will be cross-posted for the sake of transmog hunters.\n\nWisdom Has A Price (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30671/wisdom-has-a-price) is the fastest and easiest source if you can't use Item Restoration. The four quest chain starts with Sudden, Unexpected Crocolisk Aggression (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30666/sudden-unexpected-crocolisk-aggression) at Jay Cloudfall (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=60173/jay-cloudfall) at /way Krasarang Wilds 51.6, 76.8\n\nThe Gratitude of Stoneplow (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30628/the-gratitude-of-stoneplow) (zone quests culmination)\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=81479\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=81483\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=81484\n\nMuddy Water (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=29951/muddy-water) (starts here (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=29877/a-poor-grasp-of-the-basics), 17 quests follow)\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=81781\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=81785\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=81786\n\nWisdom Has A Price (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30671/wisdom-has-a-price)\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=88035\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=88036\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=88040\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=82901 and https://www.wowhead.com/item=101298 are not available to players.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=86121 is a BoP 0.8% drop from a Krasarang Equipment Locker (http://www.wowhead.com/object=213651/equipment-locker)",
            date = "2015-12-14T15:40:10-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30666#comments:id=2287829",
        },
    },
    [30667] = {
        {
            id = 1727570,
            score = 10,
            author = "marianne",
            text = "If you can't see Tony Tuna when you come back to complete the quest, just log off and log on again. Just a small phasing issue.",
            date = "2012-10-01T14:27:22-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30667#comments:id=1727570",
        },
        {
            id = 1814539,
            score = 1,
            author = "vizoere",
            text = "Birds (Emerald (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=60200), Crimson (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=60198), Dusky (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=60196)) are on the island located at 47,70.\nThere are 3 large islands on the South side of Krasarang Wilds (http://www.wowhead.com/zone=6134), they are on the NE island.\n\nI had luck hanging out in the path that goes up the middle of the island, all three will eventually fly by you on their rounds around the island. Though you may get done quicker if you go looking for the birds.\n\nMake sure you also get quest, Sudden, Unexpected Crocolisk Aggression (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30666) from Jay Cloudfall (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=60173), as you'll be killing the crocs (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=60202) there at the same time.\n\nEach bird dropped 3 or 4 feathers for me so this went pretty quickly.",
            date = "2013-02-16T22:29:15-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30667#comments:id=1814539",
        },
        {
            id = 2854441,
            score = 1,
            author = "Engrelled",
            text = "Have the Crimson Lories always been really tough to kill? Had no trouble with the Emerald or Dusky, but the Crimsons were spamming Fan of Feathers for 2K a pop - got tired of dying!",
            date = "2018-11-22T19:00:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30667#comments:id=2854441",
        },
    },
