    },
    [30695] = {
        {
            id = 1735895,
            score = 32,
            author = "572789",
            text = "Just watched my husband solo this as an 87 Arms Warrior.  When the maw starts blowing his nasty breath at you, walk through him, you'll avoid the massive damage it does.  Died twice before he tried this - easy using this method.",
            date = "2012-10-08T17:04:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30695#comments:id=1735895",
        },
        {
            id = 1660887,
            score = 11,
            author = "515790",
            text = "If you loose your little \"Wrynn helper\", you can simply leave the temple area and then return, and he will respawn.",
            date = "2012-04-30T13:28:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30695#comments:id=1660887",
        },
        {
            id = 1753629,
            score = 6,
            author = "578741",
            text = "Tricky quest.\n\nUnsure if the pagoda bosses are different but I did struggle on the East Pagoda. Took 3 attempts.\n\nI am a Healer monk Lvl88 quest gear only [207k health 200k mana]\n\nI took 3 attempts on this guy, the first 2 ended miserably. Jab/kick and heals were a horrible method as stopping to heal just lets him blast with his breath so healing never kept up with the damage especially when adds arrive.\n\n3rd attempt was success though. I completely ignored trying to heal as I knew it would end in disaster anyway and instead just kept on top of him circling around all the time [a la rogue] never stopping my circling at all and used jab/kick only. The circling helped a lot and I noticed he struggles to do any major damage. I also didn't get adds for quite some time [not sure what the trigger is for adds tbh]. While circling him he actually stops trying to face me when he has to do his breath and this meant I was able to stay away from it really easy as when he stopped trying to face me I knew he was about to breath [ an easy signal to spot :)]\n\nI ignored all adds that arrived during the fight [I do not do massive damage as a healer] but ended fight at about 60% health.\n\nHope this might be of use to those that can keep moving and damage at the same time.",
            date = "2012-10-30T06:27:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30695#comments:id=1753629",
        },
        {
            id = 1792560,
            score = 3,
            author = "Jaunter",
            text = "The boss creature has two main abilities.  They can both do a tremendous amount of damage if you don't handle them correctly.\n\nThe first one that he will cast is the \"Torrent of Despair\".  It manifests as a \"sha\" breath that goes out in a cone of damage from the mob's mouth.  Just simply stay out of its path or run right through him to the other side to get out of this one.  Don't use any precious interrupts you have on this ability.\n\nThe second one that he will cast is the \"Wail of Despair\", the Big Daddy of abilities that will get you killed.  And yes, this is the 'whale of damage' he will do to you if you don't interrupt this one.  This is the one ability, that if you don't interrupt it, will make you literally wail in despair of ever getting the quest done.  THIS ABILITY MUST BE INTERRUPTED AT ALL COSTS.\n\nA rogue's kick, a hunter's silent shot, a mage's counter spell, etc. should be put on a special hot key for instant activation for interrupting this particular cast.  In fact, don't use any cool downs or anything else just especially to make very, very sure that your interrupt is ready to go for when he starts his \"Wail of Despair\".  Once this ability is interrupted, the rest is easy.  There won't be any of those annoying adds, and you just keep out of the way of his \"Torrent of Despair\" by the usual kiting methods.",
            date = "2013-01-04T16:21:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30695#comments:id=1792560",
        },
        {
            id = 1820176,
            score = 3,
            author = "1102574",
            text = "just solo'd this on my night elf druid. lvl 86. the trick is to kill one of the guys he spawns. this will give you extra health and a speed buff because of the little guy that's with you. if you look on your buffs when he's with you it says you get a health boost everytime you kill a sha. and the stronger they are the greater the buffs. WOW sure did think about this battle. please up-vote this so everyone can see. died about 20 times before trying this. when i ran in circles i didn't hit as hard as normal. definetely avoid that mist he spits out though. hope this helps",
            date = "2013-03-02T19:54:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30695#comments:id=1820176",
        },
    },
    [30699] = {
        {
            id = 1724415,
            score = 8,
            author = "Whiterock",
            text = "Sha in the Monastery Quest Tree From Whiterock\n[pre]The Ordo Warbringer (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30660){A2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30662),H1 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30661),H2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30663)}* Barrels of Fun (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30651){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30656)* Pandaren Prisoners (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30650){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30655)*\n                           └──────┼───────────────┘\nCall Out Their Leader (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30457)* [ins]S[/ins])The Shado-Pan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31455){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31453) Hit Medicine (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30460)* All of the Arrows (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30459)*\n ||                  └────┐        ||       /             /\na)Turnabout (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30670)             a)The Defense of Shado-Pan Fallback (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30665)    [ins]+[/ins])Holed Up (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30682)\na)Unmasking the Yaungol (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30690)\nb)To Winter's Blossom (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30699)\n ||                \\\nb)A Line Unbroken (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30715) b)Honor, Even in Death (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30723)\n    \\             /\n    b)To the Wall! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30724)\n    /             \\\nc)Off the Wall! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30750)   c)A Terrible Sacrifice (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30751)\n ||                /\nd)Lao-Chin's Gambit (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30994)\nd)Do a Barrel Roll! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30991)\nd)Finish This! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30992)──────>My Husband... (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30768)*\n ||\nf)Where are My Reinforcements? (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30993)\nf)Unbelievable! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30752)\n[ins]S[/ins])Into the Monastery (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31030){backup version (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31031)}(Shado-Pan Monastery)\n[ins]#[/ins])Lord of the Shado-Pan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30757)(Shado-Pan Monastery)\n\n[ins]#[/ins])The Path to Respect Lies in Violence (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31342)(Shado-Pan Monastery)\n\nLegend:\nS means Skippable\n+ means Can start anytime, prequests not needed.\n{H} means Quest Have Horde Variant, click {H} for it.\n* means another Quest Tree.[/pre]\n\nYes, there are SUCH WEIRD prequests, even more weird that it have breadcumb with other prequests.",
            date = "2012-09-29T11:23:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30699#comments:id=1724415",
        },
        {
            id = 1676642,
            score = 4,
            author = "selvin",
            text = "Note if you're like me and did the everest quest chain first you can take the FP to kota basecamp to speed things up.",
            date = "2012-06-14T15:17:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30699#comments:id=1676642",
        },
        {
            id = 1720856,
            score = 2,
            author = "slither666",
            text = "Can someone post information about where you pick up this quest?",
            date = "2012-09-26T21:57:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30699#comments:id=1720856",
        },
        {
            id = 1732623,
            score = 2,
            author = "1041422",
            text = "I had trouble trying to keep up with zygor guide with this quest, since it said to turn it in and i didn't have the quest.  I haven't even started the questline.  To start the questline you have to go to Shado Pan Fallback and speak with Shado Master Chong there.  Just finish the quests he gives you and eventually you will get this quest.",
            date = "2012-10-05T19:27:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30699#comments:id=1732623",
        },
        {
            id = 1727861,
            score = 1,
            author = "Eclipsegirl",
            text = "This may be premature, but asking other players what to do, since I didn't have the breadcrumb to Lin, they said to do the Shado-Pan quest line.\nWithout the bread crumb, I couldn't pick up the next quest from LIn, which was important in this version of the zygor leveling guide.\n\nYou pick that up the Shado-pan bread crumb by talking to Admiral Taylor in the Westwind retreat.\n\nEDIT --------------------\nOnce I got the Shado-Pan, there were 3 quests to do before the breadcrumb to Winter's blossom dropped.",
            date = "2012-10-01T19:59:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30699#comments:id=1727861",
        },
    },
