    [30782] = {
        {
            id = 1743488,
            score = 2,
            author = "692994",
            text = "In Hatred's Vice (Townlong Steppes) kill Spiteful Spirits (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30782) that are roaming the area. HOWEVER, you'll probably want to do this quest along with the other quest you got at the same time in the same area called Hatred Becomes Us (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30783).\n\nIn that case, look for the Spiteful Spirits that are attacking the Crazed Shado-Pan Rangers, click on the Spiteful Spirit. Then, use your quest item Totem of Harmony (http://www.wowhead.com/item=81430) and place it right at the spirits feet. A yellow circle called a Pool of Harmony will appear on the ground, and a Seething Hatred (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=61092) will spawn. Kill both the Spiteful Spirit and the Seething Hatred to complete both quests at the same time.\n\nAlso, note that during the quest you will notice a red bar on your screen that will climb up towards 100% as you fill with hatred. I don't know what happens when it reaches 100%, but if you don't want to be consumed with hatred, make sure you stand within the Pool of Harmony mentioned above.",
            date = "2012-10-16T16:49:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30782#comments:id=1743488",
        },
        {
            id = 1768220,
            score = 1,
            author = "Liri",
            text = "Overwhelmed by rage the world greys out and seething hatred appears out of you.  Lvl 89 with 326 k health.\n\nIt doesnt count to the quest.\n\nYou will keep your Hatred bar until you kill the Seething Hatred.",
            date = "2012-11-26T14:24:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30782#comments:id=1768220",
        },
    },
    [30783] = {
        {
            id = 1851059,
            score = 31,
            author = "1114051",
            text = "OK guys, the process that works 100% for this quest is:\n\n1) Kill the Spiteful Spirit attacking the Shadow-Pan. Do this first, before anything else.\n2) Cast the totem under your Shadow-Pan to save (which is now just sitting there not doing anything) <- IMPORTANT\n3) Get under the totem so you don't get hatred.\n4) Aggro and kill the Seething Hatreds that pop up from the ground.\n\nIt's the Spiteful Spirits that are &*!@ing things up. If you don't clear them out first and instead go on to pop up the Hatreds, you won't get credit. I just confirmed this multiple times by intentially aggroing a Spirit while attacking a Hatred, each time I didn't get credit.\n\nPLEASE vote this comment up, it will save people a lot of grief.",
            date = "2013-05-07T23:16:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30783#comments:id=1851059",
        },
        {
            id = 1721969,
            score = 27,
            author = "1033823",
            text = "Perhaps you would like to go through this quest ignoring the mechanic and succumbing to your hatred.  To be quite honest, that's fine.  It is possible that you will then pass on a nice buff that increases haste, but it is still fine.\n\nThe only thing that will happen should you choose not to stand in the golden Pools of Harmony is your screen will become progressively more dull and grey while red filters into the sides of your vision, culminating in you spawning your own Seething Hatred at 100/100 Hatred.  This Seething Hatred is a different model from the ones spawned when healing the monks, and you will not get credit towards the completion of the quest upon destroying your own mob.  You will not lose your Hatred stacks until you defeat your inner Seething Hatred: upon the add's death, your Hatred will reset back to zero.",
            date = "2012-09-27T18:26:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30783#comments:id=1721969",
        },
        {
            id = 2012036,
            score = 15,
            author = "Sqqueeky",
            text = "To open this quest you need to do the Fire Camp Osul chain starting at A Foot in the Door (http://wod.wowhead.com/quest=30814) from Taran Zhu at Longying Outpost, and then continue with all the Hatred's Vice chain from Ban Bearheart.\n\nI had previously done the Do a Barrel Roll chain for Lao Chin's Last Mug, but I think the linking quest is a breadcrumb rather than a prerequisite.",
            date = "2014-10-12T15:42:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30783#comments:id=2012036",
        },
        {
            id = 1726720,
            score = 14,
            author = "Chaoslux",
            text = "It's dangerous to go alone! Take this.",
            date = "2012-10-01T00:36:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30783#comments:id=1726720",
        },
        {
            id = 1732149,
            score = 12,
            author = "Zeror",
            text = "This is how this quest works:\nThe bar shows how much your hatred is. The bar must stay as empty as possible. If you don't place a totem on the ground or stand out of the totems range then your hatred will rise (the bar fills up). A sha creature will appear when the bar is completely filled. So stay close to the totem to prevent that from happening. When it does happen, that the bar fills up you see your vision changes to a decolourized view with red screen edges.\n\nWith aboves mechanic for this quest you need to free 8x https://www.wowhead.com/npc=61050's from their Sha corruption. If you a place a totem close to a Crazed Ranger then one or two https://www.wowhead.com/npc=61054's pops out. Kill 'm!\n\nYou get this quest together with https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30782 if you have done all previous quests.",
            date = "2012-10-05T09:53:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30783#comments:id=1732149",
        },
    },
    [30784] = {
        {
            id = 1727891,
            score = 43,
            author = "783408",
            text = "Sad story...",
            date = "2012-10-01T20:30:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30784#comments:id=1727891",
        },
        {
            id = 1720791,
            score = 31,
            author = "1034236",
            text = "Well that was dark.",
            date = "2012-09-26T21:05:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30784#comments:id=1720791",
        },
        {
            id = 1728102,
            score = 27,
            author = "673336",
            text = "She has several knockbacks.  It is possible to be knocked back far enough to reset her.  Her leash is pretty short.  I wound up fighting in the little hut she's in to keep from being knockbacked (the lazy way).",
            date = "2012-10-02T00:29:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30784#comments:id=1728102",
        },
        {
            id = 1731572,
            score = 21,
            author = "519134",
            text = "Uh, why are the cloth rewards 13 ilvl points lower than everything else?",
            date = "2012-10-04T19:10:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30784#comments:id=1731572",
        },
        {
            id = 1773540,
            score = 20,
            author = "Sketchie",
            text = "Ban Bearheart will ask you to talk to Suna Silentstrike in this quest. You are given a Totem of Harmony from a previous quest which functions the same - it's supposed to keep your Hatred at stable levels.\n\nIf you approach Suna Silentstrike at her tent, the event will begin.\n\nSuna Silentstrike says: Has Ben sent you to kill me, then? Just like he killed my husband?\nSuna Silentstrike yells: Your pitiful rituals are meaningless! I will not be saved!\n\nDuring the fight, Suna Silentstrike will basically attack you and occasionally use Roundhouse Kick to knock you back a bit. She does have a buff, Rising Hatred, which increases her damage over time, so it would be a good idea to finish her quickly. Use the Totem of Harmony to keep your Hatred down during the fight. Once you have \"killed\" her...\n\nSuna Silentstrike kneels down.\n\nSuna Silentstrike says: I see how... my hatred... consumed me. Tell Ban... all is... forgiven.\n\nSuna Silentstrike then collapses, dead. Nothing happens for a few moments, but you are then suddenly knocked up and back from where Suna Silentstrike has died, and the Sha of Hatred will pop up in her place.\n\nSha of Hatred yells: Ahahaha... you pitiful weaklings!\nSha of Hatred yells: Even your strongest warriors succumb like lambs to the slaughter.\nSha of Hatred yells: Your turn will come. Hate, will turn you all against one another until this whole world burns.\n\nThe Sha of Hatred then disappears.\n\nWhen you hand the quest to Ban Bearheart, he will say this.\n\nWhat? She was possessed by the Sha of Hatred?\n\nNo. NO!\n\nDespite our differences, she was one of us. Today, the Shado-Pan has lost a dear sister.\n\nHer death will not be in vain. I will not rest until I have defeated the Sha of Hatred!\n\nSuna, I swear this to you!\n\nThis was another quest that bought me to tears, the others being Heroes of the Horde! and Life. =_=;",
            date = "2012-12-02T02:15:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30784#comments:id=1773540",
        },
    },
    [30785] = {
        {
            id = 5278613,
            score = -9,
            author = "2207026",
            text = "The battle front is thing soldier know in additional memory plus everyboduy",
            date = "2021-11-11T09:10:50-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30785#comments:id=5278613",
        },
    },
    [30786] = {
        {
            id = 1729259,
            score = 29,
            author = "ramrad",
            text = "After seeing all the skeletons around him I decided to check out this site before attempting him. He is not that easy. He is a caster and has three abilities. He summons two icy orbs. He used this ability twice during the fight. The icy orbs do lots of damage (around 500 each every half a second) so pop defensive cooldowns and kill them fast. They have around 16k HP each and die very quickly. He also casts blizzard (he did this once during the fight). It ticked for 12k a second on a Lvl 90 hunter. Just move out of the blizzard circle on the ground. He also casts frostbolts as filler that did about 10k damage. He insta-dies at around 37%.\nTLDR: Kill the icy orbs that he summons. Stay out of blizzard.",
            date = "2012-10-02T22:32:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30786#comments:id=1729259",
        },
        {
            id = 1729917,
            score = 14,
            author = "Duecez",
            text = "One thing to note is that he will die once he reaches 33% health.",
            date = "2012-10-03T11:14:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30786#comments:id=1729917",
        },
        {
            id = 1676678,
            score = 10,
            author = "selvin",
            text = "He's on the ridge above you, circle to the west and you'll see a path up to the target.",
            date = "2012-06-14T17:02:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30786#comments:id=1676678",
        },
        {
            id = 1777918,
            score = 8,
            author = "1057704",
            text = "To get to him, run up the grassy slope just to the left of the quest giver. and follow the cliff around.\nLocated at 68,71\n\nMake sure to kill the \"Icy Orbs\" that he spits out. These things will kill you if you dont.",
            date = "2012-12-08T18:29:42-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30786#comments:id=1777918",
        },
        {
            id = 1799447,
            score = 2,
            author = "769067",
            text = "Found this very hard to do with level 88 hunter, but did achieve it. Survival Spec.\n\nAttacked first with bear. Then ran in close and dropped snake trap and explosive trap.  Then fired linx rush, dire beast and stampede. Moved away and killed orbs. Keep moving and hitting him with explosive shot and keep black arrow and serpent sting up. Keep moving to stay away from blizzard or you die very quickly. Once he gets to about 50 % health he dies very quickly.\n\nHope this helps.",
            date = "2013-01-16T11:17:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30786#comments:id=1799447",
        },
    },
    [30787] = {
        {
            id = 1720619,
            score = 40,
            author = "cherryvision",
            text = "If you're having trouble picking up the torches, I found I needed an extra bag slot empty beyond the first one for them to fit in your inventory. If your inventory is full try getting rid of some trash and it should work.",
            date = "2012-09-26T18:00:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30787#comments:id=1720619",
        },
        {
            id = 1730410,
            score = 35,
            author = "Genox113",
            text = "On the third shaman I killed the torch disappeared before I could kill him. This happened on the fourth and fifth time too. I thought maybe the quest was bugged, but then I noticed that the lurkers were dying before the shaman died, and that's when the torches disappeared. If this is happening to you as well just make sure the lurker has high health before you start, and you should be good to go.",
            date = "2012-10-03T19:56:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30787#comments:id=1730410",
        },
        {
            id = 1676680,
            score = 24,
            author = "selvin",
            text = "Note that you have to kill the shamans when they're chanelling with the lightning, otherwise you won't be able to click the torch. It's okay if the lightning goes away while you're killing them though.",
            date = "2012-06-14T17:09:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30787#comments:id=1676680",
        },
        {
            id = 1676683,
            score = 8,
            author = "selvin",
            text = "The shamans put a buff on themselves that when you kill them or dispell it from them stacks on you. At 8 stacks you get 200% extra damage and quite a bit of healing every couple seconds. It's definitely worth it to try to keep the stacks up.",
            date = "2012-06-14T17:15:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30787#comments:id=1676683",
        },
        {
            id = 1676684,
            score = 6,
            author = "selvin",
            text = "The next quests are Golgoss  (http://mop.wowhead.com/quest=30788)and Arconiss  (http://mop.wowhead.com/quest=30789).",
            date = "2012-06-14T17:17:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30787#comments:id=1676684",
        },
    },
    [30788] = {
        {
            id = 1693025,
            score = 39,
            author = "787312",
            text = "The peat clump is at 70.54, 69.65",
            date = "2012-07-28T02:25:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30788#comments:id=1693025",
        },
        {
            id = 1719599,
            score = 15,
            author = "jostor",
            text = "There is a small mound of dirt on the ground you have to use, and then defend the NPC from a few mobs as he gets summoned, overall very simple. The mound of dirt is not too easy to spot (at least it took me some time <.<) so look carefully :)",
            date = "2012-09-26T04:03:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30788#comments:id=1719599",
        },
        {
            id = 1726585,
            score = 6,
            author = "1038628",
            text = "I'd like to point out to anyone still having problems with this quest; there are TWO peat piles, if you pick both quests up together. They are a sort distance away from each other but if you look you will find them.",
            date = "2012-09-30T21:41:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30788#comments:id=1726585",
        },
        {
            id = 1722794,
            score = 3,
            author = "Afzal",
            text = "This quest and Arconiss  (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30789)(the other related quest) has bugged for a lot of people. The best thing to do, is to skip this part and continue in Hatred's Vice.",
            date = "2012-09-28T07:23:53-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30788#comments:id=1722794",
        },
        {
            id = 1777923,
            score = 3,
            author = "1057704",
            text = "Run up to the swamp, before you get to the middle island, to the right, behind a fallen tree is a blue peat mound sparkling: 71.5, 72.3.\n\nRight click it and defend it from the baddies that appear.\n\nThen head north a short ways to: 70.5, 69.6\n\nRight click and defend again.\n\nThen you are done.",
            date = "2012-12-08T18:43:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30788#comments:id=1777923",
        },
    },
    [30789] = {
        {
            id = 1693023,
            score = 24,
            author = "787312",
            text = "The peat mound is at 71.52, 72.32",
            date = "2012-07-28T02:19:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30789#comments:id=1693023",
        },
        {
            id = 1704974,
            score = 15,
            author = "Rawveggie",
            text = "This appears bugged for me today. I can see the mound of peat that is sparkling but I can't click on it. I was able to click the other mound for the other NPC just fine.\n\nUpdate/Edit: I was eventually able to complete the quest a few days later after relogging a few times.",
            date = "2012-08-27T15:26:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30789#comments:id=1704974",
        },
        {
            id = 1722146,
            score = 7,
            author = "Lestat86",
            text = "The Quest truely seems bugged a bit with the help of a nother guy i was able to do it.\n\nHe summoned the Npc while i was standing next to the mud and after the protect quest it counted for me too without being in party with him maybe this will help some people.",
            date = "2012-09-27T21:00:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30789#comments:id=1722146",
        },
        {
            id = 1726257,
            score = 6,
            author = "Cronien",
            text = "Here's a protip for you all: If this quest is bugged on your server, you're screwed. There's no way to complete it on your server anymore, seeing as it is a server wide bug.\n\nHowever, if you get a friend to invite you over to another who isn't bugged, you can click the mound and get the quest finished! I did it today and it worked.\n\nTo get invited over to another server you need a real-ID friend in the same level-range as you invite you.\n\nHope you all get this worked out! :)",
            date = "2012-09-30T15:38:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30789#comments:id=1726257",
        },
        {
            id = 1722909,
            score = 5,
            author = "Thair",
            text = "I just tried this quest and it was bugged for me too. Tried reloading, abandoning and re-obtaining the quest and nothing helps. Finally, I submitted a ticket and came here to remind you guys to do the same if it doesn't work for you either :)",
            date = "2012-09-28T09:13:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30789#comments:id=1722909",
        },
    },
    [30790] = {
        {
            id = 1676693,
            score = 3,
            author = "selvin",
            text = "If you're a herbalist the items will appear on your minimap if you're searching for herbs.\n\nEven if you arn't one though, it's pretty easy to find them, as there's a metric ton of them around the central island that rises out of the mists. They're even far enough from the clump of 3 or 4 shamans that you don't need to bother with them (though if you're at all like me you probably aggroed 237 of them anyway as you were running in...)",
            date = "2012-06-14T17:36:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30790#comments:id=1676693",
        },
    },
