    [30925] = {
        {
            id = 1720327,
            score = 146,
            author = "1017771",
            text = "kill the enemies in the north part of the area.  The panda that's with u will search them after they've died and will either say yes you've found a statue or not.",
            date = "2012-09-26T14:57:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30925#comments:id=1720327",
        },
        {
            id = 1732730,
            score = 22,
            author = "930963",
            text = "This is easily one of the hardest solo quests in the game at the moment. The mantids spawn on the northern shores of Niuzao's island. You have to run through a warzone full of elites just to get to them. Some of the elites bug out and do not leash, so be prepared to die. In fact be prepared to die anyways, because the mantids necessary to complete the quest often spawn in very large groups. The drones are particularly nasty, always coming in packs of 3 with around 330k hp each, and they do a stacking debuff that hurts a lot, as well as enrage.\n\nTo complete the quest, just kill the mantids and let your stealthed pandaren buddy loot their corpses for the statue parts. The number of kills needed seems to be random. Might be 10, might be 50.\n\nUnless you're level 90 and geared, I recommend you bring a friend or two. You'll be glad you did.",
            date = "2012-10-05T22:12:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30925#comments:id=1732730",
        },
        {
            id = 1774907,
            score = 13,
            author = "Broshimitsu",
            text = "To clarify: As of patch 5.1, these mobs are no longer elites.\n\nSimply go to the northern part of the island and kill Sra'thik Guard (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=61518), Sra'thik Wound-Mender (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=61517) and/or Sra'thik Drone (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=61516). When they die, your companion Tai Ho (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=61482) will run up to the corpses and search them for the quest items.\n\nTai Ho (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=61482) wont search the bodies of Injured Sra'thik Soldier (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=61522).",
            date = "2012-12-03T16:41:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30925#comments:id=1774907",
        },
        {
            id = 5866081,
            score = 10,
            author = "davedwtho",
            text = "I was seeing no mobs when trying to do this quest, eventually figured out that the island was phased because I was on the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31266. They came back when I completed https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31277.",
            date = "2024-05-25T14:43:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30925#comments:id=5866081",
        },
        {
            id = 1787686,
            score = 3,
            author = "Eillesthis",
            text = "When you accept https://www.wowhead.com/npc=61706 says:\nAs you wish. We will find your artifact.  - I will meet you at the Sra'thik Incursion.\n\nOut in the field, a different https://www.wowhead.com/npc=61390 says:\nSame drill as before. You do the killing, I'll do the searching.\n\nStrange... this one carries a few pieces of polished stone.\nHopefully they came from Niuzao's statuette. We can only hope.\n\nAnother stone... and it matches the markings on the others we found.\nI think we're getting somewhere, . Let's keep looking around.\n\nIf I didn't know any better, I'd say this was a stone ox tail.\nAll that's left now is the head. And it can't have gotten far.\n\nHere's the head. A perfect fit, too.\nWe've performed Niuzao's errand. Now it's time to get back to some real investigation.\n\nPlus periodically:\n\nNo... nothing of note here. Keep looking.\nThere's nothing here.  Let's keep loking.\nNothing here.  Keep moving.\nNothing on this one.\n\nWhen he's found the last piece, he runs off.\n\nWhen you turn the quest in, https://www.wowhead.com/npc=61580 says:\n Come here, . I wish to speak with you. Our secret can remain hidden no longer.\nand offers https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30926.",
            date = "2012-12-26T12:31:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30925#comments:id=1787686",
        },
    },
    [30926] = {
        {
            id = 1730585,
            score = 286,
            author = "Rothar",
            text = "After defeating the Sha boss in the lower level all the way in the back, don't leave the cave trying to find Tai Ho for the turn in!\n\nMove your character to the back of your cave, where there will be a yellow question mark.  This is where Tai Ho should be, stealthed but visible - unfortunately the quest is currently bugged.\n\nFrom your location at the back of the cave, simply log out and log back in.  Tai Ho should be there now - turn in The Terrible Truth, THEN return to Niuzao Temple for the other turn ins!",
            date = "2012-10-04T00:19:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30926#comments:id=1730585",
        },
        {
            id = 1677041,
            score = 166,
            author = "selvin",
            text = "I had quite a bit of trouble finding the catacombs. What you need to look for is a dirt road going down the side of the island on the west side of the island. It's directly accross from one of the temple towers. The actual entreance to the catacombs isn't visable till you go down the side of the island on a road that goes down.",
            date = "2012-06-15T17:40:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30926#comments:id=1677041",
        },
        {
            id = 1733837,
            score = 53,
            author = "793466",
            text = "Frankly, this was the best wow quest I had in a while. How strongly moved was I by the horrific work of Sha on guards in that damned cave! My heart stopped when the edges of the screen went red, it said 'You are dying.' on the middle and my hp went to 1 instantly. (I pressed Lay on Hands split second later. Ha, ha.) The atmosphere gave me chills and general sense of uneasiness. And when I reached the last monster, Dread Shadow, I was rather freaked out by the ingenious spell which made my screen go black for 2-3 seconds.\nBravo.\n\nThis, or I was heavily stoned and listening to Lavender Town music from Pokemon while playing.",
            date = "2012-10-06T21:26:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30926#comments:id=1733837",
        },
        {
            id = 1972249,
            score = 33,
            author = "Wimbleton",
            text = "If Tai is following you around in the cave and doesn't give you a question mark when you've completed the quest, don't leave the cave. Just log/log and he'll be fixed when you return.\n\nIf you do leave the cave, as I did, expecting Tai to have repositioned himself somewhere on the Temple steps (or more likely in the nearest bar), you'll need to fight your way back down to the bottom of the cave to find him, which was annoying but not fatal.\n\nKeep your eyes open for the Fragment of Dread off in a side passage. It's worth 90 Gold and about 425K XP. Not bad for a grungy old cave filled with ugly mobs.",
            date = "2014-06-13T22:28:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30926#comments:id=1972249",
        },
        {
            id = 1733357,
            score = 25,
            author = "876692",
            text = "The Catacombs are west of the Temple on the edge of the island. If you're near the pond w/ yaks you're too far north just follow the edge of the island until you find 2 flame posts that mark a trail down & follow it. If you're having trouble turning in the quest \"The Terrible Truth\" after killing the boss, simply log out & back on & he should appear near where you killed the boss. Good luck.",
            date = "2012-10-06T12:06:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30926#comments:id=1733357",
        },
    },
    [30927] = {
        {
            id = 1720602,
            score = 39,
            author = "20187",
            text = "34.40, 59.65.\n\nGo down the path.",
            date = "2012-09-26T17:43:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30927#comments:id=1720602",
        },
        {
            id = 1721368,
            score = 18,
            author = "ankorafeonix",
            text = "To give an exact location, head west of the Niuzao Temple until you see a grey like formation on your minimap. Head down the path and the cave is there.",
            date = "2012-09-27T06:01:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30927#comments:id=1721368",
        },
        {
            id = 1903135,
            score = 15,
            author = "evertonyuma",
            text = "from the quest giver fly over the temple to the back you will see a bridge yellow colored, at the bridge turn, right .... 31 61 got to go in the cave a fair  bit to find them.",
            date = "2013-09-26T22:09:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30927#comments:id=1903135",
        },
        {
            id = 1934706,
            score = 8,
            author = "Seethe",
            text = "Maybe I'm just incredibly nerdy, but the idea behind this quest and seeing all of those sentinels who 'died afraid' was actually really saddening, and I found this quest a lot harder to do than I thought ( and certainly not for game-mechanics reasons! ).",
            date = "2014-01-15T06:02:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30927#comments:id=1934706",
        },
        {
            id = 1760449,
            score = 5,
            author = "Magekin",
            text = "Read the notes for A Trail of Fear.  There are 2 types of mobs in the catacombs plus the end guy.  Dreadlings cast 3 spells, Fear of Heights, Fear of Death and Fear of something.  The scariest is Fear of Death; your screen flashes red and it looks like you are down to only 1 hit point.  You're not.  Just keep fighting and it will pass.  Fear of heights does nothing except levitate you off the ground a bit and the other one stuns you briefly.  The Terrorlings are weaker and come in packs of about 5 or 6.  The dying sentinels are scattered on the floor all along the route but easy to overlook sometimes because it's dark and they are dark.  You'll find nodes of ghost ore, rich ghost ore and sometimes trillium.\nThe boss at the end isn't that hard but he has a special attack makes your screen go pitch black for a few seconds.  He did it to me twice.  After killing him go to the far end of the cavern to turn in one or 2 quests to the dude who was stealthing along with you. Also note there are nodes of spinefish at the bottom.  I fished one and the end guy reappeared but ignored me (I was out of range).  The trail to get to the catacombs starts due west of the temple and winds down the cliff face.  You'll see 2 small torches at the top of the trail.",
            date = "2012-11-10T17:11:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30927#comments:id=1760449",
        },
    },
    [30928] = {
        {
            id = 1719881,
            score = 82,
            author = "Espelyn",
            text = "The opening of the path you're looking for is located at 34.3, 59.6,\n\nThe cave is just down that path at 32.5, 61.0.",
            date = "2012-09-26T08:54:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30928#comments:id=1719881",
        },
        {
            id = 1762912,
            score = 21,
            author = "Thored",
            text = "Don't forget to loot [item=86516 domain=www] while you are here",
            date = "2012-11-15T15:38:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30928#comments:id=1762912",
        },
        {
            id = 1714310,
            score = 15,
            author = "Zillions",
            text = "The https://www.wowhead.com/npc=62306 that you kill for this cast 3 abilities:\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/spell=122119 - Gives you a stun similar to Blind and friendly players/pets disappear for a few moments.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/spell=122078 - Reduces your HP to ~100, but makes you immune to damage.  Don't panic!\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/spell=122120 - Lifts you into the air and looks like you are being strangled.",
            date = "2012-09-15T23:03:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30928#comments:id=1714310",
        },
        {
            id = 1751997,
            score = 13,
            author = "alpanhell",
            text = "If you're in any kind of hurry skip this quest.  There aren't enough Dreadlings to kill in this cave if you are the only person in there, and you are NEVER the only person in there.  You'll spend a long time waiting for them to spawn with several other players also waiting.",
            date = "2012-10-27T17:42:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30928#comments:id=1751997",
        },
        {
