            text = "To find the Catacombs look for the two banners/fire lamp, go down the dirt path and go inside the cave.",
            date = "2012-06-03T21:44:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30928#comments:id=1673234",
        },
    },
    [30929] = {
        {
            id = 1728760,
            score = 48,
            author = "Kemaria",
            text = "The quest text is hilarious.  As I carried out the instructions of attempting to pat, feed, etc. the yak, this is what the npcs said:\n\nBluesaddle:  As you can see, this is a defective yak.  Go ahead, blood elf.  Try to pet it.   You see?  Bad yak.  Now go on, blood elf.  Try to feed it.\n\nYak-Keeper Kyana: I don't think you understand how the yak temple works.  Try to understand, grummle.  This is a temple to Niuzao, the great black Ox.  We are servants to him, and keepers of this temple.  We do not \"replace yaks.\"\n\nBluesaddle:   I see.  Can I at least get mine serviced?  He won't even take a rider.\n\nCousin Bag-of-Rocks:  Cousin Bluesaddle... you are too persistent.   And you are being mean to the blood elf.\n\nBluesaddle: My case is made.  This yak is very bad.  We will not leave this yak temple until you fix him or replace him.\n\nYak-Keeper Kyana: Fine.  There are plenty of wild yaks near the lake to the north.  You can \"replace\" your yak with one of those.\n\nBluesaddle:  See, Cousin Bag-of-Rocks?  Persistence pays off.\n\nCousin Bag-of-Rocks:  But... we could have found wild yaks back in Kun-Lai...\n\nGotta feel for poor ol' Cousin Bag-of-Rocks. :)",
            date = "2012-10-02T12:55:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30929#comments:id=1728760",
        },
        {
            id = 1743240,
            score = 30,
            author = "Tenjen",
            text = "May i add that the conversation goes on while you try to interact with the pet. Its hilarious in execution because the comedic effect is similar to a background event while two characters are busy chatting, like in MIB one where will smith is getting beaten teh hell up trying to get the alien mother to give birth while his Partner and the father chat nonchalantly.\n\nHere you Sllooowwlly attempt the animations  of gentle pets, offering an apple, even lightly nudging him by persistently poking with your arm and kicking him (at this point Your character is just frustrated) and then VERY slowly moving to mount on the Yak. Each time is followed with the yak (in this order), whacking you, biting you, headbutting you and flinging you away into the air...all while the npc's chat like nothings happening.",
            date = "2012-10-16T09:56:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30929#comments:id=1743240",
        },
        {
            id = 1767234,
            score = 28,
            author = "asloversgo",
            text = "> \"Light Nudge\"\n> character does backflip\n\nTHAT'S NOT A LIGHT NUDGE.",
            date = "2012-11-24T13:48:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30929#comments:id=1767234",
        },
        {
            id = 1752825,
            score = 21,
            author = "Smallfoot",
            text = "For those that don't know how animals work:\n\nAttempting to feed \"Ruthers\" while behind him will earn you a 'You must be in front of your target' error message.  Since most 'gearwheels' aren't particular about direction, I found this detail rather humorous, if not for the mental images alone.",
            date = "2012-10-28T21:12:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30929#comments:id=1752825",
        },
        {
            id = 1745905,
            score = 19,
            author = "745628",
            text = "We should have more of these short and simple quests, which are only here for the fun of it. I really liked this one =)",
            date = "2012-10-19T18:18:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30929#comments:id=1745905",
        },
    },
    [30930] = {
        {
            id = 1714305,
            score = 241,
            author = "Zillions",
            text = "It may seem random, but actually the Yaks will be found to be the following (in this order):\n\nMean\nSmelly\nAngry\nStabby\nMean Angry\nStabby Smelly\nAngry Stabby\nMean Smelly\nMean, Smelly, Angry, Stabby, Very Bad Townlong Yak\nSuitable Yak\n\nSo, basically... kill 9 yaks, the 10th will be the best.\n\nDoes this remind anyone else of the children's book: \"Alexander and the Terrible, Horrible, No Good, Very Bad Day?\"  :)",
            date = "2012-09-15T22:43:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30930#comments:id=1714305",
        },
        {
            id = 2423178,
            score = 89,
            author = "Duceman",
            text = "Really surprised this information isn't here, but in order for this quest to appear you must complete the two quests:\n\nThe Motives of the Mantid (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30921/the-motives-of-the-mantid)\n\nAnd\n\nSet the Mantid Back (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30923/set-the-mantid-back)\n\nBoth from Tai Ho at Shando-Pan Garrison (49,72).\n\nHe'll give you a quest afterwards called The Wisdom of Niuzao (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30924/the-wisdom-of-niuzao). Just fly over to the turn in (you don't actually have to turn it in), and accept the quest from Bluesaddle (standing right next to the turn in) called Bad Yak (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30929/bad-yak). Do that real quick and he'll appear at 35,57 with this quest.",
            date = "2016-10-06T22:18:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30930#comments:id=2423178",
        },
        {
            id = 1723515,
            score = 66,
            author = "Balgair",
            text = "You can run away to reset the yak, which saves on a lot of time spent killing - it'll still move on to the next step in the chain even if you don't actually kill it. (You can also just keep lassoing the same yak this way!)",
            date = "2012-09-28T19:47:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30930#comments:id=1723515",
        },
        {
            id = 1722934,
            score = 47,
            author = "littlegreenwoman",
            text = "Do the quest in one go. If you wander off for too long or log off, you have to start at the mean yak all over again.",
            date = "2012-09-28T09:40:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30930#comments:id=1722934",
        },
        {
            id = 1750084,
            score = 27,
            author = "DKVerne",
            text = "Smelly Yak (npc=67073), Smelly Yak (npc=67073), what are they feeding you...\nSmelly Yak (npc=67073), Smelly Yak (npc=67073), it's not your fault!",
            date = "2012-10-25T08:17:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30930#comments:id=1750084",
        },
    },
    [30931] = {
        {
            id = 1676993,
            score = 46,
            author = "selvin",
            text = "The mob that drops the bow is Et'kil, who is guarded by two drones in a corner of the temple a little off the road to the north west of the quest giver. The drones do a stacking debuff on you and a 40% extra damage enrage, so be careful.",
            date = "2012-06-15T13:44:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30931#comments:id=1676993",
        },
        {
            id = 1724535,
            score = 31,
            author = "Vifor",
            text = "Soloed as frost DK by kitting them all inside the court of the temple. The Niuzao Sentinels there where happy to help.",
            date = "2012-09-29T12:50:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30931#comments:id=1724535",
        },
        {
            id = 1740951,
            score = 20,
            author = "520848",
            text = "When you turn this in, the kid runs off to Sentinel Commander Qipan (www.wowhead.com/npc=61584). Qipan then has Father's Footsteps (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30932) available.",
            date = "2012-10-14T00:51:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30931#comments:id=1740951",
        },
        {
            id = 1737237,
            score = 12,
            author = "clarkeyboy",
            text = "Nearly every class has some kind of CC - Engage by Polymorphing/Hexing one of the adds, nuke down the other. When it begins to cast Caustic Spray just move to the side, they die quick with just over 300k HP. The boss hits moderately hard but can heal up in between attacks, and his Sonic Spike is the circular thing he places on the floor that does MASSIVE damage. Avoid that and you are golden.",
            date = "2012-10-10T06:25:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30931#comments:id=1737237",
        },
        {
            id = 1798936,
            score = 11,
            author = "Blazyrkh",
            text = "So.... you go fetch his father's crossbow, and then he runs of to the quest hub for next step while wielding a BOW not a CROSSBOW. :P",
            date = "2013-01-15T09:16:45-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30931#comments:id=1798936",
        },
    },
    [30932] = {
        {
            id = 1730305,
            score = 944,
            author = "Eaglesight",
            text = "Here is a picture that might come to help. It is taken when looking down onto the Niuzao Temple\n\nhttp://localhostr.com/files/wC3VV6I/fathersfootsteps.jpg\nA second mirror if localhostr is down: http://img221.imageshack.us/img221/6783/fathersfootsteps.jpg\nA third mirror if the other mirrors are down: http://i47.tinypic.com/dfgfi0.jpg",
            date = "2012-10-03T17:42:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30932#comments:id=1730305",
        },
        {
            id = 1673228,
            score = 159,
            author = "Meili",
            text = "To find the items;\n\nBedroll: Jump down and climb the stairs up north. There will be a room with 'Niuzao Sentinel' in it sleeping. The bedroll is in the middle.\nShield: Right outside of the bedroll.\nHa-Cha: Go up the ramp and go to the center where there is stairs going down. Ha-Chan will be the yak.\n\nSentinel Yalo is somewhere but I can't find him again. But everything is in the temple area.",
            date = "2012-06-03T21:10:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30932#comments:id=1673228",
        },
        {
            id = 5225144,
            score = 74,
            author = "Yotingo",
            text = "The quest markers for this in 9.1 are a little misleading. The bedroll and shield are in/near the northern tower, not on the platform with the yak.",
            date = "2021-07-20T18:10:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30932#comments:id=5225144",
        },
        {
            id = 1889828,
            score = 59,
            author = "806196",
            text = "Just to be very clear:\nSentinel Yalo is walking around on the platform to the right of the main stairs (the stairs that Ogo the Younger and the other NPCs are at the top of); to the right as you climb the stairs.\n\nHa-Cha is the Yak at 37, 63 on the platform near the Quartermaster and the other Vendors; from the top of the main stairs fly ahead above the closed door and on to the platform behind it.\n\nTo find the shield and the bedroll:\nClimb the stairs behind Ha-Cha;\nTurn left;\nGo down the (few) stairs;\nThe shield is outside the door;\nThe bedroll is inside the door.",
            date = "2013-08-24T15:48:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30932#comments:id=1889828",
        },
        {
            id = 1696878,
            score = 47,
            author = "ArgentSun",
            text = "After you complete this quest, Ku-Mo, the questgiver, will move to the Shado-Pan Garrison (all in favor that it's a pretty shabby garrison?) and offer you https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30933. As of the current beta build, this quest is not liked to the previous one as a part of the chain, and Ku-Mo doesn't indicate that you can find him in the Garrison in any way.\n\nI can't really verify the following, as the quest is obviously not repeatable, but I believe you can only get Seeking Father on a day when the Shado-Pan dailies include https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31201. If I recall correctly, I had to give a kite to the father. So there, that may be it.",
            date = "2012-08-06T17:50:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30932#comments:id=1696878",
        },
    },
    [30933] = {
        {
            id = 1739245,
            score = 62,
            author = "Tharama",
            text = "I have found the solution!\n\nDuring the daily Shado-Pan quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31201 you are tasked with helping three Trainees out of the Kunchong feeding pits Ku-Yao (Ku-Mo's father) is in. He finally spawned perfectly fine for me when I flew to his spot while doing this daily after many days of no-showing and I was finally able to hand him one of the escape kites that was intended for the Trainees giving me quest credit.\n\nSo, yeah. Apparently it is meant to be phased and you're only meant to get the quest while on this daily or something of that accord.",
            date = "2012-10-12T05:41:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30933#comments:id=1739245",
        },
        {
            id = 1750331,
            score = 60,
            author = "Lightbrand",
            text = "Kind of funny when you turn in quest the text \" \" Yet you get gold...\n\nDid I just pickpocket this kid without him noticing?",
            date = "2012-10-25T15:36:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30933#comments:id=1750331",
        },
        {
            id = 1733651,
            score = 37,
            author = "codeytherhino",
            text = "Just a heads-up, this quest doesn't give any Shado-Pan rep even though it's given at the Shado-Pan Garrison. Given the annoyance of being dismounted in an area with elite patrols, you might not want to bother unless you want to see the very short RP at the end or need the 19g 84s 50c you get from its completion.",
            date = "2012-10-06T17:39:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30933#comments:id=1733651",
        },
        {
            id = 1728133,
            score = 30,
            author = "4122",
            text = "He's bugged sometimes. The chat bubble appears on the minimap, but the NPC is nowhere to be found.",
            date = "2012-10-02T01:10:53-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30933#comments:id=1728133",
        },
        {
            id = 1797861,
            score = 18,
            author = "crazybelgium",
            text = "Ku-Mo says: I brought you your crossbow, Dad!\nKu-Mo says: Now you can shoot the mantid!\nSentinel Ku-Yao says: I think I'm done fighting for a while, Ku-Mo.\nKu-Mo says: Really?\nSentinel Ku-Yao says: Come on. I think it's time to go home.\nSentinel Ku-Yao says: You should keep that crossbow, Ku-Mo.\nKu-Mo says: Whoah...",
            date = "2013-01-13T12:10:13-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30933#comments:id=1797861",
        },
    },
    [30935] = {
        {
            id = 1755103,
            score = 35,
            author = "365918",
            text = "While you're in the Path of Conquerors, don't forget to pick up the Ancient Mogu Tablet (http://www.wowhead.com/item=86471) from behind the statue on the right (in the room with the waterfalls). Bonus XP and gold, just for looting it.",
            date = "2012-11-01T16:27:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30935#comments:id=1755103",
        },
        {
            id = 1719661,
            score = 24,
            author = "Vorona",
            text = "Also, once you are transported, just run forwards , down some stairs, and you will come out to Whispercloud Rise which is where Shin is.",
            date = "2012-09-26T05:10:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30935#comments:id=1719661",
        },
        {
            id = 1689268,
            score = 20,
            author = "Kaelani",
            text = "In case you don't read the quest text too carefully, Mishi is right outside the tomb's entrance. Make your way out and talk to her/him to continue on.",
            date = "2012-07-17T19:33:22-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30935#comments:id=1689268",
        },
