    [30973] = {
        {
            id = 1685505,
            score = 80,
            author = "986326",
            text = "Ok, a few things about this *exasperating* quest:\n1.  The mobs have a buff called timberhusk that decreases damage taken by 80%\n2.  Line up a keg such that the mob is directly on the other side of the keg and trigger it...it should roll to the mob and apply the 'keg bomb' debuff that makes them flammable.\n3.  The guys on the ridges are firing flaming arrows after something gets keg bombed, but it DOES NOT always hit the mob directly...sometimes the fire hits off to the side...so you have to pull the mob into the fire to ignite them and remove the timberhusk buff.\n4.  NOTE that the fire debuff lasts for around 4 seconds and then they get the timberhusk buff back.",
            date = "2012-07-07T08:32:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30973#comments:id=1685505",
        },
        {
            id = 1722941,
            score = 53,
            author = "Afzal",
            text = "The idea for this quest is to pull a pack of mobs and click the Keg Bombs while facing them, so their buff will be removed. Though you can dispell their buff. So it's easier if you do that.\nIf you're playing priest you can use https://www.wowhead.com/spell=528, https://www.wowhead.com/spell=370 if you're Shammy, https://www.wowhead.com/spell=19801 for hunters and last but not least https://www.wowhead.com/spell=23922 for Warriors.",
            date = "2012-09-28T09:50:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30973#comments:id=1722941",
        },
        {
            id = 1704360,
            score = 33,
            author = "Chaix",
            text = "something that'll make this easier for most people: their buff can be dispelled by player abilities, or it will be removed when they take any fire damage, not just from the npc's fire arrows.",
            date = "2012-08-25T19:31:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30973#comments:id=1704360",
        },
        {
            id = 1721768,
            score = 25,
            author = "973143",
            text = "Okay, simple:\n\nFind a keg, pull a bug toward the keg.  Kick the keg and it'll break on the bug.  Archers will light a fire when the keg bursts.  Move to bug so he's standing in the fire.  Win.",
            date = "2012-09-27T14:05:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30973#comments:id=1721768",
        },
        {
            id = 1726246,
            score = 23,
            author = "StarlinX",
            text = "If you have the [item=88583 domain=www], from the quest [quest=30773 domain=www], it does aoe fire damage.  It removes the debuff without dealing with the kegs/arrows.",
            date = "2012-09-30T15:29:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30973#comments:id=1726246",
        },
    },
    [30974] = {
        {
            id = 1984200,
            score = 14,
            author = "Treekachu",
            text = "According to its Wowpedia page (http://wowpedia.org/Quest:Raising_Spirits_%28Townlong_Steppes%29), this quest did not ever make it to live. However, its reward has been flagged as an item for the Toy Box. As of now, plans to implement this quest are uncertain.",
            date = "2014-07-24T23:56:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30974#comments:id=1984200",
        },
        {
            id = 2010285,
            score = 5,
            author = "Aydwen",
            text = "For Anyone who is trying to get as many Toys for their Toy Box before WoD hits, as I am. Here is some information that I hope helps save you some time.\n\nUsing the Achievement \"One Steppe Forwards, Two Steppes Back as a guide, I went back to Townlong Steppes to finish every quest in the zone to ensure that this quest was indeed never put into the game. I had already completed the Fire Camp Osul and Mistlurkers in the Sumprushes. Other than that, I hadn't done a single quest in the zone.\n\nI started by going to the Gao-Ran Battlefront in the southwestern area of Townlong. I picked up all the quests from Taran Zhu and the other surrounding NPCs. I finished them all, and simply followed the quest line from Taran Zhu. It lead me east near Dusklight Hollow. I did the few quests there, which sent me east again to Rensai's Watchpost and Shado-Pan Garrison. I did all the quests there, and then the questline led me to Niuzao Temple. There was about 10 or so quests in and around Niuzao Temple and then the questline ended.\n\nOnce I finished the last quest I was awarded the One Steppe Forward, Two Steppes Back. I checked all the quest hubs in the zone and found no more quests.\n\nI feel confident in stating that this item, and the quest that awards it never made it into Live MoP.",
            date = "2014-10-06T06:13:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30974#comments:id=2010285",
        },
        {
            id = 2617559,
            score = 1,
            author = "Aestua",
            text = "The quest reward item has been flagged \"This item is not available to players.\" 'Iron Belly\" is not shown in the Toybox, even in the Not Collected filter.",
            date = "2018-09-21T20:25:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30974#comments:id=2617559",
        },
        {
            id = 1759138,
            score = -3,
            author = "Qoko",
            text = "Seems only one of the few quests (if not the only one) eventually not implemented for Pandaria loremaster, as this is the only quest on my Wholly (quest addon) overview of Pandaria that is red, aka not obtainable. The ones that are yellow are breadcrumb quests and https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32011 (see my comment on that quest) that I cannot complete anymore.",
            date = "2012-11-08T06:38:42-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30974#comments:id=1759138",
        },
        {
            id = 1674743,
