    [30987] = {
        {
            id = 2373109,
            score = 35,
            author = "Dougeh",
            text = "So, for 7.0, since [spoiler]Varian's dead (RIP),[/spoiler] they decided to replace the Boxing Match quest you used to do against him with just a simple meet-and-greet with the brand new grown-up Anduin.\nWhat I don't understand is how that makes sense in the timeline:  Is Shen-zin Su getting a new boat rammed into him every time a Pandaren wakes up on the Isle?  I assumed it was a one-time thing at a certain point in the timeline when you could punch Varian in the face, and all the Pandaren from the Isle joined at that one time, but now we know that these new Pandaren are joining The Alliance years after the first Pandaren joined, and they still had to get that boat out.\nIs The Wandering Isle some kind of time-looped hell?\n/conspiracy",
            date = "2016-08-25T01:01:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30987#comments:id=2373109",
        },
        {
            id = 1891562,
            score = 28,
            author = "Argentrose",
            text = "As you wander through Stormwind, various people will speak with you, and Aysa will stop and make a few comments.\n\nFirst is a guard on the path into the city.\nStormwind City Guard says: Never thought I'd see one of your kind walk through here.\n\nNext is General Hammond Clay.\nGeneral Hammond Clay says: Pandaren? What business do you have in Stormwind?\nAysa Cloudsinger says: We're here to join the Alliance. We seek audience with your Emperor.\nGeneral Hammond Clay says: Emperor? You'll find KING Varian inside Stormwind Keep.\nGeneral Hammond Clay eyes Jojo's pillar.\nGeneral Hammond Clay says: Behave yourselves inside Stormwind, pandaren. You're in Alliance territory now.\n\nSome children on the way under the first bridge into the city have the following conversation.\nMarty says: Hey, look! Gnolls!\nJosie says: Those aren't gnolls, silly. Use your eyes.\nJosie says: Those are FURBOLGS.\n\nThen as you approach the Alliance Hero's Baord (where you can get quests), Aysa does the following:\nAysa Cloudsinger yells: Look at this!\nAysa Cloudsinger says: Well, that's good news. Once we join the Alliance, we certainly won't run out of things to do.\n\nNext is the gnome and her teacher on the corner leading toward the Old Town District.\nMoni Widdlesprock says: Teacher... look!\nAlyn Black says: Yes. Those are pandaren, Moni.\nMoni Widdlesprock says: Pandaren? Here, in Stormwind?\n\nAs you pass under the bridge leading toward the canals, a stealthed Worgen has the following to say:\nGavin Marlsbury says: Heh... pandaren. You must be here to join the Alliance.\nGavin Marlsbury says: Good move. It worked out well for me.\nJojo Ironbrow says: Let's... just keep moving.\n\nA night elf on the bridge passing over the canal then greets you.\nLeria Nightwind says: Welcome to Stormwind!\n\nAs you grow close to the Palace, a drunken, lying down dwarf says the following:\nBrunn Goldenmug says: Pandaren? I mussht be seein' thingssh...\n\nOn your way into the castle, a paladin and a draenei have the following conversation:\nLucas Severing says: Quiet, Naanae. Outsiders approach.\nNaanae says: Outsiders, yes - but their intentions are good.\nNaanae says: Look carefully, Lucas. The Light is strong with them. Particularly that one.\nAysa Cloudsinger says: Let's keep moving.\nJojo Ironbrow says: What's the Light?\n\nI haven't found any further people to comment on Aysa, Jojo, or your pandaren's entrance into the city, but if you have, please leave a comment so we all benefit!",
            date = "2013-08-30T20:09:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30987#comments:id=1891562",
        },
        {
            id = 1788507,
            score = 23,
            author = "979563",
            text = "King Varian Wrynn is in the large castle to the far east of Stormwind.\n\nEDIT: why downvote? It's the big honking castle that's on your right when you enter.",
            date = "2012-12-28T07:46:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30987#comments:id=1788507",
        },
        {
            id = 3307068,
            score = 11,
            author = "DrugB4r0n97",
            text = "I too had the issue where King Anduin Wrynn was not spawning in the throne room. I abandoned this quest, the proceeded to do the one he gives you to speak to Jaina Proudmoore to go to kul tiras (got this quest from a room on the left as you go into stormwind keep from King Anduin Wrynn)  i completed this quest, logged out of wow, deleted cache folder (program filex x86-world of warcraft-retail-cache)   logged back in, accepted the joining the alliance quest again and King Anduin Wrynn then appeared on the throne in the throne room and the issue was fixed for me. I hope this helps any others who have or are experiencing this rather irritating issue. ( character was a PANDAREN)\n\nDELETE THE ENTIRE CACHE FOLDER!",
            date = "2021-03-08T16:53:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30987#comments:id=3307068",
        },
        {
            id = 2174408,
