            score = 8,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "Starts from a quest item mailed to the player upon completion of the achievement\nBetween a Saurok and a Hard Place (http://mop.wowhead.com/achievement=6716).\n\nWhen you turn in the quest, Lorewalker Cho tells you a story complete with a play-like reenactment and casts Storytime (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=120589) on the player.\n\"Let us talk about the nature of power.  In my hands I hold a sword.  I ask you: Who wields the power?  I do, for I wield the sword!\n\nMany thousands of years ago, the mogu held all the power.  They ruled this land with fists of iron.  But as their empire grew, they needed a way to police it and control it.\n\nThey used the powers of the Vale, and their own flesh-warping magics, to twist and shape a race of ferocious lizards into a living weapon.  They created an army.  An army of Saurok.  Bloodthirsty savages created to enforce the will of the emperor.\n\nAh, but there is a problem with creating a living weapon.  Do you see?  Who, now, wields the power?  The heartless saurok, even with their tiny lizard brains, soon realized the truth of their position.  They killed the enemies of the mogu.  Then they killed the subjects of the mogu.  Soon, they started killing the mogu themselves.  The mogu emperor then ordered all of the saurok to be purged.  He tried to wipe out their entire race, to no avail.  They still plague Pandaria to this day.\n\nSo you see - power is easily taken, but should not be lightly given.\n\nOh... I seem to have lost my sword.\"\n\nYou can have Lorewalker Cho tell the story again by talking to him or clicking on the book that is added to your bookcase in the Seat of Knowledge.",
            date = "2012-08-03T21:14:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31055#comments:id=1695762",
        },
        {
            id = 1765018,
            score = 6,
            author = "364053",
            text = "The cinematic story Lorewalker Cho tells upon turning in this quest is a good one with a lesson to be learned.  And it can be replayed again and again if you wish.  Nicely done, Blizzard!  ;-)  Love them cinematics!",
            date = "2012-11-19T21:50:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31055#comments:id=1765018",
        },
    },
    [31058] = {
        {
            id = 1703076,
            score = 164,
            author = "Nooska",
            text = "This is a quest that requires you to complete the Scenario Unga Ingoo (http://mop.wowhead.com/zone=6309).\nYou find your scenarios in the Dungeon Finder (default key: I)\nAlternatively, you can speak to the questgiver for an option to queue, as Farmbuyer (http://www.wowhead.com/user=Farmbuyer) added in below\nBe aware that the quest turn-in area is a phased area, so the npcs do not load till you are relatively near, resulting in n o turnin ? on the minimap untill you are close.",
            date = "2012-08-22T13:07:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31058#comments:id=1703076",
        },
        {
            id = 2087258,
            score = 46,
            author = "BJRubino",
            text = "I am trying to do this scenario, but I keep getting a message that I do not meet the requirements.\n\nI am a level 100 with almost all the world quests completed.\n\nAny idea what I am missing here?\n\nThanks,\nBJR",
            date = "2015-01-12T12:39:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31058#comments:id=2087258",
        },
        {
            id = 2860829,
            score = 33,
            author = "1937563",
            text = "If you are high level and want to enter the scenario go to\npandaria > vale of eternal blossoms > ABOVE  mogu'san palace > lonewalker fu(npc) > tell me of unga ingoo\n\nu can solo it",
            date = "2018-12-20T15:40:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31058#comments:id=2860829",
        },
        {
            id = 1849379,
            score = 19,
            author = "Turpentine",
            text = "The turn in for this quest is the inn right next to the flight point on Marista island in Krasarang Wilds.  The turn in does not display a yellow question mark unless you are close to the inn.  Most quest turn in ? can be seen on the map, this one for some reason does not.\n\nQuest giver/turn in Brewmaster Bo walks in and out of the inn but he always returns to the inn.",
            date = "2013-05-02T17:51:53-05:00",
