    [31093] = {
        {
            id = 1749105,
            score = 15,
            author = "Soeroah",
            text = "Almost appears to me as if Lorewalker Cho was talking about himself and his father, considering his very hands-on approach to learning. Though perhaps I am meditating on it too much.",
            date = "2012-10-24T01:24:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31093#comments:id=1749105",
        },
        {
            id = 1695749,
            score = 13,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "Starts from a quest item mailed to the player upon completion of the achievement Hozen in the Mist (http://mop.wowhead.com/achievement=6850).\n\nWhen you turn in the quest, Lorewalker Cho tells you a story complete with a play-like reenactment and casts Storytime (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=120589) on the player.\n\"One day, a father grew tired of his young cub's misbehavior.  'You act just like a hozen!' the father scolded.  Still, his son misbehaved.\n\nTo teach him a lesson, the father dragged the cub out to the forest, to watch how the hozen live.  'Do you see what the hozen are like?' he asked.  'Do you want to live like that?'\n\nThe hozen are quite lively indeed.  A short-lived race, few hozen survive past their 20th birthday.  Their leaders are all 14 or 15.  How mature were you at 14 years old?  Meditate on that!\n\nAfterwards, the father asked his cub what he had learned.\n\n'I learned that we work and toil on our little farm, but the hozen have the whole world as their garden.' the cub said.  'I learned that we squint by the light of a single candle, but that the hozen enjoy the light of the stars.  I learned that I go to school every day, but that the hozen learn by doing.'\n\nAnd the cub concluded, 'I should very much like to live like a hozen!'\n\nWho then, was the wiser?  The father or the cub?  That, my friend, is for you to decide.\"\n\nYou can have Lorewalker Cho tell the story again by talking to him or clicking on the book that is added to your bookcase in the Seat of Knowledge.",
            date = "2012-08-03T20:20:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31093#comments:id=1695749",
        },
        {
            id = 1795378,
            score = 7,
            author = "650120",
            text = "The story Lorewalker Cho tells, appears to be based off a story that goes by a couple different names. \"Rich dad, Wise Son\" or \"Through the Eye's of a Child\". Telling of a wealthy big city father taking his son to the country to live the life of a poor farmer for a week. The father does not expect the answers he receives.\nLink (http://www.sherdog.net/forums/f48/importance-our-perceptions-insightful-1807009/)",
            date = "2013-01-09T14:27:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31093#comments:id=1795378",
        },
    },
    [31094] = {
        {
            id = 1726112,
            score = 13,
            author = "Missrihanna",
            text = "He's located on the top floor of the Mogu Palace (81,25 32,29 entrance)",
            date = "2012-09-30T13:29:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31094#comments:id=1726112",
        },
        {
            id = 1675859,
            score = 12,
            author = "Nulgar",
            text = "So the Jinyu are indeed magically evolved Murlocs - in fact, their origin (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l4JsEahsAks) seems to suggest an \"evolution\" very similar to that of the Kaldorei (http://www.wowpedia.org/Kaldorei).",
            date = "2012-06-12T04:10:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31094#comments:id=1675859",
        },
        {
            id = 1736939,
            score = 12,
            author = "Smadronia",
            text = "This quest starts in your mailbox, as a missive from Lorewalker Cho (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=61962) after completing the Fish Tales (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=6846) achievement.\n\nThe quest is turned in to Lorewalker Cho, top of the Mogu'shan Palace, in the Vale of Eternal Blossoms. when you do, he casts storytime (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=120589) on you, and then tells the story of the Jinyu, complete with re-enactment.\n\n\"Great events often have humble beginnings. Consider: a quiet pond. Still. The water is like a sheet of glass.\n\nUntil I throw a stone. Such a small think - but soon, ripples engulf the whole of the lake!\n\nThe jinyu also have humble origins. Once primitive creatures, they were fortunate enough to live near the enchanted pools within the Vale.\n\nThe magic of the pools expanded their minds, and grew their bodies, until they became one of the great ancient cultures of pandaria.\n\nThe wisest of the jinyu are very wise indeed - they can speak to the rivers the way you and I would consult out elders.\n\nIn the whispering waters, they can hear the future.\n\nThe jinyu and their waterspeakers stand at the very heart of the greatest events in Pandaria's history.\n\nTheir visions built empires, freed slaves, and warned our Last Emperor of the Sundering that shattered Azeroth ten thousand years ago.\n\nThink about it: the smallest voice can change the world. Consider that, friend, the next time you decide to start throwing stones.\"\n\nMiss part of the story? Lorewalker Cho will retell it to you, if you ask him.\n\nThe patterning of this comment was modeled after Calesta, who has put in a similar comment about every other lorewalker quest.",
            date = "2012-10-09T20:40:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31094#comments:id=1736939",
        },
    },
    [31095] = {
        {
            id = 1695771,
            score = 9,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "Starts from a quest item mailed to the player upon completion of the achievement The Dark Heart of the Mogu (http://mop.wowhead.com/achievement=6754).\n\nWhen you turn in the quest, Lorewalker Cho tells you a story complete with a play-like reenactment and casts Storytime (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=120589) on the player.\n\"What do you fear most in this world?  Have you conquered your fear... or has your fear conquered you?\n\nIn the ancient days before the sundering of the world, the mogu emperors ruled over Pandaria.  My people were made slaves, and they were afraid.\n\nThe mogu were masters of pain and torture, of dark magics and brutal weapons.  No pandaren, hozen, or jinyu could resist the power they held.  And my people were afraid.\n\nIt was the mogu who built the Serpent's Spine.  The most unlucky of slaves were send to aid in its construction and defense, to be fodder for the mantid.  And my people were afraid.\n\nAs the empire grew, the mogu began to experiment with the secrets of the Value.  They crafted terrible weapons of living flesh and stone.  And my people were afraid.\n\nIn their hubris, the mogu never foresaw that their downfall lay in wait, not among their enemies, but among the oppressed.  The day that one slave stood...\n\n... and was no longer afraid.\"\n\nYou can have Lorewalker Cho tell the story again by talking to him or clicking on the book that is added to your bookcase in the Seat of Knowledge.",
            date = "2012-08-03T21:47:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31095#comments:id=1695771",
        },
        {
            id = 1754814,
            score = 2,
            author = "mir000",
            text = "Quest reward is 19g 84s 50c not 141g...",
            date = "2012-11-01T06:39:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31095#comments:id=1754814",
        },
        {
            id = 1800100,
            score = 2,
            author = "gbh102",
            text = "Reputation reward with Lorewalkers is 3135.",
            date = "2013-01-17T13:17:30-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31095#comments:id=1800100",
        },
    },
    [31096] = {
        {
            id = 1695747,
            score = 7,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "Starts from a quest item mailed to the player upon completion of the achievement What Is Worth Fighting For (http://mop.wowhead.com/achievement=6858).\n\nWhen you turn in the quest, Lorewalker Cho tells you a story complete with a play-like reenactment and casts Storytime (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=120589) on the player.\n\"What is the source of YOUR power?  Think carefully before you answer.  Many adventurers point to their weapons, or their equipment, or to tomes of arcane might.\n\nLong ago, when my people were slaves of the mogu empire, we were forbidden from carrying any weapon at all.  We were not fighters.  And no one believed we could fight the mogu without magic and steel.\n\nUntil Kang, the First of Fist Dawn, opened our eyes.\n\nOne day, the beloved monk issued a challenge to his fellow slaves. 'Hit me!' he called out.  Surprised, the beleaguered Pandaren slaves tried to strike Kang.  One by one they failed, for he intercepted their blows like a dancer and sidestepped their attacks like a reed in the wind.\n\n'Our backs are hardened by the whips of the mogu,' he told them.  'Our arms are powerful from building their fortresses.  Our minds are sharp from working alongside our enemy.  You think the mogu are stronger?  I say we are their strength!'\n\nThe farmers, the bricklayers, the shepherds and the smiths... they all bowed before Kang.  'Teach us to fight.'  And when they rose... they rose as warriors.\n\nYour voice.  Your hands. THESE are the tools of true heroes.  Use them well... and you can change the world.\"\n\nYou can have Lorewalker Cho tell the story again by talking to him or clicking on the book that is added to your bookcase in the Seat of Knowledge.",
            date = "2012-08-03T20:16:12-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31096#comments:id=1695747",
        },
        {
            id = 3184469,
            score = 6,
            author = "Vanthalas",
            text = "Currently not being able to turn it in after 8.3 - Lorewalker Cho is nowhere to be found on the previous version of the area and at the current infested area he won't complete the quest.",
            date = "2020-01-21T14:12:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31096#comments:id=3184469",
        },
        {
            id = 1800766,
            score = 3,
            author = "1056001",
            text = "This inspired me",
            date = "2013-01-19T00:39:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31096#comments:id=1800766",
        },
        {
            id = 3302499,
            score = 1,
            author = "Stereotipe",
            text = "Shadowlands:\n\nMake sure you are in the original version of the zone; if not, Zidormi is on site.  Simply speak with them and request to see the older version of the vale, before BFA screwed it all up with corruption and N'Zoth.\n\nSo in the top level of Mogu'shan palace, Cho is INSIDE, but does not show up on the map, nor does the quest helper point you there or display the yellow question mark indicating quest return.  But once you go inside, he will pop up.  There you can return your quest and complete the questline\n\nIf you want to do the whole thing easily, get the addon Handynotes along with the lorewalker supplemental addon.  This will make a series of numbers pop up which will indicate where all the artifacts you need to click on are.  They also appear on your minimap.  I flew around and found them all, then he will send you stuff in the mail which begin a quest. I did them all at once.  Then you have to watch a short play as he narrates the stories of the lore you brought.",
            date = "2021-02-19T15:19:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31096#comments:id=3302499",
        },
        {
            id = 1999909,
            score = -2,
            author = "Roshi101",
            text = "Not usable on a level one - nor are the other ones you get.",
            date = "2014-09-06T06:56:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31096#comments:id=1999909",
        },
    },
    [31097] = {
        {
            id = 1688903,
            score = 9,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "Starts from a quest item mailed to the player upon completion of the achievement Heart of the Mantid Swarm (http://mop.wowhead.com/achievement=6857).\n\nWhen you turn in the quest, Lorewalker Cho tells you a story complete with a play-like reenactment and casts Storytime (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=120589) on the player.\n\"Oh my student - you wish to study the mantid?  Be warned: the pandaren frontier is littered with the graves of former pupils.  The mantid are harsh teachers.\n\nEvery generation, the mantid swarm the Serpent's Spine wall in great numbers.  They murder many pandaren, so we kill many times their number in return.  Yet each generation, they attack once more.  Why do they do this?  We pandaren do not know.\n\nOur ancient writings indicate that the mantid have always been here.  They predate even the mogu.  Where did they come from?  We pandaren do not know.\nHere is what the pandaren do know.  By massacring our people, by slaughtering tens of thousands of pandaren, generation after generation, they have taught us the value of life.  A precious but fleeting gift.  Easily snuffed out... in an instant.\n\nThat is what the mantid have taught us.\"\n\nYou can have Lorewalker Cho tell the story again by talking to him or clicking on the book that is added to your bookcase in the Seat of Knowledge.",
            date = "2012-07-16T19:20:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31097#comments:id=1688903",
        },
        {
            id = 1749745,
            score = 6,
            author = "78799",
            text = "For some reason it doesn't show up on my map, but you turn in and find him located at 83, 29 in Vale of Eternal Blossoms (just above the Mogu'shan Palace dungeon).",
            date = "2012-10-24T19:34:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31097#comments:id=1749745",
        },
        {
            id = 1675682,
            score = 5,
            author = "836112",
            text = "A reference to Star Craft 2's Heart of the Swarm Expansion which focuses on the Zerg, an Alien race that swarms over their enemies with overwhelming numbers to achieve victory.",
            date = "2012-06-11T16:04:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31097#comments:id=1675682",
        },
        {
            id = 1739482,
            score = 5,
            author = "Karadine",
            text = "During the speech to this quest, Lorewalker Cho suggests that if you can earn the trust of the mantid, you can learn why they swarm the wall and attack the Pandaren. You do in fact learn this information upon reaching exalted with [faction=1337] and completing https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31612.\n\n[spoiler]Kil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: Wakener, your deeds have earned you the trust of the Klaxxi.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: You are to be rewarded. Walk with me.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: We mantid are an elder race. The pandaren you associate with - they are but children. They have their role to play.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: Each cycle, our young swarm their walls. The pandaren slay the weak. The strong return.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: With each generation, we grow ever stronger.[/spoiler]",
            date = "2012-10-12T10:56:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31097#comments:id=1739482",
        },
        {
            id = 5384056,
            score = 3,
            author = "broadwayqtpi",
            text = "If you're not able to turn in this quest, try talking to Zidormi (right outside the entrance at about 80, 32) and changing what timeline you're in. That fixed it for me!",
            date = "2022-06-12T22:20:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31097#comments:id=5384056",
        },
    },
    [31100] = {
        {
            id = 1695805,
            score = 9,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "Starts from a quest item (http://www.wowhead.com/item=83777) mailed to the player upon completion of the achievement The Song of the Yaungol (http://mop.wowhead.com/achievement=6847).\n\nWhen you turn in the quest, Lorewalker Cho tells you a story complete with a play-like reenactment and casts Storytime (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=120589) on the player.\n\"Fire!  It is the most magical of elements.  It warms us, it cooks our food.  It is the hearthfire that makes a house a home.  In the right hands, fire can shape iron into swords or plowshares.  Left uncontrolled, fire could destroy a city.\n\nFire is the instrument of change.\n\nLong ago, a group of sturdy nomad hunters wandered the world.  By a stroke of fate, they were here in Pandaria when the Sundering split apart the continents of Azeroth.  The wanderers found themselves trapped in the Townlong Steppes, a harsh and dangerous land.\n\nThose noble hunters found a way to survive on their own.  Fire was the key.  They drew up oil from the ground.  They used it to heat their homes, cook their food, and burn their enemies.  They grew STRONG.\n\nFrom the flames of fate, the yaungol were born.  They survive beyond the wall, for they refuse to submit to any law but their own.\n\nHas fate been cruel to the yaungol?  You may as well ask if fire is good or bad.  Fate is like fire; it can shape or destroy us.  All that matters is what you do with it.\"\n\nYou can have Lorewalker Cho tell the story again by talking to him or clicking on the book that is added to your bookcase in the Seat of Knowledge.",
            date = "2012-08-03T23:37:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31100#comments:id=1695805",
        },
        {
            id = 1752887,
            score = 9,
            author = "579075",
            text = "When you turn in the quests at the end,\n\nif you have multiple ones to turn in at the same time you would have to wait for Cho to finish his stories.\n\nTo Bypass this, simply walk out of the room, mount up and fly into Mogu'Shan Palace, which is right below Cho's room.\n\nZone in, zone out, and Cho will have finished his story, repeat until all your quests are turned in !",
            date = "2012-10-28T23:21:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31100#comments:id=1752887",
        },
        {
            id = 1667070,
            score = 7,
            author = "Cielos",
            text = "You receive this quest in the mail from Lorewalker Cho after completing https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=6847.  He is located in the Mogu'shan Palace in the Vale of Eternal Blossoms.\n\nWhen you complete this quest, you will get the debuff https://www.wowhead.com/spell=120589 and hear the tale of the Yaungol.  If you miss some of it the first time, all you have to do is talk to Lorewalker Cho again and he will re-tell you it.",
            date = "2012-05-15T02:44:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31100#comments:id=1667070",
        },
        {
            id = 5788686,
            score = 1,
