    [31102] = {
        {
            id = 1700742,
            score = 12,
            author = "ArgentSun",
            text = "Here is the story of the Seven Burdens, told in a (relatively) short form.\n\nEmperor Shaohao, the last emperor of Pandaria, ruled the Pandaren sometime before the Sundering. Once, a great Jinyu Waterspeaker told him of a vision in which cataclysmic events would break the world. Shaohao, shaken by this prophecy, climbed Mount Neverest to seek advice from the Jade Serpent, one of the four godlike spirits of Pandaria. The vague response (\"... to divest himself of his burdens, to purify his spirit, and to become one with the land.\") brought him no wisdom.\n\nIt was soon after this event that Shaohao's companion, the Monkey King from the Jade Forest, decided to play a prank on the emperor and mockingly offered him a ridiculous bamboo \"mask of doubt.\" Miraculously, the mask forced all doubt to leave the emperor and manifest itself into a Sha of Doubt, which the two friends then defeated and buried after days of fighting. With the aid of another one of Pandaria's great spirits - the Red Crane - and the Mask of Despair, Shaohao and the Monkey King forced the Sha of Despair to leave the emperor's body, where they could fight and defeat it. Free of doubt and despair, the emperor sought out the Black Ox, with whose aid he and his friends defeated the Sha of Fear and imprisoned it in the earth. Empowered by his successes, Shaohao spoke with the last one of the great spirits, the White Tiger, whose wisdom taught the emperor the folly of anger. With the Monkey King's masks, the emperor and his allies summoned and defeated the Sha of Hatred, the Sha of Anger, and the Sha of Violence.\n\nWith the seven mighty Sha defeated, Shaohao charged a group of Pandaren warriors with the task of guarding Pandaria against the return of those creatures, for he knew that even defeated, they could come back if the negative emotions throughout the land sustained them enough. Those warriors became the monk brotherhood called Shado-Pan, and their oath was to stay eternally vigilant against the return of the Sha.\n\nNot too long after Shaohao had overcome his seven burdens, the Sundering began shaking the world. Unable to maintain his purity of spirit, Shaohao felt the Sha stir in their prisons as his own faith wavered. He once again sought advice from the Jade Serpent, and her words inspired him to give up his physical form and let his spirit become one with the land. Thus, even as the rest of the world heaved and shattered, Pandaria drifted away in the ocean, the mists formed of Shaohao's cloak protecting the land from all external threats...\n\nIf you wish to read the full story, or at least as much of it as the game provides us with, check out the following book objects:\n\nThe Book of Burdens, Chapter 1: The Quest Begins (/object=215799)\nThe Book of Burdens, Chapter 3: The Jade Serpent's Advice (/object=215797)\nThe Book of Burdens, Chapter 5: The Sha of Doubt (/object=213421)\nThe Book of Burdens, Chapter 9: The Sha of Despair (/object=213422)\nThe Book of Burdens, Chapter 14: The Sha of Fear (/object=213445)\nThe Book of Burdens, Chapter 19: The Sha of Hatred, Anger, and Violence (/object=213443)\nThe Shado-Pan (/object=213455)\nThe Sundering (/object=213456)",
            date = "2012-08-17T00:16:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31102#comments:id=1700742",
        },
        {
            id = 1883637,
            score = 10,
            author = "CallMeNoa",
            text = "Blizzard has turned this into a six part animated miniseries. See the first part here (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-D--GWwca0g).",
            date = "2013-08-03T14:22:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31102#comments:id=1883637",
        },
        {
            id = 1884554,
            score = 3,
            author = "Mellro",
            text = "This is currently being made into a series short videos that follow The Seven Burdens Of Shaohao. (http://us.battle.net/wow/en/blog/10534912/The_Burdens_of_Shaohao%E2%80%94Part_1_Doubt-8_5_2013) There are currently two videos up on the playlist (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-D--GWwca0g&list=PLY0KbDiiFYeNKrf7yg1O5KsHff-NdimhR), with a new video being posted each afternoon.  All videos are now up and you can see the complete legend of Emperor Shaohao,The Last Emperor of Pandaria.\n\nEach video is elegantly painted with beautiful watercolors right before your eyes as Lorewalker Cho (voiced by Jim Cummings) tells the story. It definitely fits the Asian themed Mists of Pandaria, and the style of the Lorewalkers in the way of which they tell their stories. I would love for blizzard to make a series of videos for all of the Lorewalker stories you can discover ingame. Personally, I would love to see The Ballad of Liu Lang (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31103) next after Shaohao. So far the videos have been very well recieved and interesting more people in some of the Pandaria lore characters. I would definitely recommend checking this out whether you like the lore or not, it's still great to watch. Good job, Blizzard!",
            date = "2013-08-06T15:12:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31102#comments:id=1884554",
        },
        {
            id = 5788684,
            score = 2,
            author = "Cekis",
            text = "If you're having trouble getting https://www.wowhead.com/npc=61962 to converse with you, step outside on the platform of the Seat of Knowledge and speak with https://www.wowhead.com/npc=163463 and ask to see the zone the way it used to be.  Once it changes, https://www.wowhead.com/npc=61962 will allow you to complete the quests.",
            date = "2024-02-19T01:52:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31102#comments:id=5788684",
        },
        {
            id = 1675389,
            score = 1,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "Starts from a quest item mailed to the player upon completion of the achievement The Seven Burdens of Shaonao (http://mop.wowhead.com/achievement=6855).\n\nWhen you turn in the quest, Lorewalker Cho tells you a story complete with a play-like reenactment and casts Storytime (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=120589) on the player.\n\"Ah!  You wish to learn of our last and greatest emperor, Shaohao?  My friend, I do not have the time here to recount all of his adventures, but his actions ten thousand years ago resonate to this very day.\n\nWe know that he purged his doubts in the Jade Forest.  That he cleansed himself of despair in the Krasarang Wilds.  That he overcame his fear in Townslong Steppes.  And that he defeated anger, hatred, and violence high in the mountains of Kun-Lai.\n\nThis is known; and there are temples to mark these most sacred of places.\n\nBut I want you to imagine standing in this very valley on the day he returned from his journey.  Imagine being here when the gates opened for him.  By then our emperor was a creature of pure light: No doubts, no fears, no hatred...\n\nIt is said that all the trees in the vale blossomed as he entered, and continue to blossom to this day.\n\nWould that we could all live like our most sacred emperor.  That we could put aside all our burdens and exist in harmony with the cosmos.  THAT, I believe, was his message to us... before he became one with the land, and hid Pandaria away from the terror of the Sundering.\n\nThank you, dear emperor.\"\n\nYou can have Lorewalker Cho tell the story again by talking to him or clicking on the book that is added to your bookcase in the Seat of Knowledge.",
            date = "2012-06-10T21:21:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31102#comments:id=1675389",
        },
    },
    [31103] = {
        {
            id = 1684245,
            score = 13,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "Starts from a quest item mailed to the player upon completion of the achievement Ballad of Liu Lang (http://mop.wowhead.com/achievement=6856).\n\nWhen you turn in the quest, Lorewalker Cho tells you a story complete with a play-like reenactment and casts Storytime (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=120589) on the player.\n\"When the Sundering ripped apart the continents of Azeroth, we pandaren thought that the rest of the world had been utterly destroyed. But as the centuries passed, one young explorer decided to see what was out there.  His name was Liu Lang.  And he set out to discover the world... on the back of a turtle!\n\nWe celebrate his bravery with statue and song, but if you were actually there on the beach that very day -- well I'm sure he looked quite silly, indeed.\n\nOh, how the pandaren laughed at him.  But Liu Lang was more clever than anyone thought.  Sea turtles always return to the beach where they were born.  And so, despite the mists that envelop our land, he always had a way home.\n\nEvery few years, he returned -- with tales of mysterious cities in the sand, nomadic people living on endless grassy plains, a great empire under the ice, and a magical kingdom gilded in gold.\n\nEach time he returned, more and more pandaren answered Liu Lang's call, and joined him on his growing turtle.  They were the bravest among us:  The explorers.  The adventurers.\n\nAnd that is the lesson of Liu Lang, my friend.  Everyone always laughs at the explorer.  They always laugh... until he returns.\"\n\nYou can have Lorewalker Cho tell the story again by talking to him or clicking on the book that is added to your bookcase in the Seat of Knowledge.",
            date = "2012-07-04T00:37:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31103#comments:id=1684245",
        },
        {
            id = 1736383,
            score = 12,
            author = "Louloudaki",
            text = "/way 83.22 29.68\nHe is over the dungeon entrance  in the building",
            date = "2012-10-09T06:09:53-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31103#comments:id=1736383",
        },
        {
            id = 1798962,
            score = 7,
            author = "Deihjan",
            text = "You can hear the song on Shen-zin Su as well, if you cross the bridge The Dawning Span and attend the Lorewalker's lesson below deck.\nLorewalker Amai will be telling the story of Liu Lang while her companion, Lorewalker Ruolin, sings the song.\n\nI'd always wondered why a Lorewalker would tell me about the lesson having just begun, when I never saw any text or any Lorewalkers in Morning Breeze, but today I decided to look closely around the bridge, and much to my surprise, I discovered a staircase that leads down that I had never noticed before.\n\nThus I was retold the story of Liu Lang, one of my favourite pieces of lore from MoP, and how the Wandering Isle pandaren all came to be. It also warmed my heart incredibly much that Chen and Li Li Stormstout were mentioned by one of the young pandaren cubs attending the lesson.\n\nI suggest any fan of the lore make a pandaren and attend the lesson, even if they have heard the story before, because the cubs add a special adorable flavour to the entire experience.",
            date = "2013-01-15T10:05:05-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31103#comments:id=1798962",
        },
        {
            id = 1695242,
            score = 2,
            author = "837800",
            text = "You can hear this song - http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FHM_yMCjkyc&feature=relmfu",
            date = "2012-08-02T11:47:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31103#comments:id=1695242",
        },
        {
            id = 3283352,
