    [31107] = {
        {
            id = 1763766,
            score = 2,
            author = "lionsofmercy",
            text = "The obvious: Ignore the little guys guarding the eggs and take out the Fear-Shapers first. Try to pick areas a little isolated from other groups so that when you're feared you don't pick up more attention.\n\nIn general, this area is like a lot of the rest of WoW: Come back when there are more people to help clear the area. The eggs respawn pretty quickly.\n\n(Everybody else is dying a lot too. It's not just you. ^^)",
            date = "2012-11-17T12:09:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31107#comments:id=1763766",
        },
        {
            id = 1798482,
            score = 1,
            author = "Eillesthis",
            text = "When you look at a map of the [zone=5842] (say if you're actually there), and you have quest objectives shown, this quest appears to take place in [zone=5841].  No, as you'd expect it takes place in the [zone=6138].  The game seems to know that it happens in the northern part of the zone, but since the actual location is right on the bottom edge of the map it shows it in the northern part of the wrong zone.",
            date = "2013-01-14T12:56:09-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31107#comments:id=1798482",
        },
    },
    [31108] = {
        {
            id = 1721509,
            score = 14,
            author = "QuickBASIC",
            text = "The https://www.wowhead.com/spell=128098 that https://www.wowhead.com/npc=62814 uses is miserable in this area because of the proximity of lots of other mobs. It can be interrupted or you can use stuns or silence to keep from pulling the whole area. They use it enough that using a https://www.wowhead.com/spell=42292 isn't going to cut it, although an Undead may have better luck because they have https://www.wowhead.com/spell=7744.",
            date = "2012-09-27T08:12:59-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31108#comments:id=1721509",
        },
        {
            id = 1747542,
            score = 10,
            author = "832945",
            text = "First of all the drop rate is in no way fixed and that goes for several quests in this zone.  And yes, the fear here is very miserable unless you're doing this as a group.\n\nAfter over 1500 quests I just don't have the patience anymore.",
            date = "2012-10-21T23:58:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31108#comments:id=1747542",
        },
        {
            id = 1784492,
            score = 5,
            author = "1062059",
            text = "There is a nice hiding spot @ 57, 11.  I laid in wait there for the varmits to re-spawn and eventually got what I needed.  Only one Dreadsworn patrolling that area.  Hope this helps!",
            date = "2012-12-20T06:59:28-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31108#comments:id=1784492",
        },
        {
            id = 1870932,
            score = 5,
            author = "941372",
            text = "As a druid, you can use Entangling Roots and spam Wrath. Their Fear won't reach if you entangle/wrath from a sufficient distance. Of course, then you have the misfortune of having about a (literal!) dozen other mobs ganging up on you.\n\nTHANK YOU!\n\nAs a resto druid with only 4 ranged spells, I was dreading this quest. But I did what you said and dragged the mobs to a desolate corner I cleared out, and didn't get feared once.",
            date = "2013-06-26T15:20:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31108#comments:id=1870932",
        },
        {
            id = 1763787,
            score = 3,
            author = "lionsofmercy",
            text = "(Don't forget to pick up your Klaxxi Enhancement first.)\n\nAs with much of WoW, hygiene helps--keep the area nice and clean. Your goal is to give yourself the safest possible area to be feared in.\n\nStay on the edge of the Horrid March (I was at 56, 16-20ish) and work from the outside in. Trim it of the Frightened Mushan, the little packs of Nagging Dreadlings and the Dread Lurkers. Not a bad plan to take out any Dreadsworn patrolling the perimeter. (Stay away from the blades; they won't follow as long as they do it.)\n\nThen kite your Fear-Shaper as close to this area as possible, and when Fear starts gearing up, run for the Horrid March like a scared little girl. (Before he makes you run like a scareder little girl, I mean. But hopefully you won't run into anything because you cleaned it out.) AoE the backup band as needed/wanted.\n\nMost of all, be patient. And no matter what, keep running back to the Horrid March perimeter. Worst case, it gives you an easier rez spot. :-)",
            date = "2012-11-17T12:56:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31108#comments:id=1763787",
        },
    },
    [31109] = {
        {
            id = 1727179,
            score = 122,
            author = "booster363",
            text = "The best way to get 40 kills is to look for https://www.wowhead.com/npc=62582 just south of the quest giver. They only have 118k HP and can easily be AOE'd down in large numbers. I recommend doing quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31502 first. You will get some kills from it.",
            date = "2012-10-01T08:32:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31109#comments:id=1727179",
        },
        {
            id = 1728079,
