    [31277] = {
        {
            id = 1750010,
            score = 164,
            author = "Tharama",
            text = "I just finish this quest now and... wow. Just wow. I wrote up what happens across the quest and will hide it for those not wanting to be spoiled. Enjoy.\n\n[spoiler]As you accept this quest, hundreds of Mogu appear and start besieging Niuzao Temple as well as the bridge across to it. You can easily fly over them but can also help relieve the emotionless NPC fighting them for no benefit ever then feeling better about yourself.\n\nWaiting for you on the south east side of the temple, on the path, are all nine of your daily quest companions and Ban Bearheart. After briefly speaking to him, he and the other nine companions will start advancing up the steps and into the besieged temple and find Shan Bu, safely inside a bubble channeling a dark looking spell into Niuzao who is acting stunned on the spot.\n\nOnce he notices you, Shan Bu goes into this (fully voiced, like the rest of the quest) speech:\n\nShan Bu yells: Ahahaha, the Great Niuzao, strength of the west, divine celestial, protector of the weak...\nShan Bu yells: Your charge, the sha of fear, has escaped.\nShan Bu yells: The mantid besiege you from all sides.\nShan Bu yells: You wield the powers of a god, but you are beaten!\nShan Bu yells: You bear the burden of an entire people upon your shoulders. And how have they repaid you?\nShan Bu yells: You are forgotten. This is what you fear, is it not?\nShan Bu yells: Lay your duties aside and rest.\nNizuao yells: I will NEVER yield!\nShan Bu yells: When you are dying, beast, remember that I gave you a choice.\nShan Bu yells: Shan-ze! Hei Feng! Kill him!\n\nAfter this, waves of https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63933 will come down from the north and west stairs to attack you. Meanwhile, https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63920 a heavenly wind serpent will bombard you from the air with Shadow Detonation. This does a moderate amount of damage and marks the ground with a red circle that you're supposed to step out of.\n\nAfter several waves of https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63933 and several emotes (https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63920 prepares to land! and https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63920 is landing!) https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63920 himself with land with the shout:\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=63920 yells: The storm will consume you!\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=63920 yells: I shall show you TRUE strength!\n\nAfter this, you and your band of heroes will fight the now grounded wind serpent in a rather easy fight. He will almost constantly use https://www.wowhead.com/spell=125990 which is an interruptible AoE knock for minor damage and, like most dragon, a deep breath. https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63920's deep breath is emoted before hand with \"https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63920 takes a Deep Breath! Move behind him!\" and hits in a very small frontal cone in front of him. I would also like to add he has the coolest breath I have ever seen. Ahem. Once he reaches 1% he'll become untargetable and goes:\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=63920 yells: No. NO!\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=63920 yells: Master, I have failed you...\n\nAnd then dies, allowing you to loot him. I got 1xhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=81194 :D.\n\nAfterwards, Niuzao returns to normality and thanks you:\n\nNiuzao yells: Thank you, . You have saved us all.\nNiuzao yells: Remember, it is at the darkest moment that light shines the brightest.\nNiuzao yells: Well done, heroes.\n\nThen he just stands there until you leave. Once you return to the Shado-Pan Garrison, your nine daily companions, Master Snowdrift and Ban Bearheart are standing in a half circle. After turning in the quest they induct you into the Shado-Pan formally:\n\nBan Bearheart says: Today, we welcome you into the Shado-Pan.\nBan Bearheart says: Your perseverance strengthens us. Your courage leads us. Your honor inspires us.\nBan Bearheart says: From this day forth, you walk as one of our brotherhood.\nYalia Songwhisper says: We knew you could do it!\nBan Bearheart says: Welcome , as a member of the Shado-Pan!\nLao-Chin the Iron Belly says: Good job. Guess you learned a little something from me.\nTaoshi says: Let's go for a drink!\nFei Li says: Drinks!\n\nAnd that's that. I hope you enjoyed writing this as much as I lost slept writing it and happy hunting to you all! :)\n\n[/spoiler]",
            date = "2012-10-25T05:51:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31277#comments:id=1750010",
        },
        {
            id = 1714850,
            score = 162,
            author = "Sere",
            text = "I believe you must become exalted with Shado-Pan to open this quest, since I could not see it until after I was.",
            date = "2012-09-17T02:38:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31277#comments:id=1714850",
        },
        {
            id = 1753453,
            score = 88,
            author = "Freezy3",
            text = "For anyone who was excited to get exalted like I was half way through dailies, and became sad when I couldn't find this quest at all. Make sure to finish the daily quests, the quest giver then was letting me start this chain. Hope this helps.",
            date = "2012-10-29T21:37:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31277#comments:id=1753453",
        },
        {
            id = 1756339,
            score = 66,
            author = "Esoth",
            text = "Feign death seems to cause everything to despawn.",
            date = "2012-11-03T15:02:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31277#comments:id=1756339",
        },
        {
            id = 1757666,
            score = 61,
            author = "Atratzu",
            text = "Tip for the quest:\n\nFor those of you who are aggro shy like myself. Do not feign death or vanish or any other method to lose aggro on NPC's. You'll just need to eat the damage because. (At least Feign death) resets the whole event.",
            date = "2012-11-05T13:29:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31277#comments:id=1757666",
        },
    },
    [31285] = {
        {
            id = 1853623,
            score = 17,
            author = "craftyard",
            text = "\"As long as we don't get out of the boat or make eye contact or get hit by a spear then we should be fine.\"\n\nHe said, as the boat was pelted with spears.",
            date = "2013-05-16T15:51:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31285#comments:id=1853623",
        },
        {
            id = 1768895,
            score = 9,
            author = "Sketchie",
            text = "When you approach Brewmaster Boof and Egg Shell, a very brief scene will occur.\n\nBrewmaster Boof says: Hey there. I don't think you want to go down that tunnel on foot. The saurok are out in force today and they are mighty territorial.\n\nOnce you accept The Spring Drifter quest, hop on the boat. Brewmaster Boof and Egg Shell will accompany you, and they will have a conversation on the way through the tunnel.\n\nBrewmaster Boof says: Ever been to Kun-Lai before? It's great. Long flowing farmlands. Beautiful mountains. And absolutely nothing dangerous whatsoever.\nEgg Shell says: Hozen attack grummles.\n\nWhile you are floating down the river through the cave, Saurok will be throwing spears at you, Brewmaster Boof and Egg Shell. They have really lousy aim however, and does not look like they hit even once throughout the entire ride.\n\nBrewmaster Boof says: Well... yes. There are problems with the hozen.\nEgg Shell says: Tigers.\nBrewmaster Boof says: Yes, and the tigers.\nEgg Shell says: Darkhatched saurok are very dangerous, and very powerful.\nBrewmaster Boof says: The spears are just for show. As long as we don't get out of the boat or make eye contact or get hit by a spear then we should be fine.\nEgg Shell says: Saurok are very dangerous.\nBrewmaster Boof says: It's safe. I bought Lorewalker Cho and his strange companions up this way not long back.\nEgg Shell says: The \"orc\" tried to punch me.\nBrewmaster Boof says: You had that coming. Waving your incense about in his face... wait a minute. Something doesn't feel right about this.\n\nBrewmaster Boof mentions something does not feel right once you exit the cave. On the way to Binan Village...\n\nBrewmaster Boof says: Are those refugees? What's going on over there? Do I hear fighting?\nBrewmaster Boof says: These people are farmers, not fighters! They may need our help!\n\nThe boat docks at the pier and all of you hop out.\n\nIt is likely the companions accompanying Lorewalker Cho through the cave earlier are General Nazgrim, Shademaster Kiryn, Shorkia and Rivett Clutchpop if you are playing as Horde.\n\nIf you are playing as Alliance, the quip between Brewmaster Boof and Egg Shell about the punch and incense will obviously be different. Since I don't play Alliance, I cannot really comment on this one.",
            date = "2012-11-27T15:44:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31285#comments:id=1768895",
        },
        {
            id = 1807236,
            score = 7,
            author = "Grobinder",
            text = "perhaps a reference to the patrol boat scenes in Apocalypse Now, with Lance waving the purple smoke bomb in Chief's face (the incense), arrow attack, and Chief getting hit by a spear.",
            date = "2013-01-31T13:08:32-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31285#comments:id=1807236",
        },
        {
            id = 1740846,
            score = 5,
            author = "JDLKY",
            text = "It appears that you can only take this boat ride once. God knows I tried everything possible to ride it a second time and failed. The other choices for getting into the zone after this one free trip are either grab the FP on the other side when doing the quest or make a tunnel dash.",
            date = "2012-10-13T21:08:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31285#comments:id=1740846",
        },
        {
            id = 1742968,
            score = 5,
            author = "jtbalogh",
            text = "Do not turn in this vanity quest if you want to have fun riding the boat through the tunnel again later. Luckily, I can get other quests in town without having to turn this in yet. Also handy to keep the boat and get back into Kun-Lai Summit just in case your hearth is in another zone and forget to get the flightpath here. If you are ever at the Veiled Stair, the questgiver can give you another boat when you abandon the quest.",
            date = "2012-10-16T01:12:13-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31285#comments:id=1742968",
        },
    },
    [31286] = {
        {
            id = 1719553,
            score = 46,
            author = "otakun85",
            text = "The blue marked quest area is on the west side of the road. But it's a cave underneath. The entrance of the cave is on the eastern side of the road.\nAnd it's not the cave in direction to the north. Thats the way to Kun-Lai Summit.",
            date = "2012-09-26T03:18:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31286#comments:id=1719553",
        },
        {
            id = 1720507,
            score = 21,
            author = "mournerslament",
            text = "Cave entrance at 55.70, 55.64",
            date = "2012-09-26T16:36:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31286#comments:id=1720507",
        },
        {
            id = 1752630,
            score = 13,
            author = "918850",
            text = "If you are wondering - like me - whether or not to skip this quest (kill a bunch of mobs I don't need in order to pick up some items and get to a mob I do need (educating saurok): after completing this and upon arrival in Binan Village, you will have mail from Madam Goya, informing you that you may use her services. Which is the Black Market AH close to the Tavern in the Mists. Maybe you can use the AH nonetheless, I don't know. Just thought it might be worth mentioning.\n\nEdit: So I went there on another toon and ignored this quest-giver. Continued on to Binan Village, flew back to the Tavern and checked the AH and I could use it. Thus,  you do not need to do these quests in order to use the AH.",
            date = "2012-10-28T14:08:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31286#comments:id=1752630",
        },
        {
            id = 3310007,
            score = 12,
            author = "Beoca",
            text = "This quest is currently only completable if you are at least level 30 due to the Black Market Merchandise for some reason requiring you to be level 30 before you pick them up (despite Kun-Lai Summit only requiring level 20).",
            date = "2021-03-20T10:17:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31286#comments:id=3310007",
        },
        {
            id = 1720322,
            score = 6,
            author = "Whiterock",
            text = "The Road to Kun-lai Quest Tree From Whiterock\n[pre][ins]#[/ins])Robbing Robbers of Robbers (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31286) [ins]#[/ins])Educating Saurok (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31287) [ins]#[/ins])The Spring Drifter (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31285)(The Veiled Stair)\n\n[ins]#[/ins])The Road to Kun-Lai (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31254){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31255)(Multiple zones)\n\n[ins]+[/ins])Hit Medicine (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30460) [ins]+[/ins])All of the Arrows (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30459) [ins]+[/ins])Call Out Their Leader (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30457)\n ├─────┬────────┴───────────────────┘         ||\n ||     ||                                    Turnabout (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30670)*\n || The Defense of Shado-Pan Fallback (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30665)*\n ||\n ├──────────────────────────────────────┐\na)Admiral Taylor has Awakened (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30506)(A,v2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30507),v3 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30508)) a)General Nazgrim has Awakened (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30509)(H,v2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30510),v3 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30511))\nb)Westwind Rest (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30512)(A)                     b)Eastwind Rest (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30513)(H)\n ||                   ┌──────────────────┘\nb)Challenge Accepted (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30514){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30515)\n || ||                 └───────────┬>c)Blue Dwarf Needs Food Badly (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30583)(A)\n || ├>c)Round 'Em Up (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30575){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31256)           ├>c)Best Meals Anywhere! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31251)(H)\n || └>d)Profiting off of the Past (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30595) └>d)Deanimate the Reanimated (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30593){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30594)\n ||\n ├───────────────────────────┐\nd)Mogu? Oh No-gu! (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30619){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30620)    e)Trouble on the Farmstead (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30569){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30570)\n ||                        /     \\\n ||       e)Farmhand Freedom (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30571)     e)... and the Pot, Too!  (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30581)\n ||                       └─┬───┬─┘\n || e)Back to Westwind Rest (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31252)(A) e)Back to Eastwind Rest (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31253)(H)\n ├─────────────────────────┴───┴─┬───────────────────┐\n ||                               ||                   ||\nf)In Tents Channeling (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30652){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30657)        f)Barrels of Fun (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30651){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30656) f)Pandaren Prisoners (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30650){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30655)\nf)The Ordo Warbringer (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30660){A2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30662),H1 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30661),H2 (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=30663)}  ||                   ||\n ||                           └─┬─┴─────────────────┬─┘\nMuskpaw Ranch (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31456){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31457)*              ├>The Shado-Pan (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31455){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31453)* ├>The Missing Merchant (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31452){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31451)*\n                               └>Beyond the Wall (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31695)*  └>Cho's Missive (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31460){H} (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31459)*\nLegend:\n+ means Can start anytime, prequests not needed.\n# means Other Zones\n(A)/(H) means Alliance/Horde only.\n{H} means Quest Have Horde Variant, click {H} for it.\n* means another Quest Tree.[/pre]\nAdditionall info:\n\nYes, Shado-pan questline have such weird prequests :D\nAwakened quests have 3 version of quests each starting from NPC that gave you previous quests.\nOrdo Warbringer have quest that starts via pop-up after Channelers and backup from Taylor/Nazgrim if you abandon first.",
            date = "2012-09-26T14:54:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31286#comments:id=1720322",
        },
    },
    [31287] = {
        {
            id = 1719242,
            score = 57,
            author = "731709",
            text = "I didn't find him at the cave entrance. Although I  think his actual location somewhat corresponds to the cave entrance at the top of the trail. He's not up top. I spent alot of time looking there for him!\n\nWhen you receive the quest from Len, face downhill and bear left going around the corner once it allows you to do so. Keep bearing left and you should come around to face the area underneath the trail you just road down. You should now be facing the entrance to the burrow. As a bonus - this is also where the Robbing Robbers of Robbers quest is at.\n\nEnter the burrow and head to the back of it. He's near the back somewhat in the middle. You may have to wait for him to spawn, but he regens fairly quick. I ended up using a targeting macro to help me locate him. Just a simple /tar Leechfingers will do it. And depending any addons you are using, you may see a marker on your map showing you where to go once you get in range for the macro.",
            date = "2012-09-25T21:53:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31287#comments:id=1719242",
        },
        {
            id = 1718571,
