        {
            id = 1769404,
            score = 61,
            author = "ramrad",
            text = "Once you are in the cave there are three possible bugs that can happen:\n1. Exit it blocked. Solution: Have to hearth out when quest is completed.\n2. Fish disappears. Solution: Relog.\n3. Grey ? over the treasure chest after you kill the big spider. Solution: Fish has to be present when you kill the spider. If she is not, follow step 2, wait for the spider to respawn and kill it again.\nAll these bugs happened to me so that's how I know >.<",
            date = "2012-11-28T00:27:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31314#comments:id=1769404",
        },
        {
            id = 1698310,
            score = 27,
            author = "TheStatman",
            text = "Listening to Fish Fellreed's story, she talks about a lost map, https://www.wowhead.com/item=86404 is this map, which is found in Valley of the Four Winds, and which starts a quest. The Map quest will eventually lead to getting this quest and going into the blocked off cave in the North of the zone.",
            date = "2012-08-10T12:39:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31314#comments:id=1698310",
        },
        {
            id = 1746052,
            score = 27,
            author = "silveropal3",
            text = "Well my problems seemed to have populated at the end of the quest.\n\nI killed the fish to get the map, handed the map in, went and talked to the people to figure out the clues, went back to Fish and then finally went to find the entrance to the cave.\n\nI was able to click on the rocks and they fell to rubble.  I stealthed thru the whole cave until the end because I didn't feel like killing any of the spiders.  When I got to the end of the cave I could see https://www.wowhead.com/item=86428 and a big spider that needed to be killed.  Surprisingly the spider was easy to kill even tho I'm a resto druid.  The spider rains some stuff that doesn't hit very hard and slows your movement by throwing a web over you...no biggie.\n\nAfter I killed the spider I clicked on the chest and looted https://www.wowhead.com/item=86428.\nI stealthed back to the beginning of the cave but I couldn't click on the rubble to exit the cave.\nI logged off then back in b/c I thought maybe it was having that problem where you couldn't interact with certain items unless you logged.\n\nBut nope that wasn't the problem.  Logged back in and still couldn't click on the cave entrance rubble.\n\nI ended up hearthing and then flying back to Half Hill.\n\nP.S.\nI had trouble finding where https://www.wowhead.com/npc=64314 was so to make it easy for you:\n\n1.  Find where https://www.wowhead.com/npc=64597 house is and face the entrance.\n2.  Turn to your left and you will see a bush covering up the cave entrance.\n\nWho knew there was a cave in Half Hill?  Not me.",
            date = "2012-10-19T23:24:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31314#comments:id=1746052",
        },
        {
            id = 1762879,
            score = 21,
            author = "Balgair",
            text = "Word of warning to those who might do what I did and rush in thinking the spiders don't look that bad - they actually hit kinda hard if you've got two big ones spitting 20k hits at you every second or so and three little ones stacking up a poison that ends up also ticking for 20k+. Yes, I died, and yes, it was embarrassing, luckily nobody else was there to see :-P Lesson learned and it was fine when I actually took care with my pulls - for stealth classes I recommend just using your skills to avoid the fights entirely!",
            date = "2012-11-15T14:54:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31314#comments:id=1762879",
        },
    },
