    [31487] = {
        {
            id = 1728331,
            score = 9,
            author = "569550",
            text = "After you finish this quest, you keep the Sonic Disruption Fork. WIth it, you can easily take down dread kuchongs in like 5 seconds, and they are worth 17 rep towards the Black Prince. Rounding up mobs with 1-3 dread kunchongs as a plate class and tearing thru them will get you the 6k rep for the Black Prince quest in no time.",
            date = "2012-10-02T06:07:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31487#comments:id=1728331",
        },
        {
            id = 1727653,
            score = 7,
            author = "Hvitur",
            text = "I'm not sure if this is actually how it is, but I seemed to only get credit for killing the kuchong after it killed the manipulators around it. If it died before the manipulators, I didn't receive credit.",
            date = "2012-10-01T15:38:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31487#comments:id=1727653",
        },
        {
            id = 1748265,
            score = 7,
            author = "pmakaro",
            text = "One of many quests in Pandaria that currently leaves the item in your bags after the quest is completed.\n\nHere is a list of some of the quests and their items that remain after completion.\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=80484 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30634\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=87394 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31487\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=87841 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31507\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=87400 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31496\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=89366 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30341 (Thanks Ungluck)\n\nIn addition to the above provided quest items that stick around the following are some quest items that can be over looted and extras may remain.\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=88855 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31713 (Thanks Eighjan)\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=79864 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30329\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=87401 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31502\n\nIn all these cases the provided item or the extra looted items are safe to delete after the quest is complete.",
            date = "2012-10-22T21:36:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31487#comments:id=1748265",
        },
        {
            id = 1820900,
            score = 2,
            author = "yarko",
            text = "If it died before the manipulators, I didn't receive credit.\n\nThis happened to me too. I aggroed everything, hit the disrupting fork, and while I was killing the manipulators, the kunchong died somehow and I didn't get credit.\n\nI have found that the easiest way to do this quest is to make sure that the disruptor waves hit the kunchong without getting any aggro. When that happens, he kills his captors himself, then just sits there waiting for you to kill him. The radius of the fork is pretty big, so I think most kunchong can be hit without aggroing any of the associated manipulators. The waves don't agro themselves, as far as I can tell. So just keep inching forward until it hits the kunchong. If not, just kill one of the manipulators and then the waves will hit the kunchong for sure. Make sure that you keep up the Sonic Disruption debuff that the disrupting fork gives him by redoing the fork, and run out of his Dread Slash if you don't have a lot of health because, even weakened, it still hits pretty hard.",
            date = "2013-03-04T13:19:10-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31487#comments:id=1820900",
        },
        {
            id = 1738647,
            score = 1,
            author = "fai1",
            text = "I had an issue where the quest counter stopped at 3 out of 4 killed, even though I killed at least 8. They just weren't counting. Didn't matter if I killed the kunchong before or after the manipulators.   Relogging did the trick. After I restarted wow, the kills started counting again & I could finish the quest.",
            date = "2012-10-11T15:55:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31487#comments:id=1738647",
        },
    },
    [31490] = {
    },
    [31492] = {
        {
            id = 1763846,
            score = 1041,
            author = "seitori",
            text = "This quest is a quick way to get exalted with the Sha of Anger.",
            date = "2012-11-17T15:12:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31492#comments:id=1763846",
        },
        {
            id = 1766373,
            score = 364,
            author = "1050978",
            text = "How to do this quest:\n\nIt took me about a billion tries to figure it all out, but there is a predictable and mostly safe path you can take.  Once you have the path, it's mostly cake.\n\nThe route is split into four parts.  Part one is the easiest, but I'll give my route for all of it.\n\nREAD ALL OF IT.  There are rest areas between each part except for part 3 and part 4, so make sure you understand what to do at part 4.\n\nPart 1: Gentle Slope\n\n1. Grab your torch.  Stay on the pagoda steps, and move to the extreme right.  When the path is clear on the RIGHT, move forward, hugging right, up and over the hill.\n\n  1.a) On the way, you'll pass a fast tornado that follows the path up and down.  If you know where it is, you'll know when it's safe to cross.  Remember that it can come up behind you.\n\n2.  After the hill, cross the path to the LEFT side when it is safe (see 1.a)).  Avoid the slow tornado going left and right, and move to the building. Move along the outside of the building for the next part.\n\nPart 2:  Steep Hill\n\nThe key to this one is to stay outside the chain.  I think this is harder for big avatars (i.e. easier for gnomes than tauren) but even a big Draenai can do this.\n\n3. Starting OUTSIDE the chain, on the LEFT side, go all the way up the hill.  You can probably come back inside at the third-last post or later.  Remember there's at least two tornadoes coming up behind you, but the most important ones are the ones going left to right.  Continue hugging left until you're on the stairs.  Go through the building and get ready for part 3.\n\nPart 3: Bridge\n\nThere are three lanes.  You need to wait until the center lane is halfway staggered with the left lane (the left tornado will already be halfway down by the time the center tornado reaches the top).\n\n4.  Start when the CENTER tornado leaves the closest part of the bridge.  Follow the CENTER tornado.  After the LEFT tornado has passed you on its way down, switch lanes to the LEFT lane.\n\n   4.a) How much time and space you have from switching between center and left lanes depends on how perfectly the lanes were staggered.  Once you have switched to left lane, you may have a great deal of time (say, 10+ seconds) or only a few seconds before you MUST move to phase 4, depending on how it was staggered.  I don't recommend waiting too long.\n\nPart 4:  Flat area and stairs\n\n5.  When you get to the top of the bridge, STOP at the gold line.  There are two tornadoes in front of you.  Wait until they are both passing you to the RIGHT, then move LEFT, hugging the left wall, as fast as you can.\n\n  5.a) REMEMBER:  You have left-lane tornado from part 3 coming up behind you, center-lane tornado possibly beside you, and two tornadoes in front of you.  If you don't move fast enough, either the center-lane will come up and hit you, or the first one going left and right will bounce and hit you from the right side before you're clear.\n\n6.  After you have made it past the two tornadoes, continue in a circle, hugging the wall to the LEFT, keeping an eye out for stray tornadoes.  You will pass a small staircase.  Cross it, climbing over the railing.  Then climb over the railing of the big staircase, and turn left, going up the staircase.\n\nClick the big fire at the end.  MAKE CERTAIN YOU HAVE THE QUEST COMPLETE since if other people complete it at the same time, you might THINK you have it finished but only THEY actually got the complete.\n\nFly back down to the quest giver and finish your quest.",
            date = "2012-11-22T16:24:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31492#comments:id=1766373",
        },
        {
            id = 1739860,
            score = 207,
            author = "olania",
            text = "While the tornadoes move predictably, you can't predict when you're going to get across the last bridge and the torch is randomly going to get blown out by nothing - no tornado, no wind wall, nothing.\n\nSo yeah, Blizzard can take this quest and stuff it. I'll just take a little longer to get exalted with the August Celestials.",
            date = "2012-10-12T19:50:05-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31492#comments:id=1739860",
        },
        {
            id = 1739769,
            score = 94,
            author = "321618",
            text = "The easiest way to navigate this quest, is to simply walk along the outside of the left chain railings. You can walk along the chains if you feel so inclined, but it is definitely the simplest way.",
            date = "2012-10-12T17:27:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31492#comments:id=1739769",
        },
        {
            id = 1764305,
            score = 84,
            author = "ArrynHellfire",
            text = "Now I know where https://www.wowhead.com/item=88801 is being used for...",
            date = "2012-11-18T12:25:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31492#comments:id=1764305",
        },
    },
    [31493] = {
        {
            id = 1701297,
            score = 7,
            author = "1020453",
            text = "Simply accept the quest in the Scarlet Halls, fight your way through the dungeon, kill the endboss (Flameweaver Koegler) and loot his corpse to obtain the questitem. Then return to the questgiver and hand the quest in\nThis is the lowlevel-version of this quest. The level-90-version will reward you with blue items.\n\nAnyway, the quest title implies that the questgiver doesn't want the book just for safekeeping but also for his own purposes.\nMaybe we just made things even worse...",
            date = "2012-08-18T09:20:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31493#comments:id=1701297",
        },
        {
            id = 2140929,
            score = 4,
            author = "1259200",
            text = "The name of this quest might be a reference to The Lord of the Rings, where Sam tells Frodo he took the ring from him because he thought Shelob the giant spider killed him. \"Just for safekeeping, of course\".",
            date = "2015-03-21T06:21:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31493#comments:id=2140929",
        },
    },
    [31494] = {
        {
            id = 1727346,
            score = 43,
            author = "1038854",
            text = "Just had this daily and it is a nightmare.\n\nA few tips/tricks:\n\n50%+ of the cages are bugged.  If you see a sparkling bug in a cage ignore it.  Those ones are bugged and they will never give you a quest objective.\n\nDoors will spawn on the empty cages.  These are what you need to click to get credit for the quest.  They have a 6 minute respawn timer each.\n\nI recommend getting a group together (the credit is shared) and camp a few of the empty cages until the doors spawn.",
            date = "2012-10-01T11:04:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31494#comments:id=1727346",
        },
        {
            id = 1727413,
            score = 28,
            author = "lightclaw",
            text = "This quest is completed by opening the cages that contain kuchong hatchlings.  Only cages with hatchlings count, and the bug that plagued the quest at the beginning of the expansion has been fixed.\n\nThe problem was because of druids in flight form.\n\nWhen a druid in flight form opens a door, the hatchling doesn't escape.  The door's respawn appears to be tied to the hatchling leaving the cage rather than the door being opened, so it doesn't respawn until the game resets the hatchling.  If a druid opens the door while in flight form BUT the druid is on the ground, the quest goes as intended.  The problem is that this is what druids do all the time on quests like this, so the problem will only get worse with time.\n\nUpdate: Blizzard repaired the quest in early October.  The daily now only counts those cages that contain a baby, and the baby is freed properly regardless of who opens the cage or how.  Opening an empty cage no longer rewards progress toward finishing the quest.",
            date = "2012-10-01T12:15:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31494#comments:id=1727413",
        },
        {
            id = 1727203,
            score = 8,
            author = "Kryhs",
            text = "The respawn rate is really low, and sometimes the hatchlings don't always fly out of the cages when opened so there isn't a good way to know which cages are usable short of hovering over each of them. I'm sure it'll get patched, but this daily is pretty terrible if the area is busy.\n\nBest of luck.",
            date = "2012-10-01T08:52:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31494#comments:id=1727203",
        },
        {
            id = 1727479,
            score = 8,
            author = "284961",
            text = "Confound these bugged bug dailies!",
            date = "2012-10-01T13:11:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31494#comments:id=1727479",
        },
        {
            id = 1727513,
            score = 6,
            author = "Cakemonster",
            text = "Almost all of the cages are bugged - I camped out at the one by the \"Cycle of the Mantid\" lore object.\n\nI ran a timer between when I clicked the cage to free the hatchling inside, until it spawns. My first cage was about five minutes and thirty seconds. The second release was six minutes, the third was seven minutes and twenty two seconds, and the fourth was almost eight minutes.\n\nI'd estimate it's somewhere between five and eight minutes.\n\nI think the best bet would be to get a group of people and camp multiple cages - it'll take you upwards of thirty minutes to do this by yourself on one cage, not to mention the other people with this daily trying to steal the Kunchong that you're trying to release.\n\nGood luck!",
            date = "2012-10-01T13:47:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31494#comments:id=1727513",
        },
    },
    [31495] = {
        {
            id = 2292750,
            score = 2,
            author = "Franknol",
            text = "There is also a level 31 version the this quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31490, you need to go to Normal Scarlet Halls to get it",
            date = "2015-12-28T10:22:34-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31495#comments:id=2292750",
        },
    },
    [31496] = {
        {
            id = 1738195,
            score = 502,
            author = "Eaglesight",
            text = "Here is a picture that might come to help.\n\nhttp://localhostr.com/files/IqFlC4m/sampling-the-empires-finest.jpg\nA second mirror if localhostr is down: http://img716.imageshack.us/img716/4307/samplingtheempiresfines.jpg",
            date = "2012-10-11T06:28:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31496#comments:id=1738195",
        },
        {
            id = 1739061,
            score = 84,
            author = "Xabidar",
            text = "Tomtom macro for locations to each entrance:\n\n/way 38.3 31.9 East\n/way 36.2 32.2 North\n/way 37.0 28.0 Central\n/way 39.3 29.2 Northeast",
            date = "2012-10-12T01:28:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31496#comments:id=1739061",
        },
        {
            id = 1727137,
            score = 49,
            author = "1038785",
            text = "The entries of each feeder:\n\n~36,32\n~37,28\n~38,31\n~39,29\n\nYou only have to walk down the stairs and you will find the feeder.\n(2 mobs inside btw)",
            date = "2012-10-01T07:49:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31496#comments:id=1727137",
        },
        {
            id = 1728154,
            score = 28,
            author = "sorceressdee",
            text = "1- Find the right hut - they look slightly different from the other huts, and if you fly up to their entrance you should be able to see stairs going down inside them.\n2- Go into the hut, down the stairs\n3- kill the 2 mobs and gather the sap (1 click, doesnt require channeling).\n\nHere's a map  (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=6138:396293384312373281357316)to the entrances.",
            date = "2012-10-02T01:39:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31496#comments:id=1728154",
        },
        {
            id = 1742737,
            score = 17,
            author = "jjanchan",
            text = "After someone clicks a feeder, it goes on a \"cooldown\" of sorts, preventing anyone else from clicking on it to get quest credit.  If it is glittering for you but you cannot click it, coming back later or waiting for a minute or so should allow you to interact with it.",
            date = "2012-10-15T18:05:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31496#comments:id=1742737",
        },
    },
    [31497] = {
