    [31609] = {
        {
            id = 1745576,
            score = 127,
            author = "lightclaw",
            text = "The three boss mobs spawn near groups of Klaxxi Primes -\n\nShox'tik (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=66784) is a mantid who spawns at 41.6, 40.0, at the southern end of the questing area.  If you are using Raining Blood then stunning it out of its Rapid Fire ability is trivial.\n\nAkkolon (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=66783) is a kuchong who spawns at 44.6, 35.2, across the road from the entrance to the Heart of Fear in the middle of the questing area.  Don't get hit by its slam.\n\nManifestation of Terror (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=66785) is a sha that spawns at 43.8, 29.4, at the northern end of the questing area.\n\nTheir spawns seem to be on a timer, as the first of them was already near death when I came upon it and I was forced to wait on the other two.  At most, only one will be up at any time, and it takes a few minutes for the next to spawn.\n\nI would use Raining Blood for this as the frequent AoE stuns are very useful.  None of the blue Klaxxi Augments are useful.  Painkiller might be your best bet since Battle Hymn doesn't work for these mobs, but it doesn't really matter.",
            date = "2012-10-19T09:58:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31609#comments:id=1745576",
        },
        {
            id = 1739658,
            score = 102,
            author = "elcius",
            text = "You turn the quest in back at Klaxxi'vess",
            date = "2012-10-12T15:11:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31609#comments:id=1739658",
        },
        {
            id = 1761426,
            score = 41,
            author = "663363",
            text = "Ok....this is what I noticed today.....not only will the three mobs constantly spawn on a rotating basis.....the friendly NPC's will also kill the mob with no intervention from you or anyone else.....an easy way to do this is if you have the time.....just hover over the current mob that is up and when the three friendly NPC's get it down to about 300k health.....just swoop in for a killing blow......Manifestation of Terror killed me twice before I noticed what was going on.....hope this helps some out...there is about 2 minutes between one mob going down and the next one spawning....",
            date = "2012-11-12T12:32:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31609#comments:id=1761426",
        },
        {
            id = 2580257,
            score = 31,
            author = "Graysmith",
            text = "If you're doing this quest with flying unlocked, it seems that the named elites you have to kill don't spawn unless you're nearby and on the ground. I spent a good long while flying back and forth in the area and nothing was happening at all. As soon as I touched down near where they were supposed to be, they spawned.",
            date = "2018-07-12T17:42:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31609#comments:id=2580257",
        },
        {
            id = 1747569,
            score = 18,
            author = "Brainsnack",
            text = "As a ranged class, hunter, the only small problem I ran into were when facing the Sha.\n\nShox'tik (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=66784) was basically tank and spank. He will do his volley, but the damage is nothing to be concerned about.\n\nManifestation of Terror (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=66785) has a damaging AoE ability where the ground will begin to smoke and getting caught in it will slow you down. He also pulls players back towards him when they are 30+ yards away from him (I got caught just flying passed him on my mount). This can become deadly when he has just cast the smokey ground AoE, because of the damage being done as you're being pulled in and also when trying to get out while being slowed. The damage seems to be less or maybe even zero closer to the center. So stand within 30 yards of the NPC and, when the ground starts to smoke, move in closer.\n\nAkkolon (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=66783) has a 3s cast slash that will damage players in a frontal cone. He will regularly place geysers (orange pools) underneath players. He will do a couple in a short period, but the damage is avoidable if you keep moving out of them for the short duration.\n\nWith all these fights you are helping out Klaxxi NPCs, who will do most of the tanking. After you kill one of the boss mobs, the next one will spawn within seconds and a message in chat will announce the arrival of it. If you have quest objectives shown on your minimap, the golden arrow will point you to where the mob is, although they are all in the same general area. The order in which the mobs spawn is random.\n\nNote: When fighting the boss mobs, the spell icon for the Klaxxi enhancement I was using disappeared. It reappeared after the mob was killed and I returned to killing normal mantid.",
            date = "2012-10-22T00:32:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31609#comments:id=1747569",
        },
    },
    [31611] = {
        {
            id = 1700763,
            score = 142,
            author = "Zillions",
            text = "This quest instructs you to complete the [zone=6426] scenario.  Killing the final NPC https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63528 as part of the scenario will grant you quest credit.",
            date = "2012-08-17T02:21:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31611#comments:id=1700763",
        },
        {
            id = 1824232,
            score = 31,
            author = "gardenbearz",
            text = "This quest is one of several in MoP that require that you enter a scenario to do the quest; for this particular quest it is the Brewmoon Festival Scenario.  Although the quest is picked up outside of the scenario, the npc for the turn in, Brewmaster Boof, is there in the scenario and you turn in to him before leaving.",
            date = "2013-03-08T02:03:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31611#comments:id=1824232",
        },
        {
            id = 2084709,
            score = 23,
            author = "pelicanus",
            text = "Can you do this scenario at level100?",
            date = "2015-01-08T06:03:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31611#comments:id=2084709",
        },
        {
            id = 2151023,
            score = 20,
            author = "509794",
            text = "I couldn't figure out how to set the village defenses and the comments here weren't very helpful (\"use the things they give you\"- what? what things? who gives it to me?) but I finally figured it out. I was confused because I got Briaw Shan, the big pandaren who throws barrels. You get him to throw barrels at certain points and somehow they provide defense because magic.\n\nYou only get ten of them but if you place them right on the groups of villagers in fighting stance you can just sit back and let the villagers do all the fighting while the defenses you placed do all the damage. At one point a really big guy comes out and you might need to help fight him, but mostly I was running around and all the enemy mobs were already dead by the time I got there.\n\nYou might get other defensive weapons to place. I think it's random, but the other one I got was barrels that I placed myself. They are easy to find because they have gear icons over them.",
            date = "2015-04-02T00:46:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31611#comments:id=2151023",
        },
        {
            id = 3233867,
            score = 13,
            author = "Kiewan",
            text = "This scenario in Pandaria needs to be started through https://www.wowhead.com/npc=78709. He is located in [zone=5840]",
            date = "2020-09-29T00:31:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31611#comments:id=3233867",
        },
    },
    [31612] = {
        {
            id = 1736793,
            score = 212,
            author = "Karadine",
            text = "Kil'ruk the Wind-Reaver gives you the \"big reveal\" of [faction=1337] during this quest chain which you are given upon reaching exalted:\n[spoiler]Kil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: Wakener, your deeds have earned you the trust of the Klaxxi.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: You are to be rewarded. Walk with me.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: We mantid are an elder race. The pandaren you associate with - they are but children. They have their role to play.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: Each cycle, our young swarm their walls. The pandaren slay the weak. The strong return.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: With each generation, we grow ever stronger.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: Before your history began, our empire was vast. We shared this world with our sister kingdoms, Ahn'Qiraj and Azjol-Nerub.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: Our Gods were many, and powerful. We mantid worshipped the seven heads of Y'shaarj.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: Great was the Old One, and terrible was His wrath. He consumed hope and begat despair; He inhaled courage and breathed fear.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: When the usurpers came - the ones you call \"Titans\" - Y'shaarj was destroyed.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: His last terrible breath has haunted this land ever since, but the shadows he left behind are mere whispers of his former glory.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: I tell you now, because you have earned this warning.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: Your gods are not your gods, outsider.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: If the Old Ones ever return, we mantid will once again stand by their side.\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver says: The wisest among you will do the same.[/spoiler]",
            date = "2012-10-09T16:43:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31612#comments:id=1736793",
        },
        {
            id = 1764762,
            score = 157,
            author = "671293",
            text = "For any non-super nerds out there this is a Star Wars reference to the chapter between \"Empire Strikes Back\" and \"Return of the Jedi.\" There was never a movie but it did get made into one of the most awesome Nintendo 64 games ever (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wO41M1Ap63o)!\n\nOh, and you need to be exalted with [faction=1337] and earn the https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7312 achievement to start the questline for this. Just in case that's what you're really reading the comments for.\n\n***Why all the downvotes? I'm just trying to be helpful here.***",
            date = "2012-11-19T10:45:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31612#comments:id=1764762",
        },
        {
            id = 1775265,
            score = 130,
            author = "whsocko",
            text = "Kil'ruk runs away after telling his story.  You have to leave the cave and find him at his normal spot outdoors in order to complete the quest.",
            date = "2012-12-04T06:10:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31612#comments:id=1775265",
        },
        {
            id = 1866496,
            score = 98,
            author = "Velasco",
            text = "Just on a little side note. After several years one of the greatest mysteries is solved!\nWe get to know the correct pronunciation of Ahn'Qiraj and Azjol'Nerub.\n\nAhn'Qiraj [ɑːnˌkɪərˈɑːʃ] = ahn-ki-rash\nAzjol'Nerub [ɑːʃɵlˌnɛˈruːb] = Ashol-Ne-roob",
            date = "2013-06-14T06:32:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31612#comments:id=1866496",
        },
        {
            id = 1760775,
            score = 90,
            author = "Cielos",
            text = "There are four incubating eggs in the room where Kil'ruk the Wind-Reaver takes you. I'm curious to see what will happen, especially now that I know they're involved with the Old Gods.",
            date = "2012-11-11T09:04:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31612#comments:id=1760775",
        },
    },
    [31656] = {
        {
            id = 1696754,
            score = 115,
            author = "Karadine",
            text = "https://www.wowhead.com/npc=62112 ends several breadcrumb quests offered to players as soon as they reach level 89 in order for them to begin questing in Dread Wastes. For a lot of players, its not intuitive how to reach her because she is located on the Serpent's Spine and on the border between zone maps. Here is a full guide:\n\nFrom [zone=5841] (quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31847):\nTalk to the flightmaster https://www.wowhead.com/npc=61512 that gives this quest and fly to \"Serpent's Spine, Vale of the Eternal Blossoms\". Alternately, you can ride to Shado-Pan Fallback, enter the doors and ascend the staircase to the top of the wall, you can then ride southward to get there.\n\nFrom [zone=5842]:\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=31895 - Return to Shado-Pan Garrison, talk to the flightmaster https://www.wowhead.com/npc=62909 and fly to \"Serpent's Spine, Vale of the Eternal Blossoms\".\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=31656 - This quest seems to be bugged and might not give the correct flightpath (and the text doesn't even mention flying to her). You can either drop it and take one of the alternate breadcrumbs listed here (closest is https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31000), or ride to the Dread Wastes, going to the northeast corner of the zone to the Terrace of Gurthan. Next to the wall is a very small coil of Shado-Pan Rope that you can click on to ascend to the Serpent's Spine where you can reach Bowmistress Li (and also learn that flight path).\n\nFrom [zone=5840] (quests https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31390/https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31391):\nTaking your faction's quest adds the flight path you need. Talk to the flightmaster in your city and fly to \"Serpent's Spine, Vale of the Eternal Blossoms\".\n\nFrom [zone=6138] (quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31000):\nTaking this quest adds the flight path you need. Talk to the flightmaster https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63500 at The Sunset Brewgarden and fly to \"Serpent's Spine, Vale of the Eternal Blossoms\".",
            date = "2012-08-06T10:39:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31656#comments:id=1696754",
        },
        {
            id = 1720772,
            score = 52,
            author = "hildibrandr",
            text = "They should really make the rope glow.\n\nIt's located at 75,21 in Dread Wastes, next to the opposite wall of where the spiders are trying to climb up.",
            date = "2012-09-26T20:46:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31656#comments:id=1720772",
        },
        {
            id = 1701573,
            score = 30,
            author = "Emmaleah",
            text = "I was not offered this quest.  I suspect it is because I have better dread than dead.  (which is the leadin from Kun-Lai to talk to Brewmistress Li.)",
            date = "2012-08-19T03:05:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31656#comments:id=1701573",
        },
        {
            id = 1711232,
            score = 23,
            author = "220666",
            text = "The fastest way to get up here, that I have seen is to ride in from Towlong Steppes, there is a bridge at 60,84.  Between Rensai's Watchpost and Dusklight Hollow.\n\nYou ride all the way to the north east of the Spider Ruins/Terrace of Gurthan in the Dread Wastes, at 75.10,21.10 there is a rolled up rope on the ground next to the wall.  It's called a Shado-Pan Rope.  You can click it then climb up the wall to end the quest.",
            date = "2012-09-09T00:52:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31656#comments:id=1711232",
        },
        {
            id = 1734029,
            score = 18,
            author = "manleyart",
            text = "FAIL, FAIL, FAIL!\n\nI can't stand quests like this. This harks back to vanilla WoW. The rope isn't mentioned in the quest. The rope is not sparkling so you can see it. Minor annoyance but those are the worst kind. Simple crap that should be simple.",
            date = "2012-10-07T02:41:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31656#comments:id=1734029",
        },
    },
    [31660] = {
        {
            id = 1732236,
            score = 4,
            author = "1008695",
            text = "As long as you don't have the angel of death debuff that lasts for a minute, Kil'ruk the Wind-Reaver will drop down and kill the mobs you're fighting.  He can only come once a minute though.",
            date = "2012-10-05T11:35:57-05:00",
