        },
    },
    [31713] = {
        {
            id = 1760655,
            score = 8,
            author = "pmakaro",
            text = "One of many quests in Pandaria that currently leaves the item in your bags after the quest is completed.\n\nHere is a list of some of the quests and their items that remain after completion.\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=80484 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30634\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=87394 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31487\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=87841 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31507\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=87400 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31496\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=89366 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30341 (Thanks Ungluck)\n\nIn addition to the above provided quest items that stick around the following are some quest items that can be over looted and extras may remain.\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=88855 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31713 (Thanks Eighjan)\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=79864 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=30329\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=87401 for https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31502\n\nIn all these cases the provided item or the extra looted items are safe to delete after the quest is complete.",
            date = "2012-11-11T03:16:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31713#comments:id=1760655",
        },
        {
            id = 1731291,
            score = 7,
            author = "626418",
            text = "Don't panic, there's plenty of kegs around (head to the back), you won't have to loot them one by one!",
            date = "2012-10-04T14:23:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31713#comments:id=1731291",
        },
        {
            id = 1749635,
            score = 4,
            author = "squiretoad",
            text = "Well, this is another totally BS quest.  There are a VERY few mugs scattered about, and a DAMNED lot of irate easily aggro'ed monkeys.  Plus all these misguided little dragons who will get aggro'ed in a heartbeat, so you end up fighting them too!  ALL of them die damned hard, I've been here screwing around in this stupid cave for an hour now, have 40 mugs, I've died THREE times (until I learned to just run away when mobbed, abandoning my hunter pet to his fate) .. and I'm done with this crap.\n\nOh swell, while flying out of there, I accidentally fly over the nearby cave with a spider in it .. get dismounted (all the way at the cliff tops) and fall to my death.  Great job, Blizz .. you outdid yourselves this time.",
            date = "2012-10-24T16:26:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31713#comments:id=1749635",
        },
        {
            id = 1789279,
            score = 3,
            author = "1041416",
            text = "The brewchugger hozin also drop the updates.  usually anywhere from 5-15 of the missing beer.",
            date = "2012-12-29T19:31:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31713#comments:id=1789279",
        },
        {
            id = 1818109,
            score = 3,
            author = "Vulkanius",
            text = "Do NOT delete excess Stouts (101+), otherwise you will have to redo the entire quest.",
            date = "2013-02-25T13:10:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31713#comments:id=1818109",
        },
    },
    [31714] = {
        {
            id = 1813858,
            score = 5,
            author = "720922",
            text = "As you enter the cave to do the dailies The Big Kah-Oona (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31715) and Monkey Mischief (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=31712), you will notice several cages with singles and rings with pairs of Misguided Serpent (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=65641)  in them. These are the serpents you need to rescue. As you hover your pointer over them, the pointer will change to a looting pointer and you click on them to \"rescue\" them. Be careful when using AoE spells around them as this will cause them to attack you.",
            date = "2013-02-15T07:25:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31714#comments:id=1813858",
        },
        {
            id = 1728116,
            score = 4,
            author = "950640",
            text = "\"Do you know what they are doing with wild cloud serpents? Captured hatchlings are forced to fight one another in the pits, for nothing more than the Oona's amusement.\n\nSavages!\n\nIf the young hatchlings learn such aggressive behavior at a young age, they may become violent and corrupted adults. A malicious cloud serpent is not something we want to deal with.\"\nYet the other NPC says the Cloud Serpents are perfectly fit for Pet Battles.",
            date = "2012-10-02T00:47:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31714#comments:id=1728116",
        },
        {
            id = 5890793,
            score = 1,
            author = "FLambda",
            text = "Be warned: Cleave attacks on the hozen will kill the hatchling serpents! Make sure to grab them first before attacking!",
            date = "2024-07-01T14:21:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31714#comments:id=5890793",
        },
        {
            id = 1683991,
            score = -3,
            author = "magnusfn",
            text = "In MoP, you will be able to get valor points by doing dailies. The 25 daily quest cap will be removed, and there will be hundreds of new dailies to do. Now you won't have to farm it by doing dungeons anymore, if you prefer doing dailies instead.",
            date = "2012-07-03T10:10:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31714#comments:id=1683991",
        },
    },
    [31715] = {
        {
            id = 1730823,
            score = 31,
            author = "Kittytreets",
            text = "Ummm. This is a one man quest? Not hardly. I almost died about four times, and then I let the 20 gang banger hozen kill me just so I wouldn't have to run out of the cave. Bad deal.  Kinda a bit OP on their end if you ask me. I don't mind killing my way in and out, but when it's completely absurd as it is, I tend to be frustrated immediately. It's not like I'm under level.\n\nThe boss himself is an EASY kill.... the 20 monkeys that attack you are a bit over the top.",
            date = "2012-10-04T06:01:22-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31715#comments:id=1730823",
        },
        {
            id = 1741876,
            score = 11,
            author = "297559",
            text = "Careful on approach, leaving. I discovered an auto-dismount bug while flying near the cave, on the left side if I remember correctly.",
            date = "2012-10-14T23:08:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31715#comments:id=1741876",
        },
        {
            id = 1749143,
            score = 10,
            author = "516507",
            text = "Even as a hunter, with Stampede, Dire Beast and a trinket that can get a total of 8 pets fighting on my side: I died within a minute every time I entered the cave. Wont be bothering with killing Lord Oona.\n\nAnd, I tried stealthing in, but as soon as I become visible there were half a dozen or more hozen including the Lord on me.",
            date = "2012-10-24T02:21:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31715#comments:id=1749143",
        },
        {
            id = 1751064,
            score = 7,
            author = "Hinahina",
            text = "NPC name is a reference to the Hawaiian word \"Kahuna\" and the slang term \"Big Kahuna\". From huna.org:\n\nThey were the experts of old Hawaii, experts in religion, health, crafts, science, psychology and magic.\n\"Kahuna\" was a title, like M.D. or Ph.D., and additional descriptive words were used to designate the field of expertise.\nJust as the modern use of the word \"doctor\" by itself is generally taken to mean a medical doctor, so the use of \"kahuna\" by itself generally designated a priest or healer.\nThey underwent intensive and extensive training before being recognized as experts in their field, either by their teacher or by the community.\nSome kahunas were experts in many fields.\nKahunas could be male or female.\nAlthough it is not explicitly stated above, it is clear from reading the above sources that kahunas of any kind were always attuned to the spiritual side of their expertise as well as to the material side.\nUnder the Monarchy the term \"kahuna\" began to be used for foreigners who were recognized experts in their fields, especially for ministers and health professionals.\n\nIn Territorial times, when Hawaii became a tourist destination, visitors discovered that the best surfer on the beach was called \"kahuna nui he'e nalu,\" the \"principal master surfer.\" Because of his expertise he was also the leader among the surfers, and they would follow his advice on boards and waves and the skill itself. He was called \"kahuna nui\" for short, and this soon became the phrase \"big kahuna,\" which took on meanings of \"big boss\" or even \"the biggest and the best\" in any area, including hamburgers.\n\nSome Hawaiians fear the word because they automatically relate it to sorcery, and some Hawaiians say that no one can be a kahuna who isn't Hawaiian. Visitors come to Hawaii looking for a \"kahuna,\" which for some means a psychic healer and for others means a shaman.\n\nHowever, I don't use that title any more. One aspect of Hawaiian culture I learned is to avoid offending others when you don't have to and some Hawaiians are offended by my use of it. So I am \"kahu\" to members of my organization who want to call me by a title, \"Dr. King\" to those who want to acknowledge my doctorate in psychology, and simply \"Serge\" to the rest of the world. I have Hawaiian names as well, but I honor my birth parents by publicly using the name they gave me.\n\nAs a Hawaiian, I don't know anyone who calls people Kahuna anymore because of the \"Kahuna\" title that has been bastardized. Tip though, don't come to Hawai'i and call people that. They'll laugh but it might not be with you.",
            date = "2012-10-26T15:59:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31715#comments:id=1751064",
        },
        {
            id = 1781531,
            score = 7,
            author = "942917",
            text = "ok so i just soloed this and i am a lvl 90 destro warlock .... it took me two tries till i figured out what was my mistake. this is a very difficult quest if you play alone much as i do, but i figured out a way to solo this quite easily, ... 1- buff up on extra hit food and spell power, 2- as you enter the cave, kill all your surrounding monkeys one at a time and DO NOT LOOT , wait to loot once all are dead and you can pass through to the next section of the cave. Wash ... Rinse .... Repeat till you have passed through the down hill pass killing all the monkeys one at a time, some will gank you by three's but just remain calm, and let your voidwalker take the best of the grunge healing him as needed plus use your rain of fire as often as possible on any mobs you encounter.  The boss will be atop of a very small island in the middle of the lake, continue your plan and kill all the mobs surrounding him then attack as soon as the mobs are all dead, again do not loot till you have killed the boss. Take him down and once he is dead then loot, I hearthed so as not to feel a need to fight your way out because the trails of monkey you killed on the way to him have sponed as the spone rate on these little bastages is outrageously fast. I hope this helps .... take care and enjoy :o)",
            date = "2012-12-15T00:39:17-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31715#comments:id=1781531",
        },
    },
    [31716] = {
        {
            id = 1730140,
            score = 124,
            author = "Erycius",
            text = "To ask why Blizzard always comes up with poop quests, is to ask why leaves fall. It is in their nature.",
            date = "2012-10-03T14:49:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31716#comments:id=1730140",
        },
        {
            id = 1732412,
            score = 82,
            author = "166539",
            text = "In their desperation for a new poop quest, they've come up with one that doesn't even make sense.\n\nShort version: \"Your serpent pooped everywhere, go clean it up before someone finds out\"\n\nSounds fine, and reasonable.  The problem is that the actual bags of poop are near impossible to find (on my realm, at least), so the only way to get them is to kill Siftworms.\n\nSo basically, the worms have already \"cleaned up\" all the poop, and now I literally have to go wrestle the poop out of them so nobody sees the poop... the poop that's in the worms.\n\nReal life version:\n\nYour dog poops on your neighbor's lawn.  Then a raccoon eats it.  Problem solved, right?  Nope.  According to Blizzard, we now have to kill the raccoon, remove the poop from its stomach, bag it, and throw it away so the neighbor doesn't find out.",
            date = "2012-10-05T15:23:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31716#comments:id=1732412",
        },
        {
            id = 1681643,
            score = 59,
            author = "339923",
            text = "Do you really get Valor Points for cleaning poop ? What the hell ?...",
            date = "2012-06-27T05:02:07-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31716#comments:id=1681643",
        },
        {
            id = 1728867,
            score = 44,
            author = "Gore123",
            text = "They won't always spawn on the ground.\n\nKill the Giant Siftworms (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=67084). They drop Big Bags of Poop (http://www.wowhead.com/item=89053) also.",
            date = "2012-10-02T14:41:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31716#comments:id=1728867",
        },
        {
            id = 1680331,
            score = 31,
            author = "Merylyan",
            text = "Great, more poop quests!\n\nAs an extra bonus this one is daily! Experience the exalting life of a janitor! :p",
            date = "2012-06-23T20:13:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31716#comments:id=1680331",
        },
    },
    [31717] = {
        {
            id = 1737676,
            score = 49,
            author = "Jevawty",
            text = "so\nas probably everyone i died on first try\nand then i tried gathering information about him only to find:\nthere's no trick about it or at least no one knows about it.\n\nnevertheless i killed him on 2nd try as a rogue\n(and without stealth-opener since speaking with him will un-stealth you)\n\nnow that i won i see what this fight is about.\nhe has a timer after which he has simply won, so you're fighting against time\nplus: he puts pools of fire under your feet hitting you hard.\nso your job is quite simple: never stop running !\nand try to fight effectively because every glitch you do\nwill be a wasted bit of your short amount of time\n\non my second try i also noticed that i didn't get stunned as much as before.\ni guess it has to do with the pools.\npossibly his fire breath and the pools only stun you in combination\nthus if you keep running and never stay in the pools for long\nhe has no real chance to stun you.\n\nhopefully my data helps reducing the skeletons around him\ngood luck everyone :)",
            date = "2012-10-10T16:08:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31717#comments:id=1737676",
        },
        {
            id = 1741248,
            score = 17,
            author = "Elfgar",
            text = "I stood by the gate and helped 20 toons in a row smack the crap outta him...to get even. Just bring a friend to stab him in the back.",
            date = "2012-10-14T08:49:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31717#comments:id=1741248",
        },
        {
            id = 1748563,
            score = 14,
            author = "701021",
            text = "As a kitty druid, I popped all my cooldowns (DPS, and mitigation) right before I talked to him.  You get about 3-5 seconds before he actually hits you but you can hit him, use that time to burn his face off.  I got him to about 50% before his first attack, and had all my dots up. Then just keep moving and try to refresh dots.\n\nFloat like a floatbot, sting like an automatic stinging machine.",
            date = "2012-10-23T09:11:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31717#comments:id=1748563",
        },
        {
            id = 1751237,
            score = 14,
            author = "Cohult",
            text = "I really wish any fair duel with an NPC in the game didn't kill you.  We just beat the crap out of them, or they kill us.  Not so fair.",
            date = "2012-10-26T20:24:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31717#comments:id=1751237",
        },
        {
            id = 1736711,
            score = 10,
            author = "suitedreemz",
            text = "disc priest in mixed blues and greens, had to keep moving.  instant holy fire and penance while moving, keep dots up and only stand to cast immediately after moving out of fire circle.  otherwise, stay moving to avoid the stun.  doable as a healer that has a couple of instant casts.",
            date = "2012-10-09T14:31:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31717#comments:id=1736711",
        },
    },
    [31718] = {
        {
            id = 1727230,
            score = 14,
            author = "lightclaw",
            text = "This quest requires you to defeat Big Bao (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=58508), who you access via conversation.  At current gear levels the fight is not easy.\n\nIn melee range he will use a knockback followed immediately by Force Burst (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=129858), which is difficult, but not impossible, to interrupt.  He also uses War Stomp, which has a cast time but is not interruptable, nor is it particularly easy to escape the range of it.  Your best bet is to stun him to interrupt the cast, dps for a second, and then move slightly farther out and prepare to get out of range if he begins casting it again once he wakes up.\n\nHe has a death grip style ability for casters as well.\n\nHe hits very hard, so use your cooldowns, keep dots on him to continue damage while you're stunned, and know that the quickest path back from the spirit rezzer is to head south a short distance where you'll find a path up the cliff to the Arboretum.",
            date = "2012-10-01T09:11:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31718#comments:id=1727230",
        },
        {
            id = 1741752,
            score = 10,
            author = "hollyberries",
            text = "There is a one minute time limit on this fight.\n\nIt doesn't say as much in the quest text and the timer is very tiny in his buffs, but if you can't beat him in one minute you lose. This makes the fight very challenging for classes, Protection-specced or healers, who don't have much in the way of burst damage.\n\nAdditionally if you die, it takes you to a graveyard without flight in the middle of the ocean. There is no way back other than a very long run or a spirit rez.",
            date = "2012-10-14T19:28:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31718#comments:id=1741752",
        },
        {
            id = 1735303,
            score = 7,
            author = "Farzeer",
            text = "Mages;\n\nIt's not too hard fight, but it's not too easy either. You're most likely going to lose your first fight, but don't give up! :) I did this with ilevel 340 so it doesn't require full heroic gear (340 = questing gear + 2 PvP + 2 heroic pieces). I first tried to kill him as arcane mage, but i got totally wrecked. Fire seems to be the best option.\n\n1. Before the fight, use your buffs. Remember to use Ice barrier too, if you have the talent.\n2. Wait for all the cooldowns before you start the fight. You'll lose your ice barrier quite fast so you want to have another one ready.\n\nOkay, now the fight. He uses 4 (5?) different abilities.\n\n1. Force Burst: Deals 300% weapon damage. This one is a pain in the ass. He'll spam it all the time, so better watch out. It dealt about 30k damage on me (I have 11,8k armor).\n\n2. Pull close: This ability will pull you right next to him, dealing 300% weapon damage at the same time. This spell doesn't really change anything, since most of his spells can be casted from range. I used this as an opportunity to stun him with dragon's breath. Got my distance and back to bursting him (keep some distance just in case of the next ability that i'm going to tell you about).\n\n3. War stomp: 2 second stun, 500% weapon damage. Pretty much the same as taurens racial ability, but much, much worse. Believe me, it's deadly. This ability is the reason you may want to keep your distance as a mage.\n\n4. Knock away: 125% weapon damage (AoE), knocks you back a bit. Nothing serious here. He'll just interrupt one of your spells if you're close to him. So keep your distance (at least 10 yards)!\n\nThe strategy to win is quite simple. Keep your distance(!) and CC him as much as possible. You have 1 minute to kill him. Think twice before you use your combustion (You'll need to deal a LOT of damage too, so combustion helps a lot). Keep Living bomb active at all times and just hope for good pyroblast procs and crits.\n\n(!) This fight is a great opportunity to use your Alter time ability. Big Bao is able to take down all your health quite fast so using this ability to restore some of your health is quite a huge help in this fight.",
            date = "2012-10-08T06:01:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31718#comments:id=1735303",
        },
        {
            id = 1763672,
            score = 7,
            author = "351338",
            text = "This fight seems to be all about burst DPS - you'll likely need to have all of your DPS cooldowns at the ready. The fight is on a timer, so you can't dwaddle in dishing out damage. Come in hitting hard and don't let up. Many classes may need to switch to a DPS spec for this fight.",
            date = "2012-11-17T07:37:10-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31718#comments:id=1763672",
        },
        {
            id = 1738416,
            score = 6,
            author = "1044827",
            text = "These quests can be done as a group. Tested it this morning. If you find yourself having trouble with them find a partner and burn them down.",
            date = "2012-10-11T10:40:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31718#comments:id=1738416",
        },
    },
    [31719] = {
        {
            id = 1744128,
            score = 14,
            author = "GaidinBDJ",
            text = "Another tough fight, and, same as the others, the easiest way is to just get in line and help the people before you with DPS while you wait your turn and hope someone is behind you to help you (once you've defeated her, you can't assist in the fight).\n\nShe has several direct damage abilities that was hitting my 413 Moonkin for 30k each (ranged).  She also has an AOE consisting of red spheres, if any of them touch you you take 70k over 8 seconds.  Each.  It also looked like (from other people fighting her) that her melees hit equally hard.\n\nYou'll have 1 minute to chew her down, which is why multiple people hitting her makes a big difference.\n\nOh, and dying means spawning back at that PITA graveyard out in the ocean.  Head around the south side of the mainland and there's a ramp up around 60, 50.",
            date = "2012-10-17T14:19:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31719#comments:id=1744128",
        },
        {
            id = 1753009,
            score = 7,
            author = "Sapphos",
            text = "451 Feral Druid. Best thing I found is to just pop all CD's and kill her as fast as possible.\n\nWhen she casts harmful spheres, back out of them and run around to find a decent spot to attack her. I couldn't move her away from the spheres and she just blasts you with ranged so don't wait them out.",
            date = "2012-10-29T04:48:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31719#comments:id=1753009",
        },
        {
            id = 1843572,
            score = 5,
            author = "1114966",
            text = "If you have trouble soloing these quests, try getting your terracotta fragment from Jonn-Dar in Valley of the Four Winds. It's a great trinket that gives you a Tank that scales with your lvl. At lvl 90 it has about 500k health and also aggro's right of the bat. Only thing, I can't heal it during combat, but if you could, you would nearly be invincible. Hope this helps?",
            date = "2013-04-15T18:32:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31719#comments:id=1843572",
        },
        {
            id = 1840722,
            score = 4,
            author = "TheRealSaiph",
            text = "IMO, these \"trainer's challenge\" quests seem to be way out of line with everything else I've found in MoP so far. I'm a frost mage, and beating Ningna (like Suchi) seems impossible to me. I'm leaving these quests for now, and I'll see if I can find an alternative route through the quest chains so that I don't miss out on anything.\nBlizzard, I think you've made a mistake by forcing players to take on tough PVP -style opponents if they want to progress. Players should be free to explore WoW in their own style, they should not be forced to follow a single track like this.",
            date = "2013-04-08T18:26:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31719#comments:id=1840722",
        },
        {
            id = 1762947,
            score = 3,
            author = "warmgeoff",
            text = "yes, she's tough; pop your CDs and burn her quick, or she will waste you. Did this as Survival hunter with the Rapid fire cast and then my trinks, while avoiding her red spheres. First time, got burned down with her 27-30k ranged hits.[omg I hate that long run back (see comment below re: ramp)]. Help out others in line, also as suggested, and maybe someone will help you, too...GL!  ;)",
            date = "2012-11-15T16:31:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31719#comments:id=1762947",
        },
    },
    [31720] = {
        {
            id = 1727242,
            score = 30,
            author = "lightclaw",
            text = "This quest requires you to defeat Suchi the Sweet (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=58510), who you access via conversation.  At current gear levels the fight is no joke and the fight mechanics can't be ignored.\n\nShe will spam an AoE spell called Sunfire (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=129979), which has a very short cast time to begin with and gets faster as the fight progresses.  She can be defeated by interrupting and stunning her, but a much much easier method is to simply run around in circles as she casts it, occasionally passing through her to hit her.  She will pause occasionally for perhaps five seconds, during which time you are safe to stop and dps her.\n\nShe also uses solar beam to AoE silence, so move out of it to cast.\n\nFinally, she has an aura, Radiance (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=129981), that does 15k ticks of magic damage every 2 seconds.\n\nAll of her damage is AoE, so pet classes should have an easy time with her, unless she spams Sunfire at random targets rather than the primary threat target.\n\nEach of the Trainer's Challenges has a timer, shown by a buff on the NPC called Race Against the Clock (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=129772).  You have at most 60 seconds to defeat them.\n\nAgain, it's tough.   Best of luck.  Oh yeah, and the quickest way back from the graveyard is to head south from the spirit rezzer, there's a path up the cliff just around the corner.  Ask me how I know.",
            date = "2012-10-01T09:22:08-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31720#comments:id=1727242",
        },
        {
            id = 1747577,
            score = 8,
            author = "725378",
            text = "Be careful with AOE's if there are opposing faction players who decide to walk through them otherwise you will get a nice beating by the guards, then a lovely walk back to your corpse.",
            date = "2012-10-22T00:48:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31720#comments:id=1747577",
        },
        {
            id = 1731588,
            score = 7,
            author = "lownignitus",
            text = "I tried to do this as tank spec on my paladin. No dice. afetr 60-90 secs combat ended and the npc yelled that they won.\n\nI switched to Ret and kept running around and stunning and spamming aoe and dmg. I finished them off in about 30 secs doing  25k dps.\n\nSo in summary you have a time limit to get them down to 1 hp and it requires doing massive dps to them while not getting hit by their attacks too much.\n\nPS... didnt realize they had a timer buff ... makes sense now",
            date = "2012-10-04T19:45:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31720#comments:id=1731588",
        },
        {
            id = 1839795,
            score = 6,
            author = "TheRealSaiph",
            text = "IMO, these \"trainer's challenge\" quests seem to be way out of line with everything else I've found in MoP so far. I'm a frost mage, and beating Suchi seems impossible to me. I'm leaving these quests for now, and I'll see if I can find an alternative route through the quest chains so that I don't miss out on anything.\nBlizzard, I think you've made a mistake by forcing players to take on tough PVP -style opponents if they want to progress. Players should be free to explore WoW in their own style, they should not be forced to follow a single track like this.",
            date = "2013-04-06T13:48:53-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31720#comments:id=1839795",
        },
        {
            id = 1745056,
            score = 5,
            author = "310997",
            text = "dont die or you will spend the next 15 minutes walking back to your corpse.   the graveyard is out n the water and you will have to walk up to sri-la village and then all the way back down to your corpse.  i couldnt do this as a mage without help.  after dying the first time the walk after dying almost makes me want to leave this area and never come back.",
            date = "2012-10-18T17:27:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31720#comments:id=1745056",
        },
    },
    [31721] = {
        {
            id = 1745792,
            score = 15,
            author = "GaidinBDJ",
            text = "This is easier than the other trainers if you do one thing.  Take out the images.  ASAP.  They only have 1,000 hp each, but they generally spawn a fair distance away (my bear swipe wouldn't hit them).  A larger PBAoE might be able to hit them.  Either way, burn them.  Fast.  They don't do much damage at first, but once the trainer starts hitting you with Char Burst the images can hit upwards of 50k each.\n\nHe recasts the images fairly quickly, so it cuts into your DPS, but if you focus on the images, you should be able to pull it off eventually.\n\nIf you have a fast enough interrupt, try to stop his Char Burst, as it adds a +fire damage debuff.\n\nAnd, as with the other fights, a second person will make it a fairly trivial fight.  One focus on the trainer, the other watches out for images.",
            date = "2012-10-19T15:20:42-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31721#comments:id=1745792",
        },
        {
            id = 1735499,
            score = 6,
            author = "Junyed",
            text = "The mirror images do about 40k damage for each cast they do, it might be better to kill them instead of trying to out-dps them.",
            date = "2012-10-08T10:12:06-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31721#comments:id=1735499",
        },
        {
            id = 1729874,
            score = 3,
            author = "lightclaw",
            text = "This quest requires you to defeat Qua-Ro Whitebrow (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=58511).  He is accessed via conversation and can be found near the questgiver, where he is training his black dragon, Cinder.  The fight is fairly trivial, much easier than the other trainer challenges I've seen.  He casts Char Burst, which can be interrupted if you're fast, and Conjure Image, a single copy Mirror Image spell.",
            date = "2012-10-03T10:34:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31721#comments:id=1729874",
        },
        {
            id = 1733291,
            score = 3,
            author = "wowmiri",
            text = "In order to beat this guy, you have to DPS him down to 1% in under a minute. In case you keep failing and have no clue why.",
            date = "2012-10-06T10:58:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31721#comments:id=1733291",
        },
        {
            id = 1763362,
            score = 2,
            author = "Ropers",
            text = "Anyone have any experience completing this in bear or cat form?\n\nIt IS timed!\nAfter failing numerous times, I sat there and watched everyone else complete him. Most didn't pay attention to his \"images\" and just burned him.\n\nThen I did it myself alternating from bear to cat form and finally got it. So YES it is timed.",
            date = "2012-11-16T13:43:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31721#comments:id=1763362",
        },
    },
    [31723] = {
        {
            id = 1682297,
            score = 1,
            author = "potatoe",
            text = "Talk to NPC Adm'rl Placeholder  to get this quest.\n\nHe is in the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar.\n\nApparently, this will give you a free level and a teleport.\n\nHe looks just like https://www.wowhead.com/npc=42976Capn Placeholder.\n[npc=42976 domain=www]#comments:id=1676546\n\nOnce he teleports you, the NPC you will be looking for is:\nPrivate Tim P. O'rary\n\nsee also:\nThe Lament of Captain Placeholder\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-2xuO8JBepM",
            date = "2012-06-28T21:24:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31723#comments:id=1682297",
        },
    },
    [31727] = {
        {
            id = 2062495,
            score = 24,
            author = "FireEmerald",
            text = "Part 1 - How to access the Klaxxi:\n\nStarts by:\nBowmistress Li (http://wowhead.com/npc=62112)\nFalling Down (http://wowhead.com/quest=31001)\nNope (http://wowhead.com/quest=31002)\n\nMarksman Lann (http://wowhead.com/npc=62166)\nPsycho Mantid (http://wowhead.com/quest=31003)\n\nKlaxxi'va Tik (http://wowhead.com/npc=62203)\n... some Quests - just accept all frome the questgiver ...\n\nKil'ruk the Wind-Reaver (http://wowhead.com/npc=62202)\n... some Quests - just accept all frome the questgiver ...\n\n_________________________________________________________________\n\nPart 2 - The Klaxxi:\n\nFrom:\nAmbersmith Zikk (http://wowhead.com/npc=64599)\nAmber Arms (http://wowhead.com/quest=31008)\nConcentrated Fear (http://wowhead.com/quest=31108)\n\nFrom:\nKor'ik (http://wowhead.com/npc=64815)\nDead Zone (http://wowhead.com/quest=31009)\n-> In Her Clutch (http://wowhead.com/quest=31010)\n\nUnlocks Malik the Unscathed (http://wowhead.com/npc=62774).\nThe Dreadsworn (http://wowhead.com/quest=31689)\nCitizens of a New Empire (http://wowhead.com/quest=31107)\n\n_________________________________________________________________\n\nPart 3 - Requirements to reach the Anglers:\nKor'ik (http://wowhead.com/npc=64815)\n\nComplete the quest A Cry From Darkness (http://wowhead.com/quest=31066).",
            date = "2014-12-07T09:04:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31727#comments:id=2062495",
        },
        {
            id = 1726617,
            score = 8,
            author = "fraeg",
            text = "This quest opened up after completing the second sub-section of Dread Haste Makes Waste (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=6540) \"The Might of the Klaxxi\" which includes the quests in the Lake of Stars area.",
            date = "2012-09-30T22:19:58-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31727#comments:id=1726617",
        },
        {
            id = 5310095,
            score = 6,
            author = "Niixten",
            text = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31727 showed up at https://www.wowhead.com/npc=64599 after I'v done all except for Iyyokuk the Lucid and Ka'roz the Locust in https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7312\n\nDo not touch any quests at Soggy's Gamble, otherwise you are not eligible for the breadcrumbhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=31727",
            date = "2022-01-16T11:55:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31727#comments:id=5310095",
        },
        {
            id = 2625431,
            score = 4,
            author = "1923806",
            text = "I'm not sure if this quest was removed or not but I never got this quest from the Klaxxi. After completing up to https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31026 I went back to the Klaxxi area to look for the quest but it's not available from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=64599. However I flew to back to Soggy's Gamble and https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63349 wants to give me https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31265 which is the beginning of the Anglers quest line in the Dread Wastes. To clarify I never did this quest, I even ran the script to test whether or not I did it without realizing and it came back false so I'm not sure if something was changed here between expansions but this quest either does not exist anymore or isn't required to unlock the angler quest line.",
            date = "2018-10-22T19:28:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31727#comments:id=2625431",
        },
        {
            id = 5596813,
            score = 3,
            author = "Kryptaria",
            text = "The process to open this quest is ridiculous, if you haven't done anything in MoP/Dread Wastes.\n\nIf you go to Soggy's Gambit, https://www.wowhead.com/npc=63498 should offer you https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31886. This takes you to the wall, where you'll pick up more quests from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=62112 and the NPC standing next to her. You rappel down and begin the most convoluted series of quests to awaken Klaxxi Paragons.\n\nI don't think you need to do the quest that takes you to the Sunset Brewgarden to the far north. I did do it, but I gave up, deciding instead to focus on Klaxxi, not Pandaren.\n\nKeep freeing Paragons and doing their quests. You can keep track with https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=7312. I finally got https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31727 when I had freed all the paragons except Iyyokuk the Lucid, Ka'roz the Locust, Hisek the Swarmkeeper, and Xaril the Poisoned Mind.",
            date = "2023-04-28T11:27:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31727#comments:id=5596813",
        },
    },
