            score = 2,
            author = "DaemoniKira",
            text = "https://www.wowhead.com/npc=66199:\nI'm afraid he is no longer of his own mind. There is only one way to save him, and our brewery.\nStrike swift and sure. He will not feel a thing.\n{The Champion accepts, and solemnly steps in front of the once-gentle beast.}\n{The Champion looks back at https://www.wowhead.com/npc=66199, who gives a sad nod, tears rolling down her cheeks.}\n{The Champion turns back to the magnificent beast, steeling their resolve to do this act of mercy.}\n\n{The Champion begins hacking away at the beast with semi-blunt and chipped daggers,\nrepeatedly stabbing anywhere and everywhere that they can connect steel to flesh;\nkicking the beast occasionally; https://www.wowhead.com/spell=315496; stabbing and slashing, anywhere, everywhere;\nrolling, dodging out of the way, only to appear at the beast's tail end and thrusting their dagger into its flank.}\n{All the while, the beast is screaming and yelling, a grotesque sound of pain and fear; a torturous sound.}\n{The Champion continues hacking and stabbing away,\neye, nose, shoulder, ear, ribs, eyes again, neck;\nblood spraying everywhere, turning the Champion into a swift, ferocious, glistening red demon.}\n{The beast eventually, finally lets out a mournful, tearjerking, heart wrenching moan of pain, sadness, betrayal... and becomes still.}\n\n{The Champion looks back at https://www.wowhead.com/npc=66199 and sees that she is stunned, standing frozen,\na look of pure terror mixed with disgust and regret, all apparent on her tear-soaked face.}\n\n{The Champion takes a step toward her, but stops when https://www.wowhead.com/npc=66199 flinches in fear,\nimmediately recoiling in disgust and horror.}\n\n{https://www.wowhead.com/npc=66199's disgust immediately turns to outrage.}\n\nStrained, anger wrapping its sharp claws and tightening them around her throat,\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=66199 chokes out:\nI... told... you...\n\"Strike swift and sure.\"\nI... told... you...\nNot to let him feel a thing.\n\nThe Champion stares at her, analyzing her face and wondering where this sudden rage came from,\nyet far too exhausted from bringing down this massive beast to much care, and says plainly:\nHuh. I thought you were speaking in metaphor.\nYou can clearly see I'm only level 18. I don't have all that many abilities at my disposal yet.\nNow, if you had asked a Level 60, it certainly would have been \"swift and sure\".\nBut do you see any Level 60 Champions around? Exactly. I'm all you've got.\n{The Champion pauses and begins to turn around, only to pivot once again to face the fuzzy puddle of tears.}\nRegardless, I'm a Rogue. Would you have preferred that I had switched to Assassination,\nand ended him even more slowly and painfully, as my numerous poisons slowly coursed through the beast's massive body?\nIt could have taken quite a long time, though... it could have saved me quite a bit of trouble...\nThe beast was lucky I forgot to coat my daggers with my https://www.wowhead.com/spell=315584 beforehand.\nI've heard that the few victims I've left alive have said that poison is excruciating.\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=66199, her wrath melting from sheer disbelief and incredulous shock,\nbegins to let out a typhoon of helpless sobs and manages to choke out:\nYou... didn't... have to... butcher him!\n\n{The Champion looks at her for a long moment, reading her eyes,\nthen shrugs, turns back around to the still-warm corpse, now stiff from rigor mortis, and begins skinning it.}\n\n{The Champion hears a sudden cacaphony of grief-wracked sobs,\nthe occassional soul-searing shriek splitting their eardrums.}\n\n{When the Champion finally finishes truly butchering the carcass,\nthey let out a long sigh, wipe their blade, and stuff the skins in their travel pack.}\n{They look back, ready to ask https://www.wowhead.com/npc=66199 about their reward, but find nothing but beach and ocean behind them.}\nI'm sure I'll run into her at the Village. I'll ask around for her.\n{The Champion sets off, ready for their next gruesome task, if only for a couple gold pieces.}",
            date = "2022-05-22T21:28:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31740#comments:id=5376158",
        },
        {
            id = 1984090,
            score = 1,
            author = "Shoadowolf",
            text = "Be warned: If you have a companion pet/ battle pet out with you during this fight, watch out for his belly flop, he will kill the battle pet if its in its AoE range.\n\nIt happened to my poor, poor, Murkalot.... T.T\n(However, it doesn't lower its damage, it just strangely dies....)",
            date = "2014-07-24T18:21:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31740#comments:id=1984090",
        },
    },
