    [31779] = {
        {
            id = 1718083,
            score = 84,
            author = "ParRathorne",
            text = "Just to be CLEAR, you get to this quest objective from within the camp (don't run down and around the side of the valley or jump off the edge as I did as there's no easy way back up from the water!)   From within the camp, take the small bridge (27.5, 25.1) over the valley to where you'll find a cave and the mob to kill.",
            date = "2012-09-24T20:11:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31779#comments:id=1718083",
        },
        {
            id = 1875262,
            score = 28,
            author = "SpakyTwo",
            text = "After running around for twenty minutes to a half an hour (after coming here) I decided to post about it.\n\nThe beginning to the bridge is at 27.4 25.1 it is inside the Alliance Camp pretty much across the camp from Corporal Jackson Silver  who is in a shed  like structure at 27.9 23.3.\n\nCross the bridge and the cave is obvious on the other side on the right hand side. There are two guards posted outside.  You can pull them one at a time. Then go inside the cave and kill him. He has two phases and can be challenging at level 85. You may want to try to get to Halfhill and talk with Trader Jambeezi  (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=59583)\n\nHe sells a complete set of 372 gear. I noticed someone in another comment said that that they were at ilvl 327.",
            date = "2013-07-09T19:36:39-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31779#comments:id=1875262",
        },
        {
            id = 1724111,
            score = 15,
            author = "1037729",
            text = "Am I the only one having trouble with this quest? I'm a level 85 rogue and pretty much finding it impossible to solo. I get him down to the point where he turns into the sha, but by that point my health is pretty low and for some reason he pretty much just one shots me and it's all over. Frustrating as hell.",
            date = "2012-09-29T06:11:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31779#comments:id=1724111",
        },
        {
            id = 1742681,
            score = 9,
            author = "243447",
            text = "Once the quest is completed... you turn it in at the airfield with the Gyrocopters. There is a tall flag pole there flying an Alliance flag. Turn in the quest by right-clicking on the flag pole, and it will become a Horde flag.\n\nCoordinates for flag pole are 27.59 x 24.33....\n\nGood luck to all!",
            date = "2012-10-15T16:47:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31779#comments:id=1742681",
        },
        {
            id = 1814100,
            score = 9,
            author = "1091609",
            text = "I'm finding this pretty much impossible as an 85 fury warrior. 8 or 9 deaths now. It's really disappointing that blizzard have &*!@ed up the balance this badly honestly. If you're a class without reliable self-heals, I would strongly suggest you don't bother attempting Pandaria until you've run a few heroics and gotten some good gear. The npcs constantly attack in big groups and pile into fights, leaving you no way to kill them all, and the bosses are all very tough - some, like this one, are simply impossible solo for some classes, it seems.\nI have popped every cooldown I have, tried defensive stance, hiding out of LOS round the corner and bandaging - no success. Item level 327 if anyone's wondering. The first phase is just about survivable, and once you get him down to half half you have a brief period to heal up, but unless you're playing a class with natural heals you'll probably be going into the second phase with a little over half health. You can't use food, and bandages won't heal more than that. You'll also be without cooldowns since you already used them all. This generally results in you getting raped by the breath in three seconds flat.\nI suppose I'll be forced to drop a couple of thousand gold on a shield and switch to Prot just for this one &*!@ty quest. It certainly isn't doable as-is.",
            date = "2013-02-15T21:09:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=31779#comments:id=1814100",
        },
    },
