    [32557] = {
        {
            id = 1833293,
            score = 8,
            author = "859333",
            text = "The Blades are spears standing in racks along the walls at the Conqueror's Terrace, usually beside mobs.\nOn server times with a high volume of players, these can be a bit hard to get.",
            date = "2013-03-23T15:41:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32557#comments:id=1833293",
        },
    },
    [32558] = {
        {
            id = 1831043,
            score = 6,
            author = "861121",
            text = "Both can be found in mini palaces (posh huts).\n\nSpiritbinder Tu'chek is at 59,56 (West of questgiver, follow the outer wall to avoid combat on way there)\n\nArcanital Rak'ul is at 56,46 (Follow wide path slightly to East of Tu'chek, heading North)\n\nBoth fairly easy to kill, but watch out for adds, once they start congregating they are a nightmare, especially for clothwearers.",
            date = "2013-03-19T05:57:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32558#comments:id=1831043",
        },
    },
    [32559] = {
        {
            id = 1832119,
            score = 56,
            author = "242255",
            text = "The guardian you are supposed to kill for this quest is guarded by 4 priests. Each priest gives the guardian an ability, and killing a priest will prevent the guardian from absorbing that ability. The 4 abilities are:\n\nBlessing of the Serpent (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=137290) - long cast time attack that deals lots of damage. 10s cast. Interruptible.\nBlessing of the Hydra (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=137292) - Massive heal-over-time. Dispellable.\nBlessing of the Hawk (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=137293) - summons gusts of winds that knock you around, dealing damage.\nBlessing of the Direhorn (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=137291) - summons an earthquake that deals large damage on an area beneath the guardian. 3s cast. Not interruptible.\n\nIf you are soloing this, or if there is no one else around to help you, this comment is for you. All damage abilities are very dangerous, and ideally you should try to kill as many priests as you can before the guardian awakens. If you are a class that cannot dispel magic, the Hydra priest needs to die, otherwise you have no way of outdamaging the guardian's heal.\n\nThe serpent ability can be interrupted, and should pose no threat to any class that can interrupt. If not interrupted though, it can take off more than half your health. The hawk ability can kill you quickly if you get caught in its path, since it knocks you around into other tornadoes, and each tornado can whittle your health down pretty quickly. The direhorn ability is an earthquake beneath the guardian that is easily avoided, but if you are not careful and stand in it, it deals around 40,000 damage per second.\n\nIn terms of importance and threat level, I would rate the following order in which the priests need to die: Hydra, Hawk, Direhorn, Serpent (serpent before hawk if you are a class that cannot interrupt).",
            date = "2013-03-21T02:49:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32559#comments:id=1832119",
        },
        {
            id = 1834354,
            score = 1,
            author = "Bonyfoot",
            text = "Just 2 manned this guy. Killed the 2 adds Hydra and Hawk beforehand.\n\nHe was quite easy after failed attempts of not killing the Hydra priest.",
            date = "2013-03-25T17:53:49-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32559#comments:id=1834354",
        },
        {
            id = 1870159,
            score = 1,
            author = "gpdoyon",
            text = "I was able to solo this as a Mistweaver Monk with iLevel 483 healing gear. I killed the Hydra and Serpent priest first before the Boss woke. After that it was a matter of interrupts and staying out of his way. Granted, being able to heal myself was very helpful.",
            date = "2013-06-24T12:33:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32559#comments:id=1870159",
        },
        {
            id = 1919970,
            score = 1,
            author = "Thebe2",
            text = "Here's a really easy way to do this for a BM Hunter, or for that matter, any other with a pet.\nKill Priest of Hydra and Hawk, in that order. (Don't wait too long after you kill Hydra to kill Hawk, or Tak'u will free.) Have growl on your pet. Put a shot on Tak'u and run to the wall at about 61.14 54.89. Run Stampede on your pet, spam Heal Pet, move in for a shot and a glaive toss, launch a couple traps,  and move back to the wall. Rinse, repeat: just keep pounding Heal Pet. Your pet will take him down. I didn't take a single hit. I even made the mistake of waiting too long to kill Priest of Hawk.",
            date = "2013-11-20T17:33:39-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32559#comments:id=1919970",
        },
        {
            id = 1942719,
            score = 1,
            author = "786963",
            text = "This is another crappy one for non-healing melee to solo. Not worth the 5 valor points. Thanks for kill order tho'.",
            date = "2014-02-12T13:41:55-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32559#comments:id=1942719",
        },
    },
    [32560] = {
        {
            id = 1808953,
            score = 2,
            author = "ED209",
            text = "...Keep it safe! (http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_YhpauKGgQ4)",
            date = "2013-02-04T06:07:01-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32560#comments:id=1808953",
        },
    },
    [32561] = {
    },
    [32562] = {
        {
            id = 1846745,
            score = 1,
            author = "Draewind",
            text = "I was left with the debuff \"Thermal Collapse (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=139645#comments)\" after the fight.  The debuff was endless and did 20k damage per second.  I submitted a bug ticket (it is a bug).  The only way to get rid of it is to let it kill you.  It is gone once you rez.",
            date = "2013-04-25T05:19:56-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32562#comments:id=1846745",
        },
    },
    [32563] = {
        {
            id = 1837155,
            score = 13,
            author = "998027",
            text = "For easy Horde solo:\n\nPull this guy basically straight back, toward Dawnseeker Promontory. At 42.8 42.2, there is a Mana Collector that will give you a Bloodlust buff.\n\nKill his raptor, probably while kiting him toward the mana collector, since it has 78K HP.\n\nOnce you reach the mana collector, use it and if you feel the need, charge the Sunreaver Ward. Also, ~2 horde-side guardians will attack him. Between all of this, the fight becomes trivial.\n\nThe Firespear/Icespear adds will follow you, but the Healer won't so don't worry. Stay out of the icespear/firespear's Line of Sight to avoid the 80K damage magic attacks (They will lock onto your position before firing, and stay locked in that LoS for a few seconds.).\n\nThey're fairly easy to avoid since they usually attack at the same time.",
            date = "2013-03-31T12:02:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32563#comments:id=1837155",
        },
        {
            id = 1867094,
            score = 3,
            author = "H888",
            text = "Another way of doing it solo is to kite him at any end of the beach, the healer will not follow (did not for me). Then you just have to strafe to avoid the two casters spells while killing him.",
            date = "2013-06-16T03:08:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32563#comments:id=1867094",
        },
    },
    [32564] = {
    },
    [32565] = {
        {
            id = 1827056,
            score = 2,
            author = "tr1gger",
            text = "Cords : 45,35\n\nHP : 4.7 Million\n\n220 Rep (Bonus) with the Sunreaver Onslaught, 1 https://www.wowhead.com/item=94220, 5 Valor and 5 Lesser Charms of Good Fortune.\n\nKilled him and his ads with a large group of people and was super simple. He has quite a few ads. If he isn't there, just wait a few minutes for him to spawn.",
            date = "2013-03-11T20:20:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32565#comments:id=1827056",
        },
        {
            id = 1827246,
            score = 2,
            author = "881415",
            text = "If your looking at this guy from a distance he's an eliete but once you hit him he's just a regular 90.  I pulled him away from his adds and he went down rather quickly.  Remember to stay out of the aoe on the ground, his adds throw at you. His coords are 45.99. To the east of the starting area, across the bay just beyond the felled levitian.",
            date = "2013-03-12T04:29:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32565#comments:id=1827246",
        },
        {
            id = 1828539,
            score = 1,
            author = "443183",
            text = "Just CC the healing guy and nuke Nurkala while avoiding the cone attacks of the other two adds.",
            date = "2013-03-14T11:48:59-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32565#comments:id=1828539",
        },
        {
            id = 1837156,
            score = 1,
            author = "998027",
            text = "For easy Horde solo:\n\nPull this guy basically straight back, toward Dawnseeker Promontory. At 42.8 42.2, there is a Mana Collector that will give you a Bloodlust buff.\n\nKill his raptor, probably while kiting him toward the mana collector, since it has 78K HP.\n\nOnce you reach the mana collector, use it and if you feel the need, charge the Sunreaver Ward. Also, ~2 horde-side guardians will attack him. Between all of this, the fight becomes trivial.\n\nThe Firespear/Icespear adds will follow you, but the Healer won't so don't worry. Stay out of the icespear/firespear's Line of Sight to avoid the 80K damage magic attacks (They will lock onto your position before firing, and stay locked in that LoS for a few seconds.).\n\nThey're fairly easy to avoid since they usually attack at the same time.",
            date = "2013-03-31T12:03:02-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32565#comments:id=1837156",
        },
        {
            id = 1827269,
            score = -6,
            author = "663223",
            text = "How to OFFICIALLY SOLO Nurkala\n\nThis is a very simple kite, in fact I even did it on a boomkin who only has two epics on him, I though do not suggest this kiting method to Alliance if you have to fight Nurkala near the beach where the Leviathan is.\n\nMy first try fighting this guy was impossible, nearly dying, I ran a few yards without dealing damage and the adds along Nurkala had left back to their original spot. (I am forced to solo this guy for I am on Naz'Grel, the most dead server there can ever be, even at 6:00 am.)\n\nI had to find a strategy, huntards and fartlocks can easily kite this or possibly solo this. I figured out that as long as you pop simple damage every 2-4 seconds, this guy will stay on you. If you are Horde, lead him to the base. (This will help for the guards will fight the adds and keep them off of you, though they will not harm Nurkala.)\n\nBoomkins should be using sunfire and moonfire. (Spamming atleast Sunfire 3 times, and then Moonfire once so they do more damage over time.) Nurkala is not actually a elite as what some people have mentioned.\n\nDowning him is easy, you though wish to not get hit by the AoE summoned by the Adds. (They still though will summon these AoE, and the spellcaster can hit you for 80k, so use a health pot or heal yourself if you can.) Once Nurkala is dead, most of the adds will run away. DoT's or minimal hits are what you need for this fight.\n\nI will try to find a guide out for Allaince.",
            date = "2013-03-12T05:42:12-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32565#comments:id=1827269",
        },
    },
