    [32579] = {
        {
            id = 1861513,
            score = 1,
            author = "333762",
            text = "as a ilvl 481destruction lock, I used the observer pet since it can interrupt and do some self-healing. Also used a couple of demonic gateways on either side of the boss. Optical blast to interrupt. Kil'Jaeden's Cunning talent allows me to cast and run - you gotta do a lot of casting and a lot of running. Stay out of the sparkly ground. I also used Abyssal pet to stun him when I got tired of running. If you get too close to Ihgaluk Crag, some of those mobs start spilling over to also cause some distraction to you. I looted 25 silver off the slacker!",
            date = "2013-06-01T19:23:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32579#comments:id=1861513",
        },
        {
            id = 1877281,
            score = 1,
            author = "Apheus",
            text = "Ok, just soloed him on a ilvl 484 BMstr Hunter using a direhorn for a pet.  I launched Stampede and kept moving....He only knocked me back twice and I got him down fairly quick.\n\nSorry this doesn't really help other classes.  This is the first toon I've done him on.\n\nBest of luck to you.",
            date = "2013-07-15T20:58:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32579#comments:id=1877281",
        },
        {
            id = 1881927,
            score = 1,
            author = "Netspook",
            text = "As a demo warlock, I found an easy and safe way of killing him.\n\nSend in your voidwalker while debuffing/attacking. Behind him is a large tree - this is a safe spot where nothing will hit you. Run there if you get problems, and let the vw keep his attention. Hiding behind other obstacles may work just as fine.\n\nTested this a little further. You can actually just send in your vw and then hide. It will be a slow fight, but he wasn't even able to kill my vw.",
            date = "2013-07-29T07:07:16-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32579#comments:id=1881927",
        },
        {
            id = 1894302,
            score = 1,
            author = "1144141",
            text = "As an iLevel 485 Arms PVP (Mal/Tyr/PVE gear mix) warrior I was able to solo him by kiting him out of his cubbyhole by the Saurons, up the road Northwest to the veteran marksman and Omnia veteran (located right under the \"M\" in Diremoor on the map) where they helped make short work of him.\n\nJust remember to sidestep his linear electrical attack if your undergeared or PVP",
            date = "2013-09-09T23:53:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32579#comments:id=1894302",
        },
        {
            id = 1821845,
            score = 0,
            author = "919033",
            text = "teleport back to the seabolt(ship) is at 31.5 , 83.5",
            date = "2013-03-05T21:39:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32579#comments:id=1821845",
        },
    },
    [32580] = {
        {
            id = 1827224,
            score = 19,
            author = "1080315",
            text = "Not too hard to solo.\n\nPull him back toward the cliff wall, kill his raptor pet first, then kite him in a semi circle around the rock avoiding the stuff on the ground.",
            date = "2013-03-12T03:41:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32580#comments:id=1827224",
        },
        {
            id = 1826826,
            score = 8,
            author = "1105776",
            text = "This quest is kinda bugged.   You can pick it up before doing a solo scenario that builds a beachhead for the Alliance.  You can't see him and the party until you complete the solo scenario.\n\nTo fix it, just drop the quest, go back to the ship and pick up both the solo scenario which will show up as a gold quest, and pick up encroaching force again, which will be a blue quest.\n\nDo the Solo Scenario, nothing special, you have help to burn them down, 4 stages to it.   Once that is over you can go to the place on the map for Encroaching Force and you will see him, a mini dinosaur and 4, yes 4, 90 elites, a couple of which stand back and just throw a fire path and an ice path so it keeps you moving.\n\nTake a friend, much easier.",
            date = "2013-03-11T13:32:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32580#comments:id=1826826",
        },
        {
            id = 1880609,
            score = 7,
            author = "pseudostudent",
            text = "On the Alliance side beach, there is a mana orb that will give you a 1-minute buff which increases your haste and reduces the resource cost of your abilities. There is also a Kirin Tor perimeter ward which does damage to nearby enemies.\n\nClick the mana orb to get the buff, then quickly move to the perimeter ward and charge it up by clicking on it. Pull Nurkala from range and move slightly back down the beach so you outrange the healer. The ward will zap Nurkala as he is nearby, but don't get caught up in keeping him there if you need to get more range from the healer. Watch for the two casters' warning lines - as soon as you see them move a few steps left or right.\n\nBurst down Nurkala using your offensive CDs. Once he's dead, run up the path off the beach near the mana orb. The adds will reset after a short chase.",
            date = "2013-07-25T11:45:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32580#comments:id=1880609",
        },
        {
            id = 1828342,
            score = 5,
            author = "alexrocko",
            text = "i pulled him on top of the cliff where alliance has base. the other 2 adds didint bother me and i just killed him using all buffs",
            date = "2013-03-14T02:51:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32580#comments:id=1828342",
        },
        {
            id = 1832049,
            score = 3,
            author = "Eclipsegirl",
            text = "The first time I did him, I was by the eastern sea coast.  I waited  for others to help.\n\nIt did not seem solo-able on the beach itself.\n\nIt was a tough fight.\n\n---------------\nIn Part 3, you get this NPC again to the west of the raptor pens / beast pens on the beach\n\nBeing impatient , and a caster\n\nI took out the raptor first and kited the NPC far way from the middle rocks on the beach\n\nI was far enough away that the other npcs  did not follow and their casts did not affect me.",
            date = "2013-03-20T22:21:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32580#comments:id=1832049",
        },
    },
    [32581] = {
        {
            id = 1824189,
            score = 1,
            author = "Chrome166",
            text = "This quest is given by multiple NPCs. If you finish your last hub and you are not immediately given this quest or another one like it, you probably missed a daily somewhere.",
            date = "2013-03-08T01:18:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32581#comments:id=1824189",
        },
        {
            id = 1846741,
            score = 1,
            author = "Draewind",
            text = "I was left with the debuff \"Thermal Collapse (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=139645#comments)\" after the fight.  The debuff was endless and did 20k damage per second.  I submitted a bug ticket (it is a bug).  The only way to get rid of it is to let it kill you.  It is gone once you rez.",
            date = "2013-04-25T05:18:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32581#comments:id=1846741",
        },
    },
    [32582] = {
        {
            id = 1831470,
            score = 3,
            author = "MarsJenkar",
            text = "BOOOOOONE STOOOOOOORM!",
            date = "2013-03-19T20:37:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32582#comments:id=1831470",
        },
        {
            id = 1832161,
            score = 3,
            author = "122793",
            text = "If you are doing the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32582, he 'may be' located at the pin on the map.  But he is ALSO on the central stairs, coords 54, 45.  (and it is the one on the central stairs you're supposed to be fighting.)\n\nHe's a lot easier there especially for clothies.",
            date = "2013-03-21T04:50:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32582#comments:id=1832161",
        },
        {
            id = 1883474,
            score = 1,
            author = "torin23",
            text = "Note that if he's in the lower part of the map, the easiest way to get to him is to use Skin of the Saurok (quest=32549) to run through Ihgaluk Crag and you can just jump right into where he's at.",
            date = "2013-08-03T02:05:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32582#comments:id=1883474",
        },
    },
    [32583] = {
    },
    [32584] = {
        {
            id = 1827734,
            score = 4,
            author = "1042293",
            text = "Nurkala isn't too bad once you get him away from his adds, no need to kill them.\n\nThe https://www.wowhead.com/npc=70420 heals the boss. Distract, crowd control or kill it first.\nThe https://www.wowhead.com/npc=70419  https://www.wowhead.com/spell=140377 hits you for frost damage.\nThe https://www.wowhead.com/npc=70421  https://www.wowhead.com/spell=140378 hits you for fire damage.\nThe https://www.wowhead.com/npc=70422 (Nurkala's pet) Rend and melee hits you with physical damage.",
            date = "2013-03-12T23:29:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32584#comments:id=1827734",
        },
        {
            id = 1827827,
            score = 3,
            author = "Clandes01",
            text = "The Prophet (for me; your mileage may vary) stayed put when I pulled Nurkala down the beach.  Once his heals were out of the equation, I was able to kill him. Note: the other mobs followed Nurkala and I had to deal with them as well but this made it possible for me to complete the quest.",
            date = "2013-03-13T04:49:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32584#comments:id=1827827",
        },
        {
            id = 1966903,
            score = 1,
            author = "Yogilaw",
            text = "This is a very painful quest, even for those with v.good stats.\n\nYou MUST pull the boss away from his adds (as previously stated). Once out of healing range the problem is the Firespear & Frostspear Zandalari. If you're melee you can't get close enough to them without taking massive damage, so just concentrate on the boss, kill him & then leg it. The dino is an easy kill. You need to run around a bit to try & avoid the frost/fire damage which works as a narrow cone  from the casters.\nI died twice doing this (& that's with 540+ilvl), so how a freshman is supposed to accomplish this if they're melee is beyond me.\nStill if you learn from your 1st attempts it should get easier.\n\nGood luck.",
            date = "2014-05-22T02:01:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32584#comments:id=1966903",
        },
    },
    [32585] = {
        {
            id = 1952182,
            score = 1,
            author = "Wimbleton",
            text = "Kill the Prophet first because that way he can't heal Nurkala. Otherwise, you'll be beating on Nurkala for a dog's age. But then things get interesting. I didn't know that Nurkala respawns really quickly. I stuck around after killing him the first time to knock off one of the other guys. While I was doing that, Nurkala respawned and I killed them both. 110 Black Prince points on the second round for killing Nurkala, so not all bad.\n\nBut then Nurkala went into insta-respawn mode. At that point I was feeling like Groundhog Day, so I split. And he chased me, along with his two companions, all the way back to the Violet Rise - the Alliance Camp. And no Alliance soldiers or anyone else helped out either, I might add. Fair weather friends indeed.\n\nI killed him for the 3rd time on the steps leading into the camp (110 more BP points) and that seemed to do it. The other two ran back to their campfire. Weird, but not tough, and there were those rep points...",
            date = "2014-03-19T12:22:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32585#comments:id=1952182",
        },
    },
    [32586] = {
        {
            id = 1835126,
            score = 26,
            author = "894678",
            text = "You start the quest yourself.\n\nThe entrance to the mine is  /way 54.30, 28.79\n\nMetal Lord Mono-Han is wondering around outside of the entrance. Once inside the mine just look on your map for the little gear symbols for the location of the drills. It's a no brainer.\n\nIf you don't have any type of coordinate addon go to The Emperor's Gate and run up the long set of steps.\n\nIf you don't know where The Emperor's Gate is at either open your map and locate the building above Diremoor behind the building there will be a bold solid tan line follow it North East and at the end of that bold solid tan line are the steps to The Emperor's Gate.\n\nOnce at the top turn left and into The Bloodied Crossing it will be the only opening as of right now. Continue down the steps then make the 1st right you can then make the 1st left that you can.\n\nGo down the steps and look straight ahead 100 yards there is an opening between a full statue on the left and half a statue on the right that is your opening into the mine and once inside just open your map and look for the little gear symbols for the location of the drills.\nGood luck and have fun!\n\nOk it's kinda hard to explain locations when there on different levels but when you 1st go into the cave you can go left or right but look straight ahead and there is a ledge with a small rock in front of it. Jump up onto that rock and go thru the opening then follow it into the big room and that's the upper level one.\n\nThe other 2 are on the lower level just come back out the same way then go to your right and jump down one will be back to your right the other back to your left.\n\nThere is another entrance / exit to this cave as well I use it to exit not to enter but at  /way 31.64 88.02  it brings you out into the Beast Pens. You could enter here if you wanted I just choose to exit then mount up and run back around to do the follow up quest instead of fighting my way back out. Hope it helps but cords are hard when you got different levels.",
            date = "2013-03-27T05:34:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32586#comments:id=1835126",
        },
        {
            id = 1835534,
            score = 4,
            author = "SierraFred",
            text = "Edit:\nI found that if I jumped off a shelf & went underneath I could find the other capacitor. Then, don't bother looking for the Metal-Lord inside. As the previous comment said, he is outside. The next two quest bosses are nearby, as well.\nHope you are quicker than I was!",
            date = "2013-03-27T20:32:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32586#comments:id=1835534",
        },
        {
            id = 1835521,
            score = 2,
            author = "SierraFred",
            text = "Been running around in the mine for about an hour now (well, maybe 20-30 minutes) and have killed many mobs. Only found one capacitor so far. Certainly have the cogwheels on the map, but no way to get to them. Do you have to enter different entrances (I think there are at least three) to find the other capacitors? Very frustrating.",
            date = "2013-03-27T19:58:53-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32586#comments:id=1835521",
        },
        {
            id = 1890857,
            score = 1,
            author = "985653",
            text = "I can get this done in less than 2 minutes on my Engineering Hunter utilizing Aspect of the Cheetah (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=5118) for speed, Camouflage (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=51753) to bypass mobs (just try not to get too close), Feign Death (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=5384) just in case I aggro & the tinker Invisibility Field (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=84424) just in case Camouflage (http://www.wowhead.com/spell=51753) is on cooldown. Make sure you dismiss your pet so it won't aggro.\n\nI go straight in and make a left, run all the way down to the drill at the end, on my way back up I make a left into the alcove (not the small bridge) and go to drill at the end, I run back to where I was and head back up and out of the hallway, then I go to the drill across the way in the other alcove, then I turn back and head back out through the south east exit.\n\nI then kill Metal Lord Mono-Han (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=69326) which is very easy to do with a hunter. Just cast Misdirection on your pet and shoot him down.",
            date = "2013-08-28T04:23:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32586#comments:id=1890857",
        },
        {
            id = 1986178,
            score = 1,
            author = "WokkaD",
            text = "There are several entrances :\n\n31.82 88.43  in The Beast Pens\n\n54.39 28.88 in the temple (past Itoka)",
            date = "2014-07-29T21:57:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32586#comments:id=1986178",
        },
    },
    [32587] = {
        {
            id = 1835999,
            score = 22,
            author = "910459",
            text = "I am privileged to be the very first to make this comment on this daily especially after I died just once. I tried to figure this out and quickly found the obvious way, so here it is..\n\nAfter you have entered the area and engage Itoka he will stomp out tonnes of aoe boulders in your way, strafe away from them and watch out for the lightening charges within the red circles that wander slowly around, they will do a lot of damage but are easy to avoid.\n\nP2 - He will begin to cast out his protection shell so you will have to take out all four conductors that keep him there again avoiding the circles that move around. So if you walk on the rocks and stand on the ones that look like grave stones you will be able to go right up to each conductor and switch them off via the cog until all four are done and Itoka is released from his shell. (WARNING,  do NOT tread on static electric or you will probably die within 5 seconds !),\nItoka will then commence his fight with you but you will still have to avoid his aoe damage abilities till you have nuked him down.\n\nNote;- He only casts this electric once, apart from that he doesn't do any real damage ( as much as the rest of the quest bosses that are round there ),  as long as you follow these steps you will be fine and should be a fairly easy and straight forward fight.. Have fun!",
            date = "2013-03-28T22:24:00-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32587#comments:id=1835999",
        },
        {
            id = 1843000,
            score = 20,
            author = "1070850",
            text = "If you manage to abandon/not accept this quest, it is actually given by Scout Captain Daelin at his location in Conqueror's Terrace after you have completed the previous part in the chain.",
            date = "2013-04-14T08:33:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32587#comments:id=1843000",
        },
        {
            id = 2861525,
            score = 11,
            author = "salic",
            text = "Seems to be a bug in 8.1 that doesn't let you actually auto-accept this quest.  You can however still pick it up from whatever hub you picked up \"On Her Magic-ey Secret Service\" from or whatever quest led you into the mines.",
            date = "2018-12-23T16:49:08-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32587#comments:id=2861525",
        },
        {
            id = 1837858,
            score = 6,
            author = "Eillesthis",
            text = "Short summary - take your time during the bubble phase.  There's literally no rush, and stepping in the water instead of on the stones will totally kill you, and thus slow you down.",
            date = "2013-04-02T00:25:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32587#comments:id=1837858",
        },
        {
            id = 1860751,
            score = 6,
            author = "845973",
            text = "When completing this quest, I STRONGLY recomend killing https://www.wowhead.com/npc=69435 first to obtain the https://www.wowhead.com/item=93731.  Killing https://www.wowhead.com/npc=69435 gives you the opportunity to gain https://www.wowhead.com/spell=136980 by killing https://www.wowhead.com/npc=69436.  This buff gives you +10% damage and stacks up to 12 times.  This makes the first phase of https://www.wowhead.com/npc=69461 fly past, especially if there is a group of you killing him.  Best way to max your stacks is to stand on https://www.wowhead.com/npc=69435 when he starts summoning the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=69436 and just AoE the living %&$* out of them.  Once he is dead, run straight back to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=69461 and let rip.  As bookmarker states below, the bubble phase is a time to sit back and re-gather yourself, but unless you have people ready to deactivate the pylons, you will lose the https://www.wowhead.com/spell=136980 by the time the third phase starts.",
            date = "2013-05-31T10:53:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32587#comments:id=1860751",
        },
    },
    [32588] = {
        {
            id = 1836364,
            score = 40,
            author = "Calisim",
            text = "For the morons among us (/me raises hand)....\n\nYou free the captives by using the quest item you're given.  Took me a little while to figure that out.  For the one hanging on the wall/pillar thing, you have to get up onto the lower ledge of it.",
            date = "2013-03-29T16:28:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32588#comments:id=1836364",
        },
        {
            id = 1835172,
            score = 30,
            author = "894678",
            text = "This is just like the quest..... https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32586\n\nThe entrance to the mine is /way 54.30, 28.79\n\nMetal Lord Mono-Han is wondering around outside of the entrance. Once inside the mine just look on your map for the little gear symbols for the location of the agents. It's a no brainer.\n\nIf you don't have any type of coordinate addon go to The Emperor's Gate and run up the long set of steps.\n\nIf you don't know where The Emperor's Gate is at either open your map and locate the building above Diremoor behind the building there will be a bold solid tan line follow it North East and at the end of that bold solid tan line are the steps to The Emperor's Gate.\n\nOnce at the top turn left and into The Bloodied Crossing it will be the only opening as of right now. Continue down the steps then make the 1st right you can then make the 1st left that you can.\n\nGo down the steps and look straight ahead 100 yards there is an opening between a full statue on the left and half a statue on the right that is your opening into the mine and once inside just open your map and look for the little gear symbols for the location of the agents.\nGood luck and have fun!",
            date = "2013-03-27T07:57:03-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32588#comments:id=1835172",
        },
        {
            id = 5864500,
            score = 17,
            author = "Ravij",
            text = "If you're a Druid doing this, make sure you're not in a druid form when you use the rod. You must be in your humanoid form when you use the rod to free the prisoners. As an addition to this, if you get the scroll off a mob that turns you invisible, you have to get rid of it or else you'll run into the same issue as Druids.\n\nThis seems to be a remix issue but might happen in retail as well.",
            date = "2024-05-24T12:04:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32588#comments:id=5864500",
        },
        {
            id = 1793323,
            score = 15,
            author = "Drahken",
            text = "Oh my god, ow. This quest name is a painful pun. I hope they keep it.",
            date = "2013-01-05T21:13:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32588#comments:id=1793323",
        },
        {
            id = 1837254,
            score = 12,
            author = "157913",
            text = "This quest can be a bit annoying - it's very easy for the quest item's channel to be interrupted. It may feel like it's being interrupted for no reason, but it seems to be that it's actually buffs fading from you that causes it. So, if you leave combat with some short-term buffs up (weapon enchant, trinket proc, etc.), those will interrupt the channel when they fade. You can prevent this by right-clicking off any buffs with less than 10 sec of duration left before starting the channel. Annoying, but it's the best you can do unless and until Bliz patches this.",
            date = "2013-03-31T16:35:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32588#comments:id=1837254",
        },
    },
    [32589] = {
        {
            id = 1829576,
            score = 112,
            author = "Comett",
            text = "This quest can now be completed in LFR (Halls of Flesh-Shaping) once the 3rd part of Throne of Thunder (npc=69427) will be unlocked on April 3rd (http://eu.battle.net/wow/en/blog/7477687/Throne_of_Thunder_Raid_Schedule%E2%80%94Updated-05_03_2013) (EU). Otherwise you can already complete in normal difficulty.\n\nIt's somehow frustrating that it yields 1000rep (2000 with https://www.wowhead.com/item=95548) toward Sunreaver Onslaught (faction=1388) when we just got exalted with them... Would have been nice toward [faction=1435] :)",
            date = "2013-03-16T10:09:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32589#comments:id=1829576",
        },
        {
            id = 1829152,
            score = 54,
            author = "iuha",
            text = "Just got exalted with the [faction=1388] and got this quest as well.\nYou don't need to unlock the other stage areas to complete this quest.\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=69427 is a boss within [zone=6622] raid.\nYou just need a raid to go kill and use the https://www.wowhead.com/item=94123 on him and loot https://www.wowhead.com/item=94116.",
            date = "2013-03-15T11:36:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32589#comments:id=1829152",
        },
        {
            id = 1828135,
            score = 39,
            author = "1106300",
            text = "Just hit exalted with Sunreaver Onslaught today, and can confirm this quest becomes available, even with the server at only stage 2.\n\nEdit: Interesting to note, after completing this quest, a miniature Anima Golem appears near the map that starts the quests, and buffs you with a 30 minute buff granting +15% damage on the Isle of Thunder.",
            date = "2013-03-13T16:55:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32589#comments:id=1828135",
        },
        {
            id = 1831286,
            score = 23,
            author = "MietoxD",
            text = "After completing the quest, you'll trigger a short RP, after which a friendly https://www.wowhead.com/npc=69784 will spawn. Going near it will grant you the buff https://www.wowhead.com/spell=138143, lasting 30 minutes.",
            date = "2013-03-19T13:51:59-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32589#comments:id=1831286",
        },
        {
            id = 1839570,
            score = 23,
            author = "179086",
            text = "If you're like me, you'd spent more than 3 weeks from picking up the quest to being able to kill Dark Animus.\n\nIn that time, I'd COMPLETELY forgotten that you had to use the stupid attunement crystal in order to receive the quest item.\n\nWhen I did kill the boss, it was spockling like it had loot, but I couldn't loot it.  Naturally assuming that Blizzard had made yet ANOTHER mistake, I left the instance and sent in a GM ticket.\n\nIt was only when I was checking forums for other people reporting the same issue that I realised \"THE CRYSTAL!\".\n\nWent back in and boss had despawned.\n\nDon't be like me.  Remember the crystal.",
            date = "2013-04-05T23:15:53-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32589#comments:id=1839570",
        },
    },
    [32599] = {
        {
            id = 1828237,
            score = 137,
            author = "Tyro",
            text = "Jaina Proudmoore (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=69741) gives you this quest when you hit exalted with the Kirin Tor offensive (http://www.wowhead.com/faction=1387).  You have to kill Lei Shen (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=68397), the final boss of the Throne of Thunder raid, to charge the staff she gives you.  Presumably This can be done in any difficulty, including LFR (now open!).  However, the final \"Pinnacle of Storms\" LFR raid does not open up until April 16th, 2013.\n\nThe spot on the map for the quest is just where the raid entrance is.\n\nOnce you kill Lei Shen, don't leave the instance right away!  Go to the middle of the room and click on the staff to get the quest completion.  Finally, head back to Jaina and you're done.",
            date = "2013-03-13T21:24:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32599#comments:id=1828237",
        },
        {
            id = 1829292,
            score = 87,
            author = "Malvenue",
            text = "It's interesting to note the Horde equivalent of this quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32589 only requires you to kill the 9th boss in Throne of Thunder, not the final boss.",
            date = "2013-03-15T16:54:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32599#comments:id=1829292",
        },
        {
            id = 1831333,
            score = 56,
            author = "mysticalos",
            text = "Upon completion of quest, you not only get the banner it mentions, you also get this buff every time you walk by Jaina\n\n[spell=139119 domain=www]\n\nWalk to jaina, she casts this buff on you if you don't already have it. So for grinding out kirintor exalted and defeating thunder king, you get to do, MORE DAILIES (but faster)\n\nAlso note, the trolls in zatual will dispel [spell=139119 domain=www] and annoy crap out of you when your daily hub is that area.",
            date = "2013-03-19T15:14:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32599#comments:id=1831333",
        },
        {
            id = 1832407,
            score = 48,
            author = "madmurdock",
            text = "In case for being at least as dumb as I am: DO NOT run to the position showed on the map. It is inside the raid instance... not in the daily questing zone.",
            date = "2013-03-21T14:52:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32599#comments:id=1832407",
        },
        {
            id = 1827880,
            score = 36,
            author = "Gart",
            text = "You receive this quest once you have reached exalted with the Kirin Tor offensive.",
            date = "2013-03-13T07:12:11-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32599#comments:id=1827880",
        },
    },
    [32600] = {
        {
            id = 2623597,
            score = 23,
            author = "Trollokdamus",
            text = "As of BfA, both Rastakhan and Zul's models have been updated for this story.",
            date = "2018-10-14T15:46:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32600#comments:id=2623597",
        },
        {
            id = 1819446,
            score = 16,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "Starts from a quest item (http://ptr.wowhead.com/item=94197) mailed to the player upon completion of the achievement The Zandalari Prophecy (http://ptr.wowhead.com/achievement=8049).\n\nWhen you turn in the quest, Lorewalker Cho tells you a story complete with a play-like reenactment and casts Storytime (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=120589) on the player.\n\nIt is said the God King Rastakhan, ruler of the Zandalari, lords over his mighty kingdom from a throne carved of solid gold.  Years ago, as he sat on this opulent seat of power, he was visited by his most trusted prophet: Zul.\n\nZul warned King Rastakhan of a terrible Cataclysm.  For Zul had seen a vision of a great armored dragon clenching the world in his ferocious jaws.  King Rastakhan did nothing.\n\nMonths later Zul returned, bearing more grim news from his visions.  He saw a legion of serpents pouring forth from a gaping fissure that tore open the floor of the ocean.  Still, King Rastakhan did nothing.\n\nFinally, mere months before the Cataclysm, Zul returned.  Tearing his clothes and throwing down his staff to the ground, Zul spoke of earthquakes and tidal waves.  He described the golden capital of Zandalar slowly sinking beneath the waves in the aftermath of the Cataclysm, its once-great people drowning as their mighty works slipped forever beneath the sea.\n\nKing Rastakhan grew tired of Zul and his troubling nightmares.  To be rid of the prophet, he granted Zul the use of his largest ships, so that he and his followers could seek a new land if his visions came to pass.  And his visions DID come to pass.\n\nWhen Deathwing rose from the Maelstrom, dark, angry waves crashed into the Zandalari capital.  The spine of the land broke in two, and soon, the city and all its riches began to slide into the hungry sea.  The Zandalari people turned to their King for help, but there was only one Zandalari equipped to help them: the prophet Zul.  The prophet, and the mighty warfleet he had assembled while his King sat idle.\n\nYou see, the TRUE power of kings and emperors stems from the power to aid their people.  The moment they fail, they cede their power to one who can.\n\nYou can have Lorewalker Cho tell the story again by talking to him or clicking on the book that is added to your bookcase in the Seat of Knowledge.",
            date = "2013-02-28T23:09:16-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32600#comments:id=1819446",
        },
    },
    [32601] = {
        {
            id = 1819456,
            score = 9,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "Starts from a quest item (http://ptr.wowhead.com/item=94198) mailed to the player upon completion of the achievement Rumbles of Thunder (http://ptr.wowhead.com/achievement=8050).\n\nWhen you turn in the quest, Lorewalker Cho tells you a story complete with a play-like reenactment and casts Storytime (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=120589) on the player.\n\nThe mogu tell a legend about Lei Shen, the Thunder King.\n\nIt is said that he tore out the very heart of the mogu God.  And from that hateful act he gained power over wind and storm.  His followers fell to their knees before him.  \"We will call you 'The Lightning King',\" they said.  But Lei Shen did not agree.\n\n\"Lightning strikes in an instant and is over in a flash,\" he said.  \"But, thunder.  Thunder!  Thunder proclaims the coming of the storm.  Thunder quakes the skies long before the lightning strikes, and thunder echoes in the hills long after lightning's power is spent.  It is thunder that sends animals cowering and fills the hearts of peasants with dread.  Let thunder be my herald, so that my power is felt throughout the land.\"\n\n\"I will be... The Thunder King.\"\n\nOh my friend - that awful sound.  For a hundred hundred generations the crash of thunder filled the hearts of pandaren with terror.\n\nIt is said that after the revolution, the Red Crane of Hope placed the rainbow in the sky, so that pandaren would know not to fear the storms any longer.\n\nI do not see any rainbows today.  Do you?\n\nYou can have Lorewalker Cho tell the story again by talking to him or clicking on the book that is added to your bookcase in the Seat of Knowledge.",
            date = "2013-02-28T23:25:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32601#comments:id=1819456",
        },
        {
            id = 5384500,
            score = 8,
            author = "AKiceberg",
            text = "If you are late to the party as I am and doing this/these achievements at level 60, you will have to talk to Zidormi outside on the balcony to get Loremaster Cho to talk to you so you can hand in your quest(s).  Don't forget to talk to Zidormi again when you are done to go back to the future!",
            date = "2022-06-14T08:03:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32601#comments:id=5384500",
        },
        {
            id = 2485774,
            score = 6,
            author = "1129093",
            text = "Thunder quakes the skies long before the lightning strikes\nNo, Lei Shen, first you see lightning, then you hear thunder.",
            date = "2017-04-11T14:13:20-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32601#comments:id=2485774",
        },
    },
    [32602] = {
        {
            id = 1841560,
            score = 34,
            author = "Chonar",
            text = "Truly this is one of the best stories the good Lorewalker can tell us. If only for all the cameos in his story; Deathwing and Wrathion, Terenas and Arthas.. Superb.",
            date = "2013-04-10T17:54:30-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32602#comments:id=1841560",
        },
        {
            id = 1819017,
            score = 19,
            author = "Calesta",
            text = "Starts from a quest item (ptr.wowhead.com/item=94199) mailed to the player upon completion of the achievement Gods and Monsters (http://ptr.wowhead.com/achievement=8051).\n\nWhen you turn in the quest, Lorewalker Cho tells you a story complete with a play-like reenactment and casts Storytime (http://mop.wowhead.com/spell=120589) on the player.\n\nFathers and sons.  Mothers and daughters.  As parents, we pass our legacy on to our children.\n\nWhat values do we choose to install in our progeny?  What will our children learn from our mistakes?  What sort of world will we create and leave behind for our daughters and sons?\n\nParents place their children on a path, but they do not always know where the road will take them.\n\nThe mogu were children as well.  Children of the titans.  They were once a legion of stone, heartless and obedient.  By the titans' command, they fought the terrible servants of the old gods.  They shaped the mountains and carved the rivers of the land.  And they created a magical cradle of life in a hidden valley that we now call the Vale of the Eternal Blossoms.\n\nBut eventually, the titans fell silent.  And their creations were cursed with flesh.  The mogu grew restless.  Many generations later, when the Thunder King united them, they seized upon their legacy!\n\nI truly believe now that the mogu thought they were doing the work of the titans.  They fought against the mantid and used the powers of the Vale to create new life.  Ah, but such terrible works!\n\nParents cannot always be assured of the legacy they will leave behind.   How especially true this is, when the parents are gods.  And their children - monsters.\n\nYou can have Lorewalker Cho tell the story again by talking to him or clicking on the book that is added to your bookcase in the Seat of Knowledge.",
            date = "2013-02-27T19:31:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32602#comments:id=1819017",
        },
        {
            id = 3282062,
            score = 19,
            author = "Tibast2willow",
            text = "If you have trouble handing in these quests post BFA, talk to Zidormi outside the seat to show you the earlier version of the vale",
            date = "2020-12-29T05:13:38-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32602#comments:id=3282062",
        },
        {
            id = 1943963,
            score = 7,
            author = "sitecow09",
            text = "\"I sought only to finish... the work of the gods...\" -Lei Shen upon his death\n\nThis finally explains why the Mogu were so obsessed with bringing everything (and everyone) under their order and control: The Titans were the ones who ordered Azeroth and saved it from the chaos of the Old Gods and their elemental servants (Ragnaros, Al'akir, etc). However, the Mogu mistook the Titan's policy of Lawful Good (\"law and order help maintain freedom and prosperity\") for Lawful Evil (\"I will bring peace to this world, no matter who I have to tread on to achieve it!\"). In addition, the pride of being the \"children of the Gods\" likely contributed to their feelings of supremacy over the other races.\n\nThey genuinely believed themselves to be agents of order, bringing peace to a chaotic world. An admirable sentiment, but it led to countless deaths, enslavement of the other races, and eventually, their own downfall.",
            date = "2014-02-16T16:10:29-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32602#comments:id=1943963",
        },
        {
            id = 2086358,
            score = 1,
            author = "robertalexstorm",
            text = "Great story. Glad I can watch this again. :)",
            date = "2015-01-10T20:04:47-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32602#comments:id=2086358",
        },
    },
