    [32630] = {
        {
            id = 1804669,
            score = 52,
            author = "1080988",
            text = "My first post so please forgive if i havent done it right...\n\nFrom what ive read and done on PTR it seems this will be the Engineering version of  Living Steel Ingot; [item=94111 domain=ptr] for Smiths. It's rumored to drop from Itoka; [npc=69461 domain=ptr] and will teach you how to craft Stabilized Lightning Source; [item=94113 domain=ptr].   from what i understand it can only be made once per day; similarly to the smiths version Lightning Steel Ingot and Living Steel [item=72104 domain=ptr] for alchemists.  This item, so far, will be used to make the new 2 person Engineer mount; [item=95416 domain=ptr], a pet [spell=139196 domain=ptr] and a cooking bag [spell=139197 domain=ptr]",
            date = "2013-01-26T20:10:33-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32630#comments:id=1804669",
        },
        {
            id = 1815812,
            score = 14,
            author = "RCMK",
            text = "This quest is finally added in the latest PTR build, https://www.wowhead.com/npc=69461 drops the item (https://www.wowhead.com/item=94862) for engineers to start it. Next to a https://www.wowhead.com/item=94113 you will get the https://www.wowhead.com/item=94847.\n\nWhen opening this you will get 4 schematics:\n\nSchematic: Advances Refridgeration Unit\nSchematic: Pierre\nSchematic: Sky Claw\nSchematic: Stabilized Lightning Source\n\nHappy crafting!",
            date = "2013-02-19T19:55:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32630#comments:id=1815812",
        },
        {
            id = 1835109,
            score = 5,
            author = "Mildan",
            text = "This quest was intended for the patch 5.2, but Blizzard didn't add this in the last moments anyways. They said that they weren't ready with the Skyclaw mount and would rather wait until it was ready with adding it, and my guess is that they then saw no reason to add the https://www.wowhead.com/item=94113 to the game for engineers.\nSo we got nothing new this patch, but in the future we have a Skyclaw to look forward to!",
            date = "2013-03-27T04:50:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32630#comments:id=1835109",
        },
        {
            id = 1897765,
            score = 3,
            author = "Driva",
            text = "This quest is not in patch 5.4. Now you only loot https://www.wowhead.com/item=94847, a world drop that drops if you have 600 in engineering. You don't need to be level 90 for it to drop.",
            date = "2013-09-14T09:53:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32630#comments:id=1897765",
        },
        {
            id = 1881644,
            score = 2,
            author = "Miztahchipz",
            text = "SKY GOLEM For what its worth I thought I would pass on what info I could as of 7/28/13 8AM EST.  I've spent a lot of time searching the net, fan sites, and playing the 5.4 PTR and managed to find a few things out, but none of which is absolute when it goes live.\n\nSKY GOLEM is the craziest of all engineering mounts, imo.  Its a ton of fun to fly, swaying back and forth, side to side, barrel rolls w/a turbo boost all while bouncing off anything you get too close to!  The Sky Golem transforms into a robot on the ground.  You sit atop his chest which is a big, mean goblin head and the whole thing shakes, ratttles, and rolls with all kinds of steam, whistles, buzzing, and so on.\n\nIn the Vale of Eternal Blossoms that has been corrupted by the Sha, you (an engineer of either type) can get a drop of Schematic: Chief Engineer Jard's Journal off presumably any mob here.  I don't know if it has to be a mob that's corrupted, but I went with that since it seemed logical based on the research I had done.  My journal drop was on my 6th kill, so it didn't take long at all.\n\nThe journal contained 5 new item recipes:\n\n1) Jard's Peculiar Energy Source  ***CAN BE MADE ONCE PER DAY***\n2) Sky Golem\n3) Pierre\n4) Rascal-Bot\n5) Advanced Refrigeration Unit\n\nI can't confirm the journal will have all 5 recipes when 5.4 goes live, but it seems to be what most fan site's reader's comments think.\n\nThe possible good news  about the Sky Golem mount is it at least in PTR it looks like any class can (and did, LOL) have one and is account wide.  This I base ONLY on what I saw in PTR.  Since there is some potentially pretty nasty bad news, I wonder if Blizz may make it a profession specific mount only.\n\nThe possible bad news has to do with the mats which at least for PTR are the following:\n\n1) Quantity 30 of Jard's Peculiar Energy Source ***DAILY CD***\n2) Quantity 30 of Living Steel\n\nI only notated the Jard's Peculiar Energy Source as being once per day because I didn't know if any of the other items, both new and old, will or will still have a daily CD.  I'm not a pro at this, just trying to help a bit :)\n\nNeedless to say, if the numbers and the daily CD is accurate once live it will be a month before we see SKY GOLEMs roaming our lands and skies... and maybe seas too!  Further more, it may be even longer before someone is willing to sell theirs as I would expect most engineers would want to keep the first one for themselves.  Of course there may be a few people out there like me who have at least 2 engineers that are level 90 and the profession maxed (I wanted to be able to make both new rockets in MoP), who may have one for sale in a month.\n\nI guess its possible that Blizz won't(?) make the Jard's Peculiar Energy Source soulbound so that they can be sold on the AH and in trade chat. That would surely make it one of the hottest & costly mats in trade. Regardless, those with a maxed engineer will have to create and/or come up with a stack of mats and those who don't will have to come up with a much, MUCH, MUCH, MUCH, MUCH BIGGER stack of gold to get one of the first up for grabs!\n\nHope this helps to answer some questions, gather a few thoughts, and perhaps start planning a strategy to be one of the first to get one of these crazy awesome mounts!  Best of luck to all!",
            date = "2013-07-28T10:48:37-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32630#comments:id=1881644",
        },
    },
