    [32640] = {
        {
            id = 1830180,
            score = 80,
            author = "1047022",
            text = "As of today (3/17/2013), the posting for Champions type is incorrect.  The correct Champion listing is as follows:\n\nLightning\n\nAncient Mogu Guardian (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=69767) (53.2, 47.6)\nElectromancer Ju'le (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=69339) (44.6, 60.6)\nQi'nor (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=69749) (48, 25.4)\n\nPrimal\n\nCera (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=69396) (33.2, 46)\nIncomplete Drakkari Colossus (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=69347) (49.6, 20.4)\nWindweaver Akil'amon (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=70080) (69.2, 39)\n\nSpirit\n\nEcho of Kros (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=69341) (55, 87.6)\nKor'dok (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=69633) (31, 58)\nSpirit of Warlord Teng (http://www.wowhead.com/npc=69471#comments) (35, 64)\n\nA complete list of their abilities can be found in the Wowhead 5.2 - Isle of Thunder, Summoned Elites Guide (http://www.wowhead.com/guide=1132/rare-elites-of-pandaria-glorious-5-1-5-2#5-2-isle-of-thunder-summoned-elites)",
            date = "2013-03-17T12:16:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32640#comments:id=1830180",
        },
        {
            id = 1823116,
            score = 52,
            author = "695019",
            text = "The two I've experienced/completed thus far:\n\nCera is a Primal Champion located in a small cave on the west coast of the Isle of Thunder.\nThe cave is reached by water. Approximate coords 31, 46.\n\nNotes of importance:\n-Requires 3xhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=94221 to summon.\n-Counts as a Primal Champion for the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32640.\n-Cannot be completed as a raid group.\n-Five players recommended (currently). Healer necessary. Tank necessary to a point. A plate DPS holding aggro and a competent healer with suffice.\n- Primary abilities: frontal cone attack (has ground effect). Cleave attacks.\n\n----------------------------------------------\n\nElectromancer Ju'le is a Lightning Champion located in the structure in the center of the first stage area of Isle of Thunder. Just northwest of Diremoor text on the map. Look for the outside platform with a spiral lightning rod statue.\n\nNotes of importance:\n-Requires 3x https://www.wowhead.com/item=94221 to summon.\n-Counts as a Lightning Champion for the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32640.\n-Cannot be completed as a raid group.\n-Five players recommended (currently). Healer necessary. Tank necessary to a point. A plate DPS holding aggro and a competent healer with suffice.\n- Primary abilities: Ground AOE that should be avoided. Dishes out a debuff that deals damage over time and stacks. One stack is easily healed, but once you reach two-three stacks you will want to click on the lightning rod -once- to clear your stacks. Doing so spawns an elemental that should be focused down.",
            date = "2013-03-06T19:43:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32640#comments:id=1823116",
        },
        {
            id = 1824592,
            score = 39,
            author = "975146",
            text = "Kros from the previous quest in the chain counts towards the spirit beast portion of this one. He's easier than the spirit beast you'd otherwise have to summon (the stone is in the same location as where you summon Kros slightly East).\n\nJust help out with a Kros group and kill him again and you'll get credit for the spirit portion, without using your own stones.",
            date = "2013-03-08T13:25:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32640#comments:id=1824592",
        },
        {
            id = 2524853,
            score = 34,
            author = "MarUlberg",
            text = "After finishing this quest today and being very upset in the lack of reward. I realised that this is a 5 man quest and each person is suppose to throw in about 2x Ritual Stones each. If you are solo, abandon this quest. The work of gathering 9xRitual Stones is not worth the 300 reputation with Shado-Pan Assault.",
            date = "2017-09-20T10:04:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32640#comments:id=2524853",
        },
        {
            id = 1835136,
            score = 30,
            author = "dartworth",
            text = "Here is a helpful addon for The Isle of Thunder  (http://www.wowhead.com/zone=6507/isle-of-thunder)\n\nIsle of Thunder Weekly Check (http://www.curse.com/addons/wow/isle-thunder-weekly-items)\n\nThs Isle of Thunder has a few \"once per week\" events for every character. These are not account wide so you can complete these events with every level 90 character, but it's not easy to remember which character has killed a rare.. or whether you should be looking around the isle for a trove. That's where \"Isle of Thunder Weekly Check\" can be very handy. It opens a window with a list of possible events and whether or not the current character has completed them.\n\nWe only know of 6 once a week \"events\" at the moment:\n\nDropping https://www.wowhead.com/item=94222 for the single player scenario [zone=6716].\nLooting the https://www.wowhead.com/item=94221 from the first rare monster killed.\nOpening a trove around the island (the yellow chest) which rewards a https://www.wowhead.com/item=94221.\nCompleting the quest Champions of the Thunder King (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=32640/champions-of-the-thunder-king)\nLooting one of the summoning incantations:  https://www.wowhead.com/item=94233, https://www.wowhead.com/item=93803,  https://www.wowhead.com/item=95350. These are also needed for the achievement These Mogu Have Gotta Go-gu (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=8110)\n[\nCompleting the quest The Crumbled Chamberlain (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=32505/the-crumbled-chamberlain).",
            date = "2013-03-27T06:01:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32640#comments:id=1835136",
        },
    },
    [32641] = {
        {
            id = 1823117,
            score = 62,
            author = "695019",
            text = "The two I've experienced/completed thus far:\n\nCera is a Primal Champion located in a small cave on the west coast of the Isle of Thunder.\nThe cave is reached by water. Approximate coords 31, 46.\n\nNotes of importance:\n-Requires 3xhttps://www.wowhead.com/item=94221 to summon.\n-Counts as a Primal Champion for the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32640.\n-Cannot be completed as a raid group.\n-Five players recommended (currently). Healer necessary. Tank necessary to a point. A plate DPS holding aggro and a competent healer with suffice.\n- Primary abilities: frontal cone attack (has ground effect). Cleave attacks.\n\n----------------------------------------------\n\nElectromancer Ju'le is a Lightning Champion located in the structure in the center of the first stage area of Isle of Thunder. Just northwest of Diremoor text on the map. Look for the outside platform with a spiral lightning rod statue.\n\nNotes of importance:\n-Requires 3x https://www.wowhead.com/item=94221 to summon.\n-Counts as a Lightning Champion for the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32640.\n-Cannot be completed as a raid group.\n-Five players recommended (currently). Healer necessary. Tank necessary to a point. A plate DPS holding aggro and a competent healer with suffice.\n- Primary abilities: Ground AOE that should be avoided. Dishes out a debuff that deals damage over time and stacks. One stack is easily healed, but once you reach two-three stacks you will want to click on the lightning rod -once- to clear your stacks. Doing so spawns an elemental that should be focused down.",
            date = "2013-03-06T19:43:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32641#comments:id=1823117",
        },
        {
            id = 1823638,
            score = 31,
            author = "eighty8",
            text = "Kor'dok is a Spiritual Champion located on the island at approx 31, 59 in the Court of Bones and counts towards https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32640\n\nNotes:\nRequires 3x https://www.wowhead.com/item=94221 to summon\n\nIs pretty much a tank and spank fight with one twist, he will summon a spirit at about 50% health that will deal damage and will cast a spell on 1 person that will redirect all heals towards the Spirit.\n\nKilling Kor'dok and ignoring the spirit is how we completed this part.",
            date = "2013-03-07T10:15:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32641#comments:id=1823638",
        },
        {
            id = 1824850,
            score = 21,
            author = "WizzardlordUK",
            text = "You will need a total of 3 x 3 https://www.wowhead.com/item=94221 (9 in total) Only 1 person needs to summon each mob at the cost of 3 x https://www.wowhead.com/item=94221 (3 players with 1 each will not work.)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1. Spirit Champion = https://www.wowhead.com/npc=69633\nLocation = Hall of Grand Imperion - Entrance to hall can be found on beach 33.57, 63.14\n\nSpecial Abilities:\n\nGround Attack - much like any other ground attack that does high dmg move to avoid.\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2. Lightning Champion = https://www.wowhead.com/npc=69339\nLocation = in a building behind Horgak the Enslaver 44.73, 60,65\n\nSpecial Abilities:\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/spell=137884\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/spell=136691 Stacks (Will spawn an add if cleansed, players should take these out as priority)\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/spell=138003\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3. Primal Chamion = https://www.wowhead.com/npc=69396\nLocation = in a cave east of map - entrance = 58.96, 79.63\n\nSpecial Abilities:\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/spell=136866\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/spell=136865\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/spell=138660\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ntomtom cut n paste coords\n\n/way 44.73, 60.65 Electromancer Ju'le\n/way 33.57, 63.14 Kor'dok\n/way 58.96, 79.63 Cera",
            date = "2013-03-08T20:03:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32641#comments:id=1824850",
        },
        {
            id = 1827559,
            score = 21,
            author = "Tristos",
            text = "When all players in your party die while fighting one of the summoned mobs you will need 3 new Shan'ze Ritual Stone (http://www.wowhead.com/?item=94221)s to summon the mob again. So don't die! :)",
            date = "2013-03-12T15:50:29-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32641#comments:id=1827559",
        },
        {
            id = 1824750,
            score = 18,
            author = "702860",
            text = "A few mistakes up in the description from Wowhead.\n\nOnes under spirit (Ancient Mogu Guardian and Qi'nor) should be under lightning, ones under lightning (Cera and Windweaver Akil'amon) should be under primal and ones under primal (Echo of Kros and Kor'dok)should be under spirit.",
            date = "2013-03-08T16:55:26-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32641#comments:id=1824750",
        },
    },
    [32642] = {
        {
            id = 1821637,
            score = 41,
            author = "655806",
            text = "You get the work order quests from a post which replaces Farmer Yoon after he goes to join the tillers council.\n\nTo help him along, you need to talk to Nana Mudclaw and complete the https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32682 after you have opened all 16 plots and become exalted with the Tillers.\n\nOnce you complete the quest will also now a book the house on the farm allowing you to set it as your home location.",
            date = "2013-03-05T19:18:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32642#comments:id=1821637",
        },
        {
            id = 1824398,
            score = 8,
            author = "Henderman",
            text = "Turn the quest in at the wagon near your mailbox.",
            date = "2013-03-08T08:44:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32642#comments:id=1824398",
        },
        {
            id = 1828468,
            score = 7,
            author = "silonicles",
            text = "I made the mistake of starting to harvest the leeks the next day without 'completing' the first quest because I didn't realize there was a 'part II' and it would count as you harvested all 8 crops. So I had to re-plant and wait another day.\n\nAlso, my DK is seeing no quests at all on the 'work order' pole. He's never unlocked any of the factions besides Tillers and Order of the Cloud Serpents.",
            date = "2013-03-14T08:28:15-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32642#comments:id=1828468",
        },
        {
            id = 1828146,
            score = 5,
            author = "Seaweed",
            text = "There is currently a typo in this quest, as you plant the seeds, the quest confirmation says:\n\"Plant Red Blossom Leak Seeds: 8/8\"\nAlso says so in the quest tracker.\n\nSent a bug report to Blizz, but it made me chuckle",
            date = "2013-03-13T17:21:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32642#comments:id=1828146",
        },
        {
