        {
            id = 2505172,
            score = 11,
            author = "VioletPisces",
            text = "If you are traveling to Shado-Pan Garrison on a boosted toon during Legion expecting to find either the portal to Isle of Thunder or the quest \"Thunder Calls\", it won't be there.  I never received a pop up for this quest on my toon created recently and instead went straight to the quest \"The Storm Gathers\".  If you don't see any quests at SPG, make sure you have Trivial Quests marked in your tracking settings.  This should allow you to see and accept the quest to get to Isle of Thunder.",
            date = "2017-06-30T20:30:38-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32679#comments:id=2505172",
        },
    },
    [32680] = {
        {
            id = 1827807,
            score = 13,
            author = "1094223",
            text = "For those interested in lore and whatnot for the Isle of Thunder and our reasons for taking it:\n\nScout Captain Elsia's conversation on the flight over..\n\nScout Captain Elsia says: Pandaren legends tell of Lei Shen, \"The Thunder King.\"  He was the brutal founder of the Mogu empire over 12,000 years ago.\nScout Captain Elsia says: He united the mogu, defeated the other pandaren races, and founded a glorious nation with the slave labor of those he conquered.\nScout Captain Elsia says: The Thunder King built a palatial fortress on the borders of his empire.  We should see it soon...\nScout Captain Elsia says: There!  Just ahead: The Isle of the Thunder King.\nScout Captain Elsia says: The Pandaren are terrified that the former Emperor will try to reclaim his empire, and enslave them once again.\nScout Captain Elsia says: But we have our own reasons for assisting them.  I will allow Lor'themar to explain.\nScout Captain Elsia says: Whoa! Careful - it is nearly impossible to fly anywhere near the island!\n\nOnce you have turned the quest in to Lor'themar, the speech is continued by Lor'themar.\n\nLor'themar Theron says: Aethas, leave us for a moment.\nLor'themar Theron says: Hero, you have served the Horde nobly across many campaigns.  I feel I can take you into confidence.\nLor'themar Theron says: Our Warchief's campaign across Kalimdor and Pandaria is pulling the Horde apart at the seams.\nLor'themar Theron says: We are here to fight the Thunder King.  Justice demands it, and Hellscream is too preoccupied at Domination Point to pay attention here.\nLor'themar Theron says: But, in defeating him, we must seek out the source of his great power.  We must claim it for ourselves, as leverage against our \"Warchief.\"\nLor'themar Theron says: In the event of an uprising, we must be prepared.\nLor'themar Theron says: Heads up!\nLor'themar Theron says: Ha-hah!  It will feel good to bloody my blade again.  Against Alliance or mogu, does not matter to me.\nLor'themar Theron says: Enough talk.  You know how precarious our position is.  Between the Alliance and the Thunder King, only with the help of heroes like you can we hope to succeed here.\nLor'themar Theron says: Anar'alah belore, hero.  Good luck.",
            date = "2013-03-13T03:10:40-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32680#comments:id=1827807",
        },
        {
            id = 1827684,
            score = 11,
            author = "fifth",
            text = "After you complete this quest, the portal to Isle of Thunder is located just south of the flight point at Shado-Pan Garrison.",
            date = "2013-03-12T20:18:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32680#comments:id=1827684",
        },
        {
            id = 1871327,
            score = 7,
            author = "840282",
            text = "Having some issue with this quest. I talk to her and take the flight, but don't get credit for talking to her and am unable to complete the quest.\n\nAfter dropping the quest and making a second attempt, I no longer get credit for discovering the Isle either...",
            date = "2013-06-27T17:05:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32680#comments:id=1871327",
        },
        {
            id = 5488819,
            score = 7,
            author = "Flanell",
            text = "Quest is bugged in 10.0.2. Right after the loading screen while flying to the isles of thunder I got dismounted in the ocean south of the isles instead flying to Lorthemar and his ship. Dialogue is missing too.",
            date = "2022-12-05T09:10:41-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32680#comments:id=5488819",
        },
        {
            id = 3251438,
            score = 4,
            author = "kruggs",
            text = "The quest starts with Thunder Calls (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32678/thunder-calls), which is picked up from Sunwalker Dezco (https://www.wowhead.com/npc=64566/sunwalker-dezco). If you never picked this up prior to BFA, then you'll need to talk to Zidormi (https://www.wowhead.com/npc=163463/zidormi) at the Mogu'shan Palace to travel through time before the Black Empire assault. This will phase you so that you're able to find Sunwalker Dezco.",
            date = "2020-11-21T01:09:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32680#comments:id=3251438",
        },
    },
    [32681] = {
        {
            id = 1847824,
            score = 16,
            author = "309042",
            text = "This should be obvious, but it's something that always slips my mind so I thought I'd add it here.\n\nIf you've joined a raid to kill Nalak, and you haven't done the quests leading to the Isle of Thunder before, you won't be able to get the credit for Travelling with Vareesa or discovering the Isle.",
            date = "2013-04-28T05:49:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32681#comments:id=1847824",
        },
        {
            id = 1821586,
            score = 13,
            author = "Eillesthis",
            text = "Previous: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32679\nNext: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32706, plus dailies",
            date = "2013-03-05T18:40:19-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32681#comments:id=1821586",
        },
        {
            id = 1910209,
            score = 9,
            author = "14145",
            text = "When you accept this quest you have to talk again to the quest giver and ask her to take you to the island. She will fly in front of you and take you there. As soon as you arrive to the island (after the loading screen finishes) you will get a credit for the second condition of the quest:\nIsle of Thunder discovered\n\nIt is important that you are not in a raid group while she is taking you there. For example, don't queue for LFR until the quest is completed and you get credit. If the instance timer pops up and you accept it, YOU WONT GET CREDIT for discovering the island and will have to go back to the main island and fly back in.\n\nIt is common sense, but sometimes it is easy to forget you can't complete normal quests if you are in a raid group.",
            date = "2013-10-19T15:22:24-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32681#comments:id=1910209",
        },
        {
            id = 1821366,
            score = 7,
            author = "Stealthfire13",
            text = "These proved popular with the Operation Shieldwall quests, so here's a transcript of Jaina's speech after the quest turn-in:\n\nLady Jaina Proudmoore says: This has been the worst year of my life: Theramore, destroyed. And a betrayal from within the Kirin-Tor.\nLady Jaina Proudmoore says: The lesson is clear. From here on out, I'm taking the initiative.\nLady Jaina Proudmoore says: Just down the coast, the Horde is searching for a place to land their troops.\nLady Jaina Proudmoore says: They seek to defeat the Thunder King, not to protect Pandaria, but to claim his power for themselves.\nLady Jaina Proudmoore says: But this time, we're a step ahead.\nLady Jaina Proudmoore says: The Horde will find no purchase on these shores. And when the Thunder King lies beaten, the Pandaren will see that it was Alliance heroes who stood by them in their hour of need.\nLady Jaina Proudmoore says: This fight will take everything we have. I hope you are ready.",
            date = "2013-03-05T16:07:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32681#comments:id=1821366",
        },
        {
            id = 5761907,
            score = 3,
            author = "KikeScott",
            text = "It states you need lvl 32, but you actually need to be 35",
            date = "2024-01-08T17:50:56-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32681#comments:id=5761907",
        },
    },
    [32682] = {
        {
            id = 1822780,
            score = 89,
            author = "Storn",
            text = "I loled so hard at \"I don't think I'll have time to work for The Council and run Sunsong Ranch\".\n\nLike you ever spent any time running the Ranch Yoon!",
            date = "2013-03-06T13:30:18-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32682#comments:id=1822780",
        },
        {
            id = 1839067,
            score = 85,
            author = "1056857",
            text = "Man. I play this game to get away from work, and yet here's a familiar situation: some lazy good-for-nothing who takes credit for all my work gets promoted to upper management.",
            date = "2013-04-04T16:37:04-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32682#comments:id=1839067",
        },
        {
            id = 1817576,
            score = 68,
            author = "Salogel",
            text = "You get this quest from Nana Mudclaw.\nFarmer Yoon will accept the offer but since \" I don't think I'll have time to work for The Council and run Sunsong Ranch\" he will gifting the ranch to you. \"You are in charge now\"\nThere is a book inside the house, \"Farmer's Journal\", acting as an Innkeeper, where you can set up your new Home location.\nThe option to take over the farm is available to characters that are exalted with the Tillers and have unlocked all 16 farm plots.\nEnjoy your new home.",
            date = "2013-02-24T06:02:35-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32682#comments:id=1817576",
        },
        {
            id = 1822368,
            score = 31,
            author = "Mormolyce",
            text = "I like that they decided to do it this way instead of just buying the farm. Felt a bit rude to poor Farmer Yoon who I'd grown to like that I would just buy it. Or that he would even agree to part with it given it's been in his family for generations. Now he gives it to you because he's moving on to bigger and better things and doesn't have time to run it anymore.\n\nAnd plus, now it's free :P",
            date = "2013-03-06T07:24:52-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32682#comments:id=1822368",
        },
        {
            id = 1825252,
            score = 26,
            author = "Sketchie",
            text = "After accepting the Inherit the Earth quest, go ask Farmer Yoon if he will join the Tiller Council. A brief scene will occur:\n\nFarmer Yoon says: Nana Mudclaw asked ME to join the Tillers council?\n\nFarmer Yoon will start to pace up and down the farm, pondering out loud on what to do.\n\nFarmer Yoon says: Just think of all the knowledge I could share. Think of all the food we could grow!\nFarmer Yoon says: But... I don't think I'll have time to work for the council, AND run Sunsong Ranch.\nFarmer Yoon says: This farm has been in my family for generations. How can I give it up? Yet, a greater responsiblity has fallen on me.\nFarmer Yoon says: There's only one solution. I have to join the council. As for the farm...\n\nFarmer Yoon then faces your character.\n\nFarmer Yoon says: , I'm gifting Sunsong Ranch to you. You're in charge, now!\nFarmer Yoon says: I'd better head up and talk to Nana. The farm is yours now, . I know you'll take great care of it.\n\nFarmer Yoon departs.\n\nFarmer Yoon will now hang out at the Halfhill Marketplace. He will still give you farming advice and dailies (however, he will not give you the \"single crop\" dailies anymore).\n\nIn Farmer Yoon's old place on Sunsong Ranch, you will find a post with a bill tacked on it. You can get two dailies from it which require you to plant 8 of a certain seed (it will take up all 16 plots of your farm if you decide to take on both orders), and then harvest it the next day. Note that you can actually choose who to plant and harvest crops for each day from a pool of MoP-exclusive factions. You will gain 400 rep with that faction, 800 if you have used the faction-exclusive Commendation. It of course will give more if you have the human racial, Diplomacy, and/or the guild perk, Mr. Popularity.\n\nNOTE: You NEED to accept a quest before you plant seeds for them, otherwise it won't count. You will then have to wait until the next day, or pull them up using the Dented Shovel on your farm and replant the seeds.\n\nWhat's nice is that when you put the plants into the box next to the road and finish the quest, a generic representative will arrive to pick up the box, thank you, and then depart.",
            date = "2013-03-09T09:43:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32682#comments:id=1825252",
        },
    },
    [32683] = {
