            score = 68,
            author = "Kittay",
            text = "The stones can be looted from rare mobs that are spread across the isle, 6 different mobs at Stage 1. [clicky] (http://www.mmo-champion.com/content/3139-Isle-of-Thunder-Rare-Spawns-5-2-Rare-and-Quest-NPC-Sharing-Blue-Tweets-TCG-Art)\n\nAnother way to get them is in the solo instance Thunder King's Citadel. You'll need a https://www.wowhead.com/item=94222. This is the intro quest to enter the instance: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32296. (I got 3x the stone from one loot, so it's a time-saver and worth doing if you're lucky.)\n\nYou can also get the stones if you recieve an item to summon a dead mob which you can loot. It can be done with either of these items: https://www.wowhead.com/item=94233,  https://www.wowhead.com/item=94130, https://www.wowhead.com/item=95350.\n\nYou get one stone as a reward from the weekly https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32505.\n\nYou can also get them from hidden troves on the island, but these are very hard to find and to get to before someone else does.\n\nThe last way to retrieve these stones is to do your dailies for the Sunreaver Onslaught. After you have completed the entire set, you'll get a final quest that will grant you a https://www.wowhead.com/item=94220. There's a chance you will get stones (and keys) from this box.\n\nAddition: It seems you can only loot this stone from rares and troves once per week, and the same goes for the key.",
            date = "2013-03-06T12:14:46-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32707#comments:id=1822696",
        },
        {
            id = 1821476,
            score = 63,
            author = "175042",
            text = "For those that use Tom Tom\n\n/way 58, 39.6\n/way 44.1, 56.2\n/way 59.3, 56.8\n/way 47.4, 72.4\n/way 52.9, 77.2\n/way 47.9, 82.1\n/way 43.5, 78.6",
            date = "2013-03-05T17:28:40-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32707#comments:id=1821476",
        },
        {
            id = 5876260,
            score = 35,
            author = "CrunchBoat",
            text = "For remix, this is a terrible quest. Between this one and that chamberlain quest, it's a massive annoyance. I've been doing this quest for like 2 hours now.",
            date = "2024-06-07T09:03:46-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32707#comments:id=5876260",
        },
        {
            id = 1824043,
            score = 32,
            author = "recnato",
            text = "unlocks https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32708. This is a weekly quest and you and your group will need a total of 12 https://www.wowhead.com/item=94221 to do all of the weekly chain.\n\nEdit: actually i got this wrong. the weekly quest is https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32641 and your group will need a total of 9 https://www.wowhead.com/item=94221 every week. You will need 3 more just for the first week",
            date = "2013-03-07T19:20:59-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32707#comments:id=1824043",
        },
    },
    [32708] = {
        {
            id = 1823493,
            score = 47,
            author = "Richardbro",
            text = "I recommend bringing 4-5 people.\n\nMake sure you Interrupt the Roar, which fears you. Also make sure you kill the add he summons called Skumblade, before he eats it. It will recover about 20% of his HP if he is successful in eating him. You don't have much time in killing the add either, so do it quickly.\n\nINTERESTING FACT: Kros has a high chance of dropping https://www.wowhead.com/item=94222.\n\nIf you see a group forming for him in General (\"Setting the Trap\"), I highly recommend joining! I was able to get a key this way on 4 of my toons in one day.\n\nMake sure you loot him once he dies. four out of six times he dropped 4 of these keys meaning 4/5 of the group were able to loot a key.\n\nI recommend doing this on every toon, especially alts that could benefit from the amount of https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32016 you acquire during the Treasure solo instance.",
            date = "2013-03-07T07:15:24-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32708#comments:id=1823493",
        },
        {
            id = 1852515,
            score = 34,
            author = "ullrapollo",
            text = "To bad there isn't some kind of scenario finder for these quests, would make looking for a group a lot easier",
            date = "2013-05-12T15:05:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32708#comments:id=1852515",
        },
        {
            id = 1821535,
            score = 32,
            author = "sTyLnK",
            text = "You cannot do this in a raid if you're trying to complete the quest, as you cannot do quests while in a raid group. It is doable with 5 people, so if you're trying to complete the quest, only get up to 5 people. Of course, this is nothing new, but just a reminder for people who didn't know, as you will lose your ritual stones.\n\nYou can however do it in a raid group to get credit for 'It was Worth Every Ritual Stone (http://www.wowhead.com/achievement=8101)'.",
            date = "2013-03-05T17:57:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32708#comments:id=1821535",
        },
        {
            id = 1822012,
            score = 30,
            author = "907542",
            text = "You MUST get the tag on this as soon as it is summoned as you can have the tag ninja'd from your own summon & you lose your 3 stones & still have not completed the quest!\n\nedit: it seems that the danger may only be a cross faction tag by a rouge or something.... happened to me :-(\n\nBest case scenario with this quest is to find someone on it with three stones willing to party you and summon.\nYou get the quest credit and get to save your stones for the next stage Champions of the Thunder King https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32641\nI did this to catch up after losing my stones to a ninja on first night madness.\n (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=32641)\n\nTank Krossy away from the summon stone & feed add spawn point to make it easy to kill it before he gets to feed.\nNo need for a healer if you have a self healing tank like a Blook DK or Haste build Prot Pally, Interupt Roar (fear) & dps the fk outa him.",
            date = "2013-03-06T00:13:53-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32708#comments:id=1822012",
        },
        {
            id = 1827751,
            score = 27,
            author = "Rayanna",
            text = "You get this quest after finding 3 https://www.wowhead.com/item=94221 and completing the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32707.",
            date = "2013-03-13T00:05:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=32708#comments:id=1827751",
        },
    },
