    [33342] = {
        {
            id = 1894891,
            score = 44,
            author = "Breotan",
            text = "You start out at 0 - Neutral and have to grind 9000 rep to hit Honored.  Non-elites give 5 or 6 rep each.  Elites 12 or so.  They take longer to kill than they really need to so this is going to take forever if you try to solo it.  It's reminiscent of the old rep grinds back in Vanilla.  For those of you unlucky enough to have done the Timbermaw Hold rep grind, this will feel about the same.\n\nIf you are in a party, you might want to stay farther South.  The first area by Firewalker Ruins is easy enough to farm but it is honestly over-farmed because for some reason everyone wants to do this solo.  Seriously, do not do this solo.\n\nI recommend you fill a raid and camp up by The Blazing Way.  There's a section to the North where a bunch of elites spawn and if you are organized you can farm them pretty effectively.  The drawback appears that you don't appear to get Timeless Coins or freebee purples while in a raid, except for the rare spawns.  Still, those drop off everything and anything so you shouldn't miss them here.\n\nEdit:  Just verified that these mobs do keep giving rep after you reach Honored.",
            date = "2013-09-10T22:26:32-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=33342#comments:id=1894891",
        },
        {
            id = 1897041,
            score = 29,
            author = "1144821",
            text = "Emperors daily quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=33374 also rewards 250 reputation",
            date = "2013-09-13T07:46:09-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=33342#comments:id=1897041",
        },
        {
            id = 1896716,
            score = 27,
            author = "Carotte",
            text = "Ordon Candlekeeper - 5 or 6 rep\nOrdon Oathguard - 11 rep\nOrdon Fire-Watcher - 11 rep\nBurning Berserker - 16 or 17 rep\nEternal Kilnmaster - 22 rep\nBlazebound Chanter - 22 rep\n\nThese are the reputation gains assuming you are in a level 25 guild.\n\nAll the mobs are pretty though and have abilities that can easily\nkill you if you don't pay enough attention (except the Candlekeepers which are non-elite).\n\nLike Breotan said, you should group up in order to make this grind less of a pain but also to deter people from killing you for Bloody Coins (http://www.wowhead.com/currency=789)\nClasses with lots of stuns make life a lot easier, especially against the Kilnmasters.",
            date = "2013-09-12T21:03:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=33342#comments:id=1896716",
        },
        {
            id = 1896320,
            score = 19,
            author = "1141419",
            text = "The mobs gives less reputation when you're in a group and even less than that in a raid.\nBlizzard seriously need to buff this quest or change it in some way, cause being on a high pop server as myself, this is a pain in the arsenal.\n\nI can understand why getting rep with Shaohao is hard hence there are reputation vendors that sell mounts and pets that requires you to be friendly, honored, revered or exalted.\n\nBut i would suggest blizzard changes the quest in to collecting tokens or something, cause this quest is ridiculous and i don't think it's worth the effort if i can still go and hit a ship and a shark once and get 2k coins in a matter of minutes.",
            date = "2013-09-12T09:43:51-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=33342#comments:id=1896320",
        },
        {
            id = 1894934,
            score = 18,
            author = "mosingbel",
            text = "As a human with guild bonus and https://www.wowhead.com/item=64399 Burning berzerkers, Blazebound Chanters, and Eternal Kiln masters grant 20-21 rep upon death. These are easy to farm with a group of 5 at Shrine of the Black Flame (68,35). Coins and epics DO drop while in a party. Coins do NOT drop while in a raid and epics DO drop just on a very very small scale, don't expect to see a lot drop while in a raid.",
            date = "2013-09-10T23:34:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=33342#comments:id=1894934",
        },
    },
    [33343] = {
        {
            id = 1887048,
            score = 78,
            author = "GoHF",
            text = "This quest becomes available when you reach Honored with [faction=1492] and hand in the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=33342.\n\nAs the quest text states, you need to buy (at least) one https://www.wowhead.com/item=103684 from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=73306, and then ride to the Three-Breeze Terrace and use the https://www.wowhead.com/object=223203 that is right in the middle of the terrace.\n\nAfter 4-5 seconds (during which you are advised to get back out of the terrace), a lot of Ordos yaungol will appear all over the terrace. These will be the same as the yaungol in the Ordon Sanctuary, including:\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=72896\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=72897\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=72888\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=72898\nand, of course\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/npc=73666\n\nWhile a group is not strictly necessary, it is highly advised you bring help. A ranged class with high mobility can make short work of the npc's (particularly with all the islands buffs), but others might have a harder time, and each of these npc's has abilities that will take roughly anywhere from 50% to 150% of your health.\n\n-edit-\nAs for whether the NPC's despawn after a set time or not at all, unsure. They do not despawn after killing the Archiereus, but neither do they respawn if killed before the Archiereus.",
            date = "2013-08-14T18:20:23-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=33343#comments:id=1887048",
        },
        {
            id = 1898573,
            score = 73,
            author = "Azaile",
            text = "important to note that you cannot do it in a raid group.",
            date = "2013-09-15T20:37:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=33343#comments:id=1898573",
        },
        {
            id = 2624071,
            score = 67,
            author = "Vanthalas",
            text = "In case you are wondering why you can't seem to find a stone, it has a somewhat long respawn timer (I'd guess between 10-15 minutes).",
            date = "2018-10-16T22:16:48-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=33343#comments:id=2624071",
        },
        {
            id = 1897528,
            score = 46,
            author = "Arrica42",
            text = "Point of emphasis, this quest only works if you kill the summoned version of Archiereus of Flame at Three-Breeze Terrace.  There is an Archiereus of Flame that randomly spawns like a normal rare at Ordon Sanctuary, and as I had just achieved Honored rep when he spawned in front of my group, I turned in my quest and came back and we killed him, but I did not get quest credit.",
            date = "2013-09-14T00:18:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=33343#comments:id=1897528",
        },
        {
            id = 1899028,
            score = 39,
            author = "1145548",
            text = "After struggling with this quest for a while, I found a very easy way to complete it.\n\nJust gather a group of five people at most (the quest requires a simple group so a raid group won´t do) and summon Archiereus yourself with the scroll then simply kite the mob to the celestial court when there are a lot of other players around.\n\nSince Archiereus is a rare mob most people will join the fight in and will burn the boss in no time!\n\nTo complete the quest you simply need to kill Archiereus not necessarily the adds themselves.\n\nSo, get a good tank, instruct him to taunt and kite Archiereus to the celestials court and let our fellow players do the dirty work! Kill Archiereus and you´ll be done.\n\nIt is as simple as that.\n\nGood luck!",
            date = "2013-09-16T20:06:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=33343#comments:id=1899028",
        },
    },
