        {
            id = 5539399,
            score = 3,
            author = "conjuringman1",
            text = "I didn't need to complete this one to get Blasted Lands Quests achievement as a horde character",
            date = "2023-01-31T00:12:31-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=35746#comments:id=5539399",
        },
        {
            id = 2014357,
            score = -1,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "You will pick up this quest from Thrall at Shattered Landing.  When you pick up this quest, also pick up the other two available quests.\n\nPeeking into the Portal (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=36382)\nAttack of the Iron Horde (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=35745)\n\nFly a short distance to the Northwest of Shattered Landing and you will find the Iron Demolishers.  The Ironmarch Grunts for Attack of the Iron Horde are also located in this area, as well as the telescope for Peeking into the Portal.  You have to get close to the Iron Demolishers where you will click on them to sabotage and destroy them.  Spells do not effect them, you have to click on it to destroy them.",
            date = "2014-10-16T21:23:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=35746#comments:id=2014357",
        },
    },
    [35748] = {
        {
            id = 2014359,
            score = 2,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "Pick up this quest and then immediately complete it without leaving Shattered Landing.  The Ironmarch Scouts are invisible but detectable when you get close to one and are around the perimeter of the camp at Shattered Landing.  You will also find the occasional Ironmarch Scout roaming around the camp itself.  You will find more of them in the hills to the west of the camp. If most are already killed off, hike down the road out of the camp that leads to the northwest and you will find a few along the roadside.\n\nThe Ironmarch Scouts will disappear and reappear behind you for a blind strike, so do a 180 the moment they disappear.\n\nKill 5 of them and head back to Thrall to turn the quest back in.",
            date = "2014-10-16T21:45:47-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=35748#comments:id=2014359",
        },
    },
    [35750] = {
        {
            id = 2014387,
            score = 5,
            author = "Krastopic",
            text = "When you pick up this quest, also pick up the following quests to do at the same time:\n\nRansacking Nethergarde (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=35761)\nAttack on Nethergarde (http://www.wowhead.com/quest=35751)\n\nTo find Nethergrade Keep, fly to the northeast of where Thrall gives you the quest.  Assuming you are doing all of the quests at the same time, here is the order for all three quests:\n\nRukah's Battleplan, 57,18 - Pick Up off of Rukah after kill (Lunatic Lieutenants)\nNeka's Poison Flack, 59,18 - On the picnic table, highlighted (Ransacking Nethergrade)\nFlag Planted Outside Main Keep, 60,16 - Click on outline of flag (Attack on Nethergrade)\nOverseer Struk's Shield, 61,20 - laying on ground highlighted (Ransacking Nethergrade)\nFlag planted at Nethergarde entrance, 63,23 - Click on outline of flag (Attack on Nethergrade)\nFlag planted in the center of Nethergarde, 62,19 - Click on outline of flag (Attack on Nethergrade)\nAitokk's Axe, 62,15 - Inside building, in the door frame next to Aitokk's body. Axe is roughly at eye level for your toon. (Ransacking Nethergrade)\nMokrik's Battleplan, 63,13 - Pickup after the kill (Lunatic Lieutenants)\nGar's Battleplan, enter at 60,15 - Inside the building, go to the third floor Pickup after the kill (Lunatic Lieutenants)\n\nYou will note that the flags which you have to plant for the Attack on Nethergrade will have the new outline shading to help you find the spot to plant the flag.\n\nThe Overseer Struk's Shield is laying on a boot at a slight angle in the middle of the rubble of a building.\n\nNeka is already dead.  Her poison flask is on the table.  You do not have to kill her to pick up the flask.\n\nLike Neka, Master Aitokk is already dead.  You do not have to kill him to pick up the axe.  The axe is in the door frame next to the body.\n\nYou can pick up the bombs thrown by Mokrik at the start of the fight and an icon will appear and you can throw a bomb back at him doing reasonable damage.  Just run over the bomb to pick it up.",
            date = "2014-10-16T22:35:54-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=35750#comments:id=2014387",
        },
        {
            id = 2012738,
            score = 3,
            author = "albinoette",
            text = "These mobs can be tagged after someone else has pulled and you'll still get credit/loot:\n\nMokrik Blackfingers is with the targets behind the workshop. (62,13)\nRukah the Machinist is outside the western gate. (56,17)\nGar Steelcrush is upstairs in the main Nethergarde Keep structure. (60,13 - entrance: 59,15)\n\nThe new map marks the areas they'll be in with a yellow dot.",
            date = "2014-10-14T14:51:33-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=35750#comments:id=2012738",
        },
        {
            id = 2013175,
            score = 3,
            author = "corruptbyte",
            text = "If you do these quests on a character with an ilevel less than 515 (mine was 504 at the time), you can receive loot in addition to gold. I received https://www.wowhead.com/item=118761, https://www.wowhead.com/item=118766, https://www.wowhead.com/item=118771, and https://www.wowhead.com/item=118776 for completing the whole quest chain, in addition to achievement/pet/title I received on other characters.",
            date = "2014-10-15T06:37:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=35750#comments:id=2013175",
        },
        {
            id = 3211196,
            score = 2,
