    [44930] = {
        {
            id = 2436840,
            score = 71,
            author = "D4n13le",
            text = "This quest was added in patch 7.1, and unlocks the [transmog-set=889] set. To obtain it:\n\nYou're going to need a Rogue in Outlaw specialization. You don't need to be level 110.\nEnter [zone=1581] Normal\nReach Ironclad Cove, the area with the wooden catwalk and the big boat (near the last two bosses)\nOptional: if you don't have a https://www.wowhead.com/npc=7387 keep killing https://www.wowhead.com/npc=48522 until you get a https://www.wowhead.com/item=8492 with one inside\nLocate the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=115839, found at these coordinates (http://www.wowhead.com/maps?data=1581.2:365170)\nSummon your https://www.wowhead.com/npc=7387 and stand close to the https://www.wowhead.com/npc=115839, an extra button with a https://www.wowhead.com/spell=230148 will appear. If you click it you'll climb the wall\nAccept the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=44930 from https://www.wowhead.com/npc=115818. He's gonna ask you to obtain 100 Blodied Defias Bandanas from the enemies inside the instance. If you already killed them all just reset the instance to complete it (remember that you need to do it in normal difficulty)\nTurn in the quest and enjoy your [transmog-set=889] set!\n\nCredits: Reddit users /u/LunaeLux, /u/Kaeligos,  Wowhead user Sutcliff and many others who helped discover it.",
            date = "2016-10-29T12:54:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=44930#comments:id=2436840",
        },
        {
            id = 2449391,
            score = 36,
            author = "504547",
            text = "I haven't seen this mentioned anywhere yet.  If you return to the ghostly parrot to head back up and turn in but the extra action button doesn't appear, just dismiss your Green Wing Macaw and re summon it.  I hit that issue and that caused the button to show up so I could finish.",
            date = "2016-11-29T03:40:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=44930#comments:id=2449391",
        },
        {
            id = 2438059,
            score = 33,
            author = "Boxofbeer",
            text = "Okay, there's a short guide:\nSome thing you need to know before:\n\nFirst, https://www.wowhead.com/item=142273 can be obtained by only Rogue, Outlaw spec\nYou dont have to be 110 level to be able to pick up the quest https://www.wowhead.com/quest=44930\nThere are five items in set: https://www.wowhead.com/item=10399, https://www.wowhead.com/item=10400, https://www.wowhead.com/item=10401, https://www.wowhead.com/item=10403 and https://www.wowhead.com/item=10402\nYou dont have to be rogue only to transmog the set, other leather wearers are ok too\n\nFine, now the guide:\n\nGo to [zone=1581] instance, entrance located in Westfall at 25.4 51.0 point (there's long way through the underground\nThere's also video if cant find: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H3zrzcoHqj0\nRun normal and proceed till you found a giant cave with ship inside it (Ironclad Cove). Also, skip all mobs, slay only bosses to open doors\nWhen you come into Ironclad Cove, turn left, there you'll see a ghostly parrot far away, above a corpse next to a water\nCome close and summon battle pet — https://www.wowhead.com/npc=7387. You can obtain it at AH or killing pirates on the ship — https://www.wowhead.com/item=8492. When you summon the pet, there an extra button will appear — https://www.wowhead.com/spell=230148. Use it to reach a hidden place, where https://www.wowhead.com/npc=115818 is\nPick up https://www.wowhead.com/quest=44930 quest. https://www.wowhead.com/item=142349s have 100% drop chance from each mob (including monkeys and parrots, lol). There are enough mobs in instance to get all 100 within a single run reset (if you skipped them, ofc)\nGet back to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=115818 and turn in the quest, use https://www.wowhead.com/item=142273 to get full set. Visit transmogrificator to see what you've got\n\nhttps://www.wowhead.com/quest=44930 videoguide — https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pz75NeKxoyI",
            date = "2016-10-31T09:04:31-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=44930#comments:id=2438059",
        },
        {
            id = 2438373,
            score = 18,
            author = "FlayOnDarkIron",
            text = "Just an observation, but the ensemble vendors for 750g.\n\nTwo things happen at level 10 for a rogue: first they can zone into the Deadmines. Second, they can pick outlaw as a specialization.\n\nNow I'm not suggesting this is a very time efficient way to make money, but its basically a free pile of 750g for every rogue you level to 10, as long as you have someone to run you through VC.",
            date = "2016-11-01T01:06:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=44930#comments:id=2438373",
        },
        {
            id = 3156403,
            score = 9,
            author = "Rainlover",
            text = "The  Ensemble: Blackened Defias Armor is obtained via completion of  Deadmines: Sea'in Red. Only rogues can do the following questline, but the Defias armor set can be worn on any leather wearing toon!\n\nStep One: To receive this ensemble, you must first be in Outlaw specialization and have the Green Wing Macaw pet.\n\nStep Two: After you have acquired your companion and changed your specialization to Outlaw, head over to The Deadmines in Westfall. Make sure that you have set the dungeon to Normal before entering! Mobs will not drop  Bloodied Defias Bandana on Heroic difficulty.\n\nStep Three: Once inside, make your way to the end of the dungeon. It is recommended that you do not kill any of the mobs aside from the bosses, the reason being that you will be killing and looting the mobs for the quest you receive later on at the end of the dungeon. Upon reaching the end of the dungeon, run along the boardwalk until you get to the area called Ironclad Cove where you will see a Ghostly Parrot.\n\nStep Four: Walk up to the parrot and summon your Green Wing Macaw, which will then grant you access to the  Grappling Hook extra action bar. Using this extra action button will take you up to Captain Bramblebeard, who will then grant you the quest to slay Defias in the instance until you have gathered 100  Bloodied Defias Bandanas.\n\nStep Five: Slay all the Defias! If you killed Defias on your way to the Captain prior to starting the quest, simply run out and reset the instance. Resetting the instance will spawn all of the previously killed mobs, allowing you to kill and loot them again.\n\nStep Six: After you have obtained 100 bandanas, head back to the Ghostly Parrot and summon your Green Wing Macaw to once again be taken up to Captain Bramblebeard. Turn in your quest and you will be granted the  Ensemble: Blackened Defias Armor.",
            date = "2019-09-19T08:14:17-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=44930#comments:id=3156403",
        },
    },
    [45563] = {
        {
            id = 2483864,
            score = 88,
            author = "Martika",
            text = "It would appear that you MUST turn this quest in during the week when the Pandaria timewalking weekly is active. Otherwise the turn-in NPC will not be there, and each time you activate the quest item and then fly or port anywhere or log out and in, the quest will disappear from your log and you'll have to activate it again.",
            date = "2017-04-05T23:23:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45563#comments:id=2483864",
        },
        {
            id = 2476266,
            score = 43,
            author = "Memento1960",
            text = "Whose idiotic bloody idea was it that we should be handing this thing in somewhere where the opposing faction can camp the quest mob and not let you turn in?",
            date = "2017-03-08T04:01:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45563#comments:id=2476266",
        },
        {
            id = 2476265,
            score = 24,
            author = "mymy379",
            text = "Started by Shrouded Timewarped Coin (http://www.wowhead.com/item=143776).\n\nCompletion status can be checked with:\n\n/run print(IsQuestFlaggedCompleted(45563))",
            date = "2017-03-08T03:54:58-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45563#comments:id=2476265",
        },
        {
            id = 2476824,
            score = 21,
            author = "emwowhead",
            text = "My macro to check all Timewalking-Quests so far(7.2.0)\n/run for b,c in ipairs({\"0\",\"40168_70_BC(Shattrath)\",\"40173_80_WotLK(Dalaran)\",\"40787_85_Cata.Alliance(Stormwind)\",\"40786_85_Cata.Horde(Orgrimmar)\",\"45563_90_MoP(TimelessIsle)\"}) do print(IsQuestFlaggedCompleted(c:sub(1,5))and\"+\"or\"--\",c)end\n\nAlliance only:\n\n/run for b,c in ipairs({\"0\",\"40168_70_BC(Shattrath)\",\"40173_80_WotLK(Dalaran)\",\"40787_85_Cata.Alliance(Stormwind)\",\"45563_90_MoP(TimelessIsle)\"}) do print(IsQuestFlaggedCompleted(c:sub(1,5))and\"+\"or\"--\",c)end\n\nHorde only:\n\n/run for b,c in ipairs({\"0\",\"40168_70_BC(Shattrath)\",\"40173_80_WotLK(Dalaran)\",\"40786_85_Cata.Horde(Orgrimmar)\",\"45563_90_MoP(TimelessIsle)\"}) do print(IsQuestFlaggedCompleted(c:sub(1,5))and\"+\"or\"--\",c)end",
            date = "2017-03-11T13:33:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45563#comments:id=2476824",
        },
        {
            id = 6035512,
            score = 20,
            author = "Deathswait",
            text = "As of November 20, 2024:\n\nWeekly Timewalking quests now require level 30 to drop item rewards.\n\nDevelopers’ notes: Players from level 10-29 are still able to engage with Timewalking, however, we do not want to incentivize creating a character for one run and then deleting the character.\n\nWarbands and streamlining have changed the reward structure for timewalking items.\nALL of the timewalking weekly quest drops SHOULD be a 100% drop on the last boss of your first timewalking dungeon of the week, per character.\nIt is worth noting that there have been drop bugs reported. If you experience this, report it using the in-game tool so that the devs can fix it.\nMinimum Level to get quest items dropped: 30\nFirst completion on account/warband per week: 500 [currency=1166]\nSecond and subsequent completion on account/warband per week: 200 [currency=1166]\n\nYou no longer recieve 500 [currency=1166] per character.\nRather, 500 [currency=1166] for 1st completion on warband/account and 200 [currency=1166] for any completions after that.\nHow this works cross-faction has not been made 100% clear.\n\nWorld of Warcraft Classic\n\nClassic Item: https://www.wowhead.com/item=225348\nClassic Quest: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=83285\n\nThis one is weird because it seems that some people may be able to loot it as low as level 10.\nIt is possible that characters created prior to the change may have been grandfathered in to the level 10 drop requirement by accident or on purpose.\nIt is best to assume this will eventually follow the level 30 rule.\n\nBurning Crusade\n\nBurning Crusade / Outland Item: https://www.wowhead.com/item=129747\nBurning Crusade / Outland Quest: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=40168\n\nWrath of the Lich King\n\nLich King / Northrend Item: https://www.wowhead.com/item=129928\nLich King / Northrend Quest: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=40173\n\nCataclysm\n\nAlliance Item: https://www.wowhead.com/item=133378\nAlliance Quest: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=40787\n\nHorde Item: https://www.wowhead.com/item=133377\nHorde Quest: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=40786\n\nMists of Pandaria\n\nPandaria Item: https://www.wowhead.com/item=143776\nPandaria Quest: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45563\n\nWarlord of Draenor\n\nAlliance Item: https://www.wowhead.com/item=167921\nAlliance Quest: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=55498\n\nHorde Item: https://www.wowhead.com/item=167922\nHorde Quest: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=55499\n\nLegion\n\nLegion Item: https://www.wowhead.com/item=187611\nLegion Quest: https://www.wowhead.com/quest=64710",
            date = "2024-12-24T09:46:20-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45563#comments:id=6035512",
        },
    },
    [45637] = {
        {
            id = 6266507,
            score = 1,
            author = "mlxbe",
            text = "Here’s a macro that works with the NPC, without using any addons :\n\n/run C_GossipInfo.SelectAvailableQuest(C_GossipInfo.GetAvailableQuests()[1][\"questID\"])\n/run SelectAvailableQuest(1)\n/run AcceptQuest()\n/run CompleteQuest(1)\n/run GetQuestReward(1)\n\nReplace the \"1\" in these two lines:\n\n/run C_GossipInfo.SelectAvailableQuest(C_GossipInfo.GetAvailableQuests()[1][\"questID\"])\n/run SelectAvailableQuest(1)\n\nwith the number that corresponds to the meat you want to turn in to the NPC.\n\n1 = Sandworm Meat (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45637/sandworm-meat)\n2 = Crunchy Spider Legs (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45638/crunchy-spider-legs)\n3 = Chilled Meat (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45639/chilled-meat)\n4 = Crocolisk Tails (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45640/crocolisk-tails)\n5 = Raw Tiger Steaks (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45641/raw-tiger-steaks)\n6 = Raw Clefthoof Meat (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45642/raw-clefthoof-meat)\n7 = Lean Shanks\n (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45643/lean-shanks)\nWatch the video below to see the macro in action.\n> Here (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JITPeZ8eJcQ) <\n\nYour keyboard is about to learn what true suffering is..",
            date = "2026-01-21T12:00:27-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=45637#comments:id=6266507",
        },
    },
