        {
            id = 5916502,
            score = 4,
            author = "StoneLegion",
            text = "Major Phase Issues:\n\nThere is a current issue doing this on Characters that were created after 11.0.0 and started on Exile's Reach and went past the ability to scale with chromie time it seems. There might be a lot more to this but the summery follows.\n\nWhen you make a new character and finish Exile's Reach you then go to Stormwind and there is the introduction to Stormwind Quests. Once you have finished [Home Is Where the Hearth Is]  (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=58911/home-is-where-the-hearth-is) you would normally get [An Urgent Meeting] (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=58912/an-urgent-meeting), but this has changed now because instead of BFA you go to Dragon Flight and a Different quest comes up.\n\nBecause of this the game script has locked you into this phase where normally you have [An Urgent Meeting] (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=58912/an-urgent-meeting) and you would talk to Captain Garrick in Stormwind Throne Room. Sadly this Phase is what is locked and there no way to unlock it at this time.\n\nIf you can still do chromie time there might be a way to fix it, but I'm sadly past that now.",
            date = "2024-08-12T01:38:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=53130#comments:id=5916502",
        },
        {
            id = 6148431,
            score = 4,
            author = "Arillium",
            text = "If you're having phasing issues like I had. Try completing the Kul Tiras intro chain. it fixed the phasing for me and i was able to hand it in.",
            date = "2025-07-24T03:10:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=53130#comments:id=6148431",
        },
    },
    [53370] = {
        {
            id = 5464801,
            score = 40,
            author = "Deadspear",
            text = "Okay, I've tried every possible way to get this and its not possible. I have no idea why this isn't flagged as removed from the game. Because by all account it is.\n\nThis was replaced by the quest Battle for Azeroth: Tides of War. There's no way to get this quest. You can get the Tides of War version by talking to a Herald next to mission posts in SW and other capital cities.\n\nMaybe they'll add it back when they add BFA to Chromie Time, but until then, there is no way to get it. You can replay the scenario The Battle for Lordaeron, but the quest before that is impossible to get.\n\nIt used to work like this. You'd get it automatically once you entered Stormwind.\n\nThe way it works now is that every new character get the Tides of War version, regardless if they've done Reckoning. I even tried it on a Starter Account.\nYou do the War Council -> Jaina -> You can level in BFA. Its the same if you're max level and never touched BFA.\n\nFor any quest completionists. Pretty much how it works now is that you get Tides of War right away (Even at max level) since its 10-50 (60 with Dragonflight). Once you hit 50 (60) I believe you can then get A Dying World from a speaker in Boralus.\n\nFun fact: A Dying World is marked as obsolete, yet is still obtainable, this however is not.",
            date = "2022-11-04T18:49:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=53370#comments:id=5464801",
        },
        {
            id = 3276694,
