        {
            id = 3189064,
            score = 10,
            author = "kthallus",
            text = "Upon capturing a Twilight Whelpling you get this quest.  The twilight whelplings are outside of the Grim Batol entrance in Twilight Highlands and are wild pets there are at least as far as I have seen 6 up at a time as of 8.3.  You then fly to the right side of the Grim Batol entrance and fly up about 100 feet in the air and talk to Eryna to complete the quest.  That's all there is to it.   See pic if you can't find Eryna.",
            date = "2020-02-08T09:08:43-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=56371#comments:id=3189064",
        },
        {
            id = 3155551,
            score = -4,
            author = "Hesseltine",
            text = "I received this item more or less by coincidence. Doing Grim Batol to grind rep, I noticed a pet I didn't have and, due to circumstanced, accidentally killed it. It dropped the scale, and I found that interesting and thought, I'll start it.\n\nBut here's the issue....I don't have BfA, and the quest requires it. The area isn't new, Twillight Highlands has been around since Cataclysm, so that's not relevant. Am I the only one who think that having drops that start quests for expansion you don't even have is somewhat...smelly? It cannot be hard to make sure that this item only drops for those that have BfA, after all. This feels like some sort of  underhanded urging to buy the expansion.",
            date = "2019-09-16T09:55:52-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=56371#comments:id=3155551",
        },
    },
