        {
            id = 5595374,
            score = 43,
            author = "sitecow09",
            text = "If you're wondering why the dragons at the end are shouting in disbelief at seeing a dragon egg, a bit of lore catchup:\n\nIn order to stop the N'zoth-corrupted dragon aspect Deathwing from destroying the world, the dragonflights had to give up their semidivine power they received from the Titans. This had the unfortunate side-effect of making all living dragons unable to produce any offspring, so most dragons were now resigned to the fact that their race was now doomed (with the exception of a few radical bronze dragons who tried to change the timeline and would eventually become the Infinite Dragonflight). Fast forward 10 years in-universe, and all of a sudden, this one red dragon egg represents hope for the future, that the dragonflights may not be doomed to die out after all.\n\nWhile the red dragons had plenty of eggs left by the time of Cataclysm, other flights like the blue and especially the black one had far fewer (you can see this at the Ruby Lifeshrine with the amount of eggs of each flight being tended to).",
            date = "2023-04-26T14:47:21-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=66001#comments:id=5595374",
        },
