            score = -1,
            author = "Utharkruna",
            text = "I ran 9 toons in Naxx this afternoon -got approximately 125 [Death's Bargaining Chip].\nI just burned half and got jack *!@#. Nothing that gets me even one step closer to actualy completing the set or even ONE item in my desired T3 set for that matter.\n\nThen smelling a rat, I sought out a vid on YT to see what i could expect.\nI found one first search that mirrored my experience.\n\nI believe Blizz has kept the RNG chance really @#$% because all those whales that pissed away millions of gold on their set on the BMAH will cry cuz now there is a more proactive way to do this (in theory) and it doesnt need more money/gold that yer monthly subscription.\n\nA way that doesnt require you to spend gold or buy WOW Tokens and spend gold (thus compromising the sales of WOW tokens).\nI (/Nobody outside Blizz) has seen the stats and maybe there is a corrolation between ppl with BMAH T3 sets and Buying WOW Tokens.\n\nEitherway I think i have more to do in my life that piss away this sort of time to beat an RNG algorithm that is statistically scripted to not give you jack !@#$!\n\nI smell the hand of the same thinking behind Diabolo Mobile! Keep droppnig coins in the slot to get the %^&* you want.\nThis mechanism is a way to encourage ppl to spend cash on Wow Tokens to then go buy all the [Phylacterweave] (and maybe Righeous Orbs) because the actual method of farming will steal your time, life and soul. With no guarantee of actual success at the end of it.\n\n^&*!. Even if you did go to the BMAH for yer T3 Set at least you know what winning yer auction gives you the item.\nI ran 9 toons today. Think about those ppl with only 1 or 2/3 toons...\nThe sence I have after seeing the drops and doing a little mental arithmatic is that you can commit to this activity for the next 5 years and never end up with what you want.",
            date = "2023-10-21T18:43:01-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=76268#comments:id=5708838",
        },
    },
