        {
            id = 6293399,
            score = 30,
            author = "zingzangbing",
            text = "For those of you who couldn't get out of the delve and had to hearth out, the way to get back to Harandar is to use the portal in Fairbreeze village.  Coords are 45.30 46.97 for the portal for those who have tom tom.",
            date = "2026-02-28T17:25:37-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=86912#comments:id=6293399",
        },
        {
            id = 6296253,
            score = 20,
            author = "Tamzar",
            text = "The fragment of revelation is a lightly-highlighted interactable rock with an orange symbol next to the chests in the treasure room at the end of the delve. So, if you're like me, assumed that the quest was just to complete the delve and left the instance after grabbing the chests - sorry. Got to get back in there again.\n\nOnce you've left the delve, take the immediate upper path to the left and the cave exit is \"behind\" you as you come out. Don't run forward looking for an exit, the cave system is kind of annoying with no mounted option.",
            date = "2026-03-03T06:53:22-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=86912#comments:id=6296253",
        },
        {
            id = 6251793,
            score = 14,
            author = "Snorkelbuddy",
            text = "The Fragment of Revelation is in a chest in the Treasury Room after you finish the Delve.",
            date = "2025-12-21T08:47:02-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=86912#comments:id=6251793",
        },
        {
            id = 6299436,
            score = 11,
            author = "Renaissanceman1",
            text = "\"We went looking for our goddess and didn't find her. This mad us angry and we squished some mushrooms and fought each other. This is why our elders choose to forbid going upstairs and we became xenophobic and mistrustful of outsiders.\"\n\nPeak Blizzard storytelling. Granted, this is the same race that immediately after finding an outsider, sent them to go gather up two of their kids, then held them on trial, but in order to be judged they let you fly willy-nilly to find the courthouse delve. I briefly felt like we were going through knock-off Rhuidean and witnessing the shame of our druidic Teemu Aiel, but giving the Haranir an actual reason for their isolation would make too much sense.  Perhaps expecting logical motivations was asking too much.",
            date = "2026-03-06T00:17:54-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=86912#comments:id=6299436",
        },
    },
