        {
            id = 6326720,
            score = 14,
            author = "MrGiblets",
            text = "Here are the scrolls and text, since they are easily missed. They’re all found in the nearby cave.\n\nScroll 1- Take left path down in cave and hug the left wall. Found by little bedroll and painted stone by the little pond.\nWays of the Roots--Part I: Serving\nServe the roots, and they will serve you.\n\nScroll 2- Keep going further into the cave and found on table by larger body of water.\nWays of the Roots-Part 2: Growing\n[Page 1]\nMany of the roots, and the Cradle, were here long before the haranir. Many came later. Nordrassil, Shaladrassil. Teldrassil, and others were planted over countless ages by those on the surface, but the roots reached out to Harandar.\n\n[Page 2]\nThe roots speak their names in the languages of the surface folk who planted them. If the roots reach Harandar, we know Aln'hara blesses them and we welcome them to the great knot of Harandar.\n\n[Page 3]\nThey are tended and protected, but we cannot protect them from the dangers above. The people of that world do not always protect the trees they have planted. We heal what we can. The branches may burn, but the roots will thrive.\n\nScroll 3- Take right path in cave then in larger area, go west until the pit. Jump along right side, over the root and hug the right wall (or glide over if Demon Hunter or Dracthyr). If you fall, you end up near Scroll 2; hug left wall to go back up.\nWays of the Roots-Part 3: Pruning\nIf you listen to the roots, they will tell you of most threats but what of threats they do not recognize? If we prune roots they see as healthy, will we be forgiven? Will the roots trust us again?",
            date = "2026-04-08T02:42:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88998#comments:id=6326720",
        },
        {
            id = 6326722,
            score = 5,
            author = "MrGiblets",
            text = "Trick I found for the puzzle, was to follow and “overlap” the squiggly lines. If a squiggly line goes all the way across, it probably needs to go next to the one it’s connected with. The final result of each round is a triangle.",
            date = "2026-04-08T02:48:50-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88998#comments:id=6326722",
        },
        {
            id = 6344037,
            score = 5,
            author = "JustAGirlTX",
            text = "This puzzle was really hard for me for some reason.  It's not particularly easy to see which way you are supposed to go.  I followed the previous commentor's advice and looked at the \"squiggly\" lines and just switched those to try to form a triangle and that worked.",
            date = "2026-04-26T11:52:26-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88998#comments:id=6344037",
        },
    },
