        {
            id = 6360599,
            score = 16,
            author = "d4mich4",
            text = "Somehow i am stuck and i sems i can t get/find this quest. dunno what to do :-/\n\nUPDATE 2026-06-17: As of now with the new patch 12.0.7 i could do the weekly quest again and just end it without picking an artifact an after it finished i got my missing quest for  The Root of Things  (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90739/the-root-of-things) and could end it for the part of the achivement i was stuck on.\nNow i just have to wait for next week to see if i can end the next part also.",
            date = "2026-05-25T15:07:18-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90740#comments:id=6360599",
        },
        {
            id = 6377590,
            score = 3,
            author = "Gaara3San",
            text = "If you are like me and not able to pickup up last two relics (Root of the World (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88998/root-of-the-world) and Sky's Hope (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88999/skys-hope)) for the achiev Legends Never Die (https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=61574/legends-never-die).\nYou need to progress this quest line starting with the quest The Listener (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90733/the-listener) as much as you can. On the quest A Legend to Know (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90740/a-legend-to-know) you will unlock Root of the World (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88998/root-of-the-world) and on The Empty Cradle (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90745/the-empty-cradle) you will unlock Sky's Hope (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88999/skys-hope).",
            date = "2026-07-02T13:10:35-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90740#comments:id=6377590",
        },
    },
    [90741] = {
        {
            id = 6362216,
            score = 11,
            author = "d4mich4",
            text = "This is the next quest i would need but somehow i can't pick it up.\nThe quest before 'A Legend to Know' (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90740/a-legend-to-know) shows that it is completed.\n\nBut the Achievement process for Legends Never Die (https://www.wowhead.com/achievement=61574/legends-never-die) does not show the Root of the world (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88998/root-of-the-world) as completed. even though i have the hoseing decor in my Catalog.\n\nIf someone figures out how to get \"unstuck\" please let me know.",
            date = "2026-05-30T13:07:36-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90741#comments:id=6362216",
        },
        {
            id = 6438504,
            score = 1,
            author = "Androktasiai",
            text = "Not sure if this will help anyone, but here was my catchup process. tl;dr: I was able to use an alt to do the Root of the World (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88998/root-of-the-world) weekly, which allowed my main to proceed with the quest chain through to the Chimereus kill. So it seems as of right now you may not need to do the Empty Cradle chain (https://www.wowhead.com/storyline/the-empty-cradle-5929) on the specific character who has done Root of the World (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88998/root-of-the-world).\n\nPer other comments on quests in this chain, in order to unlock the Root of the World (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88998/root-of-the-world) and Sky's Hope (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88999/skys-hope) relics, you must first do the 5 other relics on a single character. On my main I was on 4/5 of the required 5 when I decided to finish this. I had done up to In the Name of the Goddess (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90734/in-the-name-of-the-goddess) in the Empty Cradle chain (https://www.wowhead.com/storyline/the-empty-cradle-5929). So I did the 5th of the required 5 relics on my main, then went and did from The Stolen Staff (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90735/the-stolen-staff) to A Legend to Know (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90740/a-legend-to-know). After turning A Legend to Know in I was not offered Once More Into the Rift (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90741/once-more-into-the-rift), nor could I do the Root of the World (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88998/root-of-the-world) (as I'd done my weekly already).\n\nI decided to check on an alt. The alt had the Root of the World (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=88998/root-of-the-world) available now for their weekly. Did that on the alt, and did NOT otherwise do the quest chain. Logged out, logged back into my main, and now Once More Into the Rift was available. I was able to proceed from there through to The Empty Cradle (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90745/the-empty-cradle) at this point. I somewhat luckily was doing this on a tank so my wait for a Chimereus kill wasn't too arduous.\n\nSo it seems once you do all 5 pre-req relics on one character, you can do the Root of the World on any other character (my alt is a 90 so I can't say for sure if a sub-90 could do it but possibly), and that should allow any other warband character to do the entire quest chain. With this in mind I'd say make sure you do the quest chain with Aksem on a class which can tank or heal, because the LFR queue for Dreamrift right now is easily an hour or more for a DPS.",
            date = "2026-09-29T19:06:44-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90741#comments:id=6438504",
        },
    },
    [90742] = {
        {
            id = 6326845,
            score = 19,
            author = "mncristy",
            text = "NOT IN RAID\nIf you didn't follow Orweyna (https://www.wowhead.com/npc=241742/orweyna), like me and went herbing, mining, etc... she headed SE to the water at the end of the path, she spends a few secs and then runs off.\n/way 62.37, 62.58\nUse the extra action bar to gather water, then proceed to kill the bluish/yellow mobs to fill the bar ___/100; small mobs (6); large mobs (10); elites (15).\n\nsidenote: You can always delete the quest and pick it up again to follow her to the water.",
            date = "2026-04-08T09:08:28-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90742#comments:id=6326845",
