        },
    },
    [90875] = {
        {
            id = 6292981,
            score = 89,
            author = "Chasavaqe",
            text = "This quest has unique text for draenei. Main quest text:\nOne more thing before we can return to our refuge. There is a domanaar, whose name is Snaerius. He scrys the vastness of the Great Dark Beyond in search of more victims--more fighters for these pits.\n\nKill him and seize the focus he uses to spy on distant realms. It's the last piece of the puzzle.\n\nI wish I could join you in the fight, but I need to get the injured to safety. We will await your return, brother.\n\nWhen you go to turn in the quest, the following dialogue happens (in draenei):\nJuras: What do you mean you're not coming?\n\nTul'amar: I cannot let the domanaar follow you. There is no other way, brother.\n\nJuras breaks into a sob. Tul'amar looks away and wipes at the corner of her eye.\n\nTul'amar: Only I can open the way, and only I can ensure none of them come through.\n\nA gentle ocean breeze fills the cave.\n\nTul'amar pushes her staff into Juras's hands. Their fingers touch, and then she lets go.\n\nTurn in text:\nYou made this possible, (name). We kin, lost and now reunited... but they must return, and I must be the one to ensure it.\n\nI cannot walk through that portal with them. I must destroy it to ensure that no domanaar can follow them through and darken our skies as before.\n\nYou are my kin, but I cannot trust you with this. I can't rest until I know they're safe.\n\nUpon completing the quest, the following dialogue happens:\nJuras: (Draenei) Dioniss aca.\nTul'amar: (Draenei) Dioniss aca, little brother.\n\nTul'amar's name then becomes Tul'amar, Thrice-Exiled, and she has the following text when you talk with her\nDraenei. Exiled one.\n\nMy first exile was the day our great flight began. Velen's words roused my heart. All of us who stepped onto the Genedar, exiled from Argus as one. I prayed I was making the right choice.\n\nThe second was the day the Legion ambushed our world. I was with Juras, searching below ground for mineals to replace a broken power core. He had begged our mother to leave the ship and come help his big sister. The earth lurched from the steps of fel reavers. By the time we retuned to the surface, felfire cannons had forced the Genedar into the sky. They had to leave. They had no choice. I know that.\n\nAnd now... again.\n\nI need some time to be alone, but I'll find you out there-- somewhere safe, where we can talk at length.",
            date = "2026-02-28T10:49:14-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90875#comments:id=6292981",
        },
        {
            id = 6293368,
            score = 72,
            author = "EAKHawkEye",
            text = "/hug\n\nHug her when it's all done!",
            date = "2026-02-28T16:41:05-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90875#comments:id=6293368",
        },
        {
            id = 6297909,
            score = 56,
            author = "RomanVakarian",
            text = "You can also /hug her as any other race, the dialogue as it follows:\n\nYou hug Tul'amar, Thrice-Exiled\nTul'amar, Thrice-Exiled chokes back a sob and gives you a meaningful, thankful look\n\nGreat, between this and the paladin couple questline I've ran out of tears today. No problem, I was planning on crying today, anyway :')",
            date = "2026-03-04T18:07:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90875#comments:id=6297909",
        },
        {
            id = 6304560,
            score = 54,
            author = "Eddafred",
            text = "After turning in the quest, you can find her in the Howling Ridge, at 50.9 68.6\n\nTalking to her opens up several dialogue options, regarding things like her World her people settled, the Naaru, and the Vanguard of the Light.\nYou can also talk to https://www.wowhead.com/npc=253003 standing beside her to have https://www.wowhead.com/spell=210086 cast on you, giving Tul'Amar more fluent dialogue options.\n\nHonestly, kudos to whoever worked on designing this quest chain. It's very evident that a lot of work went into the minor details, considering the sheer amount of alternate dialogue.\nQuest chains of this quality are sadly lacking.",
            date = "2026-03-12T02:29:19-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=90875#comments:id=6304560",
        },
        {
