        {
            id = 6304103,
            score = 13,
            author = "Qellian",
            text = "\"We were young when our mother died. My sister held de tribes together with force of her will -without the loa.\nI could never be the warrior Zul'jarra is. I talk my way through problems. She plow through them head on.\nWe have different goals for de Amani. Zul'jarra focuses on growing and preserving de Amani tribes within Zul'Aman. I see strenght of the Amani -our tribe. We should conquer those around us! Zul'jarra doesnt understand.\nWhen Mor'duun came, I waw my vision of de Amani coming to life. With de lightwood, we would conquer de Twilight's Blade and then Eversong.\nZul'jarra could not see my vision. But i saw no other way. De loa? Feh.\nDe Loa say our grandfather, de great Zul'jin betrayed them. But why believe them? Or my dotterin' uncle. Or any gokinye?\nThey abandoned us. They. Abandoned. Us. How do we know they wont do again?\nI see your eyes are widening, \"hash'ura\". You are right. Forget what I have said. We have won. Zul'jarra has won. I'll go back to village and celebrate with my sister.\"\n\nif only we got a 'shove' option right after that... How is this guy even 'talk' out of his problems?",
