        },
        {
            id = 6434121,
            score = 1,
            author = "ohvist",
            text = "When Halduron burst into a war council shouting about hidden worlds and ancient warriors, I thought he had gone mad. But now that I've seen the Haranir with my own eyes...\n\nWe are lucky to have them as potential allies. And lucky to have you, I'd say, in brokering that relationship.\n\nYeah, yeah, yeah. I'm awesome. Sure I could have gone out of our way to cashing in my sociopolitical clout as Jarl of the Jandvik (https://www.wowhead.com/quest=40336/turning-the-tidemistress) to get the Vrykul, or cashing in those favors I made with Vorrik (https://www.wowhead.com/ptr/quest=50551/temple-of-sethraliss-avatar-of-the-loa) to recruit the Sethrak, maybe convinced my Alliance counterpart to help integrate the Pearlfin and Waveblade Ankoan together to help stabilize their populations to get Jinyu, or make an argument with Eternus' faction of Infinite Dragons to tear open another time portal to Alternate Draenor so we could bring the Arakkoa over just like the Horde did with the Mag'har...\n\nWhat was I talking about? Oh. Right, thanking me for saving you and unknowingly damning us all to playing host to these pathetic Dark Trolls who offer no significant tactical or combat advantage beyond serving as glorified meat shields.",
            date = "2026-09-23T10:50:43-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=91084#comments:id=6434121",
        },
    },
