        {
            id = 6308596,
            score = 1,
            author = "Jeolene",
            text = "Hagar: \"Champion, the smell of smoke fills me with the same dread I felt on that terrible day.\"  Followed up with dialogue in the next quest: \"I do not know what losses you have experience, or what pain you carry\".\n\nMe, a night elf, also happen to be mounted on the Teldrassil hypogryph when turning the quest in:  \"I think we need to sit down and have a chat, lady.\"\n\nI swear, blizz can be so incompetent with their writing,  I don't see why night elves didn't have some kind of weigh-in on these quests.  You know, the very race that lived in that tree and are directly related to the creation of world trees?\n\nI am so sick of our characters being the fifth wheel in these quests, only the main story characters are recognized for doing great things.  We just have to pick up everyone else's poop.",
            date = "2026-03-16T08:56:10-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=91874#comments:id=6308596",
        },
