        {
            id = 6301299,
            score = 0,
            author = "Lovecraft666",
            text = "This quest seems like a clear reference to Berserk and the Brand of Sacrifice created by late manga author Kentaro Miura.\n\nIn Berserk, the Brand of Sacrifice is a mark carved into someone’s flesh that marks them as an offering to demonic entities. Those branded are constantly hunted by dark creatures, and the mark often bleeds in the presence of evil.\n\nThe quest text here strongly echoes that idea:\n\n“The tattoos that mark our flesh are more than just ink. They're a promise inscribed across our flesh… our lifeblood is a currency used to purchase Azeroth's future.”\n\nA permanent mark tied to sacrifice, blood, and holding back dark forces feels very reminiscent of the Brand’s symbolism in Berserk. Considering Blizzard’s long history of anime/manga nods, this feels like a deliberate homage.",
            date = "2026-03-07T22:13:57-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=92508#comments:id=6301299",
        },
    },
